QuestLocFlavor[3] = {
[1501]={"Reinn está muerto... ¡y su asesino está cerca!","Has encontrado un rastro que indica que Khîl vino por aquí (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Busca rastros de Khîl (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Habla con Mögr en el Gran Salón de Durin","'Desearía haberte seguido, ${PLAYER}, pero para cuando me di cuenta ya te habías ido, pues eres más valientes y mejor que yo.\
\
'¡Pobre Reinn! Fui cruel por mi parte mandarlo lejos, y murió para traerme una información que estaba dispuesto a ignorar. Solo tú le hiciste justicia, pues lo vengaste.\
\
'Honraré su memoria en la Sala Vigesimoprimera para siempre, y nunca bajaremos de nuevo la guardia. ¡Fui un necio! ¡Un loco!'","Has derrotado a Ozût, el asesino de Reinn, pero la investigación no ha terminado...","¡Khîl se acerca!","Busca en la plataforma rastros de Khîl","Reinn nunca llegó a la Sala Vigesimoprimera para entregar su informe a Mögr. Con los peligros de Zelem-melek acechando en su camino, no puedes evitar preocuparte por él.","Khîl probablemente se dirigió hacia la plataforma de lo alto del centro del Gran Salón de Durin.\
\
Deberías buscar en lo alto de la plataforma más rastros de Khîl.","Has vengado al pobre Reinn... y te das cuenta de que alguien te observa","Reinn intentaba llegar a la Sala Vigesimoprimera desde el Gran Salón de Durin.\
\
Deberías volver sobre tus pasos desde la Sala Vigesimoprimera y buscar a Reinn, yendo hacia el sur y luego girando a la derecha en el pasadizo.","'Si a ti te preocupa... yo también debería estar preocupado. Espero que encuentres a Reinn y le envíes de vuelta aquí. De verdad que de menos a ese insensato.\
\
'Prometo que intentaré hacerlo mejor y escucharle. Creo que no estaba completamente equivocado en ser tan prudente.\
\
'¡Por favor, vuelve con Reinn, ${PLAYER}!'","Ozût mencionó a otro orco implicado en la muerte de Reinn.\
\
Deberías buscar en los pasadizos hacia el Gran Salón de Durin pistas para localizar a Khîl.","Volviendo sobre sus pasos","Busca a Reinn","Mögr te ha seguido hasta aquí. Está quieto y en silencio.\
\
Deberías hablar con Mögr."},
[1502]={"'¿Puedes decir palabras de aliento a algunos de mis vecinos y decirles que incluso en días oscuros, trabajar con las manos en artesanía y comercio puede hacer que los días parezcan más brillantes? ¡Eso ayudará, seguramente!'","'¿Me rechazó? Hmmph. Bueno, tomaré esa bolsa de monedas.\
\
'De todos modos, agradezco que se lo hayas preguntado por mí. Toma, llévate algunas de las monedas que le habría dado a Edhan. Aun así, tengo que pensar en qué puedo hacer ahora. Mi problema persiste: ¡si la gente tiene miedo de trabajar en el Salón de Artesanía, mi negocio se verá afectado!\
\
'¿Qué está pasando en Herne estos días?'","Edhan está fuera de la puerta trasera de la Posada de la Encrucijada.","Los vecinos desanimados de Alwena necesitan algunas palabras de aliento.","Alwena está preocupada por la falta de visitantes al Salón de Artesanía.","Habla con Alwena fuera del Salón de Artesanía","Malo para el negocio","'Lleva esa bolsa de monedas a Edhan, que trabaja en la Posada de la Encrucijada. ¡Es un joven fuerte y robusto, y he notado sus músculos en más de una ocasión! Dile que esas monedas deberían aliviar cualquier reticencia que pueda sentir a dejar de trabajar para Maddoc en la posada, ¡y en el futuro será muy bien pagado por trabajar para mí en su lugar!'","Edhan escucha con el ceño fruncido mientras le explicas que Alwena desea contratarlo para vigilar el Salón de Artesanía.\
\
'Hay muchas monedas aquí, pero no creo que pueda dejar a Maddoc solo así. Ha sido bueno conmigo, y no sé cómo la Posada de la Encrucijada logrará mantenerse abierta sin mí haciendo el trabajo pesado.\
\
'Dile a Alwena que aprecio la oferta, pero debo rechazarla. Sé que me quejo de llevar tantas cajas todo el día, pero creo que estar de pie en un solo lugar en el Salón de Artesanía me agotaría aún más rápido... ¡de aburrimiento!'","Habla con Edhan fuera de la Posada de la Encrucijada","'Es una oferta muy generosa, pero creo que debo rechazarla.'","Alwena está fuera del Salón de Artesanía en Herne.","'Mi nombre es Alwena, y dirijo el Salón de Artesanía aquí en Herne. Sin embargo, últimamente ha habido una disminución de clientes, ¡y quiero llegar al fondo del asunto! ¿Puedes decir palabras de aliento a algunos de mis vecinos y decirles que incluso en días oscuros, trabajar con las manos en artesanía y comercio puede hacer que los días parezcan más brillantes?\
\
'¡Eso ayudará, seguramente!'","Di palabras de aliento a los vecinos de Alwena (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'¿La gente parece asustada? ¡Necesito que se sientan seguros cuando vengan al Salón de Artesanía, o mi negocio se verá afectado!\
\
'Necesito contratar a un guardia para que vigile dentro del Salón de Artesanía, y entonces se sentirán más seguros. Toma, lleva esta bolsa de monedas a Edhan, que trabaja en la Posada de la Encrucijada. ¡Es un joven fuerte y robusto, y he notado sus músculos en más de una ocasión! Dile que esas monedas deberían aliviar cualquier reticencia que pueda sentir a dejar de trabajar para Maddoc en la posada, ¡y en el futuro será muy bien pagado por trabajar para mí en su lugar!'"},
[1504]={"Recolecta pieles de tejón en el Páramo Alto (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","¡Ah, gracias, ${PLAYER}! Estas servirán muy bien.'","'Quizá lo sepas, quizá no, pero un grupo de visitantes de tierras lejanas se está preparando para partir. Algunos de ellos son de alto renombre, y es apropiado que partan con todas las provisiones que necesitan.\
\
'Por esa razón, quisiera que cases a los tejones del Páramo Alto y me traigas sus pieles. Servirán para hacer guantes cálidos y forros de capucha para los viajeros.\
\
'¿Me ayudarás con esto?'","Pieles de tejón recolectadas en el Páramo Alto (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Canaddal está apostado en lo alto del sendero que desciende hacia las Gargantas del Bruinen desde el Páramo Alto.\
\
Deberías llevar las pieles de tejón que recolectaste a Canaddal.","'¿Has traído las pieles que te pedí?'","Los tejones pueden encontrarse por toda el Páramo Alto, en el Bosque de los Trolls.\
\
Canaddal te ha pedido que cases tejones para obtener sus pieles.","El explorador elfo Canaddal está encargado de equipar y abastecer a un grupo de visitantes que se prepara para partir de Rivendel.","Lleva las pieles de tejón a Canaddal","Cacería de tejones"},
[1505]={"Derrota a los capataces de la Mano Blanca (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Habla con Borgar en Jazârgund","Capataces de la Mano Blanca derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Los enanos de Jazârgund están preocupados por la presencia de los uruks de la Mano Blanca tan dentro de Moria.","'Me han informado de que hay uruks de la Mano Blanca por toda la Gran Excavación, pero no creía que hubieran llegado tan dentro. Los he visto, apoderándose de los salones hacia el oeste, y temo qué propósitos podrían tener aquí. Sospechaba que su plan sería alistar a algunas de las tribus de trasgos para suplir sus fuerzas, pero ahora temo que sea algo más siniestro.\
\
'Los que me tienen especialmente preocupados son los capataces de la Mano Blanca. Parece que tienen una influencia considerable sobre los orcos de Khazad-dûm. Te pido que derrotes a tantos de ellos como puedas... quizá eso desmoralice a los otros.'","Los capataces de la Mano Blanca se encuentran en Fehem-dûm y Hadâd-dûm, al este de Jazârgund.\
\
Borgar tema que los uruks de la Mano Blanca estén intentando controlar a los orcos y trasgos de Moria. Quiere ver su número reducido.","'Si la Mano Blanca se apodera de Khazad-dûm, o se alía con las fuerzas de aquí, seremos los primeros en caer en esta guerra.'","'Así que la mayoría de ellos ha caído... eso está bien. Me atrevería a decir que les va a ser difícil reclutar trasgos sin ellos.\
\
'¡Hasta que la Mano Blanca sea expulsada de estos salones no estaré satisfecho! ¡Gracias por tu ayuda, ${PLAYER}!","Emisarios de la Mano Blanca","Borgar está en Jazârgund, al oeste de Hadâd-dûm y Fehem-dûm.\
\
Borgar se alegrará de saber que el número de los uruks de la Mano Blanca se ha reducido en gran medida."},
[1506]={"'Watch for these tokens in your battles here in Gathbúrz, ${PLAYER}. These black badges display the favour of the masters of Dol Guldur, and they are awarded to those among our enemies who have slain valiant defenders of the West in battle here or abroad.\
\
'Each of these you gather from a foe signifies a fallen comrade avenged, be they Elf, Man, dwarf or even from among the brave little halflings.\
\
'I wish you good hunting.'","'So, another handful of those who have fallen before the Dark Lord's power have been avenged.\
\
'Soon, this darkness shall lift from the world, and the people of the West will no longer live under the fear of utter dominion.'","Collect black badges (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Badges of Dishonour","'I wish to see the badges of the Enemy to know that his minions have fallen at your hands....'","The black badges of Dol Guldur may be found upon enemy soldiers in Gathbúrz.\
\
Rodelleth has asked you to collect the black badges of Dol Guldur in memory of the fallen.","The Black Badges of Dol Guldur are awarded to soldiers who have slain valiant defenders of the West.","YOU SHOULD NOT SEE THIS","Collected black badges (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Bring black badges to Rodelleth","Rodelleth is at Thangúlhad in Gathbúrz.\
\
You should bring the badges you have claimed to Rodelleth."},
[1507]={"¡Frodo Bolsón busca a un aventurero que le ayude a preparar una sorpresa de cumpleaños para su tío Bilbo! Viaja a Rivendel para descubrir cómo puedes ayudarle.","'¡Hola! Ah, ¿estás aquí para ayudarme con la sorpresa de cumpleaños para mi tío Bilbo?'","Puedes encontrar a Frodo en Rivendel, en el interior de la Última Morada.\
\
¡El cumpleaños de Frodo y Bilbo Bolsón está próximo! Frodo está buscando a un aventurero que le ayude a preparar una sorpresa de cumpleaños para su tío Bilbo.","Con los cumpleaños de Frodo y Bilbo Bolsón a la vuelta de la esquina, Frodo busca a un aventurero que le ayude a preparar una sorpresa para su tío Bilbo. Viaja a Rivendel para ayudar a Frodo con sus planes.","Viaja a Rivendel y habla con Frodo Bolsón","El cumpleaños de los Bolsón","Habla con Frodo Bolsón en la Última Morada, en Rivendel"},
[1508]={"Escucha la historia del niño.","El cumpleaños de los Bolsón: la historia de un niño","'¿Perdón? ¿Qué es lo que preguntas? ¡Ah, sí! ¡Sé un montón de historias sobre Bilbo! Mamá me las cuenta algunas noches cuando no puedo dormirme.'","Un joven niño hobbit ha accedido a compartir una historia sobre Bilbo Bolsón y sus aventuras.","'Mamá me cuenta historias del señor Bilbo algunas noches cuando no consigo dormirme. ¡Mis favoritas son las de la Montaña Solitaria, con el dragón y el tesoro!\
\
'Creo que me gustaría tener un dragón, pero solo uno bueno, no uno malo. Mi dragón bueno viviría conmigo y nos traería cosas brillantes para jugar, ¡y yo volaría con él por el cielo! Los dragones son súper listos, ya sabes, y el mío me contaría historias y me enseñaría cosas que solo saben los dragones.\
\
'Pero, ¿sabes?, no dejo de pensar en esa pobre montaña. ¡Si hasta se llama la Montaña Solitaria, y eso era cuando todavía tenía un dragón amigo! Pero desde que Bilbo espantó al dragón, apuesto a que esa montaña está todavía más sola. Me da tanta pena que algunas noches lloro abrazado a mi oveja de peluche, Petunia.\
\
'Y entonces pensé en el buen señor Bilbo, ¡y seguro que él siente lo mismo! Apostaría a que volvió a esa pobre montaña para hacerle compañía. ¡Si yo fuera él, le llevaría otro dragón, pero uno bueno esta vez, para que le hiciera compañía durante años y años y años! ¡Seguro que eso es justo lo que hizo!'","Habla con el niño"},
[1509]={"Cumpleaños de Bolsón - El regalo de Bilbo","Cuéntale a Bilbo sobre la solicitud de Frodo.","'¿Historias? ¿De la Comarca? ¿Y todas sobre mí? ¡No puedo esperar a escucharlas! Por favor, cuéntame tus relatos.'","Bilbo está encantado con tus historias y quiere recompensarte por tu tiempo.","Cuenta las historias que has recopilado a Bilbo Bolsón para su entretenimiento.","'¡Oh, cielos! ¡Oh, Dios mío! ¡Son incluso mejores de lo que pensaba! La imaginación de los hobbits realmente no tiene límites. ¿La Montaña Solitaria? ¿Las tartas de Holly Corneta? ¿¡Incluso un cruzado con capa!? ¡Oh, por todos los cielos!\
\
'Has hecho muy feliz a este viejo hobbit, y me has hecho reír como no lo hacía desde hace tiempo. Los elfos, con todos sus encantos, tienen un sentido del humor más esotérico. ¡Extrañaba las historias que cuentan los hobbits!\
\
'Toma esto con mi agradecimiento. Claramente tienes un don para registrar y contar historias. Espero que continúes con ello durante tus aventuras, ya que siento que tendrás muchas historias que contar!'","Habla con Bilbo Bolsón","Cuéntale a Bilbo las historias que has recopilado","'¡Me imagino que esas historias tienen a alguien esperándolas! ¡Vete ahora!'","'¡Hola, ${PLAYER}! Espero que estés muy bien, estoy seguro. ¿Y qué te ha traído aquí en este buen día?'","Cuéntale a Bilbo las historias que has recopilado."},
[1510]={"Escucha la historia de Bogo Redondo.","'Así que te preguntas qué ha estado haciendo Bilbo desde que desapareció, ¿eh? Pues resulta que he oído que no está en ninguna tierra lejana, sino que sigue aquí mismo, en la Comarca.\
\
'Todo aquel asunto de la fiesta fue una elaborada artimaña para hacer que la gente hablara, difundiera rumores y pensara que estaba lejos, viviendo nuevas aventuras. ¡No fue más que la manera de Bilbo de crear una distracción mientras se escabullía para esconderse a plena vista!\
\
'La gente dice que por la noche a veces se le puede ver, vestido de negro, con el rostro oculto tras una máscara oscura y una capa aún más oscura ondeando a su espalda, cabalgando por los caminos de la Comarca. Se ha convertido en una especie de vigilante, protegiéndonos a todos de bandidos, trasgos y cualquier otra cosa desagradable que intente colarse en nuestros pueblos.\
\
'Bilbo ha logrado mantenerse oculto gracias a sus agujeros hobbit secretos repartidos por toda la Comarca. Fueron construidos en secreto y pagados con su fortuna, y se mueve entre ellos, sin pasar demasiado tiempo en un mismo lugar, siempre atento y esperando que aparezca el peligro.'","'¿Por Bilbo Bolsón preguntas, eh? La mayoría cree que anda por ahí de aventuras en sabe el cielo dónde, pero yo tengo una historia muy distinta que contarte, si quieres escucharla.'","El cumpleaños de los Bolsón: la historia de Bogo Redondo","Habla con Bogo Redondo","Bogo Redondo ha accedido a compartir una historia sobre Bilbo Bolsón y sus aventuras."},
[1511]={"El cumpleaños de los Bolsón: la historia de Dudo Redondo","'Oh, reuniendo historias sobre Bilbo Bolsón, el pez gordo, ¿eh? Desde luego hay más que suficientes como para repartir.\
\
'Por suerte para ti, resulta que yo conozco la verdad de ese extraño truco de desaparición que hizo en su fiesta, ¡claro que sí!'","Dudo Redondo ha accedido a compartir una historia sobre Bilbo Bolsón y sus aventuras.","Escucha la historia de Dudo Redondo.","'Como iba diciendo, esto es lo que pasó en aquella fiesta de cumpleaños de Bilbo.\
\
'Verás, durante sus aventuras se encontró con un montón de enanos. ¡Sí, enanos! Cualquiera que sepa algo sabe que algunos de esos enanos se volvieron bastante peculiares tras perder su hogar en aquellas montañas lejanas hace tanto tiempo.\
\
'Desde entonces, cuentan las historias, algunos andan de aquí para allá en cuadrilla, haciendo casi cualquier cosa para salir adelante, y eso, si me preguntas, acaba relajando mucho la moral. Suponiendo que alguna vez la tuvieran, que con gente que no es de la Comarca nunca se sabe, no señor.\
\
'He oído que uno de esos enanos ayudó a Bilbo a excavar un entramado de túneles bajo Bolsón Cerrado, ¡y que él simplemente se coló por allí en el momento oportuno! Solo el cielo sabe qué habrá estado tramando desde entonces, pero puedes apostar a que no es nada en lo que se vería envuelto un hobbit respetable.'","Habla con Dudo Redondo"},
[1512]={"Habla con El Tío Gamyi en Hobbiton-Delagua","Frodo Bolsón te pide que viajes a la Comarca para recopilar las historias que cuentan los hobbits acerca de la misteriosa desaparición de su tío Bilbo, su paradero actual y las aventuras que ha vivido.","', me alegra que estés aquí. Necesito a un ${PLAYERNAME:un aventurero[m]|una aventurera[f]} como tú para ayudarme con una sorpresa de cumpleaños para mi tío Bilbo.\
\
'Cuando Bilbo decidió establecerse en Rivendel, lo hizo a su manera, como quizá hayas oído: ¡con un estallido y un destello, desapareciendo en pleno festejo de su propio cumpleaños!\
\
'En ese instante, Bilbo se convirtió en tema de innumerables historias exageradas y leyendas cada vez más desmesuradas. Sé que le divertiría enormemente oírlas, pero yo no puedo ir a recogerlas. La próxima vez que estés en la Comarca, ¿podrías hacerlo por mí?\
\
'Si yo fuera tú, empezaría por El Tío Gamyi. Oye casi todo lo que merece ser escuchado y sabrá con toda seguridad a quién debes acudir para conseguir los mejores relatos.'","El Tío Gamyi se encuentra justo al sur del Árbol de la Fiesta y al noroeste del Puente de Delagua.\
\
Frodo te ha pedido que recopiles los relatos que cuentan los hobbits de la Comarca acerca de su tío Bilbo. Ha sugerido que hables con El Tío Gamyi para averiguar qué hobbits son los que tienen las mejores historias que contar.","El cumpleaños de los Bolsón: la petición de Frodo","'¡Buenas! ¿Así que te envía Frodo para hablar conmigo? ¿Qué estará tramando ahora ese jovenzuelo?'"},
[1513]={"Habla con El Tío Gamyi","'¿Tiene sentido la nota, entonces?\
\
'Si yo fuera tú, empezaría hablando con Ted Arenas. Solo tienes que seguir este camino hacia el este y luego girar al sur. Ted está justo al sur del Puente de Delagua.\
\
'Sé que ahora Ted tiene tiempo, así que estará encantado de compartir su historia. Recuerda que no todos los hobbits de la lista tendrán siempre una historia que contar; vuelve a verlos de vez en cuando y seguro que los pillas en buen momento.'","Escucha el resto de las historias de los hobbits.","Escucha el relato de la narradora","Escucha la historia de Robin Madriguera","Habla con El Tío Gamyi; seguramente sabrá con quién deberías hablar primero.","Lee la nota de El Tío Gamyi","Escucha la historia de Lobelia Sacovilla-Bolsón","'¿Has conseguido hablar con todos los hobbits de mi lista? ¡Estupendo!\
\
'Si con eso ya tienes lo que necesitabas, adelante entonces. ¡Es hora de llevar estas historias a su destinatario final!'","Escucha la historia de Lotho Sacovilla-Bolsón","Desde la casa de El Tío Gamyi, sigue este camino hacia el este y luego gira al sur. Ted está justo al sur del Puente de Delagua.\
\
Habla con Ted Arenas para escuchar la primera de las historias sobre Bilbo y sus aventuras.","Escucha la historia del cartero Cavada","Escucha la historia del niño","Escucha la historia de Ted Arenas","Regresa junto a El Tío Gamyi","El Tío Gamyi es quien mejor sabe qué hobbits tienen las mejores historias que contar sobre la desaparición de Bilbo, sus aventuras y su paradero desde entonces.","Habla con El Tío Gamyi para obtener su lista de hobbits con historias que merecen la pena recopilar.","Ya has hablado con todos los hobbits. Deberías volver a consultar con El Tío Gamyi.","Escucha la historia de Hereward Lomatierra","Escucha la historia de Hal Corneta","'Muy bien, aquí tienes la lista. Échale un vistazo rápido para asegurarte de que puedes leer mi letra.'","El Tío Gamyi te ha dado una nota","Lee la nota de El Tío Gamyi.","Escucha la historia de Bogo Redondo","Escucha la historia de Dudo Redondo","El cumpleaños de los Bolsón: la lista de Gamyi","'Así que estás aquí para recopilar historias sobre Bilbo Bolsón, ¿eh? ¿Y te han dicho que yo sabría con quién hablar? Naturalmente, han acertado. Dame un momento y te escribiré una lista de los hobbits a los que deberías ir a ver.\
\
'Ten en cuenta que tendrás que pillarlos en el momento adecuado. Si no parecen tener ninguna historia para ti, vuelve a verlos al cabo de un rato. ¡Si quieres oírlas todas, necesitarás un poco de perseverancia!'"},
[1514]={"Hal Corneta ha accedido a compartir una historia sobre Bilbo Bolsón y sus aventuras.","Escucha la historia de Hal Corneta.","Habla con Hal Corneta","'¿Bilbo, eh? La gente te contará cualquier tontería sobre lo que pasó en su fiesta de cumpleaños, pero ¿qué gracia tiene eso? Si me preguntas, todo fue humo y espejos.\
\
'La verdadera historia está en lo que ocurrió después. Y, por casualidad, ¡de eso sí que sé un montón!'","'Yo siempre ando con la oreja pegada al suelo, y puedo asegurarte sin lugar a dudas que Bilbo regresó junto a los Elfos. Siempre contaba historias sobre ellos que no te creerías.\
\
'Dicen que una Reina Élfica le ha estado enseñando a cultivar las patatas más grandes que nadie podría imaginar. Muy propio de Bilbo, marcharse hasta tierras élficas para adquirir conocimientos con tal de arrebatarle al granjero Maggot el primer premio en una de esas Ferias Agrícolas.\
\
'Algunos se esforzarían más en su propio huerto, pero Bilbo jamás fue de hacer las cosas por la vía fácil cuando podía convertirlas en una aventura. Me imagino que volverá cualquier día de estos para borrar esa sonrisilla satisfecha de la cara del granjero Maggot y poner fin a su racha de sesenta años ganando.'","El cumpleaños de los Bolsón: la historia de Hal Corneta"},
[1515]={"Hereward Lomatierra ha accedido a compartir una historia sobre Bilbo Bolsón y sus aventuras.","El cumpleaños de los Bolsón: la historia de Hereward Lomatierra","'¡Ah! ¿Estás reuniendo historias sobre Bilbo Bolsón? Pues tengo una de las buenas para ti; ese individuo ha estado en muchos lugares y ha visto muchas cosas, desde luego que sí.'","'He oído que Bilbo vivió un buen montón de aventuras después de su fiesta, pero tú quieres saber qué anda haciendo ahora, ¿verdad?\
\
'Pues te contaré que al final, por lo que he oído, se topó con esa gente grande que siempre va a caballo… ¿cómo se llamaban… los Jinetes de Ronald? ¿Roger? No, casi… lo tengo en la punta de la lengua… ¡Rohan! ¡Eso es! He oído que se hizo con un poney de guerra y que le enseñaron a ser un auténtico maestro de los caballos y todo eso.\
\
'Cabalgando en la compañía de… maldita sea, ¿cómo se llamaba ese tipo…? Theon… no… Teorema… ah, tampoco… espera un momento… ¡Théoden! ¡Ese es! Allí está nuestro Bilbo, cabalgando con esa gente grande, con estandartes ondeando y caballos relinchando, cruzando esas enormes llanuras de hierba tan alta que podría esconder a un hobbit entero, ¡o eso dicen!'","Escucha la historia de Hereward Lomatierra.","Habla con Hereward Lomatierra"},
[1516]={"Habla con Holly Corneta","El cumpleaños de Bolsón - El relato de Holly Corneta","Holly Corneta ha accedido a compartir una historia sobre Bilbo Bolsón y sus aventuras.","'¿Qué es eso? Oh, ¿te preguntas dónde está Bilbo ahora? ¡Resulta que has preguntado a la hobbit correcta!'","'¡Les aseguro que tengo información de excelente fuente de que en sus viajes Bilbo se encontró con un enorme oso! Sí, un oso enorme, nada que ver con los pequeños osos que viven por aquí. ¿Y qué hizo Bilbo?\
\
'No, no seas imbécil, el oso no se lo comió de un bocado. ¡Imagínate la indigestión con todos esos botones de cobre!\
\
'Ahora, Bilbo puede que no sea un hobbit respetable, pero sigue siendo un hobbit, y eso significa que llevaba consigo una gran cantidad de cosas deliciosas que ese oso nunca había olido o probado antes. Con eso, el astuto Bilbo domó a ese oso, ¡de hecho lo hizo! Y eso no es todo, no, no es así. Justo llegamos a la mejor parte, si lo crees.\
\
'Radagast el Pardo, ¿has oído hablar de él? Guardián de los animales dicen y un mago respetable por derecho propio, bueno, Radagast escuchó sobre Bilbo y el oso y estaba tan impresionado que entrenó al viejo Bilbo para que se convirtiera en un Sabio.\
\
'Ni bromeando ni jugando estoy hablando en serio, así es, el primer Sabio Hobbit es nuestro Bilbo, y ahora cabalga por ahí en su gran oso, acompañando a Radagast por todas las tierras!'","Escucha la historia de Holly Corneta."},
[1517]={"Lobelia Sacovilla-Bolsón ha accedido a compartir una historia sobre Bilbo Bolsón y sus aventuras.","Escucha la historia de Lobelia Sacovilla-Bolsón.","'¡Ay, si aquí no se habla de otra cosa que de Bilbo Bolsón! Pero, mira tú por dónde, sé un detalle de lo más jugoso que no me importa compartir con alguien como tú.'","Habla con Lobelia Sacovilla-Bolsón","El cumpleaños de los Bolsón: la historia de Lobelia Sacovilla-Bolsón","'Escucha bien y quizá aprendas algo que merezca la pena saber. Más temprano ese mismo día, el día de la fiesta quiero decir, te haré saber que vi a Bilbo probando un buen número de las empanadas de Holly Corneta.\
\
'Siempre tienen un aspecto delicioso, pero juraría que usa ingredientes secretos que echarían para atrás hasta al comilón más decidido. No es que yo sienta celos, ojo. Mis empanadas siempre quedan en segundo lugar y me quedo tranquilo sabiendo que están hechas solo con las mejores frutas, no con esas nuevas tonterías de las que se oyen rumores, no como hacen ALGUNAS personas que yo conozco, y si eso es suficiente para mí, pues bueno... perdona, ¿qué estaba diciendo? Eso es, el señor Bilbo.\
\
'Como decía, he oído que Holly estaba experimentando y metía a escondidas setas molidas, robadas del campo del granjero Maggot. Si escuchas a los jovenzuelos de por aquí que se han colado en su campo y han comido algunas, sabes que provocan efectos de lo más extraños.\
\
'Así que, si quieres saber lo que yo pienso, y está claro que sí porque me lo estás preguntando, creo que fue comer esas empanadas y Bilbo desapareció. Menos mal que ese raro de Gandalf andaba cerca para taparlo todo con una nubecilla de humo y ahorrarnos el escándalo, aunque algunos piensan que se perdió una lección importante por el camino.'"},
[1518]={"Lotho Sacovilla-Bolsón ha accedido a compartir una historia sobre Bilbo Bolsón y sus aventuras.","'Oh, ¿te preguntas qué habrá estado tramando el Loco Bolsón? ¡Ja! Si me preguntas a mí, era todo ingenio y nada de buen juicio. Y resulta que conozco una historia de lo más divertida sobre el lío en el que se ha metido, claro que sí.'","Habla con Lotho Sacovilla-Bolsón","Escucha la historia de Lotho Sacovilla-Bolsón.","'Bueno, según lo último que he oído, el viejo Bolsón había dilapidado por completo su fortuna, aunque yo nunca creí que fuera ni la mitad de grande de lo que decía la gente, así que tampoco era tan difícil perderla toda, ¿no?\
\
'Pero como iba diciendo, sin su fortuna, he oído que se fue a una de esas ciudades de la Gente Grande y se compró la mejor barba postiza que pudo pagar con el dinero que le quedaba. Vamos, no empieces a reírte todavía, que aún no has oído lo mejor, y recuerda lo que dije de que era muy listo, pero con poco sentido común.\
\
'¡Pues bien! Con la barba falsa puesta, ¡se fue a vivir con los enanos! ¡Sí, enanos! Se coló entre ellos, en sus cuevas y sus excavaciones. Por lo que tengo entendido, los enanos no son muy despiertos, y esas cuevas deben de estar llenas de sombras y humo por las antorchas, ¿no te parece?\
\
'Con la barba puede ocultarse y trabajar codo con codo junto a ellos, mientras poco a poco se va forjando una nueva fortuna a base de gemas y metales preciosos guardados en los bolsillos. Apuesto a que volverá algún día para presumir otra vez de sus aventuras y de sus supuestas riquezas delante de todos nosotros.'","El cumpleaños de los Bolsón: la historia de Lotho Sacovilla‑Bolsón"},
[1519]={"Cumpleaños de Bolsón - el relato del Cartero Cavada","'¿Buscas historias sobre Bilbo, verdad? Bueno, como cartero, conozco a la mayoría de la gente y escucho muchas cosas. Sin duda puedo dedicar un poco de tiempo para contarte un relato.'","Escucha la historia del cartero Cavada.","El cartero Cavada ha accedido a compartir una historia sobre Bilbo Bolsón y sus aventuras.","'¿Quieres saber dónde se ha metido Bilbo? Bueno, si preguntas por aquí, la gente te contará todo tipo de tonterías. ¡Que lo secuestraron o que vuela en su propio dragón o que lidera una tribu de arañas guerreras!\
\
'La credulidad de los hobbits a veces es increíble. Se aferran a cualquier historia que escuchan, ¡y cuanto más exótica, mejor! ¿Puedes imaginar a Bilbo haciendo alguna de esas cosas a su edad? ¡Dios mío, es un hobbit único pero tiene límites!\
\
'Puedo ver que eres del tipo sensato, así que te diré la verdad real: Bilbo siempre ha tenido una terrible afición por los Elfos. Francamente inquietante si me preguntas, pero él nunca fue de los que se preocupan por las convenciones. De todos modos, decidió pasar el resto de sus días con ellos, ¡invitado por los líderes elfos y todo!\
\
'Ha pasado sus años de declive viviendo con ellos y disfrutando de su hospitalidad, mientras escribe sus memorias en forma de una obra de un solo acto “Donde hay Smaug, hay fuego.” He oído que la Gala de la Hermandad de la Brigada del Cubo Benevolente para los Magullados y Quemados de Los Gamos tiene los derechos exclusivos para la apertura!'","Habla con el cartero Cavada"},
[1520]={"'Bilbo Bolsón era algo excéntrico por estos lares. ¡Sus aventuras dieron lugar a tantas historias que todavía hoy se oyen nuevas cada día! Hace poco hablaba con el sobrino de la cuñada del primo de mi sobrina, y decía que sabía lo que realmente ocurrió en aquella fiesta de cumpleaños tan rara.\
\
'Toda la gente de la zona asistió, pero entre la comida, la bebida, los bailes y todos los chavales correteando, solo unos pocos presenciaron de verdad el truco de la desaparición.\
\
'El primo de la hermana de mi sobrina… en fin, ya sabes, el muchacho con el que hablaba decía que vio al mago Gandalf meter al viejo señor Bilbo en un saco enorme. Apenas se distinguía entre la niebla, decía, ¡y el señor Bilbo retorciéndose y forcejeando como un poseso! Y entonces desaparecieron sin dejar rastro.\
\
'Vete tú a saber qué le pasó después al pobre hombre, pero francamente… con todas las historias que se cuentan de sus aventuras, compañías y andanzas, ¿qué otro final podía esperar un hobbit sino uno bien pegajoso?'","Habla con Robin Madriguera","El cumpleaños de los Bolsón: la historia de Robin Madriguera","Escucha la historia del alguacil Robin Madriguera.","Ted Arenas ha accedido a compartir una historia sobre Bilbo Bolsón y sus aventuras.","'¿Qué es eso que preguntas ahora? ¿El viejo señor Bilbo, dices? ¡Claro que sé lo que pasó en su fiesta de cumpleaños!\
\
'Escucha bien y te contaré los hechos tal como ocurrieron.'"},
[1521]={"'Bilbo Bolsón podría mantenerme ocupada durante años con todas las historias que la gente de por aquí intercambia sobre él. Con gusto te contaré mis propias teorías sobre por qué desapareció durante su fiesta de cumpleaños.'","La narradora local ha accedido a compartir un relato sobre Bilbo Bolsón y sus aventuras.","'Algunos por aquí nunca estuvieron muy seguros de él, pero yo echo de menos al querido Bilbo. Siempre tuvo ese aire de misterio, lo cual ya es decir mucho, porque el único aire que rodea a la mayoría de los hobbits es el del humo de la hierba para pipa y su última comida.\
\
'Bilbo era refrescante, sí que lo era: nos removió a todos un poco, y eso es algo bueno, sin duda. ¡Necesitamos que nos saquen de nuestra rutina habitual! No todos tenemos madera de exploradores, así que cuando aparece un hobbit con historias auténticas que contar, es algo verdaderamente valioso.\
\
'En fin, he oído que Bilbo se estaba aburriendo, y ¿quién puede culparle? Así que cuando Gandalf empezó a lanzar sus preciosos fuegos artificiales, Bilbo se agarró a uno ¡y salió disparado! ¡Surcó el cielo dejando una estela de chispas! Sacude la cabeza si quieres, pero yo creo que Bilbo Bolsón era capaz de casi cualquier cosa que se propusiera, ¡y no pienso cambiar mi historia!\
\
'Ah, cómo me gustaría saber dónde aterrizó y qué travesuras habrá hecho desde entonces. Ojalá regrese a casa algún día, o puede que la curiosidad me haga estallar a mí misma como un estallido de estrellas.'","Habla con la narradora","El cumpleaños de los Bolsón: el relato de la narradora","Escucha el relato de la narradora."},
[1522]={"Escucha la historia de Ted Arenas.","'Bueno, pues lo que yo he oído es que Bilbo ya estaba harto en su cumpleaños. ¡Tanta gente, todos discutiendo, graznando e intentando colarse en Bolsón Cerrado para buscar tesoros! Cualquiera acabaría cansándose y queriendo que aquello terminara.\
\
'Bilbo siempre fue un hobbit... poco convencional, así que por lo visto decidió darles un buen susto a todos y escabullirse. Se fue a disfrutar donde no estaba su familia, ¡y se dedicó a recorrer tabernas y posadas probando sus bebidas!\
\
'Ahora bien, por lo que tengo entendido, nadie sabe con certeza qué pasó después, pero el primo del amigo del hijo de mi hermano trabaja en El Dragón Verde, y jura que al día siguiente envió un barril más pesado que los demás, que rodaba de forma extraña, como si hubiera algo dentro. ¡Y no se le ocurrió preguntarse nada hasta después!\
\
'Yo diría que Bilbo disfrutó un poco más de la cuenta, acabó metido en un barril bien cómodo... ¡y lo enviaron fuera! Solo el cielo sabe dónde estará ahora. Me pregunto qué bebidas tan curiosas habrá podido probar en tierras lejanas.'","El cumpleaños de los Bolsón: la historia de Ted Arenas","Habla con Ted Arenas","Ted Arenas ha accedido a compartir una historia sobre Bilbo Bolsón y sus aventuras.","'Claro que puedo contarte una historia sobre Bilbo Bolsón y su desaparición durante la fiesta de su cumpleaños hace ya tantos años. Solo préstame atención un momento.'"},
[1523]={"Lure out the massive ukhrash from its pond north of Bárgstad and collect its chitin","Talk to Fúsi Gem-cutter","Fúsi is at Bárgstad in the Pit of Stonejaws.\
\
Now that you have collected the massive chitin, you should bring it back to Fúsi.","The chitin from this beast is massive!","'${PLAYER}! I hope you have been well. We Gem-cutters are here to help! There may not be much use for rings and bracelets in time of war, but we're plenty resourceful folk; I know I can put my craft-skill to some other use.\
\
'Have you seen the strange shelled creatures that crawl hereabouts? They look a bit like crabs, but they are much larger. Their strange and bulbous eyes fill me with unease, I don't mind telling you. The Orcs call them 'Ukhrâsh.'\
\
'Well, I have had a thought, and that thought is this: perhaps we could use their shells to fashion useful articles for the war effort: shields, armour, who knows what else? But the shells of the small ones aren't thick enough to serve. Fret not! I have caught glimpses of a huge one! Only glimpses. I think it spends most of its time underwater, but I have a feeling that one's shell will be worth its weight in gold! I doubt you'll catch it out in the open, but perhaps you can lure it out with meat from the smaller uhkrâsh in the Pit of Stonejaws. I am hoping the big one is both scavenger and cannibal!'","Collected foul meat (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collect foul meat (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You present the massive ukhrash shell to Fúsi.\
\
'My goodness, ${PLAYER}! What a monster that must have been! I will be able to make something sturdy from this chitin, or my name is not Fúsi Gem-cutter! I mean, this is no gemstone, but my abilities are more wide-ranging than my name would suggest! And so it is with you, my friend.\
\
'Thank you for your help!'","Bait for the Big One","You should lure out the massive ukhrash from its pond north of Bárgstad.","You can find foul meat from ukhrâsh throughout the Pit of Stonejaws.","Fúsi Gem-cutter has requested your help with an unorthodox plan."},
[1524]={"Cuero extraordinario hervido obtenido (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Lleva el cuero extraordinario hervido a Hasta (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¿Has reunido los materiales que pedí, ${PLAYER}?'","Los cueros extraordinarios hervidos pueden ser preparados por los guardabosques de la Tierra Media.\
\
Hasta quiere que le lleves veinte cueros extraordinarios hervidos.","Lleva los cueros a Hasta","Hasta pide que quienes estén dispuestos a ayudarle reúnan los diversos ingredientes necesarios para atraer a la amenaza que se oculta bajo las Obras Hidráulicas.","'Me alegra mucho contar con tu ayuda en este asunto, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Parte de nuestro señuelo requerirá una buena cantidad de pieles que actúen como la cubierta de nuestro falso \\qpez.\\q Tráeme veinte cueros extraordinarios hervidos y los añadiré a nuestra colección.'","'¡Bien hecho, ${PLAYER}! Aprecio enormemente tu contribución.\
\
'Vuelve a hablar conmigo si tienes más ingredientes que añadir al conjunto.'","Cebando a la Bestia: Envoltorio de Regalo"},
[1525]={"Lleva el acero de Khazâd a Hasta","'¿Has reunido los materiales que pedí, ${PLAYER}?'","Lingote de acero de Khazâd obtenido (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Los lingotes de acero de Khazâd pueden ser elaborados por los Prospeccionistas de toda la Tierra Media.\
\
Hasta quiere que le lleves cinco lingotes de acero de Khazâd.","'Me alegra mucho contar con tu ayuda en este asunto, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Parte de nuestro señuelo requerirá un metal resistente que pueda moldearse en anzuelos y cable. Tráeme diez lingotes de acero de Khazâd y los añadiré a nuestra colección.'","Cebando a la Bestia: Enganchado","Hasta pide que quienes estén dispuestos a ayudarle reúnan los diversos ingredientes necesarios para atraer a la amenaza que se oculta bajo las Obras Hidráulicas.","'¡Bien hecho, ${PLAYER}! Aprecio enormemente tu contribución.\
\
'Vuelve a hablar conmigo si tienes más ingredientes que añadir al conjunto.'","Lleva el acero de Khazâd a Hasta (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[1526]={"'¿Has reunido los materiales que pedí, ${PLAYER}?'","Cebando a la Bestia: Caliente como el Fuego","Aceite ígneo puro recogido para Hasta (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Recoge aceite ígneo puro para Hasta (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","El aceite ígneo puro puede ser preparado por Eruditos en toda la Tierra Media.\
\
Hasta quiere que le lleves veinte contenedores de aceite ígneo.","Hasta pide que quienes estén dispuestos a ayudarle reúnan los diversos ingredientes necesarios para atraer a la amenaza que se oculta bajo las Obras Hidráulicas.","Lleva el aceite ígneo puro a Hasta","'Me alegra mucho contar con tu ayuda en este asunto, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Atraer a nuestra presa a campo abierto es uno de mis objetivos, pero el otro, naturalmente, es someter a la bestia. El propósito de un señuelo como este es ser devorado, por lo que me gustaría añadir un veneno a nuestro cebo.\
\
'Los eruditos pueden producir una mezcla volátil muy apreciada por los cazadores: aceite ígneo puro. Tráeme veinte contenedores de este aceite inflamable y lo añadiré al resto de los materiales.'","'¡Bien hecho, ${PLAYER}! Aprecio enormemente tu contribución.\
\
'Vuelve a hablar conmigo si tienes más ingredientes que añadir al conjunto.'"},
[1527]={"Espinoso de tres púas obtenido (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¿Has reunido los materiales que pedí, ${PLAYER}?'","Puedes pescar espinosos de tres púas en las Obras Hidráulicas.\
\
Hasta quiere que le lleves cinco espinosos de tres púas.","'Me alegra mucho contar con tu ayuda en este asunto, ${PLAYER}. Para darle a nuestro señuelo la textura adecuada, necesitaremos un alimento similar al que nuestra presa consume normalmente.\
\
'Las criaturas que investigamos antes parecen alimentarse de un pez peculiar que solo se encuentra aquí, en las Obras Hidráulicas: el espinoso de tres púas.\
\
'Si eres alguien experimentado, podrás usar tus habilidades para capturar estos peces raros. Tráeme una cantidad razonable y lo añadiré a nuestra colección.'","Cebando a la Bestia: Dándole Carne al Hueso","Lleva los peces a Hasta","Hasta pide que quienes estén dispuestos a ayudarle reúnan los diversos ingredientes necesarios para atraer a la amenaza que se oculta bajo las Obras Hidráulicas.","Lleva espinosos de tres púas a Hasta (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¡Bien hecho, ${PLAYER}! Aprecio enormemente tu contribución.\
\
'Vuelve a hablar conmigo si tienes más ingredientes que añadir al conjunto.'"},
[1528]={"Puedes encontrar a Hasta en la Bodega Putrefacta, en las Obras Hidráulicas de Moria.\
\
Hasta quiere que le traigas diez frascos de salsa de menta y diez porciones de puré de papas reales.","'¿Has reunido los materiales que pedí, ${PLAYER}?'","Has obtenido un frasco de salsa de menta (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Me alegra mucho que hayas decidido ayudarme con esta tarea, ${PLAYER}. Estos ingredientes serían difíciles de reunir para una sola persona.\
\
'Aunque los demás materiales crearán la apariencia necesaria para engañar a nuestra presa, el sabor de nuestro señuelo requerirá una mezcla especial de hierbas y especias.\
\
'Tráeme lo siguiente y lo pondré junto al resto de los materiales:\
\
'Diez frascos de salsa de menta.\
'Diez porciones de puré de papas reales.'","Has obtenido una porción de puré de papas reales (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Hasta pide que quienes estén dispuestos a ayudarle reúnan los diversos ingredientes necesarios para atraer a la amenaza que se oculta bajo las Obras Hidráulicas.","Lleva el puré de papas reales a Hasta (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Lleva los objetos a Hasta","Lleva los frascos de salsa de menta a Hasta (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Cebando a la Bestia: El Sabor de la Vida","'¡Muy bien hecho, ${PLAYER}! Aprecio enormemente tu contribución. Asegúrate de volver a hablar conmigo si tienes más ingredientes para añadir a la mezcla.'"},
[1529]={"'Fish are part of everyone's diet in this area. We all eat fish, however, not all fish are eaten. There are many varieties that have their own distinct flavours and textures.\
\
'My favourite is also one of the most difficult to catch. Like me, it has a selective appetite and will only bite if there is specific bait on the hook.\
\
'Find the bait in Calembel, use it and apply it to your hook. It won't last long, so be quick about getting to the water and seeing if you can catch any.'","Torchuil is in Dol Amroth.\
\
Torchuil will be pleased to see the fish you caught.","'These delicacies will sell well on the market.'","Calembel Carp can be caught at Calembel to the north-east of Dol Amroth.\
\
Torchuil asked you to go to Calembel, gather some bait and catch some special fish.","Use worms to catch Calembel Carp (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Baiting the Hook","You have baited your pole, time to fish!","Caught Calembel Carp (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Calembel Carp are a delicacy in this area. However, they can only be caught when using a special type of bait, which must be found."},
[1530]={"Has conseguido atraer a muchas de las presas hacia las trampas vacías que los Pueblos Libres han colocado en el Bosque Salvaje. Sin duda, tus esfuerzos serán recompensados.","Coloca cebo en trampas vacías (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Alguien ha puesto una tarea para colocar cebos en trampas vacías destinadas a la captura de caza menor.","Consigue cebo","Coloca cebo en trampas vacías","Cebo conseguido","El anuncio del tablón dice:\
\
'Se necesitan: trampas vacías llenas de cebo en el Bosque Salvaje para capturar caza menor. Coge el cebo de la caja que hay cerca. Se te recompensará por tu esfuerzo.'","Completado","El cebo se encuentra en un cofre cercano.\
\
Deberías recoger el cebo.","Cebo colocado en trampas vacías (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","En el Bosque Salvaje se pueden encontrar trampas vacías.\
\
Deberías poner cebo en las trampas vacías.","Cebo en las trampas"},
[1531]={"Healing herbs are in short supply in Wildermore with the snows settling in, and you have been asked to search the Balewood for any surviving plants whose seeds may be used.","Ealswith is in Forlaw.\
\
You should return to Ealswith.","Balewood: A Strong Resemblance","<rgb=#FF0000>Completing Wildermore's Recovery will cancel this quest.</rgb>","Plants that might be used for healing purposes can likely be found throughout the south-eastern edge of the Balewood.\
\
You should search the south-eastern Balewood for promising plants.","Collect promising-looking plants (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I've heard many folk complaining about our dwindling supplies of healing herbs and plants, what with the snows settled in. The only place folk haven't scoured is the Balewood, where our people don't go.\
\
'Will you search for any plants that resemble healing herbs you've seen on your travels? If you can bring them back intact, they shall be used to grow more.\
\
'I would begin searching in the south-eastern Balewood.'","Regresa con Ealswith","'You have gathered some promising-looking plants to bolster the stores of the healers of Forlaw. The seeds of these should be able to support a new crop of herbs.'","Collected a promising plant (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[1532]={"The forces of Isengard can be found in the Balewood.\
\
You should ride to the Balewood and defeat the enemies of Wildermore.","Defeat enemies in the Balewood (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Has derrotado a un enemigo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Núrzum is dead, but the enemy still roams free throughout much of Wildermore.","Ealswith is in Forlaw.\
\
You should return to Ealswith.","<rgb=#FF0000>Completing Wildermore's Recovery will cancel this quest.</rgb>","'Hail, ${PLAYER}! Your valour drove back Núrzum, but the forces of Isengard do not seem to care that their leader has fallen. They continue to swarm our lands in great numbers.\
\
'The enemy is especially strong in the Balewood today. Go there, and show them that Wildermore will endure!'","Balewood: Driving Back the Enemy","Regresa con Ealswith","'Well done! You have driven back the enemies of Wildermore for the day.'"},
[1533]={"Balhest derrotado","Balhest, señor de Ost Elendil","Balhest, uno de los tenientes Númenóreanos negros más fuertes de Amarthiel, está en Ost Elendil.\
\
Legrindavor te ha pedido que pongas fin a Balhest para que Ost Elendil pueda ser reclamada.","Ost Elendil, más allá del puente de Ariant, fue una vez el hogar de los reyes de Annúminas. Ya no es así... tras permanecer abandonado durante un periodo de años terriblemente largo, ahora está ocupado por el mal que llegó desde Angmar.\
\
De los tenientes de Amarthiel, el Númenóreano negro llamado Balhest es sin duda el más cruel. Él es quien ocupa Ost Elendil y lo defiende de nosotros con un ejército de espíritus malvados y Angmarim que le han jurado lealtad.\
\
Balhest debe ser derrotado para que podamos retomar la ciudad, ${PLAYER}. Si es posible, debemos intentarlo. Los Dúnedain no podemos luchar contra este enemigo solos. Si no estoy aquí cuando vuelvas, lleva estas noticias al capitán general Daerdan en Echad Garthadir. ¡Le complacerá escuchar que has tenido éxito!","Derrota a Balhest"},
[1534]={"Balin, hijo de Fundin, llegó a Moria hace años y probablemente acampó cerca de la Sala Vigesimoprimera.","El orgullo de Balin","En el campamento de Balin en Nud-melek se pueden encontrar insectos y otros enemigos.\
\
Deberás eliminar las criaturas enemigas del campamento de Balin.","Criatura derrotada (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Completado","El campamento de Balin se encuentra al oeste del Cruce Profundo, al norte de Khurjezer, que se encuentra al este de la Sala Vigesimoprimera.\
\
Busca en el campamento de Balin reliquias de la expedición y examina minuciosamente los restos del campamento.","Has descubierto un campamento que una vez estuvo habitado por Balin, hijo de Fundin, cuando lideró su propia expedición a Moria.\
\
Está completamente infestado de alimañas, pero quizás haya artefactos por descubrir que se encuentren cerca.","Has limpiado el campamento de Balin de la peor parte de su infestación, y ahora puedes investigar para encontrar reliquias u otros objetos de interés.","Elimina las plagas del campamento de Balin","Elimina las criaturas del campamento de Balin (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[1535]={"Huargos blancos derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Ballard Wilmer y el huargo blanco","'¿Ya te has encontrado con los temibles huargos blancos de Tyrn Fornech, ${PLAYER}? ¡Esas criaturas son bestias despiadadas y sedientas de sangre, y atacan sin previo aviso! Hace unas noches, estaba tomando el aire alrededor del muro norte de Ost Forod, y me pareció ver algo brillando a la luz de la luna. Caminé hacia allí... qué imprudencia, lo sé, pero tenía curiosidad por saber qué podría ser. Al poco tiempo, me había adentrado bajo la espesura del bosque y me había desorientado bastante.\
\
'¡De repente, oí un gruñido a mi izquierda! Al girarme hacia el sonido, solo vi un destello de pelaje blanco brillante, apelmazado con sangre y barro. ¡Corrí, y la gran bestia me persiguió! Saltó hacia mí con un gran brinco; ¡sentí su aliento caliente humeando en el aire fresco de la noche! Y entonces... ¡luces! ¡Luces de Ost Forod! Basilio Resinas había venido a las afueras con un grupo y con faroles y, al verlos, ¡el huargo abandonó su persecución!\
\
'Esas bestias son peligrosas, ${PLAYER}, y hay que hacer algo. No todo el mundo tendrá el beneficio de un encuentro fortuito con nuestro árbitro, ya sabes. Si te ves capaz, te pediría que derrotes a algunos de los feroces huargos blancos. Los encontrarás por todo Tyrn Fornech, pero especialmente en la Hendidura del Ocaso, al norte de Ost Forod.'","'¡Encuentra y derrota a los huargos blancos de Tyrn Fornech, ${PLAYER}! Los encontrarás por todas las colinas, ¡pero especialmente cerca de la Hendidura del Ocaso, al norte de Ost Forod!'","'Me da miedo salir de las murallas después del anochecer debido a esos huargos blancos.'","Los huargos blancos acechan las colinas de Tyrn Fornech, pero se pueden encontrar especialmente en las cercanías de la Hendidura del Ocaso, al norte de Ost Forod.\
\
Ballard Wilmer te habló de su angustioso encuentro con un huargo y te ha pedido que derrotes a algunos de los feroces huargos blancos de Tyrn Fornech.","Ballard Wilmer tuvo un encuentro con huargos blancos en las colinas de Tyrn Fornech y ahora tiene un miedo mortal a esas criaturas.","'¡Ese día del que hablamos se acerca, ${PLAYER}!'","Ballard Wilmer está en el antiguo puesto de vigilancia de Ost Forod, en las colinas de Tyrn Fornech, al sur de la Hendidura del Ocaso.\
\
Has derrotado a muchos huargos blancos y ahora deberías informar de tu victoria a Ballard Wilmer.","'Has sobrevivido a tus encuentros con los huargos blancos, ${PLAYER}, me alegra mucho verlo... ¡buen trabajo! ¡Algún día, tal vez, un viajero podrá caminar por estas tierras sin temor al peligro!\
\
'Algún día, tal vez. Por ahora, te daré esta recompensa y espero que ese día llegue más pronto que tarde.'","Derrota huargos blancos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[1537]={"'¿Tienes las hojas? Necesitaré unos cuantos montones de hojas para hacer la solución para los vendajes de Callum. Crecen en arbustos al sureste de Bolgovado, cerca del agua.'","'Debería haber muchas matas de retama al sureste de Bolgovado, cerca del agua. Reúne algunas hojas de ellas, para que pueda hacer el ungüento que necesito para los vendajes de Callum.'","Vendajes recogidos","'Por favor, lleva esos vendajes a Callum. ¡Espero que le ayuden a sanar, y quizás él pierda su malicia hacia mí! Su campamento está al oeste de aquí, cerca del extremo occidental del Pantano de la Rana.'","Vendajes para Callum","Hojas de retama recogidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","El campamento de Callum está en el extremo oeste del Pantano de la Rana, al oeste de Bolgovado.\
\
Con las hojas de retama que recogiste, Wilimar pudo preparar un ungüento en el que empapar los vendajes. Además de darle los vendajes a Callum, Wilimar te ha pedido que le digas a Callum que no le guarda rencor y espera que él haga lo mismo.","Llevar hojas de retama a Wilimar Bolger","'¿Entonces Callum me dejará en paz? ¡Ah, qué alivio!'","'Puede que no acepte caridad de mí, su \"enemigo jurado\", pero creo que debería intentar ayudar a Callum de todos modos.\
\
'Esta herida suya, causada por el jabalí, seguramente necesita ser vendada. Para evitar infecciones y ayudar a que sane, deberíamos empapar los vendajes en un ungüento de... veamos, ¿qué sería lo mejor?\
\
'Retama, creo. Ya tengo los vendajes, pero no tengo las hojas de retama. ¿Podrías ayudarme una vez más y recoger algunas hojas de retama de los arbustos al sureste de Bolgovado, cerca del agua?'","'¿Por qué me molestas? ¡Déjame morir en paz!'","La retama crece junto al agua, al sureste de Bolgovado.\
\
Wilimar ha decidido proporcionar vendajes a Callum para su herida, pero para ayudar en su curación, quiere empapar los vendajes en un ungüento hecho de hojas de retama. Te ha pedido que recojas estas hojas para él.","Recolectar vendajes","Wilimar Bolger se encuentra cerca de su agujero, al noroeste de Bolgovado.\
\
Wilimar ha decidido proporcionar vendajes a Callum para su herida, pero para ayudar en su curación, quiere empapar los vendajes en un ungüento hecho de hojas de retama. Te ha pedido que recojas estas hojas para él.","Al seguir leyendo el diario, Wilimar ha comenzado a sentir simpatía por Callum, el montañés que juró matarlo. Al conocer la dura vida de Callum en un reino lejano del norte, ha decidido ayudarlo y curar la herida que sufrió por el jabalí salvaje.","'¡Tenía tanto miedo por mi vida! Gracias por tu ayuda, ${PLAYERNAME:Frontero[m]|Frontera[f]}.'","Recolectar hojas de retama (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¿Vendajes? ¿Del hombrecito? Yo... ¿y esto no es una traición de algún tipo? Yo... no estoy seguro de qué decir. He odiado esta marca contra mi familia durante tanto tiempo, pensé que finalmente se borraría si el hombrecito estaba muerto... pero estas no son las acciones de un enemigo....\
\
'¿Debería dirigir mi ira contra aquellos que forzaron a mi ancestro a la batalla? ¿O debería culpar al destino y dejar mi ira atrás? Tengo mucho en qué pensar.\
\
'Gracias. Este Wilimar no tiene nada que temer de mí.'","Llevar vendajes a Callum","'Quizás el honor de Wilimar borrará la marca de deshonra de mi familia. Solo el tiempo lo dirá.'","'No estoy acostumbrado a la misericordia de un enemigo. Quizás he malinterpretado a estas pequeñas personas.'","'¡Ah, tienes las hojas! Por favor, dámelas. Esto solo tomará un momento...\
\
'Por favor, lleva estos vendajes al campamento de Callum, en el extremo oeste del Pantano de la Rana. Dile que debe cambiar los vendajes a diario. Hay suficientes para siete días. Espero que sea suficiente para ayudarle a sanar.\
\
'También, hazle saber que no le guardo rencor... y pídele que haga lo mismo por mí!'"},
[1538]={"You defeated Iarvael","'There is a deadly creature laired just beyond the outskirts of Carn Dûm - a morroval named Iarvael who has learned of the existence of the Council of the North, and has begun to hunt down their forces one by one as they risk their lives to delay the growth of Angmar's power. She must be stopped, ${PLAYER}!\
\
'Gather your most stalwart allies and hunt her down before she should discover the hidden refuge of the Council.'","Defeat Iarvael","Bane of the Council","You must hunt down and defeat Iarvael, who is laired in the hills north of Bail Dílas.","'I have received a missive from the Wardens telling me of your heroic efforts in support of their cause, I thank you for taking such risks on their behalf and ours.'","Tell Handarod in Esteldín of your victory in Angmar.","The dread morroval Iarvael has been hunting down the Council of the North. You must gather your allies and destroy her before she discovers their refuge. Her lair lies somewhere to the north of Bail Dílas in Angmar."},
[1539]={"King Thranduil can be found in Felegoth.\
\
You have defeated Iphantemel and forever banished her blight from Eryn Lasgalen. You should talk to King Thranduil.","'The time has come! We must put an end to Iphantemel!'","Talk to King Thranduil","Bane of the Elvenking","'You have done well to aid me and my kin, ${PLAYER}. While a few of Iphantemel's children may linger in the forest, the last great evil of Mirkwood is no more.\
\
'As for the matter of Karazgar, I believe he has returned to seek something within Caras Tilion. I will not send you there - not yet, for this is a matter of great import to me and me alone.\
\
'I shall search the ruins myself, and when I have need of you again, I will call upon you.'\
\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Next week: 'Karazgar's Gambit'</rgb>","Despite uncovering evidence that Karazgar may still lurk in Eryn Lasgalen, King Thranduil has turned his attention to his hated foe of old: Iphantemel.","King Thranduil can be found in Felegoth.\
\
King Thranduil has asked you to accompany him and his warriors to Torech Emel in an effort to put an end to the blight of Iphantemel.","'It has been mere days, ${PLAYER}, but I have learned much of things that were beyond our sight. My scouts have travelled much of Eryn Lasgalen and they have discovered far more than what we sought.\
\
'It seems the Old Mother, Iphantemel, has become trapped in Torech Emel by the excess of her own appetite. It was she that bound Caras Tilion and blighted Mirkwood before Sauron hid within Dol Guldur. It was she who wounded me in that failed battle of old!\
\
'Do not think I have forgotten your purpose in coming here. I have great reason to suspect that the Weeping Warrior remains in my realm, but that matter must be set aside for the moment. If I have guessed Karazgar's true purpose in returning to Eryn Lasgalen, he will not find what he seeks. Indeed, there shall be time enough to find him when this task is done.\
\
'Iphantemel must be brought low and her blight forever banished from Eryn Lasgalen!'"},
[1540]={"Bane of the Serpent","Defeated Rujateng","Complete Quest: The Eyes and The Blind","Complete Quest: Dwindling Rations","Gladhir has asked you to stop the Haradrim camped in the hills from discovering Haerondir and threatening the Host of the West.","Return to Gladhir","'${PLAYER}, it is good to have you here with us on the doorstep of the Enemy. After you left Osgiliath, the other Rangers and I had little difficulty finding and defeating the last Orcs hiding amongst the city ruins.\
\
'Now then, to the matter at hand. As you may have heard, the Enemy does not venture into the ruins of Haerondir, for they believe it haunted. In truth, this is not the case. It is an appearance we keep up so that we may occupy this most northern look-out for Gondor undisturbed.\
\
'Not long ago, Haradrim set up camp just over the western hills. We have noticed their patrols widen as each day passes. While we have been able to trick the Orcs for many years, I fear the Haradrim are shrewder foes.\
\
'We must stop this camp from spreading and uncovering the truth about Haerondir. Would you take on this task while we guard the western gate from assault?'","Complete Quest: Beneath the Snake","'With all you have done for us, both past and present, no reward could suffice. I am glad to have you as a trusted ally, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'I believe the Haradrim will no longer pose a threat to Haerondir. From what our look-out, Dornach, was able to surmise, their numbers should not be able to fully organize until well after the Host of the West passes their camp.\
\
'We need not fear any ambush from that direction, at least, thanks to you.'","Enter Dûm Boha","You should find the Haradrim encampment of Dûm Boha, located on the western slopes of the Slag-hills.","You should return to Gladhir, who can be found at Haerondir.","There is much to be done to impede the Haradrim here","You should find and defeat Rujateng at Dûm Boha.","Complete Quest: The Poisoned Mind","Defeat Rujateng"},
[1541]={"Destruye las catapultas de Moria (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Las máquinas de asedio y catapultas de Moria se encuentran en Drû-garmadh, al sureste de Mekhem-bizru.\
\
Alrekur teme las armas de asedio que se están construyendo en Drû-garmadh y quiere que destruyas varias máquinas de asedio y catapultas.","Catapultas de Moria destruidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Azote del Bosque","Habla con Alrekur en Mekhem-bizru","'Así, las grandes armas de guerra han sido reducidas a pedazos. Esta es una buena noticia, ${PLAYER}, pero hasta que el constructor responsable de ellas sea derrotado, solo habrá más que destruir mañana.'","Los orcos en Drû-garmadh han comenzado a construir máquinas de asedio y catapultas con las que guerrear contra los enanos de Khazad-dûm y los elfos del Bosque de Oro.","Máquinas de asedio de Moria destruidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Las armas de asedio que viste en Drû-garmadh me preocupan mucho. No creo que los orcos puedan usarlas eficazmente en Khazad-dûm, pero con ellas podrían dominar el Valle del Arroyo Sombrío y posiblemente amenazar las afueras de Lothlórien, aunque parece haber algún poder dentro del Bosque que los desafía.\
\
'Vente de nuevo a Drû-garmadh, al sureste de aquí, y destruye las máquinas de asedio y catapultas de Moria. Es vital para nuestra capacidad de mantener el Valle del Arroyo Sombrío como una ubicación estratégica.'","Alrekur se encuentra en Mekhem-bizru, al noroeste de Drû-garmadh.\
\
Alrekur estará encantado de saber que las máquinas de asedio y catapultas de Moria construidas en Drû-garmadh han sido destruidas.","'¡Esas máquinas de asedio deben ser destruidas, por la seguridad de todos!'","Destruye las máquinas de asedio de Moria (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[1542]={"Los espíritus malvados se encuentran en Imlad Balchorth, al oeste de Myrkworth.\
\
Sigar te ha pedido que destruyas a los espíritus malvados de Imlad Balchorth. Pueden encontrarse vagando por Imlad Balchorth.","'Los espíritus malvados de Morgoth moran en Imlad Balchorth... temo que nunca podremos escapar de este lugar a menos que los expulsemos.'","'Has aliviado mi carga y me has ayudado a dormir mejor por las noches, o eso espero. Gracias, ${PLAYER}. ¡Espero trabajar contigo de nuevo!'","Espíritus malvados derrotados en Imlad Balchorth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Derrota a los espíritus malvados en Imlad Balchorth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","A pesar del número de espíritus malvados que has expulsado de Imlad Balchorth, nunca parecen terminarse.","Expulsar a los espíritus","Sigar está en Myrkworth, al este de Imlad Balchorth.\
\
Tras destruir a los espíritus malvados como se te pidió, deberías volver a ver a Sigar en Myrkworth y contarle la tarea ha sido completada.","'Los tiempos son difíciles aquí en Angmar. Echo de menos el calor de mi hogar. ¡Cuanto antes detengamos a los Angmarim, antes podremos irnos de este maldito lugar! Necesito que me ayudes como a los demás.\
\
'Hay muchos espíritus malvados en Imlad Balchorth, que dan lugar a más espectros para el ejército de Angmar. Debemos diezmar sus filas. ¡Me da escalofríos solo pensar en ellos!\
\
'Si podemos reducir su número, quizá podamos volver a nuestros acogedores hogares más rápido.'"},
[1543]={"Banishing Nightmares","'You didn't see anything strange? But what if...\
\
'No... you're telling the truth, right? All right. All right, I believe you. I'm coming out now.'","You have found a place to \\qscout\\q for Candron","Plagued by bad dreams and memories, a young boy has barricaded himself from the outside world.","Go to the top of the stairs near the Minardil statue","Candron has asked you to \\qscout\\q three places in East Pelargir.\
\
He mentioned the district with the destroyed Castamir monument, the top of the stairs near the Minardil statue, and the courtyard of Lord Sirgon's manor.","\\qScouted\\q places (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","You have \\qscouted\\q all three places in East Pelargir.\
\
You should return to Heniawen in East Pelargir and talk to Candron through the door of their home.","'Candron, please come out. It's safe. Nobody will hurt you, and I won't let that happen.'\
\
Upon hearing your footsteps, the girl turns away from the door to face you.\
\
'Oh! Um, hello, could you help me? My little brother's barricaded himself into our home. He's been having lots of bad dreams since the war, and he hasn't gotten better.\
\
'He won't listen to me, but maybe he'll listen to a grown-up like you.'","Talk to Heniawen","<rgb=#00ff00>Look</rgb> at the top of the stairs near the Minardil statue","<rgb=#00ff00>Look</rgb> in the courtyard of Lord Sirgon's manor","<rgb=#00ff00>Look</rgb> in the district with the destroyed Castamir monument","Heniawen has asked you to reassure Candron that there is no danger in Pelargir.\
\
You should talk to him through the door.","You have helped Candron find the courage to leave the house.\
\
You should talk to Heniawen in East Pelargir.","Candron warily emerges from the house, but relaxes upon seeing Heniawen","'Thank you! The next time Candron has bad dreams, I'll help him the same way you did. Maybe he'll feel safe in the city again soon.'","Go to the district with the destroyed Castamir monument","'But what if the Corsairs and the angry people come back and the guards don't know?'\
\
The boy pauses -- perhaps taking a moment to collect himself.\
\
'You can fight, can't you? Could you help me check if it's really safe outside?\
\
'If you go... east, I think, you'll see a broken statue. I -- I remember lots of angry people being there during the war. And at the city gates, there's a really tall statue. I bet you'll see anyone who's hiding if you go up to the top of the stairs there. And if you go... west, there's Lord Sirgon's home. You should make sure it's safe outside his home too.'","Talk to Candron through the door","Go to the courtyard of Lord Sirgon's manor"},
[1544]={"Los nigromantes de Imlad Balchorth se encuentran en las ruinas situadas en lo alto de las colinas del sur.\
\
El hechicero jefe de los nigromantes, el Maestro de los Espíritus, sin duda controla a Deluches, el capitán de los espíritus. Gautar te ha pedido que lo derrotes y así destierres a Deluches para siempre.","'Has deshecho los planes de los nigromantes de Angmar. ¡Bien hecho!'","'Has hecho un trabajo muy bueno. Deluches era evidentemente la clave del control de los nigromantes sobre esos espíritus. Es solo desafortunado que aquellos que han sido desterrados sean solo una pequeña parte de las fuerzas de Angmar.'","Gautar se encuentra en Valleoscuro, al este y un poco al norte de Eithel Úmfaer.\
\
Has derrotado a Deluches y desterrado al menos algunos de los espíritus crueles de Angmar. Deberías llevar estas buenas noticias a Gautar.","La aparición repentina de Deluches, el capitán de los espíritus crueles, te impidió desterrar a las criaturas del santuario.","'Esto me hace pensar que el espíritu al que has combatido es después de todo una criatura del mismo tipo que aquellos a los que buscamos desterrar. No debe estar controlado por el santuario, o no habría podido huir de ti tan fácilmente cuando estaba a punto de ser derrotado.\
\
'Mi suposición es que otro controla a Deluches. Los necromantes de Imlad Balchorth se esconden en una ruina en lo alto de las colinas al sur del área. Es bastante posible que uno de ellos sea el protector de Deluches mismo. Sospecho también que encontrarás un segundo santuario en su guarida. Fui un tonto por pensar que solo tenían uno.\
\
'Encuentra este santuario principal. No hay duda de que volverás a encontrarte con tu enemigo, y tal vez incluso con el jefe de los necromantes, pero esta vez si eres victorioso, su derrota será definitiva... espero'","Eithel Úmfaer se encuentra en el sur de Imlad Balchorth, al oeste de Valleoscuro.\
\
Deluches, el capitán de los espíritus crueles, ha sido convocado a Eithel Úmfaer, el santuario principal de Imlad Balchorth, donde debe ser destruido.","'Deluches ya ha escapado una vez... ¡no debe volver a hacerlo!'","Desterrando la oscuridad"},
[1545]={"Bagmund is at Aculf's camp in the Rushgore, north-west of Atburg.\
\
Eowils told you to return to Bagmund and let him know that you have dealt with Brúngwath.","Brúngwath is at Atburg, south-east of Aculf's camp in the Rushgore.\
\
Bagmund has asked you to drive Brúngwath from the Rushgore, in hopes that the shades will not return.","'You who should have shown my kindred compassion have shown them hatred instead.\
\
'You are hereafter my enemy!'","Defeated Brúngwath at Atburg","Talk to Bagmund at Aculf's camp in the Rushgore","Eowils knows that Bagmund will be pleased by your decision to help drive the shades from the Rushgore, but is concerned that they will return as long as their leader remains at Atburg.","'You have made the right decision, ${PLAYER}. These Oathbreakers are an abomination to the living and must be driven from this place. We might not be able to remove them from the haunted battlefield of old, but this place, at least, should be free of them.\
\
'However, they may be more likely to return if this Brúngwath does not return himself to Parth Celebrant. Perhaps you would be willing to show him that he and his kind are not welcome here?\
\
'When you have completed this deed, return to Bagmund...he will be pleased by your decision.'","Banishing the Dishonoured","'You are worthless! Can you do nothing right? Now the accursed Oathbreakers are angrier than ever!\
\
'Leave me, you dolt, and take this with you!'","Defeat Brúngwath at Atburg"},
[1546]={"'Seek out and defeat the fell spirit Umhen and his minions. They can be found in and around the small island  at the centre of the Bleakmere.'","Umhen's isle lies to the south of Barad Angol, at the centre of the Bleakmere.\
\
Faerchiril has asked you to seek out and defeat the fell spirit Umhen and his minions.","'With Umhen and his servants banished from the Bleakmere, the fell spirits of Morgoth should not trouble us too greatly.\
\
'The Malledhrim are grateful for your assistance, ${PLAYER}.'","Faerchiril is at Barad Angol due north of Umhen's isle, up the mountain.\
  \
You should return to Faerchiril and let her know that Umhen and his minions have been defeated.","Defeat Umhen","'The foul sorcery of Sâd Doldúr has attracted many fell spirits of Morgoth into the Ashenslades. Among them is a singularly evil creature known as Umhen. This spirit summons all others to a small isle at the centre of the Bleakmere, though we know not for what nefarious purpose. \
\
'These spirits do not belong in Middle-earth and can only mean ill for the Malledhrim. I would ask you to seek out Umhen and his minions and banish them back beyond the Void.\
\
'Umhen's isle can be found by travelling south down the mountain, past Sâd Doldúr, at the centre of the Bleakmere.'","At the centre of the Bleakmere, there lies a small isle, upon which a fell spirit named Umhen has gathered his foul minions.","Derrota a los espíritus malvados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Faerchiril","Defeated Umhen","Espíritus malignos derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Banishing the Shadows"},
[1547]={"Replace banners of Umbar with banners of Gondor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Raised a banner of Dol Amroth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You have littered Hashadîr with the flags of Gondor, which will do much to dishearten the Corsairs who have begun to raid these southern lands.","Banners of Umbar","Banners of Umbar fly in Hashadîr, the Corsair camp south-west of Dol Amroth in Belfalas.\
\
You should replace the Corsairs' banners with Gondorian ones.","The Corsairs boldly fly their colours in Hashadîr, the encampment near Dol Amroth. \
\
You should replace their banners with Gondorian colours, for this land has not yet been claimed for Umbar.","Completado","The Corsairs boldly fly their colours in Hashadîr, the encampment near Dol Amroth."},
[1548]={"Enter the field","You have struck the west banner's shield","You have struck the south banner's shield","Hit the east banner's shield","The four farms are spread out to the north, east, and west of the rock.\
\
Gladsnel asked you to throw a spear through four shields on Orc-banners.","You have struck the east banner's shield","Hit all of the shields rapidly","Gladsnel is in Cliving.\
\
Gladsnel will be pleased to hear that a spear was thrown through each of the four shields.","'While we cannot strike directly at the Orcs, we can continue to damage their morale.'","'It saddens me to see what has become of the Norcrofts. The farms where we once proudly grew our food are now overrun by Orcs and foul creatures, yet we are told to stay within the gates of the city and to not engage them.\
\
'The Enemy has placed shields on banners at four farms just to the south of here. While I cannot ask you to defeat the Orcs, we are not disallowed from defiling their flags. There is a rock south of Cliving. Just north of that rock, the four farms are spread out.\
\
'Take this spear. When you get near the banner, ready it, then throw it with all of your might. Be warned: the faster you are moving, the more likely you are to miss the shield....but you must also be quick. The Orcs will replace the shields swiftly, and I wish them all to be ripped at once.'","Hit the north banner's shield","The rock is south of Cliving.\
\
Gladsnel asked you to throw a spear through several shields on Orc-banners planted at Norcrofts farms.","<rgb=#FF0000>Completing Aiding the Eastemnet will cancel this quest</rgb>","You have struck the north banner's shield","Hit the west banner's shield","Talk to Gladsnel","South of Cliving, several shields have been placed on banners of the Enemy planted around former farmhouses.","Banners of the Enemy","Hit the south banner's shield"},
[1549]={"Quema estandartes de la Corona de Hierro (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Estandartes de la Corona de Hierro","Las fuerzas de Angmar suelen usar estandartes que muestran la imagen de la Corona de Hierro para identificar sus campamentos.","Orchalwë quiere que quemes los estandartes de la Corona de Hierro en el patio.","'Los angmarim usan estos estandartes para marcar lo que han reclamado. La Corona de Hierro recuerda a todos que sirven al Rey Brujo de Angmar, sirviente del Señor Oscuro.\
\
'Incluso cuando las tropas no están presentes, esos estandartes son un vil recordatorio de su ocupación aquí. Enviémosles un mensaje claro reduciéndolos a cenizas. ¡Al menos por hoy, este patio será nuestro!'","'El olor a tela quemada no suele ser algo que uno espere con ansias, pero en este caso, huele tan bien como cualquier otra cosa que pueda recordar.'","Estandartes de la Corona de Hierro quemados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Habla con Orchalwë","Orchalwë querrá hablar sobre la quema de los estandartes."},
[1551]={"'¿Has derribado los estandartes de los semiorcos? Los dedos de la Mano Blanca se han alargado, pero no lo suficiente como para que tengamos que soportar la vista de sus símbolos en nuestra puerta.'","La Puerta del Cuerno Rojo se encuentra al noreste de Echad Dúnann.\
\
Rostoriel te ha pedido que retires los estandartes de los semiorcos de la Puerta del Cuerno Rojo.","Los semiorcos han colocado estandartes por toda la Puerta del Cuerno Rojo para proclamar su lealtad a Saruman el Blanco y reclamar esta zona como suya.","Habla con Rostoriel en Echad Dúnann","Estandartes recogidos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¡Has asestado un gran golpe a la Mano Blanca, ${PLAYER}!'","'Los semiorcos han osado ir mucho más lejos de lo que pensábamos, incluso hasta la Puerta del Cuerno Rojo.\
\
'Aunque no dejaron rastro de su paso, no lo hicieron en secreto, ya que plantaron infames estandartes de la Mano Blanca en las laderas. Ve y quita estos estandartes. No debemos permitir que los semiorcos crean que pueden vagar libremente por esta tierra, que una vez perteneció a los Elfos.\
\
'Los estandartes de los semiorcos se pueden encontrar por toda la Puerta del Cuerno Rojo al noreste.'","'¿Has regresado con los estandartes, ${PLAYER}? Se pueden encontrar por toda la Puerta del Cuerno Rojo al noreste.'","Recoge los estandartes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Estandartes del Paso"},
[1552]={"The Elf-lady Maliriel has long organized the great banquets of Lothlórien, held for honoured guests and special occasions. The strains of unrest and war have distracted many from the preparations needed, and she has asked you to aid the Elves responsible for completing the preparations for an upcoming banquet.","'${PLAYER}, I am delighted! You have made all the preparations seem so much less arduous and allowed me to more fully devote my time and attention to the complicated ones. \
\
'Please accept this reward, and know that it comes with Maliriel's warmest regards.'","'${PLAYER}, you have considerably lightened my burdens! You have my gratitude.'","Galhíril can be found near the gate to Imlad Lalaith. Aesbrennil and Hadhelen can be found within the Vineyards of Lórien, south of Imlad Lalaith. Glasnír can be found at the entrance to the vineyards, south of Imlad Lalaith.\
\
Maliriel has asked you to help her and her companions to complete all the preparations for the upcoming feast.","Banquet Preparations","Talk to Maliriel at Imlad Lalaith","'We have many preparations for the feast... speak with my assistants and aid them as you may.'","Maliriel is at Imlad Lalaith.\
\
You should report to Maliriel that all the banquet preparations she asked you to finish are complete.","'Greetings, ${PLAYER}. You come at an auspicious time -- but one that finds me ill prepared for my duties. You see, I am the Mistress of the Feast for Lothlórien, and it falls to me to prepare a great banquet.\
\
'Yet I find myself with few hands to prepare such an event, for many have been called away to guard the borders of our forest or to sojourn further afield against the foes of the Elves.\
\
'So I ask you, if you will, to seek out my companions who labour here and to the south towards the vineyards, and offer them whatever aid you may in these preparations, for time grows short!'","Finish banquet preparations (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Finished banquet preparations (${CURRENT}/${MAX})"},
[1555]={"Defeat Uruk-hai (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Banám Lugaun: Orkish Might","Defeated Uruk-hai (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated Laugshat","Defeat Laugshat","An Orc camp sits between Minas Morgul and Cirith Ungol, and troops and supplies use it as they move through the treacherous terrain.","The Orc encampment of Banám Lugaun watches Minas Morgul from across the Morgulduin River. The encampment seems to be a waypoint of sorts, with Orcs coming and going: some to the city of Minas Morgul, others over the mountains towards Cirith Ungol. It is important that the Orcs at this encampment are dealt with, and swiftly.","Defeat many Orcs and Uruk-hai in Banám Lugaun.","Completado","Orcs and Uruk-hai can be found in Banám Lugaun in Rath Dúath.\
\
You should defeat Orcs and Uruk-hai in Banám Lugaun.","Has derrotado orcos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Derrota orcos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You have defeated many of those encamped at Banám Lugaun and learned from the camp's leader that the Orcs here rally under the banner of Ugrukhôr.","Defeat Orcs and Uruk-hai in Banám Lugaun"},
[1556]={"Campamento de Barachen","Habla con Barachen en su campamento en el Bosque de los Trolls","'¿Ya has hablado con Barachen? Tiene un campamento en el Bosque de los Trolls'","'¿Así que los Montaraces de Evendim te han enviado para ayudar?'","'A menudo mantenemos el contacto con los elfos de Rivendel. A uno de ellos, llamado Barachen, lo considero un amigo íntimo. Hace poco recibí una carta suya en la que me indicaba que se avecinaban problemas en el Bosque de los Trolls y que buscaba mi consejo. Me preocupo por él.\
\
'Tiene un pequeño campamento muy al este de aquí, en el Bosque de los Trolls, justo más allá del Último Puente desde las Tierras Solitarias. ¿Irias a verle para averiguar qué le preocupa?'","El campamento de Barachen se encuentra muy al este de Evendim, en el Bosque de los Trolls, justo al otro lado del Último Puente desde las Tierras Solitarias.\
\
Orchalwë te ha pedido que hables con su amigo Barachen.","Barachen tiene un pequeño campamento al este de Evendim, en el Bosque de los Trolls."},
[1557]={"Barad Guldur: Gruesome Relics and Tomes","These odd trinkets are sure to interest the Elves","The Malledhrim have asked you and your companions to enter Barad Guldur in an attempt to strike at the heart of the forces of Dol Guldur.","'Hail, mellon! I am glad to see that you have returned in one piece. Do tell of what you saw in the tower....'","These dusty shelves contain a book that will certainly be of interest to the Elves","Search amongst book-shelves","Anglú awaits you in Barad Guldur.\
\
You should hasten back to Anglú and tell him of your findings throughout the tower.","Search for any curious relics","'You must search for anything that will be informative to the Malledhrim. This will be of great use to us.'","The relics and tomes of the Necromancer can be found throughout Barad Guldur.\
\
You should keep an eye out for any useful clues or information that will aid the efforts of the Malledhrim as you ascend Barad Guldur.","Talk to Anglú in Barad Guldur","'Belvaer, the commander here, has given some instructions for you, ${PLAYER}. Further up this tower lie horrors of Mordor which yearn to smother the light of the world beyond these fell eaves, corrupting Middle-earth as they have corrupted Mirkwood.\
\
'If you are to march further, you do so in the face of great peril. If you feel able, you should scour this place for any clues or information that will be of use in our campaign against the Enemy, whether it be within these walls or abroad in the greater fight against the Enemy.\
\
'I wish you luck, ${CLASS}! Please bring your findings to me -- but this is not a path that you should walk alone. Bring many strong friends with you upon this venture.'","Search for notable objects","This foul tome will surely interest the Elves"},
[1558]={"The Malledhrim have asked you and your companions to enter Barad Guldur in an attempt to strike at the heart of the forces of Dol Guldur.","'Well met, ${PLAYER}! Your foray into this evil tower shall not be soon forgotten by the Elves who survive the offensive. We are indebted to you for breaching the lower defences of Barad Guldur.\
\
'From here I believe we can look to advancing further up the tower -- not a small feat, I assure you.\
\
'But for now, take a moment's respite.  You have earned it.'","You have broken through the forces in lower Barad Guldur","Anglú is in Barad Guldur.\
\
You should speak with the Elf-lieutenant Anglú for further instruction on your offensive.","Establish a staging point in Barad Guldur","Talk to Anglú in Barad Guldur","Barad Guldur is the mighty tower at the fortress of Dol Guldur.\
\
Once inside, Belvaer has asked you to sever the flow of enemy reinforcements streaming from the tower. Belvaer seems to think that the captain of the guard should be found soon after beginning your ascent of the tower.","Barad Guldur: The Deep Assault"},
[1565]={"Cleanse ash mounds (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat Darkwaters at Gaerlond (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You should report your success at Gaerlond to Garvir.\
\
Garvir can be found at Barad Rill.","Darkwaters defeated (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'It seems we cannot be rid of you that easily, ${PLAYER}, but I need your aid here again.'","Garvir has asked you to assist in the cleansing of Gaerlond to the north-east.\
\
Fell creatures have been sighted and are scaring the workers.","'Now that the war is over, I have been meaning to return here to see that the lighthouse be rebuilt.\
\
'It was vital in our efforts to rout Corsairs on approach. Dolgimil is no more.\
\
'We must reclaim this beacon once more so that it may once again serve the Bay of Belfalas, but work has halted. The workers are frightened. Rumours abound of unsightly apparitions in the ruins of Gaerlond, to the north-east.\
\
'They dare not resume their work until that place is cleansed. Would you aid me once more, ${PLAYER}?'","Garvir told you that Herion once again needs your help. You should talk to Herion at Parth Rest.\
\
Parth Rest can be found to the north.","The efforts to rebuild the lighthouse have been hindered by the hauntings at Gaerlond.\
\
Gaerlond can be found to the north-east.","Talk to Herion at Parth Rest","'It is good to have you back, ${PLAYER}!\
\
'Now that things have settled down at Gaerlond, there is no doubt the workers will return and resume the effort.\
\
'Thank you for aiding me.\
\
'I received word from Herion that he needs your help. You should return to Parth Rest and see what he has to say.'","Barad Rill Runs Dark","Ash mounds cleansed (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Garvir"},
[1566]={"Bring the ancient tomes to Candúr","'These rare texts should be studied by the Lore-masters of Minas Tirith. I will give these tomes to Isnír for study.'","Collect ancient tomes","A wealth of lore awaits those who brave the Bones of Barad-dûr.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Warning: This quest requires Barad-dûr: Realm of the Black Word to be underway. If that quest has been completed or failed, you will be unable to exit and re-enter this instance in order to complete this quest.</rgb>","Bring the ancient tomes to Candúr.","Collect ancient tomes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collected ancient tomes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Barad-dûr: Lore of the Past","Collect ancient tomes."},
[1567]={"Defeat Kathanûl.","'You have slain one of the Black Word's knights? I praise you for your valiant efforts.'","You ran out of time...","Defeat Kathanûl","Talk to Candúr","You should return to Candúr and apprise him of your efforts.","'Careful now on your journeys.'","Defeated Kathanûl","A wealth of lore awaits those who brave the Bones of Barad-dûr.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Warning: This quest has a one hour time limit. The timer will begin upon accepting the quest.</rgb>","Barad-dûr: Realm of the Black Word","'Within the bones of Barad-dûr lie many secrets and strange objects collected by Sauron during his reign of Mordor. If we were to penetrate the ruined tower's defences, we may just yet be able to obtain some of these lost relics. Many I am sure rightfully belong to Gondor. I fear the Barad-dûr is still under command of those who serve the Black Word. Are you willing to risk a dive into the Sauron's ruins for Gondor?'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Warning: This quest has a one hour time limit. The timer will begin upon accepting the quest. This quest can be completed with one or two adventurers.</rgb>"},
[1568]={"'You have done well, friend. Your efforts will be duly noted!'","Defeat Black Númenóreans in Barad-dûr","Defeat Black Númenóreans in Barad-dûr (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","A wealth of lore awaits those who brave the Bones of Barad-dûr.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Warning: This quest requires Barad-dûr: Realm of the Black Word to be underway. If that quest has been completed or failed, you will be unable to exit and re-enter this instance in order to complete this quest.</rgb>","Talk to Candúr","Defeat Black Númenóreans in Barad-dûr.","Talk to Candúr.","Defeated Black Númenóreans (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Barad-dûr: Ruins of Darkness"},
[1569]={"You have safely returned to Nashûbu.\
\
You should talk to Numûru.","Numûru has asked you to assist him with investigating the city guard barracks.\
\
You should talk to Numûru and complete 'Instance: Barging into the Barracks'.","Complete 'Instance: Barging into the Barracks'","'Despite it being a trap, our mission was a great success! I will ensure all of the weapons in the armoury are... 'reallocated' to further our cause. Excellent work, ${PLAYER}.'","Barging into the Barracks","El cuartel de guardias de Emax Dûl aún puede albergar un almacén de armas valiosas.","Talk to Numûru","'We have located the city guards' barracks on the western side of Emax Dûl. Our scouts tell me it has become unusually quiet; the guards no longer seem to be coming and going. They have also spotted an Utûgi group in the area. We are unsure why, as they have mostly seemed stay near their stronghold on the other side of the city.\
\
'I would like to investigate the barracks, as we believe it is also the location of the city's armoury, but I sense something is amiss. The two of us will go alone, so as not to put anyone else at risk in the event that this is a trap. We will investigate the barracks, and return with any weapons we can find. We can surely use them to arm our growing rebellion!'","'Are you ready to go to the barracks? This may be a trap, so ensure you are well prepared.'"},
[1570]={"Retrieved stolen barrels from the river Blackroot (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I know you are duly familiar with the strange goings-on in the vale, ${PLAYER}...\
\
'However, something troubling has been happening around Sardol. I do not know if the others have noticed as I have, but some of our goods have disappeared. Perhaps they missed it in the wake of our troubles with the spiders, but these were taken, not destroyed.\
\
'You see, I found one of our barrels washed up on the shore of the Blackroot this morning. I believe someone seeks to send them south into Tarlang's Crown, but I do not know why. Would you aid me in recovering them?'","Retrieve stolen barrels from the river Blackroot (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Concerned that goods are being floated south into Tarlang's Crown on the river Blackroot, Gordir seeks to investigate a troubling theft of barrels from Sardol.","Barrels Out of Blackroot","DNT -- will not be seen","Gordir can be found near the river Blackroot to the west of Sardol.\
\
You have recovered as many barrels as you can find, and should now return to Gordir.","'I am glad you were able to recover what you did, but I am not satisfied leaving this alone.\
\
'To what end were these goods taken and sent down the Blackroot?'","Barrels can be found on the shores of the river Blackroot in far south-western of Blackroot Vale.\
\
Gordir has asked you to recover barrels that were stolen from Sardol. He suspects someone has been using the river Blackroot to transport them south into Tarlang's Crown.","Talk to Gordir"},
[1571]={"'Hail to you, ${CLASS}. I imagine you are familiar with siege tactics, defensive positioning, and the like. Do our farmsteads appear ready to withstand an enemy's charge? I believe that more must be done to protect our homes.\
\
'I beg of you, assist us in boarding the openings. A well boarded window will make it difficult for an Orc to penetrate or to easily peer inside to look for prey. Use the planks I have cut to cover the windows of unprotected homes.'","'Our homes are now much more difficult to infiltrate, a welcome trait once the fighting begins. Thank you for the assistance. If our advanced efforts have saved the life of even a single crofter than they were worthwhile!'","The unprotected crofter homes can be found all around the town of Faldham.\
\
Thurgyr has asked you to place boards across the windows of the unprotected crofter homes in Faldham.","Speak to Thurgyr about the boarded windows","Collect sturdy planks from a wood pile","The wood pile can be found outside of Thurgyr's home.\
\
Thurgyr has asked you to collect planks from the wood pile, in order to help barricade the windows of homes.","You have collected several wooden planks","Barricading the Homes","Thurgyr can be found at his home at the southern edge of Faldham, just outside the mead hall area.\
\
Thurgyr should be pleased to hear that you have helped to protect the homes and families of his neighbours, in preparation for the siege.","Board up windows on farmstead homes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Thurgyr has observed that many of the farmsteads around Faldham will be easy to breach for the attacking armies, even with locked doors. He has begun collecting planks of wood for barricading the windows of the homes.","Boarded windows of homes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[1572]={"'¡Lo has logrado! ¡Miren todos, ${PLAYER} no tuvo miedo de subir a esas viejas colinas, ja!\
\
'No hagas caso de los demás cazadores, son un puñado de supersticiosos. ¡Se creen que las Quebradas de los Túmulos están embrujadas, imagínate!'","'Saludos, ${PLAYER}. He estado muy interesado en lo que ocurre aquí en el pabellón de caza. Parece ser el único lugar en Bree donde a la gente se le ocurre siquiera pensar en acercarse a las viejas Quebradas de los Túmulos. Vaya, ya estoy hablando sin explicar nada. Verás, me interesa mucho el lugar... las Quebradas, quiero decir. ¡Ciudades antiguas, reyes de antaño y tesoros más allá de toda imaginación! Mi padre, Newbold, me contó historias maravillosas. Al parecer consiguió unas cuantas piezas de antiguas historias de los Túmulos, aunque nunca quiso decirme cómo.\
\
'He pedido a cada cazador que viene por aquí que viaje a las Quebradas de los Túmulos y recupere algo del tesoro de los túmulos, pero parece que ninguno tiene el valor. Y en cuanto a esos Montaraces, no son de los que se puedan presionar, si me entiendes. He oído decir que los tesoros que hay en los túmulos subterráneos son de los mejores. Uno de los cazadores no deja de hablar de llevarse el tesoro y romper no sé qué maldición puesta sobre él... tonterías, si me preguntas.\
\
'Si pudieras viajar a las Quebradas de los Túmulos, adentrarte en los túmulos subterráneos y recuperar algunos de los viejos tesoros, estoy seguro de que te tendríamos en gran estima.'","Desde hace mucho, entre la gente de Bree se dice que grandes tesoros permanecen enterrados en los túmulos de las Quebradas de los Túmulos, pero pocos tienen el valor de ir a buscarlos.","'¿Has vuelto sin los tesoros de los túmulos? Y yo que esperaba que no te asustaran unos huesos viejos en las colinas...'","Los túmulos están dispersos por las Quebradas de los Túmulos del Norte y del Sur. Tad Cortahoja está en el Pabellón de Caza de Bree, al este de las Quebradas.\
\
Tad Cortahoja te ha pedido que entres en los distintos túmulos de las Quebradas de los Túmulos y recuperes algunos de los tesoros que allí reposan.","Tesoros de los túmulos recogidos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Recoge tesoros de los túmulos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Tesoro de los Túmulos — Introducción","Lleva los tesoros de los túmulos a Tad Cortahoja"},
[1573]={"Maestros arqueros tumularios derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Derrota a maestros arqueros tumularios (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Los muertos ancestrales se han alzado en el Gran Túmulo.","Los maestros arqueros tumularios se pueden encontrar en el ala inundada del Gran Túmulo.","Maestros arqueros tumularios"},
[1574]={"Los muertos ancestrales se han alzado en el Gran Túmulo.","Derrota a flecheros tumularios (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Derrota a tumularios ancestrales (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Tumularios ancestrales derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Los tumularios se pueden encontrar en el ala inundada del Gran Túmulo.","Tumularios","Flecheros tumularios derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[1575]={"Return to Sârwi in Sormedân with his recovered items","Recover Sârwi's wooden shield","You have recovered Sârwi's wooden \\qsword\\q","Sârwi, the young son of Sênjar, has asked you to retrieve his lost toys from the angry bees swarming in Medân Makhai.","Recover Fang","You have recovered Sârwi's wooden shield","Return to Sârwi in Sormedân with his recovered items.","Bash, Block, and Fang","Sârwi, the young son of Sênjar, has asked you to retrieve his sword, shield, and carved lion lost to the angry bees swarming in Medân Makhai. Medân Makhai can be found north-west of Sormedân.","Recover Sârwi's wooden \\qsword\\q","'Oh you found them! Now don't go running off, Fang! I tell him things but I don't know if he listens sometimes. You know how lions are. They never listen.\
\
'Now I can fight! I can protect Sormedân from the vicious Jázgai. Not here, Bloodtooth! Bash will make quick work of you!\
\
'Thanks, now I can be a hero like you!'","'Well! You look like a hero! I'm a hero too, although my da says I can't fight yet. But I can! Well I did. I lost my weapons!\
\
'I went with my da to get honey from the bees, but then the bees started stinging my da and we had to run away! Sometimes heroes have to run away, my da says.\
\
'Anyway, I lost my sword and my shield. And Fang! He's a lion, so he's fearsome, and he comes with me on my adventures, so I'm not lonely. And he protects me. But who is going to protect him?\
\
'Could you get Fang, and my sword, and my shield, so I can be a hero again, just like you?'","You have recovered Fang"},
[1576]={"'These idols are strange indeed, you did fine work ${PLAYER}.'","Bat-idols","Collected bat-idols (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The morroval of Dol Guldur possess many idols in the form of bats.","Collect bat-idols (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Merrevail can be found at Sâd-en-Dagor in Dol Guldur, north-east of Helethir.\
\
Stirnir has asked you to collect bat-idols from the merrevail in Dol Guldur."},
[1577]={"Talk to Mírdiniel at the Haunted Inn","Bats Among the Ruins","Defeat ruins-bats in Dannenglor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Bats lend added protection to the stronghold of the morroval-inhabitants of Dannenglor.","Mírdiniel is at the Haunted Inn in the Dourstocks of Mirkwood, south of Dannenglor.\
\
You should speak with Mírdiniel and tell her of your efforts in dealing with the problem of bat-swarms in the woods.","Ruins-bats can be found in the ruined Elf-stronghold of Dannenglor, north of the Haunted Inn in the Dourstocks.\
\
Mírdiniel has asked you to defeat several bats in Dannenglor when you venture next into the wilds of the Dourstocks.","Defeated ruins-bats in Dannenglor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I am glad to see you well after your venture into Dannenglor...and not a scratch upon you! You have done a considerable kindness to all the Elves of Middle-earth, ${PLAYER}; you have my thanks!'","'Dannenglor is north of here. I believe you will find many ruins-bats there.'","'I am glad that you have come to our aid, my good ${RACE}. As our path leads us through Mirkwood, we see many evil things which we wish to make right. Alas that we have not the resources for such a great undertaking. Even the smallest good deeds must often go undone, for our eyes are fixed upon one target only.\
\
'Dannenglor was once an Elven-home and is overrun now by shrieking beasts of all kinds. The merrevail and mervyl are violations of nature, and even the bats of this forest are unwholesome and evil.\
\
'If you wish to make Mirkwood a little better on behalf of the Galadhrim who must pass through it, you should cleanse those ruins of the vile swarms of bats that give strength to the presence of the merrevail. Will you do this for us? Dannenglor will never be fair again, but you can perhaps begin to cast the evil from within its walls.'"},
[1578]={"Talk to Hetbrúda at Gazathrug's outpost","'The hobgoblins and Orcs are at odds? Why am I not surprised to hear that? Their pact has been tenuous at best since the war began! I will make sure no hobgoblins get past the Steepset!'","Talk to Hetbrúda at Zidir-nesad","'It would seem that a large number of Zhélruka venture to the Steepset, following Prince Ingór, no doubt. Well, we should tell someone about the hobgoblins and Orcs fighting each other. I'm sure there is a high ranking Zhélruka commander around here somewhere!\
\
'Before you go, I just wanted to thank you for accompanying me on this adventure. It turned out somewhat differently than I expected, but I suppose that is the way of adventuring, is it not? I might stick to exploring Máttugard, for now, but if you decide to explore deeper into Gundabad, I will understand. Best of luck to you, ${PLAYER}.'","'Wait, ${PLAYER}, do you hear that? Someone is coming!'","'We need to find out what happened here and where Gazathrug is. Let us search the outpost. Perhaps Gazathrug left a clue to his whereabouts.'","Talk to Voina at Zidir-nesad","Zidir-nesad, the Steepset, can be found in the western part of Máttugard.\
\
You should talk to Hetbrúda at Zidir-nesad.","Gazathrug's outpost can be found in the southern part of Máttugard.\
\
You should talk to Hetbrúda at Gazathrug's outpost.","Battle For the Upper Reaches","Zidir-nesad, the Steepset, can be found in the western part of Máttugard.\
\
You should talk to Voina at Zidir-nesad.","Gazathrug's fear of losing the Upper Reaches of Máttugard are quite warranted."},
[1586]={"Battle Task: Ultimate Slaughter","'Look who has returned. Well, ${PLAYER}, if only every warrior was as proficient as you we'd soon wipe this world clean of these disgusting cretins.'","'I expect more of you, ${PLAYER}. Stop wasting my time.'","Completed Battle Task: Eliminate the Free People (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Battle in the Ettenmoors rages! You are called to slaughter the enemy in great numbers.","Speak with War-tyrant Akúlhun","Do your part in the battle. Slay the Free People where they are found and earn your place in the army of Angmar!","Complete Battle Task: Eliminate the Free People (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Brag to War-tyrant Akúlhun of your glorious efforts","Make your way into the Ettenmoors and slaughter all the Free People you find."},
[1587]={"<rgb=#00ff00>Velzájar has fallen!</rgb>","Complete Quest 'Battle at the Forge: Orcs and Grims'","You should return to Agátur the Boastful and apprise him of your efforts.","<rgb=#FF0000>The terrible Velzájar has entered the fray!</rgb>","A planned assault against enemy forces at the Forges of Gundabad is underway, but the battle will not be won without additional reinforcements.","<rgb=#00ff00>Shakalog has fallen!</rgb>","Agátur the Boastful can be found at Zidir-nesad, The Steepset in Máttugard.\
\
You should talk to Agátur the Boastful and enter the fray in order to complete some of his tasks.","'The forges of Gundabad are under attack! The forces there must be defeated if we are to keep our hold on Gundabad!\
\
'Will you travel there and see this threat banished?'","<rgb=#FF0000>The terrible Shakalog has entered the fray!</rgb>","Complete Quest 'Battle at the Forge: Velzájar'","Complete Quest 'Battle at the Forge: Fire-trolls'","'Go and protect the forges!'","<rgb=#FF0000>Enemy forces have renewed their assault upon the western forges!</rgb>","Complete Quest 'Battle at the Forge: Fire-drakes'","<rgb=#FF0000>Enemy forces have renewed their assault upon the northern forges!</rgb>","Talk to Agátur the Boastful","<rgb=#FF0000>The fire grims have reignited their hateful flames!</rgb>","Battle at the Forge","<rgb=#FF0000>Enemy forces have renewed their assault upon the eastern forges!</rgb>","<rgb=#FF0000>Enemy forces have renewed their assault upon the southern forges!</rgb>","Complete Quest 'Battle at the Forge: Shakalog'","'You have dealt a mighty blow to our enemies! They had better not try anything like that again or they shall surely meet the same fate!'"},
[1593]={"'The Welkin-lofts of Gundabad are under attack! The forces there must be defeated if we are to keep our hold on Gundabad!\
\
'Will you travel there and see this threat banished?'","Complete Quest 'Battle at the Lofts: Cold-drakes'","<rgb=#FF0000>Enemy forces have renewed their assault upon the northern Thing-fold!</rgb>","You should return to Agátur the Boastful and apprise him of your efforts.","<rgb=#00ff00>Grazmauk has fallen!</rgb>","Complete Quest 'Battle at the Lofts: Hobgoblins and Angmarim'","Agátur the Boastful can be found at Zidir-nesad, The Steepset in Máttugard.\
\
You should talk to Agátur the Boastful and enter the fray in order to complete some of his tasks.","A planned assault against enemy forces at the Welkin-lofts is underway, but the battle will not be won without additional reinforcements.","Battle at the Lofts","<rgb=#FF0000>Enemy forces have renewed their assault upon the south-east Thing-fold!</rgb>","Complete Quest 'Battle at the Lofts: Frost-tusks'","Complete Quest 'Battle at the Lofts: Grazmauk'","<rgb=#FF0000>The terrible Ulshatarg has entered the fray!</rgb>","<rgb=#FF0000>Enemy forces have renewed their assault upon the southern Thing-fold!</rgb>","'Go and protect the Welkin-lofts!'","<rgb=#00ff00>Ulshatarg has fallen!</rgb>","Complete Quest 'Battle at the Lofts: Ulshatarg'","<rgb=#FF0000>Enemy forces have renewed their assault upon the north-west Thing-fold!</rgb>","<rgb=#FF0000>The terrible Grazmauk has entered the fray!</rgb>","Talk to Agátur the Boastful","'You have dealt a mighty blow to our enemies! They had better not try anything like that again or they shall surely meet the same fate!'"},
[1594]={"Dragonzuelos de escarcha derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The scout gives you a missive to defeat the cold-drakes attacking Ibdêkh-buzru in Gundabad.","A planned assault against enemy forces at the Welkin-lofts is underway, but the battle will not be won without additional reinforcements.","Battle at the Lofts: Cold-drakes","Derrota a los dragonzuelos de escarcha (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat cold-drakes."},
[1599]={"'You want shields? Everybody wants shields. Sârgud is so popular all of the sudden.\
\
'For Mizâdi? Oh a Shâra wants them. Well, of course. Of course. Sârgud do this, Sârgud do that. Every day it's the same.\
\
'I have many orders, friend. Many orders. I love Shagâna as much as anyone, but even the Shâra cannot cut the line.\
\
'I'll tell you what I can do. Sârgud performs miracles, you'll see! I have some shields almost ready. You gather me some more ore from the north-eastern hills to replace what I used here, and I will give the Shâra these shields. Yes, Sârgud's amazing. I know, I know, you don't even need to tell me.\
\
'Get me that ore and you can have the shields.'","Gathered shields (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Speak with Sârgud, the blacksmith in Iridír.","Battle for Hamât, Part 1","Speak with Girhâzi and Amalíbi in Iridír.","'Excellent. Tomorrow is the day, ${PLAYER}. Tomorrow is the day Bârshud's reign of terror ends in Shagâna.'","Bring the ore to Sârgud in Iridír","Speak with Sârgud, the blacksmith in Iridír","Speak with Amalíbi outside Iridír, in her encampment","Speak with Mizâdi in Iridír","Speak with Girhâzi in Iridír","Gather shields from Sârgud's table (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Speak with Mizâdi in Iridír.","'Thank you for swiftly gathering those supplies, and for dealing with Sârgud. What a headache.\
\
'Now we need to assess whether the others are ready as well. If they are, we will leave at first light tomorrow and make our way south to Dun Shûma. You should speak with Girhâzi and Amalíbi to ensure they and their fighters are ready to leave so soon.'","Bring the ore to Sârgud in Iridír.","Collected ore for Sârgud (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Having found Bârshud's new location, the formidable fortress of Dun Shûma in Khud Zagin, Mizâdi asks you to gather supplies and help rally the local people for one last assault to rid Shagâna of Bârshud for good.","'Oho, these shields are well made! Sârgud is lucky that his boasts are equal to his craft. And look at this! This is enough for our Subuzûri to feast on for a fortnight. We shall not go hungry with this much grain!\
\
'I will take those off your hands. You should speak with Mizâdi, I believe she has another ask of you.'","Gathered supplies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Ah, yes. That should do nicely. See how good Sârgud is at both smithing and negotiation? Here are your shields. Only the best for the Shâra.'","Gather ore for Sârgud in the hills north-east of Iridír.","Bring the supplies and shields to Numûru in Iridír.","'Yes, what warriors I have that can still fight will be ready at dawn's light. Tell Mizâdi we will see this through to the end.'","'Yes, we will be ready. You can count on us.'","Gather shields from Sârgud, the local blacksmith.","Gather supplies from around Iridír (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collect ore for Sârgud in the hills north-east of Iridír (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Bring the supplies and shields to Numûru in Iridír","Gather supplies and provisions from around Iridír.","'My scouts have excellent news, ${PLAYER}. We've found where Bârshud's army is located. He is in southern Khûd Zagin, at a place known as Dun Shûma. What he is doing there, we have no idea. But this is our chance. Before he fortifies his position and brings all his forces to Dun Shûma, we have time to strike him quickly.\
\
'If we can defeat him, it should cause his army to scatter to the winds. We could have peace in Shagâna, friend, real peace for the first time in a very long time.\
\
'But first we need to prepare for this battle. Could you gather shields and supplies for our warriors, and then bring them to Numûru? You might start with the local blacksmith, Sârgud.'"},
[1600]={"Speak with Mizâdi in Khûd Zagin on the hilltop","Journey to Khûd Zagin and meet with Mizâdi outside of Dun Shûma","'Let us press into Dun Shûma. For glorious victory!'","Mizâdi has tracked Bârshud to the fortress of Dun Shûma in Khûd Zagin. The time has come to meet Bârshud in pitched battle and defeat him for good.","'The crucial hour has arrived, friend! Meet us outside of Dun Shûma, ${PLAYER}. There we will end Bârshud's reign of terror, and drive him out of Shagâna for good.'","Journey to Khûd Zagin and meet with Mizâdi outside of Bârshud's fortress, Dun Shûma.","Speak with Mizâdi in Khûd Zagin on the hilltop outside of Dun Shûma.","'This is a good spot to rest a moment. We will gather here and then press on into the fortress proper.'","Speak with Mizâdi outside of Bârshud's fortress, Dun Shûma when you are ready to go.","Battle for Hamât, Part 2","Speak with Mizâdi when you are ready to go","'Bârshud is close, I can feel it. It is time we drove him out of Shagâna for good.\
\
'Come on, ${PLAYER}! For Shagâna, and for Hamât!'"},
[1601]={"'We are as ready as we'll ever be. Now we must confront Bârshud and end this fight!'","'We are close enough that I can taste victory, ${PLAYER}. I would see this Bârshud answer for his crimes against the peoples of Shagâna. He thinks me a fool and a child? We shall soon see which one of us is the fool.'","Push into Dun Shûma and end the threat of Bârshud!","'We must celebrate this victory, but I know my celebration shall be bittersweet. I meant to see the end of Bârshud, but he has survived. If left alone, he will regain an army and make war on Shagâna once more. I must think more on this, but Shagâna is not safe - cannot be safe - whilst Bârshud still breathes.\
\
'But that is a matter for another day. Now we should gather the others and celebrate this victory, incomplete as it feels to me. We have driven Bârshud out of Shagâna, and destroyed his fighting force, and that is cause enough for rejoicing today.'","Speak with Mizâdi in Dun Shûma","Battle for Hamât, Part 3","Speak with Mizâdi to begin the assault.","Speak with Mizâdi in Dun Shûma in Khûd Zagin.","Speak with Mizâdi to begin the assault"},
[1602]={"Speak with Galâmka","'The day has come. Today, we will retake our home!'\
\
'We are as prepared as we can be for the fight ahead. I feel the determination in every one of our hearts. Some of us may not see tomorrow, but know that we all fight for our home, for what is ours! We fight to show these Orcs that these are our lands and they will not drive us from them!\
\
'Let us go now. Let us retake Maurûsh from the monsters who defile it!\
\
'With me my friends! Into Maurûsh and into the fires of battle!'","Speak with Galâmka about the battle.","Galâmka takes a moment before looking up at you to speak.\
\
'Maurûsh is lost.'\
\
Galâmka pauses again.\
\
'There was such hope after all we had done. After all you had helped us to achieve. We fought our hardest, but it was all for nothing. None of us expected that monster to be there. He must be one of them who came from the demon pits. I did not expect them to have such power.\
\
'We may have lost this fight, but Maurûsh is still our home. We must take our time to heal and recover, but this is not the end of our struggle.\
\
'Thank you for standing with us, ${PLAYER}. At the very least, thanks to you, those of us here still remain to fight another day and will continue to fight until our final breath.'","The preparations are complete and Galâmka is ready to begin the battle to retake Maurûsh.","The time has come to fight for Maurûsh and retake the stronghold from the Orcs. All the preparations are complete and Galâmka is ready to lead the charge.","Battle for Maurûsh","Speak with Galâmka when you are ready to begin"},
[1603]={"Rescue injured Rohirrim (0/4)","Rescued injured Rohirrim (4/4)","Rescued injured Rohirrim (3/4)","The Dunlendings relentlessly harry the Rohirrim soldiers atop Dol Baran, affording them little chance to rest or recover their wounded. Several soldiers lie upon the battlefield, seemingly beyond aid.","'I saw you return with a number of our injured warriors to our lines. Your valour speaks well of you!'","Wounded Rohirrim warriors lie atop Dol Baran, beyond the Rohirrim encampment.\
\
Captain Féarn has asked you to rescue injured Rohirrim warriors atop Dol Baran.","Captain Féarn can be found atop Dol Baran.\
\
You should return to Captain Féarn with tidings of your victory.","'You came! I thought I would die out here.'","Rescued injured Rohirrim (2/4)","Rescue injured Rohirrim (1/4)","Talk to Captain Féarn atop Dol Baran","Rescue injured Rohirrim (2/4)","Rescued injured Rohirrim (1/4)","Rescue injured Rohirrim (3/4)","'The Dunlendings have been attacking our positions for nearly three days... not in any great numbers, but in small bands, attacking and withdrawing, then sending fresh men into the fray.\
\
'My own men are exhausted, and some have been caught away from our fortifications, suffering serious injuries. The Dunlendings have let them lie where they fell, hoping to draw us out.\
\
'If you could find some way to rescue my fallen men, I would be indebted to you, for we are sorely put upon.'","Battle of Dol Baran: Bravely Fallen"},
[1604]={"Battle of Dol Baran: Minding the Fort","Doused burning fortifications (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Well fought out there, but I fear these attacks are just a prelude to a larger assault.\
\
'If they were going to give up so easily, they would have done so by now. Be on your guard, ${PLAYER}.'","Captain Féarn is atop Dol Baran.\
\
You should inform Captain Féarn of your victory.","'The Dunlendings are testing our resolve to hold Dol Baran, but they underestimate us.\
\
'We must hold this position, or we will be blind to the approach of their main force when it marches out of Wulf's Cleft. If that happens, Grimbold will have to pull us back across the ford without a fight.\
\
'Aid my men by the fortifications and hold off the Dunlendings. If we can force them to give up on Dol Baran and march their army past us, we will have a critical advantage in the battle to come.'","The Dunlendings assaulting Dol Baran have set the makeshift fortifications alight.","Talk to Captain Féarn atop Dol Baran","Dunlendings are assaulting the barricades atop Dol Baran.\
\
Captain Féarn has asked you to defeat the Dunlending warriors by the barricades atop Dol Baran.","Douse burning fortifications (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[1605]={"Defeat Dunlending warriors (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Well fought out there, but I fear these attacks are just a prelude to a larger assault.\
\
'If they were going to give up so easily, they would have done so by now. Be on your guard, ${PLAYER}.'","Captain Féarn awaits your return atop Dol Baran.\
\
You should bring Captain Féarn news of your success.","The Dunlendings are mounting a series of attacks upon the hill-top of Dol Baran in an attempt to test the resolve of the Rohirrim defenders.","Talk to Captain Féarn","Defeated Dunlending warriors (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Battle of Dol Baran: Testing our Strength","'The Dunlendings are testing our resolve to hold Dol Baran, the great hill to the west, but they underestimate us.\
\
'We must hold that position, or we will be blind to the approach of their main force when it marches out of Wulf's Cleft. If that happens, we may have to pull back across the Ford without a fight.\
\
'Aid my men by the fortifications and hold off the Dunlendings. If we can force them to give up on Dol Baran and march their army past it, we will have a critical advantage in the battle to come.'","Dunlending warriors can be found near the barricades atop Dol Baran.\
\
Grimbold has asked you to defeat Dunlending warriors by the barricades atop Dol Baran."},
[1607]={"Te has cobrado una víctima (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","El campo de batalla de bolas de nieve se enuentra al sur de Farol Escarchado.\
\
Debes entrar en el campo de batalla.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>ATENCIÓN: Solo puedes participar en la batalla de bolas de nieve dentro de los límites del terreno desginado para ella.</rgb>","Entra en el campo de batalla de bolas de nieve","Este asalto ha terminado. Pronto empezará otra, y podrás continuar con la batalla.","(Haz clic derecho en las bolas de nieve para atacar a los objetivos seleccionados.)","¡Comienza la batalla! Puedes empezar a lanzar bolas de nieve (y a esconderte)","Espera a que empiece la batalla de bolas de nieve","Recoge bolas de nieve y ataca a tus contrincantes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Batalla de bolas de nieve (fácil)","Te han desafiado a superar a los más habilidosos adversarios en la gran batalla de bolas de nieve en los campos de Risco Invernal.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Esta misión se eliminará de tu registro cuando finalice el festival actual.</rgb>","Debes esperar a que comience la batalla en el interior de los límites del campo de juego.","'El campo de batalla está aquí... ¡solo tienes que entrar en él! Si estás ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]}, claro...'","Puedes empezar a lanzar bolas de nieve a tus enemigos.","Ahora debes esperar a que la batalla comience","Puedes hacer bolas de nieve utilizando los montones de nieve repartidos por todo el campo de batalla. Aparecerán en tu inventario y serán destuidas cuando las lances a otro jugador.\
\
Debes recoger bolas de nieve y atacar a tus adversarios.","No has llegado al campo de batalla al tiempo. La siguiente ronda empezará en breve.","'¡Saludos! ¿Te gustaría saber cómo funciona la batalla de bolas de nieve? Te daré algunas instrucciones...\
\
'Cuando empiece el evento, los jugadores que se encuentren en el campo de batalla podrán hacer bolas de nieve utilizando los montones de nieve del suelo.\
\
'La bola de nieve aparecerá en tu inventario. Hecho esto, podrás hacer objetivo a otro jugador y hacer clic derecho para lanzarle la bola de nieve... ¡y hacer otra después!\
\
'En esta misión en particular, puedes unirte al juego tantas veces como sea necesario para completar los objetivos.'"},
[1608]={"El campo de batalla de bolas de nieve se enuentra al sur de Farol Escarchado.\
\
Debes entrar en el campo de batalla.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>ATENCIÓN: Solo puedes participar en la batalla de bolas de nieve dentro de los límites del terreno desginado para ella.</rgb>","Te han desafiado a superar a los más habilidosos adversarios en la gran batalla de bolas de nieve en los campos de Risco Invernal.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Esta misión se eliminará de tu registro cuando finalice el festival actual.</rgb>","Debes esperar a que comience la batalla en el interior de los límites del campo de juego.","'¡Saludos! ¿Te gustaría saber cómo funciona la batalla de bolas de nieve? Te daré algunas instrucciones...\
\
'Cuando empiece el evento, los jugadores que se encuentren en el campo de batalla podrán hacer bolas de nieve utilizando los montones de nieve del suelo.\
\
'La bola de nieve aparecerá en tu inventario. Hecho esto, podrás hacer objetivo a otro jugador y hacer clic derecho para lanzarle la bola de nieve... ¡y hacer otra después!\
\
'En esta misión en particular, puedes unirte al juego tantas veces como sea necesario para completar los objetivos. Debes darte más prisa y tener más precisión, ya que esta misión fallará si no tienes éxito en el primer intento.'","Recoge bolas de nieve y ataca a tus contrincantes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Se te ha acabado el tiempo","Entra en el campo de batalla de bolas de nieve","'El campo de batalla está aquí... ¡solo tienes que entrar en él! Si estás ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]}, claro...'","No has llegado a tiempo al campo de batalla","Puedes hacer bolas con las pilas de nieve que hay repartidas por el campo de batalla.\
\
Debes hacer bolas de nieves y atacar a tus adversarios.","¡Comienza la batalla! Puedes empezar a lanzar bolas de nieve (y a esconderte)","(Haz clic derecho en las bolas de nieve para atacar a los objetivos seleccionados.)","Te has cobrado una víctima (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Has dejado el campo de batalla","Espera a que empiece la batalla de bolas de nieve","Batalla de bolas de nieve (difícil)","No dejes el campo de batalla","Ahora debes esperar a que la batalla comience","Has dejado el campo de batalla. Podrás intentarlo de nuevo cuando comience la siguiente ronda."},
[1609]={"'Hello there, good patron! While you can complete the Snowball-fight as many times per day as you like, I'll only reward you for it once!  \
\
'Complete either the easy or the more difficult snowball challenge and then return to me for your reward.'","Complete a snowball fight! \
\
<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>","Battle of the Snowballs - Daily","Participate in the Snowball-fight!","Complete Battle of the Snowballs (Easy)","'¡Bien hecho, ${PLAYER}! Parece que tienes un don para este deporte. Apostaría a que hay mucha gente tiritando por aquí, gracias a ti.'","Habla con Cecil Voller","Complete Battle of the Snowballs (Hard)","Cecil Voller te espera en el borde de campo de batalla.\
\
Deberías hablar con Cecil Voller para contarle tu éxito en la batalla de bolas de nieve."},
[1610]={"'${PLAYER}!¡Llegan noticias del Pasillo Norte, el se Enemigo está preparando para asaltarlo!\
\
'Debemos ir de inmediato... El resto de la guardia avanzada se encargará de defender la Vigésimo primera Sala de nuevos asaltos.'","'Nuestro destino se aciago, ${PLAYER}. Esta horda no tiene final, y somos todo lo que queda. Preparaos, pues podría ser nuestra última resistencia'\
\
'¡A las armas!'","'¡Bien hecho, ${PLAYER}, pero la batalla no ha hecho más que empezar! ¿Ves allí?¡Regresa otro de los guardias de la avanzada!'","El cuarto asalto a la Vigésimo primera Sala ha comenzado. ¡Defended el Pasillo del Norte!","El primer asalto a la Vigésimo Primera Sala ha comenzado. ¡Defended el baluarte este!","Wili se encuentra en el centro de la Vigésimo primera Sala.\
\
Hablad con Wili para recibir más instrucciones.","<rgb=#00FF00>El primer asalto ha sido repelido.Regresad con Wíli para recibir más órdenes</rgb>","<rgb=#00FF00>Has repelido el segundo asalto. Regresad con Wíli pare recibir más órdenes</rgb>","Has viajado hasta la Vigésimo Primera Sala para participar en su defensa.¡Sigue las instrucciones de Wíli y ayuda a los enanos de Moria!","Hablad con Wíli en la Cámara de Mazarbul","Wíli está en el centro de la Vigésimo Primera Sala.\
\
Volved con Wíli para obtener instrucciones.","El tercer asalto a la Vigésimo Primera Sala ha comenzado. ¡Defended el baluarte oeste!","'Completaré los preparativos aquí, ${PLAYER}. Si el pasillo cae, esta cámara será nuestra última esperanza para resistir.\
\
'¡Escucha!¿Oyes los cuernos! Ya vienen... ¡prepárate!'","Esperad a que Wíli termine de transmitir sus órdenes a sus hombres.","Wíli debe sobrevivir al asalto","Wili se encuentra en la Cámara de Mazarbul, al este del Pasillo del Norte.\
\
Hablad con Wili y preparaos para los asaltos finales.","<rgb=#00FF00>Has repelido el asalto final. Deberías regresar junto a Wíli</rgb>","Wíli está en la Cámara de Mazarbul, al este del Pasillo del Norte.\
\
Deberíais regresar con Wíli para hablar de vuestra victoria contra los orcos de Mazog.","Batalla de la Sala Vigesimoprimera","Wíli está en la Cámara de Mazarbul, al este del Pasillo del Norte.\
\
Los enanos se han retirado a la Cámara de Mazarbul. Deberíais reuniros con Wíli y prepararos para el asalto final..","'Nuestras defensas están en orden. Ahora sabrás el papel que vas a desempeñar en la batalla que se avecina.'","Repeled el cuarto asalto","Habla con Wíli en la Vigésimo primera Sala","Repele el segundo asalto","<rgb=#00FF00>Has repelido el cuarto asalto. Deberías regresar junto a Wíli para recibir más instrucciones</rgb>","Hablad con Wíli para ver qué ayuda podéis prestar a los enanos.","'Otra vez, bien hecho, ${PLAYER}.¡Sin embargo temo que los orcos no abandonarán el asalto tan fácilmente!¡Mira, allí hay otro de los guardias!'","<rgb=#00FF00>Has repelido el tercer asalto. Regresad con Wíli pare recibir más órdenes</rgb>","El segundo asalto a la Vigésimo Primera Sala ha comenzado. ¡Defended el baluarte sur!","El asalto final a la Vigésimo primera Sala ha comenzado. Defended la Cámara de Mazarbul!","Repeled el asalto final y derrotad al comandamente orco","Repele el tercer asalto","<rgb=#FF0000>Wíli ha caído</rgb>","'Bien hecho, ${PLAYER}! Pero temo que nuestra victoria aquí será efímera. Los orcos nos superan en número. Esta expedición está condenada al fracaso. Pasarán años antes de que podamos limpiar estas estancias.\
\
'Pero no es momento de lamentarse. Hoy has conseguido defender esta sala.'","'Regresemos a la Vigésimo primera sala y comencemos las reparaciones.'","Repele el primer asalto"},
[1613]={"Defeated Trév Duvárdain in western Angmar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Handarod is at Esteldín in the North Downs, far to the south of Angmar.\
\
You should return to Handarod and tell him of your battles against the Trév Duvárdain.","The Hillmen of the Trév Duvárdain can be throughout western Angmar, far to the north of Esteldín.\
\
Handarod has asked you to defeat the Trév Duvárdain in western Angmar.","'Your battles with the Trév Duvárdain have been well-fought. I commend you for your efforts on the part of the Free Peoples.\
\
'The Trév Duvárdain shall rue the day when they threw in their lot with the lords of Angmar....'","Talk to Handarod","Defeat Trév Duvárdain in western Angmar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I have spoken with an emmisary of the Trév Gállorg of western Angmar. They have requested our aid in their battles against their Duvárdain bretheren, who serve the dark powers of Angmar.\
\
'Go forth and make war against any of the Duvárdain you find in western Angmar and help turn the tide in favour of those who may become our allies.'","Handarod is concerned with the Trév Duvárdain who harry the friendly Trév Gallorg of Angmar.","Battles of the Western Wastes"},
[1617]={"The foetid pools are located near Bazanmanar.\
\
Golodhril has asked you to add drops of the antidote to the foetid pools.","'Did you fall in? Do you have the clay?'\
\
You show her the wet clay.\
\
'Excellent! This will serve perfectly. Take the clay to the workbench and mix it with the ingredients in the mortar. When you are done, add a few drops to the pools and the waters shall run clear once more!\
\
'Ah - if you do not mind, that is. My sister has informed me that I am not to order you around.'","'At the bottom of the nearby stairs, there are multiple fountains whose pools are clogged with something foetid and foul. Go and fetch me some of the plants, that I might study them with my own eyes.'","Collect clay from Kurdushâlak","Bring the clay to Golodhril","Golodhril is located in Bazanmanar.\
\
You should bring the clay to Golodhril.","'You bring plants from the pools? Ech, smells almost as bad those sarrowstones Mother Amma is forever crushing. Give it here then, let me see.\
\
'It is as I expected. The plants are indeed causing the pools to turn sour. Fortunately, I know the remedy! Go on down to Kurdushâlak, the river what cuts through the centre of the gap. On its banks, you will find clay. Bring the clay to me and we shall craft an antidote for the pools.'","Golodhril is located in Bazanmanar.\
\
You should bring the plant samples to Golodhril.","Kurdushâlak runs the length of Clovengap.\
\
Golodhril has asked you to collect clay from the banks of Kurdushâlak.","Collected plant samples (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Golodhril's workbench is located in Bazanmanar.\
\
You should mix the clay with the ingredients in the mortar on Golodhril's workbench.","Slime and unnatural plants choke the once-majestic fountains about Bazanmanar.","Golodhril is located in Bazanmanar.\
\
You should give Golodhril the good news.","Bazanmanar's Foetid Pools","'You finished cleaning the pools? Wonderful! It is essential that the dwarves have clean drinking water, lest their conquest of this place continue to draw out.'","The foetid fountain pools are located near Bazanmanar.\
\
Golodhril has asked you to bring her samples of the plants from the foetid pools.","Treat foetid pools (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Mix the clay in the mortar","Treated foetid pools (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collect plant samples (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'This plant should be nowhere near the fountains. I am sure the Hobgoblins brought it in with them, the filth.'","Return to Golodhril"},
[1618]={"Repara el Kantâ-vilkku","'¿Has terminado las reparaciones? Muy bien, ${PLAYER}. Debido a las recientes tormentas, el Kantâ-vilkku se usará mucho más de lo que se ha utilizado en muchos años.'","Consigue carbón (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Habla con Matti","'¿Cómo van las reparaciones? Muchos viajeros y cazadores perdidos dependen del Kantâ-vilkku para sobrevivir. Asegurarnos que está bien mantenido es muy importante.\
'El Kantâ-vilkku está al este y un poco al sur de Sûri-kylä, en los ventisqueros sobre la bahía de hielo de Forochel. Una vez que tu trabajo esté completo, vuelve aquí para que hablemos de nuevo.'","Kantâ-vilkku reparado","'Bienvenido a Sûri-kylä. ¿Has visto el Kantâ-vilkku en el camino? El Kantâ-vilkku guía a los viajeros y provee de los medios para sobrevivir en las duras tormentas que a menudo tenemos por aquí.\
\
'De hecho, las tormentas y los fuertes vendavales han causado bastante daño a nuestra baliza. Si deseas ayudarnos, quizá pudieras ayudarnos a repararla.\
\
'El Kantâ-vilkku está al este y al sur de Sûri-kylä, en los ventisqueros sobre la bahía. Encontrarás las partes disperas por el suelo de los alrededores.'","'¿Cómo van las reparaciones? Muchos viajeros y cazadores perdidos dependen del Kantâ-vilkku para sobrevivir. Asegurarnos que está bien mantenido es muy importante.\
'El Kantâ-vilkku está al este y un poco al sur de Sûri-kylä. Una vez que tu trabajo esté completo, vuelve aquí para que hablemos de nuevo.'","El Kantâ-vilkku está al este y un poco al sur de Sûri-kylä, en los ventisqueros sobre la bahía de hielo de Forochel.\
\
Matti te ha pedido que vayas al Kantâ-vilkku y utilices las partes que encuentres allí para repararlo.","'Gracias por reparar el Kantâ-vilkku, ${PLAYER}.'","Consigue puntales de balizas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Consigue trozos de estandarte (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Puntales de baliza conseguidos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Matti está en Sûri-kylä, al oeste y un poco al norte del Kantâ-vilkku.\
\
Deberías volver a ver a Matti y contarle que has tenido éxtio.","Trozos de estandarte conseguidos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Los Lossoth utilizan las balizas para ayudar a la gente que se pierde a encontrar el camino y pedir ayuda cuando sea necesario.","La baliza en la nieve","Carbón conseguido (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[1619]={"Fragmentos de saber recogidos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Recoge fragmentos de saber (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Los fragmentos de saber pueden encontrarse a lo largo de las Obras Hidráulicas.\
\
Winiel te ha pedido que busques fragmentos del saber de los antiguos enanos.","Winiel está en la Bodega Putrefacta, en las Obras Hidráulicas.\
\
Debes llevar los fragmentos de saber de vuelta a Winiel.","Faro de esperanza","'Bien ${PLAYERNAME:hallado[m]|hallada[f]}, . Es bueno que hayas venido. Veo en tus ojos el mismo afán de conocimiento que me impulsó a grandes empresas en épocas ya lejanas.\
\
'Aquí, en las Obras Hidráulicas, es fácil encontrar fragmentos del saber enano que se creían perdidos con el paso de los siglos. Si estás a la altura del desafío, quiero que reúnas algunos de estos textos y me los traigas. Seguramente ambos terminaremos aprendiendo mucho juntos.\
\
'Deberías centrar tu búsqueda en los edificios más grandes de las Obras Hidráulicas, así como en cualquier lugar donde haya grandes concentraciones de criaturas corruptas. Vuelve a verme cuando hayas encontrado una cantidad significativa de material para estudiar.'","Lleva los fragmentos de saber a Winiel","Winiel ha venido a las Obras Hidráulicas en busca del conocimiento perdido de los enanos.","'Bien hecho, ${PLAYER}. Estos fragmentos serán muy valiosos en los días venideros.\
\
'Debemos pasar a tu siguiente tarea, pues no hay tiempo que perder.'","'Continúa buscando más conocimiento perdido aquí en las Obras Hidráulicas.\
\
'Es probable que dicho saber se encuentre dentro y alrededor de los edificios más grandes, aunque no me sorprendería que parte de él haya sido recogido por algunas criaturas locales, movidas por la curiosidad.'"},
[1620]={"The signal-fire is lit","'I do wish that the tidings I gave you were merry ones instead of these, but dark times call for a martial bent to my tone. We are at war, and we must fight to retake what is lost.\
\
'Tol Ascarnen lay to the north over the bridge that leads to the Hoardale. I have assembled a force that awaits a signal fire upon the far shore of the island.\
\
'If you are willing to sneak to the shore and light the fire, the forces will come to you and enter the fortress.'","Use Grimwood kindling to light a signal-fire on the eastern shore of the Hoarwell near Tol Ascarnen","Beacon-fire of Tol Ascarnen","The beacon-fire must be built on the far shore of the Hoarwell.\
\
Sergeant-at-Arms Inuelen directed you to cross to the eastern shore of the Hoarwell, and there light a signal-fire to summon a force to assail Tol Ascarnen.","You must not be defeated","A force is needed to take back Tol Ascarnen from the forces of Angmar. Sergeant-at-Arms Inuelen wishes to assail the fortress and has prepared a company to attack.","This location is well-suited for the signal-fire","You failed to light the fire. Angmar prevails!"},
[1621]={"Placed traps on the battlefield (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Bear Traps","Place traps on the battlefield (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Good places to place traps can be found around the battlefield.\
\
You should place traps around the battlefield.","The Beorning Thyra has constructed traps to set upon the battlefield, made from the jaws of avanc.","Placed many traps on the battlefield.","Completado","Thyra holds out a trap made from the jaws of an avanc from Misthallow.\
\
'What do you think? I made them myself. Yrsa thought they might be useful so I brought them with us. These traps would catch the enemy if buried on the battlefield. Would you take these traps and bury them for me when you next go into battle?'","You have successfully placed many of Thyra's traps on the battlefield. Those in the war effort will be thankful for all that you have accomplished."},
[1622]={"Vuelve con Onora y háblale del refugio.","Onora y su marido Rúdhan necesitan un lugar más resguardado para descansar.","Onora te ha pedido que investigues las rocas del noroeste en busca de comida para recolectar.","'¿Un oso y un troll? ¡Por lo visto estas tierras salvajes son de lo más peligrosas! Pero has superado estas amenazas y has vuelto con comida, ¡y por ello cuentas con el agradecimiento tanto de Onora como de Rúdhan!'","'La herida de Rúdhan es peor de lo que pensábamos. Tal vez tengamos que quedarnos aquí más tiempo del que esperaba.\
\
'Pero siempre se puede encontrar comida en la naturaleza, si se sabe dónde buscar. Debería haber algunos arbustos de bayas por aquí cerca, tal vez entre las rocas del noroeste. Claro que semejante festín atraerá a bestias salvajes, pero eso no debería suponer un peligro real para alguien como tú, ¿verdad? Oímos el gruñido de lo que parecía un gran oso poco antes de llegar a este río... pero tal vez ya se haya marchado.\
\
'Ambos te agradeceríamos enormemente cualquier alimento que puedas traernos: bayas, carne o verduras. Cuando mi marido haya recuperado las fuerzas, seguiremos nuestro camino'.","Osos y bayas","Llévales la comida que has recolectado a Onora y Rúdhan","Recoge algo de carne del oso fallecido recientemente","Rúdhan estira la pierna con cuidado y reclama tu atención","Un cadáver reciente de oso podría proporcionar comida abundante a Onora y Rúdhan durante su recuperación.","¡Justo cuando coges un poco de carne, un fuerte rugido perturba la quietud!","Puñados de bayas recolectados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Encuentra comida para Onora y Rúdhan (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[1623]={"Lleva la piel perfecta de oso a un herrero elfo en Rivendel","Armadura de Piel de Oso","Mientras cazabas osos en las Gargantas del Bruinen, obtuviste una piel de dureza poco común. La bestia de la que provenía era fuerte y resistente, poseedora de un pelaje espeso y de una piel aún más gruesa.","'Esta piel es verdaderamente magnífica, ${PLAYER}, y tú lo eres igualmente por haber vencido a la poderosa criatura de la que proviene!\
\
'¡Sería un honor forjar una buena armadura con ella, ${RACE}. Llévala con orgullo y sin costo alguno: el honor de trabajar con un material tan fino es pago suficiente!'","Es probable que un herrero de suficiente habilidad habite en el valle oculto de Rivendel, muy al este de las Gargantas del Bruinen, más allá del Vado del Bruinen.\
\
Hará falta un herrero de gran talento para forjar una armadura digna de la bestia de la que proviene esta piel perfecta.","Nunca has visto una piel tan magnífica. El pelaje es espeso y frondoso, sin rastro de abrojos ni enredos. Los golpes que acabaron con la vida de su anterior dueño fueron tan precisos que la parte utilizable de la piel quedó intacta.\
\
Un herrero de suficiente habilidad podría convertir esta piel en una armadura formidable. Es probable que algún Elfo en Rivendel posea tanto la pericia como el deseo de hacerlo por ti."},
[1624]={"Carne de oso recogida (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Bien, bien. Esa carne debería durarnos bastante tiempo. Gracias por tu ayuda, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}.","Recoge carne de oso (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Los Enanos de Othrikar tienen problemas de suministros, causados por la incursión de orcos y huargos desde el norte y la traición de los Duramano.","Devuelve la carne de oso a Hornbori","Cazador de osos","'Se necesitará mucha carne de oso para alimentar a los mineros hambrientos.'","'Escucha, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}, tenemos problemas aquí. Grandes problemas. Esos malditos Duramano no se conformaron con arruinar la operación de las minas mientras estuvieron aquí, sino que al irse, arruinaron o robaron la comida que teníamos.\
\
Luego están los orcos y huargos que vinieron del norte, expulsando a los granjeros que solían abastecernos de sus campos. Y cuando salimos de Othrikar, tenemos que hacerlo en grupo, por los Duramano acampados cerca. En resumen, tenemos muchos problemas de suministros.\
\
Necesitamos carne. Puedo pagarte en buena plata si cazas algunos osos para nosotros. Deambulan por las colinas al sur.'","Los osos viven en las colinas al sur de Othrikar.\
\
Para ayudar a aliviar la escasez de suministros de Othrikar, Hornbori te ha pedido que caces osos para conseguir su carne."},
[1625]={"The miners Yago and Matho were found dead in the Barnavon Mine, slain by the bugan which attacked.","Talk to Gwilum in Barnavon","Gwilum stands outside the gate to Barnavon-town, far to the west of the Barnavon Mine.\
\
Cada asked you to bring word of Yago's and Matho's deaths to Gwilum.","Portador de malas noticias","'I must ask a grave favour of you, ${PLAYER}. News of the deaths of Yago and Matho must be taken to their families in the village. Go at once to old Gwilum and tell him the tidings...he will direct you from there.'","'Alas that lives were lost in that accursed mine. The families of Yago and Matho will need to be told of their deaths.'"},
[1626]={"'Dios mío, estas son noticias preocupantes. Si había refuerzos de Ghâsh-hai en Hadâd-mezer, solo puedo suponer que también están en Ânghumu-ru y Hurmulkezer.\
\
'Debemos advertir a los demás antes de que sea demasiado tarde... ¡suponiendo que no sea ya demasiado tarde!'","Encontraste un pergamino a medio escribir, destinado a Anazârmekhem, en la mano de un enano asesinado. Sería prudente entregar este mensaje personalmente para advertir a los demás sobre los formidables Ghâsh-hai.","Lleva el mensaje a Hysing en Anazârmekhem.","Anazârmekhem se encuentra al norte de Hadâd-mezer en las Profundidades Llameantes.\
\
Debes entregarle a Anazârmekhem el mensaje que advierte sobre los formidables Ghâsh-hai.","Portador de malas noticias","Encontraste un pergamino a medio escribir, destinado a Anazârmekhem, en la mano de un enano asesinado. Sería prudente entregar este mensaje personalmente para advertir a los demás sobre los formidables Ghâsh-hai.\
\
Anazârmekhem se encuentra al norte de Hadâd-mezer."},
[1627]={"Defeat Iron Crown scouts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'The Trév Dúvardain -- the Hill-men who ally with Angmar? Aye, I can see now why Aighrig would shroud her actions from us. Still, if the Angmarim are hunting her down, her alliances are clear. We ought to help her.'","Scouts of the Iron Crown have been seen spying on Annâk-khurfu.","Talk to Rékkur","Defeated Iron Crown scouts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The scout has orders from Latharn to capture Aighrig for betraying the Trév Dúvardain","Rékkur is waiting for you at Annâk-khurfu.\
\
He will want to hear about the Angmarim orders you found.","Bearers of Bad News","'Soon after we began investigating Gáfin's death, scouts reported Angmarim activity nearby. The Angmarim appear to be searching for something, but can't venture close enough without meeting the pointy end of a dwarf-blade. They're too craven to attack us openly, but they aren't welcome!\
\
'I'd wager a couple have settled themselves behind Annâk-khurfu, while others watch the path leading up here. You won't have to look far. Find out why they're skulking around -- while getting rid of them, of course.'","Rékkur has asked you to defeat Iron Crown scouts on the outskirts of Annâk-khurfu and find out what they're searching for.\
\
A couple may be lurking behind Annâk-khurfu, while others watch the path leading up to it."},
[1628]={"Talk to Vaskorn","'Ah yes, as usual Threkmóth is more concerned with honey cakes than graver matters. Well met, ${RACE}, we have much to do.'","Collected honey from beehives (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","While Radagast tends to the poisoned animals, some nearby Beornings are looking into the cause, which is a mystery considering all the Mirkwood spiders seem to have fled the area.","Collect honey from beehives (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You should go speak with Vaskorn, who can be found in Threkmóth, deep in the Thornholt woods.","Seek Threkmóth in Skoghús","Threkmóth can be found in Skoghús, deep in the Thornholt woods.\
\
You should introduce yourself to Threkmóth, the leader of the Beorning settlement, and deliver your gift to him.","You should collect honey to present to the Beornings as a gift.","You should travel due south of Radagast, in Thornholt, to Skoghús, the Beorning camp.","Bearing Gifts","Talk to Threkmóth","'Is that honey I smell? You must be a friend of our friend Radagast. He said he would send help.\
\
'Now hand that honey over, and go talk to Vaskorn while I prepare the honey cakes! He has been leading the efforts to track down the stingers.'","'Now that you are here, ${PLAYER}, I have little need for odd and flighty dwarves! Many goodly beasts in this most northern edge of Lasgalen have been sickened with poison. I would have sworn it was spiders, yet of course it could not be, for they have all gone missing.\
\
'I have spoken with Beornings who dwell nearby to the west, and they, it seems, have a very similar tale to tell. Will you go to them and learn what you may, while I tend to my sickened friends? Bear with you a gift of honey. It will sweeten your dealings, I think you will find.\
\
'Once you have gathered some honey from over there, you will want to seek out Threkmóth, the Beorning elder, at Skoghús, due south of here.'"},
[1629]={"Received Kharishah's pledge","'Of course I have sent requests on behalf of injured or slain workers. How is it that nothing has been done to help their families? I pledge to stand witness.'","Ayaluk says that he collected written requests from the different masters in the fort. He asked that you get their verbal agreement that they submitted these reports and requests and come back to him.","Received Tankho's pedge","Gain Hûzo's pledge","Bearing Witness","'I must supply reports when there are any incidents on site. How did you learn that nothing is being done about them? It does not matter. What matters is that you have my pledge. I will bear witness.'","Received Beliash's pledge","'This is unconscionable! These lives have been damaged or lost! Their sacrifices were brushed away in the past, but the Kindred of the Coins pledged they would not allow such as this to happen here. This matter must be addressed.'","Received Hûzo's pledge","'This is what we needed. Here, take these notes to the foreman and inform him there are witnesses who will pledge that these reports were never acted upon. Go quickly. I dare not leave for fear of retribution.'","Ayaluk explained that he discovered reports from all of the masters of the different disciplines in the fort and asks that you have them pledge that the information he came upon is true.","'Each foreman submitted reports of accidents, disappearances, and deaths, requesting the effects of the victims to be returned to their families, yet none of the families were compensated. Go to the different masters in the fortress and explain everything to them and gain their pledge that their reports were accurate.\
\
'I would go, but I know I am being watched.'","'Yes, I have submitted those reports to the overseer. How were they never fulfilled? You have my pledge that I will bear witness.'","'Most recently, I sent a request to have pay sent to the family of a man who lost his arms in a terrible accident. He has not been seen since. I thought he simply returned home! I will stand witness to this.\
\
'If the family was not recompensed and the man is missing there is something terrible at work.'","Gain Kharishah's pledge","Take the evidence supplied to you and deliver it to Foreman Nûrut in Rakhatâb.","Speak with Foreman Nûrut in Rakhatâb","'I will not send this information on to the foreman until I have the pledge of witnesses from the masters. It is our custom that there are those to bear witness against the accused and I will see that I follow our ancient rules. But, please, make haste.'","Gain Beliash's pledge","Return to Ayaluk at his family home in Rakhatâb","Gain Tankho's pledge","You have gained the pledge of all the masters that they will bear witness to filing these reports. It is time to return to Ayaluk."},
[1630]={"Gírta has three tasks that need doing near and around the Beorninghús.\
\
You should make jam, butter, and gather eggs for Gírta.","It is important for all to help in the chores and daily work that keep the Beorninghús running smoothly.","'You may have only just arrived, but all who stay at the Beorninghús must assist with the daily work. Yes, Grimbeorn will give his own tasks, that is his way, but he is not the only one who commands folk here! There is much to be done in and around the Beorning-lands. I ask for the completion of three tasks. I need butter, eggs, and jam for baking. Can I count on you?'","Complete 'Joyous Jam'","'Your work has been done well and efficiently, quite like my own children would have done! You have my thanks for each task.'","Complete 'Exceptional Eggs'","Bearing the Burden","'Ah, yes, you would not know where to get started, as I did not tell you! We do not generally receive guests for extended visits, you see, despite Grimbeorn's well-known reputation for hospitality.\
\
'You will find milking cows and eggs in the fields hereabout. Grapes can be found at the orchard just west of the Beorninghús. Thank you for helping, ${PLAYER}.'","Gírta can be found at the Beorninghús.\
\
You should talk to Gírta.","Complete 'The Best Butter'","Talk to Gírta"},
[1631]={"Complete 'The Lost Message'","Completed 'A Threat Unseen'","'Very good then...it is done. You honour me with your aid, and for that, I will serve you in turn.'","Cabed has sent you to complete two tasks before he reveals what he knows about a hidden threat in Parth Celebrant. Cabed is located along the southern road of Parth Celebrant.","'I know what Doron told you, ${PLAYER}. However, there is much that you still do not know.\
\
'Something terrible has come to Ost Celebrant, and while I am not sure exactly what it is, I know it can only bring more destruction to this field.\
\
'There are two tasks I have for you. If you will honour me with your service, I will guide you to the knowledge you seek.'","Completed 'The Lost Message'","Cabed wants you to help him not only deliver a message, but also discover the identity of the threat that has taken hold in Ost Celebrant.","'Complete my tasks, I shall speak more with you.'","Talk to Cabed","Cabed is located along the southern road of Parth Celebrant.\
\
You should return to Cabed with news of your success.","Complete 'A Threat Unseen'","Bearing the Guilt"},
[1632]={"Los osos pueden encontrarse por todos los campos del norte de Bree.\
\
Ray Cardespina te pidió que redujeras el número de osos en la zona.","Osos hambrientos de miel","'¿Has visto los osos por aquí? Se acercan tanto a la granja de día y de noche que creo que se están volviendo mansos... o algo peor.\
\
'Si siguen acercándose a la granja, es posible que ataquen, y si ponemos los caballos en el establo antes de eso... bueno, los Espinar perderán mucho. Si quieres, puedo ofrecerte unas monedas por reducir el número de osos en la zona. Encontrarás los osos de los que hablo merodeando desde el Viejo Fuerte del Camino Verde en el este hasta las Colinas del Brandivino en el oeste.\
\
'Regresa a mí cuando hayas acabado con ellos.'","'Otros piensan que hay amenazas mayores que los osos en esta tierra. Dondequiera que miro, los veo como una amenaza mayor que cualquiera que haya visto. Tenemos que hacer algo sobre su invasión y su creciente población.'","Ray Cardespina espera tu regreso en los establos de la Obra de los Espinar.\
\
Se alegrará de saber que has hecho lo que pidió.","'Lo hiciste bien, y prometí ofrecerte un pago, pero no puedo decir que esté dispuesto a traer los caballos aquí todavía.\
\
'Mira a tu alrededor, míralos ahí fuera... osos. Realmente creo que son la mayor amenaza que enfrentamos aquí en las Tierras de Bree. Sin duda lo creo.'","Osos derrotados en los campos del norte de Bree (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Derrota a osos en los campos del norte de Bree (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Regresa con Ray Cardespina en la Obra de los Espinar","Ray Cardespina cree que los osos que rodean la Obra de los Espinar buscan algo más que miel y que pronto atacarán el lugar. Se niega a permitir que los caballos se trasladen al establo hasta que los osos sean expulsados."},
[1633]={"Bodo Buenavista está en Tejonera, observando los Campos Verdes.\
\
Bodo Buenavista te envió a ahuyentar a los osos de los Campos Verdes. Se alegrará al saber que has reducido la amenaza.","Algo ha hecho que los osos de los Campos Verdes se vuelvan más agresivos últimamente, y Bodo Buenavista está preocupado de que ya no sea seguro caminar allí.","Osos en los Campos Verdes","'¡Los Campos Verdes eran un lugar agradable para caminar, antes de que los animales empezaran a atacar sin avisar!'","'Siempre ha habido osos en los Campos Verdes, pero últimamente algo los ha enfadado. Han empezado a atacar tanto a pastores como a ovejas, ¡y no sé cuánto tiempo pasará antes de que alguien salga gravemente herido!\
\
'Si puedes ahuyentar a los osos de los Campos Verdes, será mucho más seguro para quienes trabajamos al norte de Tejonera, y también para quienes simplemente disfrutan de un paseo bajo el sol.\
\
'¿Podrías ayudarnos? ¡Estoy seguro de que sería muy apreciado!'","'¿Has enfrentado las garras de los osos enfadados? ¡Muchas gracias, ${PLAYER}! Avisaré a mis amigos aquí en Tejonera que pronto podrán caminar por los Campos Verdes sin miedo a los osos.'","'¿Por qué los osos han empezado a atacarnos? ¿Qué los habrá molestado?'","Se pueden encontrar osos en los Campos Verdes, al norte de Tejonera.\
\
Bodo Buenavista te ha pedido que ahuyentes a los osos de los Campos Verdes, con la esperanza de que vuelva a ser seguro para la gente ir allí.","Osos derrotados en los Campos Verdes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Los osos de los Campos Verdes, al norte de Tejonera, se han vuelto repentinamente hostiles. ¿Qué los habrá perturbado?'","Derrotar osos en los Campos Verdes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¡Gracias por tu ayuda con los osos, ${PLAYER}!'"},
[1634]={"Recoge pieles de oso del norte (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Osos del Norte","Pieles de oso del norte recogidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Puede haber grandes osos blancos al este y sur del campamento de Glóin. Puede haber osos pardos al norte del campamento de Glóin.\
\
Caza los grandes osos de las Montañas Nubladas y recoge sus pieles.","'Nunca pensé que fueras ${PLAYERNAME:un cobarde[m]|una cobarde[f]}, o tal vez hay necesidades más urgentes a las que debes atender. Entiendo que los caprichos de un viejo enano tienen menor prioridad que los pedidos de estos nobles y rectos Elfos.'","Glóin cree que los enanos pueden estar sobrepasando su tiempo de estancia en Rivendel y desea renovar su regalo de cortesía a Elrond.","Se rumorea que Glóin necesita pieles de oso para entregárselas a Elrond en Rivendel como muestra de su gratitud.\
\
Recoge pieles de oso en las Montañas Nubladas y llévalas a Glóin en su campamento.","Recoge pieles de oso del norte","'La noticia se mueve rápido. Son pieles finas, verdaderamente finas. Has demostrado ser un digno cazador de bestias, ${PLAYER}. Espero que este regalo complazca a los Elfos.'","Osos, tanto blancos como pardos, pueden encontrarse al norte, este y sur del campamento de Glóin.\
\
Caza los grandes osos de las Montañas Nubladas y recoge sus pieles.","Lleva las pieles a Glóin, ubicado en su campamento."},
[1635]={"'Un éxito y un esfuerzo increíble, ${PLAYER}. Solo puedo imaginar lo duro que fue el combate, pero has triunfado, y eso es lo único que importa.\
\
'Te lo aseguro: jamás había visto un troll con semejante destreza y poder, aun así, has vencido a la Bestia. Eres realmente ${PLAYER:un guerrero[m]|una guerrera[f]} formidable.'","'Te lo digo: nunca había visto una demostración de destrucción como la causada por esa Bestia. Lo mejor sería acabar con ella rápido… o aprender a usar los tambores.'","Los trolls son adversarios formidables y, en Moria, han tenido mucho tiempo para desarrollar pieles más gruesas y temperamentos aún peores. Es tarea de Ossur vigilar las idas y venidas de los trolls y de quienes los controlan en la Gran Escalera. Desde que comenzó a observarlos, ha visto a un troll que parecía más aterrador y letal que los demás, y a una multitud de adiestradores encargados de mantener a raya a la bestia salvaje.","'En mis primeros momentos aquí, en la Guardia Orca, supe que había cosas terribles en las profundidades. Oía retumbos a través de los muros y, una noche, mientras estaba fuera de la Gran Escalera, al noreste, escuché los tambores. Tambores gigantes, transportados por esclavos trasgos, eran golpeados con un ritmo espantoso por otros esclavos trasgos, todo bajo la vigilancia de un adiestrador uruk armado con un hierro candente. Los trasgos también transportaban unas enormes literas, y sobre ellas dormía un gigantesco troll.\
\
'Su pecho se alzaba y descendía al compás de los golpes de tambor, y pude ver una enorme cicatriz en su torso. Mientras observaba, uno de los trasgos perdió el equilibrio y se precipitó a las profundidades junto con el tambor que llevaba a la espalda. Los demás trasgos dejaron de tocar y, sin previo aviso, el troll despertó de un salto y comenzó a masacrarlos. Solo tras un rato de pinchazos y violencia administrados por el uruk logró la Bestia calmarse. Los tambores sonaron de nuevo y el troll volvió a caer en su letargo.\
\
'Tanto si se trata de un regalo como de un arma destinada a usarse contra Igash, debe ser destruido. Entra en la Gran Escalera y encuentra a esta bestia. Cuando hayas cumplido esta tarea, regresa conmigo.'","Ossur se encuentra en la Guardia Orca.\
\
Derrotaste a la Bestia en el interior de la Gran Escalera. Fue un combate difícil, pero perseveraste. Ahora debes regresar con Ossur.","La Bestia ya no existe","Habla con Ossur en la Guardia Orca","La Bestia ha sido derrotada","Derrota a la Bestia","La Gran Escalera se encuentra al noreste de la Guardia Orca.\
\
Ossur te contó que vio a un gran troll dormitar bajo el sonido calmante de los tambores y caer en una terrible frenesí cuando estos cesaban. Observó cómo los trasgos y un adiestrador uruk transportaban al gigantesco troll hasta la Gran Escalera, donde ha permanecido desde entonces."},
[1636]={"Khânah has a growing concern with the kergrim below the cliffs in Tûkurdul and asks you to get rid of them.","'Greetings, ${CLASS}. I am glad to see an adventurer such as yourself.\
\
'I have been keeping track of the kergrim in Tûkurdul below and I begin to worry for our safety. The cliff itself is our only defence, and with the lift destroyed we would be unable to escape should they choose to attack.\
\
'I ask that you travel down into Tûkurdul and thin out the number of kergrim in the area. It would make us much safer here in Ashâgir if you would.'","Return to Khânah and let him know that the hideout will now be safe from the kergrim.","Defeated kergrim near Ashagir (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'You have returned. I have noticed less activity as of late from down in Tûkurdul. I am to believe that this is your doing.\
\
'We shall be much safer now because of what you have accomplished here. I thank you.'","Return to Khânah and update him on the kergrim","Beast Patrol","Defeat kergrim near Ashagir (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Khânah has asked you to get rid of the kergrim in Tûkurdul at the bottom of the cliffs to help make the hideout safer for the people who remain."},
[1637]={"Derrota a los peikko en Länsi-mâ (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Habla con Keli","'¿Así que dices que te gusta un poco la caza? ¡Ja! ¡Claro que sí! Pocos son los que atraviesan los yermos de Forochel sin conseguir una buena variedad de trofeos. Bien, si estás buscando un desafío... uno fuera de lo ordinario, tengo algo para ti.\
\
'¿Has visto a las bestias de las nieves, antropomorfas, hocicudas y de pelaje blanco? Son listas, fuertes como un diablo y difíciles de matar. Los Lossoth las llaman peikko, y se están convirtiendo en una amenaza cada vez mayor según su número se incrementa.\
\
'Mata a varias de ellas y te asegurarás la gloria. Puedes encontrarlas por doquier, pero especialmente en una cueva que han infestado. Ve directamente hacia el este de aquí y sube la colina, buscando la entrada a la cueva.'","Los peikko han aterrorizado durante mucho tiempo la región de Länsi-mâ. Ha llegado la hora de encargarse de ellos.","'¿Qué haces por aquí? ¿Tienes miedo o se te ha olvidado algo? ¡Ve a matar a esos peikko! ¡Al este y subiendo la colina, como te he dicho!","Peikko derrotados en Länsi-mâ (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Los peikko pueden encontrarse en las montañas hacia el este de Zigilgund, en una cueva.\
\
Keli te ha pedido que derrotes a un buen número de peikko.","'¡Ja! ¡Espero que dieras a probar tu acero a esas abominables criaturas, ${PLAYER}!\
\
'Aunque no hemos terminado con este asunto, me temo... hay más por hacer.'","Keli se encuentra en Zigilgund, al oeste de la cueva de los peikko.\
\
Deberías volver a ver a Keli con las noticias de tu victoria.","Criaturas bestiales"},
[1638]={"Bestias Entre las Ruinas","Tu relato sobre lobos malignos y sierpes cadavéricas le recordó a Calenthon la locura de los osos en Nan Tornaeth.","'El relato que cuentas sobre los lobos en Drauglad y en las Gargantas del Bruinen me recuerda mucho a la locura que he visto entre los osos aquí en Nan Tornaeth. ¿Quizás te cruzaste con algunas de esas bestias en tu viaje hasta aquí?\
\
'Caza a los osos enloquecidos de estas colinas y ve si puedes encontrar alguna pista sobre la causa de su locura...aunque tengo pocas dudas de que la fuente está relacionada con el mal que invocó a las criaturas que encontraste antes. Hay muchos osos al sur y suroeste. Yo empezaría por allí.'","Collar marcado con runas encontrado","DNT -- will not be seen","Completado","Caza a los osos de Nan Tornaeth en busca de pistas sobre el origen de su locura","Al examinar el collar, casi te abruma una sensación escalofriante que parece emanar del suroeste de Nan Tornaeth, no muy lejos del campamento de Calenthon.","Osos enloquecidos merodean los pasos y valles de Nan Tornaeth, especialmente al sur y suroeste.\
\
Calenthon te pidió que cazaras a los osos enloquecidos de Nan Tornaeth y los revisaras en busca de pistas que puedan revelar la fuente de su locura.","Has encontrado un collar marcado con runas entre los osos enloquecidos."},
[1639]={"Talk to Gadda about the dangers you saw","Este es un buen punto de vista","'You must be jesting, ${PLAYER}. You did watch-duty? No one has done watch-duty since Sithric came here. Please, tell me what you saw from the towers.'\
\
Gadda listens gravely as you tell him what you saw from your high vantage point.\
\
'Orcs to our west, worms and wicked beasts to our east, and a haunted wood to the north. Things have worsened for us since the patrols lessened. Now there is no hope of us getting food from Eorlsmead without losing many men to the predators that roam the river-lands.'","Beasts at the Doors","Watch-towers have been built around the perimeter of Stangard.\
\
You should climb the perimeter watch-towers and <rgb=#FF0000>look</rgb> out at the Wailing Hills and Eorlsmead.","The watch-duties have not been performed in many long months in Stangard, and Sabert is unable to leave his post at the gate.","Gadda can be found near the Mead Hall in Stangard.\
\
You should report what you saw to Gadda.","Perform watch-tower duty (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","In the Wailing Hills you see Orcs and more Orcs, roaming the lands as if they own them","'It has been months since anyone has been posted on any of the watch-towers, ${PLAYER}. Men go out to hunt or gather to bolster our stores, and too many die on the way because they do not know what faces them.\
\
'It would be a great help to us if you could just climb the watch-towers and look at what roams Eorlsmead and the Wailing Hills.'","'You can enter the watch-towers through the doors and look out once you reach the top. Only the perimeter towers will have good vantage points.'","Too near Stangard, you see a den of vile, slavering dogs preying upon the lands","Far in the distance, you note rocky channels swarming with vile worms","You see nothing noteworthy from this vantage point"},
[1648]={"Return to Megorneth","Beating Back Brigands","Defeat Corsair raiders at Munadhor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Are they gone? Have you done it?'\
\
When you tell her of your deeds, Megorneth slumps with relief, but her eyes lose none of their venom.\
\
'They had it coming! I hope you were thorough!'","With its defender lost at war, Munadhor Farm in Pinnath Gelin has been overrun by beasts and brigands.","You should let Megorneth know that you have defeated many Corsairs at Munadhor Farm.\
\
Megorneth is at Munadhor Farm in Pinnath Gelin.","Defeat Corsair sneaks at Munadhor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Who are you?! Here to plunder our farm too, are you?'\
\
The younger woman places a gentle hand on the elder's arm and tries to sooth her. Cúronel says, 'I do not think they're one of the thieves, mother. I think they may be here to help.'\
\
The elder woman glares up at you, saying, 'If that's the case, go kill as many of the thieves as you can! We may not be able to live here anymore, but I won't see our farm plundered!'","Defeated Corsair raiders at Munadhor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I am sorry about my mother - well, she was my husband's mother. He was a knight but... he did not return from the war.\
\
'Megorneth has been full of rage since, and having our farm overrun by all sorts of beasts and brigands has done nothing to alleviate her pain. I thank you for your help.'","Megorneth has asked you to drive away thieves who have come to plunder her farm.\
\
Corsairs can be found at Munadhor Farm."},
[1649]={"'Mi esposa, Gírta, quiere que vuelva al Beorninghús con algunas de las mejores flores de Lossarnach. Si pudieras recogerlas por mí y entregárselas a mis perros, te daré una recompensa extra. ¿Qué dices?'","Entrega algunas flores a Star","Entrega las flores a los perros de Grimbeorn","Recoge flores de Lossarnach (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Entrega algunas flores a Bud","Entrega algunas flores a Sprout","Recoge todas las flores necesarias para crear el ramo perfecto para el Beorninghús.","Entrega algunas flores a Rose","Has recogido flores de Lossarnach (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Ramo Hermoso — Opcional","'¡Yip!'","'¡Guau!'","'¡Guau guau!'","¡El Beorninghús necesita un hermoso ramo de flores!"},
[1651]={"Habla con Brungos al noreste","Encuentra el lugar elegido por Ravaedron, justo al este de Thelgarth y bajo la colina sobre la que se alzan las ruinas","'Va por buen camino, ${PLAYER}, pero aún no he terminado. ¿Quizá Brungos podría necesitar tu ayuda mientras yo sigo con mi obra? Está justo al noreste, y estoy seguro de que agradecerá tu compañía tanto como Demúr.'","Piedras de pigmento gris recogidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Ravaedron ha elegido un lugar justo al este de Thelgarth, bajo la colina sobre la que se alzan las ruinas, para pintar su regalo para Maddoc y Glenys Astaciervo.","Piedras de pigmento rojo recogidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Ya veo. Sí, Prestadír decía la verdad: esta tierra encierra muchos recuerdos infelices para mí. Pasaron muchos años antes de que volviera a caminar por estas colinas, y mis amigos entre los Fuertes aliviaron un poco ese dolor, pero no se quedaron aquí mucho tiempo. Cuando se marcharon, yo también lo hice, y no deseaba regresar. Solo el deseo de Elrond o de sus hijos podía traerme de vuelta al Mitheithel, y así fue. No encontré rastro de los jinetes negros que buscaban, pero me hice amigo de Maddoc y Glenys Astaciervo, y esa amistad fue un recuerdo luminoso, a diferencia de los que tengo de la guerra de Sauron contra los elfos. ¡Espero no haber dañado sus cimientos!\
\
'Pero eso me ha dado una idea, ${PLAYER}. Los Astaciervo han vivido en el Ángulo durante la mayor parte de su vida, pero no tienen la longevidad de los Eldar. Esta siempre ha sido una tierra hermosa para ellos, sin la mácula del recuerdo de la guerra. ¡Les haré un regalo, un paisaje pintado del Mitheithel, y eso sanará el daño causado por nuestra disputa!\
\
'No he olvidado las lecciones de Wenna, la talentosa pintora de los Fuertes que conocí en Glynafon. Elaboraremos los pigmentos que necesito a partir de materiales naturales de todo el Mitheithel, ¡y así el cuadro estará hecho del paisaje que representa! Va a funcionar, ${PLAYER}. ¿Puedo pedirte que me ayudes a reunir las piedras blandas que necesitaré para hacer estas pinturas? Las encontrarás en las orillas de los ríos de todo el Ángulo. Te veré fuera de Thelgarth cuando tengamos suficientes, ¡pues creo que desde ese lugar elevado encontraré unas vistas dignas de pintar!'","'¡Son perfectas, ${PLAYER:amigo mío[m]|amiga mía[f]}! Las moleré en las cantidades adecuadas para crear exactamente los tonos que necesito para plasmar el paisaje del Mitheithel.\
\
'He elegido un buen lugar para pintar, ${PLAYER}. Está justo al este de Thelgarth, bajo la colina sobre la que se alzan las ruinas.'","Habla con Ravaedron en el lugar que ha elegido para pintar","'Esto servirá.'","Brungos y tú habéis defendido con éxito a Ravaedron desde esta dirección","Piedras de pigmento amarillo recogidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Ravaedron te ha pedido que rastrees las orillas de los ríos que rodean y atraviesan el Ángulo en busca de piedras de pigmento adecuadas para hacer pinturas y tintes.","Demúr ha accedido a ayudarte a rechazar cualquier amenaza que pueda estorbar a Ravaedron mientras pinta, y te está esperando al suroeste.","Ravaedron te ha pedido que te reúnas con él a las afueras de Thelgarth, las ruinas situadas en lo alto de la colina más meridional del Ángulo, cuando encontraras suficientes piedras de pigmento.","La belleza de la tierra","'¡He terminado mi obra! No me atrevo a dar ni una pincelada más, pues temo que mi cuadro se resista a mejorar. ¡Si continuara, me arriesgaría a estropearlo todo!'","Llévale las piedras de pigmento a Ravaedron, dentro de Thelgarth","Habla con Ravaedron al este de Thelgarth","Ravaedron ha tenido una revelación y ahora sabe cómo arreglar las cosas con sus amigos los Astaciervo antes de abandonar la Tierra Media.","Habla con Demúr al suroeste","Brungos ha accedido a ayudarte a rechazar cualquier amenaza que pueda estorbar a Ravaedron mientras pinta, y te está esperando al noreste.","'Saludos, ${PLAYER}. Evitemos que cualquier amenaza curiosa o enemigo peligroso moleste a nuestro artista.'","Encuentra piedras de pigmento gris por las orillas de los ríos del Ángulo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Encuentra piedras de pigmento rojo por las orillas de los ríos del Ángulo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Encuentra piedras de pigmento amarillo por las orillas de los ríos del Ángulo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Demúr y tú habéis defendido con éxito a Ravaedron desde esta dirección","Ravaedron se encuentra al este de Thelgarth y bajo sus ruinas.","Ravaedron ha empezado a pintar su regalo para Maddoc y Glenys Astaciervo, al este de Thelgarth.","'He elegido un buen lugar para pintar, ${PLAYER}. Está justo al este de Thelgarth, bajo la colina en la que se alzan las ruinas.'","'¿Acaso no es un lugar encantador? Envidio a quienes pueden pasear entre estos ríos y ver solo la belleza de la tierra, y no las cicatrices de la guerra que yo he visto aquí. Mi reto será pintar la vista que tengo delante y no la que recuerdo, pero dejaré que mi pincel guíe el baile y veré adónde me lleva.\
\
'Varios Dúnedain han accedido a montar guardia para que nadie me moleste mientras pinto. Demúr está justo al suroeste. Si tú también quieres ayudar, sé que agradecerá tu compañía, y en este poco tiempo he aprendido de tu gran destreza.'","'No he olvidado las lecciones de Wenna, la talentosa pintora de los Fuertes que conocí en Glynafon. Elaboraremos los pigmentos que necesito a partir de materiales naturales de todo el Mitheithel, ¡y así el cuadro estará hecho del paisaje que representa! Esto va a funcionar, ${PLAYER}. ¿Puedo pedirte que me ayudes a reunir las piedras blandas que necesitaré para hacer estas pinturas? Las encontrarás en las orillas de los ríos de todo el Ángulo. Te veré fuera de Thelgarth cuando tengamos suficientes.'","'¡Desde aquí he oído de tus hazañas junto a Demúr, ${PLAYER}, y ahora estoy preparado para superar el trabajo de mi compañero! ¡Que ni bestias ni enemigos perturben la labor de Ravaedron!'","Ravaedron está pintando un regalo para Maddoc y Glenys Astaciervo al este de Thelgarth y bajo sus ruinas."},
[1652]={"'Well, well. Another duvodiad trying to please us. I am tired of your kind coming into our bog, thinking you can change the world with your mere presence. Well, it will not happen, but you can make my life easier, and I will let you live.\
\
'Fetch me bog-reeds so I can string these bows. The reeds around here grow strong, like us. They are better than any other material out here.\
\
'You doubt me? One more word and I will... never mind. Go gather reeds!'","Bog-reeds be found the north-east area of the Dunbog. Nye is also encamped in the north-east Dunbog.\
\
Nye has intimidated you into fetching him more bog-reeds for bow-strings.","Talk to Nye at the scouts' camp","Collected bog-reeds (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Because I Said So","Collect bog-reeds (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The scouts of the Dunbog have tasked you with several gathering exercises. Nye specifically does not like you and has instructed you to do his task for him.","'Perhaps you should get me some more bog-reeds?'","'Well, you are not completely useless like the others I have seen come through here. Still, my life is no better, and the Elders will just send me out for more bow-strings tomorrow. Thank you for nothing, ${RACE}.\
\
'Now get out of here before I decide to stop being nice.'"},
[1653]={"Hechiceros de Ekhamâti derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Arqueros de Ekhamâti derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Kósikul derrotado","Derrota a los hechiceros de Ekhamâti (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Derrota a los arqueros de Ekhamâti (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Guerreros de Ekhamâti derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","¡Kósikul ha llegado para defender el campamento! ¡Derrótalo!","Derrota a Kósikul","¡Kósikul ha llegado para defender el campamento!","Tu misión es sabotear las máquinas de asedio que se han descubierto en un campamento de Ekhamâti cercano y eliminar a cualquier soldado que intente detenerte.","Catapultas ekhamâti saboteadas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Derrota a los guerreros de Ekhamâti (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Buen trabajo destruyendo esas máquinas de asedio. Regresemos a Iridír.'","Sabotea las catapultas ekhamâti (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Convirtiéndose en una espina"},
[1654]={"'Thórvilon told me you are to be our tree-bearer? It is quite the honour. Almost never given to an outsider. Thórvilon must think quite highly of you.\
\
'Well, your task is simple enough. Gather rich soil into this sack from throughout Vartúlin. Then come back here and carefully remove these young tree saplings you see. You are then to replant them in greater Adagím. Dig a small hole out, replant them and then cover their roots with the rich soil you collect. They are to be about 20 paces east, beyond the edge of Vartúlin. This will allow us to check them easily, to ensure they are truly hardy enough to withstand the Lâg Dávrit. Off with you then.'","Becoming a Tree-bearer","Speak with Thórvilon in Vartúlin","Go to the edge of Vartúlin then march north around the rock formation","'You have borne the first of many trees back to the forests of Favrathór. It is not again Laithór, the Emerald Wood, nor will it be for many years. But we have hope now, because of your actions.\
\
'The Adúrhid use 'Tree-bearer' to denote someone who has done great works for the lands near their home. Though you are not Adúrhid, you have done great works near our home. You should know that not many outsiders get to wear this title. But for you, we will make a special exception. You may wear this name with pride.'","Speak with Culvair the grove-tender in Vartúlin","Speak with Thórvilon in Vartúlin.","'I have a final task for you, my friend. Though this is less a task, and more an honour befitting all you have done for us. You are to be an Adúrhid tree-bearer.\
\
'The first young tree saplings we have grown resistant to the Lâg Dávrit, the Pale Blight, are ready to be transported out of Vartúlin and into the forests of Adagím proper. I have instructed the grove-tenders that you are the one to be given the honour of doing this. Speak with Culvair, one of our grove-tenders. He will explain more deeply. And, once more, thank you for all you have done for us, ${PLAYER}.'","Thórvilon has given you the honour of being a tree-bearer for the Adúrhid. You are to transplant the first young tree saplings into the greater forests of Adagím.","Carefully gather the tree saplings (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collect rich soil from around Vartúlin.","Collected rich soil from around Vartúlin (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collect rich soil from around Vartúlin (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Plant the tree saplings in Favrathór (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Speak with Culvair the grove-tender in Vartúlin.","Plant the young tree saplings in the forest just outside Vartúlin.","Go to the where the forest of Favrathór meets the edge of Vartúlin. Go to the edge of Vartúlin then march east and north around the rock formation. Plant the tree saplings there.","Planted the tree saplings in Favrathór (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Go to Ulthral's nursery and carefully remove tree saplings for planting in the greater forest.","This seems the perfect place to plant these saplings","Gathered the tree saplings (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[1655]={"Examina la cama de Gamli","Gamli se encuentra en el campamento del Umbral de Durin.\
\
Deberías hablar con Gamli acerca de lo que encontraste en su cama.","Has encontrado insectos en la cama de Gamli","'¿No ves esas horribles cosas arrastrándose en mi cama?'","Habla con Gamli","'¡Eh, ${PLAYER:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}! No ves nada... moviéndose... en mi cama, ¿verdad?\
\
'Últimamente mi sueño se ha visto muy perturbado por la sensación de que algo se arrastra por mi piel. Me niego a volver a meterme bajo esas mantas hasta estar seguro de que no hay nada vivo en ellas.\
\
'Échale un vistazo por mí, ${PLAYER}. No me atrevo a tocar las mantas.'","La cama de Gamli se encuentra en el campamento del Umbral de Durin.\
\
Gamli parece preocupado por la posibilidad de que algo se esté escondiendo en su cama.","Chinches","'¡Esto es intolerable! ¡Insectos revoloteando donde apoyo la cabeza es completamente inaceptable! ¡No puede tolerarse, te lo digo!\
\
'¿De dónde han salido esas horribles criaturas? Apenas llevamos un día aquí y ya estamos infestados.\
\
'Creo que ahora necesitaré lavarme a conciencia....'","Gamli el enano teme que algo pueda estar ocultándose entre sus mantas."},
[1656]={"You replaced the first horse's bedding","Replace the bedding of the third horse","Collect fresh hay in the north field (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Éogar and inform him the bedding has been replaced","'Thank you for taking care of the horses' bedding for me!'","Replace the bedding of the first horse","The hay-piles can be found at Hengstacer Farm, in the field north of the stables.","Éogar can always use more help on his farm, and today he needs the hay for the horse's bedding replaced.","You replaced the fourth horse's bedding","<rgb=#FF0000>Your brittle hay-fork breaks after too many uses on horse bedding hay (${NUMBER}/7)</rgb>","'Are you occupied? A stable-help ran by on his way to finish an errand and told me the bedding in the new horse's stable needs to be replaced, and as soon as possible. Unfortunately, Billy, Bobby, Lizzie, and Henry -- as the stable-hands have named them -- are finicky about who gets attention first, as they have a bit of a pecking order. We need to be careful to care for them in the right order, as we must not upset them too much.\
\
'It seems the stable-help has taken all the good hay-forks, and all I have left are old and brittle ones. You will only be able to use these old hay-forks on the dirty hay so many times before they will break, at which point you will have to come see me again for another.'","That was not the right one...","Collected fresh hay (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You replaced the third horse's bedding","That was not the right one....","Billy, Bobby, Lizzie, and Henry are finicky about who gets attention first. They must be cared for in the right order.\
\
Éogar's old hay-fork is well worn and can be used on the dirty hay only so often before it breaks.","Replace the bedding of the fourth horse","Replace the bedding of the second horse","You replaced the second horse's bedding","Bedbugs Bite","Éogar may be found at Hengstacer Farm in the Horse-fields of Bree-land."},
[1658]={"Delivered bone combs (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'The army has been on the move and on the attack for so long that I fear some of our brethren have forgotten better days. What seems a small thing may in truth be a large comfort. I have carved these combs from bone and horn. Please, bring them to those in need. Our beards are our pride, and our bedraggled friends will appreciate freeing their locks from the tangles and knots travel and fighting have brought on.'","Deliver bone combs (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'What's this now? A comb? I was going to get around to that... give it here, then.'","Elgur is located in Amdân.\
\
You should return to Elgur.","The Haban’akkâ have been at war and away from home for months. Simple acts can do much to improve morale.","Bedraggled dwarves can be found in Amdân.\
\
You should distribute bone combs to bedraggled dwarves.","'For me? You have my thanks. I will be sure to pass this along to others in need as well.'","'Oh! Give it here, will you? My own comb broke weeks ago. Well, I suppose you could tell that.'","'A beard comb? What are you implying! Well, give it here. Might as well put it to use.'","'Excellently done, friend. This was a small thing, but is one that has the potential to impact our brethren greatly. No dwarf should go to war with his beard a tangled mess.'","'What now? No, I haven't got a comb for you. Oh! You offer it to me! Well isn't that finely made. Give Elgur my thanks.'","Return to Elgur","'Have you delivered all of the combs?'","'Ah, a comb? Thank you, friend. My thick fingers are no match for these snarls.'","Bedraggled Dwarves"},
[1659]={"Poliniza los grandes lirios de Lossarnach.","'¡Bzz bzz!'","Comprueba si las abejas están listas para continuar.","<rgb=#FF0000>¡Debe sobrevivir al menos un gran lirio de Lossarnach!</rgb>","¡Las abejas están listas para continuar!","Escolta a las abejas de vuelta con Grimbeorn","Comprueba si las abejas están listas para partir","Poliniza el segundo campo de flores.","Comprueba si las abejas están listas para continuar","Habla con Grimbeorn.","'¿Por qué has tardado tanto? ¿Te detuviste a oler todas y cada una de las flores? ¡Ja, solo es un poco de humor beórnida, amigo mío! ¡Me alegra que me hayas devuelto a mis abejas!'\
\
Grimbeorn se vuelve hacia sus abejas.\
\
'¡Abejas! ¡¿Os habéis dado un buen festín?! ¡Estoy seguro de que sí!'","Comprueba si las abejas están listas para volver con Grimbeorn","'¡Bzz!'","Comprueba si las abejas están listas para partir.","La gran tarea de las abejas","Escolta a las abejas de vuelta con Grimbeorn.","<rgb=#FF0000>¡Las abejas de Grimbeorn deben terminar su tarea!</rgb>","Poliniza los grandes lirios de Lossarnach","¡Las abejas parecen ansiosas por polinizar!","Grimbeorn y sus perros se quedarán aquí mientras ayudas a las abejas a orientarse por el bosque","¡Parece que el trabajo de las abejas aquí ha terminado!","Comprueba si las abejas están listas para volver con Grimbeorn.","Habla con Grimbeorn","<rgb=#FF0000>¡Se han comido un gran lirio de Lossarnach!</rgb>","'Bueno, aquí estamos. ¿Que por qué accedí a prestar mis abejas para ayudar a Gondor a polinizar los campos de Lossarnach? ¡Pues porque, mi fiel ${RACE}, Gondor ha derrotado a muchos enemigos que algún día podrían amenazar la seguridad de mi Valle! ¡Es lo menos que podía hacer!\
\
'Sí, te he pedido que me acompañes porque no conozco las tierras de Lossarnach. ¿Cómo voy a guiar a mis abejas por tierras que desconozco? Tú, sin embargo, sí las conoces. Por eso guiarás a mis abejas por mí. ¡No te preocupes! Todo lo que tienes que hacer es asegurarte de que mis abejas no se alejen mucho y que no sufran ningún daño. ¡Debería ser bastante fácil! ¡No es más que un bosque lleno de flores!'","<rgb=#FF0000>¡Una abeja se ha rendido!</rgb>","¡Es hora de polinizar los prados!","Poliniza el segundo campo de flores","Poliniza el primer campo de flores"},
[1660]={"Completa 'El Gran Negocio de las Abejas'","El Gran Negocio de las Abejas — Diaria","'Hmm, si me traes todas mis abejas bien alimentadas, te daré una recompensa extra. ¿Qué dices?'","'El Gran Negocio de las Abejas' completado","Un juego diario: ¡la primavera es sencillamente maravillosa!"},
[1662]={"'Thank goodness you came when you did! My harvest would have been devastated for the entire year, otherwise!\
\
'Right, I can breathe now and give you the answer you're looking for.'","'Stay where you are! We don't need any more trouble here!'\
\
You assure Nordach that you're here to help and tell him that Lúmar sent you.\
\
'He must be looking for Igerna, eh? She's not here, and I wish she was. My fields have been infiltrated by enormous beetles! They are eating up my precious grapes. You get rid of them for me, and I'll tell you what I know about Igerna.'","You should let Nordach know that you have helped to clear the Winbury vineyards of beetles.\
\
Nordach is at Winbury.","Defeat beetles (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Nordach","Defeated beetles (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Nordach seems to know where Igerna is, but won't share the information until you have helped clear his vineyards of an infestation of beetles.\
\
You should defeat beetles at Winbury, in northern Pinnath Gelin.","The vineyards of Pinnath Gelin are renowned for producing the finest wines and spirits. One of this year's delicate crops is playing host to a most unwelcome guest.","'I must stay here to receive reports from the rest of my scouts. We are working hard alongside the Knights to ensure that the king's visit is untroubled. Will you go east to Winbury and speak with Nordach? He may have seen or spoken with Igerna!'","Beetles Among the Vines","Lúmar has asked you to search for signs of Igerna and speak to Nordach at Winbury.\
\
Winbury is in northern Pinnath Gelin.","Return to Nordach"},
[1664]={"'The Host of the West has passed northward, and even now they make camp on the border of Dagorlad.'\
\
'The pass of Cirith Negen has been made safe, the roadway north is clear, but the lands of Dagorlad are steeped in the Enemy's corruption.\
\
'The Host of the West shall have need of you in the coming days - of this I have no doubt. Although my men are familiar with the lands of Dagorlad, its harsh terrain and wide plains make it deadly to those who do not move with care. By sharp stone, Orc, or worse terrors of the Black Land, death follows closely upon the battle plain.\
\
'Bear this in mind, ${PLAYER}, for it is there you and the Host of the West will challenge the Dark Lord. I ask that you rejoin them as swiftly as you are able and travel to their camp to the north.\
\
'If you see Damrod, please speak to him on my behalf. A great test lies before us... and we must not fail.'","Countless members of the Host of the West are camped nearby...","Habla con Aragorn","Before the Battle Plain","'${PLAYER}! For a moment, I was afraid you had left our company behind! It was a foolish worry, but fear has a smothering presence so close to the Black Land.'\
\
Damrod shifts uneasily, but is quick to hide his concern.\
\
'This is it, my friend... soon we shall pass from the lands of Gondor onto the battle plain, Dagorlad.\
\
'While the Rangers and I often patrol the lands of Dagorlad, the Enemy cannot mistake our purpose in mustering so many to its border.\
\
'We have fought through exhaustion, and now we must draw up our weapons once more. I am glad that all of us shall stand together as we march on the Black Gate.'","Talk to Mithrandir at Aragorn's camp","Aragorn can be found in his encampment on the border of Dagorlad.\
\
You have spoken to Damrod and Mithrandir and should now speak to Aragorn.","'We stand on the border between Gondor and Sauron's wastes, and if any among us would turn back, now is the final moment.\
\
'I do not blame those that would turn from the coming battle. It shall cost most or all of our lives, but if Frodo can finish his quest, a victory over Sauron would be worth them all.\
\
'We must stand together as one against the Dark Lord when the time comes, and I trust that you will be at my side. We have travelled far in service of the same quest, my dear friend, and now we must see it done!'","Travel to Aragorn's camp on the border of Dagorlad","After securing the lands of Ithilien, the time has come to rejoin the Host of the West at their encampment on the border of Dagorlad, the battle plain.","Aragorn's camp can be found far to the north of Henneth Annûn on the southern border of Dagorlad.\
\
Anborn has asked you to rejoin Aragorn and the Host of the West at his encampment to the north.","Talk to Damrod at Aragorn's camp","Mithrandir and Damrod can be found within Aragorn's encampment on the border of Dagorlad.\
\
You have arrived at Aragorn's encampment and should now speak to your allies.","'The Dark Lord knows well of our approach, and we shall soon learn what manner of trap he has devised for us before the Black Gate. Let us hope that he remains blind to the trap we have laid in turn... and even moreso that our chance victory might be won.\
\
'We are nearing the end of our journey, ${PLAYER}, and Aragorn will soon have need of us all.'"},
[1665]={"Before the Heart of Darkness","Search Aufaltor for signs of Nidhlas and his men","As Mithrandir begins his study of Thuringwath, you begin your search for the lost Rangers of Ithilien.","The footprints continue along the old roadway through Thuringwath.\
\
You discovered footprints on the old roadway through Thuringwath. You should follow them.","Mithrandir can be found near Aufaltor in Thuringwath.\
\
You have found Mithrandir standing before a great watching-stone in Thuringwath. You should tell Mithrandir what you have found.","You should examine the heap of discarded flesh.\
\
You discovered the Rangers slain from bloodletting, but a heap of flesh has caught your eye. You should examine it.","This flesh has been flensed from a Man, but the body is nowhere to be found","Aufaltor can be found in Thuringwath.\
\
You have followed the footprints to the base of a great fane. You should search the fane for Nidhlas and his men.","Examine the slain Rangers in Aufaltor","Nidhlas and his men might be found somewhere in Thuringwath.\
\
Mithrandir has asked you to continue ahead in search of Nidhlas and his men.","These Rangers have been bled, but a sickening heap of flesh catches your eye","'Many are the shadows that loom upon Thuringwath, and I have not the strength to banish them.\
\
'I must rest for a short while, but you should search for the lost Rangers of Ithilien. I fear it may already be too late for them, but if any hope remains, you must seize it.\
\
'Do not wait for me, ${PLAYER}. Even now, evil does not rest in Thuringwath.'","Mithrandir stands transfixed before a great watching-stone in the form of a balrog","Examine the heap of flesh","Search for signs of Nidhlas and his men in Thuringwath","Slain Rangers can be found deep within Aufaltor.\
\
You have discovered a number of slain Rangers within Aufaltor. You should examine them.","Follow the footprints deeper into Thuringwath","Talk to Mithrandir","You notice footprints on the old roadway through Thuringwath","'Ah, tell me, what did you find?'\
\
You tell Mithrandir what you discovered within Aufaltor. You tell him of the slain Rangers and the flensed flesh left to moulder among its tombs, and that you remain uncertain if Nidhlas escaped the fate that befell his men.\
\
'I do not think he was so fortunate, ${PLAYER}. I have seen enough of Thuringwath to know that the Living do not long endure it.\
\
'Curious. I sense a presence within this watching-stone, but it refuses my summons.\
\
'We shall see about that.'","The footprints lead to the foundations of a great, deathly fane...","Mithrandir can be found in Thuringwath.\
\
You found a grisly scene at Aufaltor. You should return to Mithrandir.","Return to Mithrandir","The footprints continue along the old roadway through Thuringwath","You have discovered a number of slain Rangers in the depths of Aufaltor"},
[1672]={"You give a tasty treat to the goat!","Give a tasty treat to a Bindbole kid","Give a tasty treat to a Hollin Ridge goat","Speak with Radagast","Give a tasty treat to a Brandy Hills billy","Now what do we have here?","Da una golosina a una cabra del Páramo Alto","Radagast the Brown asks you help him rescue goats and bring them back to the safety of Rhosgobel.","Radagast can be found in Rhosgobel.\
\
You should speak with Radagast.","'Ah, thank you! I see you were able to bring back a couple of goats with you. I am glad your travels were a success.\
\
'You have a good rapport with the animals. This skill will aid you on your journeys ahead.'","Befriending Critters: Get One's Goat","'Use the special food I have given you to befriend some goats. They'll be safe in Rhosgobel where I can tend to them. I'm counting on you, ${PLAYER}.'","Goats can be found all over Middle-earth.\
\
Rescue goats using Radagast's calming treats.","Give a tasty treat to a Lune River goat","You give a tasty treat to the goat to calm him down!"},
[1674]={"You are finding it very difficult to befriend a young mûmak. Try again to use the Mûmak Trainers' Horn on young mûmakil at the Spent-lodes, and bring one back with you to Khanâg Gur.","Pick up the Mûmak Trainers' Horn","Oh, bother","Talk to Namâdi at Khanâg Gur","This is ridiculous...","Not again!","Go to the Spent-lodes","You are finding it difficult to befriend a young mûmak. Try again to use the Mûmak Trainers' Horn on young mûmakil at the Spent-lodes, and bring one back with you to Khanâg Gur.","Namâdi has asked you to use her Mûmak Trainers' Horn to train a young mûmak and bring it back to her at Khanâg Gur. You should use the horn on one of the young mûmakil.","That did not go as planned","'Saráz záro-dan, my friend! I have recently fallen upon good fortune and am looking for a courageous individual with which to share it!'\
\
The woman seems to be very pleased with herself.\
\
'I have acquired a horn that once belonged to a Gânda. It is what they use to tame and control the mighty mûmak! There are many mûmakil running free at Erakúndo, the Spent-lodes. If you are as skilled as you seem, I have a business proposition for you!\
\
'I will cut you in on the profits if you can take the horn and return here with a mûmak! People will pay well to make use of it for their various... activities. I can see it now! There would be so many people wanting to borrow our mûmak that we would need a waiting list!\
\
'Take the horn to the Spent-lodes and use it on a young mûmakil until one responds. Surely at least one will react favourably.'","Namâdi has recently come into possession of a horn that Ordâkhai Gânda use to direct and control mûmakil.","Uh oh...","<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: You must slot the horn as a skill. To do so, drag the 'Mûmak Trainers' Horn' item from your inventory to your skill bar. You then use the skill on a Young Mûmak to advance the quest.</rgb>","'What, no mûmak?'\
\
You tell her that you tried many times, but all they did was attack you.\
\
'Oh. Well, not everyone is suited to be a Gânda. I will find someone else, but thank you for trying.'","Try again to use the Mûmak Trainers' Horn on young mûmakil at the Spent-lodes, and bring one back with you to Khanâg Gur.","Try again to befriend a young mûmak using the horn","Befriend a young mûmak using the horn","This is Erakúndo, the Spent-lodes","You begin to wonder if it is even possible to befriend a young mûmak. Try again to use the Mûmak Trainers' Horn on young mûmakil at the Spent-lodes, and bring one back with you to Khanâg Gur.","Oh no...","Namâdi has asked you to use her Mûmak Trainers' Horn to train a young mûmak and bring it back to her at Khanâg Gur. You should go to the Spent-lodes in southern An Shêru.","Try once again to use the Mûmak Trainers' Horn on young mûmakil at the Spent-lodes, and bring one back with you to Khanâg Gur.","Namâdi has asked you to use her Mûmak Trainers' Horn to train a young mûmak and bring it back to her at Khanâg Gur. You should pick up the horn from atop the wall next to her.","Try once more to befriend a young mûmak using the horn","Befriending a Behemoth","You're pretty sure it is impossible to befriend a young mûmak by just using the Mûmak Trainers' Horn."},
[1675]={"Unusâli has decided she will not trust you until you prove yourself to the Beltáni.\
\
You should complete three quests in Ahâba to prove yourself.","The Beltáni chieftain, Unusâli, does not trust outsiders easily. She asks you to help the people of Ahâba with their work to prove yourself to her.","'My people are pleased with your work. You may stay.\
\
'While you were gone, Mizâdi and I spoke of how she became Shâra of Renewed Hamât. We share a bond: the cruelty of Ordâkh took both our husbands. We have agreed to help each other claim vengeance.\
\
'When the forces of Hamât gather before they march to make war on Emax Dûl, they may make camp in Ahâba. We will then add who we can to your host. May the Beltáni finally be free.'","'Unusâli seems to be a hard woman, but I suspect she only wishes to protect her village. The Ordâkhai have caused these people much grief over the years, and I do not blame her for being slow to trust.\
\
'This will be my first real chance to prove myself to Mizâdi as her diplomat. I believe I can make headway on this negotiation by appealing to our shared enemy, and their similar pasts....'","Unusâli has heard of your work for the Beltáni and is pleased.\
\
You should talk to Unusâli in Ahâba.","'I believe your Shâra when she says she wants to protect us from the Ordâkhai, but I sense you want something from us in return. We are not ones to trust outsiders so easily, not after our many years of resistance to Ordâkh. If you want an alliance, you will need to prove yourselves to us.\
\
'It is simple. Help the Beltáni, and we will help you.'","Complete quests in Ahâba (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Befriending the Beltáni","Completed quests in Ahâba (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'It seems you are being put to work! Apologies, friend!\
\
'While you are helping the locals, we will negotiate with Unusâli. Ahâba would be a perfect staging area for our soldiers to gather, but I will not force anything upon the Beltáni if they are unwilling to join our fight.'","Talk to Unusâli"},
[1676]={"Habla con Lithuifin en las Agujas de la Linde","Titanes aturdidos","Ayuda a Remmenylf en Amon Môth","Ayuda a Lithuifin en Amon Môth","Los elfos tienen alguna idea de cómo aliviar el dolor de Ramalarga.","Ayuda a Erchiel en Amon Môth","'Juuum-jom... los hombres vestidos con pieles de lobo ya no son una preocupación, eso dicen los de cabellos sedosos. Les creo, juuum. Los árboles en la cima de la montaña ya no me llaman... han vuelto a su letargo.\
\
'Sin embargo, los árboles del sur, jom, gritan de agonía. Piden ayuda. Hombres grandes, hombres gigantes, casi tan altos como Ramalarga, juuum, arrancan los árboles del suelo. Puedo sentir su agonía.'","Lithuifin está en las Agujas de la Linde.\
\
Lithuifin tiene un plan para expulsar a los gigantes para siempre.","Los gigantes que acampan en las orillas occidentales del lago son nuevos en Evendim.","'Todos los preparativos están listos. Ahora, los expulsaremos para siempre.'","'Hombres de verde, gente elfa, hombres vestidos como lobos, hombres gigantes... hay casi tantos tipos de hombres como de árboles.'"},
[1677]={"Return to Dabôr the Breaker in Hulzidâr and inform him of Umâr's demise and the recovery of the journal.","Deep within Harkhaphâr, the Nêpharai are led by Umâr. Seek him out and defeat him.","Locate Umâr within Harkhaphâr and defeat him.","Return to Dabôr the Breaker in Hulzidâr and present him with the journal","Defeat Umâr","'This journal is most disturbing. It seems that Umâr was not working alone, and was in fact sponsored to lead this revolt. I fear that The Storm may have more enemies throughout the court than he realizes. I will pass this journal along. Your hard work has put Hulzidâr on secure footing for a good deal of time.'","Behead the Snake","'Your work thus far in fighting the Nêpharai has been instrumental to our survival. The leader of the Nêpharai, Umâr organized and led the revolt, and was personally responsible for the death of a number of the refugees. His leadership endangers our people, and he must pay for what he has done.\
\
'Seek him out and dispatch him for his misdeeds.'","When Umâr falls, he leaves behind a small bound journal"},
[1678]={"Talk to Dagoras at Echad Dagoras","'My captain, Dagoras, went to visit a small encampment to the south-west of here that the Dunlendings call Lhe Lhechu. It seems that a number of the Dunlendings who were sent to fight in Eregion have since deserted and retreated back here. It was Dagoras' hope that we might be able to strike some kind of bargain with the deserters, given their obviously questionable loyalty to Isengard, but he has been gone for nearly a day now with no word.\
\
'Dagoras is a cautious man, but his strength lies in wit and cunning, more than might. If the deserters have indeed captured him he may need a hand.\
\
'Try and find some sign of him down there and free him if he is captured. We will need a man of his experience and skills once we reach Rohan!'","'If you find Dagoras, bring him back here, ${PLAYER}.'","Braigiar's companion Dagoras has been captured by the Dunlending deserters after going to negotiate an agreement with them.","'Ah, you have my thanks, friend ${PLAYER}. I was not looking forward to ending my days in some Dunlending cell. Soon, we will forge on to join with the rest of our kinsmen.'","'Braigiar will have some choice words for me, I am certain, for he advised me against parleying with the Dunlendings. First, however, we must escape this place, which means we will need a key....'","Tras las rejas","Rescue Dagoras from Lhe Lhechu","'Were you able to find Dagoras, my friend?'","Dagoras is being held in Lhe Lhechu, south-west of Echad Dagoras.\
\
You must free Dagoras and escort him from the Dunlending camp.","'${PLAYER}! Never did I think to find you here! It has been long since Esteldín, but we will have to reminisce later.\
\
'I came here to try and negotiate with these deserters, thinking they might not have much in common with the forces from Isengard after being abandoned to their fate in Eregion, but they had other ideas.\
\
'In any case, it seems these folk are not open to parley. They have been betrayed with too many false promises. Release me, and let us return to my camp.'","Dagoras ia at Echad Dagoras, north-east of Lhe Lhechu.\
\
You should speak with Dagoras at his encampment."},
[1679]={"Explora la cascada del sur","Explora la cascada del noroeste","'¡Cielos, estás ${PLAYERNAME:empapado[m]|empapada[f]}! Pero no te ahogaste, buen trabajo. ¿Y qué es eso que tienes ahí?'\
\
Le entregas el jarrón roto.\
\
'¡Pero mira eso! ¿Cuántos años tendrá, me pregunto? ¿Y encontraste también un esqueleto? ¡Oh, no puedo esperar para contarles a todos mis amigos sobre los descubrimientos que yo... eh, es decir, que nosotros... hemos hecho! ¡Gracias!'","Lleva la alfarería a Drudwen","Explora la cascada del sudeste","Este esqueleto parece demasiado grande para ser de un hobbit","Las cascadas en el tranquilo pueblo de Clegur y sus alrededores pueden ocultar secretos.","Explora la cascada detrás del puente","La cascada atronadora no te permitirá avanzar más","Drudwen te ha pedido que explores las cascadas en Clegur y sus alrededores.\
\
Clegur se encuentra en el suroeste de la Ciénaga de los Cisnes.","Nada más que rocas y agua atronadora","¡Un esqueleto yace sobre las rocas cercanas!","'Hola. ¡Tienes pinta de que te gustan las aventuras! Justo el tipo de persona que necesito. ¿Has notado todas las cascadas alrededor de Clegur? Siento una curiosidad infinita por lo que podría haber detrás de ellas.\
\
'Lamentablemente, no sé nadar. ¿Tú sabes nadar? ¿Quizás podrías explorar las cascadas por mí y decirme qué encuentras?'","Explora la cascada del este","Las rocas sobresalen detrás de la cascada rugiente","Explora la cascada del noreste","Has encontrado una pieza de alfarería antigua","Las rocas afiladas parecen ser lo único que hay aquí","Detrás de las Cascadas","Deberías informar a Drudwen con la alfarería y las noticias del esqueleto que encontraste detrás de las cascadas.\
\
Drudwen se encuentra en el pueblo de Clegur, en el sur de la Ciénaga de los Cisnes."},
[1680]={"Entrega el regalo a Frodo en Rivendel","'¿Ya encontraste a mi querido primo, ${PLAYER}? Es importante que lo hagas antes de que termine nuestro cumpleaños.'","Frodo Bolsón y su primo Bilbo -- aunque lo llama tío -- comparten el mismo cumpleaños, pero no han podido celebrarlo juntos durante diecisiete años.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000> NOTA: Esta misión se eliminará de tu bitácora de misiones cuando termine el festival actual. </rgb>","Cumpleaños tardío","'¿Eh? ¿Sí? ¿Puedo ayudarte en algo?'","'Ah, sí que disfrutó del regalo, ¡espléndido! Y aquí estoy, haciéndote llevar regalos para otros sin pensar de ti. ¡${PLAYERNAME:Un maravilloso[m]|Una maravillosa[f]}  si es que alguna vez he conocido a ${PLAYERNAME:uno[m]|una[f]}!\
\
'Creo que tengo algo aquí para ti. No es gran cosa, solo una baratija. Un pequeño juguete, en realidad. Vaya, recuerdo el día en que repartía estos en mi cumpleaños número ciento once, hace menos de diecisiete años... pero estoy volviendo a las viejas historias.\
\
'Gracias por tu ayuda, .'","'¿Qué es esto? ¿Un regalo de Frodo por nuestro cumpleaños? Bueno, qué curioso, ¡porque yo también pensaba darle un regalo al joven Frodo! Desde que llegué a Rivendel tengo la tradición de dar regalos a los Elfos en mi cumpleaños. No entienden muy bien la costumbre, pero siempre aceptan los regalos con gratitud. ¡Qué gente tan maravillosa son los Elfos!\
\
'Siempre guardo un regalo para Frodo y, de hecho, ¡lo he estado llevando conmigo durante unos días! Probablemente lo habría olvidado si no me lo hubieras recordado.\
\
'Llévale mi regalo, por favor; a menudo se preocupa y tal vez le alegre el ánimo.'","Frodo Bolsón está en la habitación de Bilbo en la planta baja de la Última Morada, en Rivendel.\
\
Bilbo Bolsón te ha pedido que le lleves un regalo de cumpleaños a Frodo a cambio.","'Hazle saber al tío Bilbo que aprecio su regalo.'","'Espero sinceramente que Frodo disfrute de mi regalo.'","Bilbo Bolsón está en el Salón del Fuego en la Última Morada, en Rivendel.\
\
Frodo Bolsón te ha pedido que le des las gracias a Bilbo por su regalo.","'Hola, me preguntaba si podrías dedicarme un momento. Mi tío Bilbo y yo compartimos cumpleaños, el veintidós de septiembre, y lo he celebrado con una pequeña reunión en su honor cada año desde que se fue de Bolsón Cerrado. Aunque el día ya ha pasado, pensé que sería bonito regalarle algo al viejo bribón por nuestro cumpleaños.\
\
'Es un pequeño regalo, pero esperaba que pudieras llevárselo. Ahora no aceptaría un regalo mío -- diría, \\qNo está bien, Frodo, muchacho, al ya haber pasado nuestro cumpleaños,\\q pero tal vez no rechazaría el regalo si se lo entregara otra persona.\
\
'¿Harías esto por mí?'","'¿Bilbo aceptó el regalo después de todo? ¡Vaya, ha salido mejor de lo que esperaba!\
\
'¿Y qué es esto? ¿Un regalo para mí, de Bilbo? Ese hobbit está lleno de sorpresas.\
\
'Vuelve y dile muchas gracias, y que iré a visitarlo más tarde.'","Entrega el regalo a Bilbo Bolsón","Bilbo Bolsón está en el Salón del Fuego en la Última Morada en Rivendel.\
\
Frodo Bolsón te ha pedido que le entregues un regalo de cumpleaños atrasado a Bilbo.","'¿Le entregaste el regalo a Bilbo?'"},
[1681]={"'Excelente, ¡así que esto es todo! Déjeme echarle un vistazo....\
\
'Sí, interesante, interesante. ¡Maravilloso! Es una copia completa del Texto y está en mejor estado que la que ya está en la Casa de los Mathoms. Gracias por sus esfuerzos. Confío en que no haya sido demasiado difícil de conseguir, ¿verdad?'","'Bueno, ¿qué necesitas ahora? ¿Buscas más trabajo?'","'¿Belco no quería que yo tuviera esta copia del Texto fundacional? ¡Qué maleducado!'","'¿Has llevado el Texto fundacional a la Casa de los Mathoms? ¡No quiero que Adelard Tuk ponga sus manos sobre él, ya sabes!'","'Espero que Brombard haya quedado satisfecho con la copia del Texto fundacional de Belco.'","'Sí, supongo que ya has hecho bastante por mí. Sin embargo, voy a echar de menos la ayuda que me has prestado en la granja. Y parece que la vieja Sally se ha encariñado contigo, aunque quizá sea solo porque le traes comida.\
\
'Aquí tienes la copia del Texto fundacional que encontré entre las cosas de mi madre. Llévasela al guardián Colazorro en la Casa de los Mathoms en Cavada Grande.\
\
'Y asegúrate de no dársela a Adelard Tuk, no quiero que acabe en su colección.'","'¿Qué haces por aquí? ¿Buscas más trabajo? Si no es así, ¡lárgate! Lleva ese Texto al guardián Colazorro en Cavada Grande.'","Texto fundacional recuperado","Después de ayudarle en la granja, Belco Tejonera por fin le ha dado la copia del Texto fundacional de la Comarca que encontró entre las cosas de su madre.","'Es una pena que se haya perdido el Texto fundacional original, ¡pero esta copia que has traído es maravillosa!'","'¿Ha podido hacerse con la copia del Texto fundacional? ¡Estoy ansioso por echarle un vistazo!'","Lleva el Texto fundacional a Brombard Colazorro","'Gracias por traerme esa copia del Texto fundacional, ${PLAYERNAME:Frontero[m]|Frontera[f]}. ¡Es un hallazgo tremendo!'","El Texto de Belco","Recupera el Texto fundacional","Brombard Colazorro está en la Casa de los Mathoms en Cavada Grande.\
\
Satisfecho con sus servicios, Belco Tejonera le ha exhortado a llevar su copia del Texto fundacional directamente al guardián Brombard Colazorro. No quiere que este documento acabe en manos de Adelard Tuk.","'¡Maravilloso, tienes el Texto fundacional! Gracias por tu trabajo. Ahora, si no te importa, ¿podrías dárselo a Brombard Colazorro con mis saludos?'"},
[1682]={"You should return to Gaumar, who stands within the Great-keep in Dale.","Those discontented with the newly-arrived refugees have been leaving angry scrawls throughout Dale.","Bells of Wrath","Return to Gaumar","Remove angry scrawls (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You should find angry scrawls on walls and doors throughout Dale and remove them.","'The discontent of Dale-folk over the new-arrived refugees has not abated, ${PLAYER}. Now angry scrawls have begun appearing on walls and doors around Dale: a bell with arrows pointing away. The meaning is clear enough to us.\
\
'Will you help us wipe these defacements from Dale? Seeing a formidable and respected foreigner such as yourself doing so will strike respect - or shame - into our people's hearts.'","'Those angry scrawls are gone? Thank you, ${PLAYER}.'","'Please, ${PLAYER}, let yourself be seen wiping these hateful scrawls off the walls and doors of Dale.'","Removed angry scrawls (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[1683]={"'¿Has visto hasta dónde me lanzó ese enorme pez junto con todas mis cosas? Seguro que ahora ya me crees. ¡Voy a intentar atrapar a esa bestia, aunque sea lo último que haga!'","Has recuperado la capa","Has recuperado la caña de pescar","Mosco Madriguera se encuentra en el estanque de Delagua, esperando que regreses con sus pertenencias encontradas.\
\
Deberías devolverle sus pertenencias a Mosco.","Has recuperado la comida perdida","Encuentra la caña de pescar de Mosco","Encuentra la capa de Mosco","Mosco Madriguera asegura haber enganchado el pez más grande que había visto jamás, pero al ser arrastrado de un extremo del estanque al otro, perdió su equipo de pesca y otras pertenencias por el camino. ¡Y para colmo, el pez consiguió escapar!\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Esta misión se eliminará de tu registro de misiones cuando finalice el festival actual.</rgb>","'¿No me crees, eh? Espera a ver hasta dónde quedaron esparcidas mis cosas mientras me peleaba con ese pez. Todo está en la nota que te di.'","Encuentra la azada de Mosco","'Jamás creerás lo que me ha pasado hoy. Lo escribí todo en cuanto me recuperé, para asegurarme de no olvidar ni un solo detalle. ¿Estás preparado para oír esto? Bien.\
\
'Atrapé un pez gigante. Tan gigante que no cabría en mi madriguera si me lo llevara a casa para cenar.\
\
'No me crees, ¿verdad? Pues me arrastró por todas partes y perdí todo lo que tenía. ¿Cómo explicas eso, eh? Aprovecho para pedirte un gran favor: ¿podrías ayudarme a encontrar todas mis pertenencias? Aquí tienes el relato de mi día; quizá te dé pistas de dónde ha ido a parar mi equipo.'","Encuentra la comida de las once de Mosco","Lleva los objetos encontrados a Mosco Madriguera","Encuentra el cebo de la suerte de Mosco","Las pertenencias se fueron de pesca","Has recuperado la azada","Has recuperado el cebo de la suerte","Las pertenencias perdidas de Mosco están esparcidas por los alrededores del estanque y la zona cercana. Si lees la nota que te dio, quizá encuentres pistas sobre el paradero exacto de su equipo.\
\
Deberías reunir las pertenencias perdidas de Mosco y devolvérselas."},
[1684]={"The Dáinlik can be found in the Ironfold.\
\
You should look out over the top of the Dáinlik.","The Dáinlik can be found in the Ironfold.\
\
You should investigate the base of the Dáinlik.","The strange creature has been defeated","'So there was something there?! I knew that we were not going mad!\
\
'You must tell Náin of what you saw! How are we to complete the Dáinlik with these beasts lurking in the rock?!'","This is a good place to <rgb=#FF0000>look</rgb> out over the Dáinlik","Rísti Graver can be found atop of the Dáinlik.\
\
You should talk to Rísti Graver.","Workers at the Dáinlik have seen shadowy things in the hills.","Talk to Rísti Graver","'It is difficult to work and to stay on schedule here at the Dáinlik. Each day I hear reports from my workers that they feel as if they are being watched. Some even speak of shadowy thing in the hills. I myself, thought I saw something today, at the base of the axe. Perhaps that would be as good a place as any to start. You must get to the bottom of this!'","Nothing seems odd below, perhaps a closer inspection of the Dáinlik's base is in order","A shadowy creature attacks from a small crevasse at the base of the axe!","Investigate the base of the Dáinlik","Below the Dáinlik","<rgb=#FF0000>Look</rgb> out from atop the Dáinlik"},
[1685]={"One of Arcah's ravens can be found at the Rushgate.\
\
After speaking with the raven, Dori has learned that the other two ravens sent from Ravenhill have not returned. You should search for one of the ravens near the Rushgate.","'Just a moment, ${PLAYER}!'\
\
Dori asks the raven if it has seen any sign of Nori or his expedition. The raven croaks and chitters in answer. All of a sudden, the raven spreads its wings and looses a shrill cry.\
\
'I understand, friend.'\
\
Dori turns his gaze to you.\
\
'These are not glad tidings, ${PLAYER}. Nori is nowhere to be found, and two of the three ravens sent to search for my brother have become lost in the Grey Mountains. One flew for the Rushgate far to the north-west, and the other... the other may have gone to Thikil-gundu. And that is not the half of it! The ravens have spied black-arrows of Gundabad lying in wait beyond the forest, and they have fletched their arrows with the feathers of ravens! It is also said they are practised in the art of stealth, but I have not known many Orcs to possess such patience. If we are to reach Thikil-gundu, we shall have to remain on guard.\
\
'Ride to the Rushgate along the Men Angrún and search for the lost raven. If you encounter any of those black-arrows, defeat them and reclaim the feathers they have stolen. Such an insult cannot go unanswered!\
\
'When you have reached the Rushgate, turn back and ride to meet us along the road to Thikil-gundu. Our journey draws near to its end, ${PLAYER}. Let us not falter at so late an hour!'","The slain, frozen raven can be found on the ground before Stánbalk, the Stone Wall.\
\
You have found the frozen remains of a raven before Stánbalk, the Stone Wall. You should examine it.","The broken form of a raven lies frozen on the ground before Stánbalk...","'Ah, ${PLAYER}!\
\
'Did you encounter the Orcs of Gundabad as well? Several harried us in our travels, but they were soon defeated. Give me the feathers you have recovered, and when at last we return to Erebor, I shall deliver them to Arcah myself!\
\
'Two of the ravens are now found, but one remains lost. Though it is now broken and ruined, the great Stone Wall before us, Stánbalk, long stood in defence of Thikil-gundu. If Arcah forbade her people from venturing too near to the Steel Keep, they would have flown no further than Stánbalk.\
\
'While the others and I take rest, I would ask that you search for the lost raven among the ruins of Stánbalk. \
\
'Be careful, ${PLAYER}. I fear Vethúg was not the last of his kind in the Grey Mountains!'","Find the lost raven near Thikil-gundu","Dori and Company have stopped upon an overlook before Thikil-gundu...","Without so much as a croak, the raven takes flight...","Dori can be found on a hilltop overlooking Stánbalk, the Stone Wall of Thikil-gundu.\
\
You have found Dori and Company along the road to Thikil-gundu. You should now speak to Dori.","Found and defeated Gundabad black-arrows (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","After discovering one of Arcah's ravens near to Óinsbridge, Dori and Company must now deal with unexpected threats if they are to make it to Thikil-gundu.","Search for the lost raven near the Rushgate","One of Arcah's ravens can be found at the Rushgate.\
\
You have found the raven at the Rushgate. You should now follow the road to Thikil-gundu to the east and rejoin Dori and Company.","Dori can be found somewhere along the road to Thikil-gundu.\
\
The raven has flown from the Rushgate. You should now find Dori and Company along the road to Thikil-gundu.","Find and defeat Gundabad black-arrows (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Gundabad black-arrows can be found along the Men Angrún, especially as it nears the Rushgate.\
\
The raven told Dori that cruel archers of Gundabad have been taking ravens' feathers for their arrows. You should defeat them and take their arrows.","'Are you all right, ${PLAYER}? Even a cold-drake as young as that one poses a great threat!\
\
'Did you find the lost raven?'\
\
You tell Dori that the lost raven was seemingly slain by a cold-drake.\
\
'When the raven did not fly to answer the call of its kin, I feared it so. Though I did not wish to believe it, I knew in my heart what fate must have befallen it.'\
\
Dori casts a sorrowful glance to the ravens, and shakes his head.\
\
'So this is the way of the Grey Wrack....'","Beneath Watchful Eyes","Talk to Dori on the road to Thikil-gundu","Examine the frozen raven, but remain on guard","Dori can be found on a hilltop overlooking Stánbalk, the Stone Wall of Thikil-gundu.\
\
You have learned that one of Arcah's ravens was slain by a cold-drake. You should return to Dori.","Deliver the raven-fletched arrows to Dori on the road to Thikil-gundu","A noticeably-agitated raven perches atop the crumbled stones of the Rushgate...","The raven perches silently....","You notice the raven's feathers are matted and frozen, but your attention is soon drawn skyward...","Direct the raven to fly to Dori and Company along the road to Thikil-gundu","The lost raven can be found somewhere near Stánbalk, the Stone Wall.\
\
Dori has asked you to seek the raven that flew near to Thikil-gundu.","Follow the road to Thikil-gundu and and find Dori and Company"},
[1687]={"Search the path to the ruins of Hadhodiant","Search the Old Ford","Examinar al orco muerto.","The road into the Beorning-lands can be found by following the road north from Hultvís.\
\
You found no sign of Hárskor or that he crossed the Old Ford. You should continue to follow the road north toward the Beorning-lands and search for Hárskor at the path to the ruins of Hadhodiant.","'Well?'\
\
You introduce yourself to Ríkmar and explain that you have not been sent by Grimbeorn with provisions, but instead to search for a Beorning named Hárskor who was thought to have arrived in Hultvís some days ago.\
\
'I am sorry, ${PLAYER}. Hultvís has suffered greatly since the end of the war and many mouths have gone unfed to preserve what little rations we have left. Even so, I won't abandon the skin-changers. Many of their kind fought and died to protect us against the Orcs, and the Woodmen will aid them in return. If Grimbeorn sent Hárskor on his errand, he has either become lost or some trouble has found him under the eaves of the forest. Alas, it is not the way of the skin-changers to lose the path in the vales. What has become of him? And what has become of the provisions he bore?\
\
'It is curious that Grimbeorn chose to send you instead of one of his kin. He does not often entrust such matters to outsiders. Perhaps he sees something of himself in you!\
\
'Here, let me mark your map. If Hárskor met with some trouble on the road to Hultvís, you must find him!'","Search the crossway to the old forest road","The slain Orc can be found on the side of the road through Woodsedge near the path to the ruins of Hadhodiant.\
\
You have discovered the mauled remains of an Orc near the path to the ruins of Hadhodiant. You should examine its corpse before continuing your search.","His hair matted with black blood, Hárskor looms over a group of slain Orcs","The source of the scent can be found somewhere around the crossway to the old forest road.\
\
You searched the crossway to the old forest road as Ríkmar suggested, but found no sign of Hárskor. However, you notice a curious scent lingering in the air.","The Old Ford can be found far to the north-west of Hultvís.\
\
You found no sign of Hárskor at the crossway, but you learned that Orcs are trapping the roads in Woodsedge. You should continue to the next location that Ríkmar marked on your map: the Old Ford.","A honey-cake? As you pause to examine it, a sudden rustling betrays an ambush!","Ríkmar of the Woodmen has grown fearful that Hárskor and the provisions he bore have fallen into the hands of Orcs still lurking in Woodsedge.","Find the source of the scent at the crossway","You find no sign of Hárskor, but the scent of honey lingers in the air...","Follow the path to the ruins of Hadhodiant","The mauled Orc has been rent by countless claw marks and deep gashes","'Who are you and why do you stand before me? Speak quickly, or you will know the wrath of the line of Beorn!'","Hárskor can be found at the ruins of Hadhodiant.\
\
You have found Hárskor alive, if battle-weary, at the ruins of Hadhodiant. You should speak to him and learn what has happened.","You find no evidence that a waggon has passed across the Old Ford...","Beneath the Eaves","Talk to Hárskor at the ruins of Hadhodiant","The path to the ruins of Hadhodiant can be found in north-west Woodsedge.\
\
You discovered a slain Orc at the foot of the path to the ruins of Hadhodiant. Its wounds were deep and not unlike those made by a skin-changer. You should follow the path to the ruins of the old bridge and search for Hárskor.","You notice a slain Orc lying on the side of the road","The crossway to the old forest road can be found by following the road to the north of Hultvís.\
\
Ríkmar has suggested that you begin your search for Hárskor at the crossway to the old forest road."},
[1688]={"Nothing seems amiss as workers continue their efforts to clear debris","The shrieking ceases","Habla con Náin","Rísti Graver can be found at the Dáinlik in the Ironfold, while Aflur Smokebeard can be found at Hammerstead in the Ironfold.\
\
You should talk to Rísti Graver and Aflur Smokebeard.","'It would seem the mines are no longer safe. I will call back all dwarves at once.\
\
'I knew this day would come, though a part of me did not want to believe it. Rukhûsh-minam!'","Complete Below the Dáinlik","Investigate the eastern mine entrance","Talk to Rísti Graver","Investigate the entrances to the mine within Járnfast.","Investigate the southern mine entrance","Whispers through the Ironfold speak of rumblings beneath the ground and strange shadows lurking just out of sight.","Shrieking sounds surround you as a nameless beast leaps over the palisade","Complete Rumblings at Hammerstead","Talk to Aflur Smokebeard","'You have returned, and I see the look upon your face is one that carries dire news. Shadowy nameless things, lurking in the Iron Hills?! What could have caused this?!\
\
'We must scout the mining entrances in Járnfast immediately!'","'Oh, Náin finally sent someone! It has been difficult to stay on schedule here. You would not believe what I and my workers have seen!'","Beneath the Fold","'${PLAYER}, I must speak with you. Ever since the Iron Hills shook and caused damage to Járnfast, I have heard strange stories. Aye, I have not paid mind to these tales of rumblings from beneath the ground and strange shadows lurking just out of sight. It would seem that I can not ignore these stories any longer.\
\
'On this day I have received similar notes of concern from both Hammerstead and the Dáinlik. I hope it is nothing more than a coincidence, ${PLAYER}. Please speak with Rísti Graver at the Dáinlik and Aflur Smokebeard at Hammerstead. Find out what it is they are concerned over and report back to me. I do not have time to dwell on this further, but I can not ignore these trusted dwarves.'","Náin can be found in Járnfast.\
\
You should return to Náin.","'Náin sent you? My friend, Easterlings are the least of our worries at Hammerstead. If only I knew what exactly it is that we should be worried about!'"},
[1689]={"Ted Abrojos se encuentra al este de Combe.\
\
Ted Abrojos te envió a recuperar el botín de su padre de debajo del Árbol de la Horca, pero descubriste que el árbol, entre otros, fue talado por los leñadores de Combe. Cavaste en varios lugares del campo, pero no encontraste señales del tesoro enterrado de Abrojos.","'¿Qué? ¿Derribaron el Árbol de la Horca? ¿Y cavaste en todos los tocones con una X? ¡Esto es terrible! ¿Cómo voy a encontrar ahora el tesoro enterrado de mi padre?'","'¿Dónde está la piqueta?'","Encuentra el Árbol de la Horca","Aunque no hay forma de saber cuál tocón fue alguna vez el Árbol de la Horca, no estaría mal cavar cerca de algunos tocones en busca del tesoro.","El Árbol de la Horca está junto a la orilla del río al sur del puesto de la condestable Wren, al sureste de Combe.\
\
El padre de Ted Abrojos fue un ladrón en el bosque de Chet y supuestamente acumuló una gran riqueza. Ted cree que las ganancias mal habidas de su padre están enterradas al pie del Árbol de la Horca, que debería estar marcado con una X.","El bosque ha sido despejado","'¿Todos los árboles han sido talados? Quizá la X siga ahí. Por favor, busca si puedes encontrar un árbol con la marca. ¡Quizá tengamos suerte y encontremos el tesoro de mi padre!'","Ted Abrojos se ha quedado casi sin dinero y en una situación desesperada. Sin embargo, el rumor sobre la riqueza robada de su padre le ha dado algo de esperanza.","'¡Mi viejo padre fue un ladrón hace años y, según escuché, consiguió muchas riquezas! El condestable lo atrapó, pero antes de que lo ahorcaran, ¡mi padre me dijo dónde enterró su botín! Nunca lo necesité hasta ahora, así que lo dejé enterrado. Pero creo que es hora de conseguir \\qriqueza suficiente para mantenerte abrigado y calzado,\\q como decía mi querido padre. ¿Puedes tomar esta piqueta y desenterrar el tesoro?\
\
'Solo toma el camino al este desde Combe hasta el puesto de la condestable Wren junto a la casa de guardia. Sube la colina a la derecha y baja hasta la orilla del río, donde crece el Árbol de la Horca; tendrá una X tallada.\
\
'¡Me estarás ayudando a empezar de nuevo y tendrás mi eterno agradecimiento!'","'Hay muchos otros árboles alrededor del Árbol de la Horca. En aquellos días había más ahorcamientos y no querían que los niños vieran demasiado, así que los árboles cercanos ayudaban a ocultar las ejecuciones de los ojos jóvenes.\
\
'Toma el camino al este desde Combe y, en el puesto de la condestable Wren, dirígete al sur. El Árbol de la Horca está en la pendiente al sur de la casa de guardia, en la orilla del río. Lo reconocerás por la X tallada en él.'","No encuentras nada de interés cerca de este tocón","Bajo el Árbol de la Horca","Cava cerca de los tocones en el campo de tocones (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Lleva la piqueta de vuelta a Ted Abrojos"},
[1691]={"Habla con Hundi en Echad Dúnann","Tras un viaje de muchas leguas, has llegado a los Muros de Moria. ¿Cómo reaccionarán los enanos ante tu llegada repentina? No fueron especialmente amistosos con Beorn ni con nadie de su estirpe.","Beórnida: La llegada repentina","'Ah, llevas tu herencia con orgullo, ¡si me perdonas el juego de palabras! Eres de la estirpe de Beorn, y no tiene sentido negarlo.\
\
'¿Has recorrido todo este camino mirando siempre hacia adelante y nunca hacia atrás? Admirable, pero si hemos de recuperar la tierra de mis padres, ¡necesitaremos que muestres tu lado más temible! Habla con Hundi en el campamento de Echad Dúnann y se asegurará de que estés ${PLAYERNAME:preparado[m]|preparada[f]}.'","Hundi se encuentra en el campamento de Echad Dúnann, fuera de los Muros de Moria, en Eregion.","'Habla con Hundi en el campamento de Echad Dúnann, ${PLAYER}. Él te preparará para lo que te espera.'","'¿Ráthwald te envió a verme? No sé por qué, ¡pues a mí me pareces lo bastante ${PLAYERNAME:preparado[m]|preparada[f]}!\
\
'Nuestros pueblos no siempre se han llevado bien, pero si puedes ayudarnos a recuperar Khazad-dûm, ¡quizás eso cambie!'"},
[1693]={"Vuelve a ver al rascacuevas hambriento","Este rascacuevas parece hambriento. Deberías recoger bayas para él.","Bayas recogidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","El rascacuevas parece menos hambriento.","Recoge bayas en el campo de tesoros para el rascacuevas hambriento.","recoge bayas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Bayas","Recoge bayas para el rascacuevas hambriento.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000> NOTA: Esta misión será eliminada de tu registro de misiones cuando termine el festival en curso. </rgb>","El rascacuevas todavía parece hambriento."},
[1694]={"Bingo está en Forlaw, al oeste del Salón de los Festines de Forlaw.","'¿Sabes ese Hombre inusual que aparece por todas partes en nuestro viaje? Sí, Bert Bartolín, ¡ese mismo! Me pidió enviarte a verlo por un asunto pequeño, pero olvidé transmitirte el mensaje. Será mejor que vayas con él de inmediato, ¡si no es tarde ya! Está justo allí al sur, junto a los establos.'","'Espera un momento, ${PLAYER:amigo mío[m]|amiga mía[f]}. Recuérdame cómo describiste al sabio desaparecido.'\
\
Repites la descripción que escuchaste del guardia de la puerta oeste, y Bert asiente, reconociéndola.\
\
'¡Conozco a ese hombre, ${PLAYER}! Se llama Hunfredo Rebuscón, y nos conocemos desde hace mucho. ¿Ves? ¡Los Rebuscón y los Bartolín eran vecinos! Nuestras casas estaban algo apartadas, así que podían pasar semanas sin ver a nadie más que a un Rebuscón o a un Bartolín. Podrías decir que eso desgasta la paciencia mutua.\
\
'Tras retirarme de la vida aventurera, una de mis primeras ventas fue a Hunfredo: le vendí la llave de las ruinas derrumbadas de Tollobel en la isla de Tyl Ruinen. Me pregunto si llegó a usarla.\
\
'Tendrás que encontrarlo y mantenerlo fuera de problemas. Los Rebuscón, y especialmente Hunfredo, nunca han sido buenos en evitar líos. Ese guardia vio que se fue por la puerta oeste, ¿no? Entonces seguramente siguió en esa dirección. Busca a Hunfredo en algún lugar al oeste de Forlaw. Si hay un asentamiento en esa dirección, probablemente fue hacia allí; Hunfredo es como una polilla curiosa hacia una llama en la noche... ¡como todos los Rebuscón!'","'¿En qué puedo ayudarte hoy, ${CLASS}?'\
\
Le dices al guardia que buscas a un sabio que llegó recientemente a Forlaw. El guardia resopla con rudeza.\
\
'Sí, lo vi. Tipo calvo, gran barba castaña, túnica sencilla; bastante corpulento. Ya se fue, ¡y me alegro! Me mostró algunas de sus mercancías, chatarra en su mayoría, ¡y uno de sus malditos lagartos me mordió el dedo! Mira, aún está rojo. Y tampoco recibí disculpas.'","Derrota tritones congelados al oeste de Dunfast (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Habla con el guardia de Forlaw en la puerta oeste","'La gente de Forlaw ha estado murmurando sobre un sabio que llegó recientemente al pueblo. Toma esta bolsa de monedas e intenta comprarle algunos pergaminos, tomos o pociones, ${PLAYER}. Oí que estaba cerca de la puerta oeste.'","Lleva los diversos artículos a Bert Bartolín en Forlaw","Bert Tiene una Palabra","'Gracias por encargarte de algunos de esos tritones. Eso quizá anime a la gente a regresar a este pueblo. O bien, ¡los tritones restantes podrían adueñarse del lugar! ¿No sería algo? Hmm... ¿qué te trae por aquí, ${CLASS}?'\
\
Le dices a Hunfredo que Bert Bartolín te envió con una bolsa de monedas para encontrarlo y comprar algunos pergaminos, tomos o pociones.\
\
'¡El señor Bartolín! Mira tú. Su familia y la mía eran vecinas, ¿sabes? Siempre había un alboroto viniendo de la casa de los Bartolín. ¡Crecer con catorce chicos hace eso! ¿Cómo están Bert y sus muchos, muchos hermanos?\
\
'Tomaré esta bolsa y te daré estos artículos. ¡Estoy seguro de que Bert encontrará algo a su gusto entre ellos!'","Habla con Hunfredo Rebuscón en la ciudad de Dunfast","El sabio fue visto por última vez cerca de la puerta oeste de Forlaw.\
\
Bert Bartolín te pidió encontrar al sabio que llegó a Forlaw y comprarle algunas pociones y pergaminos.","Bert Bartolín está junto a los establos de Forlaw, en las Tierras Feroces.\
\
Hunfredo tomó la bolsa de monedas que te dio Bert Bartolín y te entregó a cambio varios artículos.","'¡Hola, mi ${PLAYER:viajado amigo[m]|viajada amiga[f]}! Me alegra ser por fin parte de este viaje tuyo y de Bingo, ¡y espero no decepcionar! En mis días jóvenes fui todo un aventurero, pero esos tiempos quedaron atrás. La vida de mercader me sienta mejor que la de andar en búsquedas, estos días.\
\
'¿Sabes qué necesita un mercader por encima de todo? ¿Buen ánimo? Sí, ayuda. ¿Clientes? Por supuesto. ¿Sentido del humor? Nunca me ha fallado, cierto. Te lo diré directamente, .\
\
'¡Mercancías para vender o intercambiar! Sin reponer mis existencias, sería un pobre mercader. Mi buen amigo Rattlepacks tiene espacio para un poco más de carga, ¿no crees?\
\
'La gente de Forlaw murmura sobre un sabio que llegó recientemente al pueblo. Toma esta bolsa de monedas e intenta comprarle pergaminos, tomos o pociones, . Oí que estaba cerca de la puerta oeste.'","Hunfredo Rebuscón está en la ciudad abandonada de Dunfast, en las Tierras Feroces.","Tras un largo viaje, el enigmático Bert Bartolín finalmente ha decidido hablar contigo.","'¿Pudiste ayudar a Bert con lo que necesitaba, ${PLAYER}? ¡Excelente, me alegra!\
\
'Es sorprendente que hayamos visto al señor Bartolín en tantos lugares durante este viaje, y apenas había dicho nada hasta ahora. ¿Dónde habrá aprendido tal paciencia? En mis tiempos conocí a uno o dos hobbits así, ¡siempre los hermanos menores! Quizá Bert creció con varios hermanos mayores y aprendió paciencia en su hogar. ¡Es un individuo único, sin duda!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Siguiente semana: 'Identidad Equivocada' (Nivel recomendado: 90)</rgb>","'Ese sabio ya se fue, ¡y mejor así! Me mostró algunas de sus mercancías, en su mayoría chatarra, y uno de sus malditos lagartos me mordió el dedo. Mira, aún está rojo. Y tampoco recibí una disculpa.'","Hunfredo Rebuscón provocó una plaga de tritones congelados al pie de las montañas al oeste de Dunfast.","El guardia de la puerta nota que miras alrededor y te llama","Bert Bartolín está junto a los establos de Forlaw, en las Tierras Feroces.","'De todas formas, gracias por ocuparte de Hunfredo, ${PLAYER}.'","Habla con Bingo en la ciudad de Forlaw","'Ah, pareces ${PLAYERNAME:un aventurero[m]|una aventurera[f]} bastante impresionante. ¿${PLAYERNAME:un[m]|una[f]} ? ¡Lo sabía! Yo mismo soy uno de los grandes sabios del mundo. Me llamo Hunfredo Rebuscón. Tu rostro me resulta familiar, pero como nunca olvido una cara, diré que es un placer conocerte por primera vez, !\
\
'Tengo afición por los lagartos pequeños de todo tipo, y habilidad para devolverlos a la salud. ¡Un don que debo compartir con el mundo! Por eso, cuando vi un grupo de huevos junto a un pilar de hielo gigante, naturalmente los calenté para que eclosionaran. Naturalmente.\
\
'Bueno... resulta que estos pequeños tritones no toleran a la gente, ni a los animales, ni a las plantas... Creo que ahuyentaron a los habitantes de este pueblo, porque no queda nadie. Será mejor que hagas algo con esos tritones, . Están en los bosques al oeste, al pie de las montañas. Y por favor, llámalos \\qtritones\\q. Así los llaman todos los grandes sabios.'","Encuentra al sabio en la puerta oeste de Forlaw","'Creo que ya es hora de dejar atrás estas tierras nevadas. Me alegrará hacerlo, ¡pues este frío me ha calado hasta los huesos! ¡Brrr!'\
\
Bingo tiembla exageradamente y de pronto exclama sorprendido.\
\
'¡Oh no! ${PLAYER}, acabo de recordar algo que debía decirte, pero este frío lo borró completamente de mi mente. ¡Mis pensamientos deben estar congelados! ¿Sabes ese Hombre tan peculiar que aparece en todas partes en este viaje? Sí, Bert Bartolín, ¡ese mismo! Pues bien, me pidió enviarte a verlo por un asunto menor, pero olvidé darte el mensaje. Será mejor que vayas con él enseguida, ¡si no es demasiado tarde! Está justo allí al sur, junto a los establos.'","'Será mejor que hagas algo con esos tritones, ${CLASS}. Están en los bosques al oeste, al pie de las montañas. Y llámalos \\qtritones,\\q por favor. Así los llaman todos los grandes sabios.'","Habla con Bert Bartolín en Forlaw","'¿Encontraste a Hunfredo y lo salvaste de un aprieto causado por él mismo? Eso es muy típico de un Rebuscón, , ¡y exactamente lo que esperaba! Veo que le compraste algunos artículos. Déjame verlos.'\
\
Bert revisa la pequeña colección de objetos.\
\
'Ah, no hay nada de interés. Qué lástima. Bueno, tomaré las monedas que queden y... ¿qué? ¿Le diste toda la bolsa de dinero? Esperaba algunas monedas de vuelta, , ¡especialmente por este montón de nada!\
\
'No te preocupes, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo mío[m]|amiga mía[f]}. ¡No estoy enfadado! En verdad, Hunfredo puede haber salido ganando en este intercambio, pero hace muchos años yo le di unas pocas monedas y él me dio una criatura que se volvió mi amigo más querido. Diría que en ese intercambio nosotros salimos ganando frente al señor Rebuscón, ¿no es así, Rattlepacks?'","'¡Ha sido un placer hacer negocios contigo, ${CLASS}!¡Estoy seguro de que Bert encontrará algo de su gusto entre esos artículos!'","Encuentra a Hunfredo Rebuscón en algún lugar al oeste de Forlaw","Trinotes congelados derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Hunfredo Rebuscón partió de Forlaw hacia el oeste, y Bert Bartolín te ha pedido seguirle la pista.","El sabio se ha ido. Deberías regresar con Bert para informarle.","'Ese guardia vio a Hunfredo salir por la puerta oeste. Entonces seguramente siguió en esa dirección. Encuentra a Hunfredo en algún lugar al oeste de Forlaw. Si hay un asentamiento allí, es probable que se haya dirigido hacia él; Hunfredo es como una polilla curiosa hacia la llama de una antorcha, ¡y todos los Rebuscón también!'","'Ese sabio se fue hacia el oeste desde aquí, ¡y bien que se vaya! Todavía me duele el dedo donde me mordió su lagarto.\
\
'Hay una ciudad al oeste, Dunfast. Puede que ese fastidio haya ido allí a molestar a la gente, si es que queda alguien.'","Bert Bartolín está junto a los establos de Forlaw, en las Tierras Feroces.\
\
Bingo te dijo que Bert Bartolín quería hablar contigo.","Habla con Bert Bartolín en la ciudad de Forlaw","Uno de los guardias de la puerta oeste de Forlaw te ha llamado."},
[1695]={"Encuentra a Berto, Tom y Guille","'Ah, así que eso fue lo que les ocurrió a esos viejos trolls. Me alegra haber oído la historia, ${PLAYER}, ¡y gracias por traer la noticia! Es bueno saber que Berto, Tom y Guille tuvieron un final desdichado después de lo que hicieron al pueblo de mis abuelos.\
\
'Te lo agradezco, y acepta también esto.'","Has encontrado los restos pétreos de tres poderosos trolls de piedra.","Los abuelos de Garbert fueron expulsados de su aldea hace muchos años por tres trolls merodeadores, y Garbert quiere saber qué fue de aquellos villanos.","'Si buscas a quien derrotó a Berto, Tom y Guille| —tres trolls que deberían haber pasado más tiempo pensando y menos discutiendo— ¡lo has encontrado!\
\
'Pero la historia debe contarla otro; busca al saqueador Bilbo en el Salón del Fuego. Él conoce el relato mejor que nadie, y si minimiza su propio papel, es solo por modestia.'","Garbert vive en su cabaña en Tâl Bruinen, a orillas del río.\
\
Has descubierto qué fue de los trolls Bert, Tom y Bill y has visitado la arboleda donde fueron convertidos en piedra. Deberías regresar con la noticia a Garbert.","'Garbert no deja de hablar de los trolls que expulsaron a sus abuelos de su aldea. Si pudieras descubrir cómo terminaron y la historia de su caída, quizás por fin dejaría de contarlo.'","'Es bueno saber que esos trolls tuvieron un mal final.'","'Berto, Tom y Guille no volverán a molestarnos, y es un alivio.'","Encuentra a alguien que conozca el destino de Berto, Tom y Guille","'Ese Bilbo suena como un gran héroe, ¿no es verdad? Me pregunto qué más habrá escrito en su libro.'","'¡Jamás olvidaré a Bert, Tom y Bill!'","'Los trolls probablemente terminaron su historia en algún lugar del Bosque de los Trolls. No sé quién podría conocer el relato de su final, pero si das con alguien que lo sepa, te lo agradeceré.'","'¿Berto, Tom y Guille, dices? ¡Cielos! Sí, sí, los conozco, y más que eso: ¡una vez me invitaron a cenar! Bueno, digo \\qinvitaron\\q, pero eso no es del todo cierto. Digamos más bien que me invité yo mismo, aunque meter la mano en la bolsa de un troll no es tan fácil como parece, y si te descubren, ¡bien pueden cocinarte!\
\
'Yo estaba allí con los enanos, y como no regresaba de mi pequeña incursión, vinieron a ver qué ocurría. No pasó mucho tiempo antes de que los trolls los capturaran a todos, y empezaran a debatir la mejor manera de cocinarnos y comernos. Por suerte, Gandalf llegó —como suele hacerlo cuando más se le necesita— y los trolls discutieron tanto que, cuando salió el sol, quedaron convertidos en piedra. Así terminó todo. Lo he escrito en mi libro, pero vivirlo es muy diferente de leerlo.\
\
'Si quieres visitar a los viejos Berto, Tom y Guille, los encontrarás en las tierras salvajes del Bosque de los Trolls, fuera del camino.'","Berto, Tom y Guille","'Hace muchos años, mis abuelos vivían en una aldea tranquila no muy lejos de aquí. Era un lugar pacífico y eran muy felices, pero un día tres monstruosos trolls de piedra llegaron al pueblo y causaron gran destrucción. Mis abuelos huyeron, y con el tiempo mi abuelo construyó esta cabaña aquí, en la ribera del Bruinen. Su hijo vivió con ellos en la cabaña, y más tarde yo nací aquí.\
\
'Crecí y me casé, y cuando mis padres murieron, me dejaron la cabaña; Afanen y yo hemos vivido aquí desde entonces. Siempre me he preguntado qué habrá sido de aquellos tres trolls: Berto, Tom y Guille se llamaban, y sus nombres aún me ponen la piel de gallina.\
\
'Estoy seguro de que debieron de acabar mal, siendo trolls, pero si puedes encontrar dónde terminaron y descubrir la historia de su final, estaría muy agradecido de oírla.'","Los trolls que aterrorizaron la aldea donde vivieron los abuelos de Garbert seguramente encontraron su final en algún lugar de las tierras salvajes del Bosque de los Trolls. Garbert vive en una cabaña junto al río en Tâl Bruinen.\
\
Garbert te ha pedido que encuentres el lugar donde los tres trolls de los que habló encontraron su final y que descubras la historia de su caída."},
[1697]={"'¡Ese Wéthorm ha estado divirtiéndose a mi costa, si me preguntas! Bueno, ¡nosotros también nos divertiremos un poco y veremos si le gusta!\
\
'Voy a necesitar tu ayuda, ${PLAYER}. Voy a \\qmejorar\\q el guiso de sapo añadiéndole partes de gusano, y tú se lo llevarás a Wéthorm. Dile que hice algunos cambios al guiso y que ahora está aún mejor. ¡Ah, esta vez la última risa será la nuestra, mi querido ${RACE}!\
\
'Reúne algunas patas y mandíbulas de gusanos y tráemelas, y pondremos mi plan en marcha. Encontrarás gusanos por todo Tâl Bruinen, ${PLAYER}, así que ¡empieza la caza!'","'La piedra de moler está justo ahí, ${PLAYER}. Tritura todas las partes de gusanos hasta hacerlas puré, ¡y luego podré añadirlas al guiso! ¡Le enseñaremos a Wéthorm a no gastarnos bromas!'","Recoge patas erizadas de gusanos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'No me has traído todas las partes de gusano que te pedí, ${PLAYER}.'","Lleva patas y mandíbulas de gusanos a Indor","'Esto servirá perfectamente, ${PLAYER}. ¡Se ve terrible y huele peor, es perfecto!\
\
'Ahora, toma este guiso de sapo y llévaselo al enano Wéthorm en Thorenhad. Dile que hice algunas mejoras para que el guiso sepa aún mejor y que quise compartirlo con él. Y asegúrate de observar bien su cara cuando dé el primer bocado: ¡quiero que me la describas sin omitir nada! ¡La última risa será la nuestra!\
\
'Thorenhad está al norte de aquí, en el Bosque de los Trolls, a lo largo de las Gargantas del Bruinen. Wéthorm dijo que iba a visitar a uno de los suyos allí por un tiempo, y estoy seguro de que aún está allí.'","'¿Dónde está la pasta de gusano, ${PLAYER}?'","Indor está en la hoguera de Echad Candelleth, en Tâl Bruinen.\
\
Has recogido las partes de gusanos que Indor pidió y ahora debes llevárselas para que pueda añadirlas al guiso.","'Muy bien, ${PLAYER}. ¡Estas patas y mandíbulas son realmente repugnantes y servirán perfectamente!\
\
'Hazme un favor y tritúralas hasta hacerlas puré en esa piedra de moler, ¿quieres?'","Indor está en la hoguera de Echad Candelleth, en Tâl Bruinen.\
\
Has triturado las partes de gusanos que recogiste y ahora debes llevar la pasta a Indor para que pueda añadirla al guiso.","Recoge mandíbulas viscosas de gusanos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","La piedra de moler está cerca de la hoguera en Echad Candelleth.\
\
Indor te ha pedido que muelas las partes de gusano que recogiste para convertirlas en una pasta.","Tritura los pedazos de gusano en la piedra de moler","'Wéthorm está en Thorenhad, al norte de aquí en las Gargantas del Bruinen del Bosque de los Trolls, al norte de las guaridas de los osos. Presta mucha atención a su primer bocado de mi guiso de sapo, ¡quiero saborear mi venganza!'","Hay gusanos por todo Tâl Bruinen.\
\
Indor te ha pedido que recojas varias partes de los gusanos de Tâl Bruinen para que pueda vengarse del enano que le jugó una broma.","Lleva la pasta de gusano a Indor","Wéthorm está en Thorenhad, en las Gargantas del Bruinen del Bosque de los Trolls, al norte de las guaridas de los osos.\
\
Indor te ha enviado a Wéthorm con su guiso de sapo y te ha pedido que observes bien la reacción del enano al dar su primer bocado. Indor quiere saborear su venganza contra el enano que lo engañó para probar el desagradable guiso de sapo.","Trituras los pedazos de gusano hasta hacerlos puré","Llévale a Wéthorm el guiso de sapo mejorado","Se sirve mejor frío","'Hola, ${PLAYER}. ¡Wéthorm a tu servicio y al de tu familia! Ah, vienes de parte de Indor. Es un buen Hombre, aunque un poco demasiado confiado en estos tiempos peligrosos. Le haría bien aprender esa lección pronto.'\
\
Wéthorm da un enorme bocado del guiso de sapo y su rostro se ilumina. Da una segunda y una tercera cucharada antes de devolverte el cuenco.","'Hay gusanos por todo Tâl Bruinen, ${PLAYER}, pero prefieren especialmente los lugares húmedos. Tráeme algunas de sus patas erizadas y sus mandíbulas viscosas, ¡y le daremos una buena lección a Wéthorm!'","'Hola, ${PLAYER}. ¿En qué puedo ayudarte?'","Patas erizadas de gusanos recogidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Mandíbulas viscosas de gusano recogidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Indor ha decidido corresponder al mal humor de Wéthorm con una mala broma propia."},
[1698]={"As Fláthail falls defeated, the air of dread in Skáilag begins to lessen","Best-laid Plans: Skáilag","Fláthail can be found within the barrows of Skáilag.\
\
You have arrived to find Skáilag overrun by wights and other fell things. You should defeat Fláthail.","Delved into the steep hill-sides of Câr Bronach, the barrows of Skáilag are uninviting","In the barrows of Skáilag, sorcerers of the Iron Crown work to raise the remains of the Hill-men of Rhudaur into the service of Angmar once again.","Skáilag can be found to the east of Grúmachath.\
\
Rethvárd has informed you that the sorceress, Fláthail, endeavours to raise the Hill-men of Rhudaur at Skáilag. You should travel to Skáilag and defeat Fláthail.","Travel to Skáilag","Defeat Fláthail at Skáilag","You have defeated Fláthail at Skáilag.","With the defeat of Fláthail at Skáilag, the Iron Crown's plot to raise their ancient servants, the Hill-men of Rhudaur, has been undone. Your efforts have done much to ensure the success of the Zhélruka expedition in Câr Bronach.","Completado","'As you might imagine, most of us Dourhands no longer look kindly on those who dare to practise necromancy or other fell sorceries.\
\
'However, there is a barrows to the east where the Angmarim seek to raise the Hill-men of Rhudaur into their service once more. A sorceress, Fláthail, leads them in this task, but she has not yet completed her work—much to the disappointment of the High Priestess, Ásachal.\
\
'If you would help both of our peoples, put an end to her before the Dead overwhelm all of Câr Bronach.'"},
[1699]={"'It seems the Iron Crown is not content to bend other peoples' to its will. Within the cavern of Toll Oivas, the sorcerer Iärcagar has devised a means of binding fell spirits to the remain of bats.\
\
'If the Iron Crown can animate flying spies to keep watch on us and Mount Gundabad itself, we shall never be able to free ourselves of their influence.\
\
'Toll Oivas lies to the north-west from here. And while you are there, deal with his pet... Uiagal.\
\
'Iärcagar must be slain before the skies grow dark with bat-wights!'","Iärcagar and Uiagal can be found within the cavern of Toll Oivas.\
\
You have arrived to find Toll Oivas overrun by bat-wights and other fell things. You should defeat Iärcagar and Uiagal.","Travel to Toll Oivas","In the caverns of Toll Oivas, sorcerers of the Iron Crown animate the remains of bats into spies for Angmar.","Defeat Uiagal at Toll Oivas","As Iärcagar falls defeated, fell spirits begin to vanish from Toll Oivas","With the defeat of Iärcagar and Uiagal, the Iron Crown's plans to use bat-wights as spies against the Gabil'akkâ and the Orcs of Mount Gundabad have failed. Your efforts have done much to ensure the success of the Zhélruka expedition in Câr Bronach.","The greatest of Iärcagar's terrible experiments, Uiagal's lifeless remains fall to the ground","You have defeated Iärcagar and Uiagal at Toll Oivas.","Completado","Defeat Iärcagar at Toll Oivas","Toll Oivas can be found to the west of Grúmachath.\
\
Rethvárd has informed you that the sorcerer, Iärcagar and his pet, Uiagal, lead the Angmarim gathered at Toll Oivas. You should travel to Toll Oivas and defeat Iärcagar and Uiagal.","From within the cavern of Toll Oivas, the beating of bat-wings echoes into Câr Bronach","Best-laid Plans: Toll Oivas"},
[1700]={"Hoital, the uruk leading the Orcs of Maustazg, revealed that the siege was being orchestrated by Saruman the White and that Lady Góda was working against Ingmar on behalf of Saruman.","Betrayal","Ingbert is in the Mead Hall of Eaworth.\
\
You should speak with Ingbert about his mother's betrayal.","'My heart grieves, ${PLAYER}. My mother has always been wise in her ways and her counsel... why now has she turned to folly?\
\
'To know that Saruman, ever a friend to Rohan, has fallen to evil is nearly more than I can bear, but that he should take with him good folk, such as Góda daughter of Athelmar...?\
\
'Nonetheless, I cannot allow this treason to go unnoticed. ${PLAYER}, I would ask that you take my mother into custody. The guards will escort her to the jail to await trial.'","'Ah, so my son has not the courage to confront me himself? Know this, ${CLASS}, what I did, I did for the good of the Riding and of Rohan.\
\
'Théoden King has become feeble-minded, incapable of ruling the Mark. Saruman is strong and wise... he seeks only to bring order to the lands.'","Lady Góda stands near Ingbert in the Mead Hall of Eaworth.\
\
Grief-stricken, Ingbert has asked you to confront Góda about her betrayal.","Talk to Ingbert in the Mead Hall of Eaworth","Talk to Góda in the Mead Hall of Eaworth","'I doubt not that her intent was true, ${PLAYER}, but our allegiance is to Théoden, not Saruman. I cannot believe that there is any good in the deeds of the Wizard, and that is a great sorrow.\
\
'We must, however, persevere, for if our hearts fail us, darkness will consume Rohan.'"},
[1701]={"Lleva pieles suaves de lince al Viejo Artemisa","Recoge pieles suaves de lince (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Siempre hay trabajo por hacer, pero por ahora todo es manejable.'","'Me has ayudado mucho, ${PLAYER}.'","Los linces merodean por Nain Enidh, al este de la Cima de los Vientos y al norte del campamento en el extremo este de Minas Eriol.\
\
El Viejo Artemisa te pidió que recogieras pieles de lince para ayudar a Arinora a hacer mantas mejores para los huéspedes más acomodados de la posada.","'Los linces merodean por las tierras al este de la posada, más allá de la Cima de los Vientos. No viajes demasiado lejos, o encontrarás orcos, arañas y toda clase de criaturas horribles.'","'La piel es ciertamente más suave. Puede que tome una para mi propia cama. \
\
Creo que te debo unas monedas, ${PLAYER}. No se me ocurre nada más que necesite por ahora. Has hecho maravillas por mí y me has liberado para ocuparme de mis otras tareas.'","Arinora está descontenta con el trato preferencial que Anlaf exige para los invitados de Bree, pero poco puede hacer al respecto. Mientras Artemisa está en el campo cazando huargos, piensa que también podría ayudar a su amiga Arinora.","Mantas mejores","Pieles suaves de lince recogidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¡Casi lo olvido! Anlaf quiere que ofrezca mejores mantas a nuestros invitados de Bree. ¡Mejores mantas! ¿Puedes creerlo? Vienes del pueblo y te dan mejores mantas. Dime, ¿eso es justo de alguna manera? ¡No, no lo es!\
\
Arinora no tiene más remedio que encargarse de ello. Tus primeras mantas son suficientemente buenas para quienes están acostumbrados a una vida dura, pero los demás necesitan algo mejor, según Anlaf.\
\
Así que pensé que podría ayudarla mientras trabajo para ahuyentar a estos trasgos. Cuando estés cazando linces en Nain Enidh, al norte de aquí y al este de la Cima de los Vientos, arráncales las pieles. Su pelaje es suave y bien cuidado. Tráemelo y haré estas mantas para devolvérselas a Arinora.'"},
[1702]={"Talk to Mekhnet","Mekhnet sits near the Kambráda encampment in the eastern part of Amdân. She might like to hear about how her fellow soldiers are doing.","Mekhnet has requested that you spend some time with soldiers who are resting around Amdân.","'Well met, stranger. Come to join this lonely soul? I can't say there's much to report. I've spent the last few months waiting for my wounds to heal, so I've been carving.' \
\
The dwarf holds up twin wooden cups. \
\
'It passes the time well enough. I mean to keep one of these cups for myself. The other is for my wife.\
\
'Hmm... you seem like a good listener, and I think our comrades would appreciate that. Why not seek out those who are resting here and talk with them a bit? Surely anything must be better than being alone with their thoughts.'","Happy memories are hard to come by during war. Mekhnet, an injured soldier, has a favour to ask.","'That was kind of you. There is nothing wrong with reminiscing about better days during dark times.\
\
'Say -- I think there's something you could help me with.'","'I have nothing to talk about, no family or friends left to speak of, but... come, sit with me.'\
\
You sit next to him for several minutes. No words are exchanged, but the dwarf seems to find comfort in the relative silence that follows.\
\
Before you get up to leave, he nods in farewell.","'These years have not been kind to me, but I hope they have been kinder to my family.'\
\
The dwarf shows you a piece of paper he's been sketching on. The rough drawing of a bright-eyed child smiles from the page.\
\
'My daughter, or at least, how I remember her. I'll survive to see her again, mark my words.'","'Share a drink? It's just water, but I mustn't drink anything heavier.\
\
'So many soldiers miss their loved ones, but I miss the taste of ale. Not the ale we get here, but the ale from taverns. Tied to good memories, mostly. Drinking with friends.'\
\
She sips some water.\
\
'Ah well. Can't get everything we want.'","Talk to resting soldiers (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Talked to resting soldiers (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Better Days"},
[1704]={"Recoge champiñones silvestres (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Vuelve con Meregrot","Recoge la cesta de picnic","Meregrot está sentada junto al río, al sureste de Quiebra Larga.\
\
Lleva los champiñones y las fresas a Meregrot.","Champiñones silvestres recogidos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Entre lo almendrado y lo ácido","Vuelve con Rosalinda","Habla con Meregrot","El aire se llena de una mezcla de fragancias almendradas y cítricas.","Meregrot está sentada junto al río, al sureste de Quiebra Larga.\
\
Habla con Meregrot.","Las fresas crecen silvestre a lo largo de ciertos senderos, y los champiñones están por todo el suelo del bosque cerca del río de Quiebra Larga.\
\
Meregrot Nortuk te ha pedido que recojas fresas y champiñones silvestres.","Rosalinda Nortuk está en Quiebra Larga.\
\
Meregrot te ha pedido que le lleves la cesta de picnic a su hija Rosalinda.","Recoge fresas silvestres (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","A Meregrot Nortuk le gustaría llevar a casa para cenar algunos champiñones y fresas silvestres y así aliviar de trabajo a su hija, Rosalinda.","Fresas silvestres recogidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Meregrot está sentada junto al río, al sureste de Quiebra Larga.\
\
Meregrot Nortuk te ha pedido que coloques los champiñones y las fresas en la cesta de picnic que está en la manta junto a ella.","'¡Ah, ya has vuelto! ¡Ahh, puedo oler los champiñones desde aquí! Justo a tiempo. Acabo de terminar de comer y la cesta de picnic está vacía... un lugar perfecto para esas fresas y champiñones.'","'Mi hija se carga con demasiado. Siempre le repito una de mis reglas más importantes: muchos hobbits hacen el trabajo más ligero.\
\
'¡Rosa tiene que aprender a delegar más sus deberes! Reparte el trabajo, ¡como hago yo! Hablando de eso, ¿por qué no le llevas la cesta de vuelta? Creo que el que la entregues tú ayudará a reforzar mi punto de vista.'","La cesta está llena una vez más","'¿No es agradable sentarse junto al agua y disfrutar un momento lejos de todo el ajetreo? A mi hija Rosa le vendría bien un respiro. Intenta cargarse con demasiadas responsabilidades. Dime, si no tienes mucho que hacer, ¿podrías hacerme un favor?\
\
'Rosa probablemente ya tenga la cena planeada, pero no hará ningún daño que yo lleve algo a casa para contribuir. ¿Podrías recoger algunos ingredientes para mí? A Rosa le encantan las fresas silvetres. Demasiado ácidas para mí, pero la chica parece que nunca come suficientes. ¡Yo prefiero un buen champiñón con su notas almendradas! Puedes encontrar fresas silvestres a lo largo de ciertos senderos, y los champiñones están por todo el suelo del bosque.'","'Oh, hola otra vez. Gracias por traer la cesta de vuelta... ¡pero bueno, si está llena de champiñones y fresas! ¿Cómo ha encontrado tiempo mi hija?'\
\
Transmites las palabras de sabiduría de Meregrot.\
\
'Ah sí, a madre siempre se le dio bien conseguir que la gente le ayudara. No quiero cargar a nadie, especialmente cuando tengo una hija que es perfectamente capaz de ayudarme.'","Coloca los champiñones y las fresas en la cesta de picnic","La cesta está junto a Meregrot, al sureste de Quiebra Larga.\
\
Meregrot Nortuk te ha pedido que recojas la cesta de picnic que está en la manta junto a ella y la lleves a su hija, Rosalinda."},
[1705]={"Somewhere in Duskenvale, the massive hart known as Skadhurn protects his herd.\
\
You should find and defeat Skadhurn.","You present the massive antlers to Goslim. His jaw goes slack.\
\
'You... you killed Skadhurn? The storytellers must know of this! They will tell the tale of your victory over that massive beast for years to come!'","'As you are preparing to enter the wilds seeking the deer, you should hear of their protector. The story of a massive black hart known as Skadhurn has been passed down for what seems like many generations. He guards his herd jealously, and is known to gore any who would dare hunt them on his massive crown of antlers. I have never seen the beast myself, but the elders swear he is out there. Hunt him at your own risk!'","The villagers of Arhaim tell the legend of a massive black hart that protects the deer within Duskenvale. Draw his ire at your own risk!","Talk to Goslim","Goslim can be found in the village Arhaim in Duskenvale.\
\
You should bring the antlers to Goslim.","Defeat Skadhurn","Beware of Skadhurn","You take the antlers as proof of your victory"},
[1706]={"Destroyed dread-wards in the Circle of Death (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Dread-wards can be found in the Circle of Death in Minas Morgul.\
\
Faramir has asked you to destroy dread-wards so their magic in the Circle of Death magic might be undone.","'It is done, then?'\
\
Faramir approaches the doors of Uialrond and slowly opens one, emanating from it a loud and long creak as it slides along the stones of Minas Morgul.\
\
'It is time we learned the truth of Uialrond.'","Destroy dread-wards in the Circle of Death (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Concerned that Gothmog has laid a trap for the Rangers of Ithilien, Faramir hopes to overcome the fell magic sealing the door to Uialrond, the Dome of Evening.","Faramir can be found outside Uialrond, the Dome of Evening in Minas Morgul.\
\
You have destroyed the dread-wards of Minas Morgul and should now return to Faramir.","Beyond All Light","Talk to Faramir at Uialrond, the Dome of Evening","'I fear that Gothmog has laid a trap for us, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'If we were to assail the Tower of the Crescent Moon, would we not be doing exactly as Gothmog intends? There is foul magic upon this city... and much of it seems to lead here to Uialrond. I know little of it save for old tales, but it is said that it was once a great council-hall of Minas Ithil. Yet, when I reach to open its doors... I feel some sort of presence resist me. Has Gothmog locked some evil away in Uialrond to be unleashed upon us?\
\
'I cannot be certain, but I will not allow Gothmog to gain the advantage through deception. I have seen great, terrible wards of dread throughout the Circle of Death. I know not their true purpose, but if their magic holds fast the doors of Uialrond, they must be destroyed.\
\
'We must learn what lies within Uialrond!'"},
[1707]={"'Bueno, es un placer conocerte, ${PLAYER}. Supongo que Cardoso quiere que lleve a mi esposa y a los trabajadores a la ciudad, ¿verdad? Pues te lo digo ahora: ¡ningún bandido me echará de mis tierras!\
\
No me mires así. Estamos más seguros aquí que detrás de unos muros viejos y endebles.\
\
Cardoso es buena gente y agradezco que se preocupe por nosotros, pero nada ni nadie nos hará abandonar nuestras tierras!'","Debe completarse antes de la \\qIntroducción.\\q","Más allá de las murallas","La granja de Cal Sprigley se encuentra al sur del Capricho de Bronwe.\
\
El condestable Cardoso te ha pedido que vayas a la granja de Cal Sprigley y convenzas a Sprigley de traer a su familia a Archet, donde podrán estar protegidos de los Montebruno.","'¡Hola, ${PLAYER}! Necesito tu ayuda. Tengo un amigo, Cal Sprigley, que tiene una granja fuera de Archet. Por lo que he oído sobre el ataque de los Montebruno contra Archet, me preocupa que los bandidos puedan hacerle daño a él y a su gente.\
\
¿Podrías hablar con él? Tal vez puedas convencerlo de venir aquí.\
\
La granja de Cal está al sur del Capricho de Bronwe. Dile que estará más seguro aquí en Archet. ¡Espero que escuche a la razón!'","El condestable Cardoso está preocupado por su amigo Cal Sprigley, un granjero en las afueras del sur de Archet. La granja de Sprigley es vulnerable a un ataque de bandidos.","Habla con Cal Sprigley","'La granja de Cal Sprigley está justo al sur del Capricho de Bronwe. Por favor, ve allí y convéncelo de traer a su familia al norte.'"},
[1708]={"Talk to Legolas about Lhingris","Legolas can be found at the Ruins of Díngarth in Dor Amarth and Bregdal can be found on the border of Dor Amarth and Talath Úrui.\
\
When you have completed all you wish to do in Dor Amarth, you should speak to Legolas and Bregdal.","When you have completed all you wish to do in Dor Amarth, you should speak to Legolas about Lhingris and Bregdal about Talath Úrui.","'You have helped us a great deal ${PLAYER}. Some of our company have gone ahead to scout Mordor. When you have done all you wish to do in Dor Amarth, you may want to accompany these Men and Elves further into the realm of Gorgoroth.\
\
'A Gondorian, named Bregdal was ventured with a small group towards Talath Úrui. I have also heard the Legolas wishes aid in scouting Lhingris. I am sure both would more than welcome your company.'","'${PLAYER}, it is good to see you again. Have you come to assist us?'","'${PLAYER}, I was just about to depart. Do you wish to accompany me to Lhingris?'","Beyond the Burning Plain","'You have been of great help to us. When you have done all that you wish in Dor Amarth, I ask you to aid others in our company. Some have gone ahead of us and will surely seek assistance as the lands beyond here are neither welcoming nor hospitable. Speak to them when you have a moment.\
\
'A small group has recently headed towards Talath Úrui and your friend Legolas is about to venture into Lhingris. I am sure your companionship would be most welcomed.'","Talk to Bregdal about Talath Úrui"},
[1709]={"'¿Otra vez, ${PLAYER}? ¡Me asombra tanto tu persistencia como la de ese antiguo terrateniente! ¿Cómo dice este último acertijo?\
\
   \\qEn lo alto de Dol Haedír, más allá de las Cataratas del Anochecer,\
  los hombres de linaje lupino mi secreto han de proteger.\\q\
\
'He oído hablar de Dol Haedír, ${PLAYER}, pero tiene muy mala reputación. Está al noroeste del lago Nenuial, y de este acertijo deduzco que las Cataratas del Anochecer deben estar cerca de esta elevación.'","El tesoro podría estar bajo otro hito de piedra en algún lugar de Evendim, según el acertijo:\
\
  \\qEn lo alto de Dol Haedír, más allá de las Cataratas del Anochecer,\
  los hombres de linaje lupino mi secreto han de proteger.\\q\
\
Debes examinar el hito cuando lo encuentres en busca de alguna pista sobre la localización del tesoro.","Encuentra la solución al acertijo","El montaraz Culang ha sabido de un gran tesoro enterrado hace mucho tiempo por un terrateniente Dúnadan y quiere recuperarlo antes de que lo encuentren los saqueadores de tumbas.","El hito de piedra está rodeado de signos de excavación. Si una vez marcaba la localización del tesoro, seguro que ha sido encontrado.\
\
El hito lleva una inscripción, desgastada por el paso del tiempo.","La inscripción en este hito de piedra es apenas legible, pero se pueden distinguir las siguientes palabras:\
\
  \\qEn lo alto de Dol Haedír, más allá de las Cataratas del Anochecer,\
  los hombres de linaje lupino mi secreto han de proteger.\\q\
\
Este nuevo acertijo podría revelar la verdadera localización del tesoro.","Más allá de las Cataratas del Anochecer"},
[1710]={"Travel to Zudramdân","'As you know, our forces recently captured the old ruins of Zudramdân.\
\
'I have sent one of my scouts, Gárjan, to bolster the forces that reclaimed it and aid in scouting the approach to Mount Gundabad. Zudramdân may prove a valuable watch-post in Elderslade, but its defences are in dire need of improvement.\
\
'You are to travel to Zudramdân and meet with Gárjan at once!'","Beyond the High-threshold","Looming over Elderslade, the ruins of Zudramdân have been claimed by the Gabil'akkâ","After gaining a foothold at the dwarf-ruins of Zudramdân, Glóin hopes to expand the reach of the Gabil'akkâ in Elderslade.","Talk to Gárjan at Zudramdân","'Ah! Did Commander Glóin send you?\
\
'Very good. There is much to be done, but first you'll want to report to Náth over there.'","Gárjan can be found at Zudramdân.\
\
You have arrived at Zudramdân and should now speak to Gárjan.","Zudramdân can be found to the north-west of Annâk-khurfu in Elderslade.\
\
Glóin has asked you to travel to Zudramdân and rally with one of his scouts, Gárjan. You should travel to Zudramdân."},
[1711]={"'Por favor, busca a Golodir y Corunir en la ciudad de los Montañeses de Aughaire, en el oeste de Angmar.'","Más allá del Ram Dúath","Los Montaraces Golodir y Corunir están en la ciudad de los Montañeses llamada Aughaire, al oeste de la salida norte del Ram Dúath.\
\
Arohir te ha pedido que busques a los Montaraces perdidos Golodir y Corunir, quienes hace mucho tiempo fueron enviados a Angmar.","Arohir te ha pedido que atravieses el Ram Dúath hacia Angmar para buscar un lugar llamado Aughaire. Los Montaraces llamados Golodir y Corunir han hecho de este lugar su hogar, pero nadie ha hablado con ellos en muchos años.","Busca a Golodir y Corunir","'Hace muchos años, dos Montaraces llamados Golodir y Corunir fueron a Angmar para investigar el rumor de que el Mal había surgido nuevamente en el Norte. Desafortunadamente, no hemos sabido nada de ellos desde que los Angmarim levantaron sus ejércitos de orcos y ocuparon el Ram Dúath.\
\
'Te pediría que te dirijas al norte y busques un lugar llamado Aughaire. Es el hogar de los Montañeses del Norte, al menos algunos de los cuales Golodir reportó como hospitalarios, a diferencia de sus parientes en otros lugares. Si encuentras a nuestros dos parientes perdidos, asegúrales que no los hemos olvidado y que pronto necesitaremos de sus servicios nuevamente.\
\
'Una vez que pases por el peligroso Ram Dúath hacia el norte, deberías poder encontrar Aughaire dirigiéndote al oeste.'","'¿Vienes del sur? Hace mucho que no recibo noticias de Esteldín. Llegué a pensar que quizás habían perdido interés en mi destino. Por lo que he oído de la invasión orca de las Quebradas del Norte, no me sorprende. Mis parientes quizás han tenido asuntos más urgentes que atender últimamente.\
\
'¿Qué? No, los Angmarim aún no se han preocupado demasiado por los Pueblos Libres que viven aquí. Quizás deberías hablar con el Señor Crannog si quieres saber más, ya que estos Montañeses tienen poco más que problemas en estos días peligrosos.\
\
'¿Golodir? Lamentablemente, temo que ha caído. Al menos, hace cinco años que no veo su rostro. Más allá de la tragedia de su muerte, era un líder para los Montañeses aquí, y su pérdida les ha hecho perder el ánimo.'"},
[1712]={"Collect Wose lights (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collected Wose lights (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collect Wose lights","'I shall certainly honour the Red Sky Clan and find suitable places to plant these lights in our travels through Mordor. I hope they have the mysterious properties to heal the land, as you say they do, ${PLAYER}.'","The Red Sky Clan of Bhol Rûdh is up against impossible odds in their conflict with the forces of Seregost.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Warning: This quest requires Bhol Rûdh: Siege of Corruption to be underway. If that quest has been completed or failed, you will be unable to exit and re-enter this instance in order to complete this quest.</rgb>","Bring the Wose lights to Candúr.","Bhol Rûdh: Ancient Lights","Collect Wose lights.","Bring the Wose lights to Candúr"},
[1713]={"The Red Sky Clan of Bhol Rûdh is up against impossible odds in their conflict with the forces of Seregost.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Warning: This quest has a one hour time limit. The timer will begin upon accepting the quest.</rgb>","'In an effort to extend a hand to those in Mordor who do not rally under a banner of shadow, we will lend aid to those in need. You have spent time with the Red Sky Clan in Agarnaith, have you not?\
\
'They are continually in confrontation with the forces of Seregost. We must be vigilant for the Red Sky Clan are now one of our greatest allies in Gorgoroth.\
\
'Would you go to their village and assure them of our continued watch?'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Warning: This quest has a one hour time limit. The timer will begin upon accepting the quest. This quest can be completed with one or two adventurers.</rgb>","You ran out of time...","Defeat Khoshúg the Reeking.","'We must protect the Red Sky Clan at any cost.'","Bhol Rûdh: Siege of Corruption","'I am glad you were there, for the Red Sky Clan may not have survived that assault!'","Talk to Candúr","You should return to Candúr and apprise him of your efforts.","Defeated Khoshúg the Reeking","Defeat Khoshúg the Reeking"},
[1714]={"'You have done well, friend. Your efforts will be duly noted!'","Defeated infected Orcs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat infected Orcs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Red Sky Clan of Bhol Rûdh is up against impossible odds in their conflict with the forces of Seregost.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Warning: This quest requires Bhol Rûdh: Siege of Corruption to be underway. If that quest has been completed or failed, you will be unable to exit and re-enter this instance in order to complete this quest.</rgb>","Defeat infected Orcs on the path to Bhol Rûdh","Talk to Candúr","Defeat infected Orcs on the path to Bhol Rûdh.","Talk to Candúr.","Bhol Rûdh: Trail of Blood"},
[1715]={"No hay logro mayor que atrapar un pez grande, viejo y pesado. Sin embargo, capturar demasiados peces pequeños puede hacer que uno se cuestione su habilidad como pescador.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Esta misión se eliminará de tu registro de misiones cuando finalice el festival actual.</rgb>","Atrapa peces grandes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¡Eh! Seguro que estás haciendo trampas. Esos peces son incluso más grandes que los que atrapé yo. ¿Cuál es tu secreto? ¿Cebo de gusanos? ¿Cebo de bocadillos? Vamos, ¡suéltalo!\
\
'Bah. Ya veo cómo va a ser esto. En fin, estaré encantado de retarte de nuevo mañana. Algún día, mi suerte será mejor que la tuya…'","Bollo Bolger se encuentra cerca del lugar de pesca en Delagua.\
\
Deberías hablar con Bollo Bolger y mostrarle el pez grande e impresionante que has atrapado.","Peces grandes, peces pequeños","No atrapes peces pequeños (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Habla con Bollo Bolger","Se pueden atrapar peces (tanto grandes como pequeños) en el lugar de pesca de Delagua.\
\
Deberías intentar capturar muchos peces grandes sin atrapar demasiados pequeños. ¡Demasiados peces pequeños harán que tu suerte falle!","'Tengo muchas ganas de ver si serás tú quien lance miradas de envidia o quien las reciba de sus vecinos, ${PLAYER}.'","'¡Me encanta pescar! ¿A quién no? Es un deporte fascinante, apasionante, con toda esa competencia feroz. Sin ir más lejos, el otro día atrapé un pez enorme, mientras que los demás participantes no lograban sacar más que peces diminutos.\
\
'Las miradas de envidia que me dedicaban eran tan deliciosas como una pila de empanadas de setas.\
\
'¿Y tú qué clase de pescador eres, ${PLAYER}? ¿Pescás peces grandes o prefieres atrapar esas cosillas pequeñas, enclenques e inútiles?'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: El resultado de esta misión se basa en la suerte y no se ve afectado por la habilidad de pesca.</rgb>"},
[1716]={"'¿Has encontrado mi mochila? La perdí afuera de esa choza de piedra en el Bosque de Brandi.'","Dob Hojarena, afuera de El Poney Pisador, te ha pedido que busques su mochila en la choza de piedra en lo profundo del Bosque de Brandi, muy al norte de Los Gamos.","Lleva la mochila a Dob Hojarena","Grandes problemas","Mochila de Dob Hojarena recolectada","'¡Hola! ¿Eres la persona de la que todos han estado hablando, verdad? Bueno, podría usar tu ayuda. ¡Tengo grandes problemas, y eso es un hecho! Verás, estaba de viaje para visitar a mi padre en Los Gamos después de visitar a mi hermano Gil en Hengstacer. Pensé para mí: \\qDeberías tomar un atajo... no tiene sentido bajar todo el camino hasta el Gran Camino del Este y demás.\\q Fue entonces cuando todo salió mal.\
\
'Iba caminando tranquilamente hasta que llegó la hora del segundo desayuno, y sentí un hambre terrible. Me encontré con unas viejas piedras en el Bosque de Brandi y me senté para un ligero refrigerio. De repente, tan rápido como quieras, apareció un tipo corpulento, y con palabras nada amables, por cierto. Era mucho más grande que la gente grande de Bree... Me temo que me asusté bastante del bruto y salí corriendo sin mi mochila.\
\
'Las piedras están al norte de Los Gamos, en el Bosque del Brandivino. Dudo que ese gigante —Svalfang, así se llamó— se quede todo el día en su lúgubre choza. Tal vez puedas escabullirte y recuperar mi mochila cuando esté fuera, pisoteando y haciendo lo que sea que hagan los de su clase.'","'¡La encontraste! ¡Te lo agradezco! No sé qué habría hecho si no la recuperabas.\
\
'Parece que algo de la comida está aplastada y rota, pero la mayoría aún se ve bien. ¡Es la última vez que tomo otro atajo, y eso es un hecho!'","Dob Hojarena fue ahuyentado de su comida por un gigante. Te ha pedido que recuperes su mochila."},
[1718]={"Lleva la carta de Bilbo a Lobelia","Lobelia está tardando demasiado en leer la carta. Debes insistirle para obtener información.","'¿Sigues aquí, eh? Bueno, supongo que si eres de naturaleza inquisitiva como el propio Sr. Bilbo, te contaré algo que me dijo antes de desaparecer para siempre.\
\
'El viejo Bilbo, dijo (con un brillo en los ojos) que su aventura continuaría incluso después de que él se fuera hace mucho tiempo. Ese era el Sr. Bolsón, para ti.\
\
'Bueno, no me interpondré en tu camino. Ayúdate a revisar su última carta para nosotros, que mi hijo Sam me leyó. Tiene algunas instrucciones particulares con respecto a ese Sacovilla-Bolsón...'","Bilbo dejó una carta para los habitantes de su amada Comarca en manos de Hamfast Gamyi, afectuosamente conocido por los vecinos como el Tío Gamyi.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000> NOTA: Esta misión se eliminará de tu registro de misiones cuando finalice el evento con el que está asociada. </rgb>","'Estoy leyendo la carta. ¡Déjame en paz! ¿Cómo puede un hobbit concentrarse con gente molesta acosándolo todo el día?\
\
'¡Si no dice nada sobre esa bodega, juro que estaré positivamente furiosa!'","'¡No me molestes! Estoy leyendo. Ese Bilbo realmente sabe cómo divagar sobre nada.'","Lobelia sigue leyendo con avidez (no es de mucha ayuda)","'Quieres llevar esta carta a Lobelia, ¿eh? Adelante. No te servirá de nada quedarte aquí conmigo, ya sabes.'","Lobelia Sacovilla-Bolsón está en Bolsón Cerrado, al norte del Árbol de la Fiesta en la colina.\
\
Debes hablar con Lobelia sobre la carta de Bilbo.","Obviamente, Lobelia quiere quedarse con los tesoros de Bilbo para ella sola","Lobelia te ahuyenta y sigue leyendo","Carta de Bilbo","'Si buscas a esa vieja comadreja de Lobelia, está a unos pasos al norte de aquí. Seguramente la encontrarás en Bolsón Cerrado, discutiendo sobre cualquier cosa que se le ocurra.'","Pregunta al Tío Gamyi por la carta de Bilbo","'¿Qué es esto de una cuchara? Me dejó las cucharas de plata... ¡dice que son la clave de la bodega!'","El Tío Gamyi está afuera de su casa en Bolsón de Tirada.\
\
Debes preguntarle al Tío Gamyi si puedes mostrar la carta de Bilbo a Lobelia.","'¡Fuera! Si no me dejas en paz, te denunciaré a las autoridades.'","Lobelia Sacovilla-Bolsón está en Bolsón Cerrado, al norte del Árbol de la Fiesta en la colina.\
\
Debes llevar la carta de despedida de Bilbo a Lobelia, ya que podría dar alguna pista sobre la bodega cerrada de Bolsón Cerrado.","'¿Qué es ese sobre que tienes ahí? ¡Dámelo de inmediato! Estoy segura de que Bilbo lo destinaba al sucesor de Bolsón Cerrado y no a ese viejo jardinero tonto. De hecho, no creo que sepa leer.'","Has adquirido la carta de despedida de Bilbo","Lobelia parece confundida por la mención de la cuchara","Insiste a Lobelia para obtener información"},
[1719]={"'No te preocupes por el poney... encontrará el camino.'","Bill parece contento de avanzar","Has encontrado a Bill. Su melena parece descuidada y tiene un brillo salvaje en los ojos, pero por lo demás parece ileso.\
\
Cuando intentas guiarle duda si seguirte o no, como si estuviera esperando a algo o alguien, mirando expectante hacia los muros de Moria.\
\
Persuadiéndolo lo suficiente, eres capaz de hacer que te siga.","Habla con un elfo en Echad Dúnnan sobre el paso de Bill","Coge las riendas para animar a Bill a seguirte","Habla con Bill el poney","El regreso seguro de Bill","'Si ha tomado el camino hacia el norte, sin duda se dirige a un lugar familiar para él. No me preocupa que encuentre el camino seguro, pues tiene más sentido común que muchas de las bestias venidas de las tierras de los Hombres.'","Has encontrado a Bill el poney y debes escoltarle hasta un lugar seguro.","Los depredadores se aproximan...","Bill puede ser invocado utilizando el cuerno que tienes contigo. Las huellas de Bill pueden encontrarse yendo hacia el camino, seguidas de cerca por los huargos.\
\
Deberías encontrar las huellas de Bill para descubrir y derrotar a los huargos que intentan darle caza.\
\
(Puedes utilizar el cuerno de invocación para llamarlo en cualquier momento.)","Escuchas los aullidos de caza de los huargos cerca...","Has conseguido llegar al camino con Bill, y parece tener estar convencido de dejar las puertas de Moria atrás.\
\
Deberías hablar con Bill.\
\
(Puedes utilizar el cuerno de invocación para llamarlo en cualquier momento.)","Encuentra las huellas de Bill para encontrar a los huargos que le dan caza (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Debes guiar a Bill el poney a un lugar seguro.","Has conseguido llegar al camino con Bill, y parece tener estar convencido de dejar las puertas de Moria atrás.\
\
Este pequeño y robusto poney llegará donde tenga que ir sin que tengas que seguir dándole empujoncitos, pero has hecho bien en persuadirlo para que saliera de territorio peligroso.","Glavroleth está en Echad Dúnnan.\
\
Deberías decirle a Glavroleth que guiaste a Bill hasta el camino."},
[1720]={"'¡El amor por los libros se propagará por todo el vecindario, y espero que también lo haga en el tuyo!'","Bingo Regresa a Casa","'¡Por favor, salda mi deuda con la biblioteca, ${PLAYER}! Ese tesoro debería ser más que suficiente, y estaré encantado de donar el resto para el mantenimiento continuo de la biblioteca... ¡siempre que conserven un ejemplar de mi libro y lo presten cuando esté terminado!'","El agujero hobbit de Bingo está en Cavada Grande, al norte del Ayuntamiento.","Bingo está a punto de llegar al final de su viaje.","Bingo está dentro de su agujero hobbit en Cavada Grande, al norte del Ayuntamiento.","'¡La prolongada ausencia de Bingo de La Comarca nos ha dejado a todos en muy mala reputación!'","'¡Mira este lugar, ${PLAYER}! A los hobbits les gusta que todo esté ordenado, y ver mi hogar en este estado resulta bastante perturbador.\
\
'¿Te importaría ayudarme a quitar algunas de estas telarañas? Ahora que he vuelto a casa, debo retomar mi rutina habitual: quitar el polvo de la repisa de la chimenea y barrer los rincones cada tres días. Y si llego a arrastrar los pies con la tarea, bastará con recordar lo desordenado que quedó mi hogar mientras estuve de viaje para acelerar mi plumero y apurar mi escoba.'","'¡Bingo Boffin! ¿Cuántas semanas han pasado desde que un hobbit respetable te vio dentro de los setos o por los senderos de la Comarca? ¡Más de las apropiadas, te lo aseguro!\
\
'¡No tienes ningún respeto por tus vecinos, Bingo! ¿Pensaste siquiera en lo que NOSOTROS podríamos estar pasando durante tu imprudente e impropia excursión a tierras extranjeras? Un vecindario necesita vecinos, ¡y tú has estado ausente durante muchas estaciones! ¡Y los rumores! ¡Los susurros! Han dejado esta calle y a quienes vivimos aquí en muy mala luz, ¡y todas nuestras reputaciones se han visto manchadas solo por estar asociados contigo!\
\
'Esperaríamos ese comportamiento de alguien como ${PLAYER}, ¡pero no de ti, Bingo! Tú no eres ningún aventurero... ¿o sí?'","Examina el aviso clavado en la puerta de Bingo","'Lamento que Myrtle se haya disgustado tanto por mi ausencia del vecindario... ¡No sabía que le importara tanto! Para ser sincero, es una sorpresa. Haré todo lo posible por compensarlo.\
\
'Pero ¿qué es eso que está clavado en mi puerta, ${PLAYER}? Parece algún tipo de aviso. ¿Puedes ver de qué se trata?'","Habla con Bingo fuera de su hogar en Cavada Grande","Donnamira Tuk es la bibliotecaria de la biblioteca de los Grandes Smials, situada en lo alto de la colina en Alforzaburgo.\
\
Bingo ha acumulado muchas multas por retraso con el libro de cocina que dio inicio a su viaje, y te pidió que saldaras su deuda.","'¡Hola, Myrtle! ¿Cómo te han tratado estas semanas?'","Telarañas retiradas (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'Myrtle no parece muy contenta con esto. Pobrecilla.'","'Pero ¿qué es eso que está clavado en mi puerta, ${PLAYER}? Parece algún tipo de aviso. ¿Podrías ver de qué se trata?'","Myrtle Cenagales está de pie frente al hogar de Bingo, con los brazos cruzados en señal de desaprobación.","'Ah, así está mucho mejor. ¡Gracias!\
\
Bingo mira alrededor de su hogar y suspira.\
\
'¿No te parece más grande que cuando nos fuimos? A mí me lo parece: más grande y más vacío. Fue la soledad lo que me impulsó a emprender el viaje, y aquí estoy, al final del camino, ¡y sigo sintiéndome solo! Sé lo que necesito, ${PLAYER}. Extraño a mis amistades nuevas y a las de siempre. ¡Organizaré una cena! Permíteme escribir algunas invitaciones, ¡y tú podrás repartirlas por mí!\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Siguiente semana: 'A Mano, y en Mano' (Nivel recomendado: 93)</rgb>","Hay un aviso clavado en la puerta del agujero hobbit de Bingo.","Habla con Donnamira Tuk en la biblioteca de los Grandes Smials y salda la deuda de Bingo","Habla con Bingo en el interior de su agujero hobbit, en Cavada Grande","Elimina las telarañas del hogar de Bingo (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Este es un aviso de retraso de la biblioteca. Ya tiene casi un año de antigüedad","'¡Has regresado, y con el libro de cocina perdido! ¡Qué inesperado y encantador! Ya había perdido toda esperanza de volver a ver este libro, pero siempre he estado tan dedicada al funcionamiento de esta biblioteca que incluso había pensado en intentar recrear algunas de las recetas de memoria.\
\
'Es un alivio saber que eso no será necesario. Sin embargo, sigue estando el asunto de la multa. ¿Bingo te dio el dinero para saldar su deuda? Me alegra recuperar el libro, pero las multas por retraso existen por una razón.\
\
Le muestras el tesoro de los bandidos y explicas que Bingo desea usarlo para pagar la multa y donar el resto directamente a la biblioteca.\
\
'¡Esto mantendrá la biblioteca abierta durante muchos años! ¡Bingo es realmente una persona caritativa! Ambos tienen mi agradecimiento, pues con este dinero podremos continuar con la educación de los jóvenes hobbits de la Comarca. ¡El amor por los libros se propagará por todo el vecindario, y espero que también lo haga en el tuyo!'","Habla con Myrtle Cenagales fuera del hogar de Bingo en Cavada Grande","'Esperaríamos ese comportamiento de alguien como ${PLAYER}, pero no de ti, Bingo. Tú no eres ningún aventurero... ¿o sí?'","'¿Un aviso de retraso de la biblioteca de Alforzaburgo? Me da mucha vergüenza, ${PLAYER}. Estoy seguro de que me dijiste que devolviera ese libro de cocina antes de comenzar mi viaje, pero confieso que nunca llegué a hacerlo.\
\
'¿Te importaría muchísimo llevar ese libro de cocina de vuelta a la biblioteca de los Grandes Smials por mí? Aquí, lleva también el tesoro de los bandidos. ¡Debería servir para pagar la multa por retraso varias veces!\
\
'Es más, creo que deberíamos donar ese tesoro para el mantenimiento y conservación de la biblioteca. ¡Que algo bueno salga de todo esto! Mi única condición para esa donación es que la biblioteca conserve un ejemplar de mi libro cuando esté terminado.'","Bingo te entrega el libro de cocina con mucho retraso y el tesoro de los bandidos","'¡Mi viaje está llegando a su fin! No falta mucho para que volvamos a mi puerta en Cavada Grande.\
\
'Debo confesar cierta reticencia en esta última etapa de nuestra aventura, . ¡Piensa en todas esas colinas que no subimos, en todos esos cruces donde tomamos el camino izquierdo y no el derecho! Me alegrará volver a ver mi hogar, no lo dudes. Pero cuanto más nos acercamos al final del viaje, ¡más pienso en el siguiente! Es algo realmente curioso.\
\
'¡Sigamos hasta Cavada Grande, mi ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}! ¡Estoy listo para volver a ver el viejo lugar!'","'¡Mira este lugar! A los hobbits les gusta que todo esté limpio y ordenado, y ver mi hogar en este estado es realmente inquietante.'","La mansión Boffin se ha llenado de telarañas durante la prolongada ausencia de Bingo, y él te pidió que lo ayudes a ordenar.","Bingo está fuera de su agujero hobbit en Cavada Grande, al norte del Ayuntamiento.","Viaja al agujero hobbit de Bingo en Cavada Grande","'¡Sigamos hasta Cavada Grande, mi ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}! ¡Estoy listo para volver a ver el viejo lugar!'","Myrtle Cenagales está de pie frente al hogar de Bingo, con los brazos cruzados en señal de desaprobación"},
[1721]={"'¿Así que este es Rohan, eh? La gente de aquí parece muy tensa, como si estuvieran esperando que algo malo ocurriera. ¡No sé si culparlos, ${PLAYER}! Es un bonito pueblo, pero parece rodeado por todos lados de peligro, ¡y no hay suficientes guardias para protegerlo!\
\
'Bueno, están de suerte, porque tres valientes aventureros han llegado a Langhold: tú, yo y Willem Bigote, ¡por supuesto! Una breve charla con algunos niños me ha dado toda la información necesaria para ayudar a mejorar la situación. Si derrotamos salamandras, bandidos y orientales por todo el Páramo, creo que habremos hecho este lugar mucho más seguro para la gente de Langhold. ¡Vamos, amigo mío!'","'Sabes, ${PLAYER}, quizá tenías razón con lo del caballo. Sabert y Egwylf también. Rohan es bastante más grande de lo que pensaba, y quizá yo también deba conseguir un caballo. Hablé con un hombre de aquí y dijo que hay caballos a la venta en la ciudad de Harwick, al sur. Supongo que deberíamos ir y ver.'","'¡Estoy listo para una buena caminata si tú lo estás, ${PLAYER}! Nunca habría sugerido algo así al inicio de nuestro viaje, ¡pero ahora somos aventureros curtidos y no temo una caminata de este tamaño!'","Habla con Bingo dentro de Stangard","'¡Buen trabajo, ${PLAYER}! La gente de Langhold sigue pareciendo preocupada, pero hemos mejorado la situación en el Páramo, ¡aunque no estén seguros de que sea prudente alegrarse!\
\
Bingo respira hondo, preparándose aparentemente para algo.\
\
'Sabes, ${PLAYER}, quizá tenías razón con lo del caballo. Sabert y Egwylf también. Rohan es bastante más grande de lo que pensaba, y quizá yo también deba conseguir un caballo. Hablé con un hombre de aquí y dijo que hay caballos a la venta en la ciudad de Harwick, al sur. Supongo que deberíamos ir y ver.'","Orientales derrotados en el Páramo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Hay muchas amenazas en el Páramo del Este de Rohan que ponen en peligro a la gente de Langhold: salamandras, bandidos y orientales.\
\
Bingo quiere ayudar a la gente de Langhold luchando contra los peligros de El Páramo.","Derrota salamandras en el Páramo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Bingo está fuera de la entrada principal de Harwick, al norte de la ciudad, en el Páramo.","Bingo está en el patio superior de Stangard.\
\
Sabert ha dejado claro que cruzar Rohan a pie y sin caballo no es una buena idea, y deberías volver con esa noticia para Bingo.","Sabert está en la puerta este de Stangard, el puesto avanzado del Rohan junto a las orillas del Gran Río.\
\
Bingo es reacio a montar un caballo en Rohan y quiere saber por Sabert si el reino es lo bastante pequeño como para recorrerlo a pie.","Bingo está en el patio superior de Stangard.\
\
Bingo espera hablar contigo para comenzar la larga caminata hacia Rohan.","Bingo está en la ciudad de Langhold, en la zona norte de El Páramo en el Este de Rohan.\
\
Has derrotado muchas amenazas en el Páramo para ayudar a la gente de Langhold.","Sabert parece a punto de echarse a reír otra vez ante la idea de cruzar Rohan a pie, así que decides no decir nada.","Habla con Sabert en la puerta este de Stangard","Habla con Bingo en la entrada de Harwick, en el Páramo","'Sabes, ${PLAYER}, quizá tenías razón con lo del caballo. Sabert y Egwylf también. Rohan es bastante más grande de lo que pensaba, y quizá yo también deba conseguir un caballo. Aparentemente hay caballos a la venta en la ciudad de Harwick, al sur. Supongo que deberíamos ir y ver.'","'No sé realmente adónde deberíamos ir ahora, ${PLAYER}. Hemos ido más allá del borde del viejo mapa de Bilbo, ¡y nuestros pasos nos han llevado a un territorio desconocido! Podríamos viajar al reino de Rohan propiamente dicho, supongo, pero... bueno, quizá haya otro camino que seguir. Aman a sus caballos, ¿ves? Mira cuántas figuras equinas han tallado en los edificios de Stangard, ¡y esto es solo un puesto avanzado, fuera de las fronteras del reino!\
\
'En lo que a mí respecta, nunca he sido muy amigo de los caballos. ¡Son tan grandes y aterradores, siempre pisoteando con sus pesadas pezuñas y mordiendo a hobbits desprevenidos con sus fuertes dientes! Me mordió casi un caballo cuando era un tween, ¿sabes?, y nunca he conseguido perdonar a esas criaturas.\
\
'¿Crees que podrías bajar a la puerta este de Stangard y preguntarle a Sabert si podríamos disfrutar un recorrido a pie por el reino de Rohan? No es un lugar muy grande, ¿verdad? Si nuestros pies bastan, entonces digo que eso es lo que debemos hacer, ¡y dejar completamente fuera a los caballos!'","'¿El reino de Rohan es adecuado para recorrerlo a pie? ¿Me estás preguntando si es buena idea caminar de un extremo al otro de Rohan en vez de montar un caballo?'\
\
Sabert estalla en sonoras carcajadas y, aunque es una respuesta un poco descortés, admites que más o menos lo esperabas. A Bingo no le va a gustar nada esto.","'Aquí estamos, aquí estamos. Muy pronto podremos ver si venden caballos, ${PLAYER}. ¡Muy pronto! Si es que hace falta. ¿Hace falta de verdad?'\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>Después de completar esta misión, Bartolín llegará cerca del maestro de establos en Harwick, en el Este de Rohan.</rgb>\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>La semana que viene: '¿Sí o Neigh?' (Nivel recomendado: 80)</rgb>","Salamandras derrotadas en el Páramo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Bingo está dentro del pueblo de Langhold, en el área norte de El Páramo en el Este de Rohan.\
\
Has entrado en el reino de Rohan con Bingo, y el hobbit desea hacer algo por la gente de Langhold.","'¡Esto es terrible, ${PLAYER}! ¡Acabamos de llegar a Rohan y ya veo que el mal ha llegado realmente a este reino! Puede que este pueblo haya sido agradable antaño, pero ahora está abandonado, ¡una cáscara quemada!\
\
Le dices a Bingo que la gente de Langhold huyó hacia Harwick, y él asiente.\
\
'Me alegra saber que algunos escaparon, pero si se parecen a los hobbits que conozco, querrán volver a sus hogares en cuanto puedan. ¡Deberíamos hacer la zona lo más segura posible para ellos! ¡Luchemos contra los enemigos que acechan cerca: salamandras, bandidos y orientales! Entonces habremos hecho nuestra parte para ayudar a la gente de Langhold a regresar algún día a sus hogares.'","'He oído que el primer pueblo que encontraremos en el reino de Rohan se llama Langhold. ¡Vamos allí sin demora!'","'En lo que a mí respecta, nunca he sido muy amigo de los caballos. ¡Son tan grandes y aterradores, siempre pisoteando con sus pesadas pezuñas y mordiendo a hobbits desprevenidos con sus fuertes dientes! Me mordió casi un caballo cuando era un tween, ¿sabes?, y nunca he conseguido perdonar a esas criaturas.\
\
'¿Crees que podrías bajar a la puerta este de Stangard y preguntarle a Sabert si podríamos disfrutar un recorrido a pie por el reino de Rohan? No es un lugar muy grande, ¿verdad? Si nuestros pies bastan, entonces digo que eso es lo que debemos hacer, ¡y dejar completamente fuera a los caballos!'","Derrota bandidos en el Páramo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","La carga de Bingo","Bandidos derrotados en el Páramo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Habla con Bingo en el pueblo de Langhold, en el Páramo","'¿Qué dijo Sabert sobre recorrer Rohan a pie, ${PLAYER}? ¿Es el reino lo bastante pequeño como para que eso sea razonable?'\
\
Le dices a Bingo que Sabert realmente cree que es mejor montar a caballo en Rohan.\
\
'Él diría eso, claro. Los rohirrim sin duda aman a sus caballos. Yo no siento necesidad alguna de subirme a una de esas temibles bestias. ¡Yo digo que caminemos! ¿Qué piensas tú, ${PLAYER}? ¿Es esta nuestra aventura o la de Sabert? ¡Un poco de ejercicio no nos vendrá mal! Háblame cuando podamos comenzar nuestra caminata por Rohan.'","'¡Buen trabajo, ${PLAYER}! Langhold no está en condiciones de recibir a su gente todavía, y no lo estará por un tiempo, pero quizá nuestros esfuerzos en el Páramo les ayuden cuando regresen.'\
\
Bingo respira hondo, preparándose aparentemente para algo.\
\
'Sabes, ${PLAYER}, quizá tenías razón con lo del caballo. Sabert y Egwylf también. Rohan es bastante más grande de lo que pensaba, y quizá yo también deba conseguir un caballo. Por lo visto, hay caballos a la venta en la ciudad de Harwick, al sur. Supongo que deberíamos ir y ver.'","Bingo sabe que debe viajar al reino de Rohan, pero su miedo a los caballos hace que esa idea le resulte aterradora y enlentezca sus pasos.","'Si podemos derrotar salamandras, bandidos y orientales por todo el Páramo, creo que habremos hecho este lugar mucho más seguro para la gente de Langhold. ¡Vamos!'","Habla con Bingo en Stangard y camina con él hacia Rohan","'¡Luchemos contra los diversos enemigos que acechan cerca: salamandras, bandidos y orientales! Entonces estaremos haciendo nuestra parte para ayudar a la gente de Langhold a regresar algún día a sus hogares.'","Derrota orientales en el Páramo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[1722]={"'Deberías seguir estas pistas y ver si puedes encontrar las páginas restantes del manuscrito de Bingo.\
\
'Los merrevail de la Fosa de los Colmillos podrían tener algunas páginas. Los orcos y los jinetes de huargos recorren grandes distancias por Zelem-melek, y podrían haber encontrado páginas. Se formó un consejo de guerra en Anazârmekhem, en las Profundidades Llameantes, y sus líderes podrían haber descubierto páginas. Los enanos de la Sala Vigesimoprimera que reciben mucho tránsito por sus servicios, como los guardianes de cofres o los bardos, también podrían haber llegado a poseer páginas.'","'¡Recordé algo más, ${PLAYER}! Cuando Spalvi y yo huimos de la fortaleza Duramano en las Montañas Nubladas y caí a las cavernas de abajo, ¿sabes qué ocurrió? ¡Caí en un río subterráneo! El agua me heló hasta los huesos, y creo que el impacto repentino con el agua helada fue lo que expulsó los recuerdos de mi mente.\
\
'¿Pero sabes qué recordé? Cuando toqué el agua, debí de olvidar también que no sabía nadar, ¡porque seguí la corriente como un pez! ¡Supongo que solo necesitaba un poco de motivación extra! ¿Qué te parece?'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>La próxima semana: 'Una despedida' (Nivel recomendado: 58)</rgb>","'Hola, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo nuevo[m]|amiga nueva[f]}:. Siento no recordarte y, no solo eso: ¡no puedo recordar por qué no puedo recordar! Sí, ¿qué es esto?'\
\
Le entregas a Bingo la página de su manuscrito que Willem Bigotes sacó de la poza junto al Camino de Durin, y él la mira entornando los ojos durante unos instantes.\
\
'Veamos... Nuevoburgo... Los Gamos... Claro que sé dónde están esos lugares. ¡Todo hobbit de la Comarca lo sabe! Vaya, esta hobbit tiene muchos hijos. Angélica, Berilac, Camelia, Dinodas, Esmeralda, Fosco, Griffo... oh, ahí se termina la página. ¿Sabes una cosa? Casi creí recordar a alguien, una muchacha pelirroja y... ¿una espada? No, no es del todo correcto.\
\
'Lo siento, pero de verdad no me acuerdo.'","Habla con Bingo en la Sala Vigesimoprimera","'Sabes, hay algo que podríamos intentar. ¿Recuerdas la página del manuscrito que encontró Willem? Está casi seca ahora y casi legible. Quizá si se la mostraras a Bingo podría ser justo el recordatorio que necesita nuestro autor para recuperar su memoria perdida.\
\
'¡Yo digo que vale la pena intentarlo, ${PLAYER}!'","La memoria de Bingo ha regresado!","'Fue una historia interesante, y no me importaría leer más. ¡Pero si se suponía que debía hacerme recordar, lamento decir que no lo hizo!'","Bingo está en Sala Vigesimoprimera, listo para leer el manuscrito que ensamblaste.","Habla con Willem Bigotes en la Sala Vigesimoprimera","Sigue las pistas de Spalvi para encontrar páginas del manuscrito de Bingo (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'Bueno, ¿funcionó?'","'¡Debes estar buscando esto!', exclama Vagun, levantando tres trozos de pergamino que han visto días mejores.\
\
'Los de este consejo hemos estado llevando a cabo una campaña contra los orcos, y debo decirte que ¡estos papeles nos han tenido bastante desconcertados! ¿Ves esta página? ¡Esta secuencia de letras es claramente un código! ¡Y todo este hablar de gansos y ocas! Creíamos que los orcos tramaban algún plan, ¡y es un alivio saber que no!\
\
'Toma, puedes quedártelos. ¡Ya hemos perdido suficiente tiempo con estas páginas!'","Bingo está en la Sala Vigesimoprimera de Moria.\
\
Bingo ha terminado de leer su manuscrito, y deberías hablar con él para ver si eso le ha ayudado a recuperar la memoria.","Spalvi dijo que se reuniría contigo en la Sala Vigesimoprimera después de que siguieras todas sus pistas.","Spalvi te dio varias pistas a seguir que podrían ayudarte a reunir las páginas perdidas del manuscrito de Bingo: \
\
'Los merrevail de la Fosa de los Colmillos podrían tener algunas páginas. Los orcos y los jinetes de huargos recorren grandes distancias por Zelem-melek, y podrían haber encontrado páginas. Se formó un consejo de guerra en Anazârmekhem, en las Profundidades Llameantes, y sus líderes podrían haber descubierto páginas. Los enanos de la Sala Vigesimoprimera que reciben mucho tránsito por sus servicios, como los guardianes de cofres o los bardos, también podrían haber conseguido páginas.'","Espera a que Bingo termine de leer el relato de su viaje","'¡Recuerda! Me alegra muchísimo ver que todo ha salido bien, ${PLAYER}! Pido disculpas por todos los problemas que causé, y espero que me perdones por ellos, pero debes admitir que todos hemos aprendido mucho desde que nuestro hobbit cayó en las montañas.\
\
'En realidad, parece que su aventura aún está en sus primeras etapas, ¡y planea escribir muchos capítulos después de este!'","'Bueno, ese fue un relato interesante, pero no puedo decir que nada de él me resulte familiar.'\
\
Bingo te mira fijamente y de pronto rompe en una amplia sonrisa.\
\
'¡Solo bromeo, ${PLAYER}! Para ser sincero, lo recordé todo por completo después de la primera página de este relato, pero pensé que sería un buen momento para leerlo entero y ver si mi opinión sobre la opinión de Bilbo había cambiado. ¡Creo que puede ser bastante emocionante después de todo, pero ahora temo que sea demasiado corto! ¡Necesitaremos tener más aventuras, sin duda!\
\
'Pero hay algo más que debo decirte. Este Spalvi es un buen tipo, y quiero que sepas que lo perdono completamente por aquel malentendido con los Duramano. En realidad me trató con amabilidad, y en la primera oportunidad me liberó de aquella jaula a pesar de que su gente se enfadaría mucho con él por ello. ¡Espero que no hayas desconfiado demasiado de él por mi culpa!'","'Dale ese libro a Bingo y que lo lea, ¡y veremos si esto funciona!'","Spalvi Corazonrecio está en el campamento enano cerca de la Fosa de los Colmillos.","Por primera vez desde que Bingo desapareció, Willem Bigotes parece genuinamente feliz. Si escuchas con atención, quizá incluso oigas un zumbido en lo profundo: Willem está ronroneando satisfecho.","'Alguien sí me dio un par de páginas para que las guardara, pero, siendo sincero, no recuerdo quién fue. ¿Fuiste tú? ${RACE}, ¿Es eso? Seguro que es eso. ¡Son todas tuyas!'","'No fue suficiente, ¡pero creo que podríamos ir por buen camino! Si localizáramos las páginas restantes del manuscrito de Bingo y se las mostráramos, ¡podría ser justo el recordatorio que necesita para recuperar sus memorias perdidas! Debemos suponer que dejó caer su manuscrito cuando cayó, y las páginas se dispersaron por todo Khazad-dûm. Cualquiera podría haberlas recogido.\
\
'Pero hay algunos lugares en los que podemos mirar:\
\
'Los merrevail de la Fosa de los Colmillos podrían tener algunas páginas.\
\
'Los orcos y los jinetes de huargos recorren grandes distancias por Zelem-melek, y podrían haber encontrado algunas páginas.\
\
'Se formó un consejo de guerra en Anazârmekhem, en las Profundidades Llameantes, y sus líderes podrían haber descubierto páginas.\
\
'Los enanos de la Sala Vigesimoprimera que reciben mucho tránsito por sus servicios, como los guardianes de cofres o los bardos, también podrían haber adquirido páginas.\
\
'¡Cuando hayas seguido todas estas pistas, me reuniré contigo en la Sala Vigesimoprimera!'","Spalvi y Willem Bigotes están en la Sala Vigesimoprimera, esperando ver si Bingo ha recuperado sus recuerdos.","Habla con Spalvi en la Sala Vigesimoprimera","'Este Spalvi es un buen tipo, y quiero que sepas que lo perdono completamente por aquel malentendido con los Duramano. De verdad me trató con amabilidad, y a la primera oportunidad me soltó de esa jaula a pesar de que su gente se enfadaría mucho con él por ello. ¡Espero que no hayas desconfiado demasiado de él por mi culpa!'","Bingo ha terminado de leer su manuscrito... ¿ha funcionado?","Bingo está leyendo su propio manuscrito... ¡pero no lo sabe!","'¡Espero que esto funcione!'","Tres páginas dispersas recogidas","Bingo Boffin está en la Fosa de los Colmillos.\
\
Spalvi te ha dado la página del manuscrito que Willem Bigotes encontró en Moria y cree que, si se la muestras a Bingo, podría ayudarle a recuperar la memoria.","Estás seguro de que Bingo casi recordó. ¡Si tan solo hubiera más páginas!","Lleva las páginas del manuscrito de Bingo a Spalvi en la Sala Vigesimoprimera","'¿Estás buscando páginas de un manuscrito? ¡Tengo una justo aquí! Disfruté bastante leyendo sobre la tranquila paz del Bosque de los Trolls, pero por desgracia la historia no estaba terminada: se corta a mitad de una frase. La frase es «Desperté descansado por la mañana, listo para afrontar el día, como también...» ¡Y eso es todo!\
\
'Puedes quedártela, si la quieres.'","Dos páginas dispersas recogidas","'¿Recuerdas la página del manuscrito que encontró Willem? Ahora está casi seca y casi legible. Quizá, si se la mostrases a Bingo, podría ser justo el recordatorio que necesita nuestro autor para recuperar su memoria perdida.'","Los pensamientos dispersos de Bingo","Bingo está en la Sala Vigesimoprimera de Moria.","Habla con Spalvi en la Fosa de los Colmillos","'Ah, ¿me has traído más páginas de ese relato para leer? ¡Me encantaría tener algo de lectura, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]} amante de los libros!\
\
'Dámelo, y me acomodaré para una buena lectura. Solo tomará un instante o dos.'","Lleva el manuscrito restaurado a Bingo en la Sala Vigesimoprimera","Seguiste las pistas de Spalvi (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Muestra a Bingo la página seca de su manuscrito en la Fosa de los Colmillos","Página dispersa recogida","Has encontrado a Bingo, pero él perdió algo suyo mientras estuvo fuera: ¡su memoria!","'¿Encontraste el resto del manuscrito de Bingo? ¡Bien hecho, ${PLAYER}! Déjame poner estas páginas en orden... ¡listo!\
\
'Ahora dale este libro a Bingo y que lo lea, ¡y veremos si esto funciona!'"},
[1723]={"Sendiel se encuentra en el Claro Apacible, al sur y ligeramente al oeste de Cerin Brethil.\
\
Deberías regresar con Sendiel con las semillas.","Se pueden encontrar musarañas en Taur Hith, en particular en la zona alrededor de Cerin Brethil, al norte y ligeramente al este del Claro Apacible.\
\
Sendiel te ha pedido que recuperes semillas de las musarañas.","Cantaste a los retoños de malbrethil para mejorar su salud. Ahora Sendiel desea aumentar su número.","Recupera semillas de malbrethil (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¿Has encontrado las semillas que te pedí? ¡Por favor, tráemelas lo antes posible!'","Habla con Sendiel en el Claro Apacible","Semillas de malbrethil recuperadas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¡Has regresado! Veamos... sí, maravilloso. Estas semillas deberían haber sobrevivido a su pequeño desvío por las musarañas. No preveo ninguna dificultad para plantarlas.\
\
'Con suerte, pronto veremos más retoños de malbrethil, si todo marcha bien.'","'Has sido de gran ayuda, ${PLAYER}. Gracias a ti, no solo sabemos qué estaba debilitando a nuestros queridos melbrethil, sino que también puedo enviar aviso a Mallendathor para reclutar a otros visitantes que ayuden a reparar el daño que su presencia en Lothlórien está causando.\
\
'Está claro que hemos descuidado nuestra vigilancia sobre los melbrethil. Tengo una tarea más para ti: dirígete a Taur Hith, en particular a la zona que rodea Cerin Brethil.\
\
'Sospecho que la razón por la que hemos visto menos melbrethil es que las musarañas de la zona se están alimentando de sus semillas. Por favor, recupera algunas de esas semillas y tráelas aquí... los animales las acumulan en gran número para las estaciones más frías.'","Madre de los abedules"},
[1724]={"Los morrovals utilizan varios percheros como nidos. Gúri cree que si se destruyeran, la colonia quedaría paralizada.","El campamento de los morrovals se encuentra en Skoiruzg, al este del campamento de la Fosa Colmilluda.\
\
Gúri te ha pedido que destruyas los percheros de los morrovals y derrotes a varios frondeadores.","'¡Excelente trabajo, ${PLAYER}! Ahora los morrovals se verán obligados a bajar al suelo, donde estaremos a la par, y con menos frondeadores, podremos atacar con nuestras hachas sin temor a sus dardos. ¡Ahora se han convertido en la presa!\
\
¡Ja! Me pregunto qué pensará su reina de sus frondeadores ahora que han fallado en proteger sus áreas de anidación. \
\
Sí, su reina. Parece que están gobernados por una criatura a la que llaman Aquella-Que-Debe-Ser-Obedecida-En-Todo.'","Destruye los nidos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Derrota a los frondeadores en Skoiruzg (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Gúri está en el campamento de la Fosa Colmilluda, al oeste de Skoiruzg.\
\
Gúri se alegrará de saber que los percheros de los morrovals han sido destruidos y que el camino hacia el campamento está libre de ataques de los frondeadores.","Frondeadores derrotados en Skoiruzg (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Aves de presa","'Los morrovals que vuelan por encima del suelo se alzan por la noche. Sin embargo, en Khazad-dûm, anidan y duermen en varios percheros altos sobre las cavernas, como si fueran extrañas aves. Si esos percheros cayeran, se verían obligados a bajar al suelo, donde podríamos enfrentarlos con nuestro acero.\
\
La mayor colección de percheros se encuentra en el campamento más alejado al este, Skoiruzg. Mientras asaltas sus nidos, ten cuidado con los frondeadores que te encuentres. Cuando ataquemos, necesitamos asegurarnos de poder acercarnos, y su capacidad para luchar a distancia podría suponer un problema.\
\
Date prisa, ${PLAYER}. Mucho depende de tu éxito.'","Habla con Gúri en el campamento de la Fosa Colmilluda","'Debemos forzar a los morrovals a bajar al suelo y asegurarnos de que nuestro acercamiento no se vea obstaculizado.'","Nidos destruidos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[1725]={"Los hendrevail han comenzado a anidar en Kamskut, una estructura de aspecto siniestro situada en las montañas al noreste de Othrikar.\
\
Deberías investigar Kamskut, pues este comportamiento de anidación seguramente no es natural.","Derrota a los Halconero Duramano (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Los hendrevail han comenzado a anidar en Kamskut, una estructura de aspecto siniestro situada en las montañas al noreste de Othrikar.","El Halconero Brúni está en Kamskut, en las Quebradas del Norte, al noreste de Othrikar.\
\
Debes derrotar a Brúni y a sus fauconeros.","Derrota a Brúni y a sus Halconeros","Pájaros de un mismo plumaje","Completado","Halconero Duramano derrotado (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Has derrotado a Brúni, un Halconero Duramano, y a sus compañeros en Kamskut."},
[1727]={"Continue learning the history of the Rohirrim with Léothred","Framsburg can be found in Misthallow.\
\
You should learn the history of the Rohirrim with Léothred.","Hlithseld is located in the north of Misthallow.\
\
You should talk to Léothred at Hlithseld.","Framsburg can be found in Misthallow.\
\
You should find Fram's silver horn, buried somewhere in the ruins of Framsburg.","Talk to Léothred at Hlithseld","Learn the history of the Rohirrim with Léothred","Léothred, the Rohirric scholar, seeks to learn more of his people's history in Misthallow.","'Nine years into Eorl’s rule, a man in green came to the Wells, bloodied and exhausted from long riding without rest. Borondir was his name, and he was of mixed Dúnadan and Thíuda blood. Cirion, Steward of Gondor, had sent him as one of six errand-riders in search of aid from the Northmen against an army of Orcs and Balchoth, Easterlings who had come to invade the South-kingdom in force.'","Léothred can be found at Framsburg.\
\
You should talk to Léothred at Framsburg.","Find Fram's silver horn","Talk to Léothred at Framsburg","'Our time researching the Éothéod nears its end. This is a joyous finale, as it signals the birth of the Eorlingas. Let us continue!'","Birth of the Eorlingas","Talk to Léothred elsewhere at Framsburg","Travel to Hlithseld to rest","'The arrival of the Éothéod at the Field of Celebrant helped win the day and defeat the hosts of the East, saving the South-kingdom from ruin. As thanks for their aid, Cirion granted to the Éothéod the lands that Lord Cendric had spoken of, and which Eorl’s ancestors had desired since the fall of Wilderland. These were the green fields of Calenardhon, now all but emptied as the Dúnedain’s numbers dwindled. Swearing an oath of fealty forever to Gondor, Eorl accepted Cirion’s offer and sent riders to summon the rest of his people to join him in his new realm. Henceforth, the Éothéod, now known as the Eorlingas, would dwell in the Riddermark of Rohan, and Eorl and his descendants would be its kings.\
\
'Let us return to Hlithseld, ${PLAYER}. It has been a long day.'","'There, I have traced the history of my people as best I could. I have filled in the gaps from the Ai-thúda to the Éothéod, and their journey to Rohan. I could not have done it alone. I thank you for your assistance, many times over!\
\
'You are free to leave me here if you must. Yes, I have writing to do, and there is not a better place to write all this down than near the ruins of Framsburg. There are gaps yet to fill in the tale, this much I can see.\
\
'I am still puzzled by many of the old tales and songs. What about the worm, Scatha, that Fram fought? Fram's deeds will need uncovering! The dwarves in the mountains must have played their part in history of the Éothéod too, yes? Hmm, I have much to think about. Perhaps I will call upon you again soon. Until then, my friend!'","Hlithseld is located in the north of Misthallow.\
\
You should travel to Hlithseld and rest."},
[1728]={"Wisewood the Ent is in the north-east corner of Fangorn's eaves.\
\
You should speak with Wisewood once more.","The Ent is perfectly still, but its eyes are open. You could swear that this one has an angry red gleam in his greenish eyes... or perhaps a flare of panic. It is hard to tell when his outward behaviour is so still.\
\
You smell smoke here and see the orange glow of fire. It is not hard to guess why this Ent may be angry.","Helped Wisewood (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Help Wisewood (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","You have found another sleeping Ent in need of assistance.","Biting and Burning","A Huorn stands near the White Hand encampment, watching your every move.\
\
You should approach the Huorn cautiously.","Approach the Huorn who watches you","The Huorn makes no move to attack you, but regards you with interest. It is likely that you and it have the same goals, for now."},
[1729]={"Biting the Hand that Feeds","Complete Guidance of the White Hand","Complete Servants of the White Hand","Evidence supports Gwilum's beliefs that the Warg-riders plaguing Carreglyn are in fact servants of Saruman the White... and that his own rulers are in league with them.","Talk to Amlan at his camp in the Gravenwood","Gwilum is at the gate to Barnavon.\
\
Gwilum has asked you to help him against the Warg-riders in the north.","Complete Hounds of the White Hand","'Well met again, ${PLAYER}. So you were able to bring aid to old Gwilum and the Boar-clan? That is well.\
\
'Now, however, I have a vital task for you....'","Complete Summons of the White Hand","Amlan is encamped beneath the eaves of the Gravenwood.\
\
Gwilum asked you to bring word of your successes to the Ranger Amlan.","'While you were lending aid to the Turch-lûth, I looked over the items you brought me from your hunt. I fear the news is grim. It is clear to me now that the Warg-riders are in fact servants of Saruman of Many Colours. It also appears that the Brenin and his brehur are in league with them!\
\
'I believe I now know the origin of the Wargs... one of the items you brought to me was a piece of rune-marked tree-bark. It is in the tongue of my own people and can be found upon ritual trees in the Gravenwood. I believe that the Warg-riders must be encamped somewhere near the Gravenwood, along the road to the north.\
\
'You should know as well that other duvodiad from the north passed that way, Men allied with the Boar-clan resistance. One of them -- Amlan, I believe his name is -- is encamped just within the eaves of the Gravenwood. If you would help me against the riders, I am certain Amlan will have a reward for you.'"},
[1730]={"Acaba con dunlendinos en la Escuela de Tham Mírdain (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Líderes de la Mano Blanca derrotado (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Dunlendinos derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Ataque a la Mano Blanca","Acaba con arqueros de la Mano Blanca (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","La Escuela de Tham Mírdain se encuentra al sureste de Echad Mirobel.\
\
Lefnuichen, un elfo de Echad Mirobel, te ha pedido que expulses por la fuerza a la Mano Blanca, ya que los uruks y los dunlendinos se han apoderado de la Escuela que, por derecho, pertenece a los elfos.","Los uruk-hai y los hombres de las Tierras Brunas controlan la Escuela de Tham Mírdain, y poco podemos hacer al respecto. He oído que hay pequeñas fuerzas que se dirigen a la Biblioteca de Tham Mírdain para hacer frente a la amenaza del norte. Espero hacer lo mismo contra los enemigos a los que nos enfrentamos desde el sur.\
\
La Escuela de Tham Mírdain fue en su día un lugar de aprendizaje donde se intercambiaban ideas libremente, y los elfos debatían asuntos importantes y conocimientos. Ahora yace en ruinas, pero las fuerzas de la Mano Blanca creen que aún puede haber algo dentro de esos muros que merezca la pena llevarse.\
\
Pido a cualquiera que desee ayudarnos que entre en la Escuela de Tham Mírdain y expulse a la Mano Blanca de ese lugar abandonado. Encontraréis la entrada al sureste de nuestra posición.","Arqueros de la Mano Blanca derrotado (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Acaba con líderes de la Mano Blanca (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[1731]={"Recover valuable goods (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Recovered valuable goods (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Return to Yâshri with the valuable goods","Bits and Baubles","Find and recover valuable goods scattered amongst the Dead in Ghâr Mejet.","Return to Yâshri with the valuable goods.\
\
Yâshri can be found just north of Ghâr Mejet.","'Your work is excellent, and these valuable goods will go a long way to support our cause. I cannot express my thanks greatly enough, as now my family and friends have food to eat for the coming months.'","Yâshri has requested that you help recover items of value from Ghâr Mejet.","'Scattered throughout this cursed place are bits and baubles that can be sold topside so that our small settlement can afford supplies and food. While this is dangerous work, it is necessary for our people's survival.\
\
'If you are brave enough, could you scour the area and recover some of these objects?'"},
[1732]={"Fredegar ya está trabajando en un plan para encargarse de Lotho y sus Fronteros","Habla con Lotho Sacovilla-Bolsón fuera de Ojo de Aguja","'¡No dejaré que te salgas con la tuya, Lotho!'\
\
Fredegar respira profundamente y se calma antes de hablarte en tono bajo.\
\
'${PLAYER}, tengo un plan. Hay un almacén de la Guardia de Allende no lejos de aquí, que se ha convertido en un escondite secreto para mí y mis amigos. ¡Reúnete conmigo allí en cuanto puedas!'\
\
Fredegar se vuelve hacia Lotho.\
\
'Hasta la próxima vez, Lotho. ¡Esto no ha acabado!'","Fronteras amargas","'¡Lo has conseguido! Ese Lotho no ha sido nunca mucho de discutir, y con la edad ha ido a peor.\
\
'Desafortunadamente para él, nosotros nos hemos vuelto más serios e inteligentes, ¿no?'","Lotho Sacovilla-Bolsón se encuentra en el este de la Comarca Allende, fuera de Ojo de Aguja.\
\
Debes hablar con Lotho Sacovilla-Bolsón.","Habla con Fredegar Bolger","Lotho y algunos de sus compinches han llegado a la Comarca Allende","'Buenas, ¿qué tienes ahí?'\
\
Lotho te mira con el ceño fruncido.\
\
'¿Crees que agitar esta lista de nombres delante de mi cara va a hacerme cambiar de idea? Las viejas fronteras funcionaban bien, ¡cuando la Cuaderna del Oeste y la Cuaderna del Norte terminaban donde debían! ¿Quién necesita que la Comarca Allende sea parte de la Comarca? Ni yo, ni nadie, ¡al menos ningún hobbit de bien!\
\
'¡Escuchad bien, personajillos! Neceistamos cambiar las fronteras para poder mantener la Comarca propiamente dicha segura. U os movéis o ya no estaréis en la Comarca. Es así de sencillo.\
\
'No tiene sentido intentar discutirlo, y la Guardia de Allende no tiene nada que decir al respecto. De hecho, voy a mandar a mis Fronteros personales a la Comarca Allende para asegurarme de que nadie intenta manipular las fronteras establecidas. ¡Ja!'","Lotho Sacovilla-Bolsón se encuentra en el este de la Comarca Allende, fuera de Ojo de Aguja.\
\
Debes viajar hacia Ojo de Aguja con Fredegar Bolger.","Fredegar Bolger planea disputar a Lotho Sacovilla-Bolsón el marcado oficial de las fronteras.","Hay un almacén secreto de la Guardia de Allende en los bosques entre Gamwich y Quiebra Larga.\
\
Debes hablar con Fredegar Bolger en el almacén de la Guardia de Allende.","'Qué bienque hayas vuelto, porque este asunto se ha vuelto más urgente. ¡La Guardia de Allende me ha informado que el hobbit buscando cambiar las fronteras ha sido avistado cerca de Ojo de Aguja! Es un tipo agrio llamado Lotho Sacovilla-Bolsón. ¿Lo conoces?\
\
'Vamos a buscarle y veamos si está dispuesto a abandonar esta equivocada campaña suya.'","Hay un almacén secreto de la Guardia de Allende en los bosques entre Gamwich y Quiebra Larga.\
\
Fredegar Bolger te ha pedido que te reagrupes en el almacén secreto de la Guardia de Allende.","Habla con Lotho Sacovilla-Bolsón entre Ojo de Aguja y la Comarca Allende","Fredegar Bolger se encuentra en el este de la Comarca Allende, fuera de Ojo de Aguja.\
\
Debes hablar con Fredegar Bolger.","Reagrúpate en el almacén secreto de la Guardia de Allende","Habla con Fredegar Bolger en el escondite secreto"},
[1734]={"Lleva las Insignias Negras a Cannuion en Tinnudir.","Insignia negra recogida (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Los Angmarim, bajo el mando de Númenóreanos Negros, han ocupado la ciudad en ruinas de Annúminas.","Insignias Negras — Introducción","'Noticias inquietantes nos llegan de nuestros agentes dentro de la ciudad en ruinas de Annúminas. Los Angmarim han desplazado grandes fuerzas al interior de los muros. Se rumorea que muchos de los que allí sirven lo hacen bajo el estandarte de un Númenóreano Negro enviado desde el propio Mordor, portando insignias negras de lealtad al Señor Oscuro.\
\
'Si logras infiltrarte en la ciudad, derrotar a quienes profanan sus calles y traerme sus insignias negras como prueba, ¡ganarás gran prestigio entre los Guardianes de Annúminas!'","'Eres, sin duda, alguien valiente por haber osado recorrer las calles en ruinas de Annúminas. Te felicito por tu valor, aunque aún nos quedan muchas batallas antes de poder arrebatar la ciudad de sus manos.'","Se pueden encontrar Angmarim dentro de los muros en ruinas de Annúminas. Cannuion está en Tinnudir.\
\
Cannuion te ha pedido que le lleves las insignias negras de los Angmarim de Annúminas.","'Entiendo que enfrentarse a los invasores en las calles de Annúminas no es tarea para corazones débiles, pero no te he considerado nunca de ese tipo. Confío en que, a su tiempo, tu fuerza se demostrará ante nuestros enemigos.'","Recoge Insignias Negras (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[1735]={"Vatnar is concerned that the Orkish ballistae mounted around Gathbúrz pose a serious threat to Rodelleth's warriors.","Orkish ballistae can be found throughout northern Gathbúrz.\
\
Vatnar has asked you to destroy several Orkish ballistae to clear the way for the Malledhrim.","'Good day, ${PLAYER}! It is a fine day for a battle, don't you think? It will be a pleasure indeed to see that dark spire crumble, but we've got some messy business to attend to in Gathbúrz first.\
\
'The goblins have built a number of nasty little toys for the Orcs of Gathbúrz, a few of which we have captured here... but the rest have to go. These Elves may be the finest warriors I've seen outside of Thorin's Hall, but fancy swords and bows don't help much with a yard-long bolt pinning them to the ground!\
\
'Those ballistae are the greatest threat to Rodelleth and her warriors, so you should deal with those first. They are easy enough to break once you reach them. A couple of good strikes with a hammer or blade will put them out of commission quickly.'","Talk to Vatnar in Thangúlhad","Vatnar is at Thangúlhad in Gathbúrz.\
\
You should return to Vatnar with news of your success.","'So you managed to wreck a few of the Orc's toys? Well that's done then, on to the next order of business shall we?\
\
'Time is of the essence, if we are to bring that great pile of rock down around the ears of those cloaked fiends!'","Black Bolts","'Destroy the ballistae of the Enemy, ${PLAYER}, else they will prove a bane to the Golden Host.'","Destroyed ballistae (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Destroy ballistae (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[1736]={"Desafío Negro","Este tosco fragmento de texto está escrito en la Lengua Negra. Los garabatos extranjeros y apresurados no tienen significado para tus ojos. Se dice que los Elfos de Rivendel comprenden la lengua de Mordor. Quizá alguno de ellos pueda traducir el mensaje y revelar su propósito.","Encuentra a un erudito en Rivendel que pueda traducir el Lenguaje Negro.","El Enemigo habla un lenguaje terrible conocido como la Lengua Negra. Planes y mensajes al Falso Rey, sus generales y comandantes, son frecuentemente llevados al combate por sus secuaces.","'¿La Lengua Negra? Sí, he visto este tipo de cosas antes. Aunque las palabras hieren como veneno en mi lengua, la situación requiere la habilidad de leer la lengua del Enemigo, aunque ninguna palabra de ella se había pronunciado antes —hasta hace poco— en Imladris.\
\
'Este es un desafío a un campeón oscuro de algún tipo. Será mejor que transcriba una versión traducida y la conserve en mi biblioteca.'","Rivendel se encuentra en las Trollshaws, muy al sur de Angmar.\
\
Has descubierto un extraño texto, escrito en el Lenguaje Negro. Los Elfos de Rivendel podrían ser capaces de traducirlo."},
[1738]={"'You found and extinguished a number of strange black torches?\
\
'I think you have likely found the power behind the Shadow-wolves. I cannot say whether your efforts will destroy them for good or not, but I will be most surprised if they are able to take up the hunt for us again so soon with their dark power so diminished.\
\
'You have my gratitude, ${PLAYER}.'","The black torch on the wall before you casts twisted shadows upon the cavern floor....","'Seek the source of the Shadow-wolves' power in the Black Dens to the south-east.'","Find the source of the Shadow-wolves' power","Torch doused (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Amarion is at Echad Dagoras, north-west of the Black Dens.\
\
You should return to Amarion with tidings of what you found in the Black Dens.","The Black Dens lie to the south-east of Echad Dagoras.\
\
Amarion has asked you to enter the Black Dens and find the source of the Shadow-wolves' power.","Shadow-torches can be found throughout the caverns of the Black Dens.\
\
You should douse the torches within the Black Dens to break the strange enchantment that summons forth the Shadow-wolves.","'Our attempts to stop these Shadow-wolves have borne no fruit thus far.\
\
'The source of their evil must lie within the caverns in the Black Dens. If you can find your way into them and destroy it, we may gain some respite from their relentless hunt.\
\
'Go now, and may the Valar watch over you.'","'Have you found the source of the Shadow-wolves' power yet?'","Douse torches (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Amarion at Echad Dagoras","Black Flames","The Shadow-wolves of the Black Dens are clearly no ordinary wolves. Some spirit of evil empowers them and guides them."},
[1739]={"Collect black heartwood from Black Huorns (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Blackthorn can be found in the eaves of Fangorn, north of Tordag's encampment.\
\
You should bring the Black Huorn heartwood to the Ent Blackthorn.","Bring the black heartwood you collected to Blackthorn","The Ent Blackthorn is disturbed by the emergence of Black Huorns from the heart of Fangorn, which do not heed his voice.","'You could find no more black heartwood? Perhaps it is not as bad as I thought.'","Black Huorns may be found throughout the eaves of Fangorn bordering the Broadacres.\
\
Blackthorn asked you to bring him more of the black heartwood, so that he might learn the origin of the corruption.","Black Hearts","'Little ${RACE}, this black heartwood concerns me. No natural ailment afflicted it. Hoom, I need more to study. Bring me the heartwood of the Black Huorns, so that I might determine what evil has come to this wood.\
\
'Ta-rum, if it is as widespread as I fear, much of the forest might be ruined....'","'Ta-rum! It is as I thought! There is sorcery in these hearts, and there is but one power near Fangorn capable of this evil.\
\
'Young Saruman has, hoom, has much to account for. He and his burárum have wrought great destruction in this wood. Now he shall see me positively hasty!'","Collected black heartwood from Black Huorns (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[1740]={"Collect black heartwood from Black Huorns (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Bring the black heartwood you collected to Blackthorn","The Ent Blackthorn is disturbed by the emergence of Black Huorns from the heart of Fangorn, which do not heed his voice.","'You could find no more black heartwood? Perhaps it is not as bad as I thought.'","Black Huorns may be found throughout the eaves of Fangorn bordering the Broadacres.\
\
Blackthorn asked you to bring him more of the black heartwood, so that he might learn the origin of the corruption.","Black Hearts","'Little ${RACE}, this black heartwood concerns me. No natural ailment afflicted it. Hoom, I need more to study. Bring me the heartwood of the Black Huorns, so that I might determine what evil has come to this wood.\
\
'Ta-rum, if it is as widespread as I fear, much of the forest might be ruined....'","Blackthorn awaits your return in the eaves of Fangorn, bordering the Broadacres.\
\
You should bring the black heartwood that you collected to Blackthorn the Ent.","'Ta-rum! It is as I thought! There is sorcery in these hearts, and there is but one power near Fangorn capable of this evil.\
\
'Young Saruman has, hoom, has much to account for. He and his burárum have wrought great destruction in this wood. Now he shall see me positively hasty!'","Collected black heartwood from Black Huorns (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[1742]={"Rivendel está en el Bosque de los Trolls, al sur de Angmar.\
\
Has descubierto un extraño fragmento de texto, escrito en la Lengua Negra. Los Elfos de Rivendel podrían traducirlo.","Este tosco fragmento de texto está escrito en la Lengua Negra. Los garabatos extranjeros y apresurados no tienen significado para tus ojos. Se dice que los Elfos de Rivendel comprenden la lengua de Mordor. Quizá alguno de ellos pueda traducir el mensaje y revelar su propósito.","Encuentra a un erudito en Rivendel que pueda traducir el Lenguaje Negro.","El Enemigo habla un lenguaje terrible conocido como la Lengua Negra. Planes y mensajes al Falso Rey, sus generales y comandantes, son frecuentemente llevados al combate por sus secuaces.","Maldiciones Negras","'¿La Lengua Negra? Sí, he visto este tipo de cosas antes. Aunque las palabras hieren como veneno en mi lengua, la situación requiere la habilidad de leer la lengua del Enemigo, aunque ninguna palabra de ella se había pronunciado antes —hasta hace poco— en Imladris.\
\
'Este es un desafío a un campeón oscuro de algún tipo. Será mejor que transcriba una versión traducida y la conserve en mi biblioteca.'"},
[1743]={"Encantamientos Negros","Rivendel está en el Bosque de los Trolls, al sur de Angmar.\
\
Has descubierto un extraño fragmento de texto, escrito en la Lengua Negra. Los Elfos de Rivendel podrían traducirlo.","Este tosco fragmento de texto está escrito en la Lengua Negra. Los garabatos extranjeros y apresurados no tienen significado para tus ojos. Se dice que los Elfos de Rivendel comprenden la lengua de Mordor. Quizá alguno de ellos pueda traducir el mensaje y revelar su propósito.","Encuentra un erudito en Rivendel que pueda traducir la Lengua Negra.","El Enemigo habla un lenguaje terrible conocido como la Lengua Negra. Planes y mensajes al Falso Rey, sus generales y comandantes, son frecuentemente llevados al combate por sus secuaces.","'¿La Lengua Negra? Sí, he visto este tipo de cosas antes. Aunque las palabras hieren como veneno en mi lengua, la situación requiere la habilidad de leer la lengua del Enemigo, aunque ninguna palabra de ella se había pronunciado antes —hasta hace poco— en Imladris.\
\
'Este es un desafío a un campeón oscuro de algún tipo. Será mejor que transcriba una versión traducida y la conserve en mi biblioteca.'"},
[1744]={"Rivendel está en el Bosque de los Trolls, al sur de Angmar.\
\
Has descubierto un extraño fragmento de texto, escrito en la Lengua Negra. Los Elfos de Rivendel podrían traducirlo.","Este tosco fragmento de texto está escrito en la Lengua Negra. Los garabatos extranjeros y apresurados no tienen significado para tus ojos. Se dice que los Elfos de Rivendel comprenden la lengua de Mordor. Quizá alguno de ellos pueda traducir el mensaje y revelar su propósito.","Encuentra a un erudito en Rivendel que pueda traducir el Lenguaje Negro.","El Enemigo habla un lenguaje terrible conocido como la Lengua Negra. Planes y mensajes al Falso Rey, sus generales y comandantes, son frecuentemente llevados al combate por sus secuaces.","'¿La Lengua Negra? Sí, he visto este tipo de cosas antes. Aunque las palabras hieren como veneno en mi lengua, la situación requiere la habilidad de leer la lengua del Enemigo, aunque ninguna palabra de ella se había pronunciado antes —hasta hace poco— en Imladris.\
\
'Este es un desafío a un campeón oscuro de algún tipo. Será mejor que transcriba una versión traducida y la conserve en mi biblioteca.'","Conocimiento Negro"},
[1745]={"Talk to Langlas at the Camp of the Grey Host","'Ah, you had more success at the weapon-gathering than I did, but I too have done some good. These folk were fortunate I was here to see to their wounds! I know the plan is for us to leave this city, and it is important for us to do so, but we should try to help as many of the people here as we can.\
\
'I will put these weapons into a barrel and ask Celairant where he wants it brought, but you should return to Langlas and tell him that I will be on short rations for the rest of our journey. I wish to give a portion of my provisions to some of the families the attack from Umbar hit hardest.'","Mandan is at the north-west entrance to Pelargir.\
\
You have gathered up a number of Corsair blades and should bring them to Mandan.","'Did you fight in the battle, ${PLAYER}? I was stricken with a great fear as the shades of the Dead joined the battle, and I confess to you that I felt a great urge to run from them, as the Corsairs did. And yet, before my heart betrayed me and I succumbed to the terror, I felt a hand upon my arm, and I was reassured.\
\
'Do you know who it was? It was Celairant, the young Ranger I took under my wing in Ered Luin. He is not as young as he was, and this journey has put some steel in him. It was an honour to stand with Aragorn, and the presence of Celairant was a comfort. I am proud to call him brother.\
\
'When the Corsairs fled, many of them cast their weapons to the ground. Mandan went ahead to gather up the fallen blades. Find him at the north-west entrance to Pelargir and help him with this task, for there are many weapons to be recovered.'","'Oh! Langlas sent you to check on me? That was quite unnecessary, ${PLAYER}.'\
\
Mandan scowls.\
\
'Well, perhaps it was a little necessary. You see, I began to gather some of the weapons the Corsairs cast aside when they fled, but it was slow work and I decided my own skills might be better used elsewhere. You know of my talent for fashioning and applying salves, of course? There are many wounded folk who could use such treatment, and I will see to them immediately.\
\
'Anyway, Celairant was gathering up the weapons already. You are welcome to go down to the docks and help him with that task, if you like.'","'Celairant was gathering up the weapons already. You are welcome to go down to the docks and help him with that task, if you like.'","Collect fallen Corsair swords by the docks in Pelargir (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Rangers of the Grey Company are hard at work in the port-city of Pelargir, cleaning up after the defeat of the Corsairs. The streets of Pelargir are littered with the weapons the Corsairs cast aside in their terror, and now it is up to the Rangers to remove the fallen arms.","Bring Corsair swords to Mandan at the north-west entrance to Pelargir","Black Sails: Fallen Arms","'You should return to Langlas and tell him that I will be on short rations for the rest of our journey. I wish to give a portion of my provisions to some of the families the attack from Umbar hit hardest.'","'How did you find the task, ${PLAYER}? I hope it was not too onerous for you.'\
\
You tell Langlas what Mandan asked you to say to him, and he sighs.\
\
'I sent Mandan with Celairant in hopes that my young friend would be able to keep Mandan in line, but it seems he is still trying to peddle those salves and poultices of his. During our stay in Enedwaith, most of us looked forward to his excursions into the coomb seeking herbs... because it meant a respite from his sale-speak! He would inevitably return with more flowers and roots to add to his concoctions, but aside from worsening the smell I daresay they did not otherwise affect their properties.\
\
'Thank you for completing his task for him, my friend.'","'When the Corsairs fled, many of them cast their weapons to the ground. Mandan went ahead to gather up the fallen blades. Find him at the north-west entrance to Pelargir and help him with this task, for there are many weapons to be recovered.'","Collected fallen Corsair swords (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Corsairs cast aside their blades when they fled from the Oath-breakers, and the fallen arms can be found at many places near the docks of Pelargir.","Mandan is inside the entrance to Pelargir.\
\
Langlas and Mandan are organizing the effort to gather up the weapons the Corsairs cast aside when they fled from the Oath-breakers at Pelargir.","Talk to Mandan at the north-west entrance to Pelargir","Langlas is at the Camp of the Grey Host, west of the port-city of Pelargir."},
[1746]={"Techeron reluctantly thanks you for the supplies, though it lost him a wager","Techeron is on the Corsair flagship moored at the large southern dock in the Market Ward, in Pelargir.\
\
You have delivered some supplies to the flagship, and now Techeron wants to speak with you.","'I simply could not believe that Lothrandir's strength could be taken from him, but Saruman has turned him into a shell of his former self. Such treatment in the dungeons of the Wizard would kill a lesser man, I have no doubt, but it pains me to see Lothrandir so weak, so tired. I think I wagered against you with the hope that it was not so.\
\
'I am sorry for taking up so much of your time, my friend. I wanted you to know.'","'These need to go to the Corsair flagship, for that's the one that has the most room. Techeron is waiting for these supplies on the flagship moored at the large southern dock of the Market Ward. You can't miss it: it's the big one.'","Lothrandir is upset at his condition, still weakened from his imprisonment in Isengard, and wants to help the Grey Company ready the ships.","'Hold a moment, ${PLAYER}. Did you know that Radanir and I had a bit of a friendly wager? It was just to amuse us during a bit of tedium, and I do not want you to take it too greatly to heart.\
\
'You see, I wagered that Lothrandir would return to the city and finish the task of loading the ships, instead of you, but I did not mean to disparage your strength or ability! All know of your great deeds and the help you have provided to us on this journey!\
\
'No, I based my wager on how hardy Lothrandir always appears. He chose to live in distant Forochel, after all! Such inhospitable places breed stalwart men, and Lothrandir was strong to start! He is the toughest Ranger I have ever met, and... well... perhaps that is the reason for my wager, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'I simply could not believe that Lothrandir's strength could be taken from him, but Saruman has turned him into a shell of his former self. Such treatment in the dungeons of the Wizard would kill a lesser man, I have no doubt, but it pains me to see Lothrandir so weak, so tired. I think I wagered against you with the hope that it was not so.\
\
'I am sorry for taking up so much of your time, my friend. I wanted you to know.'","'Find Radanir and help him carry my share of the supplies onto the Corsair flagship. You will find him in the West-garth, by one of the bridges that leads to the Court of the Ship-kings.'","Talk to Techeron on the Corsair flagship","There are crates that need to be carried to the Corsair flagship moored at the large dock on the south end of the Market Ward. Crates can be found by Radanir's position in the West-garth, near one of the bridges to the Market Ward.","Pick up the supply crate by Radanir in the West-garth","Lothrandir is at the Camp of the Grey Host, west of the port-city of Pelargir.","'Looks like Techeron owes me some coins, ${PLAYER}. We had a friendly wager concerning what would happen first: Lothrandir returning to try and carry these crates, or you showing up to carry them in his stead.\
\
'I never doubted you for a moment, and now you've won me some coins. I thank you for being so honourable. And predictable!'\
\
Radanir laughs.\
\
'These need to go to the Corsair flagship, for that's the one that has the most room. Techeron is waiting for these supplies on the flagship moored at the large southern dock of the Market Ward. You can't miss it: it's the big one.'","There are barrels that need to be carried to the Corsair flagship moored at the large dock on the south end of the Market Ward. Barrels can be found by Radanir's position in the West-garth, near one of the bridges to the Market Ward.","'You should go back to Techeron and ask him about my coins. You know, just to make sure he has not forgotten about our little wager.'","Black Sails: Loading the Ships","'Thank you for doing my part, ${PLAYER}. Asking for help does not come naturally for me, and I beg you forgive me for it. I hope to regain my strength before long. This weakness and fatigue pains me more than any of the injuries I sustained in Saruman's care!'","Pick up the supply barrel by Radanir in the West-garth","Talk to Radanir in the West-garth of Pelargir","'I do not know what I am doing, ${PLAYER}. I could do little more than stay atop the horse Dagoras provided for me on the ride from Rohan. I am still weak from my stay within Saruman's dungeons, and even lifting a sword leaves me fatigued. I am exhausted and frustrated!\
\
'I volunteered to help load the ships with supplies, expecting to struggle through and beyond the unfair limitations of my strength, but Radanir took my place and sent me back here. My face was red with shame, but I must admit he was right. I need to rest and recover my strength. Curse the traitor-Wizard!\
\
'Find Radanir and help him carry my share of the supplies onto the Corsair flagship. You will find him in the West-garth, by one of the bridges that leads to the Court of the Ship-kings.'","Talk to Lothrandir in the Camp of the Grey Host","Radanir is in the West-garth of Pelargir, by one of the bridges that leads to the Court of the Ship-kings.\
\
Lothrandir has asked you to find Radanir and help him load the ships with supplies.","Techeron thanks you for the supplies"},
[1747]={"The crate does not contain that which you seek","Talk to Daervunn in the Camp of the Grey Host","Faeron is in the Court of the Ship-kings, in Pelargir.\
\
Ranger Faeron heard your conversation with Orthonn and has sought your attention.","'I have been fruitlessly searching for maps ever since the battle ended, ${PLAYER}! If I never see another crate, it will be far too soon for me!\
\
'I have searched all the crates in this area. The only place I have not yet searched is to the north-east, at the very tip of the Market Ward.\
\
'I do not think any of those crates will have river-maps in them, but just to be safe we should search them anyway.'","Talk to Faeron in the Court of the Ship-kings","'I think you should bring those maps to Orthonn, for he is a master of lore and should be skilled at reading them.\
\
'I think you will find him to the south-east, somewhere in the Court of the Ship-kings.'","'I urge that Aragorn not fly the standard of the king when we sail up the Anduin. I have trained many light-fingered folk in the art of burglary, and I know the value of surprise. Sometimes it can make all the difference.\
\
'If he keeps secret the fact of our departure and the manner of our travel, any foe we face may be put off its guard upon our arrival. My heart tells me there is value in this. Please tell Daervunn my message, ${PLAYER}.'","'Yes? With what can I help you, my friend? What do you have there?'\
\
You hand Orthonn the maps of the Anduin, and with each one his smile grows.\
\
'What a fine gift, ${PLAYER}! I did not think you knew of my interest in cartography! It is a vanishing talent these days, I am afraid, but I have done my best to craft maps of the lands through which we have travelled. This will be a great help in improving the accuracy of my own efforts in this field! Not that they are in great need of such improvement, but I believe there is always room for honing one's skills!\
\
'Oh. This gift has a more practical purpose? I will of course study these maps of the river closely and give my findings to Aragorn, so we may travel the Anduin as safely and quickly as we can!'","Amlan is in the Market Ward, in Pelargir.\
\
You found some maps of the Anduin and should bring them to Amlan.","Search crates in the Market Ward for river-maps","Bring the river maps to Orthonn in the Court of the Ship-kings","Orthonn is one of the lore-masters of the Grey Company, and can be found in the Court of the Ship-kings, in Pelargir.\
\
Amlan cannot read the maps of the Anduin you recovered, but thinks that Orthonn might be able to learn some useful knowledge from them.","'You found some maps of the Anduin? Perfect!'\
\
You tell Daervunn that Orthonn was delighted for the chance to practice his hobby of map-reading, and also relay Faeron's concerns about flying the standard of the king from atop the lead Corsair ship.\
\
'I share Faeron's concerns, and spoke with Aragorn about this very matter while you were in the city. It has been his plan all along to keep secret the standard that Halbarad holds for him. I think he is not yet decided when to fly the standard, for it will be a message to both the Enemy and our allies that cannot be easily taken back, can it?\
\
'Thank you for finding the maps, my friend, and for helping with all these matters. We will have many ships ready to sail, sooner and safer than I expected!'","Amlan is in the Market Ward in the port-city of Pelargir.\
\
Daervunn asked you to help Amlan find maps of the river Anduin to help Aragorn with his journey.","Black Sails: Secret Knowledge","Daervunn is at the Camp of the Grey Host, west of the port-city of Pelargir.","Bring the river maps to Amlan in the Market Ward","Daervunn sent Amlan into Pelargir to look for river-maps that will be useful for navigating the Anduin, but he has not yet returned.","Amlan did not yet search the crates in a small area in the north-eastern corner of the Market Ward, and they may contain the river-maps you seek.","'If you are willing, return to the city and help Amlan find any such maps that might prove helpful. Pelargir is the great port-city of Gondor, and there must have been much use of the river for trade and passage. Surely some maps can be found that show the hazards and bends of the Anduin?\
\
'I believe Amlan was going to begin his search in the Market Ward.'","'You found some maps of the Anduin? I cannot believe it! It is always the last place you check, or the first place you never checked, is it not?'\
\
Amlan takes the map from you and peers at it for a moment.\
\
'Well, I see Pelargir here, and Osgiliath up here, which means that these four black lines here must be the Anduin... but what do these marks in the river's course mean? I cannot ascertain anything useful from these maps, ${PLAYER}. I think you should bring them to Orthonn, for he is a master of lore and should be skilled at reading maps.\
\
'I think you will find him to the south-east, somewhere in the Court of the Ship-kings.'","'I will of course study these maps of the river closely and give my findings to Aragorn, so we may travel the Anduin as safely and quickly as we can!'","Talk to Amlan in the Market Ward, in Pelargir","The Ranger Faeron, standing nearby, beckons you to speak with him","'Aragorn hopes to sail up the Anduin on the decks of the Corsair ships, but we are not watermen, and if we are to do this we will need every advantage. To that end, I sent Amlan into the city to look for maps of the river that might aid us in this endeavour.\
\
'If you are willing, return to the city and help Amlan find any such maps that might prove helpful. Pelargir is the great port-city of Gondor, and there must have been much use of the river for trade and passage. Surely some maps can be found that show the hazards and bends of the Anduin?\
\
'I believe Amlan was going to begin his search in the Market Ward.'","'I have searched all the crates in this area. The only place I have not yet searched is to the north-east, at the very tip of the Market Ward.\
\
'I do not think any of those crates will have river-maps in them, but just to be safe we should search them anyway.'","You find some folded parchments in the crate: maps of the Anduin's course","'I overheard your conversation with Orthonn, and have a suggestion of my own. I hope you will bring it to Daervunn, for I know he has the ear of Aragorn.\
\
'I urge that he not fly the standard of the king when we sail up the Anduin. I have trained many light-fingered folk in the art of burglary, and I know the value of surprise. Sometimes it can make all the difference.\
\
'If he keeps secret the fact of our departure and the manner of our travel, any foe we face may be put off its guard upon our arrival. My heart tells me there is value in this. Please tell Daervunn my message, ${PLAYER}.'"},
[1748]={"Talk to Golodir somewhere south of Corunir, in Pelargir","'Golodir's ill mood has returned after a short time at low ebb, and now he shouts at his own dear friends! If you seek him out, know that I left him standing on a dock to the south, looking out at the water. I will not be held responsible if he treats you unkindly, for it seems he does not know his friends.'","'I will master these voices. I have been troubled by these feelings ever since we began this journey, and I have managed to stifle them. It has become more difficult of late, perhaps because of the unnatural skies... the evil presence of the Dead Men...\
\
'Do not worry about me, my friend. I will apologize to Corunir, and my outburst will remain between us, I hope?'","Talk to Halbarad near the north-west entrance to Pelargir","Talk to Corunir in Pelargir, somewhere south of Halbarad","'I like this land, ${PLAYER}. It reminds me of the twilit wilds, far away in the North, where my heart remains. The wooded slopes encircling Lake Nenuial must be slowly shaking off the grip of winter, and in a few weeks the leaves of their trees may begin to fight through the remaining chill. No Winter lasts forever, and the coming of Spring will banish even the coldest of memories. Will this war be any different?'\
\
Calenglad stands silently for a short while, musing on the question. Eventually he smiles, and gives you a conspiratorial wink.\
\
'Radanir told me you agreed to treat him to a meal and drinks at a tavern of your choosing, once this is all over. If you have no objection, I would like to join the two of you there. I will look forward to that happy meeting!\
\
'But there is still much hardship ahead of us, and with all my musings I forgot to tell you something! Halbarad wanted me to send you to him. He has returned to Pelargir already. If you leave now you should find him just inside the north-west entrance to the city.'","Halbarad is located in the large courtyard just inside the north-west entrance to the port-city of Pelargir.","Talk to Calenglad at the Camp of the Grey Host","'I would follow Aragorn anywhere, ${PLAYER}, and standing here with the smell of smoke on the air and the memory of battle still fresh in my mind, I feel as if I have done so!\
\
'I did not blanch when he led us through the Dimholt road, nor when we emerged from the mountain with the shades of Dead Men all around us. Still, I am glad they have departed. It is not natural for such men to linger in the world. An Elf once told me that death is a gift for all Men, but I did not understand what he meant until today. I think now he was right.\
\
'The appearance of the Dead Men may weigh heavily upon some others of our company. Golodir in particular seemed distraught by the passage under the mountain. Find Corunir, somewhere to the south of here, and see if he knows where Golodir can be found. The two of them are rarely apart.'","'The appearance of the Dead Men may weigh heavily upon some others of our company. Golodir in particular seemed distraught by the passage under the mountain. Find Corunir, somewhere to the south of here, and see if he knows where Golodir can be found. The two of them are rarely apart.'","Corunir left Golodir standing on a dock somewhere to the south, in the city of Pelargir.","Calenglad is at the Camp of the Grey Host, outside the port-city of Pelargir.\
\
Golodir was possessed of an unusually ill temper, and you should return to Calenglad and see what he thinks of the Grey Company's mood following the battle.","'With all my musings I forgot to tell you something! Halbarad wanted me to send you to him. He has returned to Pelargir already. If you leave now you should find him just inside the north-west entrance to the city.'","'I am not in the mood to talk, ${PLAYER}. This has been a trying experience for all of us. I hope you do not mind.'\
\
As you turn to go, Corunir holds up his hand.\
\
'I am sorry, friend. I am fine. With what can I help you?'\
\
You tell him that you are looking for Golodir, and thought he might know where you could find the Ranger.\
\
'Golodir is the cause of my ill temperament and I have no desire to speak with him any further. Do you remember the fell mood that seized him in Angmar, before the Grey Company was assembled? I thought he had left it behind him. Indeed, it seemed that the journey was doing him some good, but it returned again in Tûr Morva, only to be overcome by the gentle laughter of the Dunlending girl, Wenda.\
\
'But like the rising and falling brimstone pools of Malenhad, his ill mood has returned after a short time at low ebb, and now he shouts at his own dear friends! If you seek him out, know that I left him standing on a dock to the south, looking out at the water. I will not be held responsible if he treats you unkindly, for it seems he does not know his friends.'","Corunir is somewhere south of Halbarad's position, in Pelargir.\
\
Halbarad has asked you to find Corunir and learn how Golodir fares after the passing of the Dead Men.","Black Sails: Voices of the Past","'Did you find Halbarad? Were you able to help him with whatever it was he needed?'\
\
You ask Calenglad how he feels about the mood of the Grey Company.\
\
'I think we are doing fine, for the most part. We have been through a great deal already, and there is more hardship ahead, but if we stay true to each other there is nothing we need fear.\
\
'We have lost friends along the way, and brothers, but our memories of them give us the strength to go on. If I close my eyes I can still hear their voices, and they urge me to stand with Aragorn and honour my pledge. And one day, you will buy Radanir and Daervunn and me a meal, and drinks, and we will all toast the successful journey of the Grey Company.\
\
'Oh, yes. I told Daervunn about our agreement once this is all done. I did not think you would mind.'","'Yes? What do you want? Are you here to chastise me for treating Corunir unkindly? He has been a sharp thorn for these past few days, constantly asking questions about my well-being. He should have expected a rebuke!'\
\
There is an angry fire in Golodir's eyes, an unfamiliar, smouldering rage.\
\
'I know why, ${PLAYER}. Around matters of the Dead they treat me with delicate gloves. They look at me and they see my daughter, Lorniel. My grief was strong and will never truly pass, but this treatment fills me with such an anger I would strike them all down: Corunir, Halbarad, even my own chief, Aragorn!'\
\
He falls silent. When he speaks again, his voice is little more than a whisper, and there are tears in his eyes.\
\
'I... I do not know from where this anger comes, ${PLAYER}. It feels as if I hear voices of the past, unflagging and unrelenting, calling my name, taunting me...\
\
'I will master these voices. I have been troubled by these feelings ever since we began this journey, and I have managed to stifle them. It has become more difficult of late, perhaps because of the unnatural skies... the evil presence of the Dead Men...\
\
'Do not worry about me, my friend. I will apologize to Corunir, and my outburst will remain between us, I hope?'","The Rangers of the Grey Company have helped deliver the port-city from danger, but their journey is not yet ended. Some of the Rangers are troubled by the things they have seen, and tensions run high among Aragorn's folk."},
[1749]={"Miluimil se encuentra en el campamento de Ivorel en las Hondonadas Enmarañadas.\
\
Deberías regresar con Miluimil con las glándulas de veneno que has recogido.","Habla con Miluimil en el campamento de Ivorel","'Ten cuidado con eso, ${PLAYER}: el veneno de la prole no es tan mortal como el de la propia Delúris, pero no debe tomarse a la ligera.\
\
Es lo bastante similar como para que pueda preparar un antídoto a partir de él, y entonces quizá puedas derrotar a Delúris sin temer su letal aguijón.'","Glándulas de veneno negro recogidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Veneno negro I","Las arañas Venenonegro pueden encontrarse en las cuevas del extremo norte de las Hondonadas Enmarañadas.\
\
Miluimil te ha pedido que recojas glándulas de veneno de la prole Venenonegro de las Hondonadas Enmarañadas para que pueda elaborar un antídoto contra el veneno de Delúris.","'He recibido noticias verdaderamente sombrías, ${PLAYER}. Uno de mis exploradores me ha hablado de una letal reina de las arañas Venenonegro: una prole que infesta las cuevas del norte de las Hondonadas Enmarañadas. Uno de sus compañeros cayó ante ella, sucumbiendo a un veneno tan rápido y mortal que se vio obligado a huir de la criatura tan deprisa como pudo.\
\
Tenemos pocas posibilidades de destruir esa prole mientras esta criatura siga con vida, pero no creo que debas atreverte a enfrentarte a ella sin algún medio para contrarrestar su veneno.\
\
Si puedes reunir muestras del veneno de las arañas Venenonegro, tal vez pueda ayudarte a preparar un antídoto. Reúne algunas glándulas de veneno de la prole de Delúris y luego haremos los preparativos.'","Los exploradores de Miluimil han informado de la existencia de una mortal reina araña llamada Delúris que acecha en las profundidades del norte de las Hondonadas Enmarañadas. Su veneno es tan letal que nadie que se haya atrevido a enfrentarse a ella ha sobrevivido.","'Mantén los ojos abiertos por una elfa llamada Gladiel. Pasó por aquí hace un tiempo buscando algún paso y murmurando sobre otra prole de arañas a la que llamaba los Saewathel.\
\
Como si una sola prole de estas criaturas no fuera suficiente... No sé nada sobre los Saewathel, pero parecía preocupada por su presencia y buscaba algún camino a través de las Hondonadas Enmarañadas hacia Dol Guldur. Me temo que no pude ayudarla.'","Recoge glándulas de veneno negro (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","NO DEBERÍAS VER ESTO"},
[1750]={"'¿Estás ${PLAYER:listo[m]|lista[f]} para enfrentarte a Delúris, ${PLAYER}? He terminado el antídoto. Asegúrate de usarlo con rapidez si sientes el aguijón de su veneno, pues no tendrás mucho tiempo.\
\
Los efectos del antídoto son breves; si la batalla se alarga, puede que tengas que usar más, pero unas pocas gotas deberían bastar para contrarrestar su ataque.\
\
Habita en las cuevas del extremo norte de las Hondonadas Enmarañadas, y muchos de sus engendros se agrupan allí, así que ten mucho cuidado de no verte superado por su número antes incluso de llegar hasta ella.'","Habla con Miluimil en las Hondonadas Enmarañadas","'Me pregunto de dónde han salido todas estas horribles arañas. Agorin no habló de tales criaturas cuando relató la época en que vivía en el Gran Bosque Verde.\
\
Sin embargo, Celeborn habló una vez de una criatura negra y malvada que pasó por aquí en los años en que los bosques se oscurecieron, saliendo de las Montañas Nubladas y atravesando los bosques hacia el sur, donde volvió a desaparecer.\
\
¿Podría ser que estas criaturas sean la descendencia de ese mal?'","Derrota a Delúris","Tras ayudar a Miluimil a elaborar un antídoto a partir del veneno de su propia prole, ahora estás preparado para enfrentarte a Delúris, la reina de la prole de las Hondonadas Enmarañadas.","El nido de Delúris se encuentra en el norte de las Hondonadas Enmarañadas, al norte del campamento de Ivorel.\
\
Miluimil te ha pedido que te enfrentes y derrotes a la reina araña Delúris, y te ha proporcionado el antídoto contra su veneno.","'Así que la malvada reina de la prole ha caído. Bien hecho, ${PLAYER}... sin su progenitora, la vil prole menguará a medida que sea cazada hasta su extinción. Pero gran parte de esa tarea tendrá que esperar hasta después de la caída de Dol Guldur.\
\
Por ahora, basta con saber que Delúris ha desaparecido y que mis exploradores ya no tienen que temer su venenoso aguijón negro.'","Miluimil se encuentra en el campamento de Ivorel en las Hondonadas Enmarañadas, al sur del nido de Delúris.\
\
Deberías regresar junto a Miluimil para contarle la derrota de Delúris.","Veneno negro II","Has derrotado a Delúris"},
[1751]={"Scuttledells crows can be found throughout the Scuttledells.\
\
Ivorel has asked you to hunt down Scuttledells crows to prevent them from finding her scouts or reporting back to Dol Guldur.","Defeated Scuttledells crows (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Agorin tells me that even when our Silvan kin still inhabited Ost Galadh, they warned their children to stay away from these dangerous ravines and dells, but that later they would challenge each other to dare the maze despite their elders' warnings.\
\
'Now only a hardened warrior has any chance of surviving in this place. It is hard to imagine her holding fond memories of this death-trap.'","Black Wings","'So, there are fewer of the Enemy's crow-spies about? Excellent.\
\
'If we can move about unseen, we have a better chance of rescuing a few of our people from these cursed ravines.'","Habla con Ivorel en su campamento","Ivorel is at her camp in the Scuttledells.\
\
You should speak with Ivorel and tell her that many of the Enemy's flying scouts have been slain.","If Ivorel's scouts are to have any hope of moving without the Enemy knowing their every step, the crows of the Enemy will need to be kept at bay.","'Keep one eye to the skies, ${PLAYER}. There are a number of the Enemy's black-feathered servants about. My scouts will be hard pressed to move unseen with such keen eyes above us.\
\
'Defeat them quickly if you should come upon them in the ravines and gullies below... the fewer that make it back to Dol Guldur alive, the better.'","Defeat Scuttledells crows (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[1752]={"Corrupted Huorns can be found in the Black Heart of Fangorn.\
\
You should defeat many corrupted Huorns in the darkest part of the forest.","Derrota a los ucornos corruptos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat Huorns in the Black Heart","You have defeated many of the bloodthirsty Huorns of Greenroot's corrupted herd. The forest will not be so treacherous for the creatures who wind up lost in the Black Heart.","Black-hearted Trees","Completado","Defeated a Huorn (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The trees in the Black Heart of Fangorn are evil to the core, coming after you without provocation, and with a worrisome bloodlust."},
[1753]={"Noche más negra","Devuelve los cristales a Gerwith en Tharâkh Bazân","Gerwith necesita los cristales de las cuevas que crecen en Tharâkh Bazân para reemplazar muchas de las fuentes de luz que han sido destruidas en toda Moria.","Has recogido un cristal luminoso (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Gerwith está en el campamento en el extremo este de Tharâkh Bazân.\
\
Gerwith espera tu regreso con los cristales luminosos que pueden usarse como fuentes de luz.","Recolecta cristales que crecen de forma natural en Tharâkh Bazân (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Los cristales se encuentran en Tharâkh Bazân, al oeste de Jazârgund en el Camino de Durin.\
\
Gerwith te ha pedido que busques cristales naturales en Tharâkh Bazân para reemplazar los que han sido destruidos.","'La belleza de estos jardines no deja de impresionarme. Muchos de los cristales que crecen naturalmente aquí en Tharâkh Bazân se utilizan en toda Moria como fuente de luz.\
\
'En algunos lugares, los morrovals han estado destruyendo los cristales que hemos colocado, para extinguir cualquier luz visible. Muchos de nuestros pasillos y salas se han vuelto más oscuros que la noche más negra.\
\
'Debemos recolectar más cristales para reemplazar los que han sido destruidos. Busca en Tharâkh Bazân cristales formados naturalmente, y me aseguraré de que se les dé un buen uso.'","'Me has traído una gran variedad de cristales, ¡buen trabajo! Los usaremos para llevar algo del calor y la belleza de estos jardines a los rincones oscuros donde ninguna otra luz puede penetrar.'"},
[1754]={"Colmillo Negro derrotado","'Busca el Tótem del Desafío de los huargos, ${PLAYER}... quizá descubras algo sobre el destino de Glorwen.'","Regresa con Nogmeldir en Vindurhal y cuéntale que Glorwen ha sido capturada por los trasgos de la Ciudad de los Trasgos.","Colmillo Negro","Thorgest te dijo que podrías conocer el destino de Glorwen enfrentándote al líder de la manada, Colmillo Negro.","El desafío ha sido lanzado","'Sé que te pido mucho, pero si Thorgest cree que la única manera de aprender algo de los huargos de Starkhath es desafiar a su líder, entonces no veo otro camino a seguir.\
\
'La vida de Glorwen puede pender de un hilo —si es que aún vive. Por su bien y por el tuyo, ten cuidado y prepárate bien.'","El tótem del desafío está en el centro de las ruinas de Starkhath.\
\
Nogmeldir te ha pedido que encuentres el tótem y provoques al líder de los huargos, Colmillo Negro.","'¿Quién osa venir? No eres de la manada, ¿y aun así me desafías? Que así sea...'","Encuentra el tótem del desafío y derrota a Colmillo Negro","'Tus noticias me hielan la sangre, ${PLAYER}. Son pocos los que han escapado de las oscuras y retorcidas cavernas de la Ciudad de los Trasgos una vez que se han adentrado en ellas.\
\
'El odio de los trasgos hacia los de mi pueblo es grande, y los tormentos de Glorwen a sus manos serán largos y crueles.\
\
'Debemos prepararnos —ya sea mediante el sigilo o por la fuerza de las armas— para rescatarla, pues aun si perdiéramos a una docena de héroes bajo los dardos y cuchillas de los trasgos, nuestro sufrimiento no sería nada comparado con el suyo si la dejamos a merced de ellos.'"},
[1756]={"'¡La encontraste! Excelente trabajo, y puedo decir que nos alegra que haya un Montebruno menos de quien preocuparnos.\
\
Ahora, , podemos descubrir lo que los bandidos ocultaron en este cofre.\
Has hecho un trabajo maravilloso, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}, y mereces esta recompensa.'","Lleva la llave maestra de Rurik al condestable Vadosalvia","Encuentra la llave maestra de Rurik (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¡Ah, sí! Lo recuerdo. Un explorador regresó hace unas horas y mencionó que había un Manzaneda dando órdenes a los reclutas. Luego se dirigió al campamento principal de Montebruno en las ruinas en la parte más al norte del bosque de Chet.\
\
'Si Manzaneda tiene la llave, debemos conseguirla para ayudar a quienes han sufrido tanto a manos de Montebruno. Ten cuidado, , los informes de esas ruinas hablan de una gran sensación de temor y desánimo. Deberás ser ${PLAYERNAME:cauteloso[m]|cautelosa[f]} si intentas encontrar a Manzaneda y obtener la llave.\
\
'Cuando encuentres la llave, regresa conmigo y veremos qué buenas noticias llevaremos a la gente de Archet y Combe.'","El condestable Vadosalvia recordó que un explorador mencionó haber oído a un recluta de Montebruno obedecer órdenes del sargento Manzaneda cerca del campamento principal de Montebruno.","El condestable Vadosalvia se encuentra cerca del centro de Combe.\
\
Tras encontrar y derrotar a Manzaneda, recuperaste la llave de él. Ahora debes regresar con el condestable Vadosalvia.","'Si puedes encontrar a Manzaneda en el campamento principal de Montebruno, deberías poder recuperar la llave de Rurik, y entonces podremos empezar a devolver la esperanza a la gente de Combe y Archet.'","'Has hecho un buen trabajo aquí, ${PLAYER}.'","'¡Archet y Combe se beneficiarán enormemente de tu trabajo!'","Se ha visto a Manzaneda entrando al campamento principal de Montebruno en la parte más al norte del bosque de Chet.\
\
Tras saber que Rurik solo era culpable de miedo, Vadosalvia recordó el nombre que Rurik proporcionó como un bandido dentro del campamento principal de Montebruno en el bosque de Chet. Vadosalvia quiere que busques a Manzaneda y obtengas la llave que le robó a Rurik.","Llave maestra de Rurik encontrada (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Ladrones Montebruno"},
[1757]={"Has encontrado un recibo","El condestable Vadosalvia se puede encontrar cerca del centro de Combe, con sus compañeros.\
\
Vadosalvia te envió a confrontar al líder de los Montebruno en la granja del Viejo Bauman. Encontraste un recibo firmado por un 'Rurik' en el cuerpo del Montebruno. El condestable Vadosalvia querrá saber sobre esto.","'Después de las primeras incursiones, cuando la gente comenzó a huir hacia aldeas como Archet y Entibo, los Montebruno encontraron que ya no podían depender solo de las incursiones para mantenerse. Tomaron la granja del Viejo Bauman y comenzaron a cultivar la tierra, aunque mal y sin cuidar la tierra.\
\
'Se supone que los bandidos en la granja están bajo la supervisión de algún líder Montebruno, de lo contrario caerían en la pereza. Si confrontas al líder de los Montebruno en la granja, podrías recuperar algunos de los objetos de valor que han robado. La granja del Viejo Bauman está en lo profundo del bosque de Chet, al final del camino hacia el este.\
\
'Agradecería mucho si pudieras al menos intentarlo. Hay mucha gente que se beneficiaría de la recuperación de este tesoro.'","'La granja del viejo Bauman está al final del camino al noreste de Combe, en lo profundo del bosque de Chet. Probablemente haya un bandido importante supervisando el trabajo allí.'","'¿Qué es esto?\
\
¿Rurik? Hay un Rurik Fennel viviendo aquí en Combe. Es... cerrajero. ¿Pero por qué estaría ayudando a los Montebruno, ${PLAYER}? La casa de Rurik está al suroeste de aquí, justo detrás de la Comba y la Cresta.\
\
Será mejor que hables con Rurik. Me interesará mucho saber por qué ha estado cerrando cajas para los Montebruno. Mucho interés, de verdad.'","Buscar objetos de valor","El condestable Vadosalvia ha aprendido que los bandidos Montebruno han estado tratando de mantenerse trabajando en una granja que ocuparon en lo profundo del bosque de Chet, al este de Combe.","Objetos de valor de Montebruno","La granja del Viejo Bauman está en lo profundo del bosque de Chet, al final del camino hacia el este.\
\
El condestable Vadosalvia cree que si enfrentas al líder de los Montebruno en la granja del Viejo Bauman, podrías recuperar algunos de los objetos de valor que los Montebruno han robado.","Llevar el pergamino al condestable Vadosalvia","Llevar el recibo al condestable Vadosalvia en Combe","'¡Las granjas al noreste de Combe seguro que están bajo la atenta mirada de algún Montebruno importante!'"},
[1758]={"Llygad el Filo ha sido derrotado","Llygad el Filo lidera las fuerzas de las Tierras Brunas desde el interior de la Escuela de Tham Mírdain, cuya entrada se encuentra al sureste de Echad Mirobel.\
\
Faellion desea que derrotes al campeón para disuadir a las fuerzas de las Tierras Brunas de sus intenciones belicistas.","Acaba con Llygad el Filo","Filo de los dunledinos","'Gelirwen me informó de que un gran líder —no, un campeón— de los dunlendinos ha entrado en la Escuela de Tham Mírdain para ayudar a las fuerzas de los uruk-hai y los dunlendinos en sus saqueos. Este líder de los dunlendinos cumplirá su cometido a la perfección si no se le detiene.\
\
'Te pido que te dirijas al sureste de Echad Mirobel y entres en la Escuela de Tham Mírdain; allí deberás derrotar a Llygad el Filo. Con su líder derrotado, tal vez podamos infundir miedo en los corazones de los Hombres de las Tierras Brunas.\
\
'Quizá quieras traer amigos contigo, ${PLAYER}. Será una aventura peligrosa, pues hay muchos guerreros dentro de la escuela que se interponen entre tú y tu presa.'"},
[1759]={"Dagbert is at Etheburg in the Brown Lands.\
\
You should bring news of your victory to Dagbert.","The Khundolar have swept into the Brown Lands in preparation to descend upon the Riddermark like a double-edged sword.","'Uh...good work, ${PLAYER}. I confess I was not sure I would see you again, but you have proven quite hardy!'","'Dagbert sent you to attack the Easterlings at Lashkarg? He is an idiot! We are fortunate the Khundolar have not yet seen fit to descend upon us.\
\
'Well, I cannot blame you for Dagbert's foolishness. You meant well.'","'Céola delays too long. We must move against the Khundolar now, ${PLAYER}. They have come in great force, and my people will be unable to defend against them.\
\
'Will you help me, ${PLAYER}? Will you enter Lashkarg, their war-camp to the south-east, and put the fear of the Rohirrim into them?\
\
'If so, you should leave at once.'","Talk to Dagbert in the Brown Lands","Defeat Khundolar at Lashkarg in the Brown Lands (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Blade of the East","Khundolar Easterlings can be found at Lashkarg, south-east of Etheburg in the Brown Lands.\
\
Dagbert has asked you to enter Lashkarg, war-camp of the Khundolar, and defeat the Easterling warriors there.","Defeated Khundolar at Lashkarg in the Brown Lands (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[1760]={"'Thanks to Dagbert's treason, we are forced to deal with the Khundolar sooner than expected, but perhaps there are ways to weaken or discourage them.\
\
'Make a foray against Lashkarg and defeat some of the Easterlings there. Perhaps by making a show of strength against their encampment, they will believe our numbers are greater than they actually are.\
\
'If you find Dagbert among them, do not hesitate to end his life. Treason is a crime punishable only by death....'","The Khundolar have swept into the Brown Lands in preparation to descend upon the Riddermark like a double-edged sword.","'Uh...good work, ${PLAYER}. I confess I was not sure I would see you again, but you have proven quite hardy!'","'As vast as you say Lashkarg is, I doubt this attack has deterred them at all.\
\
'Thank you for your efforts nonetheless.'","Khundolar Easterlings can be found at Lashkarg, south-east of Etheburg in the Brown Lands.\
\
Céola has asked you to enter Lashkarg, war-camp of the Khundolar, and defeat the Easterling warriors there in hopes that they will believe Etheburg's numbers greater than they truly are.","Defeat Khundolar at Lashkarg in the Brown Lands (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Blade of the East","Céola is at Etheburg in the Brown Lands.\
\
You should bring news of your victory to Céola.","Talk to Céola at Etheburg in the Brown Lands","Defeated Khundolar at Lashkarg in the Brown Lands (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[1762]={"Radigond can be found in Díngarth.\
\
You should give the sharpened swords to Radigond.","Blunt swords can be found in Díngarth.\
\
You should gather blunt swords.","Sharpen swords on the grindstone (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Sharpened swords (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Blades for the Coming Storm","Give the sharpened swords to Radigond","Radigond, daughter of Huneric Hundred-slayer, has been tasked with maintaining Díngarth's weapon stores.","A grindstone can be found in Díngarth.\
\
You should sharpen the swords on the grindstone.","Gather blunt swords (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Do you know aught about maintaining weapons? Do not lie to me! If you do not know of such things, simply say so! It is not as easy as you might think, unless you have given it study! Ah, you do know the art? Why did you not simply say so?\
\
'My father the Hundred-slayer taught me everything there is to know about keeping swords balanced and sharp, and those are both traits that our Alliance will need in the days to come! Take some of the blunt swords in Díngarth and give them a sharpen on the grindstone. Show me what you know about maintaining weapons.'","Gathered blunt swords (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Let me see those weapons. Hmm...\
\
'Yes, these are not bad at all. You show promise, and lack only the practice. Oh, it is not an insult! Not even I have mastered the art, and I have spent all the days of my life training in it with my father!\
\
'There are many more weapons that need inspection and maintenance, but these will see use soon, for the Storm of Wrath is coming. Perhaps these blades will be sharp enough to give that horde something to think upon.'"},
[1763]={"Orc weapons seized (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Blades of the Enemy","Using the information from the scouting report gathered from Emlû, Galâmka has asked you to take weapons from the Orcs in Maurûsh so they can arm themselves.","Galâmka has asked you to gather weapons from the Orcs in Maurûsh to help arm the fighters in Ub Nishir.","Give the weapons to Galâmka in Ub Nishir","Return to Galâmka in Ub Nishir with the weapons you have retrieved in Maurûsh.","'You return with weapons! You are a true help, my friend.\
\
'This day you have furthered our cause yet again as well as ensured that Emlû's death was not in vain. We all thank you for that.\
\
'Come back when you can. We still have more to do before we can strike back in Maurûsh, but we are growing stronger by the day.'","Seize Orc weapons (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Now that you are here, we can begin. Emlû gave his life for this valuable information and it saddens me that you found him the way that you did. His report that you were able to retrieve details of locations within Maurûsh where the Orcs are keeping their weapon stores.'\
\
Galâmka indicates to locations on the map where Emlû claimed there are weapons.\
\
'I need you again to make your way into Maurûsh, and take what weapons you can from these locations. This would be would of great use to arm the fighters here.'"},
[1765]={"Hay osos de montaña que habitan en las Gargantas del Bruinen, en el Bosque de los Trolls.\
\
Mientras estés en las Gargantas del Bruinen, deberías cazar osos para obtener pieles.","Entrega las pieles que recolectaste a uno de los enanos acampados en Thorenhad","'¿Puedo ayudarte?'","Recolecta pieles de los osos de montaña de las Gargantas del Bruinen (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Mantas para los Enanos","Pieles recolectadas de los osos de montaña de las Gargantas del Bruinen (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Los osos de montaña que viven en las Gargantas del Bruinen proporcionarían abundantes pieles que los enanos podrían usar para confeccionar mantas.","Recolecta pieles de los osos de montaña de las Gargantas del Bruinen","'Ha sido muy amable de tu parte traernos estas pieles. ¡Estos Elfos quizá no sientan el frío, pero nuestros viejos huesos sí!'","Hay enanos acampando con los Elfos en Thorenhad, en las Gargantas del Bruinen.\
\
Debes entregar las pieles que recolectaste a uno de los enanos en Thorenhad."},
[1766]={"Offram, pleased by your hunting prowess and offering of meat, hides, and ivory, has more tasks for you.","'The impending siege promises to be a long one. Many of the people of Eaworth will need blankets to keep them warm during the harsh winter.\
\
'Take these hides you collected to the infirmary's sewing-table and make some blankets. You will need to find some thread and needles as well. For the former, you should speak with Nothgyth in the southern part of the city. For the needles, speak with Ordbéorth... he is somewhat mercenary, but he will provide you with what you need.\
\
'When you have sewn the blankets, distribute them throughout the city, then return to me.'","Delivered warm blankets (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Sew warm blankets for the people of Eaworth","Talk to Offram outside the Vendor Hall in Eaworth","Collect aurochs-hides (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The infirmary's sewing-table can be found outside the infirmary in Eaworth.\
\
Offram asked you to sew warm blankets for the people of Eaworth.","'Have you something for me?'","Collected sewing-needles from Ordbéorth","Collect sewing-needles from Ordbéorth","People in need of warm blankets can be found throughout Eaworth.\
\
Offram wants you to deliver the warm blankets you sewed to the people of Eaworth.","'My thanks to you... this will be a boon in the coming days!'","Blankets for the Winter","'You ask much in this dark time. Nevertheless, I will not have it said that Ordbéorth of Eaworth did not do his part to prepare for the siege. Here are the needles you requested.'","Collected aurochs-hides (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collected spools of thread from Nothgyth","'Thank you for this gift, ${PLAYER}. It will bring warmth on cold nights.'","Offram stands guard outside the Vendor Hall in Eaworth.\
\
You should let Offram know that you have delivered the blankets as he had asked.","'You have shown kindness to my people... I will gladly provide you with the thread you need.'","'Offram thinks ahead... my family will need warmth now that our home is gone.'","Offram has given you the hides you need. Thread can be obtained from Nothgyth in the southern part of the city. Ordbéorth in the northern part of the city can provide sewing-needles.\
\
Offram has asked you to collect the hides, thread, and needles necessary to make warm blankets for the people of Eaworth.","'We shall make good use of this blanket... thank you!'","Collect spools of thread from Nothgyth","Deliver warm blankets (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'Thank you for your kindness and your diligence, ${PLAYER}. You are a true friend to Eaworth.'","'I have lost everything, and you bring me a blanket? A BLANKET?\
\
'Nay, I should not be so hard on you. It is not your fault that Ingbert protects us not.'"},
[1767]={"Lleva pieles de lobo a Arinora","'Siempre hay trabajo por hacer aquí.'","'Hay algunos lugares donde puedes buscar lobos con buenas pieles. Los lobos merodean entre las ruinas de Minas Eriol al sur, aunque ese lugar también está lleno de huargos y trasgos. Los lobos también cazan en las Colinas de los Vientos, al este y norte. Finalmente, podrías viajar aún más al norte, pero el Paso de Moscagua es peligroso y está lleno de cosas peores que los lobos.'","'¡Estas pieles son realmente buenas! Las curaré y coseré un buen lote de mantas nuevas para los huéspedes.\
\
Te agradeceré tu tiempo con unas monedas de mi bolsa.'","Se pueden encontrar lobos en las ruinas de Minas Eriol al sur de la Posada Abandonada, en las Colinas de los Vientos al noreste y en el Paso de Moscagua al norte.\
\
Arinora de la Posada Abandonada te pidió que recogieras pieles de lobo para que pueda hacer mantas para los huéspedes de la posada.","Arinora está abrumada por las muchas responsabilidades que tiene para el mantenimiento de la Posada Abandonada.","'Hay demasiados viajeros, incluso en esta tierra remota, y el agua más cercana está sucia y estancada. Tenemos el pozo, por supuesto, pero el agua se raciona entre todos los huéspedes y no alcanza para todos.\
\
Las mantas necesitan hacerse y remendarse, y no hay mejores pieles que las de los lobos. La piel de un huargo es demasiado áspera, pero el pelaje de un lobo puede suavizarse con un peine. Si tienes tiempo y buen corazón, te pediría ayuda; ¡no me verás atravesando los matorrales para llegar a los lobos, tan peligrosos como son!\
\
Hay algunos lugares donde puedes buscar lobos con buenas pieles. Los lobos merodean entre las ruinas de Minas Eriol al sur, aunque ese lugar también está lleno de huargos y trasgos. Los lobos también cazan en las Colinas de los Vientos, al este y norte. Finalmente, podrías viajar aún más al norte, pero el Paso de Moscagua es peligroso y está lleno de cosas peores que los lobos. Cuando tengas las pieles de lobo, vuelve a verme y me aseguraré de que recibas tu recompensa.'","Pieles de lobo recogidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Recoge pieles de lobo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Las pieles de lobo pueden convertirse en buenas mantas para quienes no tienen ninguna, si es necesario.'","Mantas de los lobos aulladores"},
[1768]={"Building a horn to summon reinforcements to Tol Ascarnen requires that several pieces be collected and assembled for an Orc to watch over and use when the Free Peoples make their assault against the fort.","The Leafcull Huorns make their home in the southern woods of Hithlad. Find the Huorn amonst the trees south of the Grimwood Lumber Camp in Hithlad, to the south-west of Tol Ascarnen.\
\
Angmar's forces at Tol Ascarnen are building a horn to call reinforcements to the fight when the Free Peoples return to assault the area. Kaasak has tasked you with collecting the heartwood of a Leafcull Huorn to act as the stand upon which the horn will rest. Damaging the heartwood will make it useless.","'Get a move on, sluggard. We need that heartwood, or the horn cannot be built. If I have need to warn you again, things will get very uncomfortable for you at the sulphur pits.'","'Listen well. In order to build a horn with which to call reinforcements to Tol Ascarnen, we need to gather some more parts, such as a strong and tall piece of heartwood to place the horn and sinew upon. Your task is to head south into Hithlad -- more importantly, the Grimwood -- to collect the heartwood of a Leafcull Huorn.\
\
'You must be certain to collect a perfect heartwood, for no other will be able to withstand an assault from the Free Peoples. We must build a strong horn, understand?\
\
'Go now and collect the heartwood from the Leafcull in Hithald.'","Bleeding Heart","Talk to Soldier Kaasak at Tol Ascarnen","'A good find. When the horn and sinew are collected, we will have all that we need to build the horn.'"},
[1769]={"Tu misión es viajar al norte a Thalat Tîr para reducir el número de arañas despiadadas en la zona, así como traer muestras de su veneno para los eruditos de Sul Madásh.","Derrota a las arañas en Thalat Tîr (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","¡La matriarca de la plaga ha aparecido para defender a su prole!","Veneno recolectado (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","La plaga en la mordida","Derrota a la matriarca de la plaga","'Menos arañas es una buena noticia para todos. Has hecho bien en reunir el veneno necesario. Regresa a Sul Madásh con los eruditos para que puedan hacer buen uso de él.'","Arañas eliminadas en Thalat Tîr (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Reúne veneno (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[1770]={"Blight of the Thyrsir","Although you came too late to save the livestock of Tríubad from the poisons of the Taurogrim, you have done much to help protect the Woodmen and other folk of the Vales of Anduin from their blight.","The gnarled branches of the Taurogrim contain a potent poison fatal to Men and beasts alike.","Livestock slain by the blight of the Taurogrim can be found throughout Tríubad.\
\
Fearing the blight of the Taurogrim will spread from those that succumbed to it, Vilibald has asked you to burn the remains of slain livestock at Tríubad.","'I thought such sorrowful days were behind us, ${PLAYER}, but what am I to think now?\
\
'In mere days, all of our livestock was taken by some cruel sickness. Some believe the forest has become angry with us, but I say it is the work of the wood-demons. I have heard enough of the tales of the Thyrsir to know that their sap runs with blight!\
\
'I do not know if the blight lingers in the dead, but if it can spread, it must be prevented. I would ask you to burn the remains of our fallen livestock. No more injuries will be done to them by the wood-demons!'","You burned the remains of slain livestock at Tríubad.","Completado","Burned the remains of blighted livestock (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Burn the remains of blighted livestock (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[1771]={"Return to Málacál near Sul Madásh and report your success of defeating spiders in eastern Adagím.","'You return. I trust your hunt for spiders has been a success?\
\
'We know they will return and their numbers will replenish, but that only keeps the hunt going! Your efforts made us proud, friend.'","Málacál has asked that you travel to the east of Sul Madásh and help her and her hunters thin the number of blighted spiders that can be found.","Return to Málacál","Blighted spiders defeated (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Blight-weavers","'The spiders here are quite the challenge for the hunt. They are cunning and hide in their shadows and webs.\
\
'If you can, thin their numbers in the east and make the guild proud. You may need to gather some allies for the task.'","Defeat blighted spiders east of Sul Madásh (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[1774]={"Corsair snipers can be found around Dol Brannor in Dor-en-Ernil.\
\
You have discovered a group of Corsairs led by a Haradrim War-master. You should defeat them before they can slay more travellers on the roads below.","'I have heard talk of more violence to the north-west. Our scouts lead us to believe that the Corsairs have seized Dol Brannor, one of our south-beacons, and now use it as a perch to slay our people from afar.\
\
'They cannot be allowed to hold such an advantage within our lands, for it makes supplying our men a great challenge and travel nigh impossible.\
\
'Travel to Dol Brannor and see if their forces are still camped at the beacon. If they have been so bold, make certain they regret their arrogance.'","Blinding the Enemy","Patrol Dol Brannor","The Haradrim and Corsairs have laid claim to Dol Brannor, and now their cruel archers use the beacon's perch to slay those who would dare to travel the roads below.","Defeat the Haradrim War-master at Dol Brannor","Defeated Corsair snipers at Dol Brannor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Dol Brannor can be found to north-west of Linhir in Dor-en-Ernil.\
\
Herion has asked you to patrol the beacon of Dol Brannor and defeat any of the Enemy's forces that have made camp there.","Defeat Corsair snipers at Dol Brannor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Herion in Linhir","'High-ground or not, I hope the Corsairs and Haradrim know to keep away from our beacons now.\
\
'Should they be foolish enough to attempt to reclaim it, I shall call upon your aid once more. You have my thanks.'","Dol Brannor has been seized by Corsair sentries!","The Haradrim War-master has been defeated!","Herion can be found in Linhir in eastern Dor-en-Ernil.\
\
You have crippled the forces at Dol Brannor, at least for the moment, and should now return to Herion."},
[1776]={"Spakorth can be found outside the lower gates to Lûghash in Dor Amarth.\
\
You have forced Zôreth's fell spirits from the watching-stones, but some appear to have returned to her keeping in Lûghash. You should meet with Spakorth and tell him what has happened.","Zôreth, Mistress of Lûghash, has bound foul spirits to many of the intact watching-stones in Dor Amarth and now they keep watch on her servants and foes alike.","A fell spirit flies from the stone and begins to attack!","Talk to Spakorth at Lûghash","'Some of the spirits fled into Lûghash, you say? That is no good, no good at all....\
\
'It is certain that Mistress Zôreth shall wish to speak with me about what her spirits saw, so it shall be my task to convince her that no threat comes to the Flaming Spire.\
\
'I doubt she shall protest when I tell her that we drove you and your armies from Mordor! Ha-ha!'","Forced from its stone vessel, the fell spirit turns and flees toward Lûghash!","'Lûghash rises to the east, nestled within a rocky hill atop a deep valley. Alas, the Stout-axes are not the only ones in service of the Mistress of Lûghash....\
\
'You see, Mistress Zôreth has grown emboldened since the fall of the Dark Lord, and she has drawn many vile spirits into the watching-stones of this land.\
\
'Through their eyes, both servants and foes are revealed... and their designs exposed. She is distrustful, even of her own kin, and so she instead wields her spirits as servants and spies. In this way, She seeks to find the resting places of the Dark Lord's most powerful trinkets. We Stout-axes think it a foolish search and we would have no part of it... were the choice ours!\
\
'If you wish to come to Lûghash, you must challenge Her Watching-stones and banish the spirits from them! If you do not, she shall soon know of you and Gimli!\
\
'When it is done and Her spirits have been cast back to the shadows, I shall meet you at the lower gates of Lûghash!'","Blinding the Watching-stones","Zôreth's watching-stones can be found along the causeway to Lûghash and Barad-dûr in Dor Amarth.\
\
Spakorth has asked you to challenge Zôreth's watching-stones and drive out the evil spirits bound to them.","<rgb=#FF00FF>Challenge</rgb> and defeat Zôreth's watching-stones (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Although it is unclear if a spirit dwells within it, the statue of the Enemy seems to resist your efforts..."},
[1777]={"'¡Qué terrible! Buscaba pruebas, sí... pero no esperaba que las cosas hubieran llegado a esto. Examinemos el cráneo del pobre enano para buscar pistas sobre lo que le sucedió. Si podemos vengarlo, será suficiente para tu desafío.\
\
'Lo mataron hace poco. También faltan algunos dientes. ¿Qué podemos deducir de esto?'","Cráneo de enano adquirido","Obtén evidencia del paso del enano","Regresa con Brazofero en las Vetas del Cuerno Rojo","Brazofero te ha pedido rastrear el camino de un enano desaparecido y traerle cualquier evidencia que encuentres de su paso.","Se rumorea que el enano pasó por el corazón de las Vetas del Cuerno Rojo, cerca de la vía del carro minero que corre de este a oeste, justo al norte del pasaje que lleva a las Profundidades Llameantes.\
\
Deberías reunir pruebas de su paso y llevarlas a Brazofero, que desea conocer el progreso de la misión del enano.","Brazofero está en la Guardia Orca, en las Vetas del Cuerno Rojo de Moria, al noroeste del lugar donde encontraste los restos del enano.\
\
Deberías regresar junto a él con el cráneo, ya limpio de toda carne.","Punto ciego","'¿Has encontrado algo ya, ${PLAYER}?'","'Here we come to it, ${PLAYER}. You wish to learn, and I am willing to teach you, if you can do what I ask.\
\
'You have the look of an experienced enough woodsman and hunter. I know of a skill that will aid you greatly, but the path you must follow to attain it will not be easy. Sometimes it is more useful to track friend than foe, so let us start there. \
\
'One of the dwarf-workers of the expedition went out many days ago on a scouting mission that took him through the southern region of the Redhorn Lodes. You should search there for evidence of his passage, and see how he fares.'"},
[1779]={"Raise a banner of the Haban'akkâ of Thráin at Zaghúth","The Haban'akkâ of Thráin will be victorious!","Destroy Orkish barricades at Zaghúth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Blockade on Barazinbar","Destroyed Orkish barricades at Zaghúth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You have done much to hinder the Orcs and their vile allies at Zaghúth.\
\
You should raise a banner of the Haban'akkâ of Thráin at Zaghúth.","'The Haban'akkâ has need of your aid, my friend.\
\
'I have received word that our enemies at Zaghúth have repaired and reinforced their encampment upon the slopes of Barazinbar. We cannot suffer the Redhorn Pass to be held by our foes, and neither can we allow the Orcs to flee to safety beyond the northern reaches of the dale should the battle turn swiftly against them. This war will end at Azanulbizar!\
\
'Let our enemies at Zaghúth know the wrath of the Haban'akkâ!'","Defeat Orcs and goblins at Zaghúth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Upon the slopes of Barazinbar at Zaghúth, the Orcs and goblins of Moria have constructed a blockade to hinder the Haban'akkâ of Thráin at Azanulbizar.","Orcs, goblins, Warg-riders, and barricades can be found at Zaghúth.\
\
King Thráin has commanded you to join in the assault at Zaghúth. You should aid the Haban'akkâ of Thráin.","Defeated Warg-riders at Zaghúth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat Warg-riders at Zaghúth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[1780]={"Although the Redhorn Pass remains blocked, your efforts to impair the defences of Zaghúth has loosened the Orcs' grip on Barazinbar.","While exploring the heights of the Redhorn Pass, you have come across the Orkish encampment of Zaghúth. Within Zaghúth, the Orcs have constructed a number of crude barricades to hinder the passage of the dwarves of the Haban'akkâ. In fact, it was this very blockade that forced the Haban'akkâ to approach Azanulbizar from the south instead of taking the Redhorn Pass.\
\
You should destroy the Orkish barricades at Zaghúth and help to make clear the way for the Haban'akkâ.","Orkish barricades can be found at Zaghúth.\
\
You should destroy Orkish barricades at Zaghúth.","Destroy Orkish barricades at Zaghúth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Blocking the Pass","Destroyed Orkish barricades at Zaghúth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You have destroyed many Orkish barricades at Zaghúth.","Destroy Orkish barricades at Zaghúth","Completado","Discovered when the Haban'akkâ first attempted to travel to Azanulbizar, the Orcs of Moria have constructed a crude blockade on the slopes of Barazinbar, the Redhorn."},
[1787]={"The Corsairs and Haradrim make ready once more for battle at Linhir as the Heirs of Castamir seek to avenge their fallen.","'I have failed my brother, ${PLAYER}....\
\
'He had the best mind of us all for how to approach battle, and I allowed him to fall. I should have been here... I should have -'\
\
Erchar trails off, obviously overcome.\
\
'You have done much for my brothers and I, my friend... I have but one more thing to ask of you.'","'You have returned to us just in time, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'We have heard the horns and shouts of the Corsairs and Haradrim in the distance. They come again for Linhir and I doubt there shall be a host of spirits to drive them off this time....\
\
'I fear this shall be no short battle, for your efforts on the coast have surely raised their ire. When you are ready, we shall take the western gates, and my brothers shall guard the entrance to Lebennin.\
\
'Ready your arms, my friend!'","Talk to Erchar in Linhir","Erchar can be found in Linhir in eastern Dor-en-Ernil.\
\
Erchar has asked you to aid him in protecting Linhir from a renewed attack. You should speak to him when you are ready.","Erchar can be found in Linhir in eastern Dor-en-Ernil.\
\
You have defeated the attacking forces from Dor-en-Ernil and Lebennin, but at the cost of Garvir's life. You should speak to Erchar.","Blood for Blood","DNT -- will not be seen","'Let us face down these invaders together, my friend!'","Talk to Erchar"},
[1789]={"'Ah, ${PLAYER}! It is good to see you here once again, my friend.\
\
'For my part, I have not sat idle since the battle at the gates of Mount Gundabad! After the death of Ránulur, Gorgar fled in fear from the Gabil'akkâ! And yes, I am quite aware that Hrímil Frost-heart may have influenced his actions, but it was a victory nonetheless. After so much hardship, a mere wall of ice cannot keep me from my prize!\
\
'I saw you speaking with Glóin. All is well, I hope?'\
\
You tell Durin that Glóin told you of a new plan to reclaim the Mountain-home and you request that you might be the one to bring word of it to Náin.\
\
'Indeed! It is my belief that we should breach the ice on the morrow and hunt down Gorgar within the halls of Gundabad. Dwarves are hardier than Orcs, after all, and if we grant our enemies too much rest, all of our efforts in this war would be for naught. We are so near to victory, my friend! We mustn't let up now!\
\
'As for your request, it is granted. Deliver word of my plans to Náin, and see if he finds it to his liking!'","'So you return, ${PLAYER}. What did they have to say of Prince Durin's plans?'\
\
You inform Náin of what Agnar, Lági, and Reithvald told you.\
\
'I should have expected such wisdom from the Dwarves of the Kharum-ubnâr! In truth, I find myself in agreement with them, but a dwarf of my reputation could hardly deliver such news to Durin. I would be called Náin the Slaked, and that is no title for the Lord of the Iron Hills!\
\
'Were it my army, I would muster more forces to Elderslade and call upon distant cousins and allies, but that would be a matter to bring before my brother, Thorin. Ah, for once, I am pleased such a decision is not left to me!\
\
'You must return to Annâk-khurfu on my behalf, ${PLAYER}. Let this be my guidance to the Prince: seek the wisdom of your father and stay your hand for the moment that it might soon swing with renewed strength.'","'Ah, for once, I am pleased such a decision is not left to me!'","Durin can be found in the war-room at Annâk-khurfu.\
\
Náin the Slakeless has advised you to bring word to Prince Durin that he should stay his hand in the war and consult his father, Thorin, at the Lonely Mountain.","'Before this war began, King Thorin sent three elder warriors to aid his son: Agnar Brokentooth, Lági Helmbiter, and Reithvald Red-ember. They are Dwarves of the Kharum-ubnâr, the Brethren of Survivors. It is an order little known outside the line of Durin's Folk, but its members hold a place of high esteem in the eyes of King Thorin, and more importantly, those of his brother, Náin.\
\
'I would wager there is little that might temper his fervour for battle as much as the word of one of the Kharum-ubnâr — let alone three of them!\
\
'I believe Prince Durin intends to send word to Zarkul-sulûn that his uncle might be apprised of the plan to reclaim Mount Gundabad. It so happens that Agnar, Lági, and Reithvald are among his garrison. Need I explain myself further, ${PLAYER}? This must be done delicately, that the Prince is not undermined in the eyes of the Gabil'akkâ.\
\
'You are a trusted friend, ${PLAYER}, and I am certain the Prince would send you on this errand should you ask.'","Talk to Agnar Brokentooth","Enemies can be found throughout the War of Three Peaks. Agnar Brokentooth, Lági Helmbiter, and Reithvald Red-ember of the Kharum-ubnâr can be found at Zarkul-sulûn and nearby encampments during the War of Three Peaks.\
\
Náin the Slakeless, uncle of Durin, has asked you to present Durin's plan to reclaim Mount Gundabad to Agnar Brokentooth, Lági Helmbiter, and Reithvald Red-ember. He has also asked you to slay enemies of the Gabil'akkâ in the War of Three Peaks.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: You may access the War of Three Peaks by using the Blazon of the Gabil'akkâ behind Durin in Annâk-khurfu or by taking a travel route from the stable-master outside Annâk-khurfu.</rgb>","Defeated enemies in the War of Three Peaks (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'If my uncle and I are in agreement, we will press the attack at dawn!'","Talk to Durin at Annâk-khurfu","Zarkul-sulûn can be found in the War of Three Peaks.\
\
Durin has asked you to return to the war-front and seek the counsel of his uncle, Náin, at Zarkul-sulûn.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: You may access the War of Three Peaks by using the Blazon of the Gabil'akkâ behind Durin in Annâk-khurfu or by taking a travel route from the stable-master outside Annâk-khurfu.</rgb>","'Let us hope the guidance of the Kharum-ubnâr is enough!'","Talk to Lági Helmbiter","Travel to Zarkul-sulûn in the War of Three Peaks","'Lord Náin has sent you? I have much to report, ${PLAYER}, some for good and some for ill.\
\
'Of the good, our defences have held against the Orcs and their numbers have dwindled since our encounter at the gates of Mount Gundabad. Those few that make their way to our line are unorganized and easy prey for the Zhélruka. In the past several days, I am proud to report that we have not lost a single dwarf!\
\
'Ah, but of the bad, it should come as little surprise. We are still engaged in war, my friend. There is no time to simply take shelter and rest while Gorgar hides within the Mountain-home. After all, there are other ways out of that mountain and the Orcs must know all of them.'\
\
You interject to ask Reithvald about Prince Durin's plan to reclaim Gundabad.\
\
'Ah, that is not so simple a matter. My soldiers are in need of rest. I have seen enough of battle to know the signs of fatigue, even if they are too proud to admit it.\
\
'Durin holds some of his army in reserve at Annâk-khurfu, and I would urge him to send as many soldiers as he can spare to relieve us. Even if only for a short time, it would be of great help to us for the coming battles!'","'How fares my nephew at Annâk-khurfu, ${PLAYER}?'\
\
You exchange welcomes with Náin, and then tell him of Prince Durin's plans to reclaim Gundabad. After a moment, you ask Náin what the Kharum-ubnâr in his garrison might make of it.\
\
'It is a sound plan to my ear, but my eagerness for battle is well-known. I would not even wait for the morrow, were I a younger dwarf!'\
\
Náin pauses.\
\
'It may be that Thorin is not as well-suited to battle as I am, but he is keen in judgement. It was not by a mere whim that my brother sent three of the Kharum-ubnâr to aid the Prince. Beyond those three warriors, none of the Longbeards in the Gabil'akkâ, even old Glóin, have seen so much of battle and its costs.\
\
'I will honour your request, if you would honour one of my own. I have seen Gorgar's ilk, all manner of evil beasts, and even some of those wicked Men of Angmar drawing nearer to Zarkul-sulûn since the battle at the gates, and I would not have them doubt our mettle. Slay them to the last!\
\
'Let us see how the Kharum-ubnâr judge Durin's plan, ${PLAYER}.'","Although the din of war can be heard in the distance, Zarkul-sulûn is quiet","Náin the Slakeless can be found at Zarkul-sulûn in the War of Three Peaks.\
\
Durin has asked you to return to the war-front and seek the counsel of his uncle, Náin, at Zarkul-sulûn.","Náin the Slakeless can be found at Zarkul-sulûn in the War of Three Peaks.\
\
You have slain many foes in the War of Three Peaks, and you have heard the guidance of Agnar, Lági, and Reithvald in regard to Prince Durin's plan to reclaim Gundabad. You should return to Náin.","'${PLAYER}, what did Náin have to say of my plan?'\
\
You deliver Náin's guidance to Prince Durin. The Prince's face becomes stern, betraying the faintest hint of embarrassment.\
\
'I must admit, my friend, that is not the response I expected. But if uncle Náin believes I should send word to my father that the Gabil'akkâ might be the better for it, I have no reason to doubt his judgment. After all, it was not so long ago that I spent my days at the Quenching Trough in Járnfast, spared the battle before the Lonely Mountain by the will of my father. Ah, but when it is my uncle who urges restraint, only a fool would ignore his counsel!\
\
'Perhaps I was too swift to dismiss Glóin's concerns. I shall have to apologize to him for my imprudence, if I might.\
\
'It seems I have much still to learn, despite my station.'","'It is good to see you, ${PLAYER}. But what has brought you here?'\
\
You present Prince Durin's plan to reclaim Mount Gundabad to Lági and ask his thoughts on it.\
\
'Although he has led the Gabil'akkâ admirably through this war, I have many misgivings in regard to the Prince's plan.\
\
'Just look at the soldiers here in Zarkul-sulûn. They are tired.\
\
'We spent the lives of many dwarves to win the gates of Mount Gundabad, but for those who survived, it is now a matter of will — and not all of the dwarves in the Gabil'akkâ can bear such a burden. Hardship is to be expected in war, but many of these soldiers do not know it as I do.\
\
'In my youth, we spent six years of bitter war fighting our enemies, but even in the height of his fury, King Thráin knew the value of respite from battle. Many look back at that war as a single, great battle at Azanulbizar, but had we fought those years without rest, we would never have made it to the gates of Khazad-dûm.\
\
'If Prince Durin would hear my advice, it is that our soldiers need rest and the time to heal for the coming battles. We have been fortunate thus far in the War of Three Peaks, but winning a battle does not win a war!'","Eager to put an end to the War of Three Peaks, Durin has devised a plan to reclaim Mount Gundabad.","Defeat enemies in the War of Three Peaks (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Blood of Azog: A Lesson Hard-learned","'Well, what had the elders of the Kharum-ubnâr to say of the Prince's plan?'","Talk to Reithvald Red-ember","Talk to Náin the Slakeless at Zarkul-sulûn","Durin can be found in the war-room at Annâk-khurfu.\
\
Glóin has asked you to speak to Durin.","'What does Lord Náin ask of me?'\
\
You tell Agnar about Prince Durin's plan to reclaim Mount Gundabad and ask what he thinks of it.\
\
'We did what we could to hinder Gorgar and his army of Orcs on the field, but these old bones are not as strong as they were when I was a younger dwarf. I am as eager as Prince Durin to return to Gundabad, but it is a difficult prize to grasp — and I should know!\
\
'After all, I was there when Komog, son of Azog, fell broken in its halls, and I remember how it fell just as quickly back into the hands of the Orcs after the war!\
\
'Do not misunderstand me, ${PLAYER}. I think much better of our chances this time, but I would not press the attack until we are better prepared for what awaits us within.'"},
[1790]={"Travel to Annâk-khurfu in Elderslade","'It's time we set out, I think!\
\
'I am not the young dwarf I once was, so better we travel sooner than later. Ah, but before we go, you should speak to King Thorin. After all, he will wish to know that another dwarf is coming with us!'\
\
Hermáth gestures to Hersegg.\
\
'Come along, ${PLAYER}. We ought to find him in the Hall Under the Mountain!'","Find Prince Durin and Hermáth Stormhammer in the war-room at Annâk-khurfu","With Hermáth Stormhammer near at his side, Durin appears both confused and awed","Hersegg can be found outside Annâk-khurfu in Elderslade.\
\
You have arrived at Annâk-khurfu in Elderslade and Hermáth Stormhammer has gone to speak to Prince Durin. You should talk to Hersegg.","'Ah, ${PLAYER}!\
\
'It is high time you returned to my son, I think. After all, there is a war to be won and the Mountain-home awaits!\
\
'Although I am certain my father Dáin would have been just as eager to join in the reclamation of Mount Gundabad, I am pleased that Hermáth will be there to guide Durin in the coming days of his campaign.\
\
'You have done much to aid my son. For that, I and all of Durin's Folk thank you. May the Gabil'akkâ triumph!'","Talk to Hermáth Stormhammer at Annâk-khurfu","Talk to Hermáth Stormhammer in the Hall Under the Mountain, in Erebor","'When I asked my father to send his aid, I did not expect you to return with Hermáth Stormhammer!'\
\
Durin appears overwhelmed.\
\
'Hermáth and I have spoken since his arrival, and we have agreed that the Gabil'akkâ will march on Mount Gundabad at dawn—in seven days, of course! Those that would answer the muster will need time to travel to Elderslade, and I eagerly await their arrival. Every dwarf shall have a role to play in the reclamation of Mount Gundabad!'","King Thorin can be found at his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain at Erebor.\
\
After preparing for the journey to Elderslade, Hermáth Stormhammer has suggested the three of you speak to King Thorin. You should talk to King Thorin.","Talk to Durin at Annâk-khurfu","Dashing off, Hersegg enters Annâk-khurfu","Hermáth Stormhammer can be found before King Thorin's throne in the Hall Under the Mountain at Erebor.\
\
After bidding farewell to King Thorin, Hermáth and Hersegg appear ready to begin the journey to Elderslade. You should talk to Hermáth Stormhammer.","As Hermáth walks into Annâk-khurfu, Hersegg sighs","As you arrive at Annâk-khurfu, Hermáth and Hersegg look out upon Elderslade","Durin can be found in the war-room at Annâk-khurfu.\
\
After Hermáth Stormhammer's arrival at Annâk-khurfu, Durin appears equally confused and awed. You should find and talk to Durin.","King Thorin can be found in the Hall Under the Mountain, in Erebor.\
\
Hoping to set out for Elderslade, Hermáth Stormhammer has urged you to bid your farewells to King Thorin. You should find King Thorin in the Hall Under the Mountain.","'So this is Elderslade? Hmmph, it is smaller than it seemed in grandfather's stories!'\
\
Hersegg pauses.\
\
'It is beautiful, though, and Mount Gundabad is greater than I could have ever imagined. Ah, but this is not a time for tours. I should introduce myself to the Dwarves of the Gabil'akkâ and see what needs to be done!\
\
'I'm sure I'll see you around, ${PLAYER}. After all, this won't be the last time you hear my name!'","Durin can be found in the war-room at Annâk-khurfu.\
\
You have returned to Annâk-khurfu at last. You should find and talk to Durin.","Find King Thorin in the Hall Under the Mountain, in Erebor","Hermáth Stormhammer can be found outside Annâk-khurfu in Elderslade.\
\
You have arrived at Annâk-khurfu in Elderslade. You should talk to Hermáth Stormhammer.","Annâk-khurfu can be found in Elderslade.\
\
You should travel to Annâk-khurfu in Elderslade with Hermáth and Hersegg.","After resolving to aid King Thorin Stonehelm and Prince Durin, Hermáth Stormhammer and Hersegg prepare to join the Gabil'akkâ at Elderslade.","'It has been a long time... but the Slade is still as I remember it.\
\
'This old fortress had a different name during the Sixth War, but Annâk-khurfu is more fitting, I think.\
\
'I am glad that our paths have crossed, ${PLAYER}. When the time comes to reclaim Gundabad, I will consider myself fortunate to have you at my side—and I am sure Durin will think much the same!\
\
'I ought to not keep Prince Durin waiting, so I will meet you inside, my friend.'","'A moment, ${PLAYER}....'\
\
Hermáth Stormhammer looks to King Thorin and speaks.\
\
'Do not fear for your son, Thorin. Your father, Dáin, was so proud when he was born, and rightly so! Each of us hoped that our sons would be Durin reborn... and though it was not fated to be for my son, I still hold hope that Durin will embody his namesake when the time is right.'\
\
Hermáth Stormhammer turns back to you.\
\
'Lead the way, my new friend... the Prince awaits us!'\
\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: You will swiftly travel to Annâk-khurfu in Elderslade when you advance this quest.</rgb>","Talk to King Thorin in the Hall Under the Mountain, in Erebor","Talk to Hersegg at Annâk-khurfu","Blood of Azog: At Seventh Light","You arrive at King Thorin's throne with Hermáth and Hersegg at your side"},
[1791]={"Blood of Azog: Brethren of Past and Present","<rgb=#FF00FF>Hail</rgb> Nár at Akrâz-zahar","Travel to Akrâz-zahar in the Dwelling-halls of Tumnu-dûm, in Erebor","Across the dimly-lit hall of Akrâz-zahar, you spot a young dwarf matching King Thorin's description","Hersegg stands behind a bar within Akrâz-zahar, dutifully cleaning plates and mugs.","'What business have you with the Kharum-ubnâr?'\
\
Hersegg appears to tighten her grip on a weapon beneath your view. You swiftly explain that you have been sent by King Thorin to deliver a missive to Hersegg.\
\
'A missive from King Thorin? I do hope this isn't about the cave-claws again. Last time was an accident, I swear it!'","Find Hersegg in Akrâz-zahar","As King Thorin prepares to call upon the Longbeards and their allies to muster to Mount Gundabad, his thoughts turn to the Kharum-ubnâr of the Lonely Mountain.","Nár can be found at Akrâz-zahar in the Dwelling-halls of Tumnu-dûm, in Erebor.\
\
Frithgeir hopes Nár might bid you well in your quest before he returns home to rest. You should hail Nár, and see if he wishes to say anything.","Hersegg can be found at Akrâz-zahar in the Dwelling-halls of Tumnu-dûm, in Erebor.\
\
After seeing Frithgeir and Nár off, you should return to your task and find Hersegg at Akrâz-zahar.","As you enter Akrâz-zahar, a familiar dwarf greets you!","Nár smiles happily, but he does not appear to notice you.","'My son asks my guidance in winning a war.'\
\
Thorin chuckles to himself.\
\
'I may not be a warrior in the manner of my father, ${PLAYER}, but I know well enough that those of Kharum-ubnâr learned such lessons long ago.\
\
'After all, it was Dáin who organized the Kharum-ubnâr after the war's end. It was to be comprised of those who survived the Sixth War, and those descended from Marasrân—the Burned Dwarves of Azanulbizar. Agnar, Lági, and Reithvald are not the only dwarves of that order who still dwell within the Lonely Mountain, my friend. Perhaps their wisdom might be of use to my son....'\
\
Thorin thinks for a moment, stroking his beard. After a moment, he produces a small scrap of paper and writes upon it a short message.\
\
'Within the Dwelling-halls of Tumnu-dûm, there is an order-hall of the Kharum-ubnâr. It is known among Durin's Folk as Akrâz-zahar, and there you might find a dwarf named Hersegg. She is barely beyond the age of a stripling, but she is the granddaughter of one of the greatest heroes of Azanulbizar, and more importantly, one of the dearest friends of my father, Dáin.\
\
'I have written her a note asking that she might introduce you to the works of her grandfather, Hermáth Stormhammer. She, too, is well-studied in the lore of Durin's Folk, possessing wisdom beyond her years.\
\
'Deliver this missive to her, and she will understand what I ask.'","Frithgeir can be found at Akrâz-zahar in the Dwelling-halls of Tumnu-dûm, in Erebor.\
\
Nár's mind appears clouded, but he seemed to wish you well. You should talk to Frithgeir.","Nár shuffles for a moment, but his gaze soon fixes upon you","Hersegg can be found at Akrâz-zahar in the Dwelling-halls of Tumnu-dûm, in Erebor.\
\
You have found Hersegg at Akrâz-zahar. You should deliver King Thorin's missive to Hersegg.","Deliver King Thorin's missive to Hersegg at Akrâz-zahar","'${PLAYER}! What brings you back to the Lonely Mountain?\
\
'I heard you followed Prince Durin in his quest. Was that not so?'\
\
You explain to Frithgeir that you have returned at Durin's request to seek the aid of King Thorin.\
\
'I see. Well, do not let me keep you, my friend. For my part, I was just about to take Nár home. It has been a long day, and although he was more himself this morning, his mind... has wandered. Perhaps Nár might wish you well in your quest, but I can make no promise.\
\
'Nár?'","Talk to Frithgeir at Akrâz-zahar","'Deliver this missive to Hersegg at Akrâz-zahar, my friend.'","Akrâz-zahar can be found in the Dwelling-halls of Tumnu-dûm, in Erebor.\
\
King Thorin has asked you to deliver a missive to Hersegg, granddaughter of Hermáth Stormhammer, at Akrâz-zahar that the wisdom of the Kharum-ubnâr might help guide Durin to victory. You should travel to Akrâz-zahar.","After a moment, Frithgeir and Nár depart Akrâz-zahar","'Thank you, ${PLAYER}. It means a great deal to me, and I know it does Nár good to see his friends.\
\
'Wherever Prince Durin's quest might lead you, I hope you take care of yourself, my friend. Perhaps we will see you when next you return to the Lonely Mountain!'","Nár glances around Akrâz-zahar, seemingly unaware of your presence","Frithgeir can be found at Akrâz-zahar in the Dwelling-halls of Tumnu-dûm, in Erebor.\
\
Upon entering Akrâz-zahar, you have come across the dwarf, Frithgeir, and his companion, Nár. You should talk to Frithgeir."},
[1792]={"Listen to King Thorin's thoughts of his father, Dáin","King Thorin can be found at his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain at Erebor.\
\
You should talk to King Thorin.","'A moment, my friend.'\
\
King Thorin reads the missive from Durin.\
\
'I see. Tell me, ${PLAYER}, how did my son come to change his mind, truly?'\
\
You tell King Thorin of Glóin's concern and of his suggestion to speak to the Dwarves of the Kharum-ubnâr among the Gabil'akkâ.\
\
'It was for that reason I sent them, and I am heartened that Glóin warned him against plans borne of vengeance. I only wish my son had heeded his words. Durin leads the greatest Longbeard army we have brought to bear in seventy years, but he is still young and, in truth, untested. Yes, he has found victory at many stops along his journey from the Iron Hills, but it is hardship that shapes a dwarf!\
\
'Durin was fortunate to know my father, Dáin, in his time. He, too, was young when he answered the call of war, and I often wonder what he would think of how swiftly Durin has grown into his name.'","Deliver the letters, parcels, and Durin's missive to King Thorin in the Hall Under the Mountain, in Erebor","King Thorin can be found at his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain at Erebor.\
\
Durin has written a missive to be delivered to his father, Thorin, at Erebor. You should deliver the letters, parcels, and Durin's missive to King Thorin at Erebor.","Collected parcels (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'So be it, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'I must admit, I had not expected to send another messenger to the Lonely Mountain until this war was ended. I had hoped to send tidings of victory to my father—that I might finally prove myself a dwarf worthy of the name \\qDurin\\q!\
\
'Bah, perhaps it was folly to entertain such stubbornness! If my uncle believes the Gabil'akkâ would be helped by again swelling its numbers, I see no reason to argue with him.'\
\
Durin looks across the upper hall of Annâk-khurfu.\
\
'I will need some time to draft a missive to my father, but I have had an idea!\
\
'Many of the Longbeards here at Annâk-khurfu have written letters and prepared parcels to be delivered to their kin at the Lonely Mountain. Unfortunately, a great deal of them have gone unsent in recent days. It would please me to correct this oversight at the same time!\
\
'I will set to writing my father at once. After you have gathered all of the letters and parcels, return to me.'","King Thorin can be found at his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain at Erebor.\
\
King Thorin is musing on thoughts of his son, Durin, and his father, Dáin.","With great relief, you set everything on the landing before King Thorin's throne","Talk to Durin at Annâk-khurfu","Blood of Azog: Fathers and Sons","Durin can be found in the war-room at Annâk-khurfu.\
\
You have collected all of the letters and parcels prepared by the Longbeards of the Gabil'akkâ. You should return to Durin.","As his thoughts turn to Durin, Thorin's voice swells:\
\
'I have always been the more cautious of Dáin's sons, and it has served me well. But for too long, I believed it would suit Durin in much the same manner.\
\
'It was not so long ago that I sequestered Durin in the Iron Hills while battle raged in the Dale-lands, but now my son leads an army to reclaim the Mountain-home. I dared not dream that Gundabad might be within reach, especially after the failure of the Iron Garrison, and yet, my son has proven its possibility, both to me and to all of Durin's Folk.\
\
'Durin is not as hot-tempered as my brother, nor is he as measured as his father—he is himself, and that is enough. Durin will err, as any dwarf will in his time, but I did not name him Durin that he would earn the name in his life—the name will earn him through his deeds.'","'I have thought often both of my son, and of my father, Dáin, since Durin set off into the Grey Mountains.'","'It is true that many Dwarves of the Iron Garrison pledged themselves into the service of my son, and more still journeyed from our holdings in the Misty Mountains to aid the Gabil'akkâ. Even so, there are many Longbeards and trustworthy Dwarves of the Landorrim and Narfanghoth that might still be called upon.\
\
'Durin has requested that I send a new muster to the Mountain-home. It will be done!'\
\
Thorin pauses for a moment and strokes his beard.\
\
'But so too does my son ask for my guidance, and that has given me much to consider.'","Collected letters (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collect letters (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","As he reminisces about Dáin, Thorin's voice softens:\
\
'What can be said of my father, Dáin, that has not been etched into the very history of Durin's Folk?\
\
'He was but a stripling when he slew the Great-orc, Azog, at Azanulbizar. It was he who answered the call of Thorin Oakenshield and defended the Lonely Mountain against Bolg and the goblins of the North, and in so doing, ushered in a time of peace between Men, Elves, and dwarves. And again, when the Enemy sent his servants to the gates of the Lonely Mountain, he died in defence of his people—a hero to his last breath!\
\
'But despite all of his great deeds, I knew him as my father. I was his son, and Durin, his beloved grandson.\
\
'I must confess that I often saw more of Dáin in Durin than I did in myself, but what greater dwarf could one aspire to be?'","Collect parcels (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to King Thorin in the Hall Under the Mountain, in Erebor","Letters and parcels can be found within and without at Annâk-khurfu.\
\
Durin has asked you to collect the letters and parcels of Longbeards fighting in the War of Three Peaks before you depart for the Lonely Mountain.","'I will need some time to draft a missive to my father, so gather the letters and parcels here at Annâk-khurfu.'","'Ah, very good!\
\
'I have written my father a formal request for a new muster to Elderslade—one that comprises all of our trusted allies, even those unskilled in combat. When the time comes to reclaim Gundabad, we will have need for dwarves of every vocation!\
\
'I have also made special note that I will not begin the assault on Mount Gundabad until the time of your return. If my father wishes to offer any guidance, I would prefer to hear it before the battle is upon us!'\
\
Durin seals the missive he has written to his father and hands it to you.\
\
'By entrusting you with this missive, I am entrusting you with the success of the Gabil'akkâ, my friend.\
\
'Be swift and let nothing turn you from your path to the Lonely Mountain!'","King Thorin's mind turns to thoughts of Dáin and Durin","After seeking the counsel of his uncle, Náin, Durin has chosen to send word to his father, King Thorin III Stonehelm, at the Lonely Mountain.","'Deliver the missive to my father as swiftly as you are able, ${PLAYER}!'","'Welcome, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'It has been some time since Glóin's message-raven arrived, bearing a warning that the line of Azog remains unbroken in Gundabad. What news do you bring of my son? How fares his campaign?'\
\
You inform King Thorin of the events that have transpired since he sent the remnants of the Iron Garrison to Annâk-khurfu. You tell the tale of the battle on the threshold of Gundabad—of Gorgar's near-defeat and of the sudden danger of Hrímil Frost-heart, returned from the Anvil of Winterstith. You also tell King Thorin of Durin's desire to press the attack and how he was persuaded against it, at least for the moment, by Náin and dwarves of the Kharum-ubnâr.\
\
'I feared you had come bearing ill tidings, my friend. So long as my son is well, it puts my heart at ease.'\
\
Thorin glances at the mass of letters and parcels you have brought to Erebor.\
\
'I appreciate that you answered me as swiftly as you did, but please, set all of that down. My subjects will see that they are delivered to the proper dwarves here in the Lonely Mountain.\
\
'As for his missive, let us see what he has written.'","Listen to King Thorin's thoughts of his son, Durin"},
[1793]={"'Let us make certain that Durin receives his reinforcements, ${PLAYER}. The Gabil'akkâ must be well-prepared for the conquest of the Mountain-home!\
\
'To that end, I have written a number of missives to be delivered to other Longbeard holdings across the world as well as those of our cousins, the Landorrim and Narfanghoth. Among several others, I have called upon all the dwarves of Thorin's Hall, Gabilazan, and even Gabilshathûr in the realm of old Angmar. None shall be excluded from joining the Gabil'akkâ, for as my son rightly said, there will be need for dwarves of all vocations at Gundabad in the days ahead.\
\
In addition, I have drafted missives to the Kings of the Temámir, the Abnúzhu, and... the Kámbrada. After all, it is high time they learned of their cousins from Mordor! I do not know if any among them will send word in return, but I hold hope that the old friendships between our peoples have not been forgotten.\
\
'I ask that you seek out Skalla, Vísbur, Fregi, Garni, and Uddvar here at Erebor, and see that they bring word of the muster to the Mountain-home!\
\
'Will you deliver these missives to my riders, ${PLAYER}?'","Deliver a missive to Garni at Erebor","Vísbur accepts the missive, and prepares to set off","Deliver a missive to Fregi at Erebor","King Thorin's riders can be found at the Lonely Mountain, Erebor.\
\
King Thorin has asked you to deliver missives to his riders at Erebor. You should deliver missives to King Thorin's riders.","After you delivered a missive to Hersegg, granddaughter of Hermáth Stormhammer, and learned of the Sixth War of the Dwarves and Orcs, King Thorin has tasked you with guiding his swiftest riders to send word of the muster to the Mountain-home.","King Thorin can be found at his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain at Erebor.\
\
You have delivered all of the missives to King Thorin's riders at Erebor. You should return to King Thorin.","Deliver a missive to Uddvar at Erebor","'Deliver these missives to my riders at once!'","'It is done? Very good, my friend.\
\
'Let us hope their errands are done swiftly and without incident. If the reclamation is to succeed, a great many dwarves must answer the call to Elderslade!'","Talk to King Thorin in the Hall Under the Mountain, in Erebor","Deliver a missive to Vísbur at Erebor","Garni accepts the missive, and prepares to set off","Blood of Azog: Muster to the Mountain-home","Skalla accepts the missive, and prepares to set off","Deliver a missive to Skalla at Erebor","Fregi accepts the missive, and prepares to set off","Uddvar accepts the missive, and prepares to set off"},
[1794]={"'Tales of Yore: Azanulbizar' can be found at Akrâz-zahar within the Lonely Mountain.\
\
You have begun your study of Hermáth Stormhammer's account of the Battle of Azanulbizar. You should complete your study before returning to King Thorin.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: You must complete the deed 'The Battle of Azanulbizar' to advance this quest.</rgb>","'As for Nár, I think it's good that he has finally left Zudrugund behind.\
\
'Since his return, Nár has made many friends in the Lonely Mountain. When he feels well enough to visit us here in Akrâz-zahar, I have heard his laugh and seen the light in his eye when he smiles. Although it pains me to even think such a thing, perhaps his addlement has been something of a mercy — some small kindness bestowed upon him by the First Crafter.\
\
'Let us hope that Nár has found some measure of happiness again, even at so old an age. It is the very least he deserves!\
\
'Now then, I must tend to the task King Thorin gave to me, and you ought to begin your studies of my grandfather's work!'\
\
Hersegg gestures to a stack of books atop the nearby table.\
\
'Those will tell you all you need to know about the Battle of Azanulbizar, ${PLAYER}. When you've studied it enough for your liking, you are to return to the King Under the Mountain.\
\
'With any luck, I'll see you again soon.'","Complete your study of Hermáth Stormhammer's account of the Battle of Azanulbizar","Blood of Azog: The Sixth War","Hersegg can be found at Akrâz-zahar in Erebor, the Lonely Mountain.\
\
You have listened to Hersegg's telling of Nár's tale as transcribed by her grandfather, Hermáth Stormhammer. You should talk to Hersegg.","King Thorin can be found at his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain at Erebor.\
\
You have finished your study of Hermáth Stormhammer's account of the Battle of Azanulbizar. You should return to King Thorin.","Talk to King Thorin in the Hall Under the Mountain, in Erebor","'Tales of Yore: Azanulbizar' can be found at Akrâz-zahar within the Lonely Mountain.\
\
After learning that King Thorin wishes for you to learn more of the Battle of Azanulbizar, Hersegg has directed you to the works of her grandfather, Hermáth Stormhammer, collected in a volume known as 'Tales of Yore: Azanulbizar'.","Talk to Hersegg and learn of 'Nár's Tale'","To the surprise of both you and the dwarf Hersegg, King Thorin's missive directed Hersegg to share with you her grandfather's account of the Battle of Azanulbizar.","Begin your study of Hermáth Stormhammer's account of the Battle of Azanulbizar\
<rgb=#FF0000>(Use 'Tales of Yore: Azanulbizar' in Akrâz-zahar to travel to Azanulbizar, T.A. 2799)</rgb>","Talk to Hersegg at Akrâz-zahar","'Let me see what all this is about!'\
\
Hersegg looks over the missive from King Thorin. Her bushy eyebrows raise and lower a few times until finally she lets out what seems to be a sigh of relief.\
\
'Well, that wasn't what I expected....\
\
'I must apologize for my curt introduction, ${PLAYER}. I am Hersegg, and I tend to Akrâz-zahar on behalf of the Kharum-ubnâr.\
\
'As for that missive, it seems King Thorin wishes for me to introduce you to the works of my grandfather, Hermáth Stormhammer. He kept a detailed account of his experiences in the Sixth War of the Dwarves and Orcs, especially the Battle of Azanulbizar. In fact, a collection of his volumes are right over there! Although I am sure Prince Durin has heard tales of that war before, the King insists your study of it will be of use to his son and the Gabil'akkâ.\
\
'But it's no use studying the battle without hearing the beginning of the tale, I say. King Thorin has given me a task of my own, but since I have a little time, I'd be honoured to read it to you.\
\
'So, what do you say?'","'What did you make of Hermáth's account, my friend?'\
\
You talk to King Thorin about Hermáth's account of the battle, making note of certain moments.\
\
'Ah, very good. I am told it is quite a faithful retelling of the battle... speaking as a dwarf who wasn't there, of course!\
\
'While you were off with the Kharum-ubnâr, I had time to consider our next course of action. My son awaits his reinforcements!'","Hersegg can be found at Akrâz-zahar in Erebor, the Lonely Mountain.\
\
Hersegg has offered to tell you Nár's tale as transcribed by her grandfather, Hermáth Stormhammer. You should talk to Hersegg."},
[1795]={"'I couldn't keep her here even if I wanted to, ${PLAYER}....'\
\
Hermáth smiles to himself. After a moment, he looks around his room, his gaze landing upon his old armour and hammer.\
\
'Wait outside a moment, and I will meet you in the Dwelling-halls.'\
\
'Would you please give this old dwarf a moment to equip himself? Go on!'","Talk to Hermáth Stormhammer at Vosh Torú","King Thorin can be found at Vosh Torú in the Lonely Mountain.\
\
After talking with King Thorin, Hermáth Stormhammer has agreed to aid Prince Durin and the Gabil'akkâ. You should talk to King Thorin.","King Thorin can be found at his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain at Erebor.\
\
King Thorin has asked you to accompany him to Vosh Torú for a meeting with one of the Kharum-ubnâr. You should talk to King Thorin.","Hersegg can be found at Vosh Torú in the Lonely Mountain.\
\
As King Thorin left Vosh Torú, Hersegg called you over. You should talk to Hersegg.","Determined to aid his son, Durin, and the Dwarves of the Gabil'akkâ to reclaim Mount Gundabad, King Thorin Stonehelm hopes to enlist the aid of an old friend.","Talk to Hersegg at Vosh Torú","'If my grandfather is going to join the Gabil'akkâ, then so am I!'\
\
From the other room, you hear Hermáth chuckle to himself.\
\
'I'm no younger than your old friend, Dáin, was when he went to war! Who knows what sort of title I might win for myself?\
\
'I'm going to gather my things, ${PLAYER}. My grandfather can try to stop me if he wishes!'","'You must understand, ${PLAYER}. Hermáth was my father's friend, not mine.\
\
'After what happened at the end of the War, I feared he would want nothing to do with me. I know how dear Durin was to him, and my heart aches that his son fell in the defence of the Lonely Mountain.\
\
'Yet, young Hersegg has her father's spirit. If Hermáth honours my request as he says, I think he will have a difficult time convincing Hersegg to stay behind!\
\
'Ah, I must return to the Hall Under the Mountain, my friend. But, thank you for helping me to clear the air between us!'","Leave Vosh Torú and await Hermáth Stormhammer in the Dwelling-halls","Hermáth Stormhammer can be found outside Vosh Torú in the Lonely Mountain.\
\
Hermáth Stormhammer has equipped himself, and it appears Hersegg has convinced him to let her join the Gabil'akkâ. You should talk to Hermáth Stormhammer.","After a brief wait, Hermáth and Hersegg walk out of Vosh Torú","You should wait for Hermáth Stormhammer outside Vosh Torú.","Hermáth Stormhammer can be found at Vosh Torú in the Lonely Mountain.\
\
In an effort to aid King Thorin, Hermáth Stormhammer has agreed to travel to Elderslade and join Prince Durin and the Gabil'akkâ in the reclamation of Mount Gundabad. You should talk to Hermáth Stormhammer.","Talk to King Thorin","Talk to King Thorin at Vosh Torú","Wait for Hermáth Stormhammer outside Vosh Torú","Vosh Torú can be found in the Lonely Mountain.\
\
Hermáth Stormhammer has asked you to wait outside Vosh Torú as he equips himself. You should leave Vosh Torú and wait outside.","'There! Now that is more like it!'","You have left Vosh Torú and should now wait for Hermáth Stormhammer","'It is time we dealt with the matter at hand, my friend.\
\
'When I sent you to seek out Hersegg at Akrâz-zahar, I also gave to her an errand. Although I sent Agnar, Lági, and Reithvald to aid my son in his campaign, I must admit I hesitated to enlist another of my father's old friends in the Kharum-ubnâr. Not because I did not think him suited to the task, but for reasons I am ashamed to give voice. But I have shrunken from my duty for long enough!\
\
'As I had hoped, Hersegg has sent word that I have been invited to visit her family's home at Vosh Torú. Whether this meeting goes well or ill, Durin awaits your return.\
\
'What say you, ${PLAYER}? Will you accompany me?'","'I will show you the way to Vosh Torú, my friend.'","As King Thorin leaves, Hersegg calls you over","Blood of Azog: Will of the Stormhammer","Talk to Hermáth Stormhammer"},
[1796]={"'I wonder if you might help me. It is a delicate matter.\
\
'My brother Zûfan has been shaving down his coins, you see, giving the overseer less than her share. I told him not to, but he said he would never get caught. He started doing it for some of the other workers as well.\
\
'Well, this morning I heard a rumour that the overseer caught on to these ruses, and now my brother has vanished. Even if he has run away, I just want to know he's all right. He may be a fool, but he is family.\
\
'Go to our home and see if you can find any clue to where he went. Please, ${PLAYER}, can you help me?'","'He took enough to survive for some time out in the wild. There is a place we used to go as children. It is north, outside the fort here and then west down toward the shoreline. He must have gone there. Please, see if he is well.'","Ayaluk directed you to a location north-west along the shoreline","Ayaluk is concerned that the overseer in Rakhatâb has injured or killed his brother Zûfan.","Find Ayaluk's brother Zûfan","Find clues to Zûfan's disappearance (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","It appears that trail rations were taken","Speak with Ayaluk in Rakhatâb","Ulanor found Zûfan before you and exacted the blood price for his debts. You need to deliver this sad news to Ayaluk.","Bring the sad news to Ayaluk in Rakhatâb","Ayaluk's brother is dead by Overseer Ulanor's hand","It appears an oil lantern was taken","'Thank you for trying. The fool knew the risks. I warned him.'\
\
Tears well in his eyes.\
\
'I am going to build a cairn for my brother down at the shoreline. I will try to remember our days of happiness and laughter. Feel free to visit me there.'","It appears a pack was taken","Witness the tragedy","Ayaluk is concerned about his brother. He went missing several days ago after a visit from a collector of debts.","Zûfan likely went to the place where the siblings used to hide as children, north from the city and then west along the cliffs near the shoreline. Go there and ensure that the brother is well.","Blood of My Blood","You discovered that there was a missing pack, oil lantern, and trail rations taken from the home."},
[1798]={"The spear can be found somewhere in the southern reaches of the Dead Marshes.\
\
Faramir has asked you to seek the Wainrider spear that slew him in the Dead Marshes in the hope that it might grant you passage into Dol Acharn.","Sangre de Númenor","Faramir can be found near the foot of Dol Acharn.\
\
You have recovered the remains of the Wainrider spearhead and should now return it to Faramir.","'Yes, ${PLAYER}... that is the one.\
\
'It is rotted and rusted with the passage of time, but it can be no other. I can feel the spear piercing my chest anew even now...\
\
'This pain... it cannot stop me now. It is time our ruse is tested! Let us see if the chieftain's weapon of old might be wielded against him, ${PLAYER}!'","Search the Dead Marshes for the spear that slew Faramir","An evil presence lingers about the Wainriders upon the hill of Dol Acharn, and it urges even the hardiest warriors away.","Deliver the spearhead to Faramir near Dol Acharn","'I have looked upon the faces of the Wainriders at Dol Acharn, and though many of them are lost to my memory - one has never been forgotten. It is the face of their chieftain - the face of the man who slew me!\
\
'Even now, I remember facing down the Wainrider chieftain with the north-men. All at once, it felt as if each of us stood alone in the battle against him and his kin. After his horse and chariot became stranded in the marshes, he ran me down himself and I could not flee in the shallows. The mud and murk held my feet and soon he was upon me. I fell, and the blood of the king's line spilled into the marshes. My folly had grown a terrible defeat into no less than a disaster for my people.\
\
'His spear tasted the blood of Númenor, and he knew the victory he had won over Gondor could not be contested by any Man. Such a triumph grew a great arrogance within him, and as your friend Artamir told us, his death soon followed.\
\
'You must gain an audience with the Wainrider chieftain if our ruse is to succeed, but it seems you shall find no such kindness without bearing a trinket of their peoples.\
\
'I would have you seek the very spear that slew me in the marshes to the north. It is unlikely they will yield even once you bear it, but it is the only means we have to speak to their master.'","You have recovered a rusting, rotted spearhead of early Easterling make"},
[1801]={"'I do not trust these rumours... Castamir's sons escaped when he was slain, but I do not believe his line could have continued for so long.\
\
'I will follow them if it allows me to keep my life, but they are cruel, vicious men and I do not think them proper leaders for Gondor.'","Nimithil can be found in the lowest section of Ost Anglebed with her guards.\
\
You have spoken to many folk of Ost Anglebed and should now seek out Nimithil.","Maerien is uncertain, but recalls folk loyal to Castamir in her line","'I care not if they are of the blood-line - Castamir the Usurper was a monster who spat in the faces of his people, and these brutal men have proven to be no better than him. To grant any of them the throne would be madness!\
\
'Were I a warrior, I would drive them from Gondor myself!'","'I am Nimithil of Pelargir. Why have you come to me?'\
\
You introduce yourself and tell Nimithil of the Steward's curiosity.\
\
'I do not care to know their goals, ${PLAYER}. When you bear the name of one as reviled as Castamir the Usurper, you cannot seek to do good for the people of Gondor.\
\
'Trouble is growing in Lebennin, and it must be dealt with soon.'","'The folk of my line once counted themselves amongst the followers of Castamir. His dishonour tainted our family's name for years, but perhaps his descendants can restore it.\
\
'The people of Gondor have waited long enough for the rightful Heir - let us celebrate anew!'","'I do not care for this man or the outcome of his bid for the throne. I merely wish to make it through this war with my family intact.\
\
'If he can stop the fighting, so be it.'","Talk to people of Ost Anglebed about the Heirs (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Blood of the King","'I have heard rumours of the might of the one they call the Scourge. It is said he commands a vast army and can outsmart any foe in battle.\
\
'It has been many years since Gondor has had a King upon the throne, and should he return the throne to Pelargir, the people of Lebennin might prosper greatly. This fighting is brutal to be sure, but for this cause, I would throw my lot in with him.'","Thorgant only seems interested in surviving the war","Malthellim's folk can be found throughout Ost Anglebed.\
\
Steward Malthellim has asked you to speak to the people of Ost Anglebed about the various rumours surrounding the Heirs of Castamir.","Nembadir is disgusted by the Heirs and wishes them driven from Gondor","Celairoth is intrigued by the idea of a new King of Gondor","Steward Malthellim's curiosity grows as the rumours of the Heirs of Castamir continue to spread throughout Lebennin.","'Rumours surround these men known as the Heirs of Castamir for his name was once held in great regard in Gondor... at least by some. There was a dark time in our history known as the Kin-strife, when our people fought amongst themselves to determine who was the true claimant to the throne. \
\
'Castamir and his followers forced the opposition from these lands and soon ruled in Pelargir, but he was killed years later. The Kin-strife's ending was a bloody one, ${PLAYER}, and as long as it has been, many of the wounds between brothers have never fully healed.\
\
'I have heard my own folk talk of them, and I grow more curious as to what they believe these Heirs seek in Gondor.'","Doliel is fearful of the Heirs and thinks they shall bring ruin to Gondor","Talk to Nimithil in Ost Anglebed"},
[1802]={"Seal leaks in Járnfast (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Do you hear that, ${CLASS}?\
\
'It is the sound of the River Carnen... spouting into our halls! Ever since those tremors shook Járnfast, we have had leaks. They have appeared all about, and the water is red with rust. I have worked to seal them, but it is too great a task for one dwarf, I think!\
\
'Will you aid me?'","You have sealed many leaks within Járnfast.","You have sealed many leaks and prevented the River Carnen from flooding Járnfast. As a result, the Dwarves of the Ironfold will be able to work unhindered to repair the halls of Járnfast.","Sealed leaks in Járnfast (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Completado","Leaks can be found throughout Járnfast.\
\
Holkur has asked you to aid the Dwarves of the Iron Hills in sealing leaks from the underground source of the River Carnen in Járnfast.","Blood of the Mountain","When the earth shook following Sauron's defeat, great tremors came to the Emyn Engrin and now the River Carnen spills into the halls of Járnfast."},
[1803]={"Beckberry bushes can be found on the islet of Avabárg.\
\
Hoping to ward off illness and regain his youthful strength, Germund has asked you to seek out beckberries on the islet of Avabárg.","Blood of the North-men","Deliver the beckberries to Germund","Native to the western reaches of Wilderland, beckberries are considered a delicacy to the Woodmen.","Germund can be found in Hultvís.\
\
You have gathered several handfuls of beckberries and should now deliver them to Germund.","'Ah, let's see what you have gathered!'\
\
Germund takes the handfuls of beckberries from you and sets them into a small, woven basket. He takes one of the berries and bites into it. A pale, pink juice runs down his chin as he grins.\
\
'These ought to do the trick! I will distill them into a tincture of my own recipe, and I will see that all in need drink of its extract!\
\
'The North-men may have abandoned the vales long ago, but what a great gift they have left for us!'","Collect handfuls of beckberries (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collected handfuls of beckberries (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'All is not well in Hultvís, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'There is talk of Orcs in the hills and disease has come to the woods' edge. You see, the men who labour at Tríubad have come down with some awful cough, and many others of my folk still suffer injuries from the war.\
\
'Although I wish to help them, I cannot do better than offer them fish! And trust me, none with a broken limb or gouged eye clamour for a fish to heal their ills! \
\
'If I had some beckberries, though, I think I could do some real good for them.  I have only known beckberries to grow upon Avabárg for they were tended by the North-men of old. And those who drank of their extract could endure great hardship and even the Plague! Indeed, it is said that beckberries run with the very blood of the North-men. And hale Men they were! \
\
'Such a berry might offer my people a resistance to disease and harden their wills... and their bones, I hope! Will you go to Avabárg and see if you can find any beckberries for my people?'"},
[1805]={"'¿Qué has aprendido? ¿Qué? ¡No! ¡Es imposible!\
\
'No... pero debo aceptar la verdad de lo que me dices. Muirnë siempre fue una niña voluntariosa, egoísta y mimada. Pero aún así, ¡convertirse en guardiana de las arañas de la Corona de Hierro! ¡He desperdiciado un año de mi vida llorando por el destino de un monstruo!\
\
'¡Ay, esta es una amarga bebida para tragar! Pero aunque estas noticias sean oscuras, has hecho lo que te pedí. Tienes mi agradecimiento... Estoy demasiado en deuda contigo, pero intentaré pagarte lo que pueda.'","'Ojalá hubieras podido salvar a mi hermana, ${PLAYER}, pero lamentablemente no pudo ser.'","¡Has matado a Muirnë!","Has enfrentado a la Dama de Seda y has sabido que en realidad era la hermana de Lornë, Muirnë. Has derrotado a la Dama de Seda en combate y ahora debes llevar las malas noticias de vuelta a Lornë.\
\
Lornë se encuentra en Tyrn Lhuig, en Malenhad.","Regresa con Lornë y cuéntale lo que le ha pasado a Muirnë","'¡Ay, pobre Muirnë! Pero es mejor que esté muerta a que siga sirviendo a los malvados hombres de Angmar.'","'Parece que la Dama de Seda tiene la clave del destino de mi hermana, y que se encuentra cerca en un puesto avanzado.\
\
Debo decirte, sin embargo, que el puesto avanzado está fuertemente custodiado, y por lo que he oído de la Dama de Seda, temo que no podrías luchar para encontrarla por tu cuenta. Si vas a emprender la tarea de conocer el destino de mi hermana, deberías traer aliados contigo.\
\
Si decides enfrentarte a ella, toma estos tokens y acércate a su torre. Habiendo matado a varios de sus minions favoritos, no debería rechazar tal desafío de tu parte.'","Desafía a la Dama de Seda","La Dama de Seda está en la fortaleza angmarim de Bail Boglakh, que guarda el camino hacia el este de Angmar, al norte de Malenhad.\
\
Lornë te ha pedido a ti y a tus compañeros que enfrenten a la Dama de Seda en la gran torre de la fortaleza, con la esperanza de encontrar y liberar a su hermana Muirnë.","Lornë cree que la Dama de Seda tiene a su hermana Muirnë cautiva en la torre alta de Bail Boglakh.\
\
Ella te ha pedido que enfrentes a la Dama de Seda con la esperanza de liberarla por fin.","Pacto de sangre"},
[1806]={"Runas manchadas de sangre","Me apena ver Ost Elendil en manos del Enemigo, ${PLAYER}. El gran palacio de los reyes debería estar libre de la corrupción de las fuerzas del mal, ¡no doblegada por las maquinaciones de Angmar y su regente!\
\
Espíritus malvados y sus amos Angmarim acechan ahora en los salones de Ost Elendil bajo las órdenes de Amarthiel. Debemos expulsarlos de allí.\
\
Derrota a los espíritus en el interior del palacio y recupera de sus amos Angmarim las runas manchas de sangre que los controlan. Eso debería debilitar el control de Angmar en el palacio, esa joya de antaño.","Los espíritus malvados y sus amos Angmarim se encuentran en Ost Elendil, más allá del puente de Ariant.\
\
Debes derrotar a los espíritus malvados en el interior de Ost Elendil y recuperar las runas cubiertas de sangre utilizadas por los Angmarim para controlarlos.","Runas manchadas de sangre recuperadas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Recupera las runas manchadas de sangre (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[1807]={"Find a veteran of many battles somewhere in the East Wall who can shed light on the bloodstained tree","If you are able to find a veteran of many battles and combats in war somewhere in the East Wall, he may be able to shed some light on what happened at the Dead Orc Glade.","Blood-stained Tree","A dark stain discolours the bark of a solitary oak at the outskirts of a glade filled with the bodies of dead Orcs. The sight of blood is unmistakeable, but whose blood was it? And where did the wounded warrior go?\
\
Someone who has seen many battles in war might be able to shed some light on what happened here.","You have found a dark stain on the large oak tree in the glade filled with the bodies of dead Orcs.","Wilferth listens as you describe the blood-stained tree at the Dead Orc Glade.\
\
'Interesting,' he says after a moment. \
\
'You say there was no body near the tree? And no trail of blood leading from the base of the oak anywhere nearby? It seems to me that our unknown warrior must have rested at the base of that tree after slaying the Orcs in that glade.\
\
'One thing still puzzles me, ${PLAYER}. Where did our mystery warrior go after his great deed? If he succumbed to his wounds, his body would remain by the tree. Did he survive? Or did he have friends to bear his body away?\
\
'We may never know.'"},
[1808]={"Las bestias de las colinas de Fasach-larran suelen llevar piedras de sangre que encuentran en el suelo. Muchas de estas criaturas tienen su hogar en Nád Nathair, al norte de Aughaire.\
\
Lakhina te ha pedido que derrotes a las bestias de las colinas y recuperes las piedras de sangre opacas que suelen llevar.","'Las bestias de las colinas son criaturas feroces, y has sido muy valiente al cazarlas.'","'Las bestias de las colinas de Fasach-larran suelen llevar piedras de sangre. Búscalas al norte de Aughaire, especialmente entre las grietas de Nád Nathair.'","Reúne piedras de sangre opacas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Puliré las piedras de sangre que trajiste hasta darles un brillo espejado.'","Has reunido piedras de sangre opacas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Lo has hecho muy bien, ${PLAYER}. Le contaré a Crannog sobre tu servicio y puliré estas piedras de sangre opacas hasta darles el brillo que merecen. Luego se usarán en las artesanías de mi pueblo.'","Lakhina está en la isla central de Aughaire, al este del asiento de Crannog.\
\
Has reunido piedras de sangre opacas de las bestias de las colinas en Fasach-larran y ahora debes devolverlas a Lakhina.","Lakhina se ha enterado del desafío que Crannog te ha impuesto y sabe lo que quiere que hagas.","Lleva las piedras de sangre opacas a Lakhina","'Las bestias de las colinas al norte de Aughaire, especialmente entre las grietas de Nád Nathair, llevarán las piedras de sangre opacas que busco.'","'He oído hablar de tu tarea, ${PLAYER}, y sé exactamente cómo puedes demostrar tu valía... ante mí y ante todos nosotros.\
\
'Esta tierra debe ser persuadida para darnos alimento, pero es más generosa con gemas, como las piedras de sangre que usamos en varias artesanías. Pero las piedras brillantes atraen más que a los Trév Gállorg que las buscan; las bestias de las colinas codician las piedras de sangre y a menudo lucharán hasta la muerte para recuperarlas. Una vez que las criaturas han obtenido una piedra de sangre, la gema pierde su brillo. ¡Solo mediante los secretos de los Trév Gállorg puede devolverse el brillo a las piedras!\
\
'Demuestra tu temple y recupera piedras de sangre opacas de las bestias de las colinas al norte de Aughaire. Encontrarás muchas de estas criaturas entre las grietas de Nád Nathair, aunque sus primos errantes también pueden llevar las piedras.'","Piedras de Sangre"},
[1809]={"Achassoth el sanguinario","Derrota a Achassoth","Has derrotado a un líder de las fuerzas del mal en los Campos de Fornost.","Te has topado con Achassoth, una presencia aterradora en los Campos de Fornost...","Achassoth se encuentra en el centro de los Campos de Fornost, al norte del camino que conduce al oeste hacia Evendim.\
\
Debes derrotar a Achassoth, ya que este ser ha arrebatado toda calidez a los Campos de Fornost.","Completado","Sientes un odio cerniéndose sobre ti, y te das cuenta que cerca hay una presencia llena de furia.\
\
Te has topado con Achassoth, un ser terrorífico, en los Campos de Fornost. La sed de sangre de esta entidad fantasmagórica ha crecido al arrebatar la vida a las tierras que la rodean.","Has expulsado a Achassoth","Has derrotado a un líder de las fuerzas del mal en los Campos de Fornost: Achassoth el sanguinario, azote de los Hombres.","'Acércate, cálida criatura. Más cerca.'"},
[1810]={"Derrota a los dragonzuelos en Nad Nathair (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Cuithorn te habló del gran dragonzuelo Ala Sanguinaria y te encomendó la tarea de matarlo.","Dragonzuelos derrotados en Nad Nathair (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Cuinthorn está en el Búth Sánkhas de Aughaire, al sureste del mercado.\
\
Cuinthorn espera escuchar sobre tu éxito contra Ala Sanguinaria y su camada de dragonzuelos.","'Ala Sanguinaria gobierna su camada desde lo alto de los acantilados de Nad Nathair, al norte de Aughaire en Fasach-larran. Sube más allá de las laderas donde habitan las bestias de las colinas, y llegarás al nido del dragonzuelo.'","'Este, el Búth Sánkhas, ha sido testigo de muchas historias, tanto trágicas como triunfantes, pues las canciones de los Trév Gállorg lo registran todo. Muchos de mi gente han perecido mientras ponían a prueba su valentía y buscaban dejar un legado glorioso, y sus historias se transmiten de uno a otro aquí en el Búth Sánkhas.\
\
'Ala Sanguinaria, el más poderoso de los dragonzuelos de Nad Nathair, ha reclamado la vida de muchos de esos buscadores de gloria. Él se posa en lo alto de los grandes acantilados al norte de Aughaire y gobierna su camada de dragonzuelos con afilados dientes y crueles garras.\
\
'La historia será realmente grandiosa si tú y tus aliados pueden vencer a Ala Sanguinaria y su camada. Viaja al norte hacia Nad Nathair y sube más allá de las laderas inferiores donde habitan las bestias de las colinas y busca a Ala Sanguinaria en lo alto de los acantilados. Es una poderosa enemiga, no debe ser desafiada a la ligera. Tu historia será mejor por ello.'","'Luchaste valientemente contra Ala Sanguinaria y serás ${PLAYERNAME:recordado[m]|recordada[f]} por ello durante mucho tiempo.'","'El Búth Sánkhas resonará con canciones sobre tu batalla contra Ala Sanguinaria.'","'¿Ala Sanguinaria ha caído? Entonces, has tenido éxito donde muchos de mi gente han fracasado, ${PLAYER}. Crannog tenía razón al llamarte ${PLAYER:amigo[m]|amiga[f]} de los Trév Gállorg, porque nos has traído mucha ayuda, ¡y esta no es la primera vez!\
\
'Esta recompensa se reservó para quien derrotara a Ala Sanguinaria, aunque pocos creían que podría suceder. Ahora te la doy a ti.'","Ala Sanguinaria gobierna su camada de dragonzuelos desde la cima de los acantilados de Nad Nathair, por encima de las laderas inferiores donde habitan las bestias de las colinas. Nad Nathair se encuentra al norte de Aughaire, en Fasach-larran.\
\
Cuinthorn te habló de Ala Sanguinaria, un poderoso dragonzuelo que ha reclamado la vida de muchos grandes héroes, y se preguntó si tú y tus aliados serían los que pondrían fin a su reinado.","Ala Sanguinaria"},
[1811]={"Defeated Dievlig in the Bonevales (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Bloody Nose","The Dievlig patrol can be found upon the hill north of Echad Naeglanc.\
\
Naeglanc has asked you to defeat the remnant of the patrol which attacked him and his allies and bring him their sigils.","After their rescue, Naeglanc and his allies returned to their encampment.","'Have you dealt with the Dievlig patrols yet?'","Collect sigils (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collected sigils (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Thank you for coming to our rescue, ${PLAYER}. Several of the local Dunlendings have played an important role in bringing members of the Grey Company through the Bonevales. These fine people have risked their lives to help us, and we must do the same in kind.\
\
'I would have you seek out the Dievlig and lay them low, both to avenge the folk who have fought at our side and to secure our passage through the Bonevales.\
\
'Travel north and up the hill... there you will find the remnant of the patrol that attacked us. Bring me their sigils as evidence that the deed is done.'","'With the patrol scattered, we should be able to learn what is happening here in the Bonevales.'","Talk to Naeglanc at Echad Naeglanc in the Bonevales","Naeglanc is at Echad Naeglanc, south of the hill where you fought the Dievlig patrol.\
\
You should bring the sigils you collected to Naeglanc with news of your victory.","Defeat Dievlig in the Bonevales (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[1813]={"Canaddal está apostado al inicio del sendero que conduce al Páramo Alto, muy por encima de las Ciénagas Floridas.\
\
Debes llevar la flor que recolectaste a Canaddal de inmediato.","Una flor rara crece en un lugar a lo largo del Bruinen llamado las Ciénagas Floridas, un sitio donde habitan Acechadores de Pantano. La flor es muy hermosa y se dice que posee maravillosas propiedades curativas.","'En verdad, esta flor es una maravilla a la vista. Gracias, ${PLAYER}. Estoy seguro de que nuestras visitas apreciarán tus esfuerzos.'","Flor de las Ciénagas","La flor rara crece en las Ciénagas Floridas, a lo largo del Bruinen.\
\
Canaddal te ha pedido que recolectes una flor rara para preparar medicinas para los visitantes.","Recolecta la flor rara","'Las pieles y la carne son necesarias para nuestros visitantes, pero sería negligente enviarlos sin medicinas. A lo largo del Bruinen hay un lugar llamado las Ciénagas Floridas. Allí crece una flor rara de la que se dice que posee maravillosas propiedades curativas. No es athelas, claro está, pero serviría mejor que la mayoría de las hierbas.\
\
'¿Viajarías a las ciénagas y me traerías esa flor? Ten cuidado, porque acechadores de pantano habitan allí, y se han vuelto salvajes en estos últimos días.'","'¿Encontraste la flor?'","Entrega la flor rara a Canaddal","Has recolectado la flor rara"},
[1814]={"'Bueno, no estoy muy seguro de qué podemos hacer con esto. Quizá pueda ser usado como recipiente para recoger la ceniza cuando se fuma. Una cosa útil, aunque no sea el más glamuroso de los objetos.'","'Bien, adelante, ¡usa la forja e inténtalo! ¡Ese vidrio no se va a soplar solo!'","'Mis ayudantes me dicen que todos los suministros han sido reunidos, y que podemos de nuevo fabricar vidrio. Te doy las gracias por tu ayuda.\
\
'Soplar vidrio es un art, una de las que puede ser aprendida rápidamente, pero debe ser refinada con los años de prueba y error. Puedo enseñarte lo básico, si quieres.\
\
'Ve a la forja y, usando esta vara, intenta trabajar con el vidrio. Deberías ver que empieza a tomar forma.'","La forja de vidrio está junto a Mundarico Hojarena en Dwaling.\
\
Mundarico Hojarena te ha pedido que uses la forja para soplar algo de vidrio.","Usa la forja de vidrio (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Habla con Mundarico Hojarena en Dwaling","Mundarico Hojarena está en Dwaling.\
\
Mundarico Hojarena estará interesado en escuchar cómo ha ido tu primera experiencia soplando vidrio.","Forja de vidrio usada (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Una vez todos los materiales han sido reunidos, el vidrio debe ser forjado en el fuego y soplado para darle forma.","Soplador de vidrio"},
[1818]={"create entity/npc/mn_boar/mn_boar_brandyhills_brokentusk.wc and kill it","Matar jabalí","Prueba de matar jabalí","¡Ve a ver a ${NOS} para terminar esta misión!","Ve y mata un jabalí","Ve a ver a ${NOS}","Has terminado"},
[1819]={"Daga de Colmillo de Jabalí","Tu encuentro con un jabalí feroz no muy lejos del Gran Camino del Este te permitió obtener un colmillo de sorprendente fuerza y belleza.","Un armero en Rivendel podría ser capaz de forjar el colmillo de jabalí que obtuviste en un arma mortal.\
\
Es posible que Rivendel albergue a un armero capaz de trabajar con el colmillo de jabalí que encontraste.","No ves ningún defecto en el colmillo. Un colmillo como este podría valer buen dinero entre los Hombres o despertar la admiración de los Enanos, pero en manos de un armero élfico podría convertirse en un arma letal. Un armero de suficiente habilidad podría vivir en Rivendel.","'¿Has venido a ver mis mercancías?'","'He vivido muchos años y he visto pasar muchos dones de las criaturas del bosque a los Elfos de Imladris, pero nunca he visto un colmillo de jabalí de tanta belleza.\
\
'Sería un honor para mí forjarlo en una daga para ti, ${RACE}. Será un digno recuerdo de su poderoso antiguo dueño.'","Lleva el colmillo perfecto de jabalí a un armero élfico en Rivendel"},
[1820]={"'Bien. Con menos jabalíes merodeando, habrá más oportunidad de alimentar a los animales que pronto trasladaremos al sitio de trabajo.'","'Encontrarás jabalíes por todos los campos del norte de Bree. Puede que haya algunos al oeste de aquí también.'","'Los demás están preocupados por los carnívoros que acechan estas tierras, pero yo me preocupo por los jabalíes. Sin duda son capaces de comer carne, pero lo que me preocupa son sus hábitos para hacer camas.\
\
'El número de jabalíes en estas tierras es suficiente para arrasar los campos circundantes y destruir el suministro de alimento que necesitamos para los animales.\
\
'Por esta razón te pediría que caces a los jabalíes. ¿Me ayudarás?'","Ham Cardogris espera tu regreso en la Obra de los Espinar.\
\
Debes regresar con Ham Cardogris e informarle de tu éxito.","Jabalíes derrotados en los campos del norte de Bree (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Derrota a jabalíes en los campos del norte de Bree (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Los jabalíes pueden encontrarse por todos los campos del norte de Bree.\
\
Ham Cardogris te pidió que cazaras jabalíes para él.","Los jabalíes están por todas partes en Bree, pero no siempre son bienvenidos. Ham Cardogris no aprecia la cantidad de jabalíes que pisan los campos cercanos y quiere reducir su número, para que no destruyan algunas de las fuentes de alimento para los animales destinados a la Obra de los Espinar.","Jabalíes haciendo camas","Regresa con Ham Cardogris en la Obra de los Espinar"},
[1821]={"Hunt perturbed wild boars in the Farrowfold (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You have done as Branach asked. Return to him.\
\
Branach can be found at his farm, Cornworth, north-east of Farrowfold.","Carne recogida (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","A family of farmers has been dealing with boars encroaching on their land.","Boars by the Hathollant","You have been tasked to hunt boars for food.\
\
The boars in question may be found at the Farrowfold, south-west of Cornworth.","Talk to Branach","'This will keep us fed through the harvest. Thank you.'","'Sausages, roasts, grilled chops, braises, butter-basted herbed tenderloin, these are the things I would be eating right now if someone were to harvest some boars from where they've made their dens to the south-west. Watch out for the aggressive ones, however! They are usually covered in flies, and not fit to eat. Their perturbed cousins should be perfect for this, and plenty edible.'\
\
He smiles at you and gestures his head in the direction he just indicated.\
\
'I would pay such an adventurous person with coin.'\
\
He winks.\
\
Perhaps you should go hunt some boars."},
[1822]={"'Tu habilidad en combate no puede negarse, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'La diferencia entre un buen campeón y un gran campeón es su renombre. Los pueblos de la Tierra Media necesitan saber que hay guerreros capaces de increíbles proezas marciales, arriesgando sus vidas para luchar contra el enemigo.\
\
'Para tu segunda tarea, quiero que viajes a la Mansión de Thorin. Asciende los escalones hacia el trono de Dwalin y proclama tus proezas como ${PLAYER:campeón[m]|campeona[f]} ante todos los reunidos en los salones de los enanos.'","Habla con Thrymur en la Mansión de Thorin","Presumir","'¡Bien hecho, bien hecho!\
\
'Ahora, ${PLAYER}, pasemos a tu siguiente tarea.'","Proclama tu destreza en la Mansión de Thorin","Valthor se encuentra en el Refugio Sombrío en Khazad-dûm, muy al este de la Mansión de Thorin.\
\
Thrymur te pidió que regreses con Valthor en Moria y le repitas lo que le dijiste.","'Bien dicho, . Tus orgullosas palabras te muestran como ${PLAYERNAME:un gran guerrero[m]|una gran guerrera[f]} ante mis ojos.\
\
'Regresa con Valthor en Khazad-dûm y dile lo que has dicho aquí hoy. Incluso él quedará impresionado.'","Eso está muy bien, ${PLAYER}; pero aún tienes mucho que aprender sobre cómo contar una historia.\
\
'Tus hazañas son impresionantes, pero intenta impresionarme con tus palabras, si puedes.","Habla con Valthor en el Refugio Sombrío de Moria","Thrymur está cerca del trono de Dwalin en la Mansión de Thorin.\
\
Thrymur no quedó impresionado contigo. Deberías hablar con él nuevamente y proclamarle tus grandes hazañas.","Valthor considera que el orgullo en las propias habilidades es fundamental para un Campeón.","El trono de Dwalin se encuentra en la Mansión de Thorin, muy al oeste de Moria.\
\
Valthor te ha encargado que vayas y presumas de tus grandes hazañas ante el trono de Dwalin."},
[1824]={"Encuentra a Caléndula Boffin en las ruinas de Bâr Faroth","Esmeralda Boffin está en Quiebra Larga, bailando.","'¿Estás aquí para unirte a la competición de baile, ${PLAYER}? ¡Cuando llegué, descubrí para mi consternación que no había nada en marcha! ¡Ni un zapateo, ni un floreo de brazos, ni un giro o una pirueta! Así que empecé por mi cuenta.\
\
'Volveré a Nobotella, claro. Pero no hasta que particpes en el baile, ${PLAYER}!'","¿Cuánto tiempo debes <rgb=#00FF00>bailar</rgb>?","'Fui a buscar botes élficos, ${PLAYER}... ¡pero encontré un bote hobbit! Parece que los hobbits de Allende no tienen tanto miedo de los botes como la gente de mi hogar. Es... ¿es esta mi gente?\
\
'Me topé con mi hermana Caléndula un poco más atrás, pero no vino hacia aquí conmigo. Me dijo que iba a investigar las ruinas al norte de aquí. Eso es muy típico de nuestra Caléndula, por si no lo sabías. Siempre anda buscando aventuras. ¡Si encuentras trasgos lo más probable es que encuentres a mi hermana!\
\
'Tengo algunas preguntas más para este buen señor sobre su bote, pero una vez que me las resuelva volveré para la fiesta de Angélica. ¡No te preocupes! No tardaré.'","'¡Sigue bailando, ${PLAYER}! ¡A ver esos movimientos!'","'¡Saludos!'","Fosco Boffin está junto al río, maravillado con un bote hobbit que se mece en el agua","Habla con Berilac y los","Boffins sueltos","¡Victoria!","'¿Has venido para probar algo de comida de la Granja de Cotonorte? El conductor de la carreta muy amablemente me ha dejado probar algunas verduras, ¡y me complace anunciar que están perfectamente frescas y son de la mejor calidad! Y bueno, entonces tuve que probar este pan recién horneado, y hay una cesta de manzanas esperando para ser pboadas...\
\
'¿Supongo que la fiesta de Angélica está a punto de empezar? Entonces volveré a Nobotella, y quizás cuando llegue termine de llenar los rincones de mi barriga. ¡Seguro que para entonces mi hermana ya habrá servido los apertivos!'","'No tenemos elección, ${PLAYER}: tenemos que buscar al resto de mis hermanos y hacer que vuelvan antes de que mi madre pierda la paciencia. ¡Créeme! Está un poco contrariada ahora mismo, ¡pero será mucho peor si no nos damos prisa!\
\
'Deberías hablar primero con mi primo Bingo. Resulta que es algo parecido a un aventurero, y podría haber visto dónde ha ido todo el mundo. Creo que se fue de vuelta a Campotieso.'","'Deberías hablar primero con mi primo Bingo. Resulta que es algo parecido a un aventurero, y podría haber visto dónde ha ido todo el mundo. Creo que se fue de vuelta a Campotieso.'","Bingo está en Campotieso, y Dinodas cree que podría haber visto dónde han ido los otros hijos Boffin.","Habla con Bingo Boffin en Lhúngobel","Fosco Boffin fue aparentemente a buscar botes élficos en los ríos del oeste de la Comarca Allende.","Bingo Boffin te ha seguido a Lhúngobel.","Encuentra a Griffo Boffin","Fosco Boffin ha encontrado un bote hobbit en uno de los ríos de la Comarca Allende.","'¡Hola, hola, ${PLAYER}! ¿Estás buscando a los hijos de la prima Prisca? Bueno, ¡he visto a uno! El joven Fosco me dijo que la fiesta fue retrasada y tenía la intención de avistar un bote élfico o dos en la orilla oeste. Hacia allí es donde te interesa buscar.\
\
Te alcanzaré cuando haya terminado de comprar. Verás, estoy buscando algo de cuerda. ¡Nunca se tiene demasiada cuerda cuando vas de aventuras! ¡Te veo luego, amigo!'","Habla con Griffo Boffin","Por supuesto, has encontrado a Esmeralda Boffin en pleno baile","'Lo conseguiste: has encontrado a todos mis hermanos y hermanas! Muckhas gracias, ${PLAYER}.","Berilac soñó con un delicioso olor llegando desde la Granja de Cotonorte, al este: justo el olor que atrae la atención de su hambriento hermano Griffo.","'¡Buenas, ${PLAYER}! Mi hermano Berilac está durmiendo plácidamente... ¡pero no sabe que hay trasgos cerca! Será mejor que le protejamos.'","'Me topé con mi hermana Caléndula un poco más atrás, pero no vino hacia aquí conmigo. Me dijo que iba a investigar las ruinas al norte de aquí. Eso es muy típico de nuestra Caléndula, por si no lo sabías. Siempre anda buscando aventuras. ¡Si encuentras trasgos lo más probable es que encuentres a mi hermana!\
\
'Tengo algunas preguntas más para este buen señor sobre su bote, pero una vez que me las resuelva volveré para la fiesta de Angélica. ¡No te preocupes! No tardaré.'","'¡Mira eso!'","'El joven Fosco me dijo que la fiesta fue retrasada y tenía la intención de avistar un bote élfico o dos en la orilla oeste. Hacia allí es donde te interesa buscar.\
\
Te alcanzaré cuando haya terminado de comprar. Verás, estoy buscando algo de cuerda. ¡Nunca se tiene demasiada cuerda cuando vas de aventuras! ¡Te veo luego!'","Caléndula Boffin se ha adelantado a los Campos Viejos para detener las fechorías de los trasgos.","Griffo Boffin está cerca de un carro que trae comida de la granja de Cotonorte","Esmeralda ha visto a Caléndula yendo en dirección norte hacia Bâr Faroth","Habla con Esmeralda en Quiebra Larga","'¡Muy buenas!'","¡Felicidades! ¡Has localizado a todos los hijos Boffin!","'¡Buen trabajo, ${PLAYER}! ¡Estoy impresionada!\
\
'De todas formas, ¿estás buscando a Caléndula? Vino por aquí y le pregunté si quería participar en mi concurso de baile, pero me dijo que no. Parece ser que estaba persiguiendo a un grupo de trasgos, aunque siendo mi hermana a veces es difícil decir si lo que dice es verdad o está imaginando alguna loca aventura. De cualquier manera, fue corriendo hacia el norte, así que puedes buscarla en esa dirección.\
\
'Yo volveré a Nobotella en breve. ¡Deja que dé unos cuantos pasos de baile más!'","Bingo ha llegado, con una expresión de preocupación","Fosco te ha dicho que Caléndula fue hacia el norte en dirección a Lhúngobel, buscando enemigos que vencer.","Oyes que alguien te llama, pero no es Caléndula","Habla con Dinodas fuera del nº 8 de la calle Aguamiel","Busca a Caléndula y derrota trasgos en Lhúngobel (${CURRENT}/6)","Habla con Fosco Boffin en la orilla del río","'Eso pinta mal, ${PLAYER}. ¡Será mejor que nos apresuremos hacia el sureste! ¡Caléndula podría encontrar problemas en Campoviejo!'","Habla con Bingo Boffin en Campotieso","'Volveré a Nobotella.'","Esmeralda no volverá a Nobotella hasta que participes en su competición de baile. ¡Será mejor que <rgb=#00FF00>bailes</rgb>!","Griffo Boffin está aquí, palmeándose la barriga con satisfacción","Nárnaz el Castigador ha encontrado a un aventurero hobbit mortífero en Bâr Faroth, para su desgracia.","Bingo Boffin ha llegado a Bâr Faroth.","Interpreta otro <rgb=#00FF00>baile</rgb> o el mismo... ¡con sentimiento!","'¡Nunca me atraparás vivo!'","Bingo ha oído rumores de una competición de baile en Quiebra Larga, y piensa que podría ser el lugar donde encontrar a Esmeralda.","Dinodas Boffin ha arruinado la fiesta de inauguración de la casa de su hermana Angélica (con tu ayuda). Ahora, su madre Prisca te ha pedido que le ayudes a enmendar las cosas.","Habla con Esmeralda Boffin en Quiebra Larga","'¡No sabía que esta gente de la Comarca luchara tan fieramente! ¡Malditos sean!'\
\
Nárnaz el Castigador tose, y la sangre forma un charco bajo su armadura desgarrada.\
\
Dará igual a la larga: el resto de mis muchachos ya ha ido hacia el sureste, ¡y dictarán las reglas de un NUEVO deporte! Van a hacer pagar a esos hobbits la invención del apaleo de Golfimbul, ¡espera y verás! Este nuevo deporte usará los mismos garrotes y podrá ser jugado en los mismo campos... pero las cabezas que rodarán no serán de trasgo! ¡Ja, ja, ja!'","Interpreta un <rgb=#00FF00>baile</rgb> a tu elección","Ahora que has encontrado a todos sus hermanos y hermanas, debes volver con Dinodas en el exterior del nº 8 de la calle Aguamiel, en Nobotella.","Encuentra a Fosco Boffin","Esmeralda parece complacida con tu interpretación","'Ahora que estoy descansado, iré a ver si la fiesta de Angélica está lista para empezar. ¿Estás buscando a Griffo? Quizá debería seguir ese olor a comida deliciosa... ¡seguro que él lo haría si su olfato detectara algo semejante!'","Un trasgo herido se debate en el suelo: ¿es obra de Caléndula?","Encuentra a Esmeralda en la competición de baile en Quiebra Larga","Berilac bosteza y se despereza somnoliento.\
\
'Ah, hola, ${PLAYER}. Acabo de tener el sueño más encantador y apacible del mundo. Había un olor delicioso que llegaba a la Comarca Allende desde el este. De hecho, ¡creo que todavía lo puedo olerlo! Qué sueño tan real, ¡que ha dejado su huella de esta manera!\
\
'Ahora que estoy descansado, iré a ver si la fiesta de Angélica está lista para empezar. ¿Estás buscando a Griffo? Quizá debería seguir ese olor a comida deliciosa... ¡seguro que él lo haría si su olfato detectara algo semejante!'","Berilac ha dormido durante todo el alboroto en Campoviejo.","Trasgos derrotados en Lhúngobel (${CURRENT}/6)","Busca a Caléndula y derrota trasgos en Lhúngobel (5/6)","'Volveré a Nobotella, claro. Pero no hasta que particpes en el baile, ${PLAYER}!'","Habla con Nárnaz el Castigador cerca de Bâr Faroth","No hay nada que hacer: ¡tienes que <rgb=#00FF00>bailar</rgb>!","Esmeralda Boffin está bailando en Quiebra Larga.","Encuentra a Caléndula Boffin en Campoviejo y pon fin a las fechorías de los trasgos","'Creo que podría haber encontrado una pista sobre el paradero de otro de los hijos Boffin, ${PLAYER}. Aparentemente se está celebrando una competición de baile en Quiebra Larga. Si eso no suena como música para los oídos de Esmeralda, ¡no sé qué otra cosa podría ser!\
\
'¡A Quiebra Larga, camarada ${RACE}!'","'¿Todavía sin señales de Caléndula? Seguro que está bien: ¡de tal palo tal astilla, como se suele decir! De todos mis primos segundos es la que parece más capaz de cuidar de sí misma. Prisca diría que he sido una mala influencia, ¡pero yo digo que es el mejor tipo de influencia!\
\
'Creo que podría haber encontrado una pista sobre el paradero de otro de los hijos Boffin, ${PLAYER}. Aparentemente se está celebrando una competición de baile en Quiebra Larga. Si eso no suena como música para los oídos de Esmeralda, ¡no sé qué otra cosa podría ser!\
\
'¡A Quiebra Larga, camarada ${RACE}!'","Habla con Bingo Boffin en Bâr Faroth"},
[1826]={"'Esta próxima tarea no podrás lograrla solo, ni siquiera con una comunidad de tus aliados más cercanos. No, deberás reunir una partida de guerra si quieres derrotar a Bogbereth.\
\
'No es una criatura ordinaria, Bogbereth, la Reina del Veneno de Himbar. Debes atacar rápido y con precisión, pues su piel es como una armadura de acero y sus colmillos son dagas afiladas que gotean veneno.\
\
'Reúne a tu grupo de héroes y regresa a Torech-i-Bogbereth. La encontrarás allí, a menos que ella te encuentre primero.'","Lunathron te habló de una gran y vil araña, Bogbereth, que caza en Himbar.","'¿Ya has reunido tu grupo de guerra? Bogbereth no caerá sin luchar, y a pesar de tu valentía, no eres una amenaza para ella por ti ${PLAYERNAME:solo[m]|sola[f]}.'","Bogbereth","'¿La gran bestia ha caído? Entonces su reinado venenoso ha terminado. Esto ha sido otro golpe para la Corona de Hierro y las fuerzas de Angmar, y todo te lo debemos a ti y a tus aliados.'","Gath Forthnír está en la parte oriental de Himbar, al sur y al este de Torech-i-Bogbereth.\
\
Lunathron te pidió destruir a la gran araña, Bogbereth. Ahora que ya no existe, puedes regresar para reclamar tu victoria.","Bogbereth caza en el extremo noreste de Himbar, al oeste y luego al norte de Gath Forthnír.\
\
Lunathron te advirtió que no enfrentes a Bogbereth con menos que una partida de guerra completamente armada. Debe ser derrotada, o seguirá engendrando su vil prole."},
[1827]={"Derrota a las crías de Bogbereth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Bien hecho, ${CLASS}, pero aún queda una amenaza. Hablo de la gran araña, Bogbereth.'","Las arañas están al noreste de Himbar.\
\
Lunathron te habló de la progenie de Bogbereth, las crías de araña que son custodiadas por los Angmarim.","'¡Bien hecho! Has dado el primer paso para librarnos de Bogbereth para siempre!'","Prole de Bogbereth","Lunathron está en Gath Forthnír, al este de Himbar.\
\
Mataste a muchas arañas y a sus guardianes Angmarim, asegurando que la progenie de Bogbereth no suponga una amenaza para los Montaraces. Ahora deberías regresar con Lunathron.","'Las arañas son una amenaza y deben être detenidas. Derrótalas a ellas y a sus guardianes mayores.'","'Hay una gran araña que acecha en Himbar. Sus huevos son codiciados por la Corona de Hierro, ya que las crías pueden ser entrenadas por los Angmarim para luchar por el Enemigo.\
\
'Debes matar a las arañas y a sus protectores mayores al noreste de Himbar, en Torech-i-Bogbereth. Cuando enfrentes a las crías, ten cuidado. Pueden excavar en la tierra y escapar de tus ataques.\
\
'Debes tener precaución al cazar las arañas. Bogbereth merodea esas tierras, y puede que también te esté cazando a ti.'","Derrota a matronas, acechadoras y furtivas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Bogbereth la Araña está aliada con la Corona de Hierro. Su progenie es custodiada por los Angmarim y utilizada como soldados de muchas patas."},
[1828]={"'Busca a los exploradores de Bogrian y aprende lo que puedas de ellos. Los merrevail anidan justo al norte de nuestro campamento.'","'¿Su reina quiere huir a las Salas de los Espejos en Zirakzigil? ¡Por la barba de Durin!'","'Hemos hecho todo lo posible para vigilar esta caverna y hemos aprendido más sobre Bogrian y sus doncellas.\
\
'Hadi escuchó a algunos de los merrevail hablar, y algunas frases clave despertaron mi interés. ¿Hablarás con él y descubrirás lo que sabe?'","Folkath se encuentra en el campamento al borde oeste de la Fosa Colmilluda.\
\
Debes regresar con Folkath para contarle las noticias de tu éxito.","Habla con Folkath en su campamento en la Fosa Colmilluda","La reina morroval, Bogrian, se ha escondido. Folkath y los demás han comenzado a investigar dónde podría aparecer a continuación.","La curiosidad de Bogrian","Hadi reside en el campamento con Folkath, en el borde oeste de la Fosa Colmilluda.\
\
Folkath recomienda que le preguntes a Hadi lo que ha aprendido sobre el clan de Bogrian.","'Es cierto que escuché a algunos miembros de la tribu de Bogrian hablar de su paradero, pero antes de que pudiera aprender su ubicación me descubrieron y tuve que huir. No tengo el valor de volver allí. Tendrás que espiar a algunos de sus exploradores tú mismo para descubrir lo que realmente está pasando.\
\
'Sal del campamento hacia el norte, luego gira hacia el este y sigue la cara del acantilado. Los exploradores tienen un lugar de reunión justo al sur de la entrada de Tith-maudhul. Una vez que hayas escuchado un poco de su conversación, derrota a los exploradores: ¡cuantos menos tenga su reina, mejor para nosotros!'","Busca a los exploradores en su lugar de encuentro habitual, al sur de la entrada de Tith-maudhul, e intenta escuchar su conversación antes de derrotarlos.","Espía a los exploradores y derrota a dos de ellos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Habla con Hadi para descubrir lo que sabe","Hadi te ha hablado de un lugar desde el que podrías espiar a los exploradores de Bogrian"},
[1830]={"'¡Oh, maravilloso, los encontraste! ¡Gracias!\
\
'Aunque... si no te importa, quisiera pedirte otra cosa...'","Reforzar las Defensas","Recoge la caja de sierras","Lleva los materiales recogidos a ${NOS}","Recoge el barril de clavos","Recoge la caja de martillos","Los suministros robados se encuentran en los campamentos orcos al noreste.\
\
Elsie te dijo que los granjeros de los alrededores debían traerle un barril de clavos, una caja de martillos y una caja de sierras, pero sus granjas fueron invadidas y sus bienes robados. Te ha pedido que vayas a los campamentos orcos al norte, a lo largo del Camino Verde, y recuperes los suministros que los orcos esparcieron.","Elsie Bosquerudo recibió el encargo de conseguir los suministros necesarios para mantener las barricadas de Puente de Caballetes, pero ahora tiene dificultades para encontrar lo que necesita.","Has recogido el barril de clavos","Has recogido la caja de sierras","'¡Tú, necesito tu ayuda! Nuestro pobre pueblo está bajo la amenaza de otro ataque de esos orcos inmundos. Todos estamos haciendo nuestra parte para que Puente de Caballetes sobreviva, y a mí me han encomendado conseguir los suministros para mantener las barricadas.\
\
'El problema es que los granjeros de los alrededores debían traerme parte de los suministros, pero sus granjas fueron invadidas por los orcos. Apenas escaparon con vida y los orcos desparramaron sus cosas por todas partes. Pediría suministros desde el sur, pero los orcos bloquean también esa ruta. ¡Necesitamos recuperar esos objetos robados!\
\
'Las tres cosas que necesitamos son: el barril de clavos que llevaban, una caja de martillos y una caja de sierras. Los orcos deberían tenerlos en sus campamentos al noreste.'","'Necesito esos suministros si quiero mantener las barricadas en pie.\
\
'Deberías encontrar el barril de clavos, la caja de sierras y la caja de martillos en los campamentos orcos al norte de Puente de Caballetes, cerca del Camino Verde.'","Has recogido la caja de martillos"},
[1835]={"¡Se te ha acabado el tiempo!","Múli se encuentra en Othrikar, en las Quebradas del Norte.\
\
Deberías entregarle la Cerveza Aliento de Dragón a Múli en lugar de su querida Cerveza Barbuda de Bombur.","Barmy Nudoraíz se encuentra en El Dragón Verde, en Delagua.\
\
Deberías hablar con Barmy Nudoraíz y recoger algo de Cerveza Aliento de Dragón, que será entregada al pobre Múli en lugar de su querida Cerveza Barbuda de Bombur.","'He recibido un tipo distinto de órdenes de Jónar, el jefe de esta asociación. Odia tanto a la Liga de las Posadas que me ha asignado una tarea muy diferente de la de mi vecino de la Liga. ¡Chist, que no nos oiga!\
\
'Múli, que está en Othrikar, parece encontrarse lejos de casa sin su cerveza favorita. No tengo nada en contra de Múli: al menos es un enano sensato y anhela una cerveza enana. ¡Pero debería estar en la Asociación Cervecera, no en la Liga de las Posadas!\
\
'Así que le daremos una patética cerveza hobbit en lugar de una deliciosa lager enana. Dile que es de parte de Jónar y que Jónar bloqueará todo el suministro de Cerveza Barbuda de Bombur hasta que Múli entre en razón y se una a la sociedad correcta: la Asociación Cervecera.'","'¡La Cerveza Aliento de Dragón es una excelente elección! La mejor cerveza de toda la Comarca, si me permites decirlo, y bien que lo digo. ¿Seguro que no quieres pedir una segunda pinta por adelantado? Te garantizo que pedirás más en cuanto bebas la última gota.'","Lleva la falsa Cerveza Barbuda de Bombur a Múli","'¿Qué dice Jónar que me envía ahora? ¿Cerveza Aliento de Dragón? ¿Y no me enviará mi querida Cerveza Barbuda de Bombur hasta que abandone la Liga de las Posadasy me una a la Asociación Cervecera?\
\
'Eso es terriblemente cruel, verdaderamente cruel. Llevo ya más de dos años labrándome una reputación dentro de la Liga de las Posadas, ¡y eso avanza muy despacio, déjame decirte! Pero haría cualquier cosa por una Cerveza Barbuda de Bombur...\
\
'Dile a Jónar que lo pensaré, pero esto no me agrada en absoluto.","Se te ha encomendado entregar cosas desagradables a miembros necesitados de ayuda de la Liga de las Posadas, algo que solo haría la peor de las ${CLASS}.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Esta misión se eliminará de tu registro de misiones cuando finalice el festival actual.</rgb>","Recoge la falsa Cerveza Barbuda de Bombur en El Dragón Verde","'¡Asegúrate de decirle a Múli que se está juntando con la gente equivocada!'","Has recogido la falsa Cerveza Barbuda de Bombur","El Aliento de Bombur"},
[1836]={"Thromur can be found at Durin's Stone.\
\
You have aided in the defeat of Urro One-hand and routed Bolg and the other Orcs at Durin's Stone. You should talk to Thromur.","Thromur can be found at Amdân.\
\
Thromur, esquire of Frerin, has asked you to accompany him to confront Shálun. You should talk to Thromur.","Talk to Thromur at Durin's Stone","'I misjudged him... Shálun, I mean. My master is lost, but the King and Thorin live because of his sacrifice.'\
\
Thromur lets out a sorrowful sigh.\
\
'The Iron-folk have come at last... I only hope it is not too late!'","Bonds of Oak and Iron","'Let us confront this thief!'","'Shálun? I know him well indeed. This would not be the first time he has disrespected Frerin, but even I did not think he would stoop so low!\
\
'Let us see what excuse he makes for this insult... this theft!\
\
'Will you come with me, Hermáth? If you would bring your hammer, I would feel more at ease... though I should hope you need not use it!'","After King Thráin and his vanguard set out to assault the gates of Khazad-dûm, a sudden revelation threatens to raise tensions between the Longbeards and the Zhélruka at Amdân.","Talk to Thromur"},
[1837]={"'¿Oyes esto, hermano?\
¿Oyes la absolución?\
Descansa ahora, hermano, \
descansa como éramos\
como seremos.'","'¿Hombre Hueso? ¿Quebradas de los Túmulos? No sé nada de esas cosas, ¡ni me importa! Pero quiero deshacerme de esa maldita sombra de la callejón.\
\
'Habla con Tobold Cortahoja. Es un erudito en esas cosas oscuras y misteriosas. Se fue a pasear por las Quebradas de los Túmulos.'","'¡Ah, el Hombre Hueso! Sí, de hecho, he oído historias sobre esta terrible criatura, aunque no sé si son leyenda o verdad.\
\
'He oído que a veces acecha en la noche en las alturas de Ost Gorthad, una fortaleza en ruinas en la esquina sureste de las Quebradas de los Túmulos. Si esto es cierto, sin embargo, temería aventurarme en ese lugar, ya que se dice que el Hombre Hueso es un mal terrible.'","La sombra vaga por el norte de las Quebradas de los Túmulos.\
\
Debes regresar con la sombra e informarle que el Hombre Hueso ha sido derrotado y las sombras liberadas.","'¿Cómo lograste expulsar al espíritu, ${PLAYER}?'","'¡Oíd, oíd! ${PLAYER} ha expulsado a los fantasmas malvados de nuestros callejones!'","'Un Hombre de Hueso,\
desde debajo de la piedra de Cardolan.\
Búscalo ahora para levantar esta maldición,\
antes de que nosotros, los Hermanos, vaguemos para siempre.'","Hombre Hueso","La sombra no sabe exactamente dónde se encuentra el Hombre Hueso, salvo que está en algún lugar del sur de las Quebradas de los Túmulos.\
\
La sombra habló de los huesos de un hombre de Cardolan que ha vuelto a la vida y del juramento que él y su hermano hicieron.","Habla con la Sombra Errante","Una sombra que se encontró vagando por las Quebradas de los Túmulos --que no parece tener malas intenciones-- sintió el llamado de su hermano y lucha por apaciguar la fuerza que ha regresado para despertarlos.","Derrota al Hombre Hueso","'Al sur se levantó\
de una tumba de tierra.\
Antes carne y entero\
ahora huesos, depravado,\
por espíritus buscando un hogar.\
\
'Un hombre de hueso \
dormía bajo la piedra de Cardolan.\
Levantándose una vez, abatido,\
prometiendo a sus hermanos\
ahora separados en dos.\
\
'Hermanos, malditos,\
vuelvan otra vez \
para enfrentarse a este enemigo\
de quien robaron.\
Por actos muy nobles\
en intención.\
\
'Mientras el mal camina\
también lo haremos nosotros.\
\
'Búscalo,\\más allá de la frontera\
al sur hacia la piedra\
el país de Cardolan\
sus huesos aún vagan allí.'"},
[1838]={"'¡Bienvenido a Acebeda, ${PLAYER}! Hemos venido aquí con Bósi y Brogur, nuestros señores, para recuperar las Minas de Moria, que perdimos hace muchos años. Si deseas ayudarnos en esta empresa, te lo agradeceremos mientras las montañas se mantengan sobre las salas de nuestros padres.\
\
'Pero debes saber esto: Khazad-dûm fue tomada por los enanos hace mucho tiempo mediante violencia y matanza, y ha permanecido desierta de nuestra raza durante muchos años. Balin lideró una expedición anterior para recuperar la gran ciudad, pero no hemos tenido noticias de él durante muchos años.\
\
'No sabemos lo que podemos encontrar dentro de las Minas de Moria.'","Tulk se encuentra al este de la puerta en ruinas, cerca de los muros de Moria, al sureste de Eregion.\
\
Ráthwald os ha dicho que una expedición de enanos ha llegado a Acebeda para buscar a Balin en las salas de Khazad-dûm. Os ha dicho que ofrecierais vuestra ayuda a Tulk justo más allá de la puerta en ruinas donde él hace guardia.","'¿Qué os trae por aquí, ${PLAYERNAME:viajero[m]|viajera[f]}? Una expedición de mi pueblo ha llegado a Acebeda para buscar a nuestro pariente Balin en la vastedad de Khazad-dûm, pero creo que esto no tiene nada que ver con vuestros asuntos.\
\
'Aún así, nuestros señores Bósi y Brogur han recomendado que aceptemos cualquier ayuda que se nos ofrezca en este asunto. Me pregunto si se referían a los forasteros.\
\
'Si realmente queréis ayudar a los enanos a reclamar las salas de sus padres, hablad con Tulk al otro lado de este arco. No hemos tenido noticias de Balin durante muchos años, y podríamos encontrar las grandes salas de Khazad-dûm vacías o llenas de peligros.'","'Tulk se encuentra justo después de este arco. Búscalo si quieres ayudar a la Guarnición de Hierro a recuperar Khazad-dûm, ${PLAYER}.'","Libro 1, Capítulo 1: Extraños en Acebeda","Una expedición de enanos ha llegado a Acebeda con la intención de reclamar las perdidas salas de Khazad-dûm."},
[1839]={"Libro 1, Capítulo 10: En las Quebradas de los Túmulos","'¡Hey dol! ¡Merry dol! ¿No vas a cazar? ¿O prefieres quedarte un rato y cantar o tal vez ir a bailar?'","las Quebradas de los Túmulos están al norte y al este a lo largo de la Vieja Ruta de los Túmulos. Los crebain se detuvieron a posarse en los árboles dentro de las Quebradas de los Túmulos, al sur a lo largo de la cresta, sobre los bordes del bosque.\
\
Tom Bombadil encontró los crebain dentro de las Quebradas de los Túmulos, pero también mencionó la presencia de una mujer. Debes mantenerte alerta.","La Vieja Ruta de los Túmulos está al norte del bosque de Andraste. La casa de Tom Bombadil está al oeste y al sur a lo largo de la Vieja Ruta de los Túmulos.\
\
Andraste reveló que el Señor de los Nazgûl había ido a un lugar llamado Othrongroth, pero no pudiste aprender nada más antes de su muerte. Tom Bombadil es el Maestro del Bosque y de las Quebradas de los Túmulos. Podría saber dónde se encuentra Othrongroth.","¡Has derrotado a Andraste!","'¡Hola! ¡Quédate un rato! ¿O todavía tienes prisa?\
\
'¿Othrongroth, dices? Ese es un lugar oscuro, lleno de espectros oscuros, y no tienes necesidad de ir.\
\
'Si debes, debes, y no te detendré. Muy bien, acércate, y te lo diré.'","Tom Bombadil estaba complacido con los lirios que encontraste para Baya de Oro y te ha dicho dónde se pueden encontrar los crebain que estabas buscando. También te dijo que había una mujer allí esperando.","Habla con Tom Bombadil en su casa","'Los pájaros negros revoloteaban y aleteaban, saltando entre las ramas. Se posaron donde los inquietos caminan. ¡Cuidado con los viejos túmulos, se agitan cuando deberían estar durmiendo!\
\
'Ve al norte por el camino y sigue la Vieja Ruta de los Túmulos, luego al sur dentro del muro de los túmulos a lo largo de los bordes del bosque. ¡Hey dol! ¡Merry dol! ¡Y allí los encontrarás! Cuidado con la dama sombría.\
\
'¡Ahora salta, mi valiente! ¡Tom va a saltar!'","Encontrar y derrotar a los crebain y su amo"},
[1840]={"'You have returned from the library archives, ${PLAYER}? Have you learned anything that will help us defend against the attacks of Umbar? Why do you appear so sorrowful? What is wrong?'\
\
There is no easy way to give such tidings as you have of Boromir, but you do the best you can, and tell Lothíriel that he fell in battle protecting those who could not protect themselves. Her face betrays a confused mixture of emotion.\
\
'I do not know what to say, ${PLAYER}. Boromir was a good man. He always had my love and my respect, and I would have married him for Gondor. His father the Steward dreamed of the triumph of the kingdom, and in the dream I was a garlanded queen in Minas Tirith, beneath a fair and golden sun. My father, too, had a similar dream: he dreamt that I was in a high place, wearing a golden crown.'\
\
Lothíriel wipes at the dampness in her eyes with the back of her sleeve.\
\
'I mourn for my cousin, ${PLAYER}, and for Gondor. I was unhappy with the marriage match, but now that he is gone I am sad for his passing, glad that he attained glory, and angry for my relief. I do not know how I feel.'","'Lord Imrahil is the Prince of Dol Amroth, and he is the wise ruler of the city and its surrounding lands. He has gone to Minas Tirith with many soldiers, but he has left some of his swan-knights to serve his daughter Lothíriel, who now rules the city during his absence.\
\
'Imrahil is well-loved by the people of Belfalas, but his daughter is untested and unproven. Númenórean tradition allows women to rule, but not all folk in Gondor remember such things; I have heard some dissatisfaction that she was chosen to rule the city while her father is away.\
\
'But Lothíriel is loyal and complies with her father's wishes, despite her young age and a tendency toward recklessness. She recently disagreed with an arrangement of marriage, but it is my understanding she will go through with the proposed match, despite her feelings, or the feelings of a great many of her people. Some things are not meant to be, and I fear there will be a reckoning for it.'","'Go to the libraries of Dol Amroth and speak to Pethebir, the master of the archives. Learn from him everything you can about the Corsairs and their masters. Perhaps in so doing you will discover something we can use to our advantage.'","You convey Dorthaneth's warning about the Heirs of Castamir and the one they call 'the Scourge.' Lothíriel frowns, deep in thought.\
\
'I will take Dorthaneth's warning to heart, but I do not know a great deal about the people of Umbar or their leaders. Every child of Gondor knows the tale of Castamir the Usurper, of course, but his is a name from long ago and I thought his line was ended. I do not know.\
\
'My father has always said the finest way to combat a new foe is to learn as much of his history and temper as you can, before facing him on the battlefield. I think this is wisdom. To that end, I ask you to go to the libraries of Dol Amroth and speak to Pethebir, the master of the archives. He was my tutor, when I was just a child, and he believed I neglected my studies. This will not change his mind! But now I need information, and he will know where to find it. Learn from him everything you can about the Corsairs and their masters. Perhaps in so doing you will discover something we can use to our advantage.'","Talk to Lothíriel","'Naremil and Nosseth have travelled extensively throughout the kingdom of Gondor, and can tell you a great deal about the land and our rich history. Nosseth has a particularly keen insight for the lineages of the Kings and of the Stewards, and the political intensions of various Lords and Ladies. Cirhael can tell you a great deal about the Corsairs, and the land from which they hail: Umbar, to the south across the Bay.'","Book 1, Chapter 10: Keepers of the History","'Ah, did my scholars help you learn anything of use, ${PLAYER}? It seems to me that the Corsairs are a dangerous threat, and Lothíriel would be wise to recall the swan-knights she sent from the city. I hope the information of my scholars proves helpful to you and to Lothíriel, and awakens her to the uncertain future that awaits.'\
\
Pethebir notices your expression, and sighs.\
\
'I see that Nosseth spoke to you of Lothíriel's betrothal to Boromir. I should have counseled her to exercise restraint! None are happy about this match, save Denethor, and as he is the Ruling Steward there are none willing to speak against his wishes. All I know of it is that he had a dream of some sort that convinced him of the rightness of this match, but I do not know what it could have been.'\
\
You decide not to tell the earnest archivist that you know Boromir will never wed Lothíriel, but the young ruler of the city should be told the fate of her intended.","'The kingdom was first established in the wake of disaster. The land of Númenor fell beneath the waves; only fast ships could save the household of Elendil and bring them to these shores. High King Elendil's sons ruled the kingdom together, but when the Dark Power returned to Middle-earth, Elendil and his sons Isildur and Anárion were slain. The line continued by way of Anárion's son through many years, until Eärnur, the last king of Gondor, disappeared into Minas Morgul and was never seen again.\
\
'For more than nine hundred years, rule of the kingdom has passed down through the hereditary line of the Ruling Stewards, charged with maintaining the peace and welfare of Gondor until the line of Kings is restored. Few believe that can ever happen. Any claimant would need to prove an unbroken blood-line, a task that seems insurmountable to this poor scholar.'","'Lothíriel seeks information? What a wonder! She has never sought our knowledge before this. Perhaps she has begun to take seriously the duty with which she has been charged? At last. When I was her tutor she was the very picture of inattentive boredom. It is one of my greatest regrets that I was unable to impress upon her the importance of study.\
\
'That is ancient history! What matters now is the present need. The scholars here are at your disposal, of course! Allow me to guide the course of your study.\
\
'Naremil and Nosseth have travelled extensively throughout the kingdom of Gondor, and can tell you a great deal about the land and our rich history. Nosseth has a particularly keen insight for the lineages of the Kings and of the Stewards, and the political intentions of various Lords and Ladies. Cirhael can tell you a great deal about the Corsairs, and the port from which they hail: Umbar, to the south across the Bay.'","'I will tell you what time allows about our kingdom, but that is a rich history and there is much of which I might speak!\
\
'The kingdom was first established in the wake of disaster. The land of Númenor fell beneath the waves; only fast ships could save the household of Elendil and bring them to these shores. High King Elendil's sons ruled the kingdom together, but when the Dark Power returned to Middle-earth, Elendil and his sons Isildur and Anárion were slain. The line continued by way of Anárion's son through many years, until Eärnur, the last king of Gondor, disappeared into Minas Morgul and was never seen again.\
\
'For more than nine hundred years, rule of the kingdom has passed down through the hereditary line of the Ruling Stewards, charged with maintaining the peace and welfare of Gondor until the line of Kings is restored. Few believe that can ever happen. Any claimant would need to prove an unbroken blood-line, a task that seems insurmountable to this poor scholar.'","Pethebir is at the libraries of Dol Amroth.\
\
Lothíriel believes the best way to prepare for the threat of the Corsairs of Umbar is to learn as much about their ways as you can, and to that end she has sent you to the libraries of Dol Amroth.","'It seems to me that the Corsairs are a dangerous threat, and Lothíriel would be wise to recall the swan-knights she sent from the city. I hope the information of my scholars proves helpful to you and to Lothíriel, and awakens her to the uncertain future that awaits.'","'South of Dol Amroth, across the Bay of Belfalas, the city of Umbar stands. Its large harbour provides the mooring for many great ships, and a mighty fortress was built there. It was an important port for the Númenóreans, but when strife split the loyalties of that people, Umbar became a contested land.\
\
'It remained so throughout history, at times taken by Gondor and at others occupied by Black Númenóreans and their Haradrim allies. One of the most devastating losses of Umbar occurred following the Kin-strife, one of Gondor's darkest periods. The sons of Castamir the Usurper, chief architect of the Kin-strife, escaped from Gondor and named themselves 'Corsairs of Umbar.'\
\
'Castamir's sons were all slain, but their legacy remains. The Corsairs have caused much hardship along the coastline over the years.'","Talk to Nosseth and learn about Prince Imrahil and Lothíriel","Lothíriel is in the Great Hall of Dol Amroth.\
\
You have learned that Lothíriel is unhappily betrothed to her cousin Boromir, and should tell her of her intended's fate.","You have given Lothíriel the message from Dorthaneth, and she wants to prepare for the coming of the Heirs of Castamir by acquiring as much knowledge about them as possible.","'Lord Imrahil is the Prince of Dol Amroth, and he is the wise ruler of the city and its surrounding lands. He has gone to Minas Tirith with many soldiers, but he has left some of his Swan-knights to serve his daughter Lothíriel, who now rules the city during his absence.\
\
'Imrahil is well-loved by the people of Belfalas, but his daughter is untested and unproven. Númenórean tradition allows women to rule, but not all folk in Gondor remember such things; I have heard some dissatisfaction that she was chosen to rule the city while her father is away.\
\
'But Lothíriel is loyal and complies with her father's wishes, despite her young age and a tendency toward recklessness. She recently disagreed with an arrangement of marriage, but it is my understanding she will go through with the proposed match, despite her feelings, or the feelings of a great many of her people. Some things are not meant to be, and I fear there will be a reckoning for it.'","Talk to Cirhael and learn about Umbar","Talk to Pethebir","Talk to Pethebir in the library of Dol Amroth","Pethebir has given you the names of several scholars who may be able to help you.","Talk to Naremil and learn about Gondor"},
[1841]={"Skardí Doblafilos está detrás del mostrador de su herrería en Musgovilla.","Libro 1, Capítulo 10: Al Borde del Peligro","'Si este rumbo te parece apropiado, recomiendo que regresamos a Musgovilla para reabastecernos. ¡Pongamos a Skardí Doblafilos a trabajar una vez más antes de partir de la Ciénaga de los Cisnes y viajar al norte para entregar nuestra advertencia!'","'Tomaré la advertencia de Bregoleth en serio, y tú también deberías hacerlo.\
\
'Con ese fin, ¿podría sugerir que viajemos por un mismo camino, en lugar de dos, ${PLAYER}? Debo llevar la advertencia al caudillo de los Dúnedain acerca del peligro que representa Saruman y sus Uruk-hai. No me recibirá calurosamente, y no sé dónde se encuentra, pero esta advertencia debe entregarse igualmente. Sugiero que nos dirijamos a las ruinas del Antiguo Cardolan y consultemos con un amigo mío que vive entre ellas, Narndir de nombre. Él no dio la espalda a nuestra amistad cuando yo... cuando me fui. Él sabrá dónde encontrar al Dúnadan que buscamos.\
\
'Agradecería tu compañía en el camino. Una vez haya entregado mi mensaje, te dejaré en la mejor posada que he conocido: la Posada del Poney Pisador, en Bree. Desde allí, sin duda encontrarás un camino hacia las aventuras que desees.\
\
'¿Qué dices? Si este rumbo te parece apropiado, recomiendo que regresemos a Musgovilla para reabastecernos. ¡Pongamos a Skardí Doblafilos a trabajar una vez más antes de dejar la Ciénaga de los Cisnes y viajar al norte para entregar nuestra advertencia!'","Skardí te dedica un gruñido a modo de saludo cuando entras en su tienda.","'Y así me despediré de ti y del Montaraz Meneldir, pues debo llevar esta advertencia a Imladris: el Mago Saruman ha enviado partidas de guerra Uruk a las ruinas de Eregion y la Ciénaga de los Cisnes en busca del saber de los Anillos. Lo que desea hacer con él... el señor Elrond lo sabrá mejor que yo, pero sin duda no puede significar nada bueno. Creí que habíamos aprendido el peligro de tal artesanía, pero quizá no sea así.\
\
'Temo que estamos en el mismo borde del peligro, ${PLAYER}. Te deseo buena fortuna a ti y a Meneldir en vuestros caminos, dondequiera que los lleven, pero también tengo una advertencia propia que ofrecer.\
\
'Te insto a que seas precavido en el camino y a que no confíes demasiado pronto en los demás. Estos son días que jamás pensé ver, y sin embargo, a mi alrededor veo señales de una sombra creciente. Puede que los siervos de Saruman, o los de un enemigo que aún no percibimos, estén trabajando para deshacer todo el bien que se ha logrado en estas tierras.\
\
'¡Adiós! Quizá nos volvamos a encontrar en un día más soleado, cuando estas preocupaciones hayan quedado atrás.'","'Adiós, ustedes dos, y recuerden mi advertencia: tengan cuidado en el camino y no confíen con demasiada facilidad. Estos son tiempos peligrosos.'","Meneldir te ha recomendado que regreses a la herrería de Skardí Doblafilos en Musgovilla para reabastecerte antes de tu viaje hacia el norte, rumbo a los parientes de Meneldir.","Bregoleth se ha despedido de ti y de Meneldir, prometiendo llevar noticia de la amenaza de Saruman a Rivendel.","'Te insto a que seas precavido en el camino y a que no confíes demasiado pronto en los demás. Estos son días que jamás pensé ver, y sin embargo, a mi alrededor veo señales de una sombra creciente. Puede que los siervos de Saruman, o los de un enemigo que aún no percibimos, estén trabajando para deshacer todo el bien que se ha logrado en estas tierras.\
\
'¡Adiós! Quizá nos volvamos a encontrar en un día más soleado, cuando estas preocupaciones hayan quedado atrás.'","'No pensé que volverías a Musgovilla tan pronto. Justo sucede que Geralt y Wenna vinieron hace un rato, y me pidieron preparar algo de equipo para dártelo en caso de que regresaras. Parece que querían recompensarte por cuidar de su hijo, Tegwyn. Arreglaron el pago, así que ¿quién soy yo para discutir? Han logrado que el muchacho me moleste menos seguido de lo que solía, lo cual es casi suficiente pago, si me preguntas.\
\
'Dije casi. La tranquilidad no pone comida en la mesa, pero por suerte para ti, las monedas sí lo hacen. Así que elige lo que quieras, y no tendrás que pagar nada.'","Habla con Skardí Doblafilos en su herrería en Musgovilla.","Regresa a la herrería de Skardí Doblafilos en Musgovilla.","Meneldir está en el campamento de Idhobel, en el Eregion Occidental.","Habla con Meneldir en Idhobel."},
[1842]={"Aprendiste de la mujer Andraste que el Señor de los Nazgûl estaba viajando a un lugar llamado Othrongroth. Si pudieras espiar al Rey Brujo en este lugar, podrías aprender más sobre sus planes.","'¡Bueno, mi alegre ${PLAYERNAME:compañero[m]|compañera[f]}! ¿Listo para saltar sobre túmulos? Salta y cantaremos una canción que hará temblar a los Oscuros.'","Regresa a Tom Bombadil y reclama tu recompensa.\
\
Tú y tus aliados se enfrentaron a las oscuras profundidades de Othrongroth y salieron victoriosos.","'El Gran Túmulo no es un lugar para corazones débiles o miembros frágiles. Los malvados tumularios y los señores malignos se regocijan en su terror. Nunca han atrapado al Viejo Tom y nunca lo harán. ¡Él es el Maestro!\
\
'¡Si vas a ir, Tom te llevará!'","Habla con Tom Bombadil","'La oscuridad queda atrás en esa tumba húmeda y sombría. ¡Volveremos a la luz y sentiremos el sol en nuestros rostros una vez más!'","Libro 1, Capítulo 11: Othrongroth","Tom Bombadil ha accedido a mostrarte el camino a Othrongroth, un túmulo en las Quebradas de los Túmulos."},
[1843]={"'Tu misión debe ser de gran importancia, entonces. La nuestra también.'","Egfrith sale del río, jadeando.","Emerges chorreando del río, ${PLAYERNAME:agradecido[m]|agradecida[f]} de haber cruzado al fin.","Habla con Egfrith en la ribera norte del Gwathló.","Reúnente con Meneldir en la ribera sur del Gwathló, al noroeste de Musgovilla.","La mujer de Rohan está en la ribera sur del Gwathló, reacia a separarse de su corcel.","'El destino de Rohan descansa sobre mi misión, o no habría dejado atrás a alguien tan leal como mi Starkmód. Así lo jura Egfrith de Faldham, que ha cabalgado con toda prisa para obtener la ayuda que el rey Théoden requiere. Ahora crucemos el río, y en seguida.'","Habla con la mujer en el cruce del Gwathló.","'Skardí tiene razón. Si queremos llegar a Cardolan, necesitaremos cruzar el río Gwathló en Tharbad. Cuando los Númenóreanos construyeron la ciudad, su gran puente proporcionaba un valioso enlace con Gondor, y el comercio con las tierras del sur prosperaba.\
\
'Con el tiempo el Reino de Arnor disminuyó, y Tharbad fue abandonada. El Camino del Sur fue menos transitado que en los días prósperos. La mampostería se fue desmoronando con los años, y partes de la ciudad cayeron al río. El gran deshielo que siguió al Pico Invernal liberó riadas, y partes del puente se perdieron para siempre.\
\
'Pero la gente cruzaba el río en Tharbad antes de que se construyera el puente, y debería seguir siendo posible incluso ahora que ya no existe. Viajaremos al noroeste hacia Tharbad y lo comprobaremos por nosotros mismos, ${PLAYER}. Reunámonos a la sombra del puente roto en la ribera sur.'","El siguiente tramo de tu viaje para acompañar a Meneldir hasta los Dúnedain te llevará a Tharbad, en el río Gwathló.","Habla con Meneldir en el cruce del Gwathló.","'¿Sois amigos o enemigos? No puedo decirlo por vuestra apariencia. ¿Sois amigos de Rohan y de su pueblo?'","Meneldir ha completado el cruce y está exhausto en la ribera norte.","'Espero que Starkmód lo comprenda. Me habría seguido a donde fuera, incluso a la muerte. Él es como yo: haría cualquier cosa por Rohan.'\
\
Egfrith respira profundamente y masajea sus brazos para devolverles el calor.\
\
'Al otro lado de este río cruel me preguntaste por qué busco a los Montaraces Dúnedain. El rey Théoden ha enfermado, presa de una debilidad de la que tememos no pueda recuperarse. Me dijeron que los Montaraces del Norte conocen métodos de sanación que podrían curarlo. Debo recuperar uno de sus remedios o volver a Edoras con uno de sus sanadores, para que cure al rey.\
\
'Solo por el futuro de Rohan abandonaría a mi Starkmód. Quien lo cuestione, enfrentará mi espada.'","'Es hora. Mantente en el centro del río, si puedes, porque los orcos merodean las islas y vigilan las aguas poco profundas. Nos reuniremos en la orilla del noroeste.'","Egfrith casi ha logrado cruzar el Gwathló.","Habla con Meneldir en la herrería de Musgovilla.","Egfrith ha cruzado el río con éxito.","Libro 1, Capítulo 11: El Cruce en Tharbad","Habla con Meneldir en la ribera norte del Gwathló.","Espera a que Egfrith se reúna contigo en la ribera norte del Gwathló.","Encontraste a una mujer de Rohan en la ribera sur del Gwathló.\
\
La mujer te observa con curiosidad desde la grupa de su corcel.","'¡Deteneos, forasteros! ¿Sois amigos o enemigos? Admito que no puedo saberlo por vuestra apariencia. ¿Sois amigos de Rohan y de su pueblo?'\
\
Aseguras a la mujer que tú y Meneldir no buscáis causar problemas a la gente de bien, y que solo deseáis cruzar el río en vuestro viaje hacia el norte. La mujer reflexiona un momento y asiente. Luego fija sus ojos en Meneldir.\
\
'No creas que esta pregunta es descortés, pero debo hacerla: vas vestido como me dijeron que visten los Montaraces Dúnedain, apropiado para la vida en las tierras inhóspitas del norte. ¿Eres uno de ellos? Porque son a quienes busco, y mi misión es urgente.'","Te duelen los músculos, pero los ásperos gritos de los orcos cercanos fortalecen tu determinación.","'La gente cruzaba el río en Tharbad antes de que existiera el puente, y debería seguir siendo posible incluso ahora. Viajaremos al noroeste a Tharbad y lo comprobaremos por nosotros mismos, ${PLAYER}. Reunámonos a la sombra del puente roto en la ribera sur.'","La mujer piensa un momento y luego, con pesar, desmonta de su corcel.","Meneldir te aconsejó considerar muy bien el cruce del Gwathló en Tharbad: el río tiene una reputación peligrosa donde atraviesa la ciudad.","'Es hora. Mantente en el centro del río, si puedes, porque los orcos merodean las islas y vigilan las aguas poco profundas. Nos reuniremos todos en la orilla lejana, al noroeste.'","Meneldir está dentro de la herrería de Skardí Doblafilos en Musgovilla, considerando tus próximos pasos.","El cruce del Gwathló ha sido peligroso por muchos años, desde la inundación del puente y la pérdida de un paso seguro a través de Tharbad.","Alcanza el punto medio del cruce del Gwathló.","Nada hasta el otro lado del peligroso río Gwathló.","Una mujer se sienta a lomos de un alto corcel en la ribera del Gwathló.","'¿Así que tu camino ahora te lleva a Cardolan? ¿El Antiguo Cardolan, dices?'\
\
Skardí se acaricia la barba.\
\
'No queda mucho allí, según entiendo. Si escuchas a Meneldir hablar, pensarías que fue un gran reino, pero eso fue hace mucho. Fue reclamado por la guerra y la peste, al parecer, y ahora lo recuerdan principalmente los Montaraces y los eruditos, y aquellos con la mala fortuna de oírlos hablar sin parar sobre él.\
\
'No voy a detenerte. Pero si vas por ese camino tendrás que cruzar el río en Tharbad. El puente está destruido, y el cruce no será agradable. ¡Disfruta, ${PLAYER}! Yo me quedaré aquí en mi tienda, donde está cálido y seco.'","'Adiós, Starkmód. Que encuentres tu camino de vuelta a los campos dorados de la Marca. Te veré de nuevo cuando haya cumplido mi tarea.'\
\
La mujer se vuelve hacia ti, con la mirada helada.\
\
'El destino de Rohan descansa sobre mi misión, o no habría dejado atrás a alguien tan leal como mi Starkmód. Así lo jura Egfrith de Faldham, que ha cabalgado aquí con toda prisa para conseguir la ayuda que el rey Théoden requiere. Ahora crucemos el río, y de inmediato.'","'Eso no fue agradable, ${PLAYER}, pero al menos hemos alcanzado la ribera norte. ¡Habría sido mucho más fácil si el gran puente siguiera intacto!\
\
'Necesitaré descansar un momento antes de continuar. ¿Cómo se encuentra Egfrith?'","Meneldir está en la ribera sur del Gwathló, pensando cómo responder a la mujer de Rohan que encontraste.","'Tu pregunta no es fácil de responder. Digamos que una vez fui de ese pueblo, pero si necesitas buscar a los Dúnedain, tu búsqueda no ha terminado. Aun así, nuestros propósitos pueden alinearse, pues ${PLAYER} y yo también buscamos a los Montaraces del Norte.\
\
Meneldir dirige su mirada al tumultuoso río.\
\
'Cada uno de nuestros caminos requiere vadear el Gwathló, el Río Aguagrís, y no será sencillo. Temo que las aguas embravecidas sean demasiado para tu corcel en algunos tramos, y parece que los orcos vigilan las aguas poco profundas. Conozco a los Rohirrim solo por historias, pero sé que no se separan de sus caballos salvo por gran necesidad.\
\
'Si tal es la necesidad que te guía, quisiera saber tu nombre, y quizá nos cuentes tu misión al otro lado del río. De lo contrario, te desearía buena suerte, pues ${PLAYER} y yo no podemos demorar más.'","'Si te diriges a Cardolan, tendrás que cruzar el río en Tharbad. ¡Yo me quedaré aquí, donde está cálido y seco!'"},
[1844]={"Find the hidden villain near the beacon of Maegond","You have defeated the Corsair raiders, and now Nedhros can return","'You have returned, my friend, and with a message? Well, do not tarry in its delivery, for I have an urgent matter of my own to resolve!'\
\
Rovalang listens to your message.\
\
'I will return to the city, as Lothíriel commands. But I cannot abandon the Blackroot Vale just yet. A great evil has come south, and I cannot leave the people of the Vale at its mercy!\
\
'In form it took the shape of a great winged beast, and it flew out of the North, passing over the mountains. It circled over Erech for a time, and then passed low over Morlad. I saw it only moments before you arrived, passing low in the direction of the mountains.'\
\
Rovalang seems unaware of the nature of this evil, but you know it by the winged beast it rides, and have seen its kind before: Nazgûl! If this creature learns of Aragorn's passage and the army of the Dead that follows him, so too will the Great Enemy learn of it. The Nazgûl must be defeated.","Find and talk to Rovalang somewhere in the Blackroot Vale","Some villain is hidden atop the hill by the beacon of Maegond, in Lamedon.\
\
Heledir has agreed to return to Dol Amroth, but has asked you to seek out the hidden villain he sensed near the beacon of Maegond.","Nedhros is on the hill of Amon Lontir, by the great beacon.\
\
Lothíriel has sent you to recall Nedhros, the swan-knight she sent out of the city into the lands of Belfalas.","'If you have a taste for adventure, friend, you might travel up the hill to scout the beacon. I was just atop the hill, but saw no one, though I felt a watching presence. I think someone might be up there now, hiding from me.\
\
'If you climb the hill now, but quietly, you might surprise a hidden villain. I think you should do so, my friend!'","Rovalang was near the Hill of Erech, in Blackroot Vale, when last you saw him.\
\
Lothíriel asked you to find Rovalang, the swan-knight she sent to Blackroot Vale.","Corsair raiders have scaled the hill in secret. Defeat their leader to demoralize them!","'Lothíriel wishes for me to return to the city? I will do so at once.\
\
'If you have a taste for adventure, friend, you might travel up the hill to scout the beacon. I was just atop the hill, but saw no one, though I felt a watching presence. I think someone might be up there now, hiding from me.\
\
'If you climb the hill now, but quietly, you might surprise a hidden villain. I think you should do so, my friend!'","Heledir is by the beacon of Maegond, in Lamedon.\
\
Lothíriel has sent you to recall the Swan-knight Heledir, currently scouting on her behalf in Lamedon.","Find and defeat the Corsair leader near the beacon of Maegond","'While my father is away, I must rule in Dol Amroth. I do not have the time to come to terms with this loss, ${PLAYER}. I will grieve at another time, and reconcile my feelings then. For now I must be strong.'\
\
By the set of her jaw you see that Lothíriel is resolved, and the strength of her father is in her.\
\
'I sent forth the swan-knights for two purposes. One was the purpose of a ruler, to ensure the safety of her people. The other purpose was that of a rebellious child, acting out against the wishes of her father in the only way she could. That purpose I regret. Now is the time for the swan-knights to return to Dol Amroth, for I will have need of them if we are to survive the menace of Umbar and these Heirs of Castamir.\
\
'Travel first to the beacon on Amon Lontir, east of the city, and tell Nedhros to return. He is the nearest swan-knight, and is advanced in age, but it has not decreased his skill one measure. Travel then to the beacon of Maegond, in Lamedon. Heledir is the knight I sent to Lamedon, and he is also brave of heart.\
\
'The last of the knights I sent forth is named Rovalang, and he will be somewhere in the Blackroot Vale, I know not where.'","You assure Heledir you will search for the mysterious villain, and he can return","Book 1, Chapter 11: The Swan-knights","'Travel first to the beacon on Amon Lontir, east of the city, and tell Nedhros to return. He is the nearest swan-knight, and is advanced in age, but it has not decreased his skill one measure. Travel then to the beacon of Maegond, in Lamedon. Heledir is the knight I sent to Lamedon, and he is also brave of heart.\
\
'The last of the knights I sent forth is named Rovalang, and he will be somewhere in the Blackroot Vale, I know not where.'","You defeated the Corsair leader near Maegond, and demoralized his allies","Rovalang will return to Dol Amroth, but he has a great evil to combat first!","'You say that Lothíriel has commanded my return to the city? I will return, of course, but there is something I must say to you first, young one!'\
\
Nedhros laughs sharply.\
\
'You have interrupted me during a brief lull in the battle, my timely new friend! I routed a group of Corsair raiders, but they are certain to return. Indeed, I hear them approach once more!'","Lothíriel agrees with Pethebir that, given the unexpected severity of the Corsair threat, the swan-knights should return to Dol Amroth.","Talk to Nedhros on Amon Lontir, in Belfalas","Talk to Heledir by the beacon of Maegond, in Lamedon"},
[1845]={"Trancos espera tu regreso en su habitación del Poney Pisador, en Bree. La entrada que lleva desde las Quebradas de los Túmulos al Gran Camino del Este está al norte.\
\
Regresa a Bree y dile a Trancos lo que has aprendido sobre los planes del Rey Brujo.","Habla con Trancos","'El señor Gandalf pidió hablar con cualquiera que estuviera buscando a Trancos. Puedes encontrarlo en su habitación.'","Libro 1, Capítulo 12: Los planes del Jinete Negro","Tom Bombadil te rescató de las garras del señor de los túmulos, pero aprendiste mucho que podría ayudar a Trancos y su gente.","'Los antiguos Tumularios de Angmar han venido. Perturban la paz y molestan a quienes caminan por sus túmulos. Deja que los muertos descansen y que sus problemas queden en la tierra... a menos, claro, que los despiertes bailando sobre sus techos.\
\
'¡Eh, ven, amigo mío! No te quedes aquí más tiempo. Debes ir a Bree. ¡Allí te espera un amigo!'","'Los antiguos tumularios de Angmar han venido. Perturban la paz y molestan a quienes caminan por sus túmulos. Deja que los muertos descansen y que sus problemas queden en la tierra... a menos, claro, que los despiertes bailando sobre sus techos.\
\
'¡Eh, ven, amigo mío! No te quedes aquí más tiempo. Debes ir a Bree. ¡Allí te espera un amigo!'","Para encontrar la habitación de Gandalf en la posada El Poney Pisador de Bree, debes girar a la izquierda al salir de la sala común, hasta que solo puedas girar a la derecha. La habitación está al final del pasillo, en la parte superior de las escaleras.\
\
Cebadilla Mantecona te ha dicho que Trancos ha abandonado El Poney Pisador, pero que Gandalf, un Mago de renombre, llegó y pidió hablar con cualquiera que estuviera buscando al Montaraz. Deberías hablar con Gandalf y contarle lo que has aprendido.","Cebadilla Mantecona atiende a sus clientes en la sala común del Poney Pisador.\
\
Has regresado al Poney Pisador, pero la puerta de la habitación de Trancos está cerrada con llave. Deberías hablar con Cebadilla Mantecona para ver si sabe dónde se ha ido Trancos.","'¡Oh, hola de nuevo! Estaba tan ocupado que no te vi, pero aquí nunca hay un momento de paz, si me permites decirlo. Estaba tan preocupado de que estropeara mi cerveza por dejar que el señor, eh, Sotomonte y sus amigos se fueran con ese Montaraz.\
\
'¿Él? ¡Ah! ¡Por supuesto que es el señor Gandalf! Dicen que es un Mago o algo así, y debo decir que debe haber algo de cierto en esas historias, porque mi cerveza nunca ha estado mejor. ¡Estaba tan contento...!\
\
'Perdona, pero a veces me extiendo demasiado. ¡Gandalf dijo que enviara a cualquiera que buscara a Trancos a su habitación! Está arriba, justo después de la habitación de Trancos.'","La puerta de la habitación de Trancos está cerrada","'Has perdido el camino o me buscas con intención. Por la mirada en tus ojos, deduzco que es lo segundo, aunque también siento que buscabas a otro... ¿Trancos? Entonces ambos hemos llegado demasiado tarde. Nuestro amigo mutuo se ha ido, llevando consigo una terrible carga.\
\
'Soy Gandalf el Gris, amigo de Trancos. Si te ha encomendado una tarea, no puede ser menos urgente que la suya. Cuéntame tu historia y se la contaré a él...\
\
'¿Así que Angmar se levanta? Es una noticia sombría, pero no me sorprende. Sin embargo, no puedo apartarme de mi propia tarea, pues el destino de toda la Tierra Media depende de ello.\
\
'Coloco esta carga sobre ti en nombre de los Pueblos Libres de la Tierra Media... Contrarresta los planes del Rey Brujo si puedes. Ya sea hacia el este o hacia el norte, te deseo buena suerte. Adiós.'"},
[1846]={"Lothíriel is in the Great Hall of Dol Amroth.\
\
You faced a Nazgûl in the Blackroot Vale, and though it has been driven away formless to its master, this is a clear sign that the Great Enemy has Gondor much on his mind.","Talk to Rovalang on the Hill of Erech, in Blackroot Vale","Rovalang is on the slopes of the Hill of Erech, in the Blackroot Vale.\
\
With the help of Rovalang, you have driven off the Nazgûl that threatened to learn of Aragorn's passage with the army of the Dead.","Rovalang is on the slopes of the Hill of Erech, in the Blackroot Vale.\
\
The Nazgûl must be prevented from learning of Aragorn's passage with the army of the Dead, at any cost.","'You have heard of this winged creature, ${PLAYER}... I can see it in your eye. Will you help me find it and keep it from harming the people of the Vale?'\
\
You nod in agreement. If the Nazgûl learns that Aragorn commands an army of the Dead, much harm might be done to the desperate hope that drives him, and to the people that depend on him.\
\
'Well, let us go at once! If you have a Fellowship at your call, bring them along as well. There will be danger enough for all... but now let us chase this foe! I saw it fly in the direction of the haunted cave to the north-west. Perhaps we can bring it down, if we hurry!'","'My swan-knights have returned, ${PLAYER}, and I thank you for bringing them my message. I see from your face that you have more to say to me. What is on your mind?'\
\
You tell Lothíriel of your encounter with the Nazgûl in the Blackroot Vale. She is silent for a long time. When she speaks again, her voice is very quiet, the words not much more than a whisper.\
\
'I remember the heat of summer on the stones of the White City, ${PLAYER}. It was late in the month of June, and my father brought me and my brothers to Minas Tirith with a dozen riders. He did not reveal the purpose of the journey until we were in the Steward's chamber: I was to marry Boromir, the son of my father's sister. He was tall, and confident, and a great warrior, and I could tell that he too did not want the match.\
\
'But he was an obedient son, and consented to the betrothal. There would have been a wedding on that warm night of June, but Boromir had a journey of his own to make, and it was decided the wedding would occur on his return. 'I will bring you a wedding gift,' he said to me before I joined my father and brothers in the courtyard for the return to Dol Amroth. 'I will win this war and bring you the peace you deserve!' he called to me. I never saw him again.'\
\
Lothíriel's eyes are fierce, her mouth a thin line sharp with resolve.\
\
'I did not want to marry him, and he did not want to marry me. But we wanted the same thing. We wanted peace and happiness for our people, and we were willing to sacrifice whatever we needed to achieve it for them. Our enemies have underestimated us. They think we are soft. They think we will give in to despair and give in to grief. But we will not.\
\
'I spent more time in study than the archivist Pethebir believed. I know the name of the Great Enemy, the master of the foe you faced in the Blackroot Vale. I am not afraid to utter his name. He is Sauron, and we will stand against him to the last man, woman, and child. Gondor is not without strength. We will face the great strength of Sauron and we will defeat him, or we will die. There are no other choices for us.\
\
'I will call for you, ${PLAYER}. Enemies are everywhere, and we have only just begun to fight.'","'We should return to Dol Amroth at once. Lothíriel must be told that servants of the Great Enemy walk in Gondor!'","'I think you knew more about that creature than you let on, my friend. I am glad you were here! My tale might have ended in the shadow of the haunted mountain if you were not! But we have both faced great evil and lived, and our tales go on.\
\
'That creature brings to mind a name from the ancient years, a name of great evil. I will not speak this name, but I have now seen with my own eyes the servant of that terrible Enemy.\
\
'The time has come to return to Dol Amroth. Lothíriel must be told.'","Book 1, Chapter 12: The Shadow in Morthond","If Rovalang saw a Nazgûl on its winged steed, it must be prevented from learning of Aragorn's passage with the army of the Dead, at any cost.","Talk to Rovalang and face 'The Shadow in Morthond'","'I do not know what that creature might be, but I know it is my duty to face it. We will face it together! If you have a Fellowship at your call, bring them along as well!'","Talk to Lothíriel in the Great Hall of Dol Amroth"},
[1847]={"Rodwen is up some stairs north of the Tower of Ecthelion, beyond a doorway spanned by a flower garland, in Minas Tirith (Midsummer).\
\
Rodwen has asked to meet you outside the throne room, and away from listening ears. For what purpose does the expert wedding-planner seek this secret meeting?","'${PLAYER}, my friend! I am pleased you could return to my city in time of peace, with war safely behind us! We cannot lower our guard overmuch, it is true, but Mithrandir and the Council of Gondor both assure me that the threat of further war is at a low ebb, for now. My mind therefore turns from martial matters to those of the heart, for a day long prepared is nearly upon us. As you well know, Arwen my betrothed travels even now to Minas Tirith, where we shall be wedded before all of Gondor, and she will be the queen of my kingdom.\
\
'Long have we waited for this day! It is very important to me and to my love that the ceremony be conducted properly, but my knowledge of such matters is not sufficient. Mithrandir insists that he has an understanding of the rituals, but some members of the Council questioned the depth of his knowledge concerning the customs of Gondor. The Council therefore selected a number of Gondorian representatives to decorate the city and make ready the ceremony. The woman responsible for the wedding ceremony is named Rodwen, and I would ask you to lend her your able assistance, if you have the time and the inclination.\
\
'Arwen will be here soon with her household, and I want all the preparations to be made before she arrives.'","'Yes, hello. ${PLAYER}, is it? Hmmm... I see. You are to help me make ready the wedding ceremony? I assure you, we have things well in hand....'\
\
Rodwen appears visibly nervous, and seems to be having some trouble meeting your gaze. There is something familiar about this woman, but you cannot quite place it.\
\
'Let us meet somewhere to discuss the preparations, ${PLAYER}. There is no point in disturbing the king with such details. Surely... surely you agree? Let us find a quiet spot to discuss them. If you leave the Tower of Ecthelion and turn north, you will see a doorway spanned by a garland of flowers. Slip past that garland and climb the steps to the wall... and that is where I will meet you.'","Talk to Rodwen up some stairs north of the Tower of Ecthelion, beyond a doorway spanned by a flower garland, in Minas Tirith (Midsummer)","Book 1, Chapter 1: A Real Adventure","Your adventures during the War of the Ring gave you the honour of befriending both Aragorn, newly-crowned king of Gondor, and his bride-to-be, Arwen Undómiel, Elf-maid and daughter of Elrond of Rivendell. Their wedding approaches, and you have been invited to attend the ceremony in Minas Tirith on Midsummer's Day.","Rodwen looks around to make sure you were not followed by unfriendly forces. When she is satisfied, she lets out a deep exhalation of relief.\
\
'${PLAYER}! You remember me, surely? Rodwen, Champion of Gondor? We met near Parth Galen, along the East Wall of Rohan! My friends and I had gotten into a bit of trouble, and you helped us get out of it. I was quite surprised to see you again in the throne room of the White City, in the presence of King Elessar, no less!'\
\
You ask Rodwen what curious road took her out of the wilderness and gave to her the responsibility of planning a king's wedding. She raises her hands level to her shoulders with an energetic shrug.\
\
'Would that I could tell you! The adventuring life was hard, and to be honest with you my friends may not have been entirely prepared for it. The road we thought to take north was crawling with Orcs, so we turned south and arrived outside the Pelennor Fields just as the Gondorian force returned from Mordor in triumph. Happy timing! We joined the celebrations, of course, and decided that perhaps it was safer to put our adventuring days behind us. We no longer had a minstrel, you may remember; Cuilinn decided to try a life of farming rather than our dangerous course. Well, he has given it up already. Farming was not for him!\
\
'So we all came to settle within the White City, and through a series of misunderstandings and some ill-advised boasting my friends and I caught the attention of the Council of Gondor. The next thing I know, Isteron is speaking before those noble lords and ladies, insisting that we are expert wedding-planners all! So we have stumbled our way into something of a real adventure, ${PLAYER}. You have to help us... again!'","Talk to Rodwen in the throne room of Minas Tirith (Midsummer)","Rodwen the wedding-planner is in the throne room of Minas Tirith as Midsummer's Day approaches. The name is familiar, but the Rodwen you met was an adventurer who ran into trouble along the East Wall of Rohan in the company of her friends, and not a planner of weddings.\
\
You may use stable-masters at major towns and cities to advance to Minas Tirith (Midsummer) for the wedding festivities.","'The Council selected a Gondorian representative to make ready the ceremony and other preparations. Her name is Rodwen, and I would ask you to lend her your able assistance, if you have the time and the inclination.\
\
'Arwen will be here soon with her household, and I want all the preparations to be made before she arrives.'","'Let us meet somewhere to discuss the preparations, ${PLAYER}. There is no point in disturbing the king with such details. Surely... surely you agree? Let us find a quiet spot to discuss them. If you leave the Tower of Ecthelion and turn north, you will see a doorway spanned by a garland of flowers. Slip past that garland and climb the steps to the wall... and that is where I will meet you.'"},
[1848]={"Rodwen is up some stairs north of the Tower of Ecthelion, beyond a doorway spanned by a flower garland, in Minas Tirith (Midsummer).\
\
Rodwen has asked to meet you outside the throne room, and away from listening ears. For what purpose does the expert wedding-planner seek this secret meeting?","'${PLAYER}, my friend! I am pleased you could return to my city in time of peace, with war safely behind us! We cannot lower our guard overmuch, it is true, but Mithrandir and the Council of Gondor both assure me that the threat of further war is at a low ebb, for now. My mind therefore turns from martial matters to those of the heart, for a day long prepared is nearly upon us. As you well know, Arwen my betrothed travels even now to Minas Tirith, where we shall be wedded before all of Gondor, and she will be the queen of my kingdom.\
\
'Long have we waited for this day! It is very important to me and to my love that the ceremony be conducted properly, but my knowledge of such matters is not sufficient. Mithrandir insists that he has an understanding of the rituals, but some members of the Council questioned the depth of his knowledge concerning the customs of Gondor. The Council therefore selected a number of Gondorian representatives to decorate the city and make ready the ceremony. The woman responsible for the wedding ceremony is named Rodwen, and I would ask you to lend her your able assistance, if you have the time and the inclination.\
\
'Arwen will be here soon with her household, and I want all the preparations to be made before she arrives.'","Book 1, Chapter 1: A Real Adventure","Talk to Rodwen up some stairs north of the Tower of Ecthelion, beyond a doorway spanned by a flower garland, in Minas Tirith (Midsummer)","'The Council selected a Gondorian representative to make ready the ceremony and other preparations. Her name is Rodwen, and I would ask you to lend her your able assistance, if you have the time and the inclination.\
\
'Arwen will be here soon with her household, and I want all the preparations to be made before she arrives.'","Your adventures during the War of the Ring gave you the honour of befriending both Aragorn, newly-crowned king of Gondor, and his bride-to-be, Arwen Undómiel, Elf-maid and daughter of Elrond of Rivendell. Their wedding approaches, and you have been invited to attend the ceremony in Minas Tirith on Midsummer's Day.","'Yes, hello. ${PLAYER}, is it? Hmmm... I see. You are to help me make ready the wedding ceremony? I assure you, we have things well in hand....'\
\
Rodwen appears visibly nervous, and seems to be having some trouble meeting your gaze.\
\
'Let us meet somewhere to discuss the preparations, ${PLAYER}. There is no point in disturbing the king with such details. Surely... surely you agree? Let us find a quiet spot to discuss them. If you leave the Tower of Ecthelion and turn north, you will see a doorway spanned by a garland of flowers. Slip past that garland and climb the steps to the wall... and that is where I will meet you.'","Rodwen the wedding-planner is in the throne room of Minas Tirith as Midsummer's Day approaches.\
\
You may use stable-masters at major towns and cities to advance to Minas Tirith (Midsummer) for the wedding festivities.","'Let us meet somewhere to discuss the preparations, ${PLAYER}. There is no point in disturbing the king with such details. Surely... surely you agree? Let us find a quiet spot to discuss them. If you leave the Tower of Ecthelion and turn north, you will see a doorway spanned by a garland of flowers. Slip past that garland and climb the steps to the wall... and that is where I will meet you.'","Talk to Rodwen the wedding-planner in the throne room of Minas Tirith (Midsummer)","'I know you, ${PLAYER}. I have heard of your many heroic deeds, and word of your adventures has spread throughout the land. Is it true you can read the truth in someone's face despite their words? It is true, isn't it?'\
\
Rodwen's face is pale, and you need no special ability to determine how nervous she is in your presence.\
\
'Then I will just tell you, for you are sure to find it out anyway! I was an adventurer-for-hire, a champion of Gondor. My friends and I sought to earn coin by lending our swords and our skills to folk in need, but... we weren't very good at it. Our guardian Drafli was more brave than sensible, our minstrel Cuilinn never did learn the value of silence when enemies were about, and I have waylaid my sword at inopportune moments... more than once, I confess it! When the war ended, we decided it was best for all if we were to leave the adventuring life behind us. Cuilinn took up farming, the dear fellow, but it was a short-lived experiment and he has left that behind too; it did not suit him either.\
\
'So we all came to settle within the White City, and through a series of misunderstandings and some ill-advised boasting my friends and I caught the attention of the Council of Gondor. The next thing I know, our lore-master Isteron is speaking before those noble lords and ladies, insisting that we are expert wedding-planners all! What do I know about weddings? Little enough! So we have stumbled our way into something of a real adventure, ${PLAYER}, and if we cannot perfect this wedding ceremony we will be in real trouble! Will you help us?'"},
[1849]={"Book 1, Chapter 1: Gallant as Elf-lords","Defeated Laenan Orc-defilers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I will prepare to join the rest of my kin, ${PLAYER}, but I want you to deal with the Orc raiding-party I tracked from the Ettenmoors. You will find them among this confusing network of caves and the ruins beyond.\
\
'After you have dealt with the Orcs, return to Thorenhad and tell Elrohir that Laenan is clear of this foe.'","'You have given Radanir the message? Good. He will be able to find some others among the Dúnedain if they are to be found within the Trollshaws.\
\
'But now you must travel west to find others of Aragorn's kin.'","Elweleth is by the horses at Thorenhad, the camp of the sons of Elrond in the Trollshaws.\
\
Elrohir has told you to speak with Elweleth, for she will know where Radanir the Ranger has gone, if anyone will.","'I thought to give Radanir word of our meeting at my father's house, ${PLAYER}, so he would have some expectation of the road ahead, but it seems he has left Thorenhad and gone again into the wilderness of the Trollshaws.\
\
'He has left a few parcels here, so I am sure he intends to return, but he should be told the message you bear as soon as may be. I and my brother have already begun to assemble some of the supplies the Rangers will need as they head south, but it will take some time before they are ready.\
\
'Speak to Elweleth, by the horses, for she will know where Radanir planned to journey, if any will. Radanir is slow to laugh and to smile, but in Elweleth's company, I have observed it most frequently.'","Defeat Laenan Orc-warriors (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Elrohir is at Thorenhad, the camp of the sons of Elrond, north of the Bruinen Gorges in the Trollshaws.\
\
Pethelen has suggested a first step for your urgent errand: a visit with Elrohir at Thorenhad for an introduction to Radanir, one of the Dúnedain currently staying at Thorenhad.","Radanir is at the Laenan cave system, located in the north-west reaches of the Gladdalf, the wood-troll infested marshes of the North Trollshaws.\
\
You have spoken with Elweleth at Thorenhad, and she told you where to find Radanir the Dúnadan.","Elrohir is at Thorenhad, his camp in the Trollshaws.\
\
You have given Radanir the message for which you sought him, and he has agreed to join the Grey Company on its journey south. You should return to Elrohir now that you have dealt with the Orc raiding-party in the Laenan caves.","Talk to Elrohir at Thorenhad","Orc-warriors, Orc-defilers, and their leaders can be found within the confusing network of tunnels known as Laenan.\
\
Radanir has agreed to join the Grey Company on its journey south to aid Aragorn, but he wants you to deal with the Orc raiding-party he tracked through the Trollshaws.","Defeat Laenan Orc-defilers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated Laenan Orc-leader","'Radanir planned to investigate the Laenan cave system at the north-west reaches of the Gladdalf, the wood-troll infested marshes of the North Trollshaws. You should go there and give him your tidings, even if they will draw him from the Trollshaws and into great peril far from his friends. His road has always been through the Wild, and nothing this humble Elf-maid may say will change that.'","'Thorenhad, the camp of the sons of Elrond, is located on a hill north of the Bruinen Gorges, deep within the Trollshaws. Travel there and speak with Elrohir for an introduction to Radanir, one of the Dúnedain currently staying there. Once you have given him word that the Dúnedain must be assembled, you can seek out the rest of those suggested by Master Elrond, though it take you across much of Eriador.'","'Aragorn is my chieftain, and it is my duty to go to his aid, though all the dangers of Middle-earth lie in between. This is the moment for which the Dúnedain have prepared, and I will not now abandon my kin.\
\
'I have learned that an Orc raiding party from the Ettenmoors has established a camp within this warren of tunnels, ${PLAYER}. I cannot leave them here, unchallenged. Will you brave these caves and deal with these foes? Somewhere deep within this confusing warren is the entrance to a once-abandoned tomb of Men. If the Orcs have found it, that is where their leaders will be. Thorenhad is less than a day's march from this place, and I will not suffer these Orcs to live that they may threaten what I hold dear.\
\
'I will make ready to depart, as you have asked, but I will be grateful if you destroy the Orcs and their leaders within the Laenan tunnels and the ruins that lie at their back. After you have done so, return to Elrohir at Thorenhad and tell him of your success. The sons of Elrond lost their mother to such a party of Orcs; they would not forgive us if we let these foes be.'","'You have dealt a serious blow to the Orcs, ${PLAYER}, and I thank you for it. I go now to prepare for the journey south. You should return to Thorenhad and speak with Elrohir.'","Defeated Laenan Orc-warriors (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Elweleth at Thorenhad","You have been charged by Elrond of Rivendell with gathering Aragorn's Dúnadan kin throughout Eriador.","'You are looking for Radanir, ${PLAYER}? He left not long ago, and he took no horse; the Dúnedain will ride when they must, but he has confided to me that he is more comfortable when on foot.\
\
'Always behind his words to me was a current of...I do not know how best to say it, other than to say that Radanir seemed always to be waiting for something, somehow. I wonder if the tidings you bring are those for which he has waited so long? I wonder too if they will send him from the Trollshaws, and for how long? I will miss his visits if this be so, for I will not remain in this Middle-earth for much longer.\
\
'I will not delay your errand for personal reasons, ${PLAYER}. Radanir spoke to me of his plans. He learned that a war-band of Orcs from the Ettenmoors has established a camp within the Laenan Caves here in the Trollshaws, and sought to confront them. The Laenan Caves are in the north-west reaches of the Gladdalf, the wood-troll infested marsh of the North Trollshaws.'","Talk to Radanir","'I thought Radanir would still be here when my brother and I returned, but he had already gone again into the wild. It could be that the Elf-maid Elweleth will know where he planned to go. Speak with her by the horses here in Thorenhad.'","'The sons of Elrond have already left for Thorenhad to prepare for the coming journey. Elrohir did say that one of the Dúnedain, a Ranger named Radanir, was staying for a few days at their camp. As Thorenhad is nearest to Rivendell, you should travel there first to speak to Radanir before seeking the others.\
\
'I have met few of Aragorn's kin, but Radanir is known to me, for he journeys oft into the trackless Ettenmoors and often stays here in Rivendell. For a time, my brethren sought to convince him to join the company in song in the Hall of Fire, as Aragorn would, but Radanir would have none of it.\
\
'Travel to Thorenhad, north of the Bruinen Gorges in the Trollshaws, and speak to Elrohir. He will introduce you to Radanir. Once the Ranger is told of the messages from Lórien, you can seek out the others Master Elrond suggested.'","Defeat Laenan Orc-leader"},
[1850]={"Habla con Meneldir en el callejón entre los edificios de Musgovilla.","'Estamos siendo observados, ${PLAYER}. Alguien escucha nuestra conversación.'","'¿Viajarás al este, donde la carretera desde Enedwaith entra en Ciénaga de los Cisnes? La partida de incursión puede haber venido de allí y dejado algún rastro de su paso. Nos veremos de nuevo cuando ambos regresemos.'","El camino se extiende al noreste pasando Musgovilla y hacia Enedwaith. ¿Vinieron los Uruks de esa dirección?","Los cuerpos de los Uruks yacen en el camino donde entra en Ciénaga de los Cisnes desde Enedwaith.","Meneldir está en la plaza del pueblo de Musgovilla, esperando que regreses con noticias de la frontera con Enedwaith.","Recoge espadas Uruk caídas a lo largo del camino desde Enedwaith (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL}).","'Lleva las espadas que recogiste a Skardí. Debería poder fundirlas y darles un mejor uso que sus antiguos portadores.'","Este Uruk fue asesinado por una espada muy parecida a la que él mismo portaba.","'Creo que lo manejaste bastante bien, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo mío[m]|amiga mía[f]}... mejor de lo que yo lo habría hecho, en cualquier caso. Nunca he tenido mucha paciencia con los niños.\
\
'Planeo buscar más lejos alguna pista sobre el propósito de Saruman: ¿por qué enviaría trasgos y Uruks para atacar Musgovilla? No lo entiendo.\
\
'¿Viajarás al este, donde la carretera desde Enedwaith entra en Ciénaga de los Cisnes? La partida de incursión puede haber venido de allí y dejado algún rastro de su paso. Nos veremos de nuevo cuando ambos regresemos.'","'Esto lo sabemos con certeza: los Uruks que han llegado a Ciénaga de los Cisnes creen que lo hacen por orden de Saruman. Eso significa que el Mago Blanco no es digno de confianza.'\
\
Meneldir guarda silencio.\
\
'Estamos siendo observados, ${PLAYER}. Alguien escucha nuestra conversación.'","Tegwyn ha escuchado gran parte de tu conversación sobre Saruman y los Uruks.","'¿Qué? ¡No escuché nada que no debiera! Me dijiste que un aventurero debe estar atento a las necesidades de toda la buena gente, ¿y cómo puedo hacerlo si no mantengo los ojos y oídos abiertos?\
\
'Está bien, tal vez no dijiste EXACTAMENTE eso, ¡pero estoy seguro de que es cierto! Si un Mago está enviando trasgos y Uruks para atacar Musgovilla, ¿no deberíamos saberlo?'\
\
Le dices a Tegwyn que la mejor manera en que puede ayudar a la gente de su aldea es mantener su ánimo y ayudar a preparar las defensas.\
\
'De acuerdo. Haré lo que pueda, pero quiero que sepas que espero recibir misiones más peligrosas en los próximos días. ¡Soy un aventurero ahora, después de todo, y tú y Meneldir van a necesitar toda la ayuda posible, especialmente si nos enfrentamos a Magos y sus secuaces!'","'¿Más espadas Uruk? No pedí estas, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Bueno, supongo que Meneldir tiene razón. Las fundiré y las convertiré en armas para la defensa de Musgovilla. Nadie querrá usarlas tal como están ahora, pero el metal es metal, en mi experiencia.'","Uruks muertos yacen en el camino que entra en la Ciénaga de los Cisnes desde Enedwaith.","Lleva las espadas Uruk a Meneldir en la plaza del pueblo de Musgovilla.","Habla con Tegwyn en el callejón entre los edificios de Musgovilla.","Si los Uruks recién llegados a Ciénaga de los Cisnes están realmente al servicio del Mago Saruman, debes averiguar todo lo que puedas sobre su propósito y por qué los envió a esta tierra.","'Traes noticias interesantes, ${PLAYER}. Me parece que los Uruks discutieron entre ellos después de llegar a Ciénaga de los Cisnes. ¿Pero con qué propósito? La partida de guerra puede haber sido mucho más grande cuando viajó desde Enedwaith y dividirse en dos o más partidas de incursión al cruzar a Ciénaga de los Cisnes. ¿Quizá la decisión de atacar Musgovilla no fue del Mago sino de los propios Uruks? Es curioso.\
\
'En cuanto a las espadas que recogiste, quizá Skardí pueda fundirlas y darles un mejor uso que sus antiguos portadores.'","Libro 1, Capítulo 1: Al Servicio del Mago","Lleva las espadas Uruk a Skardí Doblafilos dentro de su tienda en Musgovilla.","'Espero recibir misiones más peligrosas en los próximos días. ¡Soy un aventurero ahora, después de todo, y tú y Meneldir van a necesitar toda la ayuda posible, especialmente si nos enfrentamos a Magos y sus secuaces!'","Meneldir querrá examinar las armas que portaban estos Uruks.","Meneldir está en un callejón entre edificios en Musgovilla.","Examina uno de los Uruks muertos a lo largo del camino.","Has reunido espadas Uruk caídas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL}).","Busca señales de los Uruks donde la carretera entra en Ciénaga de los Cisnes desde Enedwaith.","Skardí Doblafilos estará interesado en las espadas Uruk que recuperaste.\
\
Skardí siempre trabaja duro en su tienda de Musgovilla."},
[1851]={"'Aragorn must have had a good reason to take that road, but I cannot think of a single one. The Dead Men are not to be crossed lightly!'","'The grim northerners departed Dunharrow at first light, and did not stay to explain their course. I would think them cowardly had I not seen the road they took: south, along the Dimholt road. That way lies death.'\
\
You explain that Aragorn had his reasons for taking such a road, but Sídrac waves away your words.\
\
'I do not doubt he had reasons, friend, but it is clear his loyalty is not to Théoden King. We will have need of every man if we are to ride to Minas Tirith, as my King commands, and I see we are cheated of a powerful fighting force by Aragorn's choice. I count the chances of our success against the Enemy less and less with each sword he takes with him into the mountain. I saw the winged beast over Edoras. I know what dangers we face.'","Talk to Radwine at the camp in Dunharrow, by Éowyn","Éowyn is at the muster of the Rohirrim, at Dunharrow.\
\
You have spoken with some worried soldiers of the camp, and should return now to Éowyn.","Book 1, Chapter 1: The Muster of the Rohirrim","'I did not mean for it to go so far! We watched the men ride to the mountain in the morning, and then Elfdag challenged me to follow them, and I did the same to him, and before you could say 'Helm Hammerhand' we were right up to the Dark Door.\
\
'I returned to the camp after that, and I thought he followed at my heels... but now he is gone, and no one has seen him!'","Darláf shakes his head, but his mood is improved","Talk to Sídrac by the encampment's supplier","Talk to Éowyn at the camp in Dunharrow","Radwine is speaking to Éowyn at the camp in Dunharrow.","Talk to Darláf at the south-east road","'Men are still arriving at Dunharrow from all corners of the Mark, but I do not think it will be enough. I rode forth from the Hornburg, as my King commanded, and most hamlets and villages responded to his call with clear voices and proud hearts, but this day I see few of those who spoke loudest.\
\
'On my return from Forlaw, in Wildermore, I was beset by an Orc raiding party. The injuries I sustained will keep me from riding in my King's train, to my frustration and disappointment! Swords and spears need men to wield them, and that resource is in short supply. I say 'men,' but the blood of Théoden King's niece Éowyn burns for Rohan, and she would fight bravely for the kingdom, were it permitted.\
\
'Alas, it is not so, and the both of us will be kept from doing what we desire, for I am a man injured and she a woman unwounded. Unhappy fortunes!'","'It was just a game! I did not think he would go inside! S'truth!'","'This road leads to the Dwimorberg, friend. Why would anyone go to that Haunted Mountain, or tread the paths beneath it? That is not bravery! Only folly could lead my feet there.'\
\
You assure Darláf that Aragorn considers his reasons for braving that road sufficient, but the soldier shakes his head.\
\
'I hope he is not wrong, ${PLAYER}. It seems a great shame to allow a skilled warrior to disappear into such a place when we could use his talents elsewhere, at other battles.'","'We are plagued with ill fortune, ${PLAYER}! An encampment of this size is bound to attract the attention of children and others who live near, that much I expected. But I did not expect even children to act in such reckless, foolhardy fashion!\
\
'This boy tells me one of his friends, Elfdag, may have followed Aragorn into the Paths of the Dead! I thought it the mere boast of a child, but none have seen Elfdag today. I dispatched a number of men to find him, but they too have not returned.\
\
'Elfdag is the grandson of Elfhelm, ${PLAYER}. We cannot have lost him in this fashion!'","'Several of the Men saw Aragorn go, and speak words of despair. Find these Men and set their minds aright, if you can. And when you return, do the same for me, ${PLAYER}! I do not think you can, but I must wear a brave face for the Men and will not give in to sorrow, for their sake.'","Éowyn has called you to Dunharrow, where the muster of the Rohirrim is well underway. Troubles weigh heavily upon her brow, especially concerning your mutual friend Aragorn and a decision he has made of late.","'Troubles follow us like a storm-cloud, ${PLAYER}! Speak to Radwine and tell me they do not!'","Sídrac believes the fighting strength of Rohan is insufficient to aid Gondor","Bosa remains dissatisfied that his injury will keep him from war","'I would ride with my King anywhere, even along the Dimholt road. I am glad he does not wish to go that way! I do not doubt our destination will be as dangerous as Aragorn's passage, but I want to be sure to arrive as a living man!'","Darláf, Sídrac, and Bosa can be found at the encampment in Dunharrow, south of Éowyn's position.\
\
Éowyn has asked you to comfort some of the Men at the encampment in Dunharrow, for they heard of Aragorn's departure and have begun to question the wisdom of Théoden's ride to Minas Tirith.","'${PLAYER}! I am glad you have come with such haste, for these troubles weigh heavily upon me and I do not know how they may be o'erthrown! It is my uncle's choice to ride to Minas Tirith, and thereby satisfy the vows of his forefathers, but why should he not ride for Gondor with every sword he can command, either by oath or love? It is folly to allow proven warriors to abandon my uncle's course, lest it be doomed by their absence!\
\
'And yet, in the early hours, Aragorn and his kinsmen departed Dunharrow for the Paths of the Dead! He spoke of need, but I can see no need on that road, save that of a yawning tomb that hopes to be filled. The dead men of Dunharrow do not suffer the living to pass.\
\
'Several of the Men saw him go, and speak words of despair. Find these Men and set their minds aright, if you can. And when you return, do the same for me, ${PLAYER}! I do not think you can, but I must wear a brave face for the Men and will not give in to sorrow, for their sake.'","'I have the desire to ride with my King and fight at his side, but this injury will keep me from it! Must my sword and armour go to waste in this fashion?'","Talk to Bosa at the eastern camp-fire"},
[1852]={"Trancos está en su habitación de la Posada del Poney Pisador en Bree, que se encuentra girando a la izquierda por el pasillo que sale de la sala común hasta que sólo se puede girar a la derecha. La habitación está al final del pasillo, a la derecha de las escaleras.\
\
Terminada la amenaza de Amdir, deberías informar a Trancos y ver si hay algo más que quiera que hagas.","Habla con Trancos","Trancos te ha pedido que le ayudes a acabar de una vez por todas con el alboroto asesino de Amdir.","'El señor de los Duramano huyó a Bree tras su derrota, y no por mera casualidad. Veo la mano del Capitán de los Nueve en todos estos asuntos, en el oeste, en la Comarca y en las Tierras de Bree. Debemos desenredar el hilo de sus planes, y creo que sé cómo hacerlo.\
\
'En el este de Bree hay un campamento Montebruno que mis hombres han estado vigilando de cerca. Una sombra se ha extendido recientemente por el campamento... Creo que es aquí donde Amdir ha ido, y también este señor enano.\
\
'Allí debemos ir, y allí debemos acabar con la vida de Amdir, si es que aún se le puede llamar vida. Esperaremos a que caiga la noche y luego haremos nuestro movimiento contra los Montebruno. Habla conmigo de nuevo cuando estés ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para partir.'","'Me apena que el Enemigo haya podido convertir así a Amdir. Era mi amigo y pariente. Mi pueblo lo recordará como el hombre que una vez fue, bueno y noble.\
\
'Me preocupa que los Nazgûl hayan cruzado el Río y se hayan adentrado en las Tierras de Bree justo en este momento. Hay acontecimientos en marcha que podrían determinar el destino de la Tierra Media.\
\
'Si eres capaz y estás ${PLAYERNAME:dispuesto[m]|dispuesta[f]}, puede que tenga otra tarea para ti.'","'Informa a Trancos de lo que ha ocurrido.'","'¿Estás ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para partir? Si es así, cuando caiga la noche atacaremos el campamento donde se han escondido Amdir y el señor enano.'","Trancos está en su habitación de la Posada del Poney Pisador en Bree, que se encuentra girando a la izquierda por el pasillo que sale de la sala común hasta que sólo se puede girar a la derecha. La habitación está al final del pasillo, a la derecha de las escaleras.\
\
Al caer la noche, Trancos te guiará contra Amdir y los Montebruno.","Libro 1, Capítulo 1: Desenredando el Hilo","'Me temo que se avecinan tiempos oscuros para Eriador'","'¿Mis heridas? Se curarán, con el tiempo''"},
[1853]={"Book 1, Chapter 2: Experts on the Subject","Two of the helpful hobbits that helped Isteron with some of the wedding preparations are relaxing nearby: Frodo Baggins and Samwise Gamgee!","'Not everyone is as familiar with our hobbits as we are, ${PLAYER}.'","'There has been a lot of wedding chatter in the air, ${PLAYER}, and I'll have you know it's not the easiest thing for this Gamgee to talk about! Take that Isteron fellow. He spoke on and on about how grand this wedding should be, and how it'll be talked about for years and years, and maybe that's so, but I can't help but wonder if that's not the most important thing. Maybe I'm just a hobbit, with hobbit-ideas, but it seems to me that the wedding should be just as Arwen and Strider want it to be. Does it matter what the kingdom thinks of it, or for how long it's talked about?'\
\
Sam falls silent and sniffs the air.\
\
'Actually, now that I'm thinking about it, Mister Frodo and I weren't the only hobbits who spoke to the wedding planners. Merry and Pippin talked to them too, and when they finished they went off laughing, looking very pleased with themselves about something. It might be worth looking into, ${PLAYER}. Those two are always causing trouble of some kind or another, and if you follow the smell of their pipe-smoke, could be you'll get to the bottom of it!'","Legolas stands by the pile of blue decorations, and despite his solemn expression you can tell he is also rather amused at the hobbits' prank.","Pippin is atop the wall south-east of the Plaza of the Fountain in Minas Tirith (Midsummer), very pleased with some recent mischief.","'If you ask me, I'd wager those two are having a smoke and laughing at their mischief! Follow the smell of their pipes, ${PLAYER}, to the south-west!'","'We're real experts on the subject, you might say, so we gave Cúfaron a detailed account of the most important Shire wedding-traditions. It was the right thing to do, wasn't it, Pip? How did they go again?'","Frodo and Sam suggested that you follow the smell of pipe-smoke to find Merry and Pippin.\
\
Frodo and Sam provided some very helpful advice to Rodwen's wedding-planning friends, but Merry and Pippin seemed very amused about something, which strikes young Master Samwise as perhaps a troubling sign.","'Good day to you, ${PLAYER}! Why don't you stay awhile and have a smoke, there's room for all! What's on your mind, friend?'\
\
You ask Merry and Pippin about the preparations for the upcoming wedding, and they share a conspiratorial look before doubling-over with laughter. When Merry has once again caught his breath, he apologizes and tries to answer your question.\
\
'It's going to be a real sight to see, ${PLAYER}! It seemed to us that those wedding planners might not have actually been to a real wedding before, and you know Pip and I have been to plenty. We're real experts on the subject, you might say, so we gave Cúfaron a detailed account of the most important Shire wedding-traditions. It was the right thing to do, wasn't it, Pip? How did they go again?'","A faint smile flits across the Elf's face as he contemplates the pile of decorations, but he says nothing more.","You found the hobbits who helped Isteron: Frodo Baggins and Samwise Gamgee!","Examine the fruit of the hobbit's mischief at the base of the ramp from the Seventh Circle, in the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith (Midsummer)","Follow the smell of pipe-smoke to the south-west in order to find Merry and Pippin","'You are welcome to consult with the hobbits who helped me, if you like. I believe they are to the south of the Tower of Ecthelion.'","You need to find Cúfaron before it's too late","You have found a pair of amused hobbits, laughing and smoking","'Ah, you are here to help plan for the Great Wedding? There is so much still to be done, but do not let that frighten you away! I have often found that the largest tasks are the most rewarding, just so long as you do not give up before you are begun!'\
\
You ask Isteron if he needs any help researching wedding customs, and he blinks at you, the smile frozen on his face.\
\
'Oh no, I gave up on that,' he replies. 'Cúfaron and I did learn some interesting tidbits from a number of hobbits over there, but I did not find their advice very promising. Their hobbit-traditions felt very quaint to me, not at all appropriate for such a grand wedding as this must be, but you are welcome to consult with them, if you like. They are to the south of the Tower of Ecthelion, I believe.'","Find the helpful hobbits south of the Tower of Ecthelion in Minas Tirith (Midsummer)","'Something old, something new, something borrowed, everything blue!'","The decorations are indeed, as Merry and Pippin suggested, overwhelmingly blue","The fragrant smell of pipe-smoke lingers on the air. Merry and Pippin came this way!","'What a relief it is to hear you will help us! Every wedding should be perfect, of course, but the weight of responsibility for this particular wedding is even greater, for all the eyes of the kingdom will be upon it! It means a great deal to me that you will not betray our secret. With your help, it should not matter that my friends and I know so little about such preparations! Already I have sent them throughout the city to get whatever help they can.\
\
'Here, ${PLAYER}, I have penned some letters of introduction authorizing you to work on my behalf in all wedding-related matters. Bring these to our lore-master Isteron and he will tell you how best you can help us. You should find him outside the Tower of Ecthelion, in the Plaza of the Fountain.'","Talk to Legolas in the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith (Midsummer)","Cúfaron is in the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith (Midsummer).","Talk to Cúfaron in the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith (Midsummer)","Merry is atop the wall south-east of the Plaza of the Fountain in Minas Tirith (Midsummer), very pleased with some recent mischief.","Legolas speaks solemnly, but the son of Thranduil cannot completely mask his amusement.\
\
'Not everyone is as familiar with hobbits as we are, ${PLAYER}. Am I right to suggest that this must be the doing of a certain Brandybuck and Took of our acquaintance?'","'Something old, something new, something borrowed... and everything blue!\
\
'I think he was going to collect everything in the Sixth Circle, ${PLAYER}, right by the base of the ramp from the Seventh!'","'Bring those letters to our lore-master Isteron and he will tell you how best you can help us. You should find him outside the Tower of Ecthelion, in the Plaza of the Fountain.'","'Those hobbits weren't really wedding experts at all, were they?' he asks, staring wearily at the pile of blue decorations gathered from all around the city.\
\
'Not really experts at all. There's a lot of that going around these days.'","Isteron is outside the Tower of Ecthelion, in the Plaza of the Fountain, in Minas Tirith (Midsummer).\
\
Rodwen gave you some letters of introduction authorizing you to act on her behalf, and directed you to deliver them to her friend and ally Isteron.","Bring the letters of introduction to Isteron in the Plaza of the Fountain in Minas Tirith (Midsummer)","'Sam is right. The more amused with themselves our friends are, the more trouble they are likely to cause! I do think they have probably settled down somewhere to have a smoke and review the mischief they might have caused.'","Rodwen asked you to help her with the final preparations for the Great Wedding, and out of respect for the bride and the groom you have agreed to do what you can.","'${PLAYER}! How nice to see you during a time of celebration and not during time of war!'\
\
You tell Frodo that you are helping Rodwen and her companions with the preparations for the Great Wedding, and he nods thoughtfully.\
\
'That is very good of you. Aragorn is dear to me, and I want his wedding to be all for which he and his bride might hope. Are Rodwen and her companions up for such a challenge? I have spoken with a number of them now, and in each of these planners I admit to you I have recognized something.'\
\
He smiles knowingly.\
\
'They are in over their heads, just as I was during the Quest of the Ring! Just as were we all. Well, that turned out all right, in the end. So too might the wedding ceremony! If there is anything we can do, ${PLAYER}, let us know and we will help.'","Talk to Peregrin Took in Minas Tirith (Midsummer)","Talk to Samwise Gamgee in Minas Tirith (Midsummer)","Merry and Pippin, quite delighted with themselves, have caused some mischief. You should find Cúfaron at the base of the ramp from the Seventh Circle, in the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith (Midsummer), and see if it is too late to undo their handiwork.","Talk to Frodo Baggins in Minas Tirith (Midsummer)","'Well, Merry, everyone knows that in a Shire wedding you've got to follow the traditions. There are four elements that must be present if the ceremony is to be a success. The bride needs to carry or wear something old, right? And then she should pair it with something new, which represents the new life she's starting with her husband...'\
\
Merry nods solemnly, which causes Pippin to break out into laughter again before resuming.\
\
'...and then she needs something borrowed as well, maybe a garment or a cloth or a small pocket item of some kind, and then, most important of all... everything has to be blue!'\
\
The two hobbits start laughing again, and through their gales of laughter you can just make out gasps of 'everything blue! All the decorations, everything, they've got to be blue!'","Talk to Meriadoc Brandybuck in Minas Tirith (Midsummer)","Follow the smell of pipe-smoke to the south-east in order to find Merry and Pippin"},
[1854]={"Libro 1, Capítulo 2: Comienzo de una Gran Aventura","La mayoría de los aventureros comienzan con humildes inicios, y pocos pueden ver al principio cuán grandiosa será su aventura.","Habla con Tegwyn dentro de la herrería de Musgovilla.","Skardí Doblafilos te pidió que recolectaras colmillos de jabalí, garras de crébain y piedras afiladas que pueda usar para diversos fines en el pueblo.","Busca fuera del perímetro de Musgovilla alguna señal del niño desaparecido.","Las huellas son antiguas, probablemente hechas durante el ataque Uruk a Musgovilla.","'Podría usar varios objetos para reponer mis provisiones mientras sigues investigando el asunto de la partida de incursión, ${PLAYER}: piedras afiladas, colmillos de jabalí y garras de crébain.\
\
'¿Y crees que podrías hacer algo con Tegwyn? Me ha estado molestando con preguntas desde esta mañana, y necesito terminar este trabajo.'","'¿Tegwyn está desaparecido? No sería la primera vez que el niño busca problemas... pero con Uruks y trasgos cerca, podría haberse metido en algo serio esta vez.'","Skardí Doblafilos espera en su tienda en Musgovilla los objetos que recogiste.","'Estoy listo para una tarea de aventura más importante, ${PLAYER}. ¿Qué puedo hacer para ayudar al pueblo? ¿Puedo ir contigo?'\
\
Reacio a enviar al niño al peligro, le pides que patrulle la empalizada exterior de Musgovilla.\
\
'De acuerdo. Supongo que puedo hacer eso. ¿Quizá pueda acompañarte más tarde?'","Skardí Doblafilos te dijo que Tegwyn nunca volvió a su casa, y deberías revisar el perímetro del pueblo para encontrar al niño desaparecido.","Habla con Merion junto a la puerta este de Musgovilla.","Has reunido colmillos de jabalí (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL}).","'Lo último que supe, lo enviaste a explorar el borde del pueblo, así que te toca ir a buscarlo. Devuélvelo con sus padres antes de que vuelvan a molestarme, ¿de acuerdo?'","Debes informar a uno de los guardias cercanos que Tegwyn está desaparecido de Musgovilla.","Huellas pisotean la tierra aquí en las afueras de Musgovilla.","'Patrullaré las empalizadas, pero tal vez más adelante pueda acompañarte.'","Recoge colmillos de jabalí a lo largo del Viejo Camino del Sur (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL}).","Has reunido piedras afiladas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL}).","'Gracias por estos objetos, ${PLAYER}, pero quiero que sepas esto: ¡estoy bastante molesto contigo! Todo lo que quiero es que me dejen en paz, libre para hacer mi trabajo, pero la gente entra constantemente aquí, interrumpiéndome y retrasando mi labor. La madre de ese niño acaba de venir, Wenna, y dice que no ha vuelto a casa.\
\
'Lo último que supe, lo enviaste a explorar el borde del pueblo, así que te toca ir a buscarlo. Devuélvelo con sus padres antes de que vuelvan a molestarme, ¿de acuerdo?'","Recoge garras de crébain a lo largo del Viejo Camino del Sur (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL}).","Has reunido garras de crébain (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL}).","Tegwyn ha estado molestando a Skardí Doblafilos toda la mañana, y el herrero quiere que hagas algo al respecto.","Recoge piedras afiladas a lo largo del Viejo Camino del Sur (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL}).","Lleva los colmillos, las garras y las piedras afiladas a Skardí Doblafilos en su tienda.","'Necesito piedras afiladas, colmillos de jabalí y garras de crébain para reponer mis provisiones. Pero primero, ¿puedes hacer algo con Tegwyn? Me ha estado molestando con preguntas desde esta mañana, y necesito terminar este trabajo.'"},
[1855]={"You rescued Elfdag from the Paths of the Dead and should speak to him at the camp in Dunharrow.","Elfdag is safe, but his words raise further questions","Radwine is at the camp in Dunharrow, by Éowyn.\
\
Radwine has asked you to dare the darkness of the Paths of the Dead in search of his friend Elfdag.","Book 1, Chapter 2: The Ruthless Dead","Talk to Éowyn at the camp in Dunharrow","'I am not afraid, ${PLAYER}! I will bring you to the Dark Door and I will wait outside for you! I hope you are able to find Elfdag!'","'You are not going to tell my grandfather, are you? I had everything in hand, but I am certain he would not think so. If you tell him of this adventure of mine he is bound to lock me up in Underharrow, and the wife of the Thane does not appreciate young lads or lasses underfoot! She always scowls when she sees my friends and me about... I daresay we would be safer 'neath the Dwimorberg than in the house of Ellen Fremedon!'\
\
Elfdag's expression is one of horrified fear, and you quickly assure him that he will keep his freedom if he tells you what he saw.\
\
'Well, it was dark, and there were shadows flitting all about. But if you really strained your ears, you could hear whispers and sighs: the voices of the Dead. I gathered from their talk that a Man had come through hours before, and claimed he could free them from their curse. Some of the Dead followed him, and left in his wake... but others of the Dead did not believe his claim, and they stayed behind. These are especially cruel, and they have abandoned any hope of escaping the curse; these are now the Ruthless Dead, and they hate the living and the Dead alike.'\
\
Elfdag shivers.\
\
'I suppose I am glad to be back above-ground, after all.'","'You are a hero, are you not? I overheard some of the men speaking of your deeds, and by their account you seem an accomplished adventurer! If I bring you to the entrance, will you enter the mountain and search for Elfdag? I will not follow you in... I promise!\
\
'Let me know if you are ready, and I will bring you to the place. If you have a Fellowship of like-minded adventurers, bring them along too... I daresay there will be a place for them as well!'","'I cannot believe that Elfdag really braved the Dwimorberg! I thought he would turn up hiding in back of one of the tents of the encampment!'\
\
Radwine suddenly blanches.\
\
'What I mean to say is... when I told you he might have passed the Dark Door, I absolutely believed that was true. Maybe. Well he is safe, and so are you! There is no reason to be upset.'","Talk to Elfdag at the camp in Dunharrow","Talk to Radwine at Dunharrow and he will bring you to the Paths of the Dead","'You have exceeded your reputation this day, ${PLAYER}! I did not relish the thought of telling Elfhelm that his grandson had disappeared beneath the Haunted Mountain. Perhaps I would have had my brother do it.'\
\
Éowyn thinks for a moment, and then nods.\
\
'Yes. But his grumbling would have been insufferable.'","Elfhelm's grandson Elfdag may have foolishly entered the Paths of the Dead, and Éowyn wants you to save him, if he can be saved.","'It was dark beneath the Mountain, and there were shadows flitting all about. But if you really strained your ears, you could hear whispers and sighs: the voices of the Dead. I gathered from their talk that a Man had come through hours before, and claimed he could free them from their curse. Some of the Dead followed him, and left in his wake... but others of the Dead did not believe his claim, and they stayed behind. These are especially cruel, and they have abandoned any hope of escaping the curse; these are now the Ruthless Dead, and they hate the living and the Dead alike.'","'So Elfdag really braved the Dwimorberg! I thought he would turn up hiding in back of one of the tents of the encampment!'\
\
Radwine suddenly blanches.\
\
'What I mean to say is... when I told you he might have passed the Dark Door, I absolutely believed that was true. Maybe. Well he is safe, and so are you! There is no reason to be upset.'","Éowyn is at the encampment in Dunharrow."},
[1856]={"'Ah, hola, ¿hay algo en lo que pueda ayudarte? ¿Dices que los Montebruno han sido derrotados y dispersados? Son buenas noticias para Combe.\
\
'¿Así que ese Montaraz, Trancos, cree que deberíamos investigar el antiguo escondite de Zorrillero? Bueno, no estoy tan seguro. He oído que no es un lugar seguro.'","Mientras Trancos se ocupa de algunos viajeros importantes que está esperando, te ha pedido que viajes a Combe y ayudes al condestable Sotomonte a asegurarse de que la amenaza de los Montebruno ha llegado a su fin.","'Tengo curiosidad por saber quién era el enano que encontraste en el campamento de los Montebruno. Los enanos son honorables por naturaleza y no pueden ser dominados por la voluntad de nadie. No sé por qué éste serviría al Enemigo. Peor aún es la aparición de los Nazgûl. Debo ir a vigilar el Camino del Este, pues espero a algunos viajeros y ahora temo que puedan estar en peligro.\
\
'¿Viajarías a Combe y hablarías con un condestable llamado Sotomonte?. Quizá ya lo conozcas... un tipo pequeño y robusto que merodea por el centro de la ciudad. Puedes sugerirle a Sotomonte que investigue el viejo escondite de los Montebruno.\
\
'Cuando eso esté hecho, regresa aquí con tu informe. Si por casualidad no estoy aquí, asume lo peor.'","El condestable Sotomonte merodea a menudo por el centro de Combe, al este y al norte de Bree.\
\
Trancos te ha informado de que tiene un asunto importante que atender, pero te ha pedido que vayas a Combe y animes al Condestable Sotomonte a investigar el antiguo escondite de los bandidos.","'Tengo asuntos urgentes que atender, pero si buscas al condestable Sotomonte en Combe, quizá quiera investigar el antiguo escondite de los Montebruno.'","Libro 1, Capítulo 2: En Ayuda de un Condestable"},
[1857]={"'My fireworks? Ah, I am sorry, ${PLAYER}, but you may remember that it was a time of war until very recently! When Shadowfax bore me hither with young Peregrin Took, I did not have the luxury to bring any fireworks along with me.'\
\
You apologize for disturbing him, and the Wizard raises his eyebrows at you with apparent amusement.\
\
'Are you always in such a rush that you cannot wait for an old man to finish speaking? I said I did not bring any fireworks with me on the ride from Rohan. I did not say I no longer possessed any! Indeed, I have collected one or two such devices during the time since the war ended, and I have stored them in a small crate in my quarters. Now, there are not as many as I would like; it was my custom when lighting such crackers in the Shire to really fill the night sky with illumination. That was both for the delight of the hobbits and for my own, if I am speaking honestly.\
\
'But perhaps the few crackers I have assembled will still bring some small measure of enjoyment to the attendees of the wedding, ${PLAYER}. Go to my quarters in the High Guest-house in the Seventh Circle and empty the crate of its contents, and I will see what can be done.'","You retrieve Elf-fountains, which fall from the sky like gently shimmering rain","'Ah, there we are. I am sorry there were so few fireworks to gather up, my friend.'\
\
You express your surprise that the Wizard could count such an armful of fireworks as merely a few. When Mithrandir responds, it is with a twinkle in his eye and laughter in his voice.\
\
'You must have never seen one of my fireworks displays before, ${PLAYER}. These few will have to do.'","'Perhaps the few crackers I have assembled will still bring some small measure of enjoyment to the attendees of the wedding, ${PLAYER}. Go to my quarters in the High Guest-house in the Seventh Circle and empty the crate of its contents, and I will see what can be done.'","Take more fireworks out of the crate","You retrieve a few assorted squibs from the crate; not that impressive, but still important","You retrieve dwarf-candles, known for their angular shapes and geometric precision","Mithrandir is in the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith (Midsummer).\
\
Cúfaron is hopeful that some of Merry and Pippin's chatter may have had a kernel of truth, and he wants you to find the wizard of whose fireworks they spoke.","'I need to come up with a good use for these decorations. There has to be something! But now I have a more urgent worry: was any of the advice those hobbits gave to me truthful? They spoke of someone called Gandalf, a Wizard they claimed to be in this very city, and said his fireworks cannot be missed. Is it true?'\
\
You assure Cúfaron that Gandalf is indeed a master of the art, and his fireworks have a truly remarkable reputation for excellence. You say he has likely heard of the Wizard before, for in these lands he goes by another name.\
\
'Mithrandir? Ah, yes! I know of this Wizard, although I did not know he dabbled in the construction of fireworks. Perhaps you can find him for me and ask if he will contribute some of his finest creations to set off during the wedding ceremony? I saw him recently in this Circle of the city. Look for him to the west.'","There couldn't possibly be more, could there? Take more fireworks from the crate","Talk to Mithrandir in the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith (Midsummer)","Bring the impressive collection of fireworks to Mithrandir in the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith (Midsummer)","Mithrandir is in the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith (Midsummer).\
\
You have retrieved a truly impressive amount of fireworks from Mithrandir's quarters, and should now bring them to the Wizard.","The crate of fireworks is in Mithrandir's quarters in the High Guest-house in the Seventh Circle.\
\
Mithrandir did not specify which of the fireworks to bring to him. Better take everything out of the crate, just to be safe!","Gandalf's crate of fireworks is in his quarters","You retrieve goblin-barkers, which explode with harsh goblin-like cries","Take even more fireworks out of the crate","Take some more fireworks out of the crate","Why stop now? Take additional fireworks out of the crate","You retrieve thunder-claps, which have previously been mistaken for actual thunderstorms","Cúfaron is trying to sort out the good advice he received from Merry and Pippin from the bad. He hopes their words concerning 'Gandalf's fireworks' can be believed.","How many could there be? Take even more fireworks from the crate","'I did not know Mithrandir dabbled in the construction of fireworks. Perhaps you can find him for me and ask if he will contribute some of his finest creations to set off during the wedding ceremony? I saw him recently in this Circle of the city. Look for him to the west.'","You are a little disappointed to find the crate is now empty","Mithrandir told you he has assembled quite a stock of fireworks during the days following the end of the war, and he keeps them in a crate in his quarters in the High Guest-house, located in the Seventh Circle.","Book 1, Chapter 3: A Little Wizard-Magic","You retrieve a few hand-held sparklers from where they rolled into the crate's corners","Take fireworks out of the crate","Find Gandalf's quarters in the High Guest-house in the Seventh Circle of Minas Tirith (Midsummer)"},
[1858]={"Habla con el Condestable Sotomonte","'Bueno, supongo que tienes razón. Debo asegurarme de que esos Montebruno no se esconden de nuevo en esa cueva suya, reuniendo sus fuerzas. Pero necesitaré ayuda.\
\
'Viajarás conmigo al viejo escondite de Zorrillero. Está al sur de la casa del guardián, en el extremo noreste del Estanque de Entibo, cerca de las Cataratas de Entibo. Si se están reuniendo allí, ¡necesitaré ayuda para expulsarlos de nuevo! Cuando estés ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]}, vuelve, e iremos juntos al viejo escondite.'","A petición de Trancos, has viajado a Combe para ayudar al Condestable Sotomonte a investigar si los bandidos de Montebruno han dejado realmente de ser una amenaza para el pueblo del bosque de Chet.","El antiguo escondite de los Montebruno se encuentra al sur del cuerpo de guardia de Combe, cerca de las Cataratas de Entibo, en el extremo noreste del estanque de Entibo.\
\
El condestable Sotomonte ha decidido que probablemente sea buena idea echar un vistazo al antiguo escondite de los Montebruno, para asegurarse de que no vuelven a reunirse allí. Sin embargo, te ha pedido que le acompañes.","'Muy bien, estoy listo para partir. ¿Y tú?'","Habla con el Condestable Sotomonte.\
\
Te has infiltrado en el escondite de los Montebruno y has derrotado a varios de ellos, a petición del Condestable Sotomonte.","Libro 1, Capítulo 3: Montebruno Debilitados","'¡Buen espectáculo! ¡Buen espectáculo! ¡Les habéis dado una lección a esos granujas de Montebruno!'"},
[1859]={"Habla con Meneldir en Lhan Garan.","¡Has encontrado a Tegwyn en el Aguaestancada!","Busca a Tegwyn más al oeste en el Aguaestancada.","'Estoy aquí... estoy aquí, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'¡Tus lecciones de aventura no estaban completas! No mencionaste lo frío y húmedo que sería, ni cuántas cosas intentarían matarme. Me mantuve alejado de los avanc, porque no soy tonto, ¡pero incluso las tortugas aquí intentaron morderme!\
\
'Aun así... fue toda una aventura, para ser la primera. Si planeas regañarme, olvídalo... porque aprendí algo importante. ¡Sé adónde van los Uruks!'","Habla con Meneldir junto a la espada de madera abandonada en el Aguaestancada.","Visita Lhan Garan en el borde oriental del Aguaestancada y averigua si hubo alguna señal de Tegwyn.","'Esto parece ser la espada de Tegwyn...\
\
'Eso no es una buena señal, ${PLAYER}. Vamos a <rgb=#00FF00>escuchar</rgb> una vez más y esperemos que esta vez oigamos algo. Puede que no le quede mucho tiempo.'","Merion te dijo que los niños del pueblo tienen prohibido aventurarse en el Aguaestancada... lo que hace muy probable que haya sido el destino de Tegwyn.","Meneldir te pidió que <rgb=#00FF00>escucharas</rgb> a Tegwyn.","Busca a Tegwyn al noroeste en el Aguaestancada.","Escuchaste una voz débil llamándote desde el noroeste en el Aguaestancada. ¿Es Tegwyn?","Escuchas, muy débilmente, a alguien llamándote desde el noroeste.","Meneldir ha llegado a Lhan Garan, en el borde del Aguaestancada.","Una espada de madera gastada se encuentra en el barro.","Meneldir está en el centro del Aguaestancada, al oeste de Colmillar.","Esto parece ser la espada de Tegwyn, abandonada en el Aguaestancada.","'Nada.\
\
'Continuemos nuestra búsqueda más al oeste.'","La aldea dúnlendina de Lhan Garan está al noreste de Musgovilla, en el lado oriental del Aguaestancada. Sería un buen lugar para comenzar a buscar a Tegwyn.","Meneldir ha llegado a Lhan Garan antes que tú.","'¡Aquí estoy!'","'Hay criaturas en el Aguaestancada que no desearían nada más que convertir en cena a cualquiera que se acerque demasiado a su dominio. Las más peligrosas son los avanc, y deberíamos cazarlos mientras buscamos al chico.'","'¿Ninguna señal de Tegwyn? Yo tampoco he visto nada. Fui entrenado en el arte del rastreo, pero esta ciénaga ha puesto a prueba mis habilidades.\
\
'Vamos a <rgb=#00FF00>escuchar</rgb> algún sonido del chico. Debemos usar todos nuestros sentidos en esta búsqueda.'","<rgb=#00FF00>Escucha</rgb> a Tegwyn.","Has encontrado una espada de madera gastada abandonada en el barro del Aguaestancada.","Habla con Tegwyn en las zonas noroeste del Aguaestancada.","'Hola.'","Derrota avanc en el Aguaestancada (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Escuchas sonidos de vida en la ciénaga, pero nada fuera de lo común.","Libro 1, Capítulo 3: Entre el Barro y la Humedad","'Debes seguir el camino hacia el noreste hasta la aldea dúnlendina de Lhan Garan. Está en el lado oriental del Aguaestancada, y sus exploradores pueden haber visto al chico. Quizá fue a hablar con los aldeanos dúnlendinos allí, y ahora mismo disfruta de su hospitalidad o sus historias. No debemos apresurarnos a juzgar; puede que no esté en peligro en absoluto.'","Meneldir sugirió que continúes la búsqueda de Tegwyn más al oeste.","'Vamos a <rgb=#00FF00>escuchar</rgb> algún sonido del chico. Debemos usar todos nuestros sentidos en esta búsqueda.'","Has encontrado a Tegwyn en el Aguaestancada, sano y salvo.","Los avanc en el Aguaestancada serían un verdadero peligro para Tegwyn. Derrotar a cualquiera que encuentres solo puede ayudar en tus esfuerzos de rescate.","'¿Es Tegwyn? ¡Alguien llama desde el noroeste!'","'Vamos a <rgb=#00FF00>escuchar</rgb> una vez más y esperemos que esta vez oigamos algo. Puede que no le quede mucho tiempo.'","Meneldir se ha unido a ti en el Aguaestancada junto a una espada de madera abandonada.","Habla con Meneldir en el Aguaestancada, al oeste de Colmillar.","Has derrotado avanc en el Aguaestancada (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL}).","Examina la espada de madera abandonada.","Habla con Meneldir en el centro del Aguaestancada, al oeste de Colmillar.","'Escuché que Tegwyn ha desaparecido, ${PLAYER}. Con Uruks en Ciénaga de los Cisnes, pensé que lo más prudente era comenzar la búsqueda lo antes posible.\
\
'Dicho esto, si realmente se ha dirigido al Aguaestancada, creo que los Uruks pueden ser el menor de sus problemas. El terreno allí es inestable, y como cualquier ciénaga, la profundidad de las pozas puede ser engañosa. Hay criaturas en el Aguaestancada que no desearían nada más que convertir en cena a cualquiera que se acerque demasiado a su dominio. Las más peligrosas son los avanc, y deberíamos cazarlos mientras buscamos al chico.'","'Dices que el chico podría haber encontrado huellas de Uruks que llevan al norte. Si va por allí, es probable que se adentre en el Aguaestancada. Los niños del pueblo tienen prohibido ir allí, pero no te diré que eso ha impedido que los más aventureros exploren esa ciénaga. Si Tegwyn intentó seguir el rastro de los Uruks allí... bueno, ¡hay muchos peligros en el Aguaestancada, sin contar nuestros problemas recientes!\
\
'Debes seguir el camino hacia el noreste hasta la aldea dúnlendina de Lhan Garan. Está en el lado oriental del Aguaestancada, y sus exploradores pueden haber visto al chico. Quizá fue a hablar con los aldeanos dúnlendinos allí, y ahora mismo disfruta de su hospitalidad o sus historias. No debemos apresurarnos a juzgar; puede que no esté en peligro en absoluto.'"},
[1860]={"With great relief, you emerge from the cave. Now you must find a settlement","Defeat frenzied or maddened creatures throughout the Blackroot Vale (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'If this other group, these Ruthless Dead, have forever cast their lot in with Sauron, then Aragorn will have no safety from them. Neither will the folk of Gondor, and our friends' passage may have planted a dangerous seed in the minds of the Ruthless Dead: with no hope of redemption, what reason is there to remain within the Mountain? If you have no desire to atone for your evils, what would prevent you from adding to the number of your sins?\
\
'I ask you to travel the Paths of the Dead, ${PLAYER}, and by that way come into Gondor. The people there must be protected, and if they cannot be saved from the threat of the Ruthless Dead they must flee to a place of safety, if any still exists in this world.'","The cold air hangs heavily in the great open space","'You must be mighty indeed to have braved the paths under the mountain! Follow the road and it will bring you to the hilltop on which sits Morlad, my home. Help my people in any way you can and I will be most grateful to you.'","A man waves his greeting, and calls for your attention","Celegdal is at the entrance to Morlad, in the Blackroot Vale.\
\
You have defeated frenzied creatures in the Vale and should now return to Celegdal.","Journey to the Dark Door, the entrance to the Paths of the Dead","Buildings built by those who are Dead can be found beneath the Haunted Mountain, Dwimorberg.\
\
Éowyn has charged you with travelling the Paths of the Dead and coming by that way into Gondor, where she asks that you protect the people of Gondor from the threat posed by the Ruthless Dead.","The Paths of the Dead lead beneath the Haunted Mountain, Dwimorberg, to the Blackroot Vale.\
\
Éowyn has charged you with travelling the Paths of the Dead and coming by that way into Gondor, where she asks that you protect the people of Gondor from the threat posed by the Ruthless Dead.","'Thank you for the assistance, ${PLAYER}. I do not know what has caused this madness in the birds and beasts of the Vale, but there have been strange happenings here of late. If we learn the truth of them, we may learn what has so disturbed the creatures as well.\
\
'I have heard whisperings on the wind. Whispers of Death.'","Motivated by her concern for Aragorn and Elfdag's report of the Ruthless Dead, Éowyn has suggested a new course for you to follow.","Come safely through the Paths of the Dead to the Blackroot Vale","'It would ease my mind some if you could defeat a number of the frenzied creatures in the Vale, or the bears and beasts that might turn that way next. We might speak again once that is done.'","The town of Morlad is on a hill on the western side of the Blackroot Vale.\
\
Éowyn has charged you with protecting the people of Gondor from any threat posed by the Ruthless Dead.","Find the hilltop settlement of Morlad, in the Blackroot Vale","Book 1, Chapter 3: The Whisper of Death","'If you are a friend of Gondor, welcome to Morlad! If you are not, listen to my words and hasten your feet elsewhere. We have troubles enough in the Vale without your adding to them.\
\
'Strange things have been happening here of late, and it has stirred in the creatures of the Vale a form of madness. I could not say what has caused it, but I know the creatures are oft driven into a frenzy when approached. I have seen beasts cast themselves at the very walls of Morlad for no reason at all, doing themselves great injury in the process. Do you want to know what I think? I think it is the whisper of Death that has done this. But let us not speak of that now.\
\
'It is but a matter of time before one of the beasts is driven into the heart of the city. It would ease my mind some if you could defeat a number of the frenzied creatures in the Vale, or the bears and birds that might be next. We might speak again once that is done.'","Talk to Celegdal at the entrance to Morlad","Cold dread grips your heart as you approach the Dark Door once again","Defeated a frenzied creature (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Journey through the Paths of the Dead beneath the Dwimorberg","The Dark Door is south-east of the camp at Dunharrow.\
\
Éowyn has charged you with travelling the Paths of the Dead and coming by that way into Gondor, where she asks that you protect the people of Gondor from the threat posed by the Ruthless Dead.","Celegdal has asked you to defeat frenzied or maddened creatures throughout the Blackroot Vale, especially near the town of Morlad, including any creatures that might be susceptible.","'Elfdag's adventure beneath the Dwimorberg may have been ill-advised, but it has given us warning of a new danger. Aragorn has passed into Gondor, and it seems from Elfdag's report that he is followed by some number of the Dead that believe he can offer them redemption. I cannot say if it be true or if it be false, but as long as the Dead Men believe it, Aragorn need not fear them.\
\
'But this other group, these Ruthless Dead... if they have forever cast their lot in with Sauron, then Aragorn will have no safety from them. Neither will the folk of Gondor, and our friends' passage may have planted a dangerous seed in the minds of the Ruthless Dead: with no hope of redemption, what reason is there to remain within the Mountain? If you have no desire to atone for your evils, what would prevent you from adding to the number of your sins?\
\
'I ask you to travel the Paths of the Dead, ${PLAYER}, and by that way come into Gondor. The people there must be protected, and if they cannot be saved from the threat of the Ruthless Dead they must flee to a place of safety, if any still exists in this world.'","A man has called for your attention at the entrance to Morlad, in the Blackroot Vale."},
[1861]={"'If you have the stomach for it, a journey to the Hill of Erech might reveal if my supposition is true. If something did come out of the dark reaches under the mountains, I feel certain that is where it would have gone. It has always been an ill-omened place.'","Mortal men stood here, and not long ago. Their booted footprints remain.","A sudden shout breaks the stillness. 'You there! What is your business here?'","Someone has seen you, silhouetted against the sky atop the Hill of Erech!","Celegdal thinks some great evil came out of the mountains and lingered at the Hill of Erech. He does not know the details, or how close to the truth his theory may prove...","The Hill of Erech is east of Morlad, in the Blackroot Vale.\
\
Celegdal believes that a great evil came out of the mountains and went to the Hill of Erech, and wants you to see if it is true.","Someone saw you while you searched the summit of Erech, and called out to you. You should descend the hill and see if this person is a friend.","Examine patches of disturbed earth atop Erech (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Journey to the summit of the Hill of Erech, east of Morlad","If the Dead did gather here, tracks in the dirt show they were not alone","The ground here boasts many small depressions; men stood here, and recently","You have been seen against the sky atop the Hill of Erech!","'Do you want to know what this honest man of Morlad believes? You may think me a fool, but I feel certain that some great evil came out of the mountains and sped with unnatural haste through the Vale. On moonless nights, some claim to have seen the Dead dancing atop the Hill of Erech, east of here. Is it true? I cannot speak to that, but I will tell you that no one in Morlad leaves his door unbarred when the time comes to blow out his candles.\
\
'You are more brave than I am, ${PLAYER}, that much is certain! If you have the stomach for it, a journey to the Hill of Erech might reveal if my supposition is true. If something did come out of the dark reaches under the mountains, I feel certain that is where it would have gone. It has always been an ill-omened place.'","'I did not mean to startle you, but judging from your look you have seen your own share of surprises. You may be a seasoned adventurer, but I daresay what I beheld in the reaches of the night would make your blood run cold, as it did mine.\
\
'From afar I heard the blast of a great horn, and then a multitude of horns in echoing answer. I felt then the gathering of a great company of shadows all about the Stone atop this hill. A group of horsemen stood there, and their leader was grim of face and stern of countenance. Flesh and blood treated with the shadows, and though I could not understand the words, his purpose was plain enough. The company's grim leader charged the Dead with a task, and when the dawn came they departed.\
\
'I feel no shame when I tell you I hid myself as they passed, for the men of this company were as real as you or me, but in their train travelled countless shadows. This man commanded the Dead to follow, and follow him they did, down from Erech, through Tarlang's Neck, to where I do not know. I fear great evil has come to the kingdom I serve, Gondor that I love.'","The earth atop the Hill of Erech has been disturbed, and bears investigation.","Book 1, Chapter 4: Atop Erech","Descend the hill and find the man who called out to you"},
[1862]={"Trancos está en su habitación de la Posada del Poney Pisador en Bree, que se encuentra girando a la izquierda por el pasillo que sale de la sala común hasta que sólo puedes girar a la derecha. La habitación está al final del pasillo a la derecha de las escaleras.\
Deberías Volver a Trancos y contarle lo que has aprendido sobre los Montebruno y el Enano Pálido.","'Buenos días. ¿Qué hacéis todavía por aquí? Esos Montebruno se han ido, y probablemente para siempre. Ese extraño Enano puede que todavía esté por aquí, pero apuesto a que se fue a algún sitio un poco más interesante.\
\
'Deberías llevarle esa noticia a tu amigo Trancos en Bree. Si te envió aquí, ¡probablemente quiera saber lo que hemos encontrado! Probablemente estará en el Poney Pisador. A esos Montaraces seguro que les gusta su cerveza, ¡y el Poney tiene la mejor!'","'Buenos días. ¿Qué hacéis todavía por aquí? Esos Montebruno se han ido, y probablemente para siempre. Ese extraño enano puede que todavía esté por aquí, pero apuesto a que se fue a algún sitio un poco más interesante.\
\
'Deberías llevarle esas noticias a tu amigo Trancos en Bree. Si te envió aquí, ¡probablemente quiera saber lo que hemos encontrado! Probablemente estará en el Poney Pisador. A esos Montaraces seguro que les gusta su cerveza, ¡y el Poney tiene la mejor!\
\
'Gracias por tu ayuda, pero ya no tiene sentido preocuparse por los bandidos de por aquí.'","Libro 1, Capítulo 4: Diseños Oscuros","'¡Vaya! Tienes mal aspecto, sin ánimo de ofender. ¿Necesitas una cerveza? ¿No?\
\
'Bueno, si buscas a ese Montaraz, Trancos, está en su habitación. Ve por el pasillo de la izquierda y gira a la derecha al final.'","'¡Has vuelto y justo a tiempo! Han pasado muchas cosas desde que te fuiste, pero tengo poco tiempo para relatarlas. Las noticias que me has traído serán de gran utilidad para mis hombres aquí en las Tierras de Bree, pero hay una amenaza más inmediata de la que debemos ocuparnos ahora.\
\
'Mientras estabas fuera, esos mismos Nazgûl que viste con Amdir atacaron el Poney. Iban en busca de los viajeros que había estado esperando, cuatro hobbits de la Comarca. No puedo decirte por qué tenían tanto interés en mis compañeros, pero puedo decirte que volveré a necesitar tu ayuda.'","Gracias a un bandido moribundo en el antiguo escondite de Zorrillero, supiste que el extraño Enano Pálido estaba intentando intimidar a los Montebruno para que continuaran su alianza con el Reino Brujo de Angmar."},
[1863]={"'Esas son mis flechas. Si me las devuelves, podré usarlas para matar a más de estas criaturas. Creo que eso es lo mejor para todos, ¿no?'","Habla con Bregoleth en la pendiente hacia el sur.","'Llevaré al chico de vuelta a Musgovilla y me uniré a ti en el campamento de Duindil, Echad Terthas, cuando Tegwyn esté a salvo con sus padres.'","Recuperas una flecha élfica del otro cadáver y escuchas a alguien llamándote.","Sacas una flecha de la espalda del Uruk. La flecha es de fina manufactura élfica.","Un Elfo en la pendiente hacia el sur ha llamado tu atención. ¿Mató ella a estos Uruks?","Sube por el sendero inclinado al sureste de Echad Terthas.","Habla con Duindil en Echad Terthas.","Dos cadáveres Uruk yacen en la hierba fuera de Caras Gelebren.","Habla con Meneldir en el Aguaestancada noroeste.","Meneldir está en el Aguaestancada noroeste, considerando las palabras de Tegwyn.","Tegwyn escuchó a los Uruks hablar sobre la antigua ciudad élfica al noreste del Aguaestancada, y parecía que muchas más criaturas que las que atacaron Musgovilla planeaban viajar allí.","Duindil supervisa el trabajo en el campamento de Echad Terthas, con vista a la antigua ciudad élfica.","Bregoleth acepta la devolución de sus flechas con una sonrisa.","'No he visto a Duindil desde que dejé la tierra de mi gente. Búscalo en su campamento al este.'","'Me escondí entre los arbustos y no me moví ni un centímetro, ¡y una partida de exploradores Uruks pasó a pocos metros de mí! No me vieron, pero los escuché hablar sobre la antigua ciudad élfica al noreste. ¡Es allí adonde van!'","Los cuerpos de dos Uruks yacen aquí en la hierba.","Duindil, un Montaraz en Echad Terthas, puede saber sobre los Uruks que marchan dentro de Caras Gelebren. Echad Terthas está ubicado al este del Aguaestancada.","'¿Dices que traes noticias de Meneldir? No he hablado con él desde que nos dejó, deshonrado por romper su juramento. Éramos amigos una vez y crecimos juntos en Tornhad, pero demostró ser infiel. Solo me sorprende esto: que no se haya convertido en un bandido, como todos asumimos. Quizá también esto: que te envíe con un mensaje de advertencia. ¿Qué le importa a él la gente de esta tierra, o de cualquier otra?\
\
'Aun así, el mensaje que traes llega tarde. Hemos estado observando a los Uruks moverse tras los muros de Caras Gelebren durante varios días. Están buscando algo, pero aún no sabemos qué.\
\
'Te recomiendo subir por el sendero inclinado hacia el sureste que conduce a las ruinas. Quizá encuentres algo que nosotros no.'","Libro 1, Capítulo 4: Uruks en la Ciudad Élfica","Examina el otro cadáver Uruk.","Duindil te guió para espiar a los Uruks que ocupan Caras Gelebren, sugiriendo que subas por el sendero inclinado al sureste de Echad Terthas.","Duindil asiente en saludo cuando te acercas.","Encuentra Echad Terthas, el campamento del pariente de Meneldir, Duindil, al este del Aguaestancada.","'¡Habrías tenido mucho orgullo de mí, ${PLAYER}, estoy seguro! Me escondí entre los arbustos y no me moví ni un centímetro, ¡y una partida de exploradores Uruks pasó a pocos metros de mí! No me vieron, pero los escuché hablar sobre la antigua ciudad élfica al noreste. ¡Es allí adonde van!\
\
'Parece que ese era su objetivo desde el principio, y planean reunirse con muchos más de sus compinches cuando lleguen allí. ¡Es bueno que haya ido a explorar, ¿verdad?! ¿Quizá les digas a mis padres que hice lo correcto?'","Examina uno de los cadáveres Uruk.","'Te recomiendo subir por el sendero inclinado hacia el sureste que conduce a las ruinas. Quizá encuentres algo que nosotros no.'","'¿La antigua ciudad élfica? Debe ser Caras Gelebren, ${PLAYER}. Está situada en una colina al este, y lo último que supe, uno de mis antiguos parientes estableció un campamento no muy lejos de allí. Se llama Duindil, y si Tegwyn dice la verdad, debería ser advertido de que los Uruks tienen algún plan para la ciudad.\
\
'Llevaré al chico de vuelta a Musgovilla y me uniré a ti en el campamento de Duindil cuando Tegwyn esté a salvo con sus padres. Explora la ciudad élfica con la ayuda de Duindil, pero no te acerques demasiado sin mí. Aún no sabemos qué buscan los Uruks. Creía que eran simples saqueadores, pero si cumplen las órdenes de Saruman en esta tierra, debe haber algo más.'\
\
Meneldir hace una pausa.\
\
'Una cosa más, ${PLAYER}. Puede que no importe, no realmente, pero debo decirte esto antes de que hables con Duindil. Cuando dejé las tierras de mi gente y vine al sur... no me separé en buenos términos. Si Duindil parece distante contigo... puede ser por eso. No dejes que te preocupe ni interfiera con el bien que buscamos hacer en esta tierra.\
\
'¡Que la fortuna te acompañe!'"},
[1864]={"Gimli is in the Splintered Shield, in Minas Tirith (Midsummer).","You learned from Mithrandir that Gimli vowed not to emerge from the Splintered Shield until he determined the perfect words by which Arwen and Aragorn might plight their troth.","Talk to the proprietor of the Splintered Shield in Minas Tirith (Midsummer)","Drafli Broadshield is in the Splintered Shield in Minas Tirith (Midsummer).\
\
Drafli Broadshield has been working with Gimli to determine the proper vows for the Great Wedding. You should wake him up so you can hear the results.","'Ah, ${PLAYER}! You have found us... hard at work! Ha ha!\
\
'It is true! All the folk here in this tavern... have been helping us find... the finest vows to be spoken... by Aragorn at his wedding! Elessar! You know... you know who I mean...\
\
'The ale here is quite good. It was Drafli's idea... to reward every perfect sentence... with a mug...\
\
'Ah, you had better wake him up, ${PLAYER}. We have so many good... good words from which to choose!'","'The wedding-feast will not be complete without some barrels of this fine ale!'","'Well, that is settled! Now let us see to the other matter: the proper vows to be made during the wedding ceremony!\
\
'Will you gather up these papers, ${PLAYER}? Drafli and I wrote down some good options, and all of our friends here in the Splintered Shield contributed suggestions of their own, and now it is up to us to select the very best ones.'","Gimli blinks at you as you awaken him from his stupor","Gather up the messy papers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Gimli and Drafli's attempts to come up with the perfect vows for the Great Wedding are spread out on the table in front of the dwarves.","'Perhaps you should go to this tavern and check on our dwarves, ${PLAYER}. It will not do for Gimli to miss the wedding, and if he keeps his eye on the ale and not on the sun he very well might! The Splintered Shield is in the Second Circle.'","Talk to Gimli in the Splintered Shield in Minas Tirith (Midsummer)","'I would be pleased to contribute a number of barrels for the wedding-feast. It is the least I can do for the king and his bride, and I do it gladly. Gondor is in need of such happiness as theirs after so much war.\
\
'The dwarves are right on this account: the drink will loosen the tongues of all those at the feast, and the guests will frequently and at full voice toast the king's health and that of his Elf-bride. That is my promise to you, ${PLAYER}.'","Talk to Gimli in the Splintered Shield","Drafli awakens with a start, blinking the sleep and the drink from his eyes","'But on to other matters. Some time ago I observed our friend Gimli walking with one of Rodwen's companions, a dwarf I know to be called Drafli Broadshield. I greeted them both, and Gimli responded heartily that he and his new friend were going to the Splintered Shield, and they might be some time away. \\qOh?\\q I asked them, and Gimli responded that they planned to determine the words Elessar and his bride should use to bind their love during the ceremony. \\qWe will not emerge until we have settled upon just the right words for their vow!\\q he proclaimed, and I suspect he meant it.\
\
'Perhaps you should go to this tavern and check on our dwarves, ${PLAYER}. It will not do for Gimli to miss the wedding, and if he keeps his eye on the ale and not on the sun he very well might! The Splintered Shield is in the Second Circle.'","'I will see to it that some of my very best barrels are on-hand for the wedding-feast.'","Gimli is in the Splintered Shield, in Minas Tirith (Midsummer).\
\
You have awoken Gimli from the drink-induced slumber of his creative process. Perhaps you should ask him about his success coming up with the right vows for the Great Wedding.","'Tell the proprietor he simply must provide some of this ale for the wedding-feast!'","Find Gimli in the Splintered Shield, located in the Second Circle of Minas Tirith (Midsummer)","Drafli Broadshield is in the Splintered Shield in Minas Tirith (Midsummer).","Wake Drafli Broadshield in the Splintered Shield in Minas Tirith (Midsummer)","'All right, let us see what we've got.'\
\
Gimli reads aloud from one of the papers.\
\
'\\qYour beauty is without compare, even among all the gems of the earth.\\q That was one of mine, ${PLAYER}. Do you like it? \\qTogether we will lay waste to our foes, and none will stand against us!\\q Hmm, now that I see it written down, I don't know about this one, Drafli.\
\
'What else, what else? \\qI pledge to love and serve you in all things,\\q pretty good, not bad. \\qMy love for you gives me the strength to...\\q to what? This one isn't finished.'\
\
Gimli shuffles through the stack of papers, looking for more worthy vows.\
\
'Let's see, let's see. \\qTrue men of Gondor will not forget Castamir?\\q What is this? Who wrote this?'","Gimli is in the Splintered Shield in Minas Tirith (Midsummer).","Gathered up the messy papers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Give the bundle of papers to Gimli in the Splintered Shield","'I have had an idea, Gimli! We should... we should... have the proprietor provide this ale for the wedding feast! As many barrels... as many barrels as he can spare!\
\
'And that should be no small number! A wedding such as... such as this... only comes along but rarely!\
\
'Ask him this, ${PLAYER}! Ask him, and it will be the very finest of celebrations! Why, if I have anything to say about it... it will be nearly as rowdy as a dwarf-wedding! The king of Gondor should be... should be so fortunate!'","Degilion, the proprietor of the Splintered Shield, is always behind the bar.\
\
Drafli and Gimli are in agreement: the ale of the Splintered Shield should flow without limit at the feast that will follow the Great Wedding. Now it is up to you to make the arrangements with the proprietor of the tavern.","'These papers contain the fruit of Drafli's and my hard work, as well as that of all our new friends in the Splintered Shield.'","Talk to Drafli in the Splintered Shield","Book 1, Chapter 4: Vows, Speeches, and Oaths"},
[1865]={"Book 1, Chapter 5: A Difficult Road","'Did you find my boy? Did you find Nethadan?'\
\
You tell Bandron his son was attacked by raiders, but survived and seemed well enough to return very soon.\
\
'That is a relief, ${PLAYER}. I have many daughters, but he is my only son. Who else will carry on the legacy of my house, as common as it is? He is my blood, and in him I see my own visage at that age. Young, but full of dreams for the road to come. He is dear to me. You have done well by my son and my family! Now, my benefactor, what supplies have you brought from him? Give them to me and I will repair this axle, the better to return to my employer's errand.'\
\
You hand over the barrel of nails, and Bandron's eyes widen with surprise.\
\
'What is this? An entire barrel of nails?'\
\
You tell Bandron that his son should be by soon with another, similar barrel.\
\
'No, that cannot be! What am I supposed to do with two barrels of nails? I need to fix an axle, not put a nail in every tree from here to the Grey Wood! This repair will take two nails, at the most. And now we have two barrels of the things! How much coin did he spend on these barrels? Every one I gave to him, I do not doubt! All of our profit on this expedition will have gone to buying nails!\
\
'Oh, ${PLAYER}. I recommend to you a life without heirs. Every hair on my head was the colour of coal before Nethadan was born, and ever since: white hairs, each and every one!\
\
'My employer is Galengam, of Galengam's Divine and Delicate Draughts. He runs a shop in the town of Calembel, to the south-east. Kindly go to him and tell him that we ran into some difficulty, and will return as soon as the Cemenduril liquor is delivered. If you have a kindly heart, ${PLAYER}, weave a tale of raiders and robbers... and leave the nails quite out of it!'","Talk to Bandron by his cart in Tarlang's Neck","Bring the barrel of nails to Bandron by his cart in Tarlang's Neck","Talk to Galengam outside his shop in Calembel","Travel south-east through Tarlang's Neck into Lamedon","Find Nethadan somewhere south of Tarlang's Neck","'I need to return to my father's cart, up the road that way, in the Neck. Have you come from there?'\
\
Nethadan grimaces and clutches his leg.\
\
'We were bringing several bottles of Cemenduril liquor to sell at towns throughout the Vale, on behalf of Galengam's Divine and Delicate Draughts, but the cart succumbed to the harsh passage. My father sent me down to that village yonder to bring back supplies to fix the cart, and I did my duty. Well, as far as it went, for I was jumped by raiders and hurt my foot quite grievously. They ran off, but be warned: they may return in time!\
\
'If you could bring one of these barrels back to my father, I will follow with the other. I think I am just about ready to walk once more.'","A waggon has come to an early stop in Tarlang's Neck, and its driver could use your assistance.","Galengam is outside his shop in Calembel, south-east of Tarlang's Neck.\
\
Bandron has asked you to speak to his employer in the town of Calembel and explain some of the reasons for the delay.","'I sent my boy Nethadan to the nearest village for supplies we can use to fix it, but he has yet to return. Can you keep one eye open for him? The road leads south-east to the nearest village, and I hope you find him there. I need those supplies, and I need to know he has not run into trouble.'","Collect barrel of nails by Nethadan","'Take care, traveller! You pass through Tarlang's Neck, and the road here is treacherous. Many an ankle has been turned by the rough going in this pass, riders and walkers sent to the ground by one misstep. It has claimed the axle of my cart, and now my business is halted.\
\
'I sent my boy Nethadan to the nearest village for supplies we can use to fix it, but he has yet to return. Can you keep one eye open for him? I am afraid he may have run into trouble... or into the town's tavern for a short drink that became a long one!\
\
'The nearest town is called Dínadab, and it is to the south-east along the road. Nethadan may be a fool, but he is my boy and I do not want him to run afoul of trouble. Not when we have a task to perform!'","'Follow the Dead south-east through Tarlang's Neck, and help any of the people of Gondor that may have been endangered by their passage. I will remain to aid the people of the Vale, but I value your help, my new friend. May the people benefit from our friendship!'","Bandron is by his broken cart in Tarlang's Neck, between Lamedon and Blackroot Vale.\
\
You have picked up a barrel of nails from Nethadan and he asked you to bring it to his father so he can repair the cart.","You have met Rovalang, a Swan-knight of Dol Amroth. Recognising you for a great adventurer, he has asked you to journey into Lamedon and ensure that the people there are not endangered by the movement of the Dead.","'If you could bring one of these barrels back to my father, I will follow with the other. I think I am just about ready to walk once more.'","'The road through Tarlang's Neck is treacherous. Keep your eyes open for any danger!'","Rovalang has asked you to travel south-east through Tarlang's Neck, and to help any people of Gondor who may have run afoul of the Dead in their passage.","You see a waggon ahead, motionless in the road. What has happened?","'Bring that barrel of nails to my father, and with haste! I will be along quite soon.'","Nethadan has asked you to bring one of the barrels near him back to his father Bandron, in Tarlang's Neck.","If the Dead passed through here, they may have gone to Calembel. It is worth a look.","Nethadan went to the town of Dínadab in Lamedon, south-east of Tarlang's Neck, to recover supplies to fix his father's broken waggon, but he never returned. Bandron asked for you to find him.","'My name is Rovalang, and I am proud to serve Imrahil, Prince of Dol Amroth. He has marched for the White City with a company of knights and more than five hundred men at arms to defend it 'gainst all enemies.  I and several of my order he commanded to remain in the service of his daughter Lothíriel, who rules now while he is gone.\
\
'Her safety is paramount, and I and the other swan-knights who remained would die to defend her, but we are sworn to obey her commands. She sent several of us from the city to protect her people in the Vale and in Lamedon, and we could not refuse. So I came to the Vale, and beheld the scene I have reported to you. It seems Lothíriel was right: there is danger outside the walls of Dol Amroth, and the Swan-knights are needed here too.\
\
'Not just Swan-knights; brave adventurers too, as I deem you to be! Follow the Dead south-east through Tarlang's Neck, and help any of the people of Gondor that may have been endangered by their passage. I will remain to aid the people of the Vale, but I value your help, my new friend. May the people benefit from our friendship!'","'My employer is Galengam, of Galengam's Divine and Delicate Draughts. He runs a shop in the town of Calembel, to the south-east. Kindly go to him and tell him that we ran into some difficulty, and will return as soon as the Cemenduril liquor is delivered. If you have a kindly heart, ${PLAYER}, weave a tale of raiders and robbers... and leave the nails quite out of it!'","'Ah, welcome to Galengam's Divine and Delicate Draughts, purveyor of healing remedies and wholesome poultices! If you are here to purchase some of my goods, I must sadly report that you have come at a poor time; my last shipment of Cemenduril liquor is already bound for the Blackroot Vale, and my remaining stock is set aside for the Houses of Healing at Minas Tirith.'\
\
You tell Galengam of your encounter with Bandron and his son Nethadan.\
\
'The delay is unfortunate, but not unexpected. A successful merchant accounts for such things. Theirs will be the last delivery of Cemenduril liquor to the Vale for some time, because now all my goods will be needed at Minas Tirith.'"},
[1866]={"Gimli is in the Splintered Shield, in Minas Tirith (Midsummer).","Show the wrinkled note to Mithrandir in the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith (Midsummer)","'You have returned just in time, ${PLAYER}! I planned to send for you. But I see you have come to me with some purpose of your own?'\
\
You briefly mention Gandalf's worries concerning the legacy of the Kin-strife and the possibility that the folk of Gondor may not accept Elessar's marriage to Arwen. Your friend raises an eyebrow at that, and his demeanor becomes at once more Aragorn than Elessar.\
\
'That is not a concern of mine, ${PLAYER}. Arwen will be a good queen, and the kingdom will come to accept her. There will be no kin-strife this time.'","'I don't know very much about this name \\qCastamir,\\q but I know it has something to do with a dark period in the history of Gondor. Corsair leaders calling themselves \\qthe Heirs of Castamir\\q caused us some problems on the journey from Rohan here to Minas Tirith, and I know it is a name that causes Aragorn some displeasure. That is enough for me; I do not need to know the particulars.\
\
'For someone to invoke this name now, today? I do not like it, ${PLAYER}! Some villain here in the Splintered Shield snuck this paper among the others, hoping to disrupt the wedding! Find out who has done this, and we will make them pay for it!'","'What has brought you back to me so quickly, my friend? Has Gimli exhausted his store of love-words? Or has he decided to save them for another wedding? It would not surprise me to learn that our dwarf has a poet's heart, as do many of his people.'\
\
You tell Gandalf about the mention of Castamir that someone slipped among Gimli's papers in the Splintered Shield, and the Wizard nods without surprise.\
\
'Yes, I expected something like this, ${PLAYER}. The folk of Gondor have long memories. Castamir's reign was the violent culmination of the Kin-strife, a chain of events that began with a wedding of which the populace did not approve. Rómendacil, twentieth King of Gondor, sent his son Valacar to make peace with Vidugavia, the self-proclaimed King of Rhovanion. Valacar did so, but he did more as well: he fell in love with Vidumavi, Northman daughter of the king, and the two were married.\
\
'Many folk in Gondor were displeased with the match, believing that Valacar's marriage would lessen the royal Númenórean blood in any heir produced by the union. Unrest simmered throughout the kingdom. A child was born to Valacar and Vidumavi, and he was named Eldacar; the unrest continued to simmer, until at last he came to the throne. Unrest turned to violent conflict and Castamir, the Captain of Ships, brought war to unseat Eldacar. The Usurper ruled Gondor for ten years until Eldacar returned at the head of a Northmen army. Castamir was slain, but his sons and allies fled to Pelargir and Umbar, and the underlying discontent that caused the Kin-strife never truly disappeared.\
\
'Will the people of Gondor accept the marriage of their king to Arwen Undómiel, the daughter of Elrond of Rivendell? The news you bring from the Splintered Shield tells me that some, at least, may not. We should bring word of this possibility to Elessar, though it pains me to trouble him with it. Perhaps you can do this, ${PLAYER}.'","King Elessar is in the Tower of Ecthelion in Minas Tirith (Midsummer).","'Will the people of Gondor accept the marriage of their king to Arwen Undómiel, the daughter of Elrond of Rivendell? The news you bring from the Splintered Shield tells me that some, at least, may not. We should bring word of this possibility to Elessar, though it pains me to trouble him with it. Perhaps you can do this, ${PLAYER}.'","Question a woman of Gondor about the threat","'Some villain here in the Splintered Shield snuck this paper among the others, hoping to disrupt the wedding! Find out who has done this, and we will make them pay for it!'","Talk to Gimli in the Splintered Shield","The reminder of the Kin-strife in Gondor is an unpleasant one that may bode ill for the upcoming wedding of King Elessar and Arwen Undómiel.","'What is the trouble, friend? I assure you that several of my finest barrels will be brought to the hall for the wedding-feast. I am a man of my word, and I will see it done. All I ask is that the lords and ladies attending the feast know that it was Degilion of the Splintered Shield who provided the drink.'\
\
You tell Degilion that someone slipped a reference to Castamir the Usurper among the papers on Gimli's table while the dwarf and his companion were dozing.\
\
'Men speak of Castamir... in my tavern? This is an outrage! I'll have you know that we of the Splintered Shield are kings' men all, and have nothing but respect for his bride-to-be, Elf though she be. I say that with all the love in my heart, ${PLAYER}! If you find any who say otherwise, or even so much as think it, I will have them cast out upon the street, never welcome again within these walls! I swear it, ${PLAYER}. Show me the man who speaks fondly of Castamir, the usurping king-slayer, and I will report him to the Guards of the Citadel!'","Book 1, Chapter 5: A Whisper of Unrest","Mithrandir is in the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith (Midsummer).\
\
Gimli wants you to show the scrawled threat to Mithrandir and get a Wizard's advice.","Talk to King Elessar in the Tower of Ecthelion in Minas Tirith (Midsummer)","'Nobody saw anything? Ha! I wager my axe could make them talk, but this is not my kingdom and I should not wish to overstep my bounds. Not right before a wedding, anyway.\
\
'Castamir! Bah! I remember the Corsairs that invoked his name at Pelargir, ${PLAYER}, and none of them would be welcome at a wedding such as this. No, not even if they cleaned themselves up and wore their finest garb! They were cruel-hearted and evil-minded, and from my gathering it sounds like their idol Castamir was twice as bad!\
\
'You should go tell Gandalf that there are some, at least, who might wish to disrupt Aragorn's wedding. Maybe our Wizard could work some magic to sniff out these troublemakers and make them think better of it? I should say it is worth a try. If that does not do it, offer my axe in service of the task. That may prove even more effective than magic!'","These men insist they saw nothing","Question a man of Gondor about the threat","Someone in the Splintered Shield, in Minas Tirith (Midsummer), may have seen something.\
\
Someone in the Splintered Shield placed that note on the table while Gimli and Drafli were preoccupied with their ales. But who could have done this, and why would they risk notice by the dwarves or their powerful friends?","Ask Degilion, proprietor of the Splintered Shield, about the scrawled threat","These women insist they saw nothing"},
[1867]={"'Matar Uruks puede ser recompensa suficiente, ${PLAYER}, pero encontrar alguna pista sobre su propósito aquí es aún mejor. Entiendo que encontraste un informe en uno de ellos.'\
\
Le entregas el pergamino a Bregoleth y ella lo estudia atentamente.\
\
'No me alegra leer la Lengua Negra, pero hablarla es aún peor que leerla. Esto es lo que dice este informe, en una lengua que no retuerce cruelmente mi lengua:\
\
'\\q¡Guerreros! Explorad las antiguas... ¿forjas? En Acebeda. Buscad reliquias de... ¿artesanía élfica de joyas? No quiero... basura sin valor... Deseo... saber. Los Elfos hicieron anillos allí... Quiero encontrar... su conocimiento artesanal perdido.\\q'\
\
Bregoleth levanta la mirada hacia ti.\
\
'Esto es peor de lo que esperaba, ${PLAYER}. Por algún propósito insondable, Saruman el Blanco nos ha traicionado. Busca el saber de los anillos de Eregion, y ha enviado a estos Uruks para obtenerlo.'","Bregoleth está cazando Uruks al noroeste de Caras Gelebren.\
\
Debes mostrarle a Bregoleth el informe Uruk que encontraste en una de las criaturas que merodeaban en Caras Gelebren.","Derrota Uruks en Caras Gelebren (9/10).","Bregoleth querrá ver este informe.","'¿Recogiste un informe de uno de los Uruks? ¿Qué decía?'","Lleva el informe Uruk a Bregoleth en la pendiente al noroeste de Caras Gelebren.","Los Uruks acechan las callejuelas de Caras Gelebren.\
\
Bregoleth te pidió derrotar a los Uruks que ahora merodean en Caras Gelebren.","'Me complace ver que compartimos un propósito, o al menos compartimos nuestro odio hacia los orcos.\
\
'Mi nombre es Bregoleth. Vengo de la distante Imladris en un viaje propio, pero al oír de Uruks en Eregion desvié mis pasos. Ahora mato a las criaturas donde las encuentre y llevaré noticia de lo que he visto a Elrond cuando sepa más.'\
\
Le dices a Bregoleth que los Uruks hablan del Mago Saruman como si fuese su amo.\
\
'Eso es muy preocupante, pero un Uruk muerto no sirve a ningún amo. Eliminemos a las criaturas que acechan las ruinas de Caras Gelebren y, después, discutiremos si hablaron verdad o no.'","Libro 1, Capítulo 5: Bregoleth","Has derrotado Uruks en Caras Gelebren (${NUMBER}/10).","'Eliminemos a las criaturas que acechan las ruinas de Caras Gelebren y, después, podremos discutir si dijeron verdad o falsedad.'","Al enterarse de que los Uruks andaban por Eregion, Bregoleth desvió sus pasos para investigar.","Este último Uruk aferraba un pedazo de pergamino en una mano.","Tomaste un pergamino arrugado del cuerpo de un Uruk que acechaba las callejuelas de Caras Gelebren.\
\
Debes leer el informe Uruk y aprender todo lo que puedas sobre el propósito de estas criaturas en Ciénaga de los Cisnes.","Derrota Uruks en Caras Gelebren (${NUMBER}/10).","Lee el informe Uruk que recogiste."},
[1868]={"'¡Apresúrate! Debo saber dónde están los otros cuatro jinetes si quiero ayudar a los viajeros a escapar sanos y salvos de Bree. \
\
'Viaja hacia el oeste y habla con Lenglinn. Acampa al norte del Portal del Este. Puede que haya visto allí a uno o más Nazgûl.'","Libro 1, Capítulo 5: Los Otros Jinetes","'¡Aragorn ha enviado ayuda! Los Nazgûl, cuatro más, estaban en Los Gamos. Cabalgaban velozmente hacia el este, sobre corceles negros. Fui lo bastante tonto como para interponerme en su camino, y me atropellaron.\
\
'Me curaré a tiempo, pero los Jinetes han dejado una amenaza a su paso que debe ser tratada. Debo pedir tu ayuda.'","Mientras estabas fuera investigando a los bandidos de Montebruno, cinco Nazgûl atacaron El Poney Pisador en busca de cuatro viajeros de la Comarca, que Trancos tenía bajo su protección. Trancos te ha dicho que hay un total de nueve Jinetes, y que debe conocer la ubicación de los otros cuatro.","'Aunque tanto tú como yo hemos visto a cinco Nazgûl, su verdadero número es nueve. Antes de poder llevar a mis pupilos más allá de Bree, debo saber dónde se esconden los otros cuatro.\
\
'¿Podrías viajar al oeste y hablar con Lenglinn? Lo envié a Los Gamos para que vigilara a un Hobbit en particular, pero parece que el señor -- Sotomonte y sus amigos decidieron tomar un camino diferente y ahora están aquí bajo mi protección. Aun así, Lenglinn puede conocer el paradero de los Nazgûl restantes.\
\
'Acampa en una elevación justo al norte del Portal del Este y puede que haya visto algo que me ayude. Debes darte prisa. No puedo permitirme demorarme aquí demasiado tiempo.'","El campamento de Lenglinn se encuentra en una elevación al norte del Portal del Este, junto al Gran Camino del Este, al oeste de Bree. \
\
Trancos te ha pedido que hables con Lenglinn, otro Montaraz, y averigües si ha visto a algún otro Nazgûl saliendo de la Comarca."},
[1869]={"Libro 1, Capítulo 6: La Ciudadela de Celebrimbor","Lleva los artefactos que recogiste a Bregoleth al noroeste de Caras Gelebren.","'Estos son tristes recordatorios de tiempos ya pasados, ${PLAYER}, pero sin duda no son lo que Saruman busca en este lugar. En mi corazón sé lo que él desea.\
\
'Es el saber de los Anillos lo que ansía, el mismo conocimiento con el que el constructor de esta ciudad fue atrapado. Si lo encuentra, temo que pueda obrar un gran mal sobre las tierras y pueblos de la Tierra Media.'\
\
Bregoleth mira el horizonte, oscurecido por la niebla lejana. Desde la colina superior, escuchas los ásperos gritos de los orcos incluso por encima del viento. Tras un momento, la guerrera élfica vuelve a mirarte.\
\
'Te contaré la historia de la Ciudad de las Joyas y de la Fortaleza de Plata, para que sepas cómo fuimos engañados, y sepas por qué no debe volver a suceder. Debo hablarte de Annatar, el Señor de los Dones, pero lo conocerás por otro nombre, porque él es Sauron, y es el Enemigo.'","Examina la estatua semienterrada en el centro de Caras Gelebren.","Bregoleth te pidió buscar en Caras Gelebren artefactos que puedan revelar el propósito de Saruman al enviar Uruks a Ciénaga de los Cisnes.","Examina la lámpara caída en el sureste de Caras Gelebren.","Este martillo, desgastado por los años, casi se deshace en tu mano.","Bregoleth espera tu regreso en la pendiente descendente al noroeste de Caras Gelebren con los artefactos que recogiste.","Ninguna de las lámparas que iluminaban Caras Gelebren por la noche sigue en pie.","Los antaño hermosos pilares de Caras Gelebren son ahora tristes recordatorios de la guerra.","Bregoleth te habló de la historia de Caras Gelebren, la gran ciudad del herrero élfico Celebrimbor, y de su preocupación por lo que Saruman podría estar buscando dentro de sus muros.","Examina el pilar dañado en el suroeste de Caras Gelebren.","Este plato antiguo está cubierto de una telaraña de grietas, volviéndolo inservible.","'Los Elfos de Eregion fueron engañados en el pasado por palabras amables, ${PLAYER}, por ofertas de regalos y promesas de conocimiento secreto. Fue una lección difícil, pero he pasado muchos años creyendo que esto es verdad: la aprendimos bien.\
\
'Sí, digo \\qnosotros\\q, porque viví en la ciudad de Celebrimbor en aquellos días. Era un gran centro de arte y aprendizaje, con amplias praderas verdes y senderos de piedra pulida a ambos lados del río. Hablo de Mirobel, la Ciudad de las Joyas, y Caras Gelebren, la Fortaleza de Plata. Era un lugar acogedor... demasiado acogedor.'\
\
Bregoleth te mira fijamente.\
\
'Te pido que regreses a la ciudad elevada y veas en qué estado se encuentra. Puede haber artefactos dentro que debamos mantener lejos de los Uruks y de su amo, sea Mago o no. Examinaré lo que encuentres y juzgaré si aún hay peligro para los Elfos entre los huesos de la ciudadela de Celebrimbor, o si solo queda tristeza.'","Recoge un artefacto del suroeste de Caras Gelebren.","Esta antigua estatua de Celebrimbor yace ahora semienterrada en la tierra.","Recoge un artefacto del sureste de Caras Gelebren.","'Te pido que regreses a la ciudad elevada y veas en qué estado se encuentra. Puede haber artefactos dentro que debamos mantener lejos de los Uruks y de su amo, sea Mago o no. Examinaré lo que encuentres y juzgaré si aún hay peligro para los Elfos entre los huesos de la ciudadela de Celebrimbor, o si solo queda tristeza.'","Recoge un artefacto del centro de Caras Gelebren.","Este pequeño bolso ahora contiene solo polvo y astillas de roca."},
[1870]={"'En la estela de los Jinetes Negros, los crebain han tomado posada. No son de la cepa común de las Tierras Brunas, sino una raza que no he visto antes. Probablemente estas criaturas repugnantes vigilan Los Gamos y la Comarca... o al menos a mí, ya que se han dedicado a mirarme por la noche.\
\
'Aunque los crebain no vean nada de interés, el hecho de que el enemigo tenga ojos aquí es peligroso. Si pudiéramos cegar estos ojos, el enemigo no estaría tan seguro en dirigir sus esfuerzos. Si lo deseas, deshazte de los crebain que anidan al suroeste, justo más allá de mi campamento.\
\
'Incluso matar un craban ayudará mucho a cegar al enemigo.'","Deseando noticias sobre los otros Nazgûl, Trancos te envió al oeste, a las fronteras de la Comarca y Los Gamos, para hablar con Lenglinn, a quien había enviado para cuidar de un hobbit.","Los crebain han tomado posada al suroeste, justo más allá de su campamento.\
\
Lenglinn te dijo que los crebain siguieron a los Nazgûl y han tomado posada fuera de su campamento. Está seguro de que los pájaros son espías del enemigo y informarán sobre los movimientos en el oeste. Te ha pedido que te deshagas de ellos para evitar que hagan daño.","'El enemigo no debe saber lo que sucede en el oeste. De lo contrario, estarían demasiado seguros en sus esfuerzos en el este, lo que podría llevar a un desastre.\
\
'Por favor, ciega los ojos del enemigo matando a algunos de los Crebain que anidan justo al suroeste de mi campamento.'","'Bien, has matado a esos pájaros repugnantes. ¡El enemigo no estará tan seguro en sus esfuerzos ahora!\
\
'Sin embargo, todavía necesito tu ayuda. Debo pedirte que hagas algo en Los Gamos, ya que fue su llamada de cuerno la que me alertó sobre la presencia de los Nazgûl.'","El campamento de Lenglinn está al noreste del nido de crebain.\
\
Con los crebain muertos, el enemigo tiene menos ojos vigilando Los Gamos y la Comarca. Habla de nuevo con Lenglinn y aprende qué más quiere que hagas.","Libro 1, Capítulo 6: En la estela de los Jinetes Negros","Crebain derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Derrota a los crebain (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[1871]={"Habla con Glorfindel","'Mae govannen, my friend. It is no small thing to bring so many across the mountains and to these distant lands, but for the love of my daughter all here would make the journey tenfold.\
\
'The defeat of Sauron has made safer the lands hereabout. The road was not difficult, and though my grieving heart tried to slow my steps, the light of joy in Arwen's face kept steady my pace.\
\
'For all the knowledge I possess, ${PLAYER}, I cannot solve this riddle. Arwen will be parted, from her kindred or from her betrothed, and none of my wisdom can ease that parting. Still I am here, and would be nowhere else on this day, or on any day that my daughter desired.'","'I greet you once again, ${PLAYER}, and name you friend. You and I have walked in dangerous places, but let us set aside the memory of them for now, for this is a time of celebration. That there may still be such as these is welcome indeed, though the time of my people draws near to an end.'","Talk to Arwen Undómiel outside the city","'Messengers from Amon Dîn have come to the city, and they bring word that a riding of fair folk has come out of the north. Even now they draw near the walls of the Pelennor, and my betrothed is with them.\
\
'Go to the gates of the city, ${PLAYER}, and tell Húrin I will be down presently. I would ask you to then greet the party from Rivendell, and let them know they are long-awaited, and most welcome in Gondor!'","The party from Rivendell has been spotted to the north of Minas Tirith (Midsummer), and it is King Elessar's wish that you should greet them.","Book 1, Chapter 6: The Evenstar in Gondor","'It is good to see you again, my friend, far from lands where it has been our custom to meet. There are few occasions that might draw so many from the Hidden Vale to the long road, but the marriage of Elrond's daughter Arwen Undómiel is one.\
\
'She is to wed Elessar of Gondor, but that is not the only name he wore during their courtship. Aragorn he was, and Estel, and while others called him Strider that name brought laughter to her lips and amusement to her heart.\
\
'It is a time for love's joy, ${PLAYER}, but there is sadness in it too, a father's sorrow for the daughter from whom he must be parted. That is another reason so many have come south, for even amid such joy their dear friend must lose something too, and that is a grief.'","'It is good to see you, ${PLAYER}, so far from the place of our first meeting, and with so much having happened since!\
\
'I have walked for many years in Middle-earth, but I feel something I have never felt before. I am like a young sapling, my life just now beginning. I assure you it is a peculiar sensation for one of the Eldar, ${PLAYER}!'","Your friends among the travelling party wish to greet you after their long journey.","Talk to Húrin the Tall at the gates to Minas Tirith (Midsummer)","Talk to Erestor","Habla con Elrohir","'A time of great evil has passed, ${PLAYER}, and now hearts will be lightened with joy. Arwen has long-awaited this day, but its arrival was never certain. Now that it has come, let none stand in the way of love's bounty, lest they risk my granddaughter's ire or my own.\
\
'I assure you: both may be fearful.'","'Mae govannen, ${PLAYER}. We have come a long way for the wedding of Arwen Undómiel to King Elessar of Gondor, but our journey is almost at its end.\
\
'I have been chief counsellor of Elrond's household for many years, and he has long relied upon my wisdom and advice... but what of these have I to offer today? There are times a daughter's happiness must be set against a father's sorrow, but how often do the Sundering Seas lie between one and the other? Rarely, perhaps... but the choice having been made, for Lord Elrond and his daughter the answer appears to be always.'","Habla con Elladan.","The party from Rivendell has been scouted from the walls of the city: the bride has nearly arrived, and the Great Wedding is soon to commence.","The Elves nod their greetings as you approach","Habla con Elrond","Habla con Galadriel","Welcome the party from Rivendell outside the gates of Minas Tirith (Midsummer)","'The party from Rivendell is outside the gate, ${PLAYER}. I understand you are to bring them the greeting of the city, and I will await the arrival of King Elessar?\
\
'Very good. These Elves are known to you, yes? You trust they intend no harm to Gondor or to the king? Then they will be welcome here, and I will permit none to speak ill of them.'","'The party from Rivendell is outside the gate. You are to bring them the city's greeting, and I will await the arrival of King Elessar, as was his command.'","'Hail to you, friend of adventure! Let my brother and I greet you as gladly as we may, for this is a day both of gladness and of sorrow. Gladness for the joy of our sister, but sadness too, for she has chosen to walk with her love Elessar, and her people will mourn to be parted from her.\
\
'While we remain in this Middle-earth, Elladan and I will soothe the sting of this hurt with exploration and adventure, with combat and feats of martial skill. That is our way, and I know it is yours as well, ${PLAYER}!'","'The journey was a long one, but we would not miss Arwen's wedding! Let our younger sister heed the wisdom of her older brothers.'\
\
Elladan gives you a playful smile.\
\
'We are little more than a hundred years older than she, but that century makes all the difference in wisdom, ${PLAYER}. Ask anyone and they will tell you I speak true.'","Arwen Undómiel, Evenstar of her people, has come to Gondor. She wishes to speak with you.","Habla con Celeborn","Húrin the Tall, Warden of the Keys, is waiting for you to come down to the gates of the city so you may welcome the party from Rivendell.","Elrond smiles at you, his eyebrows raised with unexpected mirth. Even so, you know he feels a deep sorrow that his daughter will no longer accompany him to the Undying Lands.","'Go to the gates of the city and tell Húrin I will be down presently. I would ask you to then greet the party from Rivendell, and let them know they are long-awaited, and most welcome in Gondor!'"},
[1872]={"Retrieve harvested Cemenduril bundles (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collected Corsair weapons (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I will be glad of the company, but I hope Galengam's concerns prove to be unfounded. I am no warrior. If a raiding party does threaten our work here, I will be quite helpless. Fortunately for me you are an imposing figure indeed!'","Collected Cemenduril bundles (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Book 1, Chapter 6: The Merchant","'Yours is not the first report I have heard of raiders in Lamedon, ${PLAYER}. I am worried they may do some harm to the fields where my workers grow Cemenduril blossoms. With these crops I brew the healing liquors I sell throughout the kingdom; if they are ruined, more than my business will suffer.'\
\
Galengam scowls. 'Prince Imrahil rode east for Minas Tirith, leaving his daughter to rule Dol Amroth. Is it any wonder that raiders have taken advantage to cause trouble while the Prince is away? I wager they would not dare do so if he remained in the city, but alas! War threatens in the east, and draws him thither. Lothíriel sits in Dol Amroth, where she is safe, but what of the people outside the walls?\
\
'Several farmers in my employ work the fields even now. Will you protect them while they go about their business? I would greatly appreciate it, and you would be doing me, and Gondor, a favour.'","Galengam has asked for your help to preserve the Cemenduril fields that are his livelihood and perhaps that of Gondor as well.","'Have you seen any sign of the raiders? I fear for my workers and for the Cemenduril crop, and want no harm to come to either!'","Collect Corsair weapons (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Galengam is outside his shop in Calembel.\
\
You have protected Galengam's farmers and collected a number of weapons wielded by the Corsair raiders. The merchant will be interested to hear how you have assisted his interests.","Talk to a Cemenduril farmer in the fields","'Do you have news from the fields? Oh, you have more than that! These bundles of harvested flowers will allow me to brew a good quantity of my healing liquor... but what are these?'\
\
Galengam squints critically at the Corsair weapons you have set before him.\
\
'I do not like the look of these weapons at all. These are weapons of Umbar, I'll warrant, and that means the raiding parties that plague Lamedon come from the coast. If Prince Imrahil were here, they would not dare to land! But we have only his daughter Lothíriel to keep the coast safe, and she is not the leader that is her father.'","Galengam's farmers can be found west of Calembel, working the flower fields.\
\
A wealthy merchant has asked you to protect the farmers that grow his Cemenduril crop from the attacks of any raiders that threaten.","Bring Cemenduril bundles and Corsair weapons to Galengam"},
[1873]={"Talk to King Elessar outside the city and experience 'A Wedding at Midsummer'","Talk to Rodwen outside the feast-hall of Merethrond in Minas Tirith (Midsummer)","Book 1, Chapter 7: A Wedding at Midsummer","'I understand the preparations are nearly complete?'\
\
You tell Arwen that the Council of Gondor authorized a great number of plans and preparations for the wedding, and Aragorn believes they are nearing completion. When you tell her that Gimli had some suggestions relating to the vows she and her betrothed might speak during the ceremony, Arwen smiles fondly.\
\
'I have already given the matter some thought, and chosen words of my own; my love is certain to have done the same. But my heart is warmed by the kind thoughts of Gimli, son of Glóin. May the words of our vows measure up to those of his devising!\
\
'But is that my betrothed I see? Has he come down from the city to greet his bride?'","'Dare I believe that is the sight of my beloved, and not some illusion? For so long have we awaited this day!'","The Great Wedding will take place on Midsummer's Day, and it will be a time of celebration for all. Folk from lands near and distant will come to celebrate the joining of King Elessar and Arwen Undómiel.","'After so many labours, at last it is time. Come with me, my friend. Together my love and I will ascend the levels of the White City, and tomorrow, on Midsummer's Day, we will be married at last.'","'The sight of my beloved has stolen all speech from me, my friend! For so long have we awaited this day, and now it arrives.\
\
'Can it be so? Speak to me, ${PLAYER}, so I will know that is truly my Lady Undómiel, Arwen Evenstar, and no illusory dream of my hopeful mind!'","Rodwen is pleased at how well the ceremony was conducted, and now she wishes to speak with you outside the feast-hall of Merethrond in Minas Tirith (Midsummer).","'I must say, my good friend, that it was a beautiful wedding, and everything went according to my plan. Indeed, in that way it was quite different than the plans of my adventuring days!\
\
'Did you know that my friends and I have already been tasked with arranging further weddings later in the summer? All of a sudden, folk of high birth and low seem to require our services, and I have been unable to turn down a one!\
\
'I do hope I am not making a mistake to say so, but this Great Wedding was more successful than any of my other recent endeavours... why, no one was injured or maimed at all, which might be worth recording!'","Talk to King Elessar outside the city","King Elessar has emerged from the city, eager to greet his bride, but first he has some words for you.","The time of the wedding has arrived!"},
[1874]={"Book 1, Chapter 7: Abandoned Refuge","Galengam believes the Corsairs must have landed at the old refuge of Edhellond, in Belfalas.","Explore the north-west dock at Edhellond","Lathlorn has asked you to explore the abandoned refuge of Edhellond, defeating Corsair raiders and collecting any relics of historical interest.","An overlook of the refuge of Edhellond, west of Calembel in Belfalas, would be a good place to begin your stand against the Corsair raiders.\
\
Galengam has sent you to Edhellond to deal with some of the Corsair raiders.","'I have not travelled that way since I was a young man, but I remember an overlook with a good view of the ruins. That would be a good place to survey the situation, and you should go there first. Find it to the west, in Belfalas.'","Defeat Corsair raiders in Edhellond (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'It always warms the heart to meet a new friend in these dangerous days, ${PLAYER}. We do not have enough warriors to cast the Corsairs into the sea, but your efforts in the refuge have told them that even an abandoned refuge is never truly forgotten by the Elves.'","An Elf stands atop the overlook, surveying the refuge of Edhellond","Lathlorn is on an overlook with a good view of the Corsair landing at Edhellond.\
\
You have defeated Corsair raiders throughout Edhellond and collected a number of forgotten relics, and should bring them now to Lathlorn.","The buildings along the southern court are intact, but empty","Explore the tallest tower at Edhellond","'If you are a friend, you are welcome to share my watch. You are doubly-welcome if you defeat Corsair raiders throughout Edhellond, and return to me with any relics you find!'","'Ah, you brought me some relics from that abandoned Elf refuge? Well, why delay? Let me see them!'\
\
You remove the dusty shards from your pack, and Galengam looks puzzled.\
\
'This is it? These dirty old fragments? I expected jewels, or gems, or fine weaponry! I suppose all of those have already been taken. Thank you for trying, ${PLAYER}, but I cannot pay for any of these pieces. No one would have any interest in purchasing them!'","'I have not travelled that way since I was a young man, but I remember an overlook with a good view of the ruins. That would be a good place to survey the situation, and you should go there first.'","Explore the southern court of Edhellond","Talk to Lathlorn on the overlook near Edhellond","Defeated Corsair raiders in Edhellond (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Lathlorn is surveying the situation at Edhellond, from an overlook that provides a good view of the refuge.","Collect relics in Edhellond (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Corsair ships have moored at the docks of Edhellond","Find the overlook west of Calembel, in Belfalas, that provides a good view of Edhellond","This tallest tower at Edhellond once kept watch over the sea","'If you are a friend, you are welcome to share my watch. I would be pleased to have your company, for Men of Umbar have brought their ships to shore, and threaten Edhellond. My people have not inhabited the refuge for a thousand years, but we bear enough affection for places once dear that we cannot allow the raiders to remain.\
\
'If their goal is plunder, they will be disappointed. The only relics that remain will be of historical value only. Any valuable artifacts or jewels were taken long ago.\
\
'There are others of my people nearby. If you can defeat some of the raiders throughout Edhellond, I will bring you to them. Return hither with any relics you find, and I will be doubly-pleased, for I do have an interest in curiosities from my people's history.'","Bring the relics to Lathlorn on the overlook near Edhellond","'These Corsair raiders likely landed at the shore west of here, in Belfalas. I expect they have established a foothold in the old ruins on the coast. People say Elves once lived there, but that must have been a thousand years or more ago. No Elves have come near Calembel for as long as I have run my shop, at any rate.\
\
'If you are of a mind to deal with these Corsairs, that would be the place to do it! And while you're at those ruins, if you happen to see any old remnants of the Elves, bring them back to me and I will pay you good coin for them. The Elves won't be needing them, after all.\
\
'I have not travelled that way since I was a young man, but I remember an overlook with a good view of the ruins. That would be a good place to survey the situation, and you should go there first.'","Collected relics in Edhellond (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[1875]={"Libro 1, Capítulo 7: Llamada de cuerno de Los Gamos","'¿Dices que Sotomonte está con Aragorn? No conozco a ningún Sotomonte... Me enviaron a vigilar a un hobbit llamado Bolsón. Debo suponer que es de quien hablaba Aragorn. Que esté a salvo es una buena noticia, pues mis temores se han mitigado algo. Era tarde por la noche cuando oí la Llamada de cuerno de Los Gamos. Corriendo hacia el camino, vi a los Nazgûl abandonar Los Gamos a galope. Intenté detenerlos, pero me atropellaron. Temía que ya hubieran encontrado a Bolsón.\
\
'Los cuatro Jinetes pasaron hacia el este en dirección a Bree, pero puede que descubramos lo que aprendieron, si es que aprendieron algo, en la casa de Bolsón en Cricava. Es una cabaña rodeada por un alto seto casi directamente al sureste del Portal del Este.\
\
'Si aprendes algo allí, vuelve a verme. Las noticias que puedas traerme pueden ayudar a determinar los movimientos de los Nazgûl.'","'Encontrar esas aves en el Bosque Viejo no será una tarea sencilla. Busca a Aragorn en Bree. Con su consejo tal vez puedas encontrar esas aves asquerosas.'","'Es una noticia terrible. Aunque los cuatro hobbits que esperaba están a salvo por el momento, la protección que ofrece Bree es efímera, en el mejor de los casos. Debemos partir pronto, y si las sospechas del Enemigo fueron confirmadas por estos crebain, de que lo que buscan ya no está en la Comarca, nuestro viaje puede ser aún más peligroso.\
\
'Sin embargo, el Bosque Viejo es un laberinto sinuoso que puede llevar por mal camino incluso al rastreador más experimentado. Encontrar a estos crebain no será fácil....'","'¡El Anillo del Enemigo! ¡No es de extrañar que Aragorn fuera tan reservado en cuanto a por qué el Enemigo buscaba a Bolsón!\
\
'Si los crebain escucharon las palabras de Fredegar, el Enemigo sabrá con certeza que el Anillo ya no está en la Comarca, y todo estará perdido. Encontrar a esos pájaros en el Bosque Viejo no será una tarea sencilla. Te pediría que volvieras a ver a Aragorn en Bree y buscaras su consejo sobre cómo encontrar a esas asquerosas aves.'","'¿Has visto qué pájaros tan horribles? ¡Vinieron directos a por mí!'","El campamento de Lenglinn está al norte del Portal del Este, al noroeste de Cricava.\
\
Cuando hablaste con Fredegar Bolger, te dijo que los Jinetes Negros no lo habían capturado y por lo tanto no habían aprendido nada de él, pero se te escapó algo sobre un Anillo perteneciente al Enemigo. Mientras Fredegar hablaba, unos crebain volaron del cielo y lo atacaron, y aunque derrotaste a los crebain, dos se retiraron al Bosque Viejo. Deberías llevar estas noticias a Lenglinn.","'¿Qué? ¿Quién? ¡Yo... yo no lo tengo! Oh, espera, no eres uno de esos Jinetes Negros. Debo decirte que no he estado tan asustado en mi vida. ¿Aprendieron algo de mí? Bueno, esos Jinetes irrumpieron en la casa, pero yo ya me había escabullido por la parte de atrás. No aprendieron nada de mí.\
\
'Cuando vinieron los Oficiales, me obligaron a contarles lo de Frodo y los otros que se habían ido al Bosque Viejo, pero no dije nada sobre el Anillo del Enemigo....\
\
'¡Oh, vaya! Quiero decir... Yo... ¿qué es eso? Suena como cuervos....'","La casa de Bolsón está en Cricava, casi al sudeste del Portal del Este, al sur del campamento de Lenglinn.\
\
Para determinar los movimientos de los Nazgûl, Lenglinn te ha pedido que investigues la casa de un Hobbit llamado Bolsón.","Trancos se encuentra en su habitación de la Posada del Poney Pisador en Bree, que se encuentra girando a la izquierda por el pasillo que sale de la sala común hasta que sólo se puede girar a la derecha. La habitación está al final del pasillo, a la derecha de las escaleras.\
\
Lenglinn te ha pedido que busques el consejo de Trancos sobre cómo encontrar al crebain que ha escuchado las palabras de Fredegar Bolger y ha escapado al Bosque Viejo. Teme que si el Enemigo se entera de que el Anillo que buscan ya no está en la Comarca, todo puede estar perdido.","'Aragorn estaba preocupado porque el Enemigo pudiera estar buscando a Bolsón, y por eso me envió a vigilarlo. Me enteré de que vino a vivir aquí, a País de los Gamos, aunque no sabía que había escapado por el Bosque Viejo.\
\
'Puede que los Nazgûl lo estuvieran buscando allí. Deberías investigar, pero por el bien de Frodo, no deberías mencionarle a nadie que aún vive.'","El Llamada de cuerno de Los Gamos había alertado a Lenglinn de la presencia de los Nazgûl.","Investiga Cricava"},
[1876]={"Habla con Bregoleth y escucha los años que pasó en Eregion, hace mucho tiempo.","'Celebrimbor había guardado uno de los Tres para sí. En el momento en que Sauron se colocó el Anillo Único en su dedo, Celebrimbor comprendió su peligro. Se quitó su anillo y juró no volver a usarlo jamás, para evitar que su mente fuera dominada por el Señor Oscuro. A aquellos de los artesanos que habían guardado anillos también se les obligó a entregarlos, en ocasiones por la fuerza, y los Tres Anillos fueron enviados en secreto a portadores ocultos. Mensajes fueron enviados a Hombres, Enanos y Elfos, en los que Celebrimbor admitía su error y advertía de la guerra venidera. Así se prepararon los pueblos para defender la Tierra Media, pero no sería suficiente para salvar Eregion de los estragos de Sauron.\
\
'Las puertas de Mordor se abrieron y los ejércitos de Sauron salieron. Buscaba apoderarse de cuantos Anillos de Poder pudiera encontrar, pero los Tres permanecieron ocultos, y no los tocó.'","'Le dolió a Celebrimbor ver los bosques y pantanos tan maltratados, pero no quería dañar su alianza con los Hombres de Númenor. Les aconsejó que cuidaran mejor de la tierra, pero sus palabras no fueron escuchadas. La pena de Galadriel se volvió demasiado grande, y volvió su mirada hacia Laurelindórenan y otras tierras distantes.\
\
'Celebrimbor dejó los bosques por perdidos, dedicando toda su atención y habilidad a dominar su oficio. Junto con su hermandad de herreros de joyas, se convirtieron en los más renombrados artífices de toda la Tierra Media. Si no podían detener la lenta degradación de la belleza de la tierra, al menos buscarían suplirla y preservarla mediante sus artes.\
\
'Y así fueron atrapados.'","'¿Pero quién es este?'","'Tras la caída de Beleriand, la mayoría de mi gente vino a vivir a la tierra de Lindon, al oeste, bajo el benevolente gobierno de Gil-galad. Se forjaron lazos de amistad con los enanos de Ered Luin, pero el próspero comercio de metales y gemas con ese pueblo menguó cuando los barbiluengos sufrieron guerras y desastres propios.\
\
'Ansiando el mithril para forjar sus obras de arte y belleza, muchos de los Noldor siguieron a los enanos mientras viajaban hacia el este. Guiados por Celebrimbor, descendiente de Fëanor, los Elfos se asentaron en las colinas cubiertas de acebos bajo la puerta oeste de Khazad-dûm. Hubo nuevamente amistad y comercio entre Elfo y Enano, y la ciudad de Celebrimbor en Eregion prosperó.\
\
'Eregion aún era un reino joven cuando llegaron los Hombres de Númenor. Tar-Aldarion, el rey, navegó por el río Gwathló y desembarcó para explorar Ciénaga de los Cisnes a pie. Se hizo amigo de Celebrimbor y forjó alianzas con los herreros élficos, y a cambio enseñaron a algunos de los suyos las técnicas de forja de armaduras y el grabado de ithildin y runas lunares. Con el tiempo, Aldarion envejeció y ya no volvió a Caras Gelebren, pero la amistad entre su pueblo y el mío perduró.\
\
'La amistad perduró, pero fue puesta a prueba. Los Númenóreanos eran gente marinera, y hacía mucho que habían agotado los bosques de su isla natal; ansiaban madera para construir más y más poderosos barcos. La Dama Galadriel, que habitó un tiempo en Eregion y bailaba a menudo junto a las acequias cubiertas de lirios, se afligía al ver el daño causado a los vastos bosques por las hachas númenóreanas. Cuando los constructores de barcos comenzaron a dragar su amado Ciénaga de los Cisnes y construir diques para canalizar las aguas, suplicó a Celebrimbor que impidiera que los Hombres de Númenor dañaran la tierra.'","'¿Las puertas de Mordor? ¿Los ejércitos de Sauron?\
\
'¿Qué me perdí, ${PLAYER}? Seguramente no es tan grave. Sauron ha estado muerto por tres mil años, y hoy Mordor es una tierra vacía.'\
\
Meneldir entrecierra los ojos al mirar a Bregoleth.\
\
'A veces a los Elfos se les dificulta marcar el paso de los años. No pretendo ofender.'","Habla con Bregoleth en la pendiente al noroeste de Caras Gelebren.","Bregoleth ha accedido a hablarte de los años que vivió en Eregion y del Enemigo que vino a amenazar a su pueblo y a toda la Tierra Media.","El Montaraz Meneldir ha llegado. Le lanza una mirada interrogante a Bregoleth.","Libro 1, Capítulo 7: El Señor de los Dones","Habla con Meneldir en la pendiente al noroeste de Caras Gelebren.","Bregoleth ha accedido a hablarte de los años que vivió en Eregion, aunque los recuerdos de aquel tiempo le resultan dolorosos.","Bregoleth desea concluir su triste relato.","Meneldir ha regresado de su recado en Musgovilla."},
[1877]={"'Welcome to Belfalas, ${PLAYER}. I am called Dorthaneth, and I have chosen to care for the Elves here as a mother does. They are the Avorrim, and they have come to this land to watch over the refuge of Edhellond and keep it safe from danger.\
\
'Danger threatens it now, as you have seen. Men of Umbar have come ashore in great number, too many for my few Avorrim to drive away. A guest is lately arrived, and we just spoke about these raiders. Go to him and hear what he has to say, for his news signals trouble for the Avorrim, and for the folk of Gondor as well.\
\
'Do you see him across the way? His name is Galdor, and he is lately arrived from Imladris.'","Talk to Dorthaneth in the Cave of the Avorrim","'Speak with Galdor and hear what he has to say, for his news signals trouble for the Avorrim, and for the folk of Gondor as well.'","Galdor is in the Cave of the Avorrim, in Belfalas.","Dorthaneth is within the Cave of the Avorrim, in Belfalas.","'You can find Dorthaneth in the cave where we reside for now. If you follow the road south-west on the way to Dol Amroth, you will come to a rocky cleft in the ground to your right. Follow it down to a cliff-side path over the water, and you will come to the entrance.'","Dorthaneth is within the Cave of the Avorrim, in Belfalas.\
\
Lathlorn has sent you to speak with Dorthaneth, the leader of the Avorrim.","Book 1, Chapter 8: Dorthaneth","The Cave of the Avorrim is located in a cliff-wall overlooking the sea, on the road to Dol Amroth. Lathlorn described it in this way:  'If you follow the road south-west on the way to Dol Amroth, you will come to a rocky cleft in the ground to your right. Follow it down to a cliff-side path over the water, and you will come to the entrance.'","'It is time for me to introduce myself properly, my friend. I am Lathlorn, and I am proud to count myself among the Avorrim. We were tasked by Círdan the Shipwright with maintaining a watch on Edhellond, and have done now for some time: removing overgrown brush and keeping the paths clear, and ensuring that the docks remain free of debris. If the Havens of Mithlond become untenable, this would be the last place from which my people could depart this Middle-earth for the Undying Lands. The Men of Umbar that occupy Edhellond do us a grievous turn, and do not even know of it!\
\
'Dorthaneth is the leader of the Avorrim, and you can find her in the cave where we reside for now. If you follow the road south-west on the way to Dol Amroth, you will come to a rocky cleft in the ground to your right. Follow it down to a cliff-side path over the water, and you will come to the entrance.\
\
'Tell Dorthaneth of your experiences in this land, for she has a wisdom about her and has proven a capable leader of the Avorrim for as long as I have known her.'","'The cool breeze off the water feels so nice after the heat of the day. Do you not agree?'\
\
Dorthaneth's expression is masked by her veil, but from her tone she seems unwilling to speak of more serious matters here.\
\
'Let us speak within the Cave of the Avorrim at another time,' she says after a moment.","Dorthaneth is in the Cave of the Avorrim.\
\
Galdor, an emissary from Círdan the Shipright at Mithlond, has overheard the speech of the Corsair raiders, and is worried about the loyalty they display for their leaders.","Find Dorthaneth within the Cave of the Avorrim","'Galdor is right to worry. The Men of Umbar have not possessed loyalty like this for many years, and it was once believed their people would decline and no longer pose a threat to their neighbours across the Bay. I do not believe these Heirs of Castamir are truly descended from that king, but I have paid little attention to the histories of Gondor and could not say for certain. The lives of Men are brief; before many a season has passed they fall, like the leaves of the trees in my home. I have never recorded either.'\
\
Dorthaneth is silent for a long time, and you have almost decided to leave her in peace when she speaks again.\
\
'I would be content to remain alone, listening to the sound of the water falling and the sighing of the wind in the trees, but as long as the Avorrim must remain here I will care for and protect them. There are others, too, with whom I feel a kinship and would safe-guard.'","Find the entrance to the Cave of the Avorrim, overlooking the sea","'Do not underestimate the Corsair threat! I gave Dorthaneth the same warning. In my journey here I came near to a group of Umbar-Men and overheard their talk. They spoke in reverent tones of 'the Heirs of Castamir' and 'the Scourge,' but it is not these names that fill me with anxiety. No, the flame of my concern is kindled by the passion with which the Umbar-Men spoke of their loyalty. Any of them would die in the name of the Heirs, and gladly, which is not a trait I have heard associated with that people before now. Something has changed.'","An Elf-maid stands on the bridge, deep in thought","Talk to Galdor in the Cave of the Avorrim","'I know your face, ${PLAYER}, for I came to Imladris some months ago and saw you there. A council was held and many courses decided, but we will not speak of them here. Know that I hold you in esteem and consider you an ally, and we bear friends in common.\
\
'It is that sense of kinship that drives me to tell you this: do not underestimate the Corsair threat! I gave Dorthaneth the same warning. In my journey here I came near to a group of Umbar-Men and overheard their talk. They spoke in reverent tones of 'the Heirs of Castamir' and 'the Scourge,' but it is not these names that fill me with anxiety. No, the flame of my concern is kindled by the passion with which the Umbar-Men spoke of their loyalty. Any of them would die in the name of the Heirs, and gladly, which is not a trait I have heard associated with that people before now. Something has changed.\
\
'I will set out for Mithlond in a few days, but do not forget my warning!'","The entrance to a cave yawns in the cliff-side to your left: the hideout of the Avorrim","Lathlorn has told you how to find the location from which the Avorrim keep watch over Edhellond."},
[1878]={"'Hay uno que podría encontrar estos crebain para nosotros, si le pidiéramos tal ayuda... sin embargo, puede que no vea nuestras preocupaciones como las suyas. Es conocido por muchos pueblos con muchos nombres. Antiguamente, era conocido como Orald por los Hombres, mientras que para los enanos era simplemente Forn. Los Elfos lo llamaban Iarwain Ben-adar, el más viejo y sin padre. Sin embargo, en estos días, es conocido como Tom Bombadil por aquellos pocos que son conscientes de él.\
\
'Busca la casa del Viejo Bombadil, que se encuentra en el extremo oriental del Tornasauce, el río que fluye a través del Bosque Viejo. Puede que te ayude si le pides en mi nombre, Aragorn. Si descubres algo, te pediría que lo abordes lo mejor que puedas.\
\
'Deseo enérgicamente ayudarte en esta tarea, pero la seguridad de mis protegidos es lo primero.'","La casa de Tom Bombadil está en el extremo oriental del río Tornasauce, en el Bosque Viejo.\
\
Trancos te dijo que buscaras a alguien llamado Tom Bombadil y le pidieras ayuda para encontrar al crebain que voló al Bosque Viejo.","Cuando estabas en Los Gamos investigando la incursión de los Nazgûl, hablaste con Fredegar Bolger, que te reveló información sobre Frodo Bolsón y el Anillo del Enemigo. Crebain atacó y puede que escuchara las palabras del hobbit.","'¿Qué es todo este alboroto? ¡No habíamos tenido tantos invitados desde nuestra boda! Hay tiempo suficiente para la observación de aves, ¿pero tal vez primero una canción o dos, mi corazón?... Deja que tu corazón vuele libre y deja a un lado tus preocupaciones. ¡Estás en la casa de Tom Bombadil!'","'Más sabio que el roble más viejo es Tom Bombadil. Dirígete a su acogedor hogar en el Bosque Viejo y gánate su ayuda como puedas.'","Libro 1, Capítulo 8: El Señor de los Bosques","'¡Apresúrate! Debes ir a la casa de Tom Bombadil rápido y pídele ayuda. Si los crebain le cuentan a los Nazgûl lo que han oído, ¡podría significar el fin de la Tierra Media!\
\
'Se dice que su casa está en el extremo oriental del río Tornasauce, en el Bosque Viejo. Recuerda, si descubres algo importante, ¡debes llevárselo a Trancos inmediatamente!'"},
[1879]={"'Devolví a Tegwyn a Musgovilla y, aunque no pude conseguirle una promesa de no aventurarse de nuevo en lo salvaje, sus padres le dieron suficientes tareas para mantenerlo ocupado al menos hasta la adultez; momento en el que, creo yo, nuestra obligación de mantenerlo a salvo debería vencerse. No hice ningún juramento a los granjeros de la Ciénaga de los Cisnes.'\
\
Meneldir estudia tu expresión y suspira profundamente.\
\
'Duindil no habló bien de mí, ¿verdad? No me sorprende, ${PLAYER}. En mi corazón sigo teniendo a los Dúnedain como mi causa más querida... pero entiendo que mi gente pueda no creerlo, y no puedo negar la ruptura de mi juramento.\
\
'¿Pero quién es tu nueva amiga? Si odia a los Uruks como nosotros, y está dispuesta a ayudarnos, quizá pueda ayudarnos a dar con sus líderes. Me precede aquí el rumor de tres de esos villanos, y no puedo evitar pensar que el trabajo sería más rápido si nos dividiéramos, cada uno para encargarse de uno.'","¡Zagvar ruge un desafío y ataca!","'Bueno, ¿qué dices a eso?'","Bregoleth está al noroeste de Caras Gelebren, esperanzada en que pueda frustrarse el propósito de los Uruks en la Ciénaga de los Cisnes.","'Bregoleth dice que queda un último lugar que quiere que investiguemos, pero pronto nuestro tiempo juntos llegará a su fin. Cada uno de nosotros debe llevar noticia de los designios de Saruman a nuestros caudillos, pues pronto madurarán y traerán la ruina a la Tierra Media.'","La derrota de Holmduf redujo la ferocidad de los Uruks bajo su mando.","Idhobel está ubicado en el Eregion Occidental, junto al camino que va hacia el norte en dirección a Tham Celechir.\
\
Meneldir y Bregoleth acordaron reunirse contigo en Idhobel después de que cada uno derrotara a su propio líder Uruk.","Habla con Bregoleth en Idhobel.","Bregoleth está en el campamento de Idhobel, en el Eregion Occidental.","Investiga los rastros de Uruks en el Eregion Occidental y derrota a un líder de guerra Uruk.","La derrota de Zagvar redujo la tenacidad de los Uruks bajo su mando.","Habla con Meneldir en Idhobel.","'He odiado a los orcos desde mucho antes de que tú nacieras, Dúnadan. En cuanto a los juramentos que has tomado o roto, sé bien a quién estás jurado... o deberías estar. Sé lo que desea llegar a ser. No preguntes si yo te ayudaré, Montaraz del Norte; pregunta si tú eres lo bastante fuerte y valiente como para prestar ayuda alguna a Bregoleth de Imladris que ella pudiera necesitar.'\
\
Bregoleth sonríe con sorna a Meneldir, una luz divertida danzando en sus ojos. El Montaraz la mira boquiabierto.\
\
'Mataré a uno de tus líderes Uruk, Meneldir, y ${PLAYER} matará a otro. ¿Puedes encargarte tú del tercero? Señálanos sus ubicaciones en el mapa de ${RACE}, y lo haremos. Después podremos reunirnos en Idhobel, un campamento de mi gente al norte de aquí.'","¡Holmduf ruge un desafío y ataca!","Habla con Bregoleth en la pendiente al noroeste de Caras Gelebren.","Bregoleth habló tristemente de la Guerra de los Elfos y Sauron, pero se niega a vivir en el pasado. Si algo puede obtenerse de sus recuerdos para prevenir nuevas tristezas hoy, hará todo lo posible por aprenderlo.","Libro 1, Capítulo 8: La Mano aferradora","'Mataré a uno de tus líderes Uruk, Meneldir, y ${PLAYER} matará a otro. ¿Puedes encargarte tú del tercero? Después podremos reunirnos en Idhobel, un campamento de mi gente al norte de aquí.'","La derrota de Fakhthal redujo la moral de los Uruks bajo su mando.","Rastros de Uruks que indican las ubicaciones de líderes de guerra Uruk pueden encontrarse en tres lugares distintos del Eregion Occidental.\
\
Meneldir te pidió investigar los rastros de Uruks dentro de la Ciénaga de los Cisnes y derrotar a uno de los líderes Uruk responsables.","'Meneldir tiene razón: debo volver pronto a Imladris con estas sombrías noticias. El invierno se acerca, y debo decirle a Elrond que los vientos soplarán fríos si los Magos se han vuelto contra nosotros. La mano de Saruman se extiende para apoderarse de un conocimiento peligroso de las ruinas de Eregion, y si la Mano Blanca lo toma, ¿quién puede decir qué males pensará cometer después?'","¡Fakhthal ruge un desafío y ataca!","'¿Tuviste éxito? Son buenas noticias, pues significan que Saruman ahora tiene tres líderes de guerra menos al mando de sus fuerzas en la zona.\
\
'Hablé con Bregoleth mientras esperábamos tu regreso, y dice que hay un último lugar que quiere que investiguemos, pero pronto nuestro tiempo juntos terminará. Cada uno de nosotros debe llevar noticia de los designios de Saruman a nuestros caudillos, pues pronto madurarán y podrían significar la perdición de la Tierra Media.'"},
[1880]={"'The celebrations are not yet concluded; after all, there is still the wedding-feast to enjoy! Go to the feast-hall of Merethrond and speak to Merethien, the Master Foodmonger, once you have had your fill of merriment... there is still much of that to be had!\
\
'Do be careful, my friend.'","'I imagine my kingdom has not seen a wedding like this for many, many years; I see it reflected in the fervour of my people's celebration! The war is ended, and they are gladdened to have joyful cause!\
\
'We spoke of some trouble in the history of my kingdom, ${PLAYER}, do you remember? I told you I did not think it would be a problem, and so I still think. I have studied the faces of my people on this Midsummer's Day, and this I have learned: they will come to love their Queen. She will be a patient guardian of Gondor and all its folk, as I will be, and together we will restore what glory there is to be had in this age, and whatever ages may come.\
\
'Thank you for all you have done, ${PLAYER}. I speak not only of your service against the forces of Sauron, but also for all you have done as my dear friend. When at last the history of Gondor is written, one will be counted more important than the other, but know that in my deepest heart I measure them equal, for Aragorn may be selfish where Elessar may not.'\
\
He smiles at you, a wolfish grin that brings to mind the shadows of a distant tavern in Bree-land.\
\
'But you will not hear me admit it again, my friend. The peace of Middle-earth must come above my own happiness.'","King Elessar and Queen Arwen Undómiel have slipped away from the celebration and are in the throne room of Minas Tirith (Midsummer).","'Thank you for lending such support as you have to my husband, ${PLAYER}, during your adventures and his. There were days when it seemed the Shadow would never pass... but it has lifted, and not on its own terms. No, it was through the efforts of many folk all throughout Middle-earth, and yours not least of all!\
\
'Our wedding has been everything for which I hoped, and I am certain my husband feels the same.'\
\
Arwen looks around the throne room, and in the dim light of the grand chamber you see an amused smile dance across her fair features.\
\
'But we will need to do something about this throne,' she remarks.","Mithrandir is outside the Tower of Ecthelion in Minas Tirith (Midsummer).","'The King and Queen are in the throne room, ${PLAYER}. I understand they were awaiting you!'","The ceremony was only the beginning of the Great Wedding. Now there is the wedding-feast to be considered, where persons great and small come together throughout the city to celebrate the union of King Elessar and Arwen Undómiel.","Talk to Merethien inside Merethrond, at a table on the east side of the hall, when you are ready to conclude the wedding-feast","'Thank you for all you have done, dear ${PLAYER}.'","'The hobbits insisted this be called a banquet, in honour of one or another chieftain of theirs. I am a little unclear on the details, but it seems to have something to do with the number and varieties of foodstuffs available?'\
\
Merethien casts a weary look at her bench-mate Ioreth, who has been nattering constantly for the duration of the wedding-feast, and glances disapprovingly at Galathir, who has launched upon a long discussion of the various spices flavouring the many courses.\
\
'Come, let us inquire with the hobbits. They seem to be amusing fellows, and I would learn more of this land of theirs.'","Talk to Queen Arwen in the Tower of Ecthelion in Minas Tirith (Midsummer)","Merethien, the Master Foodmonger, can be found inside the great feast-hall of Merethrond, where the festivities continue.","Talk to King Elessar in the Tower of Ecthelion in Minas Tirith (Midsummer)","'But what am I saying? The celebrations are not yet concluded; after all, there is still the wedding-feast to enjoy! Go to the feast-hall of Merethrond and speak to Merethien, the Master Foodmonger, once you have had your fill of merriment... there is still much of that to be had!\
\
'Do be careful, my friend. If anything untoward happens at the feast and ruins the perfect wedding I planned, I will need to return to adventuring or find another profession, and I would rather not. Enjoy the wedding-feast, ${PLAYER}!'","'It has been some time since Gondor saw such revelry, ${PLAYER}. The folk thirsted for it without knowing what they desired. Such a night of celebration will be good for them.\
\
'The peace of Middle-earth is hard-won, my dear ${CLASS}, but it must be defended if it is to remain secure. Not all threats are gone with Sauron, as you well know, and other evils there are in the wide world that must be faced with bravery and resolve. Can I count on you to continue to stand against these dangers, ${PLAYER}, so that the love we celebrated today can last into the days and months ahead? A wedding is a beginning, my friend, and so is this Great Wedding, for there are those in the world that will see the joy of it and resent its presence.\
\
'My time on these shores draws nigh, my friend, and I want to know that these lands will know peace beyond my departure. I will be counting on you for this, ${PLAYER}, or for those you choose to follow in your stead. Someone will need to defend the happiness we saw today. Someone will need to safe-guard the peace of Middle-earth.\
\
'We will speak of these matters again, my friend. For now, you should do as does the city: eat, drink, and be merry!'\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>The story continues in future updates....</rgb>","Talk to Mithrandir outside the Tower of Ecthelion in Minas Tirith (Midsummer)","Book 1, Chapter 8: The Wedding Banquet","'You have my thanks and those of my kingdom for all you have done.'"},
[1881]={"'Halt and speak your business, stranger. There was a time when passage into the city was free and open, and none needed to answer questions, but those days are done. They will come again when the war is over.'\
\
You say you have come with an urgent warning for Lothíriel from Dorthaneth, the leader of the Avorrim.\
\
'Leader of the creeping Elves, you should say, for that is closer to the truth. Some say there is Elvish blood in Imrahil's line, but if so I say it is a good ways back and the Prince has done a good job of not letting it master his senses!\
\
'You may pass into the city. Lothíriel is fond of the Elves, and her father is not here to speak 'gainst the meeting. It is not my place to speak for him, though I think his mind would be clear on this.'","'What brings you to Dol Amroth, adventurer? Surely there is danger to be found everywhere, and you seem a long way from your home.'\
\
Lothíriel's face brightens considerably when you reveal that your message comes from Dorthaneth.\
\
'She is one of my closest friends, and I have treasured our conversations. Recently she had some wise counsel to provide about a delicate matter, but we need not speak of that. What message does she have for me now, friend of my friend?'","'You may pass into the city. You will find Lothíriel in the Great Hall, I shouldn't wonder.'","You have come to the entrance to the docks of Dol Amroth","'Go to Dol Amroth and give Lothíriel my warning. I do not want her to underestimate the Heirs of Castamir, for I fear they pose a greater danger to these lands than they have before.'","You have presented yourself to the guards at the entrance to Dol Amroth and should now find Lothíriel in the Great Hall of the city.","Dorthaneth has asked you to bring a message of warning to Lothíriel, who rules now in Dol Amroth.","You have come to the entrance of the great city of Dol Amroth","Book 1, Chapter 9: A Message for Lothíriel","The entrance to Dol Amroth is west of the Cave of the Avorrim.\
\
Dorthaneth has asked you to bring what she knows of the Heirs of Castamir and the Umbar raiders to Lothíriel in Dol Amroth. You should first present yourself to the guards at the gate of the city.","Talk to a guard by the entrance to Dol Amroth","'You may pass into the city. Lothíriel is fond of the Elves, and her father is not here to speak 'gainst the meeting. It is not my place to speak for him, though I think his mind would be clear on this.'","Find Lothíriel in the Great Hall of Dol Amroth","Lothíriel is dark of hair, with a somewhat Elvish appearance","'You must think I speak of leaving the world to its troubles, but even I, with every reason to do so before me, cannot truly withdraw. I have grown fond of Lothíriel, the daughter of the Prince of Dol Amroth who rules now in his absence. On several occasions she has escaped the watchful eyes of her guard, and come to visit me outside the walls of her city. The matters of which we spoke? Not war, nor armies, nor weapons. They were matters of love and of marriage, for Lothíriel is betrothed to a Man she does not wish to marry. Such things are a Lady's concerns, and I counseled her on them as best I could.\
\
'But now I must counsel her on these other concerns as well: weapons, and armies, and war. I echo the worry of Galdor: she must not underestimate the Heirs of Castamir, and the one they call 'The Scourge.' Lothíriel's father has been called to war in the East; but war finds her now in the West, and if either is lost there will be no hope for the other when the night has come.\
\
'Go to Dol Amroth and give her my warning. There is Elvish blood in her line, but it is no sense of kinship that drives me in this; it is the love I bear for the dark-haired woman who spoke to me of her hopes and her fears when the moon was high over the Sea, and banished sadness for a time.'","Travel to the entrance of Dol Amroth, and present yourself to the guards","Talk to Lothíriel in the Great Hall of Dol Amroth"},
[1882]={"'¡Mi Baya de Oro está lejos en su manantial, y yo estaba buscando lirios! ¡No tengo tiempo para perseguir pájaros! Pero, ¡hoy ahora! ¡Aragorn es un nombre que conozco, y un amigo del Viejo Tom!\
\
'Escucha entonces mi oferta: Mientras el Viejo Tom Bombadil busca cuervos agrios, tú recogerás lirios para mi hermosa. Vi algunos a lo largo del río, a un salto y un brinco de distancia. Solo sigue hasta que, ¡ding dong dillo, encuentres al el viejo Hombre-Sauce!\
\
'Cuidado con ese viejo Sauce Gris. Es un poderoso cantor. Te cantará hasta dormir y te ahogará, si no tienes cuidado.'","Trancos te dirigió a hablar con Tom Bombadil, el maestro del Bosque Viejo, para pedir su ayuda en el rastreo de los crebain que huyeron al bosque.","'¡Lirios blancos para la Hija del Río! ¡Más fuerte que los hobbits eres si superas al Hombre-Sauce en canto! ¡Ni un lirio aplastado, ni una hoja doblada!\
\
'El Viejo Tom es un tipo alegre, pero sabe cuándo es hora de bailar o de ir a cazar. Ha encontrado tus pájaros y no demasiado tarde. Si los buscas, entonces búscalos ahora, ¡a menos que desees dormir bajo la hierba verde!'","Libro 1, Capítulo 9: Lirios para la Hija del Río","Lleva los lirios a Tom Bombadil","Recolectados lirios grandes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¿Dónde están los lirios que necesito para mi hermosa dama? ¡Solo blancos para mi Baya de Oro, y hojas verdes!'","El río fluye hacia el oeste desde la casa de Tom Bombadil.\
\
Encontraste a Tom Bombadil y hablaste con la extraña criatura. Aunque al principio no estaba dispuesto a encontrar los crebain, al final cedió, si realizabas una tarea que consideraba mucho más importante. Desea que recojas lirios del río, cerca de alguien llamado Viejo Hombre-Sauce.","Recolecta lirios grandes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[1883]={"Has derrotado Uruks en Tham Celechir (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL}).","Encuentras un cuchillo corto de manufactura élfica enterrado en el montículo de escombros.","'En una colina al norte se alzan los restos de Tham Celechir. Si los Uruks esperan encontrar allí conocimientos sobre los Anillos, creo que se llevarán una decepción; pero esa ruina es el último lugar de descanso de muchos de mis parientes. ¿Trajeron consigo artefactos de poder durante su retirada? No puedo decirlo con certeza, pero debemos asegurarnos de que quede poco de lo que Saruman o sus guerreros pudieran hacer uso.\
\
'Cuando hayas hecho esto, vuelve aquí a Idhobel. Creo que entonces deberemos separarnos.'","Tanto Meneldir como Bregoleth deben volver pronto a su gente con lo que han aprendido aquí, pero primero la guerrera élfica desea oponerse a los enemigos que acechan en Tham Celechir.","Bregoleth espera en Idhobel noticias de tus éxitos en Tham Celechir, el Salón del Río Veloz.","'Encontraste Uruks en el Salón del Río Veloz, no lo dudo. ¿Pero encontraste algo más?'\
\
Le entregas a Bregoleth el cuchillo élfico que desenterraste entre los escombros de Tham Celechir. Ella sopla el polvo del puño y limpia la hoja.\
\
'A menos que esté muy equivocada, este es un puñal de la Compañía Resplandeciente, ${PLAYER}. Muchos fueron sus gloriosos hechos en la antigüedad, y lucharon largo tiempo contra Sauron y sus esbirros. De no ser por dignos como Celeborn y Glorfindel, que sobrevivieron a la guerra, o el heroico Oranoril, que no lo hizo, la caída de Eregion podría haber sido aún peor. Llevaré este puñal a Imladris, donde podrá mantenerse en un lugar de honor. Si en verdad es un arma de la Compañía Resplandeciente, es apropiado que descanse en el refugio por el cual su portador luchó y, probablemente, murió.'","'Mi pueblo huyó hacia el norte después de que Caras Gelebren fuera destruida por Sauron, y sus ejércitos los persiguieron. La historia de quienes se interpusieron en su camino y cayeron desafiándolo se cuenta en otra parte. Pero los defensores de uno de esos lugares resistieron un poco más que muchos otros: en Tham Celechir, el Salón del Río Veloz, Sauron logró su conquista a un precio amargo.\
\
'En una colina al norte aún se alzan sus ruinas. Si los Uruks esperan encontrar allí conocimientos sobre los Anillos, creo que se llevarán una decepción; pero esa ruina es el último lugar de descanso de muchos de mis parientes. ¿Trajeron consigo artefactos de poder durante su retirada? No puedo decirlo con certeza, pero debemos asegurarnos de que quede poco de lo que Saruman o sus guerreros pudieran usar.\
\
'Cuando hayas hecho esto, vuelve aquí a Idhobel. Creo que entonces deberemos separarnos.'","Busca montículos de escombros en Tham Celechir para encontrar artefactos notables.","Tham Celechir está ubicado en una colina al norte de Idhobel.\
\
Bregoleth quiere enfrentarse a los enemigos que ahora ocupan Tham Celechir, el Salón del Río Veloz.","Derrota Uruks en Tham Celechir (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL}).","Lleva el cuchillo élfico a Bregoleth en Idhobel.","Libro 1, Capítulo 9: El Salón del Río Veloz","Rebuscas en el montículo de escombros, pero no encuentras nada de interés."},
[1884]={"'Laerdan se encuentra en su habitación, en lo alto de las escaleras a la derecha al entrar en la fortaleza de esta isla. Dile que debemos recuperar Annúminas antes de que sea posible reclamar el palantír.'","Mordrambor te mira con frialdad y no dice nada.","Mordrambor se encuentra en la prisión, en lo alto de las escaleras tras la puerta de la izquierda al entrar en la fortaleza de la isla de Tinnudir, en Evendim.\
\
Tadan te ha dicho que espera con ansias la visita de Laerdan, ya que vigilar a Mordrambor no resulta agradable, especialmente desde que el prisionero ha comenzado a recitar las hazañas de sus compañeros.","'¿Lograste repeler los ataques contra tus amistades? No importa, pero admiro tu empeño frente a probabilidades tan abrumadoras.\
\
'No puedes prevalecer contra Guldurchir, ${PLAYER}, por fuerte o sabio que creas ser, pues Guldurchir empuña Tann Morgul.\
\
'La derrota de los Dúnedain será total cuando haga caer su poder sobre la ciudad.'","'Espero con ansias la visita de Laerdan, ${PLAYER}; el prisionero no es una compañía agradable, y he notado que me observa con miradas inquietantes.\
\
'Además, el aire aquí se siente sofocante. Veré si Forchon o Naethmunn pueden cubrir uno o dos turnos después de la visita de Laerdan. Me vendrá bien despejar la mente y poner fin a los constantes desvaríos del prisionero.\
\
'Se ha puesto a recitar las hazañas de sus camaradas, en especial de uno. Si no volviera a oír el nombre \\qGuldurchir\\q, sería un gran alivio.'","Mordrambor ha sido un prisionero útil, pero tanto Calenglad como Laerdan temen que aún conserve cierto poder para el engaño.","El Montaraz Tadan está de guardia en la prisión, en lo alto de las escaleras tras la puerta de la izquierda al entrar en la fortaleza de la isla de Tinnudir, en Evendim.\
\
Laerdan ha expresado su preocupación de que Mordrambor te esté manteniendo ocupado deliberadamente en Annúminas mientras Amarthiel busca a Narchuil con el palantír.","'¡Escúchalo! Es suficiente para volver loco a cualquiera, ${PLAYER}. Espero con ansias la visita de Laerdan, aunque solo sea para tener un respiro del incesante murmullo del prisionero.'","Laerdan se encuentra en su habitación, en lo alto de las escaleras tras la puerta de la derecha al entrar en la fortaleza de la isla de Tinnudir, en Evendim.\
\
Calenglad te ha dicho que Laerdan desea hablar contigo sobre el palantír y te ha pedido que intentes convencerlo de que los Dúnedain deben obtener una victoria decisiva en Annúminas antes de que sea posible recuperarlo.","'Mi intuición me dice que el prisionero se está aprovechando de nosotros, ${PLAYER}. Está tejiendo palabras para que Calenglad haga exactamente lo que Amarthiel desea: perder tiempo en batallas sin sentido mientras el verdadero trabajo, el trabajo peligroso, se lleva a cabo con el palantír.\
\
'Si te parece bien, habla con Tadan y dile que iré a verlo dentro de unas horas. Quiero recordarle el peligro que Mordrambor representa para todos, incluso estando prisionero.'","'${PLAYER}, ${PLAYER:bienvenido[m]|bienvenida[f]}. Me alegra que hayas venido. No pareces estar bien. No puedes defender toda Annúminas por tu cuenta, pese a los deseos de Calenglad.\
\
'Te pedí que vinieras porque quiero saber si Mordrambor te ha hablado del palantír. ¿No lo ha hecho? Me resulta muy significativo que te haya mantenido ocupado con asuntos militares en la ciudad, cuando sabemos que Amarthiel posee un palantír. Mi intuición me dice que Mordrambor nos está retrasando para servir a su ama. Su objetivo no ha cambiado: busca a Narchuil. No te dejes distraer por los encargos en los que intenta enredarte.\
\
'¿Podrías llevar mis palabras a Tadan, el Montaraz que custodia a Mordrambor? Dile que iré a verlo dentro de unas horas; quiero asegurarme de que esté alerta ante el peligro de los susurros del prisionero.'","'¡Escúchame! Conviene recordar las palabras de Laerdan: Mordrambor sigue siendo un servidor del Enemigo y, pese a lo útil de su información, nos causaría un gran daño si se le diera la oportunidad. Acompaño mis palabras de buen augurio con un recordatorio de cautela al tratar con él; es algo que ambos deberíamos tener muy presente.\
\
'Laerdan vino a hablar conmigo mientras estabas fuera. Quería saber si se habían logrado avances en la recuperación del palantír. Le hablé de nuestras victorias militares, pero no pareció alentado por la noticia. No coincidimos en este asunto, pero es evidente que nuestros éxitos en Annúminas son cruciales para arrebatárselo a Amarthiel.\
\
'No logré tranquilizarlo, y Laerdan pidió que lo visites en su habitación de la fortaleza cuando regreses. Tal vez puedas hacerle ver que este es el camino correcto. Annúminas debe ser recuperada antes de que podamos aspirar a arrancar el palantír de las garras de Amarthiel. Tenemos tiempo, ${PLAYER}. Díselo.'","Libro 10, Capítulo 10: No confíes en él"},
[1885]={"Nona has asked you to throw the dried herb bundles you collected into the cooking fire in the cave chamber with the dying man. She hopes it will improve his condition.","'You say that the man Nona has been trying to heal is the very man for whom we sought? Léodwig, the son of Harding? We found him, but it will be a bittersweet victory if he dies.\
\
'Everywhere we go we find rumour of this giant, ${PLAYER}, this Núrzum. What can we do about Núrzum?\
\
'We cannot engage him in combat, that much is clear. Attacking his feet might prove possible, if we could somehow avoid the attacks that were sure to follow. And by all accounts he brings the storms of winter with him wherever he treads... that will limit visibility, and make it difficult to strike him.\
\
'I have no military mind, ${PLAYER}. Núrzum seems invincible to me. But we will need to destroy him or Wildermore will not be safe. I do not know what to do.'","Nona is worried about the survivors of Byre Tor in her care, and wants you to help them if you can.","'These are just what I wanted, ${PLAYER}! Now go to the other chamber and throw these bundles on the fire. I hope the smell of the burning may revive him somewhat. It was a common practice in Lhanuch, and perhaps its magic will operate here as well.'","Collect dried herb bundles from Orcs in the High Knolls (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The smoke of the burning herbs has slightly revived the most injured of Nona's survivors.","'I do not know what can be done about the giant. I have managed to stay away from him so far, but it has not been easy.'","'The smoke has revived him? Those are happy tidings, ${PLAYER}!'","'Ah, I have nothing to contribute. What can I do against such a ferocious creature? I am no warrior. I am only an aged musician. Even Théoden King had no more use for me.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Completing this quest will unlock an optional interlude from Gléowine's map.</rgb>","You have found Léodwig, the son of Harding. He has been grievously wounded by Núrzum","'Orcs throughout the High Knolls may have dried herb bundles from Byre Tor in their possession. Defeat them and recover these bundles, for they may help my charges!'","'I am a warrior of the Uch-lûth, friend, I am no poet. I do not know this man's name, and none of the others I brought here have seen him before. His eyes do not see me, and his health is failing more rapidly with every hour that passes. He is a dying man, and that is what I call him, though it seem cruel.\
\
'I fear if nothing changes he will not live much longer.\
\
'Ymma told me the apothecary was attacked by the Orcs early during the fall of Byre Tor, and they stole many useful poultices and medicines. If you can recover these dried herb bundles from Orcs throughout the High Knolls, we might use them to slow his decline, for a time.'","Nona is in her cave in the High Knolls, and is waiting for you to return with the dried herb bundles you collected.","Throw dried herb bundles into the fire in the other chamber","'We know his size is great, but what of his intellect? Could we trick Núrzum in some way?'","'The old ways are best, it seems! I am heartened to know the magic of the healers of Lhanuch works even in the land of the horse-lords.\
\
'The most-injured of my charges is named Léodwig, and he is the man for whom you sought, ${PLAYER}? What a wonder that they should be one and the same. My father Suvulch would find some meaning in this, but for me I see fortune only. Still, it is a happy fortune, if he lives. That is not yet certain.\
\
'For as long as the giant lives, the people are in danger. What will we do about Núrzum?'","'Who is... who is there? Are you... a friend? The giant! The giant returns!'\
\
The man struggles violently for a moment before breathing deeply and attaining a measure of calm.\
\
'I... I am Léodwig, the son of Harding, Aldor of the North-march. I came into Wildermore to learn what... but no use. Separated from my men... the storm arose... lost! Lost in a gale!'\
\
Léodwig twists and turns before settling into a calm once more.\
\
'The giant's name is Núrzum. He... he brings the snows and the wind. Something he carries... I think. He saw me in the snow near the city... I was lifted in the air... a thunderous blast of hot air... and then... and then!'\
\
Léodwig shakes and will say no more, but the odour of the burning herbs seems to have broken him out of his stupor.","Bring the dried herb bundles to Nona in her cave","You have found the man you came into Wildermore to find, and should now tell your companions.","Orcs throughout the High Knolls may carry dried herb bundles.\
\
Nona has asked you to recover dried herb bundles the Orcs stole from Byre Tor to try and speed the recovery of the people in her care.","'He lives, for now, and is the very man we came here to find: Léodwig, the son of Harding. What would Harding say to know his son was saved by a Dunlending girl? Perhaps it is best not to think of that for now, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'I can piece together some of his story from what he has said. He was separated from his men when the storm rose; that must have been Núrzum approaching. He made for the most visible landmark he could find: it must have been the hill upon which Byre Tor is built. Ill fortune for Léodwig, for that seems to have been Núrzum's destination.\
\
'We must do something about Núrzum, but what? He is too strong for us to fight directly. Could we trick him in some way? I will think on it, ${PLAYER}, but I cannot promise a solution will present itself to me.'","Collected dried herb bundle (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'You have not brought me the bundles?'","Talk to the dying man","Gléowine is in Nona's cave, and wishes to speak with you.","Book 10, Chapter 10: Recipe for Remedy","'Throw the dried herb bundles into the fire in the other chamber. Perhaps that will help improve his condition. He could be doing little worse, that much at least is so.'","'Perhaps we could stay out of the giant's notice, and strike a grievous blow when he is not prepared? We know so little of him that undertaking this would be a great risk.'"},
[1886]={"'Mi patético carcelero está en lo cierto: Guldurchir supervisa la batalla desde Menelband, un patio en el nivel más alto de la ciudad. Eres fuerte, ${PLAYER}, pero Guldurchir lo es aún más. Te matará y tus amistades serán destruidas por completo.\
\
'No puedes aspirar a arrebatarle Tann Morgul. Sería una locura.'","El Montaraz Tadan se encuentra en la prisión, en lo alto de las escaleras tras la puerta de la izquierda al entrar en la fortaleza de la isla de Tinnudir, en Evendim.\
\
Tadan te sacó de tu ensimismamiento, impidiendo que liberaras a Mordrambor y le entregaras Tann Morgul.","'¡Aléjate de mi vista, gusano despreciable! ¡Pagarás por tu fracaso!'","Libro 10, Capítulo 11: La contención de Guldurchir","'Sí, ${PLAYERNAME:mi amigo[m]|mi amiga[f]}, sí...\
\
'Desata mis ataduras y entrégame la reliquia que tomaste de Guldurchir: Tann Morgul, legado del Númenor caído...'","'¡Por fin hemos llegado a este punto, ${PLAYER}, lo presiento! Custodiar al prisionero no ha sido fácil, pero todo habrá valido la pena si logramos derrotar a Guldurchir antes de que se le permita usar Tann Morgul contra nosotros.\
\
'También estamos de suerte, porque me he enfrentado a Guldurchir y sé dónde se encuentra. Poco después de que Annúminas fuera tomada, un pequeño grupo logró abrirse paso hasta el nivel más alto de la ciudad. Allí, en un patio lleno de ídolos funestos y adornos malditos sobre Echad Garthadir, nos encontramos con Guldurchir. Nos rechazó, y nuestro asalto terminó en derrota.\
\
'Ese patio se llama Menelband. Si logras avanzar por la ciudad hasta llegar a Menelband, tal vez puedas derrotar a Guldurchir y arrebatarle Tann Morgul. ¡El día podría ser nuestro!'","Lleva Tann Morgul a Mordrambor","'¿Guldurchir ha sido derrotado? ¡Estoy lleno de asombro, ${PLAYER}!'","'Guldurchir supervisa la batalla por la ciudad desde Menelband, el patio más elevado de Annúminas. ¡Derótalo y arrebátale Tann Morgul, ${PLAYER}!'","Mordrambor se encuentra en la prisión, en lo alto de las escaleras tras la puerta de la izquierda al entrar en la fortaleza de la isla de Tinnudir, en Evendim.\
\
Has logrado lo que Mordrambor creía imposible: derrotaste a Guldurchir y le arrebataste Tann Morgul. Ahora deberías llevar el artefacto a Mordrambor para demostrarle que estaba equivocado.","Mordrambor te ha dicho que uno de sus hermanos, un Númenóreano Negro llamado Guldurchir, posee un artefacto de gran maldad que será utilizado para destruir a los Dúnedain.","'¿Qué crees que estabas haciendo, ? No sé qué me ocurrió, pero algo me sacó de un profundo letargo y te vi a punto de desatar al prisionero.\
\
'Debes reforzar tu voluntad contra sus artimañas. ¿Acaso Laerdan no te lo advirtió? Nuestro prisionero es traicionero y no podemos bajar la guardia ni un instante.\
\
'Yo me encargaré de tomar Tann Morgul y llevarlo a Calenglad. Creo que no es prudente que pases demasiado tiempo en compañía de Mordrambor, . Siempre llamándote \\q${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}\\q... No confío en él, y tú tampoco deberías hacerlo.'","'¿No has tomado Tann Morgul de Guldurchir? ¿Cómo puede ser?'","'No te impediré hablar con quien me custodia, ${PLAYER}. Es sumamente molesto, pero quizás puedas enseñarle a respetar a quienes considera superiores.'","Lleva Tann Morgul a Tadan","'¿Dónde está Tann Morgul, ${PLAYER}? ¿A dónde pudo haber ido?'","'Últimamente no me he sentido muy bien, ${PLAYER}. Tengo la cabeza pesada, como si estuviera llena de agua, y no logro despejarla.\
\
'Debe ser cansancio. ¡Ojalá pudiera descansar de los constantes murmullos del prisionero!'","Guldurchir se encuentra en Menelband, un patio situado en el nivel más alto de Annúminas.\
\
El Montaraz Tadan te ha indicado dónde encontrar a Guldurchir y espera que logres derrotar a este Númenóreano Negro antes de que se le permita usar la reliquia que porta, Tann Morgul, contra los Dúnedain.","El Montaraz Tadan está de guardia en la prisión, en lo alto de las escaleras tras la puerta de la izquierda al entrar en la fortaleza de la isla de Tinnudir, en Evendim.\
\
Mordrambor te ha hablado de Tann Morgul, el artefacto que porta uno de sus hermanos, y afirma que su poder puede destruir a los Dúnedain. Tadan desea hablar contigo sobre este nuevo acontecimiento.","'Nos hemos enfrentado varias veces a Guldurchir; lo conozco bien, y cada encuentro con él ha dejado un recuerdo siniestro.\
\
'El patio de Menelband es su puesto. Dirígete al este desde Echad Garthadir hasta ver una pendiente empinada que desciende hacia el sur; súbela y gira de inmediato hacia el oeste. Eso te llevará a Menelband, en el nivel más alto de la ciudad.\
\
'No me sorprende la noticia del artefacto que porta, Tann Morgul. Lo que sí me sorprende es que Amarthiel le haya ordenado no usarlo. ¿Qué ocurrirá cuando abandone esa contención?'","'Nunca había oído hablar de Tann Morgul hasta ahora, ${PLAYER}, pero sí conozco a Guldurchir: maldad pura y sin compasión. Ten presente el peligro si decides enfrentarlo.'","'Conozco a Guldurchir: es uno de los lugartenientes Númenóreanos Negros de Amarthiel y, como tal, uno de los hermanos de Mordrambor. Me resulta extraño que nuestro prisionero lo traicione con tanta facilidad.\
\
'Aun así, Mordrambor ha dicho la verdad hasta ahora. Si este artefacto es tan mortífero como nos ha hecho creer, no podemos permitir que permanezca en manos de Guldurchir.\
\
'Menelband es un patio situado en el nivel más alto de Annúminas, y desde allí Guldurchir supervisa la batalla.'","'¿Deseas saber más sobre Tann Morgul, ${PLAYER}? Lo imaginaba. Es una reliquia del Númenor antiguo, corrompida mediante las artes oscuras de mis hermanos y confiada a Guldurchir para su custodia. ¿Te preguntas por qué no la ha usado contra la ciudad? La razón es simple: Amarthiel le prohibió hacerlo hasta haber obtenido todo el entretenimiento posible de las patéticas luchas de los Dúnedain.\
\
'Ese momento se acerca. Si deseas aplazar tu derrota total, harías bien en arrebatarle Tann Morgul a Guldurchir, y pronto. Su contención no durará para siempre.\
\
'¿Mi carcelero tiene algo que decir? ¿Qué podría ser, ${PLAYER}?'"},
[1887]={"Léodwig is still too exhausted to speak, which is good because you have no favourable news to report about Núrzum.","Léodwig is exhausted from his recent exertions, but you remember what he wanted: an end to the giant, an end to Núrzum. You are not yet certain how to bring this about.","Nona is in the other chamber of her cave in the High Knolls, and is waiting to speak with you.","Book 10, Chapter 11: Return to Byre Tor","'Thank you, my friend. Knowing those keepsakes and heirlooms are no longer in the hands of the Orcs is the best tonic for my hurts I can imagine.\
\
'When I am fully recovered, I will look for other survivors of the attack so I may return their keepsakes. It is the least I can do.'","Collected stolen heirloom (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collect stolen heirlooms from Orcs within Byre Tor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Gléowine has determined that he can best help the survivors of Byre Tor by sending you to help them with their problems. He has asked you to speak to each of them and learn what it is they most want.","Return the stolen heirlooms to Elda in Nona's cave","Defeat Foshnu or Krítar in Byre Tor","'I believe Foshnu and Krítar will still be somewhere within Byre Tor, counting their spoils. Go back to the city and show them the people of Wildermore do not give up so easily! Only slay one of these two Orcs, however. Leave me the other one, and I will complete the lesson.'","'The horses stand no chance against the Orcs while they remain tied up at the stables, ${PLAYER}. Untie the horses and set them free and they will have as much a chance of survival as they gave me. Perhaps moreso!'","Free horses from the stables of Byre Tor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'You found none?'","Gléowine is in Nona's cave in the High Knolls, and will be pleased to hear of your successful return to Byre Tor.","'Do you see how much their spirits have improved? They have been inspired by your deeds and your actions, and though Byre Tor remains in enemy hands you have helped to restore some of the fire to their hearts!\
\
'I must tell you, ${PLAYER}, you are an inspiration not only to these survivors in Nona's care, but to this old man as well. Thank you for showing me that there are those out in the world still able to do some good. Perhaps I will write another song!'","'I cannot thank you enough for recovering so many keepsakes from the Orcs.'","Speak with Nona","'Horn and I spoke about many things while you were away, ${PLAYER}. I have come to a decision.'","You have done much good in Byre Tor, and should return to Nona's cave to tell the people in her care what you accomplished.","'Thank you for freeing the horses in Byre Tor. I cannot thank you enough for showing them, and me, that kindness.'","You save the other one for Ymma, when she is healthy enough for vengeance","'What is it I want? I want the Orcs driven from Byre Tor! I want to return to my home!'\
\
Elda sighs.\
\
'That will take some doing, will it not? There is something else, though. The thing that most stirs my heart, most fills me with anger against the Orcs, is the brief sight I had before that chunk of masonry took me from the battle. I saw the Orcs looting a house, the house of one of my neighbours. They had found a wooden carving of a horse, a crude thing, to be honest, of poor craft, and were waving it about. It meant nothing to them, but I knew it for what it was: it was a child's first attempt at carving. It would mean little to most, but to that boy's family it was no doubt priceless.\
\
'I cannot bear the thought of such heirlooms in the hands of the Orcs, ${PLAYER}. When you return to Byre Tor to satisfy the requests of my fellows, please remember to recover such things from the Orcs you slay.'","Orcs in and around Byre Tor may possess stolen heirlooms for you to recover. The horses of Byre Tor can be found tied up at the stables near the top of the hill on which the city stands. Foshnu and Krítar will be somewhere within the city.\
\
You have learned what the survivors of the attack on Byre Tor under Nona's care desire of you, and now you should make certain you can accomplish what they want.","'I am still... not myself... but I will do my best to speak...'\
\
Léodwig rubs his eyes blearily.\
\
'What do I want...? I want revenge upon... that great... lumbering... giant. Núrzum... he slew my men... almost devoured me... Wídfara...'\
\
You tell him that Wídfara survived the encounter with Núrzum and made his way back to Scylfig, where you met him.\
\
'Ah... very glad... he was a tough... a tough one. In the snow I... could not see... the way to go. Núrzum must be... defeated... or...'\
\
Exhausted by the effort, Léodwig leans back and can say no more.","'Speak to each of the survivors and learn what it is will make them most happy, ${PLAYER}.'","'I cannot bear to think of the priceless heirlooms of my friends and neighbours in the hands of the Orcs. Return to Byre Tor and wrest these keepsakes from the foul creatures that have stolen them!'","'Thank you for showing this old man there is still good in the world, ${PLAYER}.'","'You are back, and I can tell you have defeated one of the Orcs responsible. Wait! Do not tell me which one you saved for me! I look forward to discovering that on my own.'\
\
Ymma gives you a truly frightening smile, and you quickly excuse yourself.","Freed a horse from the stables (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'What is it I want? That is an easy question to answer, ${PLAYER}, because my sleep has been troubled by the same thought, over and over: did I do wrong by the horses in Byre Tor?'\
\
Elfgifu frowns.\
\
'Were it not for the horses at the stable in Byre Tor, I would not be alive today. I am certain of it. Their panic caused me to learn of the attack with enough time to make it partway down the hill before the snowstorm covered everything. And with it came the giant.\
\
'I cannot bear to think of those horses still tied up at the stables, helpless against the Orcs. What do I want? I want you to untie the horses at the stables in Byre Tor and let them run free! That will give them the same chance I had of escaping a cruel death at the hands of the Orcs.'","'What do I want? I have already told you! I remember the names of the Orcs that led the attack on my friends and my family, ${PLAYER}. Foshnu. Krítar. I want them slain.'\
\
Ymma thinks for a moment.\
\
'Do not misunderstand me, my helpful friend! I want them slain... but I want them to know it was a woman of Byre Tor that has ended their lives. Perhaps this will suffice: find and slay either Foshnu or Krítar. Save one of them for me. When I am well enough to fight I will seek out the one you have spared and fulfill my vengeance upon him.\
\
'You will find Foshnu or Krítar somewhere within my city. And in a few days I will find the remaining one and end his life. We are agreed?'","'Thank you for freeing the horses. Now they will have as much of a chance of escape as I myself did. I wish them good fortune!'","Léodwig remains too exhausted to speak.","'The Orcs will learn not to treat the lives of the Rohirrim so lightly.'","'Wait a moment! What am I saying? There is still something I can do!'\
\
For the first time you can remember since arriving in Wildermore, Gléowine favours you with a smile.\
\
'How can I have forgotten my own lessons? When I was instructing Horn in the ways of music, one of the very first things I taught him was that the minstrel's greatest power is that of inspiration. Music lets us shine a light into the darkest corner of our heart, bringing into it hope and good feeling. When Horn was still young I told him this, for I believed it. And I believe it still!\
\
'Speak to the survivors of Byre Tor in this cave, ${PLAYER}, and find out what it is they desire. And then make it happen!'\
\
Gléowine's smile is even more broad this time.\
\
'What? You are the adventurer here, ${PLAYER}. I am sending them hope, that is all. I am sending them you!'","Gléowine has realized that although he is no great warrior, he can still help the people of Byre Tor sheltered by Nona in his own way."},
[1888]={"Golodir se encuentra en el campamento de los Montaraces de Gath Forthnír, en el este de Angmar.\
\
Laerdan te ha enviado a hablar con Golodir para conseguir algún medio con el que recuperar el palantír de Amarthiel.","'¡${PLAYER}, te doy la bienvenida! Te ves mejor que la última vez que te vi. ¿Por fin lograste descansar un poco? El tiempo del combate abierto ha terminado. Calenglad es sabio y fuerte, pero su orgullo lo ha cegado: no recuperará Annúminas antes de que Amarthiel localice a Narchuil.\
\
'Mordrambor es una criatura de mentiras, pero al provocarme creo que cometió un error. Dijo que Amarthiel me esperaba en Barad Tironn, ¿lo recuerdas? Barad Tironn era el lugar donde los reyes de Annúminas impartían justicia y escuchaban las preocupaciones de su gente. Las crónicas no coinciden del todo en este punto, pero varias registran que el palantír de Annúminas se guardaba en Barad Tironn para uso de los reyes. Ese palantír de Annúminas se perdió, hundido bajo el mar, pero con toda certeza es desde allí donde Amarthiel se esfuerza usando el palantír que ha recuperado.\
\
'Debemos asaltar Barad Tironn y recuperar el palantír, ${PLAYER}. ¡Pero espera! No acudas todavía a Calenglad. Este palantír ha sido ligado al mal del Enemigo, y el simple contacto con él nos causaría daño. Necesitamos algún medio para transportarlo. Golodir posee ese medio en Gath Forthnír. Aunque recordarle los hechos de su caída pueda causarle dolor, debes hablar con Golodir sobre esto. Solo él puede proporcionarnos lo que necesitamos.'","Laerdan ha descubierto la ubicación del palantír y ha determinado un medio para arrebatárselo a Amarthiel.","'Debes viajar a Gath Forthnír para hablar con Golodir, ${PLAYER}. Solo él puede proporcionarnos el medio para transportar el palantír. Cuando regreses, organizaremos un asalto a Barad Tironn junto a Calenglad y sus Montaraces.\
\
'Debemos actuar con rapidez, ${PLAYER}. Ve de inmediato a ver a Golodir.'","Mordrambor te mira con odio en los ojos, pero no dice nada.","'¡Date prisa y habla con Laerdan, ${PLAYER}! Su habitación está en lo alto de las escaleras, al otro lado de la fortaleza. ¡Te está esperando! No te preocupes, yo llevaré Tann Morgul a Calenglad.'","Laerdan se encuentra en su habitación, en lo alto de las escaleras tras la puerta de la derecha al entrar en la fortaleza de la isla de Tinnudir, en Evendim.\
\
Tadan te ha dicho que Laerdan cree haber descubierto la ubicación del palantír y sabe cómo puede recuperarse.","Libro 10, Capítulo 12: Un medio para transportarlo","'Laerdan vino a verme, tal como dijiste que haría, y me dijo prácticamente lo mismo: que nuestro prisionero sigue siendo peligroso. ¡Parece que no presté a esas palabras toda la atención que debía!\
\
'Pero hay algo que debo contarte y que este desafortunado asunto con Tann Morgul había apartado de mi mente hasta ahora. Laerdan ha descubierto la ubicación del palantír de Amarthiel y ha ideado un plan para recuperarlo.\
\
'Está esperándote en su habitación. No quiero decir nada más mientras el prisionero esté presente, pero deberías hablar con Laerdan de inmediato.'","'Golodir es alguien de buen corazón, pero no comprendo cómo puede ayudarnos a recuperar el palantír.\
\
'Se encuentra en Gath Forthnír, en el este de Angmar, si Laerdan dice que debes ir a buscarlo.'","'¡${PLAYER}! No esperaba verte de nuevo tan pronto. ¿Por qué has venido a verme?'"},
[1889]={"'I am excited to learn why Núrzum came first to Byre Tor, ${PLAYER}! Perhaps we will find some clue to defeating the giant within the city!'\
\
Horn looks slightly embarrassed.\
\
'What? Yes, it will be nice to adventure again with Nona, but this is really about defeating Núrzum. Why do you give me such a look as that, ${PLAYER}? I am thinking only of Wildermore.'","'We will find something in Byre Tor that will help us deal with Núrzum, I know we will!'","'Speak to Horn and Corudan about this journey, and tell me when you are ready to depart for Byre Tor.'","Nona is in her cave in the High Knolls, preparing to depart for Byre Tor.","Nona has decided to return to Byre Tor to learn why Núrzum came there first, and perhaps discover some means of defeating the giant.","'You agree with this plan? I do not know how I feel about it. There may be some insight to be gained concerning the giant, for he certainly seems to be drawn to Byre Tor, but I worry that Horn is letting his feelings for Nona cloud his judgement.\
\
'If you are willing to embark upon this journey, so am I. But keep your wits about you. I fear Horn may not.'","Talk to Nona and travel to Byre Tor","'That was an eye-opening experience for certain, ${PLAYER}! I have heard tales of Núrzum, as have we all! But there is nothing to compare seeing him at such a close distance. We cannot hope to defeat him by ourselves.'\
\
Corudan looks thoughtful for a moment, considering alternatives.\
\
'I believe I have the answer, ${PLAYER}. We need the very earth to turn against him. We need the strength of the Ents!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Completing this quest will unlock an optional interlude from Gléowine's map.</rgb>","Book 10, Chapter 12: Núrzum","Horn and Corudan are in Nona's cave, and you should speak to them about the day's journey.","You have narrowly survived an encounter with Núrzum and should now speak to Corudan in Nona's cave.","'Are you ready to depart for Byre Tor? I do not wish to be gone for very long, but we should search the city to learn of Núrzum's interest in it.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This instance may not be completed in a Fellowship.</rgb>","'I agree that we must do something about Núrzum. I simply do not know what we can possibly learn that will help us rid Wildermore of the threat he poses.'","'Why did Núrzum come first to Byre Tor? He seems to spend a great deal of time around that city. So many of this land's problems stem from him. Until he is defeated, none of the people here will be safe.\
\
'Horn has proposed that we return to Byre Tor and look for some means of defeating Núrzum. What is it about the city that drew the giant there so early? I cannot leave the people here for long, but for a few hours they will be fine in Gléowine's care.\
\
'What do you think? Speak with Horn and Corudan about this last adventure, and tell me when you are ready to depart.'"},
[1890]={"Talk to Corudan in Leaflock's mead","Corudan has decided that only the might of the Ents will have a chance of defeating Núrzum.","Corudan is in Leaflock's mead, in Balewood.","Find the glade of the oldest Ent in Balewood","'Look! What a wonder! If I am not very much mistaken, this Ent is even older than Rúdhrif!\
\
'See if you can get his attention, ${PLAYER}.'","Leaflock remains asleep.","You have come to Balewood to petition Leaflock the Ent for help against Núrzum.","Leaflock has gone back to sleep","Talk to the Ent and ask him for help against Núrzum","You and Corudan have stumbled upon the glade of an ancient and very tired Ent.","'We will need this Ent's help against Núrzum. Even asleep he appears to have the very strength of the earth!'","'You saw the great strength of Rúdhrif in the Eaves of Fangorn, ${PLAYER}! How unfortunate that Baldbark is so far away, or we might call upon him to help. No, we must search for aid closer at hand.\
\
'The Balewood is not far from here, and perhaps an Ent or three might be found within it! You and I should go there and seek for the oldest Ent we can find. Only he will have the authority to command such an attack as we will need if Núrzum is to be defeated.'\
\
You ask Corudan if such an Ent would trouble himself to help, considering how coldly you were received by Baldbark, and the Elf seems puzzled.\
\
'Why, of course he would. Surely a giant such as Núrzum must pose some threat to the Ents as well, mustn't he? I will mark a number of glades on the map, and we can search them until we find one with an old enough Ent for our purposes.'","Somewhere in the Balewood, an old Ent sleeps. Only he will have the authority to order an attack upon Núrzum.","You politely greet the Ent, and nothing happens for a long time. Eventually, a baleful eye slowly turns to look at you.\
\
'Hooooom?'\
\
You introduce yourself as ${PLAYER} and ask him for his name. More long minutes pass.\
\
'Leaflock...' breathe the leaves in the canopy.\
\
You ask if he knows of Núrzum the giant and the baleful eye ponderously swings closed. This may take longer than you expected.","'I have seen many wonders while on this journey with you. I do not doubt we will find Ents within the Balewood. However, we must find one old enough and with enough authority to become involved in these affairs, and that may not be as easy.'","Book 10, Chapter 13: Searching the Balewood","'Can it be? Is this the Ent for whom we seek?'","A tall and craggy figure stands in this glade. You almost passed it by!","'We have found an incredibly old Ent. That is the good.'\
\
Corudan smiles grimly, ready for a challenge.\
\
'It may take some work to wake him to our need. That is the bad.'"},
[1891]={"Laerdan se encuentra en su habitación en la fortaleza de la isla de Tinnudir, en Evendim. La habitación de Laerdan está en lo alto de las escaleras tras la puerta de la derecha al entrar en el torreón.\
\
Golodir te ha entregado una bolsa de tela finamente tejida que se utilizaba para cubrir el palantír en Carn Dûm cuando no estaba en uso. También te advirtió que no tocaras el palantír con las manos y que previnieras a Laerdan de no subestimar al enemigo.","Habla con Laerdan","'Mi carcelero es un necio, ${PLAYER}, pero ni siquiera él es tan necio como tú, con tu orgullo y tu impulso irresistible por hacer el bien. Y aun así, ¿qué es el bien? ¡No has hecho más que lo que la regente de Angmar y yo, su servidor más poderoso, deseábamos de ti! No fue una casualidad que yo llegara a la tumba del ya fallecido Elendil con tan pocos sirvientes. ¿De verdad creíste que Amarthiel arriesgaría la vida de alguien tan valioso sin motivo?\
\
'Mientras te mantenía ocupado con encargos por la ciudad y viajes a las lejanas orillas del vasto Nenuial, ella contemplaba el palantír que recuperó de Carn Dûm, forzándolo a mostrarle aquello que busca. Ahora soy más poderoso que Guldurchir, pues fue por sugerencia de Amarthiel que te dije que él portaba Tann Morgul. Pretendía usarlo para disputarle el dominio de Angmar; tú fuiste una pieza útil para eliminarlo. Amarthiel te lo agradecerá.\
\
'Pero ahora he completado mi tarea más importante, la misión para la cual ella me envió a ti, ${PLAYER}: entregar a Laerdan en Barad Tironn. Ella tiene mucho preparado para ese elfo, mucho que ha aguardado durante largo tiempo. ¿Creíste que Laerdan era inocente? Entonces eres dos veces imbécil, o incluso más. Corre a ver a quien consideras tu guía, ${PLAYER}, y dile a Calenglad cuán grande ha sido tu error: Laerdan no regresará de Barad Tironn, o si lo hace, será en una forma que nadie podrá reconocer, completamente retorcida y malvada. Solo me queda una tarea más, y saborearé cada instante de su cumplimiento.'","El Montaraz Tadan se encuentra en la prisión, en lo alto de las escaleras tras la puerta de la izquierda al entrar en la fortaleza de la isla de Tinnudir, en Evendim.\
\
Laerdan ha dejado una nota para ti en su puerta, indicando que ha partido hacia Barad Tironn para enfrentarse a Amarthiel en solitario. Debes mostrar esta nota a Tadan de inmediato.","'¡El prisionero tejió una horrible hechicería para empujar a Laerdan a aventurarse solo en Barad Tironn! ¡Pregúntale y verás si se atreve a negarlo!'","'Puedo sentir tu desesperación, ${PLAYER}. Para mí tiene un sabor dulce y anuncia que tu final se acerca.'","'Dices que vienes de parte de Laerdan y que cree que podría desempeñar algún papel en la recuperación del palantír que fue tomado de Carn Dûm. ¡La Piedra Vidente es puro mal! Ahora lo sé, y desearía no haber sido obligado nunca a posar la mirada en ella. Mordirith pagó por su tormento sobre mí, pero ni siquiera eso bastará para saldar su deuda. ¡Ningún acto de venganza devolverá a mi querida y perdida Lorniel!\
\
'Laerdan dice la verdad. Incluso cuando Mordirith me sacó de las puertas de Carn Dûm, con las imágenes odiosas del palantír aún ardiendo en mi mente, llevaba en la mano la tela negra con la que se cubría la Piedra Vidente cuando no se usaba. Los terribles sucesos de aquel día casi borraron ese recuerdo de mi mente, pero ahora lo recuerdo. Sostén el palantír solo con esta bolsa de tela finamente tejida; de lo contrario, la piedra intentará mostrarte cosas capaces de llevarte a la desesperación. ¡No toques el palantír sin esta bolsa! No deseo que sufras lo que yo tuve que sufrir.\
\
'Entrega a Laerdan mis mejores deseos, pero adviértele que no subestime a nuestro enemigo. Es un elfo noble y sincero, pero en él he reconocido la pesada carga que he llevado desde que perdí a Lorniel. Algo roe su corazón, y temo que le cause un gran daño si no se protege de ello.'","Recoge la nota de Laerdan","Laerdan considera que el momento de recuperar Annúminas ya ha pasado. Ahora toda la atención debe centrarse en arrebatarle el palantír a Amarthiel antes de que pueda descubrir la ubicación del perdido Narchuil.","'¿Qué es esto? ¿Una nota de Laerdan?\
\
'¡Es mi culpa, ${PLAYER}! ¿Cómo pude ser tan imprudente? Laerdan se ofreció a vigilar al prisionero por un tiempo y acepté. No me he sentido bien últimamente y pensé que un poco de aire fresco me vendría bien; te lo comenté, si lo recuerdas.\
\
'El prisionero debió decirle algo a Laerdan durante ese tiempo, tejiendo alguna maraña vil de palabras. ¡Qué triste ironía que Laerdan sucumbiera a esta traición, cuando tantas veces nos habló de su peligro!'","Nota de Laerdan recogida","Calenglad se encuentra en el campamento de los Montaraces de la isla de Tinnudir, en Evendim.\
\
Mordrambor te ha revelado su propósito: enviar a Laerdan junto a Amarthiel en Barad Tironn y mantenerte ocupado con tareas triviales en Annúminas y Evendim mientras su ama hacía uso del palantír que posee. Debes llevar estas dolorosas noticias a Calenglad.","Libro 10, Capítulo 13: El plan llevado a cabo","'Cada decisión que he tomado ha salido mal, ${PLAYER}. Mis pensamientos de victoria se convierten en ceniza, incluso cuando parecían tan cercanos. Que Laerdan pague este precio por el orgullo equivocado de los Dúnedain me llena de pesar. ¡Que mil maldiciones caigan sobre Mordrambor y su funesta ama!\
\
'No, no cederé al desaliento, aunque todo parezca más oscuro. Nuestro prisionero es una criatura de engaños y mentiras, y pese a sus crueles susurros, hemos logrado grandes victorias en Annúminas. ¿Podría tratarse de un ardid nacido de la desesperación de un cautivo cuyos planes no dieron el fruto esperado? ¿Es posible que la búsqueda de Amarthiel no haya avanzado como deseaba y que Mordrambor intente ahora sembrar en nosotros una desesperación infundada?\
\
'Aún podríamos salvar a Laerdan y recuperar el palantír, tal como era su intención, ${PLAYER}. Aunque se haya marchado, los Dúnedain quizá puedan corresponder a su amistad. Un último asalto en los escalones de Barad Tironn podría permitirte a ti y a tus aliados entrar en sus muros, ${PLAYER}, y entonces veremos si las palabras de Mordrambor encierran verdad. Veremos si ha llegado la hora del desaliento, o si nuestra mayor victoria está a punto de alcanzarse.'","Hay una nota clavada en la puerta de Laerdan","Lleva la nota de Laerdan a Calenglad","'¿Qué es esto? ¿Una nota en la puerta de Laerdan? Temo que solo pueda significar desgracia, ${PLAYER}, y temo por su seguridad.\
\
'Debes leer la nota, aunque sea difícil. Necesitamos saber hacia dónde ha decidido encaminarse Laerdan.'","'Si tocas el palantír con las manos, el Enemigo podría mostrarte cosas capaces de helarte el corazón. Usa únicamente la bolsa de tela finamente tejida que te entregué para transportarlo; aun así, el efecto de la Piedra Vidente sobre la mente puede ser considerable. ¡Refuerza tu voluntad frente a ello!\
\
'Regresa con esto a Laerdan junto a mis mejores deseos, pero adviértele que no subestime a nuestro enemigo. Reconozco en él la carga que he llevado desde la pérdida de Lorniel, y temo por su destino.'","Mordrambor te observa con aire autosuficiente, con una media sonrisa dibujada en los labios, pero no dice nada.","Mordrambor se encuentra en la prisión, en lo alto de las escaleras tras la puerta de la izquierda al entrar en la fortaleza de la isla de Tinnudir, en Evendim.\
\
El Montaraz Tadan te ha contado que Laerdan pidió vigilar al prisionero por un tiempo, para que Tadan pudiera tomar un respiro del aire sofocante de la prisión. Durante ese lapso, Tadan cree que Mordrambor obró una vil hechicería sobre Laerdan que llevó al elfo a aventurarse solo en Barad Tironn. Deberías hablar con Mordrambor sobre esta traición.","'¡Son noticias terribles, ${PLAYER}! Hemos sido muy imprudentes, y Laerdan debe pagar el precio de nuestro error.\
\
'Ve de inmediato a llevar estas funestas novedades a Calenglad; sin duda sabrá qué se puede hacer, si es que aún hay algo por hacer.'","'¿No tienes nada para mí, ${PLAYER}? ¿Cómo puede ser?'","Una nota de Laerdan está clavada en la puerta de su habitación en la fortaleza de la isla de Tinnudir, en Evendim.\
\
Has regresado de Gath Forthnír con una bolsa de tela finamente tejida con la que puedes transportar el palantír, pero Laerdan parece haberse marchado. Sin embargo, dejó una nota para ti en su puerta."},
[1892]={"'He demorado demasiado, con la esperanza de recuperar la ciudad de las fuerzas de Angmar, pero ahora veo que la victoria en Annúminas no será completa si Amarthiel llega a conocer la ubicación de Narchuil. Habríamos cambiado una victoria aquí por una derrota en otro lugar. Esa era la lección de Laerdan, y no supe verla.\
\
'Habla conmigo cuando tus aliados estén listos y lanzaremos el asalto final contra Barad Tironn. Si tenemos éxito, tendrás acceso a la cámara interior, donde alguien del grupo deberá tomar el palantír y llevarlo hasta la entrada, donde estaré esperando. Si cuentan con la bolsa de tela finamente tejida que te dio Golodir, el palantír no debería causar daño. Protejan a quien lleve el palantír de los ataques del enemigo.\
\
'Mucho depende de esto, ${PLAYER}, pues no tendremos otra oportunidad. Si encuentras a Laerdan en las profundidades de Barad Tironn, haz lo que puedas, pero no pongas al grupo en peligro innecesariamente. Recuperar la Piedra Vidente es la prioridad. Es lo que él habría querido: que el ojo de Angmar quede cegado una vez más.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión está pensada para una comunidad. Si decides realizarla en solitario, recibirás un bono de inspiración, pero el desafío será muy grande.</rgb>","'La victoria tiene un sabor amargo, pues Laerdan ha caído en manos del Enemigo y no contamos con fuerzas suficientes para lanzar otro asalto contra Barad Tironn. Temo que se haya perdido para nosotros y, aunque el palantír ya no esté en poder de Amarthiel, parece que logró descubrir al menos parte de lo que buscaba. Solo el tiempo la separa ahora de recuperar Narchuil, el anillo que perdió hace tanto.\
\
'Entregaré el palantír a alguien que pueda mantenerlo a salvo. Hemos hecho cuanto estaba a nuestro alcance, ${PLAYER}, pero no ha sido suficiente. ¡Cien maldiciones sobre la Corona de Hierro! Nos ha arrebatado demasiado y, por cada victoria, nos inflige una docena de heridas.\
\
'Y aun así, seguimos luchando. Siempre ha sido el camino de los Dúnedain, y sé que también es el tuyo, ${PLAYER}. ¿Qué otra cosa podríamos hacer? Lucharemos en nombre de Laerdan y de todas las personas que han caído, y algún día Amarthiel pagará por cada una de ellas. Lo juro sobre los huesos de mis antepasados y los de quienes los precedieron. Lo veremos cumplido, ${PLAYER}.'","Calenglad se encuentra en el campamento de los Montaraces de la isla de Tinnudir, en Evendim.\
\
Calenglad espera saber que tus aliados están preparados para el asalto contra Barad Tironn y la recuperación del palantír.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión está pensada para una comunidad. Si decides realizarla en solitario, recibirás un bono de inspiración, pero el desafío será muy grande.</rgb>","'¿Todo está listo, ${PLAYER}? Daré la orden cuando tú y tus aliados estén preparados, y asaltaremos Barad Tironn con toda la fuerza que podamos reunir. Recuperar el palantír dependerá de ustedes; mi gente solo puede abrirles el camino.\
\
'Si puedes hacer algo para ayudar a Laerdan dentro de Barad Tironn, te pido que lo hagas, aunque temo que ya se haya perdido.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión está pensada para una comunidad. Si decides realizarla en solitario, recibirás un bono de inspiración, pero el desafío será muy grande.</rgb>","Habla con Calenglad y adéntrate en Barad Tironn en busca del palantír","Libro 10, Capítulo 14: El Ojo de Angmar","Calenglad se encuentra en el campamento de los Montaraces de la isla de Tinnudir, en Evendim.\
\
El palantír ha sido recuperado, pero Laerdan quedó a merced de un destino incierto en las profundidades de Barad Tironn, y Amarthiel logró ver aquello que buscaba en lo más hondo de la Piedra Videncia.","Habla con Calenglad","Calenglad ha tomado su decisión: el plan para recuperar el palantír de Barad Tironn se pondrá en marcha, pese al intento imprudente de Laerdan de enfrentarse a Amarthiel en soledad."},
[1893]={"Talk to Corudan in Leaflock's mead","Orcs can be found in Balewood, especially along the path called Núrzum's Wrath.","Defeat Orcs in Balewood, and be noisy about it (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I heard the din of fighting from here! You should see if that was enough to waken our sleeping friend.'","Show the White Hand equipment to Leaflock the Ent","'Look at that, ${PLAYER}! An Ent can be truly frightening when he is roused! I do not know what Leaflock will do about Núrzum, but this is better than I had hoped we could achieve!\
\
'I will meet you back at Nona's cave, ${PLAYER}. I want to speak to Leaflock for a short while, if I may.'","You explain to Leaflock that Wildermore is held in the grip of an unnatural winter, and is at the mercy of a giant called Núrzum.\
\
The sighing of the wind through the branches is Leaflock's only response for many minutes. Then a rumbling sound slowly separates from the sound of the sleeping forest, and you realize he speaks again.\
\
'You use small names for big things, little one.'\
\
Somewhere snow falls from an upper branch and lands with a soft sound onto a drift.\
\
'Wildermore? Hooom... it is not a name I know...'","'Show that equipment to Leaflock and see if it rouses him to wakefulness.'","A sighing sound escapes from somewhere within the cracks of Leaflock's weathered face, but you see no other sign of wakefulness.","White Hand Uruks can be found at Núrzum's Wrath, in Balewood.\
\
Corudan thinks you should collect some White Hand equipment from Uruks in Balewood and show them to Leaflock.","'He is curious about what we have to say now. Before he was disturbed by our presence, but now I think he may be disturbed by our words. That is what we need, I am certain of it!'","Leaflock remains asleep.","'Of course! Leaflock would have no knowledge of the names of kingdoms or the properties of Men. He may have been asleep since before the Riddermark was founded!'","'I will meet you back at Nona's cave, ${PLAYER}. I want to speak to Leaflock for a short time.'","You have raised quite a din fighting Orcs in Balewood, and should see if it was enough to waken Leaflock.","'Defeat Orcs throughout the Balewood and perhaps the din will waken our sleeping friend, ${PLAYER}.'","Book 10, Chapter 14: Waking Leaflock","You hold up the blade and helmet bearing the mark of the White Hand. For long moments it seems nothing will happen, until finally Leaflock's eye swivels open and fixes upon the Orc-weapons.\
\
'Hooom, brooooom. Why do you wake Leaflock... Leaflock...'\
\
A deep rumbling within the Ent goes on for some time, and you wonder if he is sleepily giving you his name in his own language.","Collected a White Hand helmet","You forgot the equipment?","You describe Núrzum to the Ent as best as you are able, trying to remember his form and features as you saw them amid the flying snow at Byre Tor. Leaflock shakes and quivers, becoming more animated than you have seen him.\
\
'Hroom! Broom! You said he was a giant! That is not just a giant!'\
\
A mighty and branch-like arm angrily spears a nearby drift, sending an explosion of snow skyward.\
\
'It may have been a giant once. Now it is more than that. You describe an unnatural combination. It was a giant. It was also a Huorn. Twisted! Corrupted!'\
\
Leaflock shakes angrily.\
\
'Broom! Boom! Leaflock will not allow this! Leaflock will deal with this!'","'This is proving more difficult than I expected, ${PLAYER}.'\
\
Corudan thinks for a moment.\
\
'Perhaps the danger and the noise is too far away to draw Leaflock's attention. Go to Núrzum's Wrath and defeat some Uruks of the White Hand. Bring some of their equipment to Leaflock and see if that will stir him to wakefulness.'","'I beheld many Orcs cutting their way through Balewood while we searched for this place, ${PLAYER}. If you engage them in combat, perhaps the din will be sufficient to awaken our sleeping friend.\
\
'And if not, well... there will be fewer Orcs in Balewood. Is that not a worthy result?'","Noisily defeated Orcs in the Balewood (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Leaflock shakes angrily.\
\
'Someone must pay for this, hoom, broom! Twisting a Huorn in this way! Hoom! Broom!'","'Hoom! Boom! Broom! This Núrzum is an unnatural being and cannot be allowed to walk these lands!'","'Look at him! What a delight to meet another Ent in these fading years!'","Collect a White Hand blade from an Uruk in Balewood","Collect White Hand helmet from an Uruk in Balewood","'It is good to see you again, ${PLAYER}. I spoke with Leaflock for a time after you left, and it is difficult to say if he will help us. He remained angry, but some of his initial fury had subsided.\
\
'He cares little for the plight of Men, or Elves, but of trees and Huorns he cares a great deal. If Núrzum was simply a giant, Leaflock would not trouble himself at all to help us. If Núrzum is as he appears to be, an unnatural fusion of a giant and a Huorn, there is at least a chance that Leaflock will involve himself.\
\
'I do not know how great a chance that may be, but we have done what we could.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Completing this quest will unlock an optional interlude from Gléowine's map.</rgb>","'Until Leaflock wakes, Wildermore remains at the mercy of Núrzum... and he has none. Collect equipment from White Hand Uruks and show them to the sleeping Ent.'","You try to appeal to Leaflock's sense of duty, and speak of the hardships endured by the people of Wildermore at the hands of the Orcs and beneath Núrzum's trampling feet.\
\
'The lives of Orcs are short. They may hack and claw and burn for a time, but never for long. It is true of Men also, hoom... boom... broom.'\
\
Leaflock is silent as you gather your thoughts and try to devise another approach. Before you come up with something, the Ent unexpectedly speaks.\
\
'I do not know what beast is described by this name \\qNúrzum.\\q What do you mean by this name?'\
\
Upper branches creak and groan as a slight breeze picks up, and the forest all around seems to be listening.","Corudan has agreed to meet you back at Nona's cave after he is done speaking with Leaflock.","Leaflock stirs slightly, but remains otherwise asleep.","Defeat Orcs in Balewood, and be even noisier about it (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Noisily defeated Orcs in Balewood (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You are trying to waken Leaflock to your cause.","'I am not ready to give up. Go back out there and make even more noise!'","'That was quite a lot of noise, my friend. Do any Orcs remain in the Balewood?\
\
'Check on Leaflock and see if that was enough to wake him.'","Corudan is in Leaflock's mead, trying to devise a means of waking the slumbering Ent.","Talk to Corudan back in Nona's cave","You found Leaflock the Ent within Balewood, but now you need to wake him to your need.","Collected a White Hand blade","Corudan is in Leaflock's mead.","You have collected some White Hand equipment from Orcs in Balewood and should show them to Leaflock. That may rouse the Ent to wakefulness."},
[1894]={"'You should speak to Horn and see how he fares.'","Horn is in Nona's cave, waiting to speak with you when you are ready to take your meal.","Nona está en su cueva en las Altas Cumbres.","'We have planted a seed, ${PLAYER}: the seed of Núrzum's defeat. Now we need to let it bloom.\
\
'What did we miss while we were searching for Leaflock, ${PLAYER}? Are our friends and the survivors of Byre Tor still doing all right?'","Gléowine is in Nona's cave, and you should speak to him to see how things have been while you and Corudan sought out Leaflock.","Horn is in Nona's cave, and you should speak to him.","Book 10, Chapter 15: The Bloom","'I have never seen anything like it, ${PLAYER}. The sight of those trees marching away to fight Núrzum... Suvulch would fall down upon his face in wonder, and Wadu would never have believed me if I told him of it.\
\
'But looking at those marching trees, allies of ours in this and yet so different from us... I realized what a strange world this is, and how small our place in it. Corudan spoke of Leaflock the Tree-man. He knows not of Rohirrim, or Dunlending. To him we are nothing. And yet he sends his... his children, if that they be, to fight our enemy. Such wonders, both marvelous and terrible, all at once.\
\
'I do not want to face this strange world alone. I will no longer run from the differences between my people and Horn's people. He and I will be one. When those in my care are restored to health, I will go where he goes. Let all who oppose us beware, for together we are strongest!\
\
'Thank you for keeping him safe while I was away, ${PLAYER}. Soon we will adventure again! Núrzum will soon be defeated and we will leave this place. Until then we should rest and recover our strength. We will speak again when that happens.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Completing this quest will unlock an optional interlude from Gléowine's map.</rgb>","Talk to Horn when you are ready to eat","You have returned to Nona's cave and should speak with your friends while you wait to see if Leaflock will take action against Núrzum.","'Ready to eat?'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This instance may not be completed in a Fellowship.</rgb>","'Did you find what you wanted in Balewood, ${PLAYER}?'\
\
You tell Gléowine about Leaflock and he smiles happily.\
\
'That is great news! If such creatures are as strong as Corudan believes them to be, we may have the best ally against Núrzum we could hope to have.\
\
'Nona's survivors are improving as well. Léodwig is much stronger now than he was, and everyone's spirits are improving. It will not be long before Léodwig can get up and about.\
\
'Horn has spent a great deal of time speaking with Nona. I have been trying to give them their privacy, but I can tell they have not yet worked through their feelings. Ah, the complexities of youth! I remember them. Dimly.'","'I... don't know what to say, ${PLAYER}. The sight of those Huorns marching... suddenly I was reminded of my place in this world, and felt very, very small. Life is too short to spend it thinking of what might have been.'","'Corudan has already told me about Leaflock. I thought he was going to hurt himself smiling so widely.\
\
'As for me, I am doing fine as well, ${PLAYER}. Nona and I have been catching up while you were gone. I told her about our adventures in the Sutcrofts and Fangorn, and about our unfortunate audience with Théoden King.\
\
'She told me about her attempts to provide for those in her care, by raiding abandoned villages and stealing supplies wherever she could find them. It sounds very difficult. I wish we had been with her! We could have helped her, and... well, you understand, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Since Léodwig is improved, I thought we might all take our meal together in this chamber? Let me know when you are ready to eat!'","'We have planted the seed of Núrzum's defeat. Now we need to let it bloom.'"},
[1895]={"A jangling sound alerts you to a broken harp, which you pick up","Saruman's mounted minions threaten the people of Rohan throughout the Sutcrofts.\
\
Horn and Corudan think you should make the most of your exile from Edoras by continuing to combat Saruman's mounted minions in East Rohan.","Defeated one of Saruman's minions (${NUMBER}/5)","Horn and Corudan are at the crossing of the Entwash, in the Sutcrofts, and desire to speak with you concerning your next steps.","Horn is at the crossing of the Entwash, in the Sutcrofts, and he will wish to see the battered harp you found.","'You have no harp? No harp at all?'","'You found this harp in battle? It looks to my eye that the harp lost that battle, ${PLAYER}.'","Bring the battered harp to Horn at the crossing of the Entwash, in the Sutcrofts","Defeat Saruman's mounted minions in the Sutcrofts (${NUMBER}/5)","'The King of Rohan has forbidden us to cross the Entwash, but there is still much we can do for his people on this side of the river.\
\
'In time, perhaps the King will come to his senses, releasing his nephew Éomer from imprisonment, restoring Horn's mentor as his minstrel, discerning the difference between friend and foe...'\
\
Corudan shakes his head. 'Until he does, let us ride against the mounted foes of his people throughout the Sutcrofts and the Entwash Vale!'","'Let us ride against Saruman's minions, ${PLAYER}! They prowl throughout the Sutcrofts, and will make good targets for we three exiles!'","'We will put our exile from Edoras to good use, ${PLAYER}, if we strive to improve the lot of the needful folk on this side of the Entwash. Then, at least, some good will come from Théoden King's command that we not return to the Golden Hall.'\
\
Horn sighs heavily. 'I confess I cannot find a positive light in which to cast Éomer's imprisonment by his uncle, or the sending-away of my mentor Gléowine. We must find hope where we may, I suppose.\
\
'We should ride against the mounted minions of Saruman in the Sutcrofts. Let us bring peace to the people of East Rohan, for that be where the King commands us to stay!'","Defeat Saruman's mounted minions in the Sutcrofts (4/5)","'Saruman's minions prowl throughout the Sutcrofts. If we ride against them we will do some good for the people of Rohan.'","Book 10, Chapter 1: Exiles","'What did you find? A harp, you say? That seems an odd choice of weapon for use by Saruman's minions.'\
\
Horn's jovial expression disappears when you hand him the battered remains of the harp.\
\
'I know this instrument, ${PLAYER}! How often did I listen to its beautiful music, played first to instruct and only later to entertain? This is the harp of my mentor Gléowine. Did he run afoul of Saruman's minions?'","A jangling sound alerts you to a broken harp crushed beneath your foe"},
[1896]={"'Lee la carta que te he dado y entrégasela a Calenglad. Es de la mayor urgencia, ${PLAYER}. Se avecinan decisiones difíciles, para todos nosotros, y Calenglad deberá tomar la primera.'","Libro 10, Capítulo 1: La Campeona de Angmar","Amarthiel y sus esbirros han tomado Annúminas, la antigua ciudad de los Dúnedain, y Calenglad ahora lucha por trazar un plan con el que oponérsele.","Calenglad se encuentra en el campamento de los Montaraces, en la isla de Tinnudir, en Evendim.\
\
Laerdan ha escrito una carta para Calenglad explicando la amenaza que supone Amarthiel. Te ha pedido que leas la carta y se la entregues a Calenglad.","'Es bueno volver a verte, ${PLAYER}, pero parece que estamos destinados a encontrarnos siempre en la tristeza. El día más feliz del que te hablé en nuestro último encuentro, por desgracia, aún no ha llegado, y los días parecen oscurecerse cada vez más.\
\
'Amarthiel se ha revelado y ahora se sienta a juzgar desde las ruinas de Annúminas. Sus ejércitos combaten en las calles y bajo las sombras de las torres contra los Dúnedain; eso ya lo sabes. Pero hay más sobre la nueva regente de Angmar de lo que conocen Calenglad y los Montaraces.\
\
'He puesto por escrito gran parte de la historia en esta carta. Lee el relato y llévalo a Calenglad para que decida qué puede hacerse. Debes hacerlo con la mayor urgencia, ${PLAYER}; en nuestra respuesta al desafío de Amarthiel se juega algo más que la ciudad de los Dúnedain.'","Entrega la carta de Laerdan a Calenglad.","'¿No tienes la carta de Laerdan?'","'No puede haber mayor insulto que este, ${PLAYER}. Que la vil regente de Angmar camine hoy las mismas piedras que antiguamente caminó Elendil es una afrenta para la que no puede haber perdón. Los esbirros de Amarthiel podrán retener Annúminas por ahora, pero los Dúnedain no descansarán hasta que ella y todos sus servidores sean barridos de sus patios y hasta que incluso las losas del suelo sean limpiadas de su corrupción.\
\
'Mientras estabas fuera, un visitante llegó a Tinnudir. Su nombre es Laerdan, y es un Elfo de gran reputación; mi amigo Golodir hablaba muy bien de él en nuestra juventud, aunque yo no lo había conocido hasta ahora. Se le ha concedido el uso de la sala de reclutamiento en el torreón de Tinnudir, y dice poseer información sobre Amarthiel que nos será de utilidad. Pidió verte personalmente, ${PLAYER}. Escucha lo que tenga que decir, y ruego que regreses con algún saber secreto de los Elfos que pueda ayudarnos en esta batalla.\
\
'Gira a la derecha al entrar en el torreón, y encontrarás la estancia de Laerdan al final de las escaleras.'","'Laerdan dice saber algo sobre Amarthiel que debemos conocer, ${PLAYER}. Habla con él en la habitación que le hemos proporcionado y luego regresa conmigo con cualquier información útil que tenga para compartir.\
\
'La estancia de Laerdan se encuentra dentro de la fortaleza de esta isla, al final de las escaleras a tu derecha según entras.'","A Laerdan se le ha dado una habitación en la fortaleza de la isla de Tinnudir. Su estancia está al final de un tramo de escaleras, a la derecha según entras en el torreón.\
\
Calenglad te ha dicho que Laerdan el Elfo ha llegado a Tinnudir portando información que podría ayudarte a combatir las fuerzas de Amarthiel en Annúminas. Dijo que Laerdan preguntó por ti por tu nombre.","'¿Laerdan ha puesto por escrito sus pensamientos en una carta? Muy bien, déjame verla...\
\
'¿Laerdan me pediría que abandonara la ciudad a Amarthiel si eso significara recuperar el palantír de sus manos? ¡No sabe lo que dice! Golodir siempre habló bien de este Elfo, pero ahora debo cuestionar su juicio.\
\
'¡No dejaré Annúminas en manos del Enemigo! ¡Salvaremos tanto la ciudad como la Piedra, ${PLAYER}, o no salvaremos ninguna de las dos! ¡Esa es mi decisión!'"},
[1897]={"Gléowine is in a drunken stupor, and pays you no mind.","Gléowine spits and splutters, choking on almonds and honeyed water, and wipes the green smear of raw cabbage from his forehead. He says nothing, though his actions speak loudly of his fondness for you.","'Your friend will be of no use to anyone until you get him out of his cups. I know several remedies for drunkenness. I can share them with you if you like.'","An overpowering smell of ale greets you as you approach the drunken man","'It does not look good for Horn's master, ${PLAYER}. Gléowine is an old man, and no warrior, and the plains of Rohan are dangerous for the unready.\
\
'Even so, if Horn wishes for us to ask for news of the minstrel in Snowbourn, we should do what we can.\
\
'I do not think we will learn anything hopeful, but perhaps I will be surprised.'","Alhild is near Gléowine by the barracks in Snowbourn.\
\
You have found Gléowine, but you need him to sober up before he will be of any use to anyone. Perhaps Alhild can be of help.","'No, that description is not familiar to me. There have been many ragged folk streaming into Snowbourn of late, but I do not think I have seen your friend.\
\
'You might try south-west of here, by the barracks. There was a disturbance there earlier today, what with all these new people in town. Could be you'll find your friend there.\
\
'I'm willing to wager he did not come to Snowbourn by horse while I was here. I am sorry.'","'Yes, I can give you a bladder of water. I have been drawing water for all of the thirsty new arrivals in Snowbourn. It is the least I can do.'","You remove a comb of dripping, delicious honey","'What... what ish thish?'","'You found all the ingredients for the drunkenness remedies? Well, you should apply them to your friend there. I think he needs them.'","Heiu hands you a bladder of cool, refreshing water","'Hey... hey, what are... are...'\
\
Gléowine blinks up at you with bleary, red eyes. You offer him water infused with honey, which he drinks easily.\
\
'This mead... tastes a bit... a bit... watery...'\
\
You then give him the almonds to chew on, but at the first bite he spits them out. 'Ugh, what... what ish thish?' he slurs at you, sensing betrayal.\
\
You then rub the cabbage leaves on his forehead and he sputters angrily. 'Are you trying... poison me...?' he demands.\
\
The remedies seem to have had little effect on Gléowine, save to make him angry.","Collect a handful of Snowbourn almonds","Alhild has further information about the remedies she suggested","Obtain a bladder of water from Heiu","'Is that your friend? He has been deep in his cups since yesterday, and will be of no use to anyone until he crawls out of them again. I have a few remedies that might speed the process, if you'd like to try one. One of them involves a mixture of honey and water, another involves the chewing of almonds, and I have heard that a poultice made of raw swamp cabbage can ease drunkenness when rubbed on one's forehead. Perhaps one of those will help.'\
\
She considers Gléowine once more before continuing. 'Actually, he is pretty drunk. You might need all of them. I can tell you where to find these remedies, if you have a moment.'","'You might find your friend by the barracks, to the south-west. There was a loud commotion there earlier today, and many of the new arrivals have congregated near there.'","'See how the wooden frame has been splintered? My master's harp was trampled by heavy feet, and the strings cut. It could be repaired, given enough time and the right materials. Might the same be true of my master? Gléowine is not a young man, and he never was much of a warrior. With his dismissal fresh in his mind, did he stumble upon that thrall of Saruman's and meet his end?'\
\
Horn sadly studies the broken harp.\
\
'I cannot think this way, ${PLAYER}. He could still have escaped that fate and made his way to a settlement. Snowbourn is not far from here to the south-east. We should go there and ask for sign of my master.'","Horn is by his master Gléowine, outside the barracks in Snowbourn.\
\
You have found Gléowine and attempted to ease his drunkenness with Alhild's remedies, but none of them seem to have worked. Now Horn wants to speak with you.","Search for Gléowine near the barracks in Snowbourn","Pick some swamp cabbage (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to a guard at the entrance or stables of Snowbourn about Gléowine","Talk to Alhild, near Gléowine at the barracks","Collect a Snowbourn honeycomb","Book 10, Chapter 2: Gléowine","Gléowine is by the barracks in Snowbourn.\
\
You have obtained the ingredients for several drunkenness remedies and should now apply them to Gléowine in order to sober him up.","Guards at the entrance of Snowbourn or its stables may have seen Gléowine, if he lives.\
\
Horn hopes that his master Gléowine found his way safely to Snowbourn, despite much evidence to the contrary.","'I have not seen your friend, but you might try looking at the barracks, to the south. Many of the new arrivals to the city gathered outside the barracks earlier today.'","'Yes? Feel free to take some almonds from the bucket there, if you need them. I know how hard things are for those people who have come to Snowbourn in these difficult times.'","'My master may have escaped from his foes and made his way to Snowbourn. We should ask the guards there if they have seen him. It is a small hope, but you cannot deny it is possible.'","You have found Gléowine. He is alive, but very, very drunk.\
\
'Hey, you... you there... you? Stay out of my... my way, you? Hey!' he slurs.\
\
With that effort expended, Gléowine drifts back into his stupor.","'You might find your friend by the barracks, to the south. There was a loud commotion there earlier today, and many of the new arrivals have congregated near there.'","Talk to Gléowine by the barracks in Snowbourn","You have found Gléowine in Snowbourn, but he is very drunk.","'Gléowine lives, ${PLAYER}! Perhaps we should have just followed the smell.'","'My master Gléowine is alive! He is deep in his cups, but I cannot say I blame him his despair. I am just glad to see he lives!'","You reach into the bucket and pull out a handful of almonds","'I am sorry, but I have not seen anyone of that description. There have been many ragged folk streaming into Snowbourn of late; it is possible your friend came in a crowd and I just did not see him.\
\
'You might try south of here, by the barracks. There was a disturbance there earlier today, what with all these new people in town. Could be you'll find your friend there.'","'I suppose these remedies were worth trying, but in my experience time has always been the only sure curative.'\
\
Horn looks at his master's drunken form and sighs.\
\
'I cannot blame him, ${PLAYER}. He has experienced a great deal of suffering in recent days.'","Horn is worried about the fate of his master Gléowine, whose broken and battered harp you found in the clutches of one of Saruman's minions.","'I have not seen him, but it is possible your friend went with the other new arrivals to the barracks, south-west of here.'","The guard with whom you spoke did not recognize Gléowine from your description, but advised you to look for him near the barracks in Snowbourn, where many of the recent arrivals in the city have congregated.","Alhild knows where around Snowbourn to collect the ingredients for the various drunkenness remedies she mentioned.\
\
You need to collect the ingredients necessary to relieve Gléowine's drunkenness.","Give the honey, water, almonds, and cabbage to Gléowine to ease his drunken state","You pick the most pungent leaves from the cabbage (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Horn by the barracks in Snowbourn"},
[1898]={"Libro 10, Capítulo 2: La marea de la batalla","'${PLAYERNAME:Bienvenido[m]|Bienvenida[f]} a Echad Garthadir, . Lamento que debas ver Annúminas así: tomada por Angmar, corrompida por Amarthiel.\
\
'¡Todos haremos nuestra parte para expulsarlos! Escucha con atención, pues hay mucho que hacer y poco tiempo para hacerlo.'","'Encontrarás a Rosselloth en Gwaelband, en la entrada frontal de Annúminas. Gwaelband está al oeste de Men Erain, más allá de Minathranc. Rosselloth te dirá qué puedes hacer para ayudar en esta lucha.'","Rosselloth se encuentra en el patio de Gwaelband. Gwaelband está al oeste de Men Erain, más allá de Minathranc, en la entrada frontal de Annúminas.\
\
Calenglad ha decidido que las fuerzas de Amarthiel deben ser contenidas en Annúminas para impedir que centre su atención en el palantír. Te ha enviado a hablar con Rosselloth para que te aconseje sobre cómo puedes ayudar.","'Tienes suerte de que hayamos tomado Gwaelband; ahora que la puerta está bajo nuestro control, puedes acceder al nivel superior de manera mucho más sencilla. Solo tendrás que subir la pequeña colina al suroeste, atravesar la puerta y avanzar hacia el sur y el oeste hasta llegar a Echad Garthadir. De lo contrario, te aguardaría un largo viaje: un extenso nado hacia el oeste hasta Gaerannon y luego una trepada por la ciudad.\
\
'Fainneleg te dirá qué hacer. ¡Recuperaremos la ciudad de manos de los angmarim, ${PLAYER}!'","Laerdan te ha dicho que el palantír debe ser arrebatado a Amarthiel a cualquier precio, pero Calenglad insiste en que recuperar Annúminas debe ser lo primero.","El montaraz Fainneleg se encuentra en Echad Garthadir, un pequeño campamento al suroeste de Gwaelband, en un nivel más elevado de la ciudad. Si los Montaraces controlan Gwaelband, la puerta ofrece un acceso sencillo al nivel superior. De lo contrario, deberás nadar hacia el oeste pasando el Puerto de Annúminas hasta Gaerannon y luego trepar por la ciudad para llegar a Echad Garthadir.\
\
Rosselloth te ha dicho que hables con Fainneleg, el montaraz que organiza la defensa de Annúminas.","'Si la puerta aquí hubiera estado bajo nuestro control, podrías haber accedido al nivel superior de manera mucho más sencilla. Ahora no hay más remedio: deberás nadar hacia el oeste, pasando el Puerto de Annúminas, hasta llegar a Gaerannon, y luego trepar por la ciudad hasta Echad Garthadir.\
\
'¡Fainneleg sin duda tendrá alguna forma de que puedas ayudar, ${PLAYER}!'","Habla con Rosselloth","'Perdona mi ira, ${PLAYER}; no fue apropiada. Hay sabiduría en las palabras de Laerdan, pero debes ver el peligro de dejar Annúminas en manos de los angmarim. Si no detenemos aquí las ambiciones de Amarthiel, junto al Lago Nenuial, fortificará la antigua ciudad. ¿Y adónde crees entonces que marcharán sus ejércitos? ¡Piensa en la Comarca, a una corta marcha hacia el sur, o en Puente de Caballetes, al este, ya acosado por orcos procedentes de Angmar!\
\
'Debemos inclinar la marea de la batalla a nuestro favor, ${PLAYER}, antes de intentar recuperar el palantír. Si mantenemos la atención de Amarthiel centrada en los combates dentro de la ciudad, se verá obligada a responder a nuestros desafíos. ¡Tendrá menos tiempo para usar la piedra vidente para encontrar a Narchuil!\
\
'Mi corazón me dice que esto es lo correcto, ${PLAYER}. Si te mantienes con nosotros, habla con Rosselloth en Annúminas; ella te dirá cómo va la batalla. Cruza Minathranc frente a la ciudad y llegarás al patio de Gwaelband. Rosselloth te dirá qué puedes hacer para ayudar en esta lucha.'","'¡Silencio, ${PLAYER}! ¡Los atraerás sobre nosotros! Como puedes ver, la batalla va mal: intentamos asegurar Gwaelband frente a las fuerzas del Enemigo, pero solo hallamos derrota. Algunos aventureros trataron de ayudarnos, pero fueron pocos, muy pocos...\
\
'Querrás hablar con Fainneleg; él está coordinando nuestras defensas desde Echad Garthadir, una posición que hasta ahora hemos logrado mantener. Por desgracia, hemos quedado aislados de su campamento; se encuentra al suroeste de aquí, en un nivel más elevado de la ciudad.\
\
'Si la puerta hubiera estado bajo nuestro control, podrías haber accedido al nivel superior de manera mucho más sencilla. Ahora no hay más remedio: deberás nadar hacia el oeste, pasando el Puerto de Annúminas, hasta llegar a Gaerannon, y luego trepar por la ciudad hasta Echad Garthadir. Sin duda Fainneleg tendrá alguna forma de que puedas ayudar.'","'¡Salve, ${PLAYER}! Como puedes ver, la batalla va bien: hemos logrado asegurar Gwaelband frente a las fuerzas del enemigo. La batalla fue feroz, pero se nos unieron varios aventureros y la victoria fue nuestra.\
\
'Quieres hablar con Fainneleg; él está coordinando nuestras defensas desde Echad Garthadir, una posición que hasta ahora hemos logrado mantener. Lo encontrarás al suroeste de aquí, en un nivel más elevado de la ciudad.\
\
'Tienes suerte de que hayamos tomado Gwaelband; ahora que la puerta está bajo nuestro control, puedes acceder al nivel superior de manera mucho más sencilla. Solo tendrás que subir la pequeña colina al suroeste, atravesar la puerta y avanzar hacia el sur y el oeste hasta llegar a Echad Garthadir. De lo contrario, te aguardaría un largo viaje: un extenso nado hacia el oeste hasta Gaerannon y luego una trepada por la ciudad.'"},
[1899]={"Gléowine is on the wooden porch outside the Mead Hall in Harwick, in the Wold.\
\
Gléowine wishes to speak with you.","Horn and Corudan have learned some troubling news about the region of Rohan called Wildermore, and that has done for Gléowine what your various remedies could not.","'Our road runs into Wildermore, as we knew it must. See on the map where it leads?'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Completing this quest will unlock an optional interlude from Gléowine's map.</rgb>","'If Gléowine's map was so precious to him, why did he abandon it? Is that the way of Man, to give up hope at the first sign of sorrow or hardship?\
\
'Ah, I know it is not. Our travels with Horn have shown me that the race of Man has some resilience in it, after all! But it is not so with everyone, perhaps.'","'The boy left Snowbourn by the south gate? You should catch up to him, if you can, and ask for him to return Gléowine's map.'","Bring the map to Gléowine by the barracks in Snowbourn","'Ah, you found my map! Thank you! I hope it was not too much trouble.'\
\
Gléowine unrolls the parchment and wistfully traces a finger along its surface.\
\
'The life of a minstrel is more than just music and songs, ${PLAYER}. I served in the court of Théoden King for so long I came to forget the roads I walked in my youth. But now, well into my elder years I will once again tread the roads of Rohan, and live the travelling life. How many of the places on this map will I see before my feet stop once more, and for good?\
\
'Who can say? Yet I know what I, Gléowine, can say: I am pleased to make the journey with friends, both old and new.'","Book 10, Chapter 3: No Word from Wildermore","Talk to Aldor Harding in the Mead Hall of Harwick, in the Wold","Britred left on an adventure by the south gate of Snowbourn. How far south did he get on his quest?\
\
You were told that Britred took Gléowine's map and went on an adventure. If you find him, he may return the map to you.","One of the children of Snowbourn may know where to find Gléowine's map.\
\
Gléowine wishes to travel with you to investigate the curious silence that has enveloped Wildermore, but first he wants you to recover the map he abandoned.","Britred tosses you the map, and runs back to Snowbourn","'Speak to the children of Snowbourn. It could be that one of them knows what became of Gléowine's map.'","Talk to Gléowine outside the Mead Hall of Harwick, in the Wold","'I will not keep my master from travelling with us, ${PLAYER}, as long as he understands the danger. If I learned of trouble in Eaworth, I would not long remain in idle safety. I would travel there to learn if anything could be done for my home. It must be the same for Gléowine.\
\
'I will return his harp and learn what befell as he made the journey to Snowbourn, if you will seek for the map he abandoned. Ask the children of Snowbourn. They are sometimes the surest form of information in the city, for they see all and go unnoticed. One of them may know what happened to Gléowine's map.'","Talk to Horn by the barracks in Snowbourn","'Master Gléowine, are you feeling better?'","'I think Harding took it rather well.'","Find Britred south of Snowbourn","'You found my master's map! Very good!'","'Where is my map?'","'It appears that Gléowine may be feeling better. Time heals, after all.'","Horn and Corudan are by the barracks in Snowbourn.\
\
Gléowine wants to travel with you to investigate what has happened in Wildermore, but first he needs some of the possessions he gave away while in the depths of his despair.","'We should ride for Harwick, in the Wold. We will speak with Aldor Harding and learn if he has any more information about what is going on in Wildermore.'","'We ride for Harwick, in the Wold? Perhaps Aldor Harding has learned something of the state of Wildermore since he dispatched his messenger hither.'","'My friend Britred left Snowbourn by the south gate, and said he was going on an adventure! If you hurry you might catch up to him before he goes too far!'","'Our first destination is Harwick, in the Wold? I am ready, ${PLAYER}. Lead and I will follow. Aldor Harding may have learned something of the state of Wildermore since his messenger made for Snowbourn.'","'I hope this boy does not get himself into trouble on account of my map! Leave by the south gate and stop him before he runs afoul of something dangerous!'","'Something has happened within Wildermore, and whatever it may be is sure to endanger Harwick next. You must find out what threat it poses to us and put a stop to it.'","'What do you want? Can you not see how busy I am?'\
\
The child laughs, but keeps dancing. You explain that you're looking for Gléowine's map, and would appreciate any information about its location.\
\
'I remember that old man! He went off to the tavern after setting down his belongings by the wall over there. A bag of clothes there was, and a bundle of bread and cheese. I hope he does not expect his food back, because my friends ate it all!\
\
'Britred took the map before any of us could get at it, and he said he was going to use it to go on an adventure to save Rohan. You just missed seeing him by minutes. He left by this gate here. Maybe you can catch up to him and ask for the map back.'","Talk to Arnwi by the south gate of Snowbourn","'I see you found Gléowine's map. That did not take very long at all, ${PLAYER}. I have just returned from collecting his bag of sundries, and it was quite a task to accomplish!'","Talk to Gléowine by the barracks in Snowbourn","Talk to Corudan by the barracks in Snowbourn","'Looking back now I know I should not have abandoned my goods, but I could not see beyond the sunset. Cast out by Théoden King and forbidden to return... that is all the life I have known for many years! To have it taken away, and so suddenly... I simply could not envision caring about anything ever again.\
\
'I was wrong. I care about my home, stranger. I care about Wildermore, though I have not seen it for many years. I want to know what has happened to it, and for that I need my map. Speak to the children of Snowbourn; I think one of them will have it.'","Aldor Harding is in the Mead Hall of Harwick, in the Wold.\
\
Fastred has no men to spare in an investigation of Wildermore, and has sent you to give Harding the unfortunate tidings.","'The prospect is a daunting one, but I believe I am ready for a bit of travel.'","'I think we are ready to depart. My master has his map and the other possessions he will need, and I have arranged for a fresh horse for him to ride.\
\
'I spoke with Reeve Fastred while you were outside the city. He remains as stubborn as ever, refusing to entertain the idea that he could more easily defend his people on the other side of the river. The message from Harwick was just as I had heard second-hand: portentous and frightening. No word has come to Harwick from Wildermore for many days, and Harding desired men and horses from Fastred to investigate.\
\
'Before we go to Wildermore, we must travel to Harwick, in the Wold, and speak with Aldor Harding. I must give him the unfortunate tidings that Fastred has no men to spare. He sends us, and that is all.'","'Gléowine is not a young man, and his skill at riding may be relatively untested. I hope he is able to keep up with us on the road.'","Gléowine is by the barracks in Snowbourn.\
\
Gléowine has been brought back to sobriety by something, and seems ready to talk to you.","'If you are going to Wildermore, I want to come as well. I grew up there, and if something has happened... well, I do not have any ties keeping me here any longer.\
\
'I gave away all my possessions, however, and will need them back if I am to travel with you.'","'I am in favour of this journey to Wildermore, ${PLAYER}, if you are. We should go where we are needed, and if messages have ceased passing the bounds, I say we learn why.\
\
'I will see about procuring Gléowine's bag of sundries, but I leave the reconstruction of his harp and the finding of his map in Horn's able hands, and your own.'","'My master will not forgive himself if any harm comes to the boy on account of that map. Leave Snowbourn by the south gate and recover the map from this would-be adventurer!'","Gléowine is by the barracks in Snowbourn.\
\
You have recovered Gléowine's map and should return it to him.","'Yes? What word from Fastred, so far away and comfortable?'\
\
Harding snorts when you tell him Fastred has sent the four of you to aid him in investigating Wildermore.\
\
'I appreciate your help, of course, ${PLAYER}, but if Fastred thinks you are his to send he is mistaken! This does not satisfy his obligation. I am Aldor of the Northmarch! If my lands are threatened, all our lands are endangered!\
\
'We have heard naught from Wildermore for many days now. The last party to travel that road consisted of several brave men: Widfara, a rider of some repute, and my own son Léodwig. He would have returned, if no others did. His courage is not what I would wish. But he too remains missing!\
\
'Learn what has befallen my men and what evil has taken hold of Wildermore. That land is too near to Harwick for any of us to rest easy.'","Horn is by the barracks in Snowbourn.\
\
You have returned Gléowine's map and should now speak with Horn about your preparations to travel to Wildermore.","Gléowine stares at you with haunted eyes. It would seem something has cut through the stupor caused by his drink.\
\
'Something has happened in Wildermore? I... I was born in a small town there, and have not been back for years, but... if something has happened...\
\
'There is no reason for me to stay here, stranger. If you are going to investigate Wildermore, I would travel with you and... it is young Horn with you, is it not? He has a man's face and build now, but I still remember the years spent teaching him the lessons of history and the ways of music. He was... not the most diligent of students. I jest, of course. Who among us can say he was?\
\
'I abandoned my harp somewhere in the wild and gave away my other possessions when I thought I would have no further need for them. I cannot travel with you until I have them back again. Most of them were mere sundries, but there was a map I should not have given away. I feel foolish now, for it was a rare and precious thing and belongs not in the keeping of children.'","'While you were attempting to ease Gléowine back to sobriety, Corudan and I learned some troubling news.\
\
'Have you ever been to the lands of Wildermore, west of the Wold? I myself have not, but it seems that something might have befallen the people there. A messenger in the night from Harwick brought Reeve Fastred worrisome tidings: that no word has come out of Wildermore for some weeks. It is not a long journey from Harwick to Wildermore, so something must be keeping Harding's men from reporting back to him. I think we should go to Wildermore and see what has happened. I suspect Saruman's hand in this.'\
\
Something catches Horn's eye, and he starts suddenly.\
\
'Master Gléowine! What is it? Are you feeling better?'","An optional Interlude has been unlocked for Gléowine's map"},
[1900]={"Angmarim armados con arcos derrotados en Annúminas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Derrota a angmarim armados con arco en Annúminas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Habla con Gwonil y ayuda a defender su posición","Fainneleg se encuentra en Echad Garthadir, el campamento de los Montaraces en el nivel intermedio de Annúminas.\
\
Has hablado con Gwonil y con Torchirion y has derrotado a varios angmarim armados con arco en Annúminas, y ahora deberías regresar con Fainneleg para informarle de tus victorias.","'La puerta de Adannon sigue defendida, ${PLAYER}, pero te agradezco que hayas venido a verme. Ha pasado tiempo desde el último asalto a la puerta, y es bueno romper el tedio con un rostro nuevo.\
\
'¡La ciudad no seguirá mucho tiempo en manos de los angmarim, si me preguntas!'","'Hemos tenido tanto avances como pérdidas en los últimos días, ${PLAYER}, pero no podremos resistir indefinidamente. Estamos demasiado dispersos, y Amarthiel cuenta con fuerzas demasiado numerosas. Cada posición que perdemos nos acerca un paso más a la derrota total.\
\
'Necesito tu fuerza, ${PLAYER}, y la fuerza de tus aliados. Dos de mis Montaraces han rechazado ataques contra posiciones vitales, y temo que sus fuerzas estén flaqueando.\
\
'Gwonil ha combatido para expulsar a los angmarim del Puerto de Annúminas, al norte de aquí, junto al agua. Temo que no pueda resistir otro asalto. La situación es igual de grave para Torchirion, que actualmente hace guardia en Adannon, una pequeña puerta al oeste de los muelles que da acceso a la orilla occidental de Nenuial. Apresúrate a acudir en ayuda de Gwonil y de Torchirion y comprueba cómo resisten sus defensas. Mientras los buscas, te pido que derrotes a cualquier arquero angmarim armado con arco que veas dentro de la ciudad. Estos atacantes a distancia son extremadamente peligrosos, y varios de mis hermanos han caído por flechas lanzadas desde la ocultación.'","'Nuestra situación es grave, ${PLAYER}. Apresúrate a ayudar a Gwonil, al norte de aquí, en el Puerto de Annúminas, y a Torchirion, al oeste de los muelles, en Adannon, la puerta que da acceso a la orilla occidental del Lago Nenuial.\
\
'Temo que no puedan resistir mucho tiempo frente a las fuerzas que hostigan sus posiciones. Y, de paso, encárgate de cualquier angmarim armado con arco que veas dentro de la ciudad.'","'Tienes mi agradecimiento, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}, y también el de Gwonil y Torchirion, estoy seguro, a pesar de su insistencia en que todo está bajo control. Pero ahora queda más trabajo por hacer. Por el momento, nuestra defensa de Annúminas se mantiene firme; ahora debemos elaborar un plan de ataque.'","'¡Los angmarim no pasarán por mí!'","Los Montaraces de Fainneleg están demasiado dispersos para defender la ciudad frente a los ataques repetidos de los esbirros de Amarthiel.","Gwonil se encuentra en los muelles del Puerto de Annúminas, al norte de Echad Garthadir. Torchirion se encuentra en Adannon, una pequeña puerta de la muralla de la ciudad, al oeste de los muelles, que da acceso a la orilla occidental del Lago Nenuial. Arqueros angmarim acechan por toda la ciudad, a menudo ocultos.\
\
Fainneleg te ha pedido que acudas con urgencia en ayuda de Gwonil y de Torchirion, pues teme que estos Montaraces no puedan resistir otro asalto a sus posiciones. También desea que derrotes a cualquier angmarim armado con arco que encuentres dentro de la ciudad.","Habla con Torchirion y defiende su posición","'Tengo todo bajo control, ${PLAYER}, pero agradezco tu preocupación.'","'Fainneleg se preocupa demasiado. ¡Tengo todo bajo control aquí, pese a los repetidos ataques angmarim contra mi posición! Aún no me he enfrentado a una fuerza demasiado grande para poder manejarla. ¿Esperabas algo diferente?'","Libro 10, Capítulo 3: La batalla por Annúminas"},
[1901]={"'I listened to Wídfara's tale, as did you, but it raises more questions than we had before! This creature Núrzum must be of enormous size if he can overpower a horse of Rohan. He must be clad in thick fur to move comfortably in the midst of such a snowstorm as Wídfara related. Whether his attack was caused by need or sport is unclear to me, but the size of his appetite is less mysterious: it is large, and not easily sated.\
\
'I believe Núrzum to be a large snowbeast of the sort that frequents the Misty Mountains. How he came to this area of Rohan I cannot guess.'\
\
Corudan looks up from his musings with a puzzled expression.\
\
'Where is Gléowine? I have not seen him since we arrived. If dangers such as this Núrzum stalk Wildermore, we should stay together for safety. I hope Gléowine has not thought to leave Scylfig.'","'I feel responsible, in some small way, for the people of Scylfig. I do not want my presence here to bring hardship upon them, and if you face their mounted foes near the White Hand camp in the south-east, the haunted fishing village to the north-west, and by Thrymm Red-beard's camp to the east, my conscience will rest more easily.'","The White Hand camp is crawling with enemies. How did they come to be here?","Find Thrymm's training camp","You have arrived in Scylfig, and should search for Wídfara and Léodwig","Wídfara is in Scylfig, in the Writhendowns.\
\
You have done as he asked, and should now return to Wídfara to hear more of his tale.","Talk to Horn in Scylfig","'I will see you again when we reach Scylfig, friend. It is a small town in the northern stretch of the Writhendowns, the easternmost lands of Wildermore.'","Gléowine appears to be in a great deal of distress, and his eyes are full of sadness.\
\
'There is no fool like an old man thinking to rediscover the joys of his youth, ${PLAYER}. What happened to Wildermore in the years since I left her? The land of my childhood was a sunny place of fields and blue rivers, not this den of relentless sorrow! It was not home to such terrors as this monstrous Núrzum, bringing death so quickly and without warning! What happened to the land I remember?'\
\
Gléowine hastily wipes the tears away.\
\
'Ah, pay no attention to an old, sad man, ${PLAYER}. I will not despair. My concern must not be that these troubles have happened to my childhood homeland. It must be that these troubles could move south and threaten the rest of Rohan. We will help the people of Wildermore, and by helping them we will help even Théoden King, though he not ask for nor trust such help. Thank you for this talk, my friend. I just needed to hear these things aloud.'","Corudan is in Scylfig.\
\
Corudan listened to Wídfara's tale, and may have some thoughts about it.","'Yes, I am Wídfara, and I am a rider of Harding's, Aldor of the Northmarch. I am in this land at his request, but have fallen prey to some difficulties and could not yet make my return.'\
\
Wídfara laughs sourly and gingerly rubs his wounded leg.\
\
'This land is besieged, stranger! If you have not heard yet of the terrible apparition called Núrzum, you soon will. All of Wildermore trembles at his name, and they are not wrong to fear him! He slew my horse Windfoot, and no one will give me a new one with which to return to Harwick. It does not matter, with my leg in this state.\
\
'There is little we can hope to do against Núrzum, stranger, but other foes in the Writhendowns are less imposing. If you explore this land and fight the mounted foes near the White Hand camp in the south-east, explore the haunted fishing village to the north-west, and keep them away from Thrymm Red-beard's training camp to the east, I will tell you more of this terrible foe.'","'Can you find Gléowine? With dangers such as this Núrzum abroad in the hills of Wildermore, I hope he has not left Scylfig.'","The White Hand has established a camp in the south-east corner of the Writhendowns. The abandoned fishing village can be found to the north-west of Scylfig. Thrymm Red-beard's training camp is to the east of Scylfig.\
\
Wídfara has agreed to tell you more of what happened in Wildermore if you help the people of the Writhendowns by facing down their foes near three significant locations.","Book 10, Chapter 4: A Man of the Wold","'This, then, is our quest: to investigate the disappearance of Harding's men, the ones he sent into Wildermore. He gave us the names of two: Wídfara, a rider of no small skill, and Léodwig, Harding's own son.'\
\
Horn traces out a course on Gléowine's map.\
\
'We will ride north out of Harwick, and follow the road through the Wold until it turns west. That turning will bring us into Wildermore. This area here, do you see it? The land is called \\qWrithendowns,\\q and the first settlement we should investigate is this one here, Scylfig, located at its northern bounds.\
\
'What do you think of this course? I am ready to take it if you are, ${PLAYER}.'","Travel to the town of Scylfig, in the Writhendowns of Wildermore","'So Gléowine is fine after all? I am relieved.'","'Wídfara lives. Does Léodwig fare as well?'","'Harding's interest in the state of Wildermore is not surprising, for he is Aldor of the Northmarch. It falls within his command, and if something has happened to its people it is his duty to know. My interest in Wildermore is more personal than that, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'I was born in the town of Dunfast, a small village in the forest of the Whitshaws. As a young boy, I must have climbed to the top of every sturdy tree within a mile of the village; the view from the heights is well-known to me, and much-beloved: green fields and sunny hillsides, the crystal-blue waters of the Isingmere, the bounty of well-tilled farm-fields.\
\
'You can see little enough of that from my map, ${PLAYER}, but the words and symbols stir my heart and make me think of home. Speak to Horn for more practical guidance, and to discuss our next steps. I tread too easily upon steps of memory, as minstrels are wont to do.'","'Wídfara, at least, lives. But what of Harding's son, Léodwig?'","Defeat mounted combat foes in the Writhendowns (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","It is Corudan's hope that Gléowine remains still within Scylfig.\
\
Corudan wants you to find Gléowine if he remains in Scylfig.","Horn is in Scylfig with Corudan and Wídfara.\
\
You have comforted Gléowine and should now speak with Horn in Scylfig.","Find the possibly-haunted fishing town","Find Gléowine somewhere within Scylfig","'So Gléowine's time to himself helped him find some measure of peace? I am glad.'\
\
Horn's expression grows distant, and he seems to be speaking more to himself than to you.\
\
'Sometimes that is all it takes, is it not? Time to think. It could be like that for any one of us, only to return renewed and with greater purpose. I hope it is so.'\
\
Horn seems to notice you are still looking at him expectantly, and he turns slightly red.\
\
'Ah, yes. I am glad Gléowine is feeling better. What should... what should we do now?'","Horn is standing by Gléowine on the porch outside the Mead Hall of Harwick.\
\
You should speak with Horn about your journey into Wildermore.","The men sent by Harding into Wildermore never returned, and now he wants you to see what has happened within the borders of that land.","'Thank you, my friend. I just needed to hear my doubts aloud to know they are not as important as they seemed inside my head.'","This fishing village seems to be abandoned. What secrets does it retain?","'Wídfara weaves a frightening tale. From where did Núrzum come, and what can we do about him?'","Talk to Corudan in Scylfig","'Forgive me my musings, friend. I am an old man and a minstrel to boot, and both are given to wandering the hedgerows of memory. Horn can give you more practical guidance.'","Find Wídfara or Léodwig within Scylfig, if they are to be found","Defeated mounted combat foes in the Writhendowns (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I have not seen Gléowine since we arrived. You do not think he left Scylfig, do you?'","'We will begin our search in the town of Scylfig, in the Writhendowns. The Writhendowns are west of the Wold, in Wildermore, and according to the map Scylfig is on the northern bounds of the downs.'","Thrymm's training camp is packed with supplies and men eager for battle. But is it enough?","'Thank you for doing some good in the Writhendowns, my new friend. These people have experienced much hardship, and I fear I may have given speed to some of the dangers that threaten them.\
\
'I was riding in the High Knolls with my companions when a blizzard closed in. The snow was blinding and the wind fierce, and I dismounted to seek some measure of shelter. No sooner had my boots touched the ground than a great darkness fell upon me, and a tremendous shape towered over my poor horse Windfoot. I stumbled away, falling into a great drift of snow. It saved my life.'\
\
Wídfara stares straight ahead, his expression haunted.\
\
'Above the tumult I could hear the sound of Núrzum at feast. He made a meal of my poor Windfoot, and only when he had finished and moved away among the crags did I see that my companions were missing. Of Léodwig there was no sign, but I do not think Harding's son was spared. I made my slow way by foot back here to Scylfig, but if he were alive he would have done the same. That is my tale. I hope only that Núrzum is not drawn here by my presence, to threaten the people of Scylfig.'","'The town of Scylfig is located in the Writhendowns, to the west of the Wold. They are the easternmost lands of Wildermore, and they are where we will begin our search for Harding's men.'","'Scylfig is a small town in the Writhendowns, west of the Wold. It is larger than my home of Dunfast, and it is sensible to there begin our search for Wídfara and Léodwig.'","The town of Scylfig is located in the Writhendowns, in Wildermore, west of the Wold.\
\
Your companions have agreed that it is time to begin your search for Harding's men in Wildermore. You will begin with the town of Scylfig.","Find the White Hand camp in the south-east","Talk to Horn outside the Mead Hall in Harwick","Wídfara may be within the town of Scylfig, in the Writhendowns area of Wildermore.\
\
If Wídfara is within Scylfig, you should find him and learn why he has not returned to the Wold."},
[1902]={"'¿Has encontrado las órdenes que te pedí, ${PLAYER}?'","Libro 10, Capítulo 4: Órdenes de marcha","Entrega las órdenes a Fainneleg","'Creo que hemos ganado un pequeño respiro gracias a tus esfuerzos, ${PLAYER}. Aunque los combates siguen asolando toda la ciudad, pasará algún tiempo antes de que Amarthiel pueda reorganizarse y desafiar a nuestras fuerzas con la misma intensidad. Debemos pasar a la ofensiva, si es posible, y para ello necesitamos información.\
\
'Varias posiciones repartidas por la ciudad han cambiado de manos numerosas veces en los últimos días, y creo que estos lugares tienen un significado especial para Amarthiel. Luchamos por recuperarlos siempre que podemos, pero la posesión de estos sitios es tan cambiante como la orilla del Lago Nenuial: siempre en movimiento.\
\
'Te pediría que viajes a estas zonas volátiles y derrotes allí a los esbirros de Amarthiel, pues algunos de ellos seguramente portarán órdenes que contengan los planes futuros de sus ejércitos. Si los Dúnedain controlan el lugar, busca los cuerpos de los enemigos caídos en el combate y regístralos en busca de dichas órdenes. Necesitamos órdenes de estos tres lugares, ${PLAYER}: del patio de Gwaelband, al noreste, donde te encontraste con Rosselloth; de Clorhir, frente a los estanques de Glinghant, al este de Echad Garthadir; y de Menelband, en el nivel más alto de la ciudad.'","Fainneleg se encuentra en el campamento de los Montaraces de Echad Garthadir, en el centro de Annúminas.\
\
Has recuperado las órdenes y deberías regresar de inmediato con Fainneleg.","Recoge órdenes de los angmarim en Gwaelband, Clorhir y Menelband","'Has hecho lo que te pedí, pero me temo que estas órdenes no me dicen mucho: están escritas en la Lengua Negra, y no conozco lo suficiente esa lengua maldita como para traducirlas. Había pensado enviarte con alguien que pudiera leer tales escritos, pero parece que ahora eso quizá no sea necesario.\
\
'He recibido noticias de Calenglad que me llenan de esperanza: ¡nuestra suerte podría estar a punto de cambiar, ${PLAYER}!'","'Necesitamos órdenes de estos tres lugares, ${PLAYER}: del patio de Gwaelband, al noreste, donde te encontraste con Rosselloth; de Clorhir, frente a los estanques de Glinghant, al este de Echad Garthadir; y de Menelband, en el nivel más alto de la ciudad.'","Fainneleg busca órdenes de los angmarim que ocupan el patio de Gwaelband, al noreste de Echad Garthadir, donde te encontraste con Rosselloth; de Clorhir, frente a los estanques de Glinghant, al este de Echad Garthadir; y de Menelband, en el nivel más alto de la ciudad.\
\
Fainneleg te ha hablado de tres ubicaciones inestables en Annúminas. Quiere que derrotes a los angmarim y registres sus cuerpos en busca de cualquier orden que puedan llevar. Si los Dúnedain controlan alguno de estos lugares, Fainneleg te indicó que busques los cuerpos de los angmarim que hayan podido caer en los combates; ellos también podrían haber llevado tales órdenes.","Fainneleg ha decidido que los Montaraces deben elaborar un plan para pasar a la ofensiva y tomar a Amarthiel por sorpresa."},
[1903]={"Libro 10, Capítulo 5: Hacer saltar la trampa","Calenglad está en el campamento de los Montaraces en la isla de Tinnudir.\
\
Calenglad espera saber si aceptarás emprender la peligrosa misión de capturar a Mordrambor, uno de los lugartenientes Númenóreanos Negros de Amarthiel.","'Deberías hablar con Calenglad de inmediato, ${PLAYER}. Ha recibido nueva información que podría cambiar considerablemente la situación en Annúminas.\
\
'Calenglad está en el campamento de los Montaraces en la isla de Tinnudir. Llévale ese fajo de papeles, las órdenes que reuniste. Puede que aún las necesite.'","Habla con Calenglad y captura a Mordrambor","'¿Estás ${PLAYER:listo[m]|lista[f]}, ${PLAYER}? Puede que no tengamos otra oportunidad para capturar a uno de los lugartenientes de confianza de Amarthiel. Debes estar ${PLAYER:preparado[m]|preparada[f]}. El Montaraz Tadan ha ideado un plan, así que asegúrate de hablar con él cuando llegues.'''","'Mi corazón salta de alegría, ${PLAYER}, porque hemos hecho lo que jamás habría imaginado: ¡capturar a uno de los servidores de confianza de Amarthiel! Ella sentirá esta pérdida, ${PLAYER}, estoy seguro de ello. ¡Esta puede ser la ventaja que necesitamos para expulsar a las fuerzas de Amarthiel de Annúminas de una vez por todas!\
\
'Parece que mi decisión fue la correcta: ahora estamos más cerca que nunca de recuperar la ciudad. Cuando lo hayamos hecho, tomaremos el palantír de Amarthiel y pondremos fin para siempre a la amenaza de Angmar!'","'Fainneleg hizo bien en enviarte a mí con tanta premura, ${PLAYER}. Hemos recibido información que podría cambiar nuestra suerte en la batalla por Annúminas.\
\
'Uno de nuestros Montaraces, un buen hombre llamado Torchirion, oyó a varios Angmarim hablar cerca de Adannon, la puerta de la ciudad en la orilla occidental del lago Nenuial. Hablaban de Mordrambor, uno de los Númenóreanos Negros jurados a Amarthiel; un funesto hechicero, Mordrambor es uno de sus lugartenientes más crueles, y Torchirion supo que debía escuchar con atención.\
\
'Antes de que los Angmarim salieran de su alcance, Torchirion les oyó hablar de un encargo urgente que Mordrambor planea para mañana por la noche: viajará con un pequeño séquito, a la luz de la luna, hasta Haudh Elendil. Lo que espera lograr allí no llegó a saberlo Torchirion, ¡pero supo lo suficiente!\
\
'Esta es nuestra oportunidad, ${PLAYER}. Esta es nuestra ocasión de obtener la ventaja en esta batalla. Debemos capturar a Mordrambor. Háblame si tú y tus aliados están dispuestos a hacerlo.'","Calenglad está en el campamento de los Montaraces en la isla de Tinnudir.\
\
Fainneleg oyó unas noticias de Calenglad que renovaron su esperanza y te ha enviado con el viejo Montaraz para oírlas. Te dio las órdenes escritas en la Lengua Negra que reuniste en Gwaelband, Clorhir y Tirband, y dijo que quizá Calenglad las necesite después de todo.","Lleva el fajo de papeles a Calenglad","'¡Calenglad te ha pedido que regreses a su campamento en Tinnudir, y debes ir de inmediato! Solo diré esto: si la información que hemos recibido es fiable, Amarthiel puede haber cometido un error crucial. Si aprovechamos esta oportunidad, los Dúnedain podrían recuperar la ventaja, ${PLAYER}! ¡Annúminas podría volver a nuestras manos dentro de la semana!\
\
'Ve con toda rapidez a ver a Calenglad y podrás juzgar la noticia por ti mismo. Te devolveré las órdenes que reuniste. Puede que Calenglad las necesite después de todo.'","Calenglad está en el campamento de los Montaraces en la isla de Tinnudir.\
\
Tú y un contingente de Montaraces habéis capturado a Mordrambor, uno de los hechiceros Númenóreanos Negros jurados a Amarthiel.","Los Dúnedain han recibido noticias que llevan a Fainneleg y Calenglad a creer que su suerte podría estar a punto de cambiar","'¿Por qué estás aquí?'","'¿Entonces la información de Torchirion era cierta? Es un día de alegría, ${PLAYER}: ¡uno de los lugartenientes de confianza de Amarthiel, encarcelado por los Dúnedain! ¡Este golpe a Angmar sin duda nos ayudará a recuperar Annúminas antes de que termine la semana!'"},
[1904]={"Horn is outside the Mead Hall of Forlaw, in Wildermore.\
\
You have reassured scared villagers and should now return to Horn.","Reassured scared villagers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'You did as I asked? Good, though it be one small drop in a sea of need. I do not know how the uruk-hai made it all the way to the lakeside uncontested, but the loss of some supplies may keep them from staying for as long.\
\
'While you were gone the city shook and rumbled, and my people cowered, thinking Núrzum had come. The city has been spared his wrath thus far, but I say they were right to cower! How long will Forlaw remain out of his sight? When Núrzum does come, how can we hope to defend ourselves? We cannot!\
\
'What sort of a life is this? Is it not cruel to ask my people to live this way, in the shadow of a fear we cannot banish? This is a sorry lot to have drawn, stranger. I thank you for facing the uruk-hai, but if you take my advice you will leave Wildermore behind. Once Núrzum turns his attention to us, we will be gone. It may not happen today, or tomorrow, but I think we will all pass out of life before this unnatural winter does.'","'It is as they said in Scylfig: Reeve Gárwig has given up hope. We will find no plan for facing Núrzum here, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'But first we must reassure the people of Forlaw. We must tell them that their Reeve is still trying to get them through this, that he loves them and believes they can still survive. Winter will pass, Núrzum will fall, and the people of Wildermore will plant new crops and reap a bountiful harvest in days to come. I would not have believed Gárwig had such eloquence in him.'\
\
A smile twitches the corner of his mouth.\
\
'You did not get that impression from our visit with the Reeve? Curious. I am sure he said something like that. Be sure to comfort any scared villagers you see. It seems to me that Gárwig does not often leave his hall; this day, that helps us all.'","Defeat uruk-hai along the shores of the Isingmere (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Book 10, Chapter 5: The Lord of Widows and Orphans","The assemblage stares at Gárwig with open mouth and gloomy countenance","'How did you do? I trust you did not let the truth interfere with your errand, ${PLAYER}?'\
\
Horn laughs, but it is a short and humourless laugh.\
\
'We may have given the people false hope, ${PLAYER}, but if we can do something about Núrzum it will not be a lasting injustice. Things have gone poorly for the people of Forlaw already, but it does not take much thought to see that they could go even worse.'","'Núrzum is far too dangerous for you to face, but perhaps you can do something about the uruk-hai. They are more your size, I would say.\
\
'Go to their camp on the shores of the Isingmere and burn the supply barrels that allow them to remain there. Thin their numbers as well, and you will have done more than most to help my people.'","'The people of Forlaw need to believe that Gárwig still fights for them. Tales of his despair have already travelled too far, and that helps no one.'","Burn uruk-hai supply barrels (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Scared villagers can be found throughout Forlaw.\
\
Horn has asked you to reassure the people of Forlaw that their Reeve is working on some means of defeating Núrzum. That this is not exactly true does not seem to worry Horn very much.","Reeve Gárwig rules from within the Mead Hall of Forlaw, on the southernmost shore of the Isingmere.\
\
Horn has learned that the people of Wildermore do not have confidence in Reeve Gárwig, and thinks you should visit him and learn his plans.","Gárwig squints at you distrustfully.\
\
'Harding sent men to help me, and they were unable to provide any assistance at all! They got themselves eaten, or crushed, or lost in the snow, and worse than that: the survivors crawled back to my villages, bringing their rumbling bellies and broken limbs with them! They are of no use to anyone!\
\
'Where are my warriors? Where are the strong men of Rohan? Dead, or gone, or weakened by the cold and by hunger. All that remain in my hall are orphans and widows. They call me the Lord of Widows and Orphans, did you know that? Me, Gárwig, son of Céolgar, Reeve of Wildermore!\
\
'You cannot face Núrzum, but if you are willing to help there is no shortage of foes seeking to destroy my people! The uruk-hai have secretly been bringing supplies near to Forlaw, along the shores of the Isingmere. Defeat them and burn the barrels of supplies they have brought with them. Do this and you may forestall the end, for a time. Only for a time.'","Reassure scared villagers in Forlaw that Reeve Gárwig still fights for them (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'How can we hope to face the monstrous Núrzum? We cannot! We cannot!'","Reeve Gárwig is in the Mead Hall of Forlaw, in Wildermore.\
\
You have attempted to hinder the movements of the uruk-hai on the shores of the Isingmere, and should return to Reeve Gárwig.","'We should travel to Forlaw to speak with Reeve Gárwig. Let us learn what he plans to do about Núrzum and the suffering people of Wildermore.'","Talk to Reeve Gárwig in the Mead Hall of Forlaw","Horn is outside the Mead Hall of Forlaw.\
\
Reeve Gárwig has given up hope, but you are certain Horn has not, and should see what he intends.","Defeated uruk-hai along the shores of the Isingmere (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The uruk-hai have a camp on the shore of the Isingmere, and Reeve Gárwig has asked you to burn their supply barrels and thin their number.\
\
Reeve Gárwig knows you cannot stand against Núrzum, so he wants you to try and combat some of the uruk-hai instead.","Burned uruk-hai supply barrels (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'While you were away, I spoke to some of the townspeople. Their accounts differ in many respects: Núrzum's height and description, the time at which he first appeared, the places he seems to haunt, all of these differ. Everyone seems to agree on two points: first, that Núrzum is dangerous and must be destroyed if Wildermore is to survive, and second, Reeve Gárwig seems completely incapable of dealing with this threat.\
\
'I hope this is not so, but if it is true that the Reeve of Wildermore cannot protect his people, something must be done. Théoden King will need all of his allies in the days ahead, even if he does not see it, and Rohan cannot have a Wildermore-shaped gap in its northern defences.\
\
'Reeve Gárwig makes his home in the town of Forlaw, to the south of Scylfig, on the southernmost tip of the Isingmere. Let us travel to his Mead Hall and see what plans he has made for combatting Núrzum and aiding his people.'","Talk to Horn outside the Mead Hall of Forlaw","Wildermore faces many dangers, and its Reeve may not be up to the task of defending its people."},
[1905]={"Defeated foes at Kúthaus (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Thank you for the crops you gathered. They will be of use to us if this winter does not lift soon.'","Book 10, Chapter 6: Fallow Ground","'Have you found the provisioner yet? Look in the southern courtyard of Forlaw, and hand over the crops you managed to salvage. Not much, it is true, but better than none.'","Warg-riders can be found throughout the Fallows, in Wildermore, and some foe has shut the southern road into the Norcrofts.\
\
Horn has asked you to defeat Warg-riders in the Fallows and to investigate the southern road out of Wildermore.","Talk to Horn at Gárferth's Farm","Bring salvaged crops to the provisioner in Forlaw","Horn thinks the people of the Fallows could use your help against their enemies.","Gléowine is in Forlaw, and wishes to speak with you.\
\
You have brought some crops to the provisioner in Forlaw, and should now see what Gléowine has been doing.","The provisioner of Forlaw is in the southern courtyard of the city.\
\
You have salvaged some crops from an overrun farm in the Fallows, and should bring them to the provisioner at Forlaw.","'DNT - ¡Bah!'","Collect salvageable crops from Edsig's Farm (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'The Wargs come always from the south-west, and the people I speak with tell me that Edsig's Farm is overrun. Go there, defeat the Wargs, and salvage any crops you find. The provisioner at Forlaw will be glad of the extra supplies, as will Reeve Gárwig if it comes to a siege.'","'Ah, this cruel winter has worked much evil already for the farms of Wildermore. Once you would have found such a bounty of crops at any one of those farms! Instead, you have this small share. The provisioner is in the southern courtyard of Forlaw, and will be glad of them, at any rate.'","Collected salvageable crops (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat Warg-riders in the Fallows (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated Warg-riders in the Fallows (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Wargs and their riders stalk the Fallows, and many can be located Edsig's Farm, located in the southern reaches.\
\
Horn has asked you to defeat the Wargs and their riders in the Fallows, and to bring any salvageable crops you find from Edsig's Farm to the provisioner at Forlaw.","'Thank you for these. I am glad the Orcs did not despoil these crops. We will surely have need of them, unless this terrible winter lifts tomorrow. It came on so suddenly. Perhaps it will leave equally so!\
\
'If it does not, these crops will buy us a few days more. I suppose that is the best for which we can hope.'","Talk to Gléowine in Forlaw","'Gárwig may not see a means of defeating Núrzum, but we should not judge him too harshly. He buckles under the weight of his worry, but there is strength there. It is buried deeply, like the fields of Wildermore beneath this unnatural cold.\
\
'Gléowine tells me that the Fallows were home to the most bountiful farms in Wildermore. If they survive at all it is a testament to the strong will of their owners, but they are not warriors, and their strength will not last when faced with uruk-hai and Warg-riders.\
\
'The road runs south through the Fallows and leaves Wildermore at its southernmost reaches, but no riders or information have gone that way for some weeks. Ride among the farms of the Fallows and defeat Warg-riders on your way to that pass. I suspect some foe holds the road against us. Defeat whatever you find there, and meet me at Gárferth's Farm afterward. We will do what good we can against the foes we can manage. Núrzum must wait.'","'This chill gets into my bones, and makes me miss the Golden Wood. Still, we go where we are needed, and without complaint.\
\
'For the most part, ${PLAYER}. For the most part.'","'Warg-riders can be found throughout the Fallows, and some foe has shut the southern road out of Wildermore. I think we should put a stop to it.'","Defeat foes at the southern exit from Wildermore, in the Fallows (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Horn is waiting for you at Gárferth's Farm, in the south-east reaches of the Fallows.\
\
You have defeated both Warg-riders and the uruk-hai at Kúthaus, and should now meet Horn at Gárferth's Farm, where he said he would be waiting for you.","'It is a wonder you found any crops at all, ${PLAYER}. This unnatural cold is well on its way to choking the life from the lands of Wildermore, plant and Man alike.'","'The people hope that this unnatural winter will soon lift, but it is hard for me to think it will. It came on too suddenly to be properly of this world.'","'Oh, this cold! This feels nothing like the Wildermore of my youth, ${PLAYER}. I left as a young man and returned an old one, and the land that greets me is more different than I myself have become!\
\
'Deserted farms, frozen rivers, enemies lurking behind every tree and over every stone. What will we find when we come to my home of Dunfast?'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Completing this quest will unlock an optional interlude from Gléowine's map.</rgb>","Defeated Wargs or Warg-riders in the Fallows (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat Wargs and their riders in the Fallows (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'What did you find at the southern road into the Norcrofts?'\
\
Horn listens to your account of the uruk-hai at Kúthaus.\
\
'That is as I suspected, ${PLAYER}. If there had been no danger, word would have left Wildermore of its troubles well before now.\
\
'Speaking with what few folk I have found, I learned from where the Wargs come: a farm to the south-west, once owned by Edsig, but now overrun by the minions of Saruman and the creatures they ride. Defeat Wargs and Warg-riders in the Fallows, as you have done, but do so now in and around Edsig's Farm. You may slow their assault on the other farms. If you find salvageable crops at Edsig's Farm, bring them to the provisioner at Forlaw. If it comes to a siege, Reeve Gárwig will be glad of the additional supplies.'"},
[1906]={"'Nuestro prisionero traducirá las órdenes para ti. La única cuestión es cuándo lo hará. ¡Solo espero que los Dúnedain puedan resistir frente a Amarthiel el tiempo que sea necesario!\
\
'Lleva el fajo de papeles a Mordrambor en la fortaleza de esta isla. Al entrar en la fortaleza, la puerta de la izquierda conduce a las escaleras que suben hasta la prisión que hemos preparado para nuestro cautivo.'","Con la captura de Mordrambor, la suerte de los Dúnedain podría estar cambiando. Si se logra que traduzca las órdenes que encontraste, el curso de la batalla podría inclinarse a favor de los Pueblos Libres.","'¿Los Dúnedain han capturado al Númenóreano Negro Mordrambor? Apenas puedo creer esta noticia, ${PLAYER}, ¡pero no bajes la guardia! Incluso prisionero, Mordrambor intentará cumplir la voluntad de su ama.'","Libro 10, Capítulo 6: El secreto de las órdenes","'¿No tienes nada para mí?'","'Apenas puedo creer nuestra buena fortuna, ${PLAYER}. Toma ahora estas órdenes y muéstraselas a nuestro prisionero. Nos dirá su significado de buen grado, o se lo haremos decir. No imagino que Amarthiel inspire otra cosa que no sea temor en sus lugartenientes, y este Númenóreano Negro sin duda nos dirá lo que necesitamos saber si siente que se le perdonará la vida.\
\
'Mi gente ha preparado una prisión para el cautivo, y el Montaraz Tadan se ha ofrecido voluntario para vigilarlo. Tadan es un buen hombre, un hombre fuerte, y se asegurará de que las ataduras de Mordrambor no cedan. Entra en la fortaleza aquí en Tinnudir y toma la puerta de la izquierda para subir por las escaleras que conducen a la prisión.\
\
'Lleva este fajo de papeles a Mordrambor y exige que nos diga su significado. Sin duda conoce la Lengua Negra y nos dirá lo que debemos saber antes de mucho tiempo. Cuanto antes lo haga, mejor será nuestra suerte, y no dudo de que lo hará.'","'Hola, ${PLAYER}. ¡Aún sigo lleno de asombro por nuestra victoria a las afueras de Haudh Elendil! No creo exagerar al decir que juntos podemos haber cambiado el curso de la batalla por Annúminas, ¡y para mejor!\
\
'Me aseguraré de que este villano permanezca bien encerrado. No parece muy contento con su destino, ¿verdad?'","'Te recuerdo, imbécil ${CLASS}. Conozco el número de tus días, y son pocos. Hablemos un momento, entonces, pues pronto caerás bajo el paso de Angmar.\
\
'¿Qué me has traído? ¿Escritos en la Lengua Negra, la más hermosa de todas las lenguas? ¿No puedes leer estas palabras? Lamento tu ignorancia, imbécil ${CLASS}, pero me apiadaré de ti, pues tu lucha pronto terminará en dolor y aflicción. Te diré lo que la gran Amarthiel planea para los miserables que aún se aferran a esta mísera ciudad.\
\
'Muéstrame estas páginas. Me deleitaré al predecir tu final.'","Muestra el fajo de papeles a Mordrambor","Mordrambor se encuentra prisionero en la fortaleza de la isla de Tinnudir, en Evendim. Al entrar en el torreón, la puerta de la izquierda conduce a unas escaleras que suben hasta la prisión.\
\
Calenglad te ha dado las órdenes que reuniste de los Angmarim en Annúminas para que se las muestres al prisionero Númenóreano Negro. Mordrambor conoce la Lengua Negra y debe ser obligado a traducir las órdenes para ti."},
[1907]={"Has derrotado a Roibárd","Has derrotado a Mól Choluim","'Hacía tiempo que no te veía, ${PLAYERNAME:necio[m]|necia[f]} . ¿Has estado ocupándote de encargos inútiles?'","'¿Estas bestias no se interesan por el oro? ¡No importa! ¡Te aplastaré personalmente y llevaré tu piel a Amarthiel como un regalo inesperado!'","'Traes tanto buenas como malas noticias, ${PLAYER}. Que los emisarios hayan sido derrotados es una preocupación menos, pero temo que la lealtad de los saqueadores de tumbas de Rantost y de los Gauredain de Emyn Uial ya haya sido comprada.\
\
'Podemos considerarnos afortunados de que los Kergrim no sientan aprecio alguno por el oro de Angmar, pero eso no es una gran ventaja frente a una oposición tan numerosa.\
\
'Cuguminuial me trajo algunos alimentos horneados y varias opciones para la cena; puedes servirte si lo deseas. Creo que se sintió apenada de que deba pasar tanto tiempo en compañía del prisionero. No me gusta el pastel de zanahoria, así que me harías un favor si te llevas eso, aunque también puedes tomar algo del resto.'","'Estas palabras cantan sobre tu muerte y la de todos los Dúnedain, ${CLASS}. Las páginas indican a los servidores leales de Amarthiel que aguarden el regreso de sus emisarios, que han viajado a muchas tierras en busca de nuevos aliados.\
\
'Las aguas del lago han sido como un camino para los emisarios de Amarthiel, y transportan oro con el que comprar la lealtad de nuevos servidores: personas de corazón frío en una isla lejana al noreste; los Gauredain de las colinas del noroeste, feroces y salvajes; y los Kergrim, grandes bestias que acechan entre las criptas de reyes muertos hace mucho tiempo.\
\
'Cuando estos servidores regresen desde más allá de las grandes aguas, tal será el número de nuevos aliados jurados a la Corona de Hierro que nadie podrá albergar esperanza alguna de prevalecer contra ellos.'","Mordrambor te habló de tres emisarios Angmarim enviados para comprar la lealtad de nuevos aliados para los ejércitos de Amarthiel en Annúminas: los saqueadores de tumbas de la isla de Rantost, en el extremo noreste del lago; los Gauredain, cerca del extremo noroeste; y los Kergrim, entre las tumbas de Men Erain, a lo largo del extremo sureste del lago.\
\
Mordrambor te habló de tres emisarios enviados en barco a través del lago Nenuial para comprar la lealtad de algunas de las fuerzas malignas que asolan Evendim.","'Este es exactamente el tipo de información que Calenglad esperaba, ${PLAYER}. Si logras derrotar a estos emisarios antes de que consigan comprar la lealtad de estos tres enemigos, los planes de Amarthiel se verán obstaculizados.\
\
'Puede que no podamos confiar plenamente en las palabras de Mordrambor, pero no tenemos alternativa: esta es una oportunidad que debemos aprovechar. Si logramos impedir que Angmar obtenga estos nuevos aliados, la captura de Mordrambor habrá valido la pena con creces.\
\
'Sus palabras indican que tres emisarios Angmarim cruzaron el lago Nenuial en barco en busca de tres nuevas lealtades: los saqueadores de tumbas de la isla de Rantost, al noreste; los Gauredain de las colinas del noroeste de Emyn Uial; y los Kergrim de Men Erain. Encuentra y detén a estos emisarios del mal, ${PLAYER}. Busca sus embarcaciones a lo largo de las orillas del lago, cerca de cada una de estas amenazas, pues sin duda estarán cerca, a menos que ya sea demasiado tarde.'","Encuentra al emisario de Amarthiel ante los Kergrim","Libro 10, Capítulo 7: Emisarios del Mal","'¡Si intentas detener mis negociaciones, llegas demasiado tarde! ¡Los Gauredain ahora luchan por Amarthiel! ¡A mí, aliados!'","Mordrambor ha traducido las órdenes que recuperaste de los Angmarim en Annúminas y ha revelado un plan mortal para obtener más aliados en la lucha por la ciudad.","'¿Mordrambor tradujo las órdenes de buen grado? Debo admitir que no creí que lo haría con tanta facilidad.\
\
'Debemos actuar con cautela, ${PLAYER}, pues no es alguien digno de confianza, pero si logramos entorpecer los planes de estos emisarios, podríamos evitar mucho derramamiento de sangre.\
\
'Busca embarcaciones a lo largo de la orilla del lago, cerca de cada uno de los tres aliados de los que habló Mordrambor. Deberías encontrar a los emisarios no muy lejos de sus puntos de desembarco, a menos que ya sea demasiado tarde.'","Has derrotado a Cailin","Encuentra al emisario de Amarthiel ante la gente de Rantost","Encuentra al emisario de Amarthiel ante los Gauredain","'¿Has derrotado a los emisarios de Amarthiel? Son noticias excelentes, ${PLAYER}, incluso si algunas lealtades ya habían cambiado. Tadan se alegrará al saber que el prisionero ha aligerado nuestra carga con su información, por poco fiable que sea.'","'¡Llegas demasiado tarde, imbécil! Amarthiel recompensa a quienes le sirven con fidelidad, y así lo he hecho.\
\
'Estos pueblos le servirán bien cuando lleguen a luchar en la vieja ciudad, y seré recompensado por haberlos traído. ¡Pero antes acabaré contigo!'","'Habla con quien consideres aliado, si así lo deseas. Dile que sus días serán más cortos que los tuyos.\
\
'Amarthiel pronto contará con nuevos aliados, cuyas lealtades han sido compradas con oro, y sentirás el filo de sus armas y la ferocidad de sus colmillos.'","El Montaraz Tadan se encuentra en la prisión, en lo alto de la escalera a la izquierda al entrar en la fortaleza de la isla de Tinnudir, en Evendim.\
\
Has derrotado a los tres emisarios enviados por Amarthiel para reclutar nuevos aliados para la batalla de Annúminas, y ahora deberías informar de tus victorias a Tadan."},
[1908]={"'All is quiet. Where are the people?'","'Nona is still not ready to journey with us again. I confess I am surprised.'","'I understand Gléowine's desire completely, ${PLAYER}. I would feel the same if I heard such troubling news about Lothlórien. We would be poor companions indeed were we to refuse this request. We should travel to Dunfast, though the situation there promises to be no different than elsewhere in Wildermore. Let us hope for Gléowine's sake I am wrong.'","Book 10, Chapter 7: Unnatural Winter","Gléowine is concerned about the home in which he grew up, in the town of Dunfast, and wants to see what has become of it.","'I am ready. Let us make for the village of Dunfast, in the Whitshaws.'","'The air is so still. What happened here?'","The village of Dunfast is located in the middle of the Whitshaws, in Wildermore.\
\
Horn and Corudan agree that you should all journey to Gléowine's home, Dunfast, and see how it has been treated by this unnatural winter.","Talk to Corudan in Forlaw","'It is so quiet.'","'Would you mind asking Horn and Corudan if they mind a quick visit to Dunfast?'","Travel to the village of Dunfast, in the middle of the Whitshaws, in Wildermore","'Nothing moves. The air is very still.'","'We will go together to investigate Dunfast. What has happened here?'","'¿Dónde están todos?'","Talk to Gléowine outside Dunfast","Gléowine is outside the village of Dunfast, in the Whitshaws.\
\
Little moves among the houses of Dunfast, and Gléowine is very worried.","Talk to Horn outside Dunfast, in the Whitshaws","'I am done with worrying. I want to see for myself what has become of my home. I have not been there for many years, but when last I walked in Wildermore the land itself was very different! What could have become of the small village in which I was born?\
\
'I would not presume to divert our course without everyone's agreement, ${PLAYER}. If you consent to this journey, and so too do Horn and Corudan, then I would be grateful for a visit to Dunfast.\
\
'If not, I fully understand and ask only that you forgive me the request in the first place.'","'I may be old and not as sharp as once I was, but I can see that the Dunlending girl was dear to Horn. She wounded him, and he has still not recovered.'","Horn is waiting to speak with you outside Dunfast.\
\
Nona reappeared again, but the reunion did not proceed as Horn wished. He is waiting to speak with you.","Talk to Horn in Forlaw","'Dunfast was never a large village, but there were always people about. What has happened here? I see no signs of battle. Where are the people?\
\
'We should search the village, ${PLAYER}. Let me know when you are ready, and the four of us will explore Dunfast together.'","Talk to Gléowine and explore Dunfast together","Horn and Corudan are in the town of Forlaw, in Wildermore.\
\
Gléowine wants to visit Dunfast, the village in which he was born, to see how it has been affected by this unnatural winter.","'Dunfast is in the forest of the Whitshaws. Let us go there at once.'","'I wonder if Gléowine's reception at Dunfast will be warmer than my own at Eaworth? Will he regret the journey as I did?'\
\
Horn frowns.\
\
'Ah, it was a poor jest. I have much for which to be grateful, and only a lesser man takes as assured the health and safety of his family. Gléowine's family has long since left the village of Dunfast, but I can understand his desire to see what has become of the place. I agree to the journey. Did you think I would not?'","'Thank you, ${PLAYER}. Let us travel to the forest of the Whitshaws and see what has become of Dunfast!'","The air is very still, and Dunfast seems unnaturally quiet","'You must think me a fool, but you are kind not to say so. This is not how I imagined this day, ${PLAYER}. I thought Nona would come back into my life and all would be as I wished it to be, but this is not what I wanted! I am more confused now than ever.\
\
'This is not how love works in the songs, ${PLAYER}. It feels as if the unnatural winter that grips this land has cooled Nona's heart as well.'","Gléowine is outside Dunfast, in the Whitshaws.\
\
Gléowine wants to investigate Dunfast with you, Horn, and Corudan, and is waiting to speak with you."},
[1909]={"Corudan is outside Dunfast, in the Whitshaws.\
\
Horn is of little use to anyone, pining as he is over Nona. Perhaps Corudan will have some guidance.","Bring root vegetables to Corudan outside Dunfast","'I know what we need to do, ${PLAYER}! We need to go to the cave of which Nona spoke and help her provide for the refugees she mentioned. First, we should gather the root vegetables she needs. Do you remember? She said that... what? Why are you looking at me like that?'\
\
Horn trails off, following your gaze to the pile of root vegetables at Corudan's feet. Then he bursts out laughing.\
\
'Wonderful, ${PLAYER}! You remain two or three steps ahead of this humble minstrel, and I have no excuse but the foggy shroud of love to explain my predictability! You have my thanks, my thoughtful ${CLASS}, as you always have done!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Completing this quest will unlock an optional interlude from Gléowine's map.</rgb>","Book 10, Chapter 8: Drifting Snows","'I am glad we were able to do some good here in the Whitshaws. I think Horn is feeling better, as well. There is no cure for an aching heart quite like hard work.\
\
'Speak to him and see if I am right, ${PLAYER}.'","Has derrotado orcos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'We must do what we can to make the Whitshaws safe. Hunt Orcs within the forest, and pay particular attention to the base of trees. You should look for the root vegetables Nona mentioned.'","Defeat Orcs in the Whitshaws (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You have encountered Nona once again, but she has not changed her mind and refuses to travel with you. Horn does not know what to do, but Corudan sees the value in keeping the Rohirrim man occupied.","Horn is outside Dunfast, in the Whitshaws.\
\
Corudan has asked that you see how Horn is feeling.","'I do not know what to do. Seeing Nona again has caused me to worry more than before!\
\
'Perhaps Corudan will know what we can do.'","Horn sighs wistfully and looks off into the distance.","'It is a strange feeling, but I am glad Dunfast still stands. It may be a hollow village now, with no people, but it is oddly comforting to know the buildings still stand. That was no guarantee, of course, with Núrzum stalking this land.'","'What? What is it?'","Corudan is outside Dunfast, in the Whitshaws.\
\
You have done as Corudan asked, defeating Orcs and Warg-riders and collecting the root vegetables for which Nona asked.","Found root vegetables (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Is it strange for me to be pleased that Dunfast still stands? It may be a hollow village now, with no people, but it is oddly comforting to know the buildings still stand. That was no guarantee, of course, with Núrzum stalking this land.'","'Speak with Horn and see how he is doing. An aching heart is not easily cured, but time and hard work is the best remedy.'","'Nona said she has sheltered some refugees in a cave in the mountains of the High Knolls, but we cannot go there immediately. I do not need to ask Corudan to know such a reunion, so soon after this first meeting, would spell disaster!'\
\
Horn puts his hand to his temple, but he cannot mask the weariness on his face.\
\
'All that has happened to us in Wildermore is a muddle, ${PLAYER}! Only this encounter with Nona has any clarity in my memory. How can such a pain of the heart fill me with both delight and sadness?'","Talk to Horn outside Dunfast","'Horn may be at a loss, but I know what must be done. We must do what we can about the White Hand presence in the Whitshaws. This will aid Nona, it will aid us, and it will aid any of the people of Dunfast that may still live.\
\
'It will even aid Horn. He needs to keep himself busy or he will dwell upon losing Nona for a second time. He may dwell on it anyway, but if we can channel that energy to a good purpose there may have been some benefit in seeing her again this early.'\
\
Corudan idly toys with the string of his bow for a moment, and then speaks up again.\
\
'Those root vegetables Nona mentioned, the ones that grow at the bases of trees. I think you should collect some of them, if you see any. It is just a thought, but it may save us some time tomorrow if we collect them today.'","Find root vegetables in the Whitshaws (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Orcs can be found throughout the Whitshaws. Root vegetables can be found at the bases of many trees in the area outside Dunfast.\
\
Corudan wants you to keep busy while Horn decides what he wants to do, and this involves defeating Saruman's minions in the Whitshaws and collecting the root vegetables Nona mentioned.","Talk to Corudan outside Dunfast","Horn sighs wistfully and gazes off into the distance. You wonder what he's thinking about, and decide you'll never know.\
\
Then you wonder if Corudan's dry wit has rubbed off on you permanently.","'Our search of Dunfast revealed little to me. I hope its people survive, wherever they have gone. Perhaps some of the refugees this Nona mentioned were from Dunfast?'","An optional Interlude has been unlocked for Gléowine's map"},
[1910]={"Mordrambor se encuentra prisionero en la cárcel, en lo alto de las escaleras a la izquierda al entrar en la fortaleza de la isla de Tinnudir, en Evendim.\
\
Has entregado el mensaje de Mordrambor a Laerdan tal como pidió, y el elfo te ha advertido que tengas cuidado con la traición del Númenóreano Negro, pues incluso prisionero supone un gran peligro. Si cumple su palabra, Mordrambor debería decirte ahora el lugar del próximo asalto planeado por Amarthiel contra Annúminas.","'¿Dices que los emisarios de Amarthiel han sido derrotados? Leo más en tus ojos de lo que has dicho. Tal vez sus tareas ya estaban cumplidas, sus misiones concluidas. Sí, leo bien. Pero sigue sonriendo, imbécil ${RACE}; contra Angmar y su regente no hay esperanza para ti. Ella planea un nuevo asalto contra ciertos lugares de la ciudad, y tus amistades Dúnedain no pueden esperar resistirle.\
\
'Y aun así... te diré dónde caerán con más fuerza esos ataques. Deseo con ansias oír tu llanto y el de ese necio Montaraz cuando Amarthiel tome la ciudad pese a tus pobres defensas. Pero solo te diré dónde caerá el martillo si haces algo por mí.\
\
'Un elfo ha llegado a esta fortaleza; me observó desde lejos cuando ese necio Montaraz me trajo a esta patética prisión. Ese elfo se llama Laerdan, y quiero que le lleves un mensaje. El mensaje es este: \\qLaerdan, tu tiempo está por terminar, tus errores pronto serán juzgados. Amarthiel te espera en Barad Tironn, donde se sentará a juzgarte.\\q Lleva estas palabras, o no sabrás nada de mí.'","'Deberías intentar hablar con Mordrambor, ${PLAYER}. Sé que no es agradable, pero si logramos obtener más información sobre lo que Amarthiel ha planeado para Annúminas, estaremos mejor preparados.'","'Prepárate contra las palabras de Mordrambor, ${PLAYER}, pues es hábil en enredar los pensamientos, como lo son la mayoría de los de su calaña. Intentará confundirte con engaños elaborados y frases ambiguas, y conducirte así a la traición. Mantente alerta ante sus sutilezas y no tendrá poder alguno sobre ti.\
\
'He escuchado su mensaje y ahora te pido que prestes atención al mío: no bajes la guardia. Incluso prisionero, un Númenóreano Negro es un enemigo peligroso, y nos llevará a todos a la ruina si no nos protegemos de sus artimañas.\
\
'Regresa ahora con el prisionero y dile que has cumplido tu parte del trato. Y recuerda mis palabras.'","Mordrambor te ha dicho que Amarthiel planea nuevos asaltos en lugares concretos de la ciudad, pero solo te dirá dónde si entregas un mensaje en su nombre.","Mordrambor se encuentra en la prisión, en lo alto de las escaleras tras la puerta de la izquierda al entrar en la fortaleza de la isla de Tinnudir, en Evendim.\
\
Mordrambor ha estado murmurando sobre nuevos ataques contra la ciudad, pero se niega a darle más detalles a Tadan. Tadan espera que puedas obtener alguna información del prisionero.","'¡El prisionero no está en posición de hacer exigencias, ${PLAYER}! Pero debo admitir que es una oferta tentadora: ¿cuántas vidas podríamos salvar si supiéramos de antemano dónde golpeará Amarthiel?\
\
'Laerdan es un elfo sabio. No puede haber daño alguno en entregar el mensaje del prisionero, y hay mucho que ganar.'","'No me agrada esto, ${PLAYER}. ¿Qué daño pueden causar estas palabras, por malintencionadas y ofensivas que sean? Aun así, me inquietan. Y sin embargo, si nos dice dónde esperar el próximo asalto de Amarthiel, muchas de nuestras personas podrían salvarse.\
\
'No veo que tengamos otra opción. Laerdan es un elfo sabio; sabrá ver estas palabras por lo que son —los insultos viles de un prisionero desesperado— y las descartará.\
\
'Laerdan ha recibido una habitación en lo alto de las escaleras, tras la puerta de la derecha al entrar en la fortaleza.'","Laerdan ha recibido una habitación en la fortaleza de la isla de Tinnudir, en lo alto de las escaleras tras la puerta de la derecha al entrar en el torreón.\
\
Mordrambor te ha dicho que Amarthiel planea nuevos asaltos contra la ciudad de Annúminas, pero solo revelará los lugares exactos si entregas el siguiente mensaje a Laerdan: 'Laerdan, tu tiempo está por terminar, tus errores pronto serán juzgados. Amarthiel te espera en Barad Tironn, donde se sentará a juzgarte.'","'No necesito que Laerdan me diga que no se puede confiar en el prisionero. Aun así, nos ha sido de gran utilidad hasta ahora, y por una vez la batalla parece inclinarse a nuestro favor. ¡Amarthiel sin duda lamenta la noche en que le arrebatamos a uno de sus lugartenientes más preciados!'","'No confíes en él, ${PLAYER}. Mordrambor intentará confundirte con sus palabras, hechizarte con su discurso. Debes protegerte de ello, incluso cuando parezca inofensivo, pues no lo es.'","'El prisionero ha estado sonriendo con suficiencia durante todo el tiempo que estuviste fuera, y eso me ha tenido preocupado.\
\
'Parece muy seguro de algo. No deja de murmurar sobre nuevos ataques contra la ciudad, pero cada vez que le pregunto al respecto, se niega a hablar conmigo.\
\
'¿Tal vez puedas sacarle algo? No parece tener reparos en ocultarte información, ${PLAYER}.'","'Me alegra verte de regreso, pues sé que has entregado mi mensaje a Laerdan. También sé lo que debió decirte: \\qPrepárate contra sus palabras. Mantente alerta ante sus sutilezas.\\q\
\
'¿Cómo dijiste que te llamas? ¿${PLAYER}? Te doy las gracias, ${PLAYER}, por cumplir nuestro trato. Ahora haré lo mismo.\
\
'Te diré dónde se producirán los próximos asaltos contra la ciudad.'","'Ve de inmediato a hablar con el prisionero y dile que has cumplido nuestra parte del trato. Hay poco tiempo que perder, ${PLAYER}, pues en esto no dudo que decía la verdad: Amarthiel planea nuevos asaltos y debemos saber dónde atacará.'","'No has entregado mi mensaje al elfo Laerdan, y no te diré nada.'","Libro 10, Capítulo 8: El mensaje del prisionero"},
[1911]={"'Tienes nuevamente mi agradecimiento, ${PLAYER}. Me entristece profundamente enfrentar en batalla a la gente de Evendim; el oro de Angmar ha cambiado con demasiada facilidad sus corazones, llevándolos del extravío al mal.'","'¿Una vez más las palabras de Mordrambor nos han guiado con acierto, ${PLAYER}? Fue sin duda una gran fortuna que permitiera que tú y Tadan lo convirtieran en prisionero de los Montaraces.'","'¿Qué te ocurre, ${PLAYER}? No pareces estar bien. Tal vez deberías tomar algo de descanso. Los enemigos que tenemos enfrente son temibles, pero es necesario recuperar fuerzas de vez en cuando; no se puede combatir a un enemigo así durante tanto tiempo sin descanso.\
\
'¿Qué noticias traes? ¿Mordrambor nos ha revelado los lugares de los próximos ataques de Amarthiel contra la ciudad? ¿El puerto de Annúminas y la puerta de Adannon, como antes? ¿Qué espera lograr con este nuevo asalto? Ve de inmediato a ver a Gwonil en los muelles y a Torchirion en Adannon, y ayúdalos a repeler estos nuevos ataques.\
\
'Lo siento, ${PLAYER}. Tal vez puedas descansar cuando este ataque haya terminado. ¡No podemos perder esas posiciones ahora!'","Gwonil se encuentra en los muelles del puerto de Annúminas, al norte de Echad Garthadir. Torchirion está en Adannon, una pequeña puerta en la muralla de la ciudad, al oeste de los muelles, que da acceso a la orilla occidental del lago Nenuial.\
\
Calenglad te ha pedido que acudas con rapidez en defensa de Gwonil y Torchirion; según las palabras de Mordrambor, ellos soportarán el peso principal del último asalto de Amarthiel contra la ciudad.","Habla con Torchirion y defiende su posición","Has defendido con éxito la posición de Torchirion","Has defendido con éxito la posición de Gwonil","'Todo ha estado tranquilo desde la última vez que estuviste aquí, ${PLAYER}. Sospechaba que los Angmarim podrían estar planeando un nuevo asalto, pero hasta ahora no he visto señales de ello.'","Calenglad está en el campamento de los Montaraces de la isla de Tinnudir, en Evendim.\
\
Mordrambor te ha pedido que informes a Calenglad sobre los lugares planeados para los próximos asaltos de Amarthiel: el puerto de Annúminas y la puerta de Adannon.","Libro 10, Capítulo 9: Un asalto renovado","'Entiendo que ya has visto los lugares del próximo asalto de Amarthiel, ${PLAYER}, y que quienes los defienden confían en la solidez de sus defensas.\
\
'Pero esta vez será diferente, pues Amarthiel cuenta con nuevos servidores y todos tus esfuerzos han sido en vano. Ve ahora a informar a tu superior, Calenglad de Tinnudir, y dile dónde caerán quienes defiende: en el puerto de Annúminas y en la puerta de Adannon.\
\
'Amarthiel me ha revelado los nombres de quienes están marcados para morir: Gwonil y Torchirion. Dile a Calenglad que no volverán a salir de Annúminas. Observa con atención su dolor, ${PLAYER}... ¡aguardo con ansias las noticias que traerás!'","'¿Hablaste con Calenglad? Bien, bien. Tal vez ahora comprenda que no puede haber victoria contra la regente de Angmar. ¿Deseas ayudar a quienes defienden el puerto y Adannon, o has decidido aceptar la verdad? Estos necios no pueden oponerse a nosotros.'","Han sido tiempos difíciles para todos, ${PLAYER}, pero te lo prometo: una vez que hayas ayudado a Gwonil y a Torchirion en la defensa del puerto de Annúminas y la puerta de Adannon, intentaremos depender menos de ti. Podrás tomar algo de descanso.'","'Puede que todo lo demás caiga, pero tú y yo mantendremos la puerta de Adannon frente a cualquier agresor. ¿No es así, ${PLAYER}?'","Calenglad está en el campamento de los Montaraces de la isla de Tinnudir, en Evendim.\
\
Has defendido a Gwonil y a Torchirion de los asaltos anunciados por Mordrambor y ahora deberías regresar con Calenglad para informarle de tu éxito.","'Corre y dile a tu superior, Calenglad, que pronto tendrá motivos para lamentar a quienes defienden el puerto de Annúminas y la puerta de Adannon.\
\
'Me traerás noticias de su pesar, ${PLAYER}, ¿no es así?'","'No veo nada, ${PLAYER}. ¿Estás ${PLAYER:seguro[m]|segura[f]} de que el prisionero dijo que planeaban un nuevo asalto contra los muelles?","Habla con Gwonil y defiende su posición","A cambio de llevar su mensaje a Laerdan, Mordrambor te ha revelado los lugares del próximo asalto planeado por Amarthiel contra Annúminas.","'No prestes atención al prisionero, ${PLAYER}. Laerdan tenía razón: sus palabras son viles y no significan nada.\
\
'Juega con nosotros, pero aun así es posible extraer información valiosa. Gwonil y Torchirion son personas cercanas a mí, y si gracias a las palabras de Mordrambor podemos acudir en su defensa, estaré dispuesto a soportar sus susurros ponzoñosos.\
\
'Lleva estas noticias a Calenglad. Debe saber lo que nos aguarda.'"},
[1912]={"Defeat Orcs in Byre Tor until Gléowine has finished composing his song","The man stares foreward with sightless eyes, and his breathing is shallow and ragged. He makes no sign of seeing you.","Gléowine sings, 'A city on a hill she was, strong Byre Tor, fair Byre Tor.'","'One day I will kill the Orcs responsible for this, my new friend. One day.'","'I would like to see Byre Tor, ${PLAYER}. There is a kernel of a song in my heart, and I wish to make it grow.\
\
'The city is north of here, along the road.'","Gléowine sings, 'From each corner of the land all would ride.'","'I wonder what became of the horses of Byre Tor? I wish there was a way for me to repay them. Without their panic I might not have known to flee before it was too late! I suppose they have all been slain or eaten by now.'","Gléowine looks at the city and sighs. 'Byre Tor has indeed fallen, as we feared.'","Gléowine sings, 'But the winter came, and with it an iron tide.'","'I am fortunate Nona found me. I would be dead if she had not, and these others with me.'","'Do you see now why I cannot abandon these people, ${PLAYER}? I have to know they are safe. I have been speaking with Horn, and he... he understands.'\
\
Nona turns the full force of her scowl upon Horn, who seems to have lost his voice temporarily. 'He understands,' she continues.\
\
'Thank you all for the root vegetables, also! I will see if that will help spur the recovery of those in my care. I fear it will not be enough for the dying man in my care.'","Horn and Gléowine want you to defeat Orcs in the city of Byre Tor.\
\
Gléowine desires to compose a song about Byre Tor, and is using your battles with Orcs as inspiration.","'Gléowine has finished his song, and I am satisfied with the death we brought to the Orcs in Byre Tor. It is time to seek out the cave where Nona cares for the survivors from the wreck of that city!'","'Nona told us that the survivors in her care came from the city of Byre Tor. According to Gléowine's map, that is north of here along the road, amid the High Knolls of Wildermore.\
\
'My master has also expressed a desire to see the city. I believe he has the kernel of a song in his heart, and desires to see what has befallen Byre Tor in order to make that kernel set forth its shoots.\
\
'If we find Orcs there, as we certainly must, we will slay them. If Nona's heart beats for the people under her care, so too does mine, ${PLAYER}.'","The City of Byre Tor is in the High Knolls of Wildermore, located north of Dunfast along the road.\
\
Horn desires to see the city of Byre Tor for himself and then to proceed on to the cave of which Nona spoke.","Book 10, Chapter 9: A Song for Byre Tor","Nona está en su cueva en las Altas Cumbres.","Gléowine sings, 'And it was our day to comfort, our time to protect.'","The survivors Nona rescued from Byre Tor can be found throughout the two chambers of her cave.","'My friends... I am glad to see you, really I am. But I just cannot... I cannot leave these people. I found them dying in the snow, and I brought them here, but they have not yet recovered. I will not abandon them now.'\
\
Nona lowers her voice and speaks privately to you and Horn.\
\
'I rescued four folk from that city, and while three of them are now doing much better, I fear the fourth may succumb. Speak to them, if they will speak to you, and there may be something you can do to ease their recoveries.\
\
'I am glad to see you, ${PLAYER}, and... and Horn. I just...'\
\
Nona trails off and will speak no more for now.","Search the cave for Nona","Gléowine sings, 'To that city on the hill, strong Byre Tor, fair Byre Tor.'","If this is the cave of which Nona spoke, she will likely be somewhere inside.","Find the entrance to Nona's cave in the High Knolls","'My name is Ymma. Any friend of Nona's is a friend of mine, and a friend of my family's, though most of them be dead. The city had no chance. The Orcs climbed the stony cliffs around Byre Tor under cover of the night, and by morning the unnatural snows had come. We could fight against Orcs, even such Orcs as these, but there was more: a great shadow in the darkness!'\
\
Ymma shivers at the memory.\
\
'I will know forever the names of the Orcs that slaughtered my friends and my family as they ran, ${PLAYER}. One day when I am recovered I will hunt them down and show them what their attack on Byre Tor has cost them: their future days.'","This man is close to death and his sightless eyes cannot focus on you. You wonder what it is he is seeing, and hope he soon will find peace from it.","This may be the entrance to Nona's cave, but there is only one way to know for certain","Talk to the dying man","'I am Elfgifu, friend of Nona. I saw to the horses of Byre Tor, ${PLAYER}, and it was their panic that saved me. I was given warning enough of the Orc attack that I was partway down the hill when the giant... when the giant...'\
\
Elfgifu trails off, visibly upset by the memory.\
\
'All of us owe our lives to Nona. I never thought I would owe such a debt to a Dunlending! But there it is. Elda, Ymma, and I would be dead were it not for her ministrations. I do not know the name of the other man she saved; I do not recognize him. He may not be from Byre Tor. This may be heartless, but I fear he will die before I learn his name. That is a sad truth indeed!'","Travel to the city of Byre Tor, in the High Knolls of Wildermore","Nona has asked you to speak with the survivors from Byre Tor, but has nothing else to say for now.","Horn is ready to follow Nona to the cave she mentioned in the mountains, but the road leads first to the city of Byre Tor.","'You... you are a friend of Nona, then? She... is a remarkable girl. I did not know the Dunlendings had... the capacity for kindness.'\
\
He coughs weakly.\
\
'My name is Elda, and when the Orcs came to my city... I picked up sword and shield and thought... to fight. But a great piece of masonry crumbled... not two yards from where I stood, and...'\
\
Elda shudders with the memory.\
\
'I awoke in this cave. I think the Orcs thought... thought I was dead. I am fortunate... Nona found me... or I would be dead.'","'Byre Tor should be located north of here, along the road. We will see what has happened to the city before seeking out Nona in the cave she mentioned.'","Gléowine sings, 'From far across the plain her banners we espied.'","Nona's cave is in the north-western heights of the rocky crags in the High Knolls, in Wildermore.\
\
Gléowine has finished his song, and Horn is satisfied with the Orcs you have defeated in Byre Tor.","Gléowine sings, 'And she was a comfort in time of pain, time of want.'"},
[1913]={"'Te agradezco este servicio, ${PLAYER}, pues Ciudad de los Trasgos es un lugar vil y nada fácil de recorrer. Mi amigo se alegrará y sorprenderá de que hayas recuperado las gemas que creyó perdidas, y sin duda aprenderá mucho sobre joyería estudiándolas.'","'Los trasgos de Ciudad de los Trasgos, en las Montañas Nubladas, tendrán las gemas que busco. Tráeme un puñado y te daré las llaves que haya logrado reparar. Así, mi amigo podrá tener sus gemas de nuevo, pues yo no tengo tiempo para ir a recuperarlas por mi cuenta.'","Libro 11, Capítulo 10: Un Saquito de Gemas por una Caja de Llaves","Ciudad de los Trasgos se encuentra en el Paso Alto, en las Montañas Nubladas, al noreste de Rivendel.\
\
Merilos te ha pedido que viajes a Ciudad de los Trasgos y recuperes un puñado de preciadas gemas de los trasgos que allí viven, mientras ella trabaja en reparar las llaves que encontraste en Delossad.","Lleva las gemas a Merilos","La joyera Merilos está en la Aguja del Encuentro, en Rivendel.\
\
Has conseguido un puñado de gemas de Ciudad de los Trasgos, como Merilos te pidió, y ahora deberías llevárselas a cambio de la caja de llaves que dejaste para reparar.","Has traído a Merilos la caja de llaves rotas para repararla, y te ha dicho que puede rehacer aproximadamente la mitad. El resto no tiene arreglo.","'¿Dónde están las gemas que te pedí?'","'Me llevará algo de tiempo reparar las llaves y, si te parece bien, podrías ayudarme con un pequeño asunto.\
\
'Regalé varias gemas finas a un viajero que tenía interés en aprender los detalles del arte de la joyería, pero fue atacado por trasgos. Aunque escapó con vida, muchas de las gemas fueron robadas por esas criaturas. Viaja a Ciudad de los Trasgos, que se encuentra en el Paso Alto, y tráeme un puñado de esas preciadas gemas. Para cuando regreses, seguramente habré terminado de restaurar las llaves que me trajiste, y también podré devolver las gemas robadas a mi desafortunado amigo.\
\
'No encontrarás estas gemas en posesión de los trasgos de la superficie, pues quienes se hicieron con ellas probablemente las llevaron a Ciudad de los Trasgos para resguardarlas mejor.'"},
[1914]={"Talk to Théoden in Meduseld and watch his company ride to war","'So they are gone. May they ride to victory! It is now up to those of us who remain to carry out my uncle's will and the wishes of those who ride with him.\
\
'I hope we are both up to the challenge, ${PLAYER}.'","Book 11, Chapter 10: The King Rides West","'The riders are ready to depart, ${PLAYER}, as am I. We will ride to Isengard and remind Saruman of what he has forgotten: that the Riddermark is not his for taking. It belongs to the Eorlingas, who will refresh his memory with sword and spear!\
\
'I know that Éowyn is unhappy with her charge, and she would be on the forefront of the battle if I allowed her to ride with us. It would console her little to know that it is not her safety I seek to ensure with my command, but that of my people. They need someone to lead them in my absence, someone to give them hope for better days to come. They need Éowyn to be strong, and I know she will be. Another spear at Isengard will avail us little. A shield at home may be the difference, at the last.\
\
'I am ready to ride. Let me know when you are ready to see us off.'","Théoden King is inside the Golden Hall of Meduseld, in Edoras.\
\
Éowyn has asked you to see if the King has any further commands before he rides west to Isengard.","Talk to Éowyn outside Meduseld, in Edoras","Éowyn is outside the Golden Hall of Meduseld, in Edoras.\
\
The King and his company have left Edoras, and Éowyn is in charge of making ready the evacuation of the city.","'My uncle is ready to ride to war. Enter the Golden Hall and see if he has any further commands for those of us who must remain behind.'","Théoden is now ready to ride west to Isengard... to war.","'It is time.'","Théoden King is inside the Golden Hall of Meduseld, in Edoras.\
\
The King is waiting to speak with you before he rides west, to Isengard and war.","Talk to Théoden in Meduseld","'My preparations continue, but my uncle's are complete. Now he rides to Isengard and to war. I will remain behind, as he has commanded, but my thoughts will dwell upon him until his return!\
\
'Enter the Golden Hall and see if he has further commands for those of us who will remain.'"},
[1915]={"'¡Has vuelto! ¿Pudo Merilos reparar las llaves, tal como imaginé?'","'¿No me has traído las llaves?'","Lleva la caja de llaves reparadas a Candelleth","Merilos ha reparado tantas llaves como le fue posible, y ahora debes llevarlas a Candelleth.","'Candelleth sigue en su campamento élfico en Tâl Bruinen, ¿verdad? Llévale las llaves que he reparado y dile que, aunque no fue un servicio fácil, lo hice con gusto.'","Candelleth está en su campamento élfico en Tâl Bruinen.\
\
Merilos ha reparado tantas llaves como ha podido, y ahora debes llevárselas a Candelleth.","Libro 11, Capítulo 11: Las Llaves Reparadas","'He hecho cuanto he podido, pero cerca de la mitad de estas llaves estaban rotas sin remedio o les faltaban piezas.\
\
'Regresa con estas llaves reparadas a Candelleth y dale mis saludos. Ojalá hubiese podido arreglarlas todas, pero debes saber que he logrado más de lo que la mayoría podría. No fue una tarea sencilla.'"},
[1916]={"Libro 11, Capítulo 12: Prisionera de los Pueblos Libres","Habla con Candelleth","'¿Dónde está el diario de Sara Roblecorazón, ${PLAYER}?'","Muildir está al sureste de Echad Candelleth, frente a la entrada de Delossad.\
\
Merilos ha reparado las llaves que encontraste, y Candelleth te pidió mostrárselas a Muildir y adentrarte en los secretos de Delossad en busca de Narchuil.","'¿Has regresado con las llaves, y muchas de ellas han sido reparadas? ¡Los secretos de Delossad están ahora a nuestro alcance, ${PLAYER}, y Narchuil también!\
\
'¿Estás ${PLAYER:listo[m]|lista[f]} para buscar dentro de Delossad? Háblame cuando estés ${PLAYER:preparado[m]|preparada[f]} y pondremos en marcha nuestro plan.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta es una misión en solitario y no puede completarse con una Comunidad.</rgb>","'¡Debemos informar a Candelleth de lo ocurrido, ${PLAYER}! Ve a verla de inmediato a Echad Candelleth, al noroeste.'","Habla con Muildir y desvela los secretos de Delossad","Candelleth está en su campamento en Tâl Bruinen.\
\
Has aprendido mucho en las profundidades de Delossad, pero lo más preocupante es la noticia de que Mordrambor y las fuerzas de Amarthiel han recuperado a Narchuil, el anillo que se creía perdido.","'¡Excelente, ${PLAYER}! Ojalá una de estas llaves abra la puerta que conduce a las profundidades de las ruinas de Delossad, y podamos recuperar a Narchuil, oculta en algún lugar de su interior.\
\
'Regresa con Muildir, al sureste de Echad Candelleth, frente a la entrada de Delossad, y dile lo que debe hacerse.\
\
'¡Ahora tenemos ventaja sobre los Angmarim que buscan a ciegas, ${PLAYER}... ¡puedo sentirlo! Date prisa y que regreses con Narchuil!'","La joyera Merilos ha reparado muchas de las llaves que Sara Roblecorazón enterró frente a la entrada de Delossad, y ha llegado el momento de desvelar sus secretos.","'¿Qué ha sucedido, ${PLAYER}? ¿Por qué esa tristeza en tu semblante?'"},
[1917]={"Libro 11, Capítulo 13: El Fracaso de Laerdan","Elrond está en la biblioteca de Rivendel.\
\
Candelleth te ha pedido que lleves a Elrond las terribles noticias de que Angmar ha recuperado a Narchuil.","'Tu relato me llena de pesar, ${PLAYER}. La caída de Narmeleth es una historia triste, conocida solo por unos pocos, y aun así de forma incompleta. No sabía nada de su encierro a manos de Laerdan tras la Batalla de Fornost. Me apena que Laerdan creyera que yo no permitiría que Narmeleth siguiera con vida — quitar la vida a un prisionero no es la forma de los Eldar, y habría estado a salvo en mi casa, incluso siendo Amarthiel.\
\
'Creo que podemos intuir el destino desdichado de Sara Roblecorazón, última en la larga línea de guardianes de Narmeleth. No dudo de que trató con bondad a la hija de Laerdan, pero su recompensa fue la perdición... y algo más: Amarthiel aprendió artes oscuras de un maestro cruel, y parece que tomó el rostro de su carcelera para sí. ¡Un destino infeliz!\
\
'Pero estoy seguro de algo más, ${PLAYER}: Angmar aún no ha recuperado a Narchuil. Los caminos del Enemigo son los caminos del engaño — ¡no sucumbas a la desesperación! Si Narchuil ya hubiera sido hallada, Amarthiel habría llamado a sus servidores, y no lo ha hecho. Puede que haya aprendido algo nuevo sobre su paradero, pero sus siervos aún no la han encontrado, estoy seguro de ello. Debemos permanecer vigilantes como siempre, y continuar la búsqueda.'","En lo profundo de Delossad, Mordrambor te dio la terrible noticia de que Narchuil ha sido encontrada. Debes informar al señor Elrond.","'Habla con el señor Elrond en la biblioteca de Imladris y cuéntale lo que has visto. Entrégale también el diario de Sara Roblecorazón. Espero que él sepa qué hacer, ${PLAYER}, porque yo no.'","Lleva el diario podrido a Elrond","'¡Nada de cháchara!'","'¿Dices que las fuerzas de Amarthiel han recuperado Narchuil? Es una noticia terrible, ${PLAYER}, y echa por tierra todo lo que hemos intentado lograr aquí.\
\
'Debemos informar al señor Elrond. Búscalo en la biblioteca de Imladris y dale estas sombrías noticias, así como el diario de Sara Roblecorazón. Si alguien sabe qué hacer a continuación, será él.'"},
[1918]={"'I fear my wisdom cannot illumine your course, ${PLAYER}, beyond these words. Trust in the strength of your purpose and that of your friends. They wait for you in a cave in the High Knolls of Wildermore, do they not? The treachery of Saruman struck that land deeply, and your friends have done what they could for its people, but now the greatest danger lies in the western fields of Rohan.\
\
'Gather your friends from Nona's cave and do what you can for Rohan. That kingdom must not fall.'","'The treachery of Saruman struck Wildermore very deeply. You should recover your friends from the cave in the High Knolls and see what else you can do to counter the evil of Saruman.'","'I am sorry, but I have received no word from Edoras that your exile has been lifted. You must remain on the eastern bank of the Entwash until I have received such a word.'","Talk to Horn in Nona's Cave","Hunbald is at Entwade, the Entwash Crossing in the Sutcrofts.\
\
Horn has resolved to return to Edoras, against the commands of the King. You, Horn, and Gléowine should present yourselves to Hunbald with this decision.","Habla con Horn en la Cueva de Nona en las Altas Cumbres de las Tierras Feroces","Talk to Hunbald at the Entwade, in the Sutcrofts","'The two of us, and Gléowine, should return to the Entwash crossing in the Sutcrofts. There we will present ourselves to Hunbald and declare our intention to defy the word of the King.'","Gléowine listens to your account of Horn's decision to defy the word of the King, and smiles.\
\
'Horn can count me with him, ${PLAYER}. I will return to Edoras in defiance of Théoden King, whom I serve without question in all things save this, for I believe it is right. I am not afraid of death. If the King orders it, I will be the first to praise his justice, and will surrender to his headsman without complaint.\
\
'The King must hear of what has happened in Wildermore. I am certain he will listen when he hears what Horn has to say.'","'Nona and I will bring the survivors of Byre Tor to Forlaw, where they will be able to make a new life for themselves.'","'We must cross the Entwash. Someone must tell the King what befell in Wildermore. The threat of Saruman is greater even than we supposed.'","Danger threatens the kingdom of Rohan on all sides, and if nothing is done the land will be overrun by the forces of Saruman. Has the time come to defy the word of the King in order to save his people?","Talk to Corudan in Nona's Cave","'I believe this is the right course. Horn would not forgive himself if he did not do all in his power to help his people. I would not forgive him either. The man I love fights for the people who cannot fight for themselves. I, too, do this. I will see both you and my beloved again after we have seen to our separate charges. Do not doubt it!'","'I have seen fires burning in the fields of Rohan. Your friends are needed there, as are you. Return now to the cave in the High Knolls of Wildermore where last you saw them, and discover your next course.'","'I have received no word that you may yet pass. Find your friends and find another course to take.'","Book 11, Chapter 1: Too Great a Need","'I have seen fires, ${PLAYER}, fires burning in the fields of Rohan. Your friends are needed there, as are you. Return now to the cave in Wildermore where last you saw them. There are decisions you must make, and make well. Much depends upon the course you take.'","'Horn plans to defy the word of his King? That cannot have been an easy decision for him to make, but I understand what has driven our friend to make it. Horn may be imprisoned, or worse, but if his tidings can break the King's reverie it might be the only action that can save the people of Rohan from their enemies.\
\
'The survivors of Byre Tor are now well enough to travel. Nona and I will bring them to the city of Forlaw while Horn brings his message to the King, and we will rejoin him when we can. I think it would be... unwise... to enter the court of Théoden in the company of a Dunlending girl, even one proven so true as Nona. And it is not she alone who would raise the hackles of the Rohirrim. An Elf of Lórien would be as unwelcome. Am I mistaken?'","Talk to Gléowine in Nona's Cave","'Here we are, my friends. Now what do we do?'","Your companions are in Nona's Cave in the High Knolls of Wildermore.\
\
Horn wishes to speak with you about the road ahead.","'Our friends from Byre Tor have weathered the storm, ${PLAYER}. The worst is behind them, and with my help they will be well enough to travel. I have spoken with Horn about this, and he agrees that it is best if I bring them to a town in Wildermore where they can start anew. What is the name of the settlement on the eastern shore of the lake? Forlaw? That city will find a place for them, if any will. Sad news, this, but it be true: Núrzum's path of destruction has caused many houses throughout Wildermore to stand empty. My recovering friends will find a fresh start in Forlaw.\
\
'Horn and I spoke of other matters as well, ${PLAYER}. Speak to him and see if you share his mind.'","'Nothing has changed. I have not received word from Edoras that you may pass.'\
\
Hunbald's scowl deepens when you declare your intention to pass anyway.\
\
'Still you defy my charge and that of my King! This cannot be. I cannot allow you across the Entwash. It is a command of Théoden King, and I will not betray my duty! The two of you have seen battle, I am certain of it, but this white-haired fellow has seen none that I can tell! Would you have me raise my sword against an old man?'","'I will defy the word of my King, though it come at the cost of my honour. He must be told the great evil Saruman wrought in Wildermore, and what evils the Wizard intends for the rest of Rohan.'","'I know now what the rest of us will do, but one path remains a mystery to me. On what path will you walk, ${PLAYER}? Will you come with me to Edoras? I do not ask you to defy Théoden King, my friend. I will understand if our paths must now separate. I would not blame you! That is, most like, the way of wisdom. It is with my heart I make this choice for myself, but I would not presume to make it for you, by head or by heart.'\
\
His voice is casual, but you can tell from his eyes that worry lurks just beneath the surface. With a comforting smile, you tell him that you will accompany him to Edoras, for the good of Rohan's people, though it be against the command of their King. Horn's relief is tangible and sudden.\
\
'${PLAYER}, you are as great a fool as I am! I am overjoyed to say it! Three Men and an Elf, all returning to Edoras against the command of the King, and in the company of a Dunlending girl, would be too great an insult. We defy the King, but still seek to be polite. Is this madness, ${PLAYER}?\
\
'The two of us, and Gléowine, should now travel to Hunbald at the Entwade crossing, and tell him we will not be turned away.'","'The King must be told what has transpired in Wildermore. It shows how dangerous Saruman has become! Tell Horn I will journey with him back to Edoras, though it be against the King's command!'","'Thank you for coming to listen, my friend. I have put some thought into what we encountered in Wildermore, and I must confess it troubles me. The folk here are on the road to recovery, as are the survivors Nona rescued from Byre Tor, but the forces of Saruman attacked this land with much greater strength than I expected they could muster. How much might could Saruman raise to strike at the heart of Rohan if he spared a creature such as Núrzum to deal with Wildermore? Imagine what evils he might unleash upon Edoras!\
\
'I have decided what I must do, ${PLAYER}. My King commanded me not to cross the Entwash, and I am honour-bound to obey him. And yet I cannot remain silent. I must convince Théoden King to march against Saruman before the Wizard's plans bear fruit. If it costs me my honour as a man of Rohan, so be it. I will defy the word of my King if doing so will save even one innocent. I will accept whatever justice the King deems appropriate, but he must be told of what we witnessed in Wildermore. He must be warned, even if it means my life.\
\
'I have told Nona my decision, and she sees the need of it. She will go to Forlaw with the survivors of Byre Tor, and we will meet again once this is through. Speak now to Corudan and Gléowine and see what they think of my plan.'","Horn is in Nona's Cave in the High Knolls, in Wildermore.\
\
You have spoken with Gléowine and Corudan, and now Horn is waiting to see if you will accompany him to Edoras.","Corudan is in Nona's Cave in the High Knolls, in Wildermore.\
\
Horn has asked you to speak with Corudan and Gléowine about the course he has suggested."},
[1919]={"'Gracias por la noticia, ${PLAYER}, aunque es preocupante. Dudo que Amarthiel decida enviar a sus guerreros hacia el Bosque de los Trolls por la ruta que vigilo, pero enviaré un cuervo a Calenglad de inmediato si ocurre.\
\
Pero debo discrepar con sus deseos en un asunto: si Amarthiel decide enviar a sus Angmarim hacia el sur por este camino, no me quedaré de brazos cruzados. Aunque caiga en combate contra el Enemigo, evitaré que al menos algunos Angmarim entren en la Comarca. ¡No intentes disuadirme! No cambiaré de opinión.\
\
Pero enviaré mi cuervo primero, por supuesto.'","'No podemos lamentar ahora a Laerdan, . Amarthiel no dudará en hacer uso del conocimiento que acaba de obtener. ¡Si tan solo hubiéramos logrado apoderarnos del palantír a tiempo, su búsqueda de Narchuil habría sido en vano! Pero no sirve de nada detenernos en el pasado. Consuélate con esto, : sabemos lo que Amarthiel vio en las profundidades de la Piedra Vidente, pues habló de ello cuando tú y Laerdan entrasteis en Barad Tironn. ¿Acaso no habló de las tierras salvajes de los Bosques de los Trolls? Nos ha revelado su próximo movimiento, y si actuamos con rapidez, aún podríamos encontrar Narchuil antes que ella.\
\
No contamos con suficientes refuerzos para impedir que sus siervos salgan de Evendim, pero al menos podemos ser alertados de sus movimientos. Dos de mis hermanos vigilan los caminos que salen de Evendim y deben ser advertidos de lo que podría suceder: que Amarthiel planea enviar a sus siervos por varias rutas fuera de Evendim. Busca a Torogethir en la Puerta de Evendim, al nordeste de aquí, en el paso hacia los Campos de Fornost, y a Galthoniel en una pequeña elevación con vista al Barandalf, muy al sur de aquí y al este del poblado hobbit de Dwaling. Diles lo que sospechamos de los planes de Amarthiel, y que envíen cuervos a Tinnudir al primer signo de movimiento de los Angmarim.\
\
¡No deben enfrentarse a tales patrullas en batalla abierta! Ve con prisa, . Cuando nuestra fuerza en armas no es suficiente, la información debe ser nuestra mayor aliada.'","'No he visto señal alguna de Angmarim saliendo de Evendim. Cuando lo haga, enviaré un cuervo a Tinnudir de inmediato.'","Libro 11, Capítulo 1: Vigilando los Caminos","'Te doy las gracias, ${PLAYER}. Ojalá pudiéramos impedir que los Angmarim salgan de Evendim en busca de Narchuil, pero sé bien que no contamos con la fuerza necesaria para lograrlo. Al menos sabremos cuándo salgan las patrullas.\
\
Debería haber esperado que Galthoniel rechazara mi petición de no enfrentarse al Enemigo, pero no deseo que entregue su vida en vano. Mi corazón me dice que, si Amarthiel elige el camino largo hacia los Bosques de los Trolls y cruza el Barandalf, el sacrificio de Galthoniel no logrará retrasar lo inevitable.\
\
Ahora que sabemos que seremos advertidos cuando los Angmarim comiencen su búsqueda, debemos iniciar la nuestra, ${PLAYER}. Si hemos de encontrar Narchuil, debemos aprender todo lo que podamos sobre él. Ha llegado la hora de confrontar a Mordrambor.'","'No cambiaré de parecer en este asunto, ${PLAYER}, y Calenglad fue imprudente al pedírmelo. Enviaré un cuervo a Tinnudir al primer signo de Angmarim, pero no permitiré que pasen libremente hacia el sur.'","Torogethir está en un pequeño campamento justo al oeste de la Puerta de Evendim hacia los Campos de Fornost, al nordeste de Tinnudir. Galthoniel tiene un campamento en una elevación con vista al Barandalf, al sudeste de Tinnudir y al este del poblado hobbit de Dwaling.\
\
Calenglad te ha pedido llevar noticias de posibles movimientos de los Angmarim fuera de Evendim a Torogethir y Galthoniel, los Montaraces encargados de vigilar los caminos.","'Tendré muy en cuenta tus noticias, ${PLAYER}, y enviaré un cuervo a Calenglad al primer signo de Angmarim saliendo de Evendim. Pero hasta ahora no he visto nada. Ha estado inusualmente tranquilo.'","'Puede que no tengamos suficientes fuerzas para impedir que los Angmarim salgan de Evendim camino a los Bosques de los Trolls en busca de Narchuil, pero quiero saber en qué momento lo hagan. Torogethir y Galthoniel, los Montaraces encargados de vigilar los caminos de salida de Evendim, deben ser advertidos.\
\
Torogethir está al nordeste de aquí, justo al oeste de la Puerta de Evendim hacia los Campos de Fornost. Galthoniel tiene un pequeño campamento en una elevación con vista al Barandalf, al sudeste de Tinnudir. Búscala al este del poblado hobbit de Dwaling.\
\
Diles que no enfrenten al enemigo, sino que envíen cuervos a Tinnudir al primer indicio de Angmarim saliendo de Evendim.'","Laerdan se ha perdido en los otrora orgullosos salones de Barad Tironn, y ahora los Dúnedain deben impedir que Amarthiel actúe según el conocimiento que obtuvo mediante el uso del palantír.","Calenglad está en el campamento de los Montaraces en la isla de Tinnudir, en Evendim.\
\
Has comunicado a Torogethir y Galthoniel lo que Calenglad ha deducido sobre los planes de Amarthiel, y permanecerán vigilantes ante cualquier señal de Angmarim saliendo de Evendim."},
[1920]={"'Wait, there is something familiar about that man... is it Gléowine? Gléowine, is that you? The minstrel of Théoden! On what account do you accompany these folk?'\
\
Gléowine sheepishly steps forward, and you realize that Hunbald was never told of the minstrel's exile.\
\
'It is you!' Hunbald continues. 'Is it true what this ${RACE} says?'\
\
Gléowine responds quickly, and Hunbald muses in silence. After a time, he continues.\
\
'Gléowine, if you will speak for these others, I will allow the three of you to pass. I am merely a simple man from the Eastfold, but you are held in confidence of the King, and must know his mind more thoroughly than ever I could hope to do. For the good of my King, and the Riddermark, I will allow you to pass. Do not make me regret this choice! I would cast my blade aside before I raise it against such as you.'","Make your way into Edoras and meet up with Gléowine","'Look at this! Unless I am very much mistaken, that horse is Shadowfax, lord of the Mearas! The King gifted him to Gandalf the Wizard some months ago, rather against his wishes, truth be known. It seems the horse has found his way back home, riderless! The King will be pleased, if he does not already know mighty Shadowfax has returned! That will brighten his countenance, for certain! He may be more willing to forgive our defiance of his commands, as well.\
\
'Let us continue onward to the Golden Hall, ${PLAYER}. I am ready.'","Talk to Gléowine in Edoras, along the road","Hunbald has put his honour on the line, trusting that you and your companions mean no harm to Théoden or to the people of Rohan, and now you should ride for Edoras to bring warning to the King.","The time has come to climb the streets of Edoras to the entrance to the Golden Hall of Meduseld, there to await the judgement of Théoden.","'We have returned to Edoras, ${PLAYER}, and death is upon my mind. Will Théoden King heed the warning we bring, or will he answer our words of caution with admonishment and a more final decree than exile?'\
\
Horn looks to the mounds on the left and right side of the road.\
\
'How long has it been since Meduseld was raised, and how many Kings of Rohan sleep here in death? Ten and six mounds for ten and six kings. Will the Evermind blossoms cover another mound before this war is through, or will no good Men remain to build it? Let us continue into the city. Our errand is urgent, and we have little time for my dark musings!'","Book 11, Chapter 2: Edoras","'That was a fortunate turn, was it not?'","Climb the streets of Edoras to reach the entrance to Meduseld","'We will find Gléowine further up the road, within Edoras. Let us join him before we proceed to the Golden Hall and the judgement of Théoden.'","Háma stands before you, and he bars the way to the Golden Hall of Meduseld.","Talk to Horn by the barrows outside the entrance to Edoras","The barrows outside the entrance to Edoras will be a good place to meet up with your companions.\
\
Hunbald has allowed you to cross the Entwash, and now you should ride to the entrance of Edoras.","Gléowine stops ahead and stares at a magnificent white horse","Before the gates of Edoras, burial mounds of Kings stand beside the road","Gléowine is on the road within the entrance to Edoras, by a majestic white horse.","Horn is by the barrows outside the entrance to Edoras.\
\
You have arrived at Edoras, and should speak now to Horn by the barrows.","Ride to the barrows outside the entrance to Edoras","'We should make our way into the city, ${PLAYER}. Keep watch for anything unusual.'","'We have come to Edoras, ${PLAYER}, for good or ill.'","'This is not the first time you have come before the Golden Hall of Meduseld. It is in my mind that you were sent from here in disgrace, by command of the King. What brings you hither against the word of Théoden? How many unwanted visitors will bring ill news here today?'\
\
Háma notices your puzzled expression and continues, 'You are not the only unwelcome guests to come to Meduseld this day. Some are within the Golden Hall this very hour!'","Outside the Golden Hall of Meduseld, the doorward of Théoden bars your way","Talk to Háma outside the Golden Hall of Meduseld","'If Gléowine will speak for you, I will allow you to pass. Ride to Edoras, and do not stray from your course. Do not make me regret this decision!'","'Will you look at that, my friend? The glory of the father of horses is returned in Shadowfax, unless my old eyes betray me with hopeful sights!'","You have come to Edoras and should now make your way up through the city."},
[1921]={"Calenglad ha decidido que, antes de que comiences tu búsqueda de Narchuil, debes aprender cuanto puedas sobre el anillo a través de Mordrambor.","Habla con Calenglad y enfrenta a Mordrambor sobre Narchuil","'Mordrambor ha demostrado ser un prisionero peligroso y poco fiable hasta ahora, ${PLAYER}, pero ahora deberá pagar por su traición. Nos revelará lo que sabe del anillo perdido de Amarthiel, Narchuil, o no volverá a ver la luz del día. No puede conocer su ubicación, o su señora no habría necesitado el palantír, pero cualquier información que pueda darnos sobre su poder o su historia podría ser de utilidad.\
\
Iré contigo a hablar con el Númenóreano Negro. Ha demostrado ser capaz de hechizar las mentes de otros, y será mejor que lo enfrentemos juntos para protegernos de sus engaños.\
\
También tengo algunas palabras para nuestro prisionero sobre el destino de Laerdan. Mordrambor lamentará el día en que envió al Elfo a su muerte. Háblame cuando estés listo para partir.'","Calenglad se encuentra en el campamento de los Montaraces en la isla de Tinnudir, en Evendim.\
\
Calenglad ha decidido que, si lo enfrentáis juntos, tal vez podáis aprender del poder o la historia de Narchuil al interrogar a Mordrambor, y esta información podría ayudaros a recuperarlo antes que Amarthiel.","Libro 11, Capítulo 2: Mordrambor","'No existen palabras, ${PLAYER}, para describir el mal que Mordrambor ha causado hoy. Pensé que ya habíamos visto el final del dolor que podía provocar, pero la traición que llevó a Laerdan voluntariamente a su perdición es poca cosa comparada con la pena que siento por la pérdida de los míos.\
\
Colhamnir... Carchammadel... Tadan...\
\
Demasiadas vidas perdidas, ¡y en el mismísimo corazón del lugar que creíamos más seguro! ¿Cómo pudo Angmar golpearnos incluso aquí? No podemos buscar Narchuil ahora, ${PLAYER}. Mordrambor ha infligido un golpe casi mortal a mi gente, y debemos descansar. Mi pueblo necesita tiempo para llorar; ¡no pueden luchar eternamente frente a pérdidas tan graves! Lo siento.'","'¿Estás ${PLAYERNAME:preparado[m]|preparada[f]}, ? Mordrambor ha demostrado ser un huésped nefasto, pero podría saber algo sobre Narchuil que nos resulte útil. Aún no ha visto la ira de los Dúnedain, y deseo hablarle del destino de Laerdan. Nos dirá lo que sabe, pero debes prepararte y proteger tu mente contra su hechicería.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta es una misión en solitario y no puede completarse con una Comunidad.</rgb>","Calenglad se encuentra en el campamento de los Montaraces en la isla de Tinnudir, en Evendim.\
\
Mordrambor ha escapado del torreón de Tinnudir. Muchos Montaraces murieron durante su huida, y ahora Calenglad intenta mantener unidos a los Dúnedain pese a estas pérdidas."},
[1922]={"Calenglad se encuentra en el campamento de los Montaraces en la isla de Tinnudir, en Evendim.\
\
Has reunido piedras de Annúminas para usarlas en la construcción de túmulos para los Montaraces muertos durante la fuga de Mordrambor y deberías regresar ahora con Calenglad.","'Estas servirán perfectamente, ${PLAYER}, y te agradezco el gesto.\
\
Aún no hay noticias de Torogethir ni de Galthoniel. Parece que Amarthiel también ha sido retrasada en el inicio de su búsqueda, o quizá se ocupa de celebrar la fuga de Mordrambor y la muerte de los míos. Tendremos nuestra venganza contra ambos, pero ¡el momento de su llegada tarda demasiado!'","Lleva las piedras de Annúminas a Calenglad","'Mi pueblo necesita tiempo para llorar a los suyos, ${PLAYER}, o no podrán continuar la lucha. El arma más terrible que Angmar blande en esta guerra es la desesperanza, un temor abrumador que se apodera del corazón de la gente de bien y les roba la voluntad de oponerse al mal. Este golpe ha caído aquí, en Tinnudir, con terrible eficacia.\
\
He enviado a mis hermanos a recoger piedras de Annúminas con las que podamos construir túmulos para nuestros caídos. Si viajas a la gran ciudad y ayudas con la recolección de estas piedras de la ciudad, sé que Tadan, Colhamnir y Carchammadel habrían considerado un honor tu servicio en su memoria.'","'Aún no has reunido suficientes piedras, ${PLAYER}.'","Se pueden encontrar piedras de los edificios de Annúminas por toda la gran ciudad, y serían ideales para construir túmulos en memoria de los Montaraces caídos.\
\
Calenglad te ha pedido reunir piedras por las calles de la Ciudad de los Reyes para construir túmulos en honor de Tadan, Colhamnir y Carchammadel.","Libro 11, Capítulo 3: Túmulos para los Caídos","'Las piedras de Annúminas, al suroeste y en las orillas del Lago Nenuial, serán usadas para construir túmulos en memoria de nuestros caídos. Habría sido un honor para ellos descansar bajo las piedras de la Ciudad de los Reyes.'","Piedras de Annúminas recogidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL}","Recoge piedras de Annúminas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Calenglad teme por la determinación de los Dúnedain y los ha enviado a reunir piedras con las que construir túmulos para sus hermanos caídos."},
[1923]={"'The error was my own, if error it was. For my part, I think my heart spoke true!'","Book 11, Chapter 3: Théoden, Son of Thengel","Talk to Gandalf within Meduseld","'You are not the first to come here today, testing the word of my heart 'gainst the command of my king. Do I compound an earlier error by allowing you into the hall, or do I make all right with a single throw?'\
\
Háma sighs heavily. 'Never have I so rued this post! The will of Théoden is clear, but I do not believe you come here with evil intent. You speak of dangers to the north, and all around, but returning here brings the greatest danger upon yourselves! Is that not the truest sign of your good hearts?\
\
'The King must be told what you have seen. Speak to me when you are ready to continue into the hall, and I shall take your weapons as is the custom. Then you shall proceed before the King, and we will see if I have misjudged you. I hope for your sake, and for mine, that I have not.'","'If you are willing, I will take your weapons and bring you before the King. Know this: once you step beneath the roof of Meduseld, all chances to repent of your defiance are gone.'","Háma has grudgingly decided to allow you in to see the King, and will bring you inside the Golden Hall if you speak to him once more.","You have reunited with Gandalf within the Golden Hall of Meduseld, and should now speak to the Wizard.","'It seems your road entwines with ours for a pace or two more, ${PLAYER}. Ah, I would not celebrate so quickly were I you! War has already come to Rohan, and its drum-beat deepens with every passing hour. We are beset on all sides by evils both known and unknowable, and to be near Gandalf is to be near danger!'\
\
Gandalf laughs, but his eyes are stern.\
\
'Gríma would say I brought the danger hither, I do not doubt. But I say Gandalf goes where he is needed, and for this day and every day that is to where the danger is deepest!'","It is a day for unwelcome visitors to the Golden Hall, according to Háma, the doorward of Théoden.","Talk to Háma and he will bring you before the King"},
[1924]={"'Ha llegado el momento, ${PLAYER}. No muy lejos de aquí hay un lugar del que Carchammadel era especialmente aficionada en vida: Barad Rath, un mirador coronado por ruinas, muy por encima del Lago Nenuial. Que los saqueadores de tumbas lo utilizaran con frecuencia era un motivo de pena para ella. Hemos decidido erigir los túmulos de nuestros deudos en su cima.\
\
'¿Te unirás a nosotros para recordar a quienes hemos perdido y añadir una piedra a sus túmulos? Háblame cuando estés ${PLAYER:listo[m]|lista[f]}, y partiremos.'","'Viajaremos ahora a Barad Rath para recordar a los caídos, si estás ${PLAYERNAME:preparado[m]|preparada[f]}.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta es una misión en solitario y no puede completarse con una Comunidad.</rgb>","Habla con Calenglad y viaja con él a Barad Rath","Libro 11, Capítulo 4: Recuerdo","Los Dúnedain de Tinnudir se han reunido para construir túmulos sobre los cuerpos de sus hermanos caídos, y Calenglad te ha pedido que participes también.","'Te agradezco nuevamente, ${PLAYER}. No conociste a Tadan durante mucho tiempo, pero era un buen hombre, y sé que apreciaba tus visitas, pese al peligro constante de la misión en la que lo encontraste. No le culpo por lo sucedido, y te ruego que tú tampoco lo hagas... Mordrambor ha atrapado en sus engaños a gentes mucho más grandes que tú o yo.\
\
'Siento que mi pueblo podrá luchar otra vez, y con una determinación renovada. No olvidaremos lo que Mordrambor y Amarthiel han hecho, ¡pero tampoco nos hundiremos en nuestra pena! Nuestra venganza, cuando llegue, será diez veces más fuerte por nuestras pérdidas, y se arrepentirán de sus actos.'","Calenglad está en el campamento de Montaraces de la isla de Tinnudir, en Evendim.\
\
Has sido ${PLAYERNAME:invitado[m]|invitada[f]} a unirte a los Dúnedain en el homenaje a sus hermanos asesinados por Mordrambor durante su huida.","Calenglad está en el campamento de Montaraces de la isla de Tinnudir, en Evendim.\
\
El homenaje a los Dúnedain caídos fue interrumpido por la llegada de un cuervo enviado por Torogethir: las tropas de Amarthiel han iniciado la búsqueda de Narchuil.","Habla con Calenglad","'¿Sí, ${PLAYER}? ¿Qué ocurre?'"},
[1925]={"Talk to Gimli in Meduseld","'I feel as if a heavy shroud has been lifted from my sight. My days were filled with dark dreams, and my nights were no different. What foul craft of Gríma's is to blame? No, not his doing alone. It was my weakness that allowed him so to dominate my mind. No longer! I am myself again, and free of his whisperings. It is well that Gandalf arrived here when he did, and that Háma allowed him to pass the threshold. That transgression I will forgive.\
\
'Gríma may have intended further mischief. Indeed, I am certain of it. Leave Meduseld and speak to Háma. Tell him I want Gríma's chambers searched, and my sister-son Éomer released from imprisonment. These actions were poorly-done, and must be righted.'","Théoden is more willing to listen to you, now that Gandalf has spoken words of truth to the King of Rohan.","'No more running, I hope! Though I do not care for the beasts, I would rather be carried by a willing horse than run across the fields of Rohan once again!'","Legolas smiles at you, but he is deep in thought and has nothing to say.","'Yes? You return from within on your own power, which tells me your wager was correct and you will draw breath until tomorrow, at least.'\
\
Háma listens as you recount what befell within the Golden Hall, and his questioning face is soon aglow with smiles.\
\
'These are better tidings than I believed possible! You are a friend both new and true to bring me such words! Théoden, my King, you have been brought from the darkness by the wisdom of Gandalf! He is the Storm-crow no longer! White Wizard, friend to Rohan and its people! I rejoice to hear it! Théoden King, restored at last!'","'We meet again, my friend! I am glad of it, for it seems there is a shortage of friendly faces in this land. One man of honour I met, and he was imprisoned for his kindness to me!'\
\
You press Aragorn on the matter of Gandalf's cryptic words, and the Ranger's face falls.\
\
'Gandalf gives you the joyful tidings, and leaves the ill news to me. It has been one week since our fellowship was sundered on Parth Galen, along the banks of the Anduin. Boromir of Gondor fell there. He gave his life protecting the halflings Meriadoc and Peregrin, but they were borne away by great Orcs of Saruman. Others went... another way. I had to make a choice, and I chose it. We could not abandon Merry and Pippin.\
\
'I do not know if I chose aright. The Orcs were destroyed before our pursuit ended, and Gandalf tells me the hobbits found safety. Should I have done otherwise? I cannot say. But now we must do what we can for Rohan, and put behind us what regrets we may.'","'It is good to see you again, ${PLAYER}, though we are met on the very precipice of danger. How have you fared since last we spoke?'\
\
You tell Legolas of your adventures, and his light laughter breezily flies around the hall.\
\
'What is it that our young friends used to say? You have gone from the frying-pan into the flames, and the frying-pan was hot enough! You have had adventures to spare, ${PLAYER}; it seems we all have done. I am glad your own journey brought you to Fangorn, as did mine. I could spend years exploring beneath its canopy, never feeling the passage of time, were it not for the pull of that which moves my feet. Once our friends are safe, perhaps I will follow that pull to where it leads.'\
\
Legolas notices your quizzical expression, and his usual laughter melts away. 'The sea, ${PLAYER},' he responds, 'I speak of the sea.'","'Théoden King has been restored, and now Rohan has a chance to fight against the evils of Saruman! My heart is filled with hope, ${PLAYER}, and I am eager to see the Wizard pay for his crimes!'","'Our errand is not ended. We must do what we can, while others pursue the true course of its completion.'","'Speak to our friends and they will give you tidings both glad and sorrowful.'","'Much has transpired since last we met, but my companions can give you their account. My own would take too long to tell, and from any other would beggar belief. You would trust my tale, I am certain, but then only because you have experienced some things nearly as peculiar! Know this, ${PLAYER}: I bear tidings both glad and sorrowful. The task set before our mutual friends at the Last Homely House is still ongoing. Though some of that company are here with us in this golden hall, some others carry still the Burden to its destination. The errand is not yet done, but neither is it abandoned. Those be the glad tidings.\
\
'I will let Aragorn tell you what this joyful news has cost us, for it was not bought without strife.'","'Gríma may have intended further mischief. Indeed, I am certain of it. Leave Meduseld and speak to Háma. Tell him I want Gríma's chambers searched, and my sister-son Éomer released from imprisonment. These actions were poorly-done, and must be righted.'","'I just want what is best for the king! All of you, and especially the Wizard, want to see him weak and powerless! Only Gríma loves him and can care for him!'","Talk to Théoden in Meduseld","'The sight of Théoden King standing proudly and tall again makes me feel younger than I have done in years, ${PLAYER}.'","Aragorn, Legolas, and Gimli wait to speak with you within the Golden Hall of Meduseld.","'Théoden King has been restored! It brings joy to this old heart of mine!'","'I only want what is best for the king!'","Talk to Háma outside Meduseld","'Only Gríma cares for Théoden King! These others want him hurt, and powerless, and weak!'","After being apart for so long, you have reunited once again with Gandalf, Aragorn, Legolas, and Gimli, and eagerly press them for news about what befell them since last you saw them.","'It has been several weeks since last we met, ${PLAYER}! What have you done with the time? I have cloven a number of Orc skulls since then, but not enough to satisfy my hatred of the beasts. Some of their ilk led us on a merry chase across much of Rohan, and my chest fills with pride to tell you I outpaced even Legolas on that race! I may have been winded, true, but Gimli, Glóin's son, did not abandon the pursuit without need. When we caught up with the Uruk band at last, they had already been slain by Men of Rohan.\
\
'It has been two days since our pursuit ended, and I have nearly caught my breath again. I have never run so far or so fast in all my days, and I would be content to stay in one place for the rest of them, if that place were a mountain with good stone and deep roots!'","Talk to Aragorn in Meduseld","'Fortune was with us on this throw, ${PLAYER}! I am pleased for our sake, but more than that I am pleased for Rohan! Now, at last, Théoden has been restored and there is hope again for his kingdom!'","Book 11, Chapter 4: Tidings Glad and Sorrowful","Théoden has asked you to bring his commands to Háma, outside the Golden Hall.","Talk to Legolas in Meduseld"},
[1926]={"You found a number of stolen items in Gríma Wormtongue's chambers, and should now present them to the King.","Háma has guided you to the chambers where Gríma Wormtongue kept his bed in Edoras, so you may carry out the King's desire that the room be searched for further tendrils of Wormtongue's treachery.","Háma should be told what you discovered in Wormtongue's chambers.","How many secrets remain to be discovered within Wormtongue's chambers?","These drawers contain linens and fine clothes, rumpled now and in disarray.","Find the entrance to Gríma Wormtongue's chambers in Edoras","Beneath the chair you find a golden key","Carved into the table is the crude representation of a crying eye","Gríma Wormtongue's former chambers can be found north-east of the bottom of the Meduseld steps, in Edoras.","'Stay alert, and I will show you the way to Gríma's chambers. Then we will search them for further seeds of treachery, as Théoden King commands.'","Unlock the chest in Gríma's chambers","Gríma's chambers can be found north-east of the bottom of the Meduseld steps, in Edoras.\
\
How many secrets remain to be discovered within Wormtongue's chambers?","'Nothing?'","You found a number of stolen items in Gríma Wormtongue's chambers, and should confront him with them.","Inside the chest you find items too varied to belong to Gríma, including a valuable sword","Book 11, Chapter 5: Chamber of the Worm","'You found the key? Well done, ${PLAYER}! See if it fits the lock!'","This chest is tightly locked, and you possess no key for it.","This cabinet stands empty. Did someone get here before you?","You have found the entrance to Wormtongue's chambers. Do further treacheries await within?","A crude map lies on this table, but you cannot discern what it represents.","'What are these things? Why do you show them to me, vile ${RACE}?'\
\
You explain that the goods were taken from the chest in his chambers, and demand an explanation.\
\
'Every one of those items was a gift!' Gríma hisses. 'You are the thief! I demand that you return those things to my chambers, and when you return to my presence you come bearing an apology! I have suffered at the hands of these ingrates, and now my own possessions are being paraded before all the court, and my name dragged through the slime! These are the thanks I receive for my months of tireless service to the King?\
\
'You are a liar, ${RACE}, and a thief! Your voice drips with poison and your words are all false! I curse thee, and beg that some kind heart will defend me from your insults and your slander!'","'What did you find there? That is Herugrim, the sword of Théoden! It is possible that the King asked Gríma to keep the sword safe in his chest, but such safe-keeping is no longer necessary. I will return Herugrim to its master, once I have brought Éomer word of his release.\
\
'For now, bring these other items to Gríma in Meduseld and see what he has to say about them. These items are both too varied and too valuable to be his property, I'll warrant, and his explanation for possessing them should be interesting.'","Present to Háma the stolen items you recovered in Gríma's chambers","Search Gríma's chambers for further sign of his treachery","'You found nothing?'","Show the stolen items you recovered to Gríma in Meduseld","These books detail the geography and history of Rohan, but contain nothing of note right now.","'Ha! You have nothing!'","'I will bring Herugrim to the King after I have released Éomer from his confinement. Meanwhile, you should present those stolen items to Gríma in Meduseld and hear his explanation for how they came to be within his chest.'","A marked page in one of these books reads 'No Mere Wit, He.'","Show the stolen items to Théoden, in Meduseld","'I will guide you to Gríma's chambers, as the King instructs. We must remain alert, ${PLAYER}, for Gríma may have left the seeds of some mischief in his chambers. He may still manage to work some evil, and that would be a cruel cut indeed, to know of his treachery and still succumb to it.\
\
'Gríma's chambers are north-east of the steps that lead to Meduseld. Come, I will show you the way.'","'Where did you get these items? You say they were found within Gríma's chest? I see.'\
\
Théoden casts a dark look in the direction of his former servant.\
\
'I will have one of my men restore these items to their proper owners. I am of a mind to send this worm back to his proper owner, as well. Would it be a mercy, I wonder? On this day, and in sight of his continued crimes, I am more interested in justice than in mercy.'","'It would seem we are not the first to search Gríma's chambers this day, ${PLAYER}.'","'Lies! All lies! Your words are false!'"},
[1927]={"Encuentra la Cima de los Vientos","Al mirar hacia el este desde la Cima de los Vientos, viste una compañía de Angmarim cruzando el Último Puente hacia el Bosque de los Trolls.\
\
Has seguido a una compañía de Angmarim hacia el este, pero llegaron al Último Puente antes que tú. Debes viajar hasta el Último Puente y hablar con el explorador apostado allí para conocer noticias sobre los Angmarim.","'Los Angmarim pasaron por la Puerta de Evendim, ${PLAYER}, y envié mi cuervo a Tinnudir después de que cruzaran.\
\
'Lamento haberme perdido la construcción del túmulo de Colhamnir; luchamos juntos en el Sur durante nuestra juventud, y su muerte me pesa. Visitaré su túmulo cuando ya no sea necesario que esté de guardia.\
\
'Si planeas <rgb=#FF0000>mirar</rgb> hacia el este desde la cima de Amon Raith, deberás pasar por la Puerta de Evendim y viajar al sureste por los Campos de Fornost. Amon Raith es una colina alta al noreste de Puente de Caballetes y debería darte una vista dominante de las Quebradas.'","'Debemos encontrar Narchuil antes que los Angmarim, ${PLAYER}. Sabemos que seguramente viajan al Bosque de los Trolls, pero temo que puedan desviarse para atacar aldeas en su camino.\
\
'Sube a la cima de Amon Sûl, la colina más alta de las Tierras Solitarias, y <rgb=#FF0000>Mira</rgb> hacia el este desde su cumbre. ¡Si ves a los Angmarim en la distancia, síguelos de inmediato!'","Encuentra la cima de Amon Raith","'¿Estás aquí para rastrear el avance de los Angmarim? Pasaron por aquí hace unas horas, y marqué su rumbo. Ponte en la cima y <rgb=#FF0000>Mira</rgb> hacia el este, y deberías verlos en la distancia.'","Echad Candelleth está en Tâl Bruinen, al sur del Vado del Bruinen. Alphlanc te ha dicho que busques el sendero hacia el sur siguiendo la orilla del Bruinen y que avances por él hasta encontrar a uno de los exploradores de Candelleth, quien podrá guiarte al campamento.\
\
Alphlanc te informó que la compañía de Angmarim se internó en Tâl Bruinen y desea que viajes al campamento de su hermana Candelleth para advertirle del peligro que representan los Angmarim.","'El campamento de mi hermana se llama Echad Candelleth. Entra en Tâl Bruinen y adviértele de la presencia de los Angmarim en esas tierras.\
\
'Sigue el camino hacia el este hasta casi divisar el Bruinen; allí hallarás un sendero que desciende hacia el sur, con el Bruinen a tu izquierda y un alto risco a tu derecha. Sigue el sendero incluso al cruzar arroyos y maleza densa; Candelleth envía exploradores desde su campamento, y seguro encontrarás a uno que pueda guiarte.'","'¿Traes la advertencia de mi hermana de que los Angmarim han llegado a Tâl Bruinen? Agradezco su aviso, pero mis exploradores ya se han encontrado con el Enemigo.\
\
'¿Sabes por qué han venido hasta aquí? ¿Puedes decirme qué los trae a estos bosques, tan lejos de su tierra malvada?'","Libro 11, Capítulo 5: Viaje hacia el Este","<rgb=#FF0000>Mira</rgb> hacia el este desde la cima de Amon Raith","'Si los Angmarim ya han llegado al Último Puente, podrían estar muy cerca de encontrar Narchuil para Amarthiel.\
\
'Debes viajar al Último Puente y encontrar a alguien que sepa hacia dónde se dirigieron.'","'¿Los Angmarim han entrado en Tâl Bruinen? Regresa con Alphlanc en el Último Puente, en el extremo occidental del Bosque de los Trolls, y sigue sus instrucciones para averiguar adónde se dirigieron.'","'Debemos encontrar Narchuil antes que los Angmarim, ${PLAYER}. Sabemos que probablemente viajan al Bosque de los Trolls, pero temo que se desvíen para atacar aldeas en el camino.\
\
'Sube a Amon Raith, la colina más alta de las Quebradas del Norte, al sureste de los Campos de Fornost y al noreste de Puente de Caballetes, y <rgb=#FF0000>Mira</rgb> hacia el este desde su cima. Si ves a los Angmarim en la distancia, haz lo mismo en Amon Sûl, la Cima de los Vientos, en las Tierras Solitarias.'","<rgb=#FF0000>Mira</rgb> hacia el este desde la Cima de los Vientos","Amon Raith es una colina elevada en las Quebradas del Norte, al sureste de los Campos de Fornost y al noreste de Puente de Caballetes.\
\
Calenglad te ha pedido que asciendas a la cima de Amon Raith y que <rgb=#FF0000>Mires</rgb> hacia el este desde las alturas.","Amon Sûl, la gran colina llamada Cima de los Vientos, se encuentra en las Tierras Solitarias.\
\
Calenglad te ha pedido que asciendas a la Cima de los Vientos y que <rgb=#FF0000>Mires</rgb> hacia el este desde las alturas.","Se ha visto a compañías de Angmarim abandonar Evendim y dirigirse hacia el este, en camino al Bosque de los Trolls en busca de Narchuil.","Muy al este, una compañía de Angmarim cruza el Último Puente","'¿Buscas a los Angmarim que pasaron por aquí hace poco? Los vi desde muy lejos y pude esconderme antes de que llegaran. Temí ser descubierta, pues al frente de su compañía marchaba un hombre de enorme maldad... un Númenóreano Negro, si no me engaño. Me pareció que miraba directamente hacia mi escondite, pero en ese instante algo llamó su atención y giró la vista hacia el oeste. No sé qué pudo ser, pero enseguida reanudó la marcha y la compañía continuó hacia el este.\
\
'Tu expresión me dice que ya has tenido tratos con ese hombre, y que la memoria te llena de pesar. Por lo que alcancé a oír, su rumbo los llevaba hacia el sur, a las tierras sombrías de Tâl Bruinen. Mi hermana Candelleth tiene un campamento en Tâl Bruinen. Para llegar allí, sigue el camino hacia el este hasta casi ver el Bruinen; hallarás un sendero de tierra que serpentea hacia el sur, con el Bruinen a tu izquierda y un alto paredón rocoso a tu derecha. Sigue ese camino, incluso al cruzar arroyos y maleza densa, y tarde o temprano encontrarás uno de los exploradores de Candelleth, que podrá guiarte hasta su campamento.\
\
'Dile a Candelleth que los Angmarim han llegado a las tierras que ella vigila. Dile también que sea cauta. Me temo pensar qué misión podría traer a un Númenóreano Negro tan cerca de Imladris.'","Muy al este, una nube de polvo marca el paso de los Angmarim","'Esperaba que descubriéramos algo sobre Narchuil que nos ayudara a encontrarlo antes que los Angmarim, pero ese anhelo, como tantos otros, ha sido frustrado. Mordrambor nos ha retrasado y ahora debemos seguir a las fuerzas de Amarthiel hacia el este, cuando yo deseaba estar delante de ellos.\
\
'No importa. Hay muchas colinas altas entre aquí y las tierras salvajes del Bosque de los Trolls, y si debemos seguirlos, lo haremos con conocimiento de lo que nos espera. Debes dejar Evendim rumbo al este y atravesar los Campos de Fornost. A poca distancia al noreste de Puente de Caballetes se alza la gran colina de Amon Raith. Ponte en su cima y <rgb=#FF0000>mira</rgb> hacia el este. Si ves a los Angmarim por delante, continúa hasta Amon Sûl, al que muchos llaman Cima de los Vientos, en las Tierras Solitarias, y haz lo mismo: <rgb=#FF0000>mira</rgb> hacia el este desde su cumbre.\
\
'Temo que los Angmarim puedan atacar aldeas en su camino. Observando su avance desde las alturas podrás seguir su rastro y saber hacia dónde se dirigen.'"},
[1928]={"Candelleth está en Echad Candelleth, en Tâl Bruinen.\
\
Has derrotado a varios de los Angmarim que buscaban entre las ruinas, y ahora deberías regresar con Candelleth para ver si tiene información sobre dónde podría haberse ocultado Narchuil.","'Muchas pequeñas ruinas se encuentran dispersas por Tâl Bruinen, ${PLAYER}, y los Angmarim parecen especialmente interesados en registrarlas. Mientras derrotas a algunos de estos invasores, pensaré en los lugares donde Narchuil podría haberse mantenido oculta.'","'Tu historia me llena de preocupación, ${PLAYER}. Tâl Bruinen es una tierra oscura y boscosa, y ese anillo que busca Amarthiel podría estar en cualquier parte. Si los Angmarim tienen alguna guía hacia su paradero que nosotros no poseemos, veo pocas posibilidades de que lo encontremos antes que ellos.\
\
'Mis exploradores me dicen que los Angmarim parecen especialmente interesados en las pequeñas ruinas que salpican el paisaje de Tâl Bruinen. Si pudieras viajar a algunas de estas ruinas y derrotar a los Angmarim que las registran, yo reflexionaré sobre los posibles lugares donde un anillo como Narchuil podría haberse perdido.\
\
'Temo que esta tarea sea vana, ${PLAYER}, pero quizá Narchuil, si realmente está en estos bosques, logre también eludir a los Angmarim.'","Le has contado a Candelleth por qué los Angmarim han venido a Tâl Bruinen, y ahora ella medita sobre los posibles lugares donde podría estar escondida Narchuil.","Libro 11, Capítulo 6: Una Tierra Sombría","'Has cumplido con tu parte, pero debo confesarte que mi lista de posibles escondites para el anillo Narchuil es muy corta. Te hablaré de ellos, y podrás juzgar por ti mismo si te parecen razonables.'","Pequeñas ruinas pueden encontrarse dispersas por las colinas y valles boscosos de Tâl Bruinen.\
\
Candelleth te dijo que los Angmarim parecen tener un gran interés en las diversas ruinas de Tâl Bruinen. Mientras te enfrentas a varios de estos grupos de búsqueda, ella pensará en los lugares donde Narchuil podría haber sido escondida."},
[1929]={"'You have nothing?'","'All the people of Rohan will need to stand if the Kingdom is to survive, but their King must do so first.'","Find the entrance to Éomer's chambers","You have found the entrance to Éomer's chambers, where until today he has been imprisoned by command of the King","You study the map of Rohan for a time, but few strategies present themselves to you that could stand against the armies of Saruman.","'Wait, there is one item you should return yourself, as its owner is here in the hall.'\
\
Théoden scowls and hands you a delicate cloth. On a corner of the cloth is embroidered the name Éowyn.\
\
'I am not so poor a judge as to think my sister-daughter Éowyn intended Gríma to have this token of her favour. Return it to her and she will tell you for whom it was intended.'","Théoden has been restored and now it is time to repair some of the other wrongs worked by Gríma Wormtongue in Edoras.","Gandalf is in the Golden Hall of Meduseld, and he will likely have some advice for you.","'My brother is free of his cage? I delight to hear it, for soon I too will be free of the cage that binds me!'\
\
Éowyn's smile brightens her face in the same way as does the sun breaking through a gap in the clouds.\
\
'My cage is not made of metal or of wood, ${PLAYER}, but it is a cage all the same. In time of peace, it confines me to the Golden Hall and its out-buildings, but when war threatens, it cannot hope to withstand the force of our great need. I am a shield-maiden of Rohan, and I shall take up sword and spear to defend this land and its people! My uncle must surely ride now to Isengard to challenge Saruman, and I will not hesitate to take up arms and ride with him!'","'Did you find some strategy that could serve us against the armies of Saruman? Sadly, I did not, and I had more time to think on the problem than you had. There is no shame in it! Our strength lies on the open fields, but against such numbers as you say Saruman has assembled, I do not think our strength will suffice. The Mark is not as defensible as we need it to be!\
\
'Return to my sister and give her my thanks and my love. I will see her when I return to the hall with Háma. Perhaps we will look at the map once more, and see if there is something we have missed....'","Talk to Éomer in his chambers","Bring Éowyn's favour to her brother Éomer","Éowyn accepts the embroidered cloth from you with surprise.\
\
'I remember this token! I gave it to my brother Éomer to bring him good fortune in battle, and he wore it on his ranging throughout the Mark! It must have been taken from him when he was confined to his chambers by my uncle's command! No. The command was my lord Théoden's, but the words were Gríma's, and my brother's confinement was carried out by those men Gríma selected. One of them must have taken this token from Éomer and given it to Gríma. Had I known this, I would not have allowed it!\
\
'Bring this token of mine to my brother, and tell him our uncle is restored! He is being confined to his chambers in Edoras, north of Meduseld.'","Éowyn is in the Golden Hall of Meduseld.\
\
Éomer has asked you to return to his sister, and to thank her for her sympathy and her worry.","Even imprisoned, Éomer has continued to plan for the defence of Rohan. He has asked you to study the map in his chambers so you may better understand the geography of the Kingdom.","'Study the map of Rohan in the other room and see if some strategy presents itself to you, my friend.'","'This token of her favour belongs to the one who gave it: my sister-daughter Éowyn. She is here in the Golden Hall.'","'Bring that token of mine to my brother, and tell him our uncle is restored! He is being confined to his chambers in Edoras, north of Meduseld.'","'You have nothing for me? Why is this?'","Éowyn has asked you to return her favour to her brother Éomer, currently imprisoned at his chambers, north of Meduseld, in Edoras.","Return Éowyn's favour to her in Meduseld","Talk to Gandalf in Meduseld","'Return to my sister Éowyn and tell her I will see her soon.'","Talk to Éowyn in Meduseld","'When my uncle rides to war, I will not refuse him. I am a shield-maiden of Rohan, and I will not shrink from the challenge of war!'","Book 11, Chapter 6: The Cage","Study the map in Éomer's chambers","'${PLAYER}! I am glad to see you are well. Háma has brought me the news that I am free to leave, but that is not what lightens my heart. The most joyous tidings are that my uncle Théoden has awakened to the fact of his peril, and his treacherous counsellor has been dragged to light!'\
\
Éomer accepts the embroidered cloth from you, and crushes it in one fist. 'This was taken from me by Forthere, one of Gríma's men. I am pleased to have it back, but I would sooner teach Forthere a lesson about respecting the belongings of others.\
\
'I was treated well enough by the guards outside my chambers, but my inability to do anything for my family or for Rohan was the cruelest fact of my imprisonment. I spent many hours studying the map of Rohan in the room upstairs, trying to develop a strategy for the defence of the Kingdom that could not be undone by Saruman. Go! Study the map yourself and see if there is such a strategy I might have missed, for I came up with little of use.'","When you have fully studied the map in Éomer's chambers, you should return to him to learn what he thinks of the strategic situation in Rohan.","Éowyn is within the Golden Hall of Meduseld.\
\
Théoden has removed an embroidered handkerchief from the collection of stolen goods you recovered from Wormtongue's chambers, and wants you to return it to its original owner: his niece Éowyn."},
[1930]={"Investiga Eryn Singor con Lavanthir","Muildir está junto al estrecho desfiladero rocoso que conduce a Delossad, al sureste de Echad Candelleth. Lavanthir está frente a la entrada de Eryn Singor, hogar de los trolls silvanos en el noroeste de Tâl Bruinen.\
\
Candelleth te ha hablado de dos lugares en Tâl Bruinen que poseen un aire inquietante: unas ruinas élficas llamadas Delossad y Eryn Singor, guarida de los trolls silvanos. Dos de sus exploradores, Muildir y Lavanthir, están investigando estos lugares, y Candelleth te ha pedido que consultes con ellos para obtener orientación.","'Ciertos lugares entre los bosques y riscos de Tâl Bruinen tienen un aire desagradable. Los pocos viajeros que pasan cerca de ellos suelen hablar de una inquietud persistente, una desazón que no saben explicar. Esto, en sí mismo, no es inusual, pues la tierra recuerda muchas cosas que nosotros hemos olvidado y a veces nos hace sentir esos recuerdos, aunque no sepamos reconocerlos. Pero si una reliquia tan maligna como el anillo por el cual la Campeona de Angmar obtuvo su mayor fuerza estuviera oculta en estos bosques... eso lo explicaría todo.\
\
'¡Mira hacia el sureste! ¿Ves las ruinas de piedra en ese estrecho desfiladero entre las rocas? Ese lugar se llama Delossad, y sé muy poco sobre él. Está hecho por elfos, pero el aire a su alrededor es pesado y opresivo. Busca a Muildir junto al estrecho paso que conduce a Delossad, y él te dirá si ha visto algo digno de mención.\
\
'El otro lugar que tengo en mente es Eryn Singor, guarida de los trolls silvanos en el noroeste de Tâl Bruinen. Estas criaturas crecen desde pequeños retoños en ese arbolado y cenagoso paraje, al que rara vez entran los forasteros. ¿Podría Narchuil estar entre los juncos, enterrado en el barro de Eryn Singor, o en las profundidades de Bar-e-Therchir, bajo él? Uno de mis exploradores, Lavanthir, ha estudiado las costumbres de los trolls silvanos. Búscalo frente a la entrada de Eryn Singor.\
\
'Cuando Muildir y Lavanthir te hayan dado toda la ayuda que puedan, vuelve a mí con Narchuil o con cualquier información sobre su paradero que hayas averiguado, y decidiremos nuestro siguiente paso.'","'No te desanimes, ${PLAYER}. Pensé que Narchuil podría ser la causa de la inquietud que pesa sobre Eryn Singor y Delossad, pero solo era una suposición. Quizá el anillo esté realmente en lo profundo de Delossad... pero como no tenemos forma de acceder a las salas en ruinas sin permitir también la entrada de los Angmarim, debemos confiar en que la puerta cerrada los retrase mientras buscamos en otra parte.\
\
'¡Pero escucha! Puede que se nos haya abierto otra vía de búsqueda.'","'Delossad y Eryn Singor siempre han tenido un aire desagradable. ¿Podría ser culpa de la presencia de Narchuil?\
\
'Busca a Muildir junto al estrecho desfiladero rocoso que conduce a Delossad; puedes verlo desde aquí si miras hacia el sureste. Eryn Singor, hogar de los trolls silvanos, está en la región noroeste de Tâl Bruinen. Encontrarás a Lavanthir cerca de la entrada.\
\
'Vuelve conmigo cuando hayas encontrado Narchuil o hayas agotado la búsqueda en ambos lugares.'","Candelleth ha señalado varios lugares dentro de los bosques de Tâl Bruinen donde podría estar escondido el anillo Narchuil.","Candelleth está en Echad Candelleth, en Tâl Bruinen.\
\
Has investigado tanto Eryn Singor como Delossad, pero no has encontrado señal alguna de Narchuil. Candelleth espera noticias de tu progreso.","Libro 11, Capítulo 7: Un Aire Desagradable","Investiga Delossad con Muildir"},
[1931]={"'It is good that Théoden takes action to protect his people. Saruman's greatest ally for these past months has been the inaction of Théoden, sown by the whisperings of Wormtongue. How many Orcs were given free passage across the fields of Rohan? Even one would be too many, and it was much more than a single Orc.\
\
'I do not say that Théoden rides to victory. It is good that he comes forth, but the armies of Saruman are vast and I do not know if the Rohirrim can meet them on the field.'","'There is strength in Théoden, and that same strength will flow into the will of his people. If its King is strong, so will be the Kingdom. Gladly will I ride to Isengard with Théoden and his men, there to demand Saruman cast down his staff! Friends of mine were endangered by the commands of that Wizard, and I have a debt to repay on that score.'","Talk to Théoden and see if he is willing to step outside his hall","Théoden is in the Golden Hall of Meduseld.\
\
Gandalf has asked the King to step outside the Golden Hall and look upon the city. You should speak now to Théoden and see if he is willing to do as the Wizard entreats.","'For too long have I stayed beneath the roof of my hall, ${PLAYER}. No more will I delay! I will ride forth to Isengard with my warriors, and we will remind Saruman that the Rohirrim still live!\
\
'My sister-daughter Éowyn will chafe at my command that she remain behind and make the people ready to leave Edoras, I know. But she will carry out my wish. Speak to her outside the Golden Hall, and lend her what aid you may in this.'","Talk to Éowyn in Edoras, outside Meduseld","'Speak to Théoden and see if he is willing to step beyond the confines of his hall.'","Book 11, Chapter 7: Commands of the King","'I am ready to ride to war alongside my King!'","Talk to Théoden in Meduseld","'Éowyn will chafe against my command that she remain, but she will do her duty. Speak to her outside Meduseld and see if it be so.'","'For too long have I stayed beneath the roof of my hall, ${PLAYER}. No more will I delay! I will ride forth to Isengard with my warriors, and we will remind Saruman that the Rohirrim still live!'","Aragorn, Éomer, and Gandalf are within the Golden Hall of Meduseld.\
\
Théoden King has determined his next course of action, and those who follow him have their orders.","'I am ready to look out upon my city with unclouded eyes, ${PLAYER}, free from the shroud of Gríma's whispers. Will you walk with me as well?'","'I have been given my freedom once again, and now I am free to ride to war with my King! It is a far better day into which I walk than the one I left! We will show Saruman that Rohan is strong. For too long he has done as he will, but now we will remind him that this land is not his to despoil!\
\
'My road leads west, with the King, but he has asked you to assist Éowyn at Edoras. I am certain there will be no lack of deeds that will need doing, but if you have an opportunity, perhaps you could see how fares Aldburg in the Eastfold? That town is my home, and it would be a comfort to my mind to know that you have kept an eye on it.\
\
'There is no hurry! Assist Éowyn with her preparations here, first. But keep Aldburg in mind while I am away, if you would.'","Talk to Gandalf in Meduseld","Gandalf wishes for the King to step outside his hall and look upon the city, and to decide what can be done for the survival of Rohan.","Talk to Aragorn in Meduseld","'There is no honour in this! Why must I remain behind while my brother and my uncle ride to war? Do they care more for Rohan than do I? No! I would fight as hard for the people of the Mark as any man, and mayhap with even greater ferocity!'\
\
Éowyn's eyes blaze with a dangerous fire for a moment, and her fists clench and unclench.\
\
'I will do as my King commands, ${PLAYER}. This duty has been given to me, and I will carry it out as best I may, though it be not my desire. None will say that Éowyn betrayed the word of her King. I will protect the people of Edoras and see them to safety, while the battle rages elsewhere. It may come to us, in the end, and if it does I will be ready. I will need your help in the meantime.'","Éowyn is outside the Golden Hall of Meduseld, in Edoras.","'The time has come for Théoden to step beyond the confines of his hall and look out over his city. Speak to the King and see if he is willing to do this, ${PLAYER}.'","'This way may not lead to victory, but it may lead to a less certain defeat.'","'I will collect the debt Saruman owes for endangering my friends.'","Théoden is in the Golden Hall of Meduseld, waiting to speak with you about his next course of action: war!","Talk to Éomer in Meduseld"},
[1932]={"Encuentra la cámara suroeste en Bar-e-Therchir","'Es un placer conocerte, ${PLAYER}, pero debe ser un asunto urgente el que te ha traído tan lejos en la naturaleza salvaje.\
\
'Debo confesarte que no he visto señal alguna del anillo que buscas, pero los trolls silvanos hacen difícil cualquier exploración prolongada. Hay un aire desagradable sobre este lugar, y la presencia de una reliquia maligna podría explicar tal sensación.\
\
'Hay una caverna bajo Eryn Singor llamada Bar-e-Therchir, y creo que de allí procede ese aire malsano que cubre estas tierras. Debe ser registrada en busca de cualquier rastro de Narchuil.\
\
'Eso no será sencillo, pues la caverna es hogar de los Dâg Taushakhu, hijos de Taushakh, quien gobernó a los trolls silvanos del Norte por un tiempo. Búscalos en las cámaras más profundas de Bar-e-Therchir y determina si Narchuil descansa en una de ellas.\
\
'También frustra a cualquier Angmarim que veas registrando la cueva y vuelve conmigo cuando hayas explorado sus profundidades y derrotado a los Dâg Taushakhu. Quizá regreses con Narchuil, y la búsqueda llegue a su fin.'","Esta cámara del suroeste no revela señal alguna de la presencia de Narchuil","Encuentra la cámara norte en Bar-e-Therchir","Lavanthir ha vigilado a los trolls silvanos que viven en Eryn Singor durante varias semanas y ha notado que los Angmarim hacen lo mismo.","Esta cámara del norte no revela señal alguna de la presencia de Narchuil","Encuentra la entrada a Bar-e-Therchir","Has encontrado la entrada a Bar-e-Therchir; ¿se halla Narchuil en su interior?","Derrota a los Dâg Taushakhu (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Los Dâg Taushakhu viven en las cámaras más profundas de Bar-e-Therchir, situada bajo Eryn Singor, hogar de los trolls silvanos en la esquina noroeste de Tâl Bruinen.\
\
Lavanthir te ha pedido que explores las cámaras más profundas de Bar-e-Therchir para ver si Narchuil está oculto allí y que derrotes a los Dâg Taushakhu.","'La caverna que encontraste bajo Eryn Singor es hogar de los Dâg Taushakhu, hijos de Taushakh, quien gobernó a los trolls silvanos del Norte por un tiempo. Búscalos en las cámaras más profundas de Bar-e-Therchir y determina si Narchuil descansa allí.\
\
'Regresa conmigo cuando hayas explorado sus profundidades y derrotado a los Dâg Taushakhu. ¡Si encuentras Narchuil, tu búsqueda habrá concluido!'","Dâg Taushakhu derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Lavanthir está en el exterior de Eryn Singor, hogar de los trolls silvanos en Tâl Bruinen.\
\
Has derrotado a los Dâg Taushakhu en las profundidades de Bar-e-Therchir, pero no hallaste señal alguna de Narchuil.","La entrada a Bar-e-Therchir está en algún lugar dentro de Eryn Singor, hogar de los trolls silvanos en la región noroeste de Tâl Bruinen.\
\
Lavanthir cree que el aire desagradable que pesa sobre Eryn Singor emana de la caverna de Bar-e-Therchir y quiere que halles la entrada, derrotando trolls silvanos en el camino, y luego regreses con él.","'No sé dónde está la entrada a Bar-e-Therchir, pero se encuentra en algún punto dentro de Eryn Singor. Encuentra la entrada de la caverna y explora sus profundidades en busca de Narchuil.'","Libro 11, Capítulo 7: Secretos de Eryn Singor","'¿No encontraste señal alguna de Narchuil? Lo lamento, ${PLAYER}, pero al menos podemos consolarnos en esto: los Angmarim siguen revisando la cueva, mientras que nosotros ya sabemos que allí no está. ¡Que tarden mucho en descubrirlo!\
\
'Me alegra que hayas derrotado a los Dâg Taushakhu, pues nada bueno podría surgir de permitir que crecieran. El propio Taushakh causó muchos males en Tâl Bruinen antes de marchar al norte, y sus hijos seguramente habrían hecho lo mismo.\
\
'Lamento que tu búsqueda aquí resultara infructuosa. ¿Sugirió Candelleth algún otro lugar posible?'"},
[1933]={"La puerta parece segura; los Angmarim no han logrado forzarla.","'Derrota a algunos Angmarim aquí, en Tâl Bruinen, para ver si han conseguido abrir la puerta que conduce al interior de las ruinas de Delossad.'","'¿La puerta está segura? Me alegra oírlo, aunque significa que no estamos más cerca de saber si Narchuil está escondida detrás de ella. La llave de esa puerta sin duda se ha perdido con el tiempo, y no dudo que si los Angmarim creen que Narchuil está dentro de Delossad, intentarán abrirla por la fuerza tarde o temprano.\
\
'¿Candelleth te indicó otros lugares donde buscar pistas? La puerta de Delossad quizá nos compre algo de tiempo para encontrar Narchuil, si está oculta en otro sitio de Tâl Bruinen. Pero si está dentro de Delossad..... debo admitir que no sé qué podríamos hacer. Incluso si pudiéramos entrar de algún modo en las ruinas selladas, ¿cómo sacar Narchuil sin alertar a los Angmarim que patrullan Tâl Bruinen?'","Muildir mantiene la guardia frente a las ruinas de Delossad, al sureste de Echad Candelleth.\
\
Has comprobado que la puerta que conduce al interior de Delossad aún está asegurada. Los Angmarim no han logrado abrirla. Debes regresar ahora con Muildir para informarle.","Encuentra la puerta cerrada en lo profundo de las ruinas de Delossad","Muildir ha vigilado las ruinas de Delossad y ha notado un gran interés de los Angmarim en el sitio derrumbado.","La puerta que conduce a las profundidades de Delossad está en la parte trasera de las ruinas al sureste de Echad Candelleth.\
\
Los Angmarim han estado registrando Tâl Bruinen buscando pistas sobre la ubicación de Narchuil. Muildir te ha pedido que verifiques que la puerta hacia las profundidades de Delossad aún esté segura.","Libro 11, Capítulo 7: La Puerta de Delossad","'Me alegra conocerte, ${PLAYER}. Te vi junto a Candelleth desde lejos, pero no creo que vieras mi saludo.\
\
'Los Angmarim vinieron a Delossad tan pronto como llegaron, pero hasta donde sé no lograron acceder a las profundidades de las ruinas. Al no poder abrir la puerta, pronto se dirigieron a otras zonas de Tâl Bruinen. Deberías asegurarte de que la puerta siga segura: siempre la he conocido cerrada, y sería un alivio saber que los Angmarim no la han roto.\
\
'Y si puedes, ${PLAYER}, derrota a algunos de los Angmarim que han invadido estas tierras. Han trasladado su búsqueda a otras ruinas dispersas por Tâl Bruinen. Este no es un lugar para los Angmarim, y quiero verlos expulsados.'"},
[1934]={"Convince Herith to obey the word of Théoden","By these stairs is a good place to read the proclamation","You read the proclamation aloud, and an old woman seeks to catch your eye","Éowyn has given you a proclamation to read at the two stairs south of the north-west entrance, to prepare the people of Edoras to leave the city.","Éowyn has given you a proclamation to read at the top of the stairs, north-west of Meduseld, to prepare the people of Edoras to leave the city.","Return the proclamation to Éowyn outside Meduseld","Baduhild reluctantly agrees to leave the city","Talk to a growling dissenter","Ethryth's belongings are at the top of the stairs north-west of Meduseld. The waggon to Dunharrow is near the outside walls to the north of Ethryth.","Éowyn has given you a proclamation to read by the entrance courtyard in the north-west, to prepare the people of Edoras to leave the city.","Éowyn is outside Meduseld, in Edoras.\
\
You have helped prepare the people of Edoras prepare to leave their city, and should return to Éowyn with a report of your success.","'Read the proclamation I gave you aloud before the people of Edoras. It contains Théoden King's command to leave the city. Not all of the townsfolk will be happy to hear it, but they will need to obey the word of their king.'","'Do you have the time to spare an old woman, tidings-bearer? I have heard the commands of Théoden King, and would obey, but it has been many years since Ethryth felt the bloom of youth, and I do not have the strength I once did. My belongings are bundled in this crate, but I cannot carry it down the hill to the Dunharrow waggon without help. The waggon is to the north of here, if you follow the road.\
\
'Can you bring my possessions to the waggon north of here? Just follow the road. Ethryth will be in your debt.'","A small child, Derláf, has sought to get your attention.","'What gives you the right to order us out of our homes? Maybe those are the commands of Théoden, and maybe they are not. Maybe they are the words of Gandalf! Maybe the Wizard is working against us, and just wants our treasures for himself! Do they not say that trouble follows him wherever he goes?\
\
'I will teach you a lesson, ${RACE}! I will teach you what happens when you do the bidding of Wizards!'","Talk to Ethryth atop the stairs north-west of Meduseld","'They were insulting the King! They cannot be allowed to do that!'","'I heard you read the words of Théoden King, and I know everyone who is not going to fight needs to leave Edoras. But those men over there were laughing, and I heard them insult the name of the King!\
\
'You are not going to let them escape justice, are you? Everyone has to obey the word of Théoden King!'","'I hope it is not too much trouble for you to carry my belongings to the Dunharrow waggon. It is north of here, along the road.'","This market is a good place to read the proclamation","You read the proclamation aloud, and several people nearby begin to mutter darkly","Several of the people at the courtyard with two stairs need to be convinced of the wisdom of Éowyn's plan.","'You agreed to help an old woman carry her belongings to the Dunharrow waggon? You should do that at once!'","Ethryth is atop the steps north-west of Meduseld, and has sought to catch your eye.","You read the proclamation aloud, and several people nearby begin to grumble","Convince Colinan to obey the word of Théoden","'You read the proclamation aloud? Return and see if the people have consented to do as their king commands.'","After a brief discussion, Colinan agrees to leave Edoras","You leave Ethryth's belongings on the waggon, as she asked","You have failed to cow the growling dissenter","Read the proclamation aloud at the market north of Meduseld","Book 11, Chapter 8: People of Edoras","Read the proclamation aloud at the entrance courtyard in the north-west of the city","Éowyn has a great number of things to do before the people of Edoras can be evacuated to Dunharrow, and she needs your help to see them done.","Read the proclamation aloud at the stairs north-west of Meduseld","'¿No tienes nada para mí?'","Pick up Ethryth's belongings","'Did you encounter trouble when you read the proclamation aloud before the people?'","'There are many things to do before the people of Edoras can leave for Dunharrow. My uncle's command must be brought to the townsfolk, waggons must be loaded with provisions, belongings gathered, and there are like to be some naysayers who refuse to follow the King's will.\
\
'Take this proclamation and read it before the people at several locations throughout the city. Start with the market north of the Meduseld steps, and then work down through the streets of Edoras. Word will spread quickly; it has already begun to do so! But the King's command must be brought to the people so the preparations for their departure can be made. Not everyone will be pleased with this, ${PLAYER}. Be kind, if you can, but keep your resolve strong. This must be done. Théoden King has commanded it.'","Growling dissenters insulted the King at the courtyard near the north-west entrance to Edoras.","This entrance courtyard is a good place to read the proclamation","You successfully cowed the growling dissenter!","Convince Anwynd to obey the word of Théoden","Read the proclamation aloud at the courtyard with two stairs, south of the north-west entrance to the city","Several of the people at the market north of Meduseld need to be convinced of the wisdom of Éowyn's plan.","Talk to Derláf at the entrance courtyard in the north-west of Edoras","Herith listens to your words and eventually agrees to obey the King","'How did the people react to the proclamation? Return to the entrance courtyard in the north-west of the city and see.'","You read the proclamation aloud, and a small child seeks to catch your eye","Éowyn has given you a proclamation to read at the market north of Meduseld, to prepare the people of Edoras to leave the city.","'You have done as I asked? Good. It will be some time before all the people are ready to leave Edoras, but every journey must begin with preparation, especially one as important as this.'","Convince Baduhild to obey the word of Théoden","Anwynd grumbles, but reluctantly agrees to leave Edoras"},
[1935]={"Candelleth está en el campamento élfico de Echad Candelleth, al suroeste de la Cabaña Calcinada, en Tâl Bruinen.\
\
Has descubierto el diario de Sara Roblecorazón en las ruinas de una cabaña quemada en Tâl Bruinen y debes mostrárselo a Candelleth de inmediato.","Revisas algunos de los escombros, pero no encuentras nada","Candelleth te contó que Idhreneth informó haber alejado a una pequeña compañía de Angmarim de los restos quemados de una cabaña.","Libro 11, Capítulo 8: La Cabaña Calcinada","'¿Encontraste este diario entre las ruinas de la Cabaña Calcinada? Debes mostrárselo a Idhreneth, al noreste de Echad Candelleth, para ver qué puede decirte sobre su contenido.'","'Si los Angmarim no conocen la ubicación de Narchuil, podría ser que la intervención de Idhreneth les haya negado una pista crucial. Habla con ella cerca de la Cabaña Calcinada, al noreste de aquí.'","La Cabaña Calcinada está al noreste de Echad Candelleth.\
\
Idhreneth derrotó a una pequeña compañía de Angmarim que registraba los escombros de la Cabaña Calcinada, y te ha pedido buscar en las ruinas para descubrir qué estaban buscando.","'Candelleth me ha contado la historia, ${PLAYER}. ¿De verdad crees que Narchuil, o alguna evidencia de su paradero, podría estar oculta en Tâl Bruinen?\
\
'Una pequeña compañía de Angmarim estaba hurgando entre los escombros de la cabaña al otro lado del agua. Garbert y Afanen, que viven río abajo, la llaman la \\qCabaña Calcinada\\q, pero creo que ardió mucho antes de que Garbert llegara a estas tierras.\
\
'Deberías revisar los escombros. No imagino que encuentres nada de utilidad, pero si los Angmarim pensaron que valía la pena registrar el lugar...'","Idhreneth está cerca de la Cabaña Calcinada, no muy lejos al noreste de Echad Candelleth.\
\
Candelleth te ha pedido que hables con una de sus exploradoras, quien derrotó a varios Angmarim junto a la Cabaña Calcinada.","'¡Nada de cháchara!'","'¿Qué es esto, ${PLAYER}? ¿Un diario? ¿Puede ser? No lo comprendo... Amarthiel no podría haber... debe haber más en este enigma de lo que sabemos, ${PLAYER}, pues esto me llena de confusión. Pero escucha:\
\
\\q...traje dos gallinas para compartir con L, pero su ánimo estaba bajo y creo que la comida no le alegró en absoluto. Comprensible, claro: mantener a N dentro de los muros de Sithad debe causarle gran pena.\\q\
\
'Quienquiera que fuera Sara Roblecorazón, fuera Amarthiel disfrazada o no, es evidente de quién habla: \\qL\\q no puede ser otro que Laerdan, y \\qN\\q no puede ser otro que Narchuil. Estamos cerca. Puedo sentirlo. El secreto está dentro de este diario, ${RACE}: el diario de Sara Roblecorazón.'","Encuentras un diario podrido entre los escombros, pero aún parece legible","'Me había estado concentrando en lugares donde viajeros y mis exploradores reportaron sensaciones de inquietud y desasosiego, como la arboleda de los trolls silvanos de Eryn Singor o las ruinas élficas de Delossad, pero solo porque era el camino que parecía lógico seguir.\
\
'Los Angmarim también han estado registrando las ruinas élficas en todo Tâl Bruinen, y hasta hace unas horas creía que era porque tenían alguna información que nosotros no. Pero si supieran dónde está Narchuil, ¿por qué no concentrarían todos sus esfuerzos en un solo lugar? Si estuviera en Delossad, por ejemplo, ¿no enviarían allí a todos sus hombres? Y sin embargo no lo han hecho, lo cual me demuestra que los Angmarim no saben más que nosotros.\
\
'Una de mis exploradoras, Idhreneth, se encontró con una pequeña compañía de Angmarim cerca de los restos quemados de una cabaña, no muy lejos al noreste de Echad Candelleth... lo llaman La Cabaña Calcinada. Los derrotó y me envió aviso preguntando si conocía alguna razón por la que ellos se interesaran en un lugar tan trivial. La respuesta es clara: están registrando todo lo que pueden con la esperanza de encontrar alguna pista, ¡igual que nosotros, ${PLAYER}! Quiero que hables con Idhreneth y averigües lo que puedas.'","Registra los escombros de la Cabaña Calcinada","'¿Encontraste este diario entre las ruinas de la Cabaña Calcinada, ${PLAYER}? Probablemente no sea nada, pero veré si puedo aprender algo de sus páginas...\
\
'¡Espera! El nombre de la dueña de este diario me resulta inquietantemente familiar: ¿no usaba Amarthiel el nombre de Sara Roblecorazón cuando vagaba por las tierras en sus oscuros designios? Y mira aquí, en la cubierta: está casi ilegible, pero aún puede descifrarse: \\qSara Roblecorazón\\q.\
\
'Debes llevar este diario a Candelleth, ${PLAYER}. ¡Podría ser la pista que hemos estado buscando!'","'El secreto para encontrar Narchuil podría estar en este diario, ${PLAYER}... ¡el diario de nuestra enemiga, la que una vez se llamó Sara Roblecorazón!\
\
'Debes leerlo y llevarlo a Candelleth de inmediato.'","Lleva el diario podrido a Idhreneth","Idhreneth está al otro lado del agua desde la Cabaña Calcinada, al noreste de Echad Candelleth.\
\
Has encontrado un diario podrido entre los escombros de la Cabaña Calcinada, pero aún parece legible. Deberías leerlo y mostrárselo a Idhreneth.","'¿No tienes nada para mí? ¿Cómo puede ser?'"},
[1936]={"Talk to Éowyn outside Meduseld","These weapons are out of place. Why were they moved here?","'There are still so many tasks we must see to completion before the people are ready to leave Edoras, but something worries at the back of my mind and divides my attention. When you searched Gríma's chambers with Háma, you told my uncle that the room was already in disarray, as if it had been searched before you arrived. Why would Gríma leave his chamber in such a state? If he was seeking something specific, surely he would know where to find it. No, I think his room was searched by someone entangled deeply within his schemes.\
\
'Gríma has fled the city, but it is my belief that this ally, at least, remains. Among the papers you collected was the cryptic phrase 'No Mere Wit, He' and a number of other writings. I do not know what they mean, but mention is made of a number of locations throughout Edoras. Go to some of these and see if you can find sign of Gríma's friends or allies.'","Book 11, Chapter 9: Seeds of Treachery","This strongbox is scorched, as if it was set on fire, but the blaze did not spread.","'You found some of Gríma's allies, and defeated them? Good. Those snakes would have caused trouble for us, especially once my uncle rides to Isengard.\
\
'I hope that was all of them, ${PLAYER}. I still do not understand all of the mysteries you uncovered in Gríma's chambers, but perhaps we have ended the schemes that were plotted there.\
\
'My uncle and his riders are ready to depart.'","Hebeca was an ally of Wormtongue. But are there others?","Léofing was an ally of Wormtongue. But are there others?","Search locations mentioned in Gríma's writings (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'We have enough tasks before us without having to worry about the interference of Gríma Wormtongue, ${PLAYER}. His allies lurk still within Edoras, I am sure of it.'","Éowyn has given you some writings from the search of Gríma's chambers, and wants you to find out where in the city these clues might refer.","Éowyn has uncovered some evidence that allies of Gríma Wormtongue seek to undermine her efforts to bring the people of Edoras to safety.","Éowyn is outside Meduseld, in Edoras.\
\
You discovered several allies of Wormtongue working to hinder Éowyn's efforts in Edoras, and should report back to her that they will no longer be a problem.","Did someone put this pile of timber here with plans to set it ablaze?"},
[1937]={"Encuentras una caja de llaves rotas enterrada bajo el arbusto frondoso","Candelleth está en su campamento en Tâl Bruinen.\
\
Has recuperado una caja de llaves rotas bajo un arbusto en las ruinas de Delossad, conocido antaño como Sithad. Debes llevar la caja a Candelleth.","Lleva la caja de llaves rotas a Merilos","Has recuperado el diario de Sara Roblecorazón, y podría contener el secreto del paradero de Narchuil.","'Escucha esto, ${PLAYER}:\
\
\\qL teme lo peor. Cumpliré sus deseos rompiendo las llaves de Sithad —las piedras de Tâl Bruinen bastarán— y escondiéndolas.\\q\
\
'No sé dónde se encuentra Sithad, pero parece que Laerdan mantenía a esta \\qN\\q, Narchuil, dentro de sus muros, y que en algún momento Sara rompió las llaves de ese lugar y las ocultó. Y mira esto más adelante:\
\
\\q... estar en las escaleras de Sithad, mirando hacia la entrada. Girar a la izquierda y avanzar hasta la pared, luego girar a la derecha y seguir la curva hasta ver cuatro pilares entre dos. Pasar entre esos dos y mirar a la derecha de los cuatro. Dejaré las llaves siempre en la sombra.\\q\
\
'Me pregunto ahora si Sithad no será un nombre antiguo para un lugar que ya conocemos, ${PLAYER}. Las lenguas cambian con el tiempo, y Laerdan ha vivido muchos años; el nombre por el que él conoce un sitio puede no ser el mismo por el que otros lo llaman hoy. Al decir los nombres en voz alta, noto una semejanza entre Sithad y Delossad, ¿no te parece?\
\
'¡Creo que hemos descifrado la primera parte del acertijo, amigo ${RACE}! Ve a Delossad y usa el diario para localizar las llaves ocultas de las que escribió Sara. ¡Estoy segura de que es allí!'","'¿No tienes nada para mí?'","'Estoy segura de tener razón, ${PLAYER}. \\qSithad\\q debe de ser un nombre antiguo para \\qDelossad\\q, como llamamos hoy a esas ruinas.\
\
'Ve a Delossad y sigue las instrucciones del diario de Sara Roblecorazón para encontrar las llaves que menciona.'","'Me anima mucho tu éxito y lo que he deducido de las pistas. ¡Estoy segura de que Narchuil está en Delossad, ${PLAYER}, y que una de las llaves de esta caja nos abrirá el camino!\
\
'Una joyera de gran renombre vive en Imladris. Se llama Merilos, y podrá rehacer estas llaves para nosotros. Pero sé precavido: es estricta y tarda en tomar confianza. Sin duda nos ayudará, pero es probable que pida algún favor a cambio. Su arte es valioso y precioso, y no lo ofrece sin motivo.\
\
'Busca a Merilos en Imladris, en la Aguja del Encuentro. Llévale esta caja de llaves rotas y pídele que las repare. Te deseo buena fortuna en ello.'","'Puedo rehacer aproximadamente la mitad de estas llaves. Las demás están más allá de toda reparación. ¿Te basta con esto?","'Encontrarás a Merilos en la Aguja del Encuentro, en Imladris. Pídele que rehaga las llaves rotas, si puede. Quizá pida algo a cambio, pero es su derecho como joyera de habilidad inigualable.'","'¿No encontraste nada? ¡Estaba tan segura de que este era el lugar!'","Revisas bajo el arbusto, pero no encuentras nada","Lleva la caja de llaves rotas a Candelleth","Delossad se encuentra al sureste de Echad Candelleth, en Tâl Bruinen.\
\
Candelleth está convencida de haber resuelto el acertijo del diario de Sara Roblecorazón: cree que el lugar llamado Sithad es un antiguo nombre de Delossad, las ruinas al sureste de Echad Candelleth.","La joyera Merilos se encuentra en la Aguja del Encuentro, en Rivendel.\
\
Has encontrado una caja de llaves rotas que Sara Roblecorazón enterró en Delossad en tiempos pasados. Candelleth te ha pedido que se las lleves a Merilos para que pueda rehacerlas.","Busca las llaves mencionadas en el diario de Sara Roblecorazón","Libro 11, Capítulo 9: El Diario de Sara Roblecorazón"},
[1938]={"'¿Le diste a Elrond mis noticias acerca de Narchuil?'","Habla con Elrond en Rivendel","Libro 12, Capítulo 10: Medias Verdades","'Temo por el corazón de Laerdan.'","'¿Qué dijo el Consejo de Elrond con respecto a Narchuil?'","'¡No tienen derecho a juzgarme en esto, ni a negarme!'","'Así que Narchuil ha sido quebrado. ¡Qué noticia tan extraña! Tenía razón al dudar de que el Enemigo hubiese recuperado toda su fuerza, pero esto... esto no había entrado en mis cálculos.\
\
'No mucho antes de tu llegada, Laerdan despertó de sus sueños oscuros. Debe ser interrogado, pues sin duda sabía algo al respecto. Él ha estudiado el anillo Narchuil y los hechos de Amarthiel más de cerca que cualquier otro entre los Sabios.\
\
'Debe convocarse un consejo de los Señores Elfos y proclamarse el sino, pues debemos decidir qué se hará con el anillo Narchuil.'","'¿Estás ${PLAYER:listo[m]|lista[f]} entonces, ${PLAYER}? Convocaré a los Señores Elfos y el consejo dará comienzo.\
\
'Quisiera que la sabiduría del señor Celeborn y de la dama Galadriel estuviera a nuestro alcance.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta es una misión en solitario y no puede completarse en Comunidad.</rgb>","Elrond se encuentra en Rivendel, en el Bosque de los Trolls.\
\
Cuando estés ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para asistir al Consejo de Narchuil, vuelve a hablar con Elrond.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta es una misión en solitario y no puede completarse en Comunidad.</rgb>","Elrond se encuentra en Rivendel, en el Bosque de los Trolls.\
\
Debes hablar con Elrond de inmediato.","Habla con Elrond en su biblioteca","'Narchuil ha sido quebrado... ¡regresa a Elrond con esta noticia de inmediato!'","Descubriste en Barad Dúrgul que Narchuil había sido parcialmente deshecho y que ahora yace en dos fragmentos, de los cuales solo uno se encontraba en Barad Dúrgul.","Elrond se encuentra en Rivendel, en el Bosque de los Trolls.\
\
Gwathryn te pidió que llevaras a Elrond la mitad de Narchuil que recuperaste.","Habla con Elrond para asistir a su Consejo","'Estoy preocupado, ${PLAYER}, no solo por el destino de Narchuil, sino también por Laerdan.\
\
'Ha afrontado muchas dificultades, pero gracias a su audacia el Enemigo no ha podido recuperar a Narchuil, y por ello ha atraído su ira. Pero eso no excusa sus palabras en el Consejo, y sus acciones me han inquietado.\
\
'La ira arde en su interior, y no convocaré otro consejo aún. Regresa a mí cuando su corazón se haya calmado, pues es justo que quien le otorgó la libertad actúe como su emisario.'","'No debes demorarte aquí por mucho tiempo, aunque tu presencia me reconforta en mi pesar, pues posees algo que los Sabios deben cargar como su deber.\
\
'Parte sin demora hacia Rivendel, ${PLAYER}, y no olvides mencionar a Narucham en tu relato, pues sus actos deberían contarse entre los valientes de estos tiempos oscuros.\
\
'Apresúrate, porque Elrond debe conocer el destino de Narchuil.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Viajarás automáticamente a Rivendel, en el Bosque de los Trolls, al aceptar esta misión.</rgb>"},
[1939]={"Travel to Helm's Dike, the entrance to the Deep, in the Westfold","Talk to Nona by Brockbridge","'My father sent you to me? I am pleased he did so, but I must confess that your abilities might be more needed elsewhere! My men report that something terrible has happened at the Ford of the Isen, and no one seems able to give a clear account. Men are scattered all over the Westfold, and rumours of battle abound. Stay not at Brockbridge! Someone must learn what has befallen in the Westfold. Some say that the King himself is embroiled in the fighting, and may have ridden to Helm's Deep!\
\
'A raiding party of Dunlendings has crossed the mountains, and they strike from cover of darkness. Their delight in killing the innocent is unrivalled. Their mark is a winged talon, and the fear of them has spread like fire in the brush. I hope to stand against them, but I have been unable yet to find them. They strike and then disappear, as if they wield some skill borne of magic.\
\
'Before you leave, go to the Mead Hall and speak with the Thane. Léoferth is very weak, and the strain of rule has taken a heavy toll on his strength. It is the courteous thing to do. My father Herubrand believes I rule in Brockbridge, and perhaps it seems so in action, but I would not presume to tread upon the authority of the Thane.'","Travel to the entrance of Brockbridge, in the Stonedeans","'I do not presume to rule Brockbridge. I act only at my father's request and for the good of Thane Léoferth. Speak to him in the Mead Hall, if he is able to do so. He is very weak, and I fear his last days approach.'","Talk to Horn by Brockbridge","You have come to Helm's Dike, at the mouth of the Deep","Helm's Deep is in the southern reaches of the Westfold.\
\
You and Corudan have decided to travel to Helm's Deep in search of the King, while Horn and Nona seek out the Falcon Clan raiding party.","Talk to Herefara in Brockbridge","Thane Léoferth is in the Mead Hall of Brockbridge.\
\
Herefara has asked that you speak with the Thane before you investigate the turmoil in the Westfold.","'Farewell for now, my friend. I must hunt the Falcon Clan. It is my obligation.'","Herefara is by the barricades on the southern side of Brockbridge.\
\
You have arrived at Brockbridge and should now speak with Herefara.","'I sent my son Herefara south to the town of Brockbridge, for the bridge over that span is of great strategic importance. He was to help Thane Léoferth keep that point secure, for the Thane... well, some say his last days are nearly here. My son is strong and will help Léoferth defend the span.\
\
'Travel south to Brockbridge and meet with my son. He will know how best you and your companions can help.'","'Horn wishes to go with Nona on her search for the Falcon Clan, and I cannot blame him. He believed he could set his love aside while they were apart, but it seems to my eyes that proved incorrect. Rather than send his heart away with her, he would rather walk beside her on her own journey, until its conclusion. Of all the strange things that have been done for love, this is perhaps the least peculiar: a desire to not be apart.\
\
'He charged me with one task, in his absence. He wanted me to look after you, ${PLAYER}! As we continue southward into the Westfold in search of the King, I am to ensure you do not endanger yourself unnecessarily. I told him I would do my best.\
\
'Our farewells have been said. When you are prepared to go, let us make for Helm's Deep, in the Westfold. Horn says that this is where the King would ride if his march to war ran afoul of danger unexpected.'","'Horn told me that the King would make for Helm's Deep, in the Westfold, if things went ill on the ride to Isengard.'","The town of Brockbridge is located to the south of Woodhurst.\
\
Herubrand has asked you to speak with his son Herefara in Brockbridge.","'You spoke of the Falcon Clan to me, not long after we first met. I cannot deny their crimes, nor their evil, but I wish there was some other who could find them. Nona believes none other could track them, but surely their leader will make some error, or some mistake, that will lead to his downfall?\
\
'No, you speak wisdom. If even one innocent life could be spared, it would be folly not to act. Nona believes she can find the Falcon Clan raiding party, and I think she is right.\
\
'But I will not leave her again. This is a journey we will make together. I hope you understand, ${PLAYER}. I will see you again in time, but I cannot abandon Nona to this battle.'","'Farewell, my friend. I have asked Corudan to look after you. You should do the same for him. Keep him away from any Ents!'","'You will find my son Herefara at Brockbridge. Travel south to the city and offer him your aid, for I am certain he will have need of it. Thane Léoferth is in poor health, and Brockbridge has vital importance for the Stonedeans.'","Corudan is by the southern side of the span, in Brockbridge.","Book 12, Chapter 10: Rumours of Battle","'You have come to help us? I know not what help you can give, but I will turn none away. Things have gone ill for us.'","'I know the the mark of the winged talon, ${PLAYER}. That is the sign of the Hebog-lûth, the Falcon Clan. They became enemies of my people when they accepted the coin of Saruman. They are enemies of yours as well, and of Horn's people. Herefara says he has not been able to track their raiding party? That is because he is the son of a horse-lord, and does not know the ways of the wild. He is at home on the open fields, but the people of the Falcon are familiar with the high crag and the paths of the mountains. Lheu Brenin can lead his people wherever he will, and Herefara will never find him.\
\
'But I will. I can move silently and swiftly, and I can find the tracks no horse-lord would recognize. We must part again, ${PLAYER}, for a time. I will see you again when the Falcon Clan raiders have been defeated, but I cannot allow them to roam free unopposed. I must do this while I am still able. No others can.'","'Nona and Horn plan to find the Falcon Clan raiding party in the Stonedeans. But Horn has charged me with another task.'","Talk to Corudan by Brockbridge","Talk to Gamling at Helm's Dike","Horn and Nona are on the southern side of the span, by Brockbridge, in the Stonedeans.","Herubrand has asked you to travel to the town of Brockbridge to help his son Herefara against the Dunlending invaders.","Gamling is at Helm's Dike, at the mouth of the Deep.","You have arrived at Brockbridge and should now find Herefara","Talk to Thane Léoferth in the Mead Hall of Brockbridge","Léoferth is very weak, and cannot speak above a whisper.\
\
'You... come from... Edoras? What... news?'\
\
You tell the Thane that the King has ridden to Isengard to wage war against Saruman's forces, and Léoferth's face slowly forms a rictus grin.\
\
'Good... good! That is... the strength... the strength I remember. My son... Háma... surely rides with... with the King. He is his most... most loyal...'\
\
Léoferth's voice fades into nothing and his eyes seem far away. You nearly turn away when his eyes close, but then he speaks once more.\
\
'Help the... help the King. The Riddermark... must not... must not fall. The Eorlingas... will... will...'\
\
You respectfully wait for more, but the Thane is lost in his own thoughts, and no longer sees you."},
[1940]={"'Calenglad es sabio a su manera; confío en que podrá ayudarte a descubrir el destino de Laerdan.'","Has regresado de los parajes salvajes de Tâl Bruinen con noticias que preocupan a Elrond de Rivendel.","'Aunque creo que Angmar aún no ha recuperado a Narchuil, pronto descubrirán algo acerca de su paradero, si no por su larga búsqueda, por el propio Laerdan. Las torturas ideadas por el Enemigo pueden quebrar la mente tanto como el cuerpo, y Laerdan posee gran conocimiento.\
\
'Quiero encomendarte esta tarea, ${PLAYER}: regresa con Calenglad en Evendim y busca a Laerdan. Puede que su tiempo en la Tierra Media ya haya llegado a un fin prematuro, pero lo dudo, pues Laerdan es fuerte y voluntarioso, y no traicionaría fácilmente su propósito por la fuerza.\
\
'Ve rápidamente con Calenglad en Evendim y busca cualquier noticia que puedas encontrar sobre Laerdan, sean buenas o malas.'","Calenglad está en Tinnudir, junto a la orilla oriental del lago Nenuial, en Evendim.\
\
Elrond te ha pedido que regreses con Calenglad y comiences la búsqueda del señor elfo Laerdan.","'Calenglad mantiene a la mayoría de sus hombres en Tinnudir, frente a la orilla occidental del lago Nenuial.\
\
'Ve con rapidez, ${PLAYER}. Puede que a Laerdan no le quede mucho tiempo en la Tierra Media.'","Libro 12, Capítulo 1: El Encargo de Elrond","'¡Saludos, ${PLAYER}! Es bueno verte de regreso, aunque sea en tales circunstancias. Las noticias han llegado antes que tú: un mensajero elfo de la Casa de Elrond trajo el aviso de que venías a indagar por el destino de Laerdan."},
[1941]={"Ordwald, the blacksmith of Underharrow, has a shop to the south of the Mead Hall.\
\
Ellen Fremedon has asked you to carry a heavy barrel of spears from Ordwald's shop back to her.","'The people of Entwade will need your assistance before they can come to Edoras. Travel north-east to their village and help them as much as you can.'\
\
Éowyn pauses, her expression conflicted.\
\
'The people of Entwade may be more willing to listen to you than will be the next woman with whom you speak. Ellen Fremedon and I have never agreed upon anything. After you deal with Entwade, find Ellen Fremedon in Underharrow and tell her what my uncle has commanded: that the people of Edoras find shelter in Dunharrow. She may think they have all arrived by now, but if so she is mistaken.\
\
'I wish Thane Dúnhere had not gone to the Ford. He is more reasonable than his wife, if you ask me.'","The town of Entwade is to the north-east of Edoras.","'Ordwald has been busy at his forge. Go to his shop, south of here, and bring back a barrel of the swords he has made. I have several others doing the same.'","Éowyn has asked you to bring word to Ellen Fremedon of Harrowdale that the people of Edoras will soon be seeking shelter in her lands.","'You are here for more weapons? The Lady of Harrowdale has had folk carrying off barrels of my work all morning. Take another barrel with my regards.'","Talk to Horn at the entrance to Underharrow","'You should return to the Lady of Harrowdale, and see what she thinks of the goods you delivered to her.'","'Ordwald has been busy at his forge. Go to his shop, south of here, and bring back a barrel of the armour he has made. I have several others doing the same.'","Book 12, Chapter 1: Message for Harrowdale","'You are here for another barrel of my work? If you can lift it, bring a barrel of my armour back to the Lady of Harrowdale. She has had folk carrying off barrels of my work all morning.'","Pick up a barrel of armour from outside Ordwald's shop","You set down the barrel of swords beside some others","You set down the barrel of spears beside some others","'I see the question in your eyes, ${PLAYER}. Why have you toiled to bring these barrels here? Why does the sweat so sting your eyes? What good has it done to carry these weapons and armour to me, where they will stay?'\
\
The Lady of Harrowdale's eyes are angry embers as she springs her trap.\
\
'It has done no good, ${PLAYER}. By gift of birth Éowyn commands some little measure of respect, and I give it to her, but she has sent only trouble to Harrowdale. Do you see these swords and spears? Do you see this armour? She has sent to me townsfolk and children, the aged and the infirm. She has sent no warriors! She has sent no one to wield the bright blade, or brandish the sharp spear! These folk will die just as easily here as at Edoras. There is no purpose to this migration!\
\
'If my husband falls, and those who ride with the King are defeated, there is no safety in all of Rohan. This is the cause of my reproach, ${PLAYER}. Éowyn plays at war, as she always has, but there are women in Rohan who truly know what is at stake. I am one of these.'","Horn is at the entrance to Underharrow, in Harrowdale.\
\
Horn has come with you to Underharrow, and he wishes to speak with you by the entrance to that city.","'You are here for more weapons? The Lady of Harrowdale has had folk carrying off barrels of my work all morning. Take a barrel with my regards.'","Ordwald, the blacksmith of Underharrow, has a shop to the south of the Mead Hall.\
\
Ellen Fremedon has asked you to carry a heavy barrel of armour from Ordwald's shop back to her.","Travel to the town of Entwade, in Kingstead, and help its people with their troubles","Ellen Fremedon is in Underharrow, in Harrowdale.","'Ordwald has been busy at his forge. Go to his shop, south of here, and bring back a barrel of the spears he has made. I have several others doing the same.'","'My uncle has commanded that I bring the people of Edoras to Dunharrow, for that is a more defensible location than Edoras. Before we make our way there, we should send word to Harrowdale of the great number of people that soon will be arriving. Some have already made their way to Harrowdale, but more will be arriving soon, from all corners of Kingstead. If you have time enough to spare, I ask that you travel north-east to the town of Entwade, and ensure that the people there are prepared for what lies ahead. Afterwards, someone will need to travel to the Harrowdale.'\
\
Éowyn pauses, and she seems to be weighing something carefully before speaking.\
\
'The lord of Harrowdale is Thane Dúnhere, nephew of Erkenbrand, lord of Helm's Deep in the Westfold. He is a mighty man, accomplished in battle and most loyal to my uncle and the Mark, but... he rode to defend the Ford of the Isen some weeks ago, and his wife now rules in his stead. She and I have never been friendly. Ellen Fremedon is, by most accounts, a kind woman and as just as her husband, but she and I are as different as the badger is to the noble steed. She will not be pleased to hear that I and the folk of Edoras will soon be sheltering at her hall, but she would be less pleased to hear the news from me. After you have helped the people at Entwade, travel to Underharrow, to the south, and give Ellen Fremedon this unpleasant news. There is little other choice, and you seem to be the best available messenger for these tidings, ${PLAYER}.'","After you have helped the people of Entwade, travel to the entrance of Underharrow","Pick up a barrel of spears from outside Ordwald's shop","'Ellen Fremedon and I have never agreed upon anything. Find her in Underharrow and tell her what my uncle has commanded: that the people of Edoras find shelter in Dunharrow. If she thinks all have arrived by now, she will not be happy to hear of her mistake.\
\
'I wish Thane Dúnhere had not gone to the Ford. He is more reasonable than his wife, if you ask me.'","Ordwald, the blacksmith of Underharrow, has a shop to the south of the Mead Hall.\
\
Ellen Fremedon has asked you to carry a heavy barrel of swords from Ordwald's shop back to her.","Ellen Fremedon is outside the Mead Hall in Underharrow.","Pick up a barrel of swords from outside Ordwald's shop","'Ellen Fremedon will not be pleased at the prospect of so many sheltering on her doorstep. Indeed, some of them have already begun to arrive.'","Talk to Ellen Fremedon","'Your tidings are over-late, bringer of ill news! Ever since early this morn, ragged folk have been pouring into Underharrow, bringing hungry mouths and sad tales! I will not close my gates to them, for the word of Théoden King is law and Dúnhere my husband would be wroth were I to disobey the Lord of the Mark. I will do my duty, but Éowyn cannot expect me to be pleased about sheltering so many.\
\
'You, perhaps, can provide some help to me in return for this hospitality. The blacksmith Ordwald is forging weapons and armour by his home to the south. Go to him and carry the heavy barrels of swords, armour, and spears back to me.'","The town of Underharrow is in Kingstead, to the south of Edoras.\
\
Éowyn has asked you to bring the news to Ellen Fremedon in Harrowdale that the people of Edoras will soon be sheltering on her lands.","The people of Entwade have many concerns with which you can help","You set down the barrel of armour beside some others","'We have arrived, ${PLAYER}. Now we must find Ellen Fremedon and hope that the tapestry of her that Éowyn wove for us was an exaggeration.\
\
'I must confess that her distaste for the woman strikes me as rather strange. By all accounts, Ellen Fremedon has never spoken against the good of Rohan and has been nothing but loyal to the kingdom and to her husband Dúnhere. Indeed, she is a minstrel of no small skill herself! I heard her play the fiddle once at Eaworth several years ago, and she made it sing in a way I have never heard before nor since.\
\
'Still, make no mistake. These are unwelcome tidings we bring. Even the most reasonable lady will not be pleased to hear the news that many scores of folk are seeking shelter in her hall.'","You have arrived at Underharrow"},
[1942]={"Habla con Horn en la Puerta Oscura, en El Sagrario","Horn is at the entrance to Underharrow, in Kingstead.\
\
You have impressed Ellen Fremedon with your selfless actions on her behalf, and should let Horn know of the experience.","Talk to Horn by the entrance to Underharrow","Collected Orc sigils in Harrowdale (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I have nothing more to say to you. There are too many people here, and on their way, to waste breath on trivial matters.'","Talk to Horn at the entrance to Underharrow","Book 12, Chapter 2: Too Near to Dunharrow","Horn is by the entrance to Underharrow.\
\
Ellen Fremedon has made her displeasure clear to you, and has nothing else to say.","Ellen Fremedon is outside the Mead Hall of Underharrow, in Kingstead.\
\
You have collected Orc sigils and Warg teeth and should bring them to Ellen Fremedon to show her that she does not fight alone to defend her people.","'I did not think to find Ellen Fremedon so cold, ${PLAYER}. No one save the forces of Saruman are to blame for the unenviable situation in which we find ourselves, but I understand her frustration. We should aid her, if we can.\
\
'I spoke with some of the folk of Underharrow while you were recovering equipment from the blacksmith, and they told me a group of Orcs and Wargs have threatened the peace of Dunharrow. The townsfolk have been used to these foes lurking in the mountains, but of late they have journeyed too near to the towns for comfort. Dealing with these creatures will allow us to send two messages, one no less important than the other. The first will serve as warning to the Orcs that Harrowdale is not theirs for the taking. The second message is for Ellen Fremedon, telling her that she does not stand alone. Her worries are ours, and she need not give up the hope of survival.\
\
'Let us defeat Orcs and Wargs in Harrowdale, ${PLAYER}, collecting tokens from each, so we may send these two messages. I also wish to see the Dark Door of Dunharrow. I will meet you near it, for only few would speak of it and then only in whispers. It fills me with curiosity.'","Collect Orc sigils in Harrowdale (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'You have nothing for me? It is as I thought.'","'My heart is heavy with dread, but so too is it filled with a sense of wonder. That is the Dark Door, ${PLAYER}, and beyond are the paths where the Dead are said to walk. You must know the story of Isildur and the Men of the Mountain, and better even than I, for you have journeyed with the Dúnedain. Aragorn is the first of that line I have met, and then only briefly. He strikes me as a most unusual man. We were not long in Edoras together, but I did mark him to be skilled with words. Perhaps in time of peace he could delight the ear with tales of his people, and may yet before all is done!\
\
'I would ask for a different tale than that which concerns Isildur and the oath-breakers. Perhaps something with joy in it. For now, let us move away from the Dark Door. I am glad to have seen it, but I will be gladder still to leave it behind us!'","'Enough words. I have spoken plainly, and have nothing more to say.'","Collect Warg teeth in Harrowdale (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Ellen Fremedon is displeased at the large numbers of people who now seek shelter in her lands, and worries about the dangers that lurk in Harrowdale.","Collected Warg teeth in Harrowdale (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Horn listens with amusement as you recount Ellen Fremedon's grateful acknowledgement of the help you provided to her people.\
\
'Are you surprised by the Lady of Harrowdale's transformation? You should not be. There is no more certain way to attain the friendship of a ruler than by helping ease the problems of the ruled. We are, all of us, on the same side now. Only Saruman gains to profit if we squabble among ourselves.\
\
'We have delivered the message, and we have somewhat eased its sting. It is time to move on to the next stage of our duty.'","'Yes? I am very busy and have no time for you.'","Bring the Orc sigils and the Warg teeth to Ellen Fremedon","'Bring the items you collected to Ellen Fremedon. She may be surprised by us yet.'","'I did not expect you to put yourself in danger for the good of Harrowdale, ${PLAYER}. Perhaps I have misjudged you.'","Orcs and Wargs can be found throughout Harrowdale.\
\
Horn wants you to collect Orc sigils and Warg teeth from the invaders throughout Harrowdale.","'What are these? What have you brought me? Are these... teeth?'\
\
Her expression changes from disgust to admiration as you recount your battles against the Orcs and Wargs in Harrowdale.\
\
'I did not ask you to do this. I offered no reward. And yet still you campaigned against the creatures on my behalf? I do not know what to say, ${PLAYER}. After my husband Dúnhere rode to fight alongside his king, I believed no one would give a thought to the troubles of Harrowdale. And yet you did. Thank you, ${PLAYER}. I hope you did not take offence, earlier. I spoke from a place of despair, but you have given me reason to hope.\
\
'If there are more ${CLASS}s like you in this land, perhaps Harrowdale will yet be made safe for the folk of Edoras, if the battle for Rohan ends not in victory.'"},
[1943]={"Según Calenglad, no todo está bien en Annúminas. Los Angmarim actúan con febril actividad dentro de la ciudad en ruinas, y una gran fuerza también ha regresado a Angmar.","'¿Qué tienes ahí, órdenes del Enemigo? Esto podría ser de utilidad...'","'Alguno de los sirvientes de Amarthiel que aún plagan Annúminas podría tener la pista que buscas.'","Has recogido las Órdenes de Amarthiel","Registra a los Angmarim derrotados en Annúminas","Puedes encontrar Angmarim por toda Annúminas.\
\
Calenglad cree que podrías hallar información sobre el paradero de Laerdan entre los Angmarim.","Calenglad está en Tinnudir, al norte de Annúminas.\
\
Debes regresar con él y entregarle las Órdenes de Amarthiel.","'El Enemigo no ha permanecido ocioso durante tu ausencia. Un gran contingente ha partido hacia Angmar, o al menos sus huellas conducen en esa dirección, pues no los seguimos mucho tiempo, temiendo que se tratara de algún ardid o mala obra.\
\
'No tengo noticias del destino de Laerdan. Mis exploradores han informado que varios sirvientes de Amarthiel se mueven furtivamente alrededor de Annúminas; puede que uno de ellos tenga alguna pista de lo que buscas.\
\
'Ve y derrota a los Angmarim que aún plagan la ciudad de Annúminas. Uno de ellos debe de saber algo acerca de Laerdan.'","Libro 12, Capítulo 2: Un Destino Indigno","Lleva las Órdenes de Amarthiel a Calenglad","'¿Has encontrado alguna noticia de Laerdan, ${PLAYER}? Alguno de los Angmarim que siguen causando estragos en Annúminas podría tener las pistas que buscas.'"},
[1944]={"Puede que Laerdan aún se encuentre en Barad Tironn, en Annúminas.\
\
Calenglad te ha indicado acompañar a Forchon a Barad Tironn para continuar la búsqueda de Laerdan.\
\
Forchon se encuentra en Tinnudir, sobre la orilla occidental del lago Nenuial, en Evendim.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión está diseñada para una comunidad. Si decides emprenderla en solitario, recibirás una bonificación de inspiración, pero el desafío será grande.</rgb>","'Te fue bien en Barad Tironn. Ve ahora y reporta a Calenglad.'","Calenglad está en Tinnudir, sobre la orilla occidental del lago Nenuial, en Evendim.\
\
Deberías hablar con Calenglad y contarle tus acciones en Barad Tironn.","Las órdenes que recuperaste de los Angmarim contienen pistas sobre el paradero del Señor Elfo Laerdan.","'¡Parece que existe la posibilidad de que Laerdan aún viva! Es bueno que la vida de Laerdan no haya sido desperdiciada en las manos traicioneras de los Angmarim, pero ¿qué han aprendido de él?\
\
'Temo ahora la necedad de haber permitido el paso sin trabas del Enemigo fuera de nuestras tierras. Pero para bien o para mal, ese hecho ya está hecho, y ahora debes partir con toda prisa hacia Barad Tironn con compañeros de confianza, pues allí yace la última esperanza de Laerdan. Una vez que su utilidad para el Enemigo haya terminado, su vida será sacrificada, a menos que hayan urdido alguna otra maldad para él.\
\
'Apresúrate ahora a Barad Tironn. Mis exploradores me han informado que la mayoría de los Angmarim han abandonado ese lugar, y ahora solo queda un pequeño contingente para saquear y arrasar, creyendo en su necedad que no regresaremos. Habla con Forchon cuando estés ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para partir.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión está diseñada para una comunidad. Si decides emprenderla en solitario, recibirás una bonificación de inspiración, pero el desafío será grande.</rgb>","'Forchon podrá llevarte a Barad Tironn, ${PLAYER}. ¡Ve rápido! Tengo muchas cosas que considerar mientras realizas este encargo.'","'¿Estás ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para entrar a Barad Tironn? Calenglad me pidió llevarte allí sin que nos descubran.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión está diseñada para una comunidad. Si decides emprenderla en solitario, recibirás una bonificación de inspiración, pero el desafío será grande.</rgb>","'¿Laerdan vive, pero se lo han llevado? Has aprendido mucho de lo que ya temía en mi corazón, ${PLAYER}. Este es otro revés más que debemos considerar...'","Libro 12, Capítulo 3: Barad Tironn","'Necesitarás todo tu valor para salvar a Laerdan, ${PLAYER}.'","Habla con Forchon y entra a Barad Tironn"},
[1945]={"'We have done as Éowyn asked, and now we should fulfill our obligation to her brother as well. Éomer wished for us to travel to the home he left behind, that we may see how it fares in his absence. That home is Aldburg, in the Eastfold. It was once the seat of power in Rohan, before the King took up residence in Edoras. Now it is the home of Éomer, and it is natural for his mind to dwell on its well-being.\
\
'He spoke of Arcil its steward as a man of good motive but of short reach to accomplish such lofty aims. Perhaps when we arrive we will see that Arcil has exceeded his master's expectations?'","The building is in poor repair, and seems near to falling down","This building is in very poor repair","Talk to Arcil in the Mead Hall of Aldburg","'You did it? I am surprised and impressed, ${PLAYER}! You managed to get the craftsmen back to work? Perhaps there is hope yet for the restoration of Aldburg!'","The craftsmen sent by Arcil are camping outside the walls of Aldburg, to the south-east.\
\
Arcil is unable to get the people to listen to him, so it comes to you to remind the craftsmen of their obligations.","The craftsmen sent by Arcil to repair the walls of Aldburg have a camp outside the city, south-east of the walls.\
\
Arcil told you that if you think you can get the craftsmen to work, you are welcome to try.","Arcil is inside the Mead Hall of Aldburg.\
\
You have gotten the workers outside Aldburg to begin working again, and should report of your success to Arcil.","You have come to Aldburg, the home of Éomer","'Let us walk around the city, remaining alert to the state of Aldburg's buildings and people. Both may need our help, if we are to fulfill our promises to Éomer.'","'Ah, welcome to Aldburg, ${PLAYER}. Do you bring word from Edoras? Is Éomer preparing to return?'\
\
You give Arcil the news that Éomer is riding to war with the King, and will not return to the Eastfold until the battle is done. His face falls.\
\
'Those are poor tidings. I have done my best to keep his city for him, but the people do not listen to my commands and I fear that I have been a poor steward in his absence. Why, just today I sent a group of craftsmen to repair the outside walls, but they have not returned and I have heard rumour they drink and feast instead of doing their work! If you can inspire them to work, feel free to make the attempt! You will find them outside the walls, south-east of the town.'","Book 12, Chapter 3: In Éomer's Absence","'We have arrived at Éomer's home of Aldburg. It looks... well...'\
\
Horn looks around, and his normally diplomatic and open face is uncharacteristically clouded with disappointment.\
\
'I have never been to Aldburg before, but it does not appear as I have always pictured it. The walls are crumbling and the buildings have fallen into disrepair. I do not think the town was in this state when Éomer left for Edoras. Let us walk through the city and see if my first impression is mistaken.'","'Look at this one, boys! Grab a tankard and a crust, friend! Give us a tale or three and we will raise a cup if it be good!'\
\
The smile drains from his face.\
\
'Oh, I see how it is. You are here to get us working? I say we make Arcil do the labour, or maybe have you do it. We'll do it when we're good and ready. You have trouble hearing me, friend? Maybe you'll hear this!'","Look at the buildings by the Mead Hall in Aldburg","'I sent a group of craftsmen to repair the outer walls of the city, but it seems they have done no work! I hear they are busy feasting and drinking. None of the people listen to my commands, and it makes my stewardship of Aldburg difficult. Nay, not merely difficult. Impossible!'","Look at the buildings in the south-west corner of Aldburg","Arcil is in the Mead Hall of Aldburg.\
\
You have learned that Aldburg has fallen into disrepair, and Arcil has had difficulty maintaining its rule in the absence of Éomer.","Talk to a loutish worker","'Why are you frowning at me? There is cheer enough to go around! The work can wait, but the beer will not last!'\
\
The boorish worker stops smiling, and narrows his eyes.\
\
'You say Arcil wants us to work? Pah! You think you can end my merriment? I would like to see you try, knave!'","Talk to Arcil inside the Mead Hall in Aldburg","Talk to Tirweld in Aldburg","The loutish worker yields, and pledges to begin working","Horn is by the entrance to Aldburg, in the Eastfold.\
\
You have come to Aldburg with Horn, to see if Éomer's worries about his home are well-placed.","Find the camp of craftsmen Arcil sent to repair the Aldburg city walls","You have found the craftsmen sent by Arcil, but they are busy feasting and drinking","'Can you wield a mallet? Can you set timbers? For those are the abilities we need in Aldburg! Our buildings are falling apart around our ears, and none of the craftsmen will listen to Arcil's words of admonishment. His father would knock them into line, but alas Arkenbryt is now gone, and the strength of will does not seem to have passed from father to son.\
\
'Éomer would set things aright, but he is busy with the troubles in the wider land, and none here fault him for that! He is the treasure of the Eastfold, and we will not deprive the kingdom of our greatest son.'","The boorish worker yields, and pledges to begin working","Talk to Horn at the entrance to Aldburg","Éomer has asked you to see how his home of Aldburg is being maintained in his absence.","Talk to a boorish worker","Horn wants you to explore the city of Aldburg so you can see if his first impression of its poor state was wrong.","'It is time for us to travel to Aldburg, in the Eastfold. Only then will we see if Éomer's worries are justified.'","'We should travel to Aldburg, in the Eastfold, there to see if Éomer's worries are founded.'","Talk to Páda in the south-west corner of Aldburg","'We will find Arcil in the Mead Hall. Let us see what he has to say about his management of the city.'","Travel to the entrance of Aldburg, in the Eastfold","'If you can get the craftsmen to work, you are welcome to try! They have a camp outside the walls of Aldburg, to the south-east. They will not listen to me.'","Horn will meet you at the entrance to Aldburg, in the Eastfold.\
\
You have agreed to journey to Aldburg to see how his home fares while Éomer rides with the King.","'Aldburg has seen better days, friend. If Éomer were here, he would do something about it, but he is away helping Théoden King with more serious problems. I cannot put the well-being of my home over that of the kingdom! It may seem more pressing to me, but I know what is really at stake.\
\
'Still, I wish Arcil would do something about these buildings. A stiff breeze might be enough to knock several of them down, and then where will we be?'"},
[1946]={"'Es bueno que Calenglad haya enviado a alguien tan valiente como tú, ${PLAYER}.'","'Cuando partiste de aquí en busca de Laerdan, procuré mi propio consejo y envié por delante a exploradores liderados por Gwathryn, uno de los mejores rastreadores que aún quedan aquí, hacia mi compañía del norte.\
\
'Ve tan rápido como puedas a Tármunn Súrsa, al este de Carn Dûm. Allí deberías encontrar lo que buscas. Tu misión es ahora más urgente, ya que se sabe que Laerdan vive. Liberarlo sería un duro golpe para el Enemigo y animaría a quienes luchan contra él.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Viajarás automáticamente a Tármunn Súrsa, en Angmar, cuando aceptes esta misión.</rgb>","'¡Saludos, ${PLAYER}! Calenglad me dijo que pronto vendrías. Es bueno que hayas llegado tan pronto.\
\
'No tardamos en encontrar el rastro del grupo que partió de Evendim, pues eran muchos y no temían ser perseguidos. Llevaban varios días de ventaja y viajaban con toda rapidez de regreso a su maldita fortaleza.\
\
'Así llegaron a la vista de sus muros antes de que pudiéramos alcanzarlos, y no vi al Elfo Laerdan.'","Calenglad ha enviado por delante a Gwathryn, uno de los hombres más hábiles de su compañía, a Tármunn Súrsa para espiar los movimientos del Enemigo.","Gwathryn está en Tármunn Súrsa, al este de Carn Dûm, en Angmar.\
\
Calenglad te ha enviado a hablar con Gwathryn, uno de sus exploradores en Angmar.","'Debes buscar a Gwathryn de inmediato, en Tármunn Súrsa, en Angmar.'","Libro 12, Capítulo 4: En persecución del Enemigo"},
[1947]={"'It is good to see you again, ${PLAYER}. I can think of no better way to meet up with friends than to see them again in the thick of battle! It was a happy meeting.\
\
'Corudan and I made the journey to Forlaw with my recovered friends from Wildermore. Some families in Forlaw have opened their doors to them until my friends can find places of their own. We then rode to the river, and it was here that pride gave way to good sense. Rather than upset the guard at the crossing, Corudan suggested that we find another place to cross the river. It was not difficult.\
\
'We planned to travel to the King's seat, there to seek you and Horn, but before we left the forest we heard the cries of Orcs and diverted our course to follow them. You know the rest.'","'We are all back together again, and let the foes of Rohan beware! After we report to Arcil, we should return to Edoras. We have done as we promised for both Éowyn and Éomer, but there is sure to be more we can do for the people of the Mark.\
\
'But first, let us tell Arcil what happened to the workers that went missing in the Everholt.'","Nona, Horn, and Corudan are in the town of Aldburg, in the Eastfold, and wish to speak with you.","Impressed with your success motivating the workers in Aldburg, Arcil wants you to find another group that has gone missing.","Talk to Arcil in the Mead Hall of Aldburg","The waggon is abandoned and there are signs of struggle. Tracks lead south","'You found the waggon, but it was abandoned? You say there were signs of struggle? Did you see any tracks? Those workers may be in trouble! Return to the waggon and see if you can find them!'","Talk to Corudan in Aldburg","'Tell Arcil what we have accomplished, and then we should return to Edoras.'","Talk to Nona in Aldburg","'You have proven yourself an able motivator, ${PLAYER}, and I wish to make use of that skill once again! A number of workers took a horse and waggon into the Everholt, and have not returned. They planned to retrieve timber from the woods with which to reinforce some of the buildings of Aldburg, but now I am not certain. You may be able to follow the sound of feasting and the singing of songs.\
\
'Go out to the Everholt, if you will, and look for these workers and their waggon. Convince them to do the work they agreed to do, as you did with the workers outside the walls. With good fortune we may restore Aldburg before Éomer returns from the war.'","'Wilmund and Torwulf just left the hall, and they spoke at length of your actions on their behalf, ${PLAYER}. They, and I, cannot thank you and your friends enough!'","Find the waggon of craftsmen in the Everholt","A number of craftsmen took a waggon from Aldburg into the Everholt to collect timber.\
\
Arcil has asked you to search the Everholt for the waggon of craftsmen, and to convince them to do the work they are supposed to do.","'Find the waggon of craftsmen in the Everholt and convince them to work. You'll find them to the south-east, I wager, drinking and feasting as their brethren did.'","Follow the tracks south to the cave and complete 'Instance: The Missing'","Tracks lead south from the abandoned waggon in the Everholt to a cave entrance.","'It is good to see you again. The four of us can accomplish more together than we can apart!'","Book 12, Chapter 4: The Missing","'We would have rescued those people without incident, ${PLAYER}, but I am glad you appeared when you did in any event. Nona and I crossed the Entwash at the narrows south of the guarded crossing. I thought it the wisest course, and did not want to put Hunbald in an unfortunate position regarding his orders. Nona would have put him in an unfortunate position, as well: under the ground. I thought it might be best to avoid the Entwade altogether.\
\
'That is what brought us to the Everholt, where I heard the Orc attack in the woods. We followed them into that cave, and that is where you enter the tale.\
\
'It is good to see you again.'","Arcil is in the Mead Hall of Aldburg, in the Eastfold.\
\
Horn has asked you to report of your success in the Everholt to Arcil in the Mead Hall.","Talk to Horn in Aldburg","'It is good to be back with you, ${PLAYER}.'"},
[1948]={"Horn is by the barrows outside Edoras, in Kingstead.\
\
Horn has asked you to tell him when you are ready to walk through the streets of Edoras with him and your companions.","'I cannot thank you enough for all you have done. You have aided Aldburg and its people in ways I was unable to do myself, but I should not be surprised at your ability. After all, Éomer did send you to assist me! Éomer possesses wisdom far beyond his years, and he uses it not just on the field of battle but in times of peace, as well!\
\
'There have been fewer of those in recent memory, alas.\
\
'You return now to Edoras? Go with my good wishes, and may you help the folk there as you helped the people of Aldburg!'","'You have my thanks for all you have done. Now you and your companions travel to Edoras? Give my regards to Éowyn, and tell her that I am doing what I can to maintain her brother's home.'","Book 12, Chapter 5: Eyes of Edoras","You have made good on your promise to Éomer and have provided for the continued maintenance of Aldburg. Now you should see how Éowyn's work has progressed.","Talk to Éowyn outside Meduseld, in Edoras","Talk to Horn by the barrows outside Edoras, in Kingstead","'A picture begins to shape itself, ${PLAYER}. The writings you recovered from Gríma's chambers spoke in vague and shrouded terms, in order to keep the identities of his allies a secret, but we have found some few of them already. Hebeca, Léofing, and Forthere have been defeated or imprisoned for their part in Gríma's schemes, but it seems there was a fourth conspirator. It seems he used several names, among them Ednoth and Góding. There may have been more that we know not.\
\
'But now we have a common thread, ${PLAYER}. Our mysterious foe seems overly fond of a blood-red brooch, and it is by this jewellery you will know him. We cannot risk his return! Only by tracking this secret enemy can we ensure he does not return to cause deadlier mischief!'","'Are you ready? Let us remain alert. Allies of Gríma Wormtongue could be anywhere. Do not think that we cleansed the city of them when last we were here!'","Talk to Horn by the barrows outside Edoras, and walk with him through the streets","Horn will speak to you again by the barrows outside Edoras, as he did once before.","Éowyn is outside Meduseld, in Edoras.\
\
You have learned that an ally of Wormtongue's attempted to sabotage the evacuation efforts, but may have fled the city.","'Éowyn waits for us outside Meduseld. We cannot abandon her to her task without aid!'","'We have come once again to Edoras, this time in the company of both Corudan and Nona. Are you ready to walk through the streets and speak once more to Éowyn? Let me know if you are prepared. Allies of Wormtongue could be anywhere, and we must remain alert.'"},
[1949]={"Gwathryn cree que Laerdan fue llevado a Sammath Baul, que actualmente está custodiado por los brutales Tarkrîp.","Sammath Baul se encuentra en Carn Dûm, al oeste de Tármunn Súrsa.\
\
Gwathryn te ha ordenado reducir la horda Tarkrîp y obtener la llave de Sammath Baul de Lozudurkh.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>La Piedra Élfica centelleante podrá usarse en un objetivo próximo de esta misión para acceder a la bonificación de inspiración si juegas en solitario o en una comunidad pequeña.</rgb>","Carceleros Tarkrîp derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Derrota a los carceleros Tarkrîp (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Usa la Piedra Élfica para obtener inspiración","¡Tienes mucha inspiración!","'He enviado exploradores para espiar los movimientos del Enemigo, y creo que Laerdan ha sido llevado a Sammath Baul. Cuando el grupo de Evendim llegó aquí por primera vez, permanecieron un breve tiempo, pero luego partieron. En su lugar, ha llegado una compañía de orcos para custodiar Sammath Baul.\
\
'Uno de mis exploradores también vio a un mensajero de Carn Dûm que entró en un cuerpo de guardia. Cuando salió de allí, llamó a la criatura Lozudurkh, al que llamó Maestro de Llaves, y este dio acceso al mensajero a Sammath Baul por la puerta principal. Estas noticias me inquietan, que los brutales Tarkrîp custodien ahora Sammath Baul, pues los Krahjarn y los Ongbúrz siempre han sido sus combatientes más feroces, y los más fiables y fieles a su causa.\
\
'Si has de entrar en Sammath Baul sin impedimentos, debes reducir el número de Tarkrîp y obtener la llave de la puerta. Regresa a mí cuando hayas completado esta tarea, y atacaremos al Enemigo tan rápido como podamos.\
\
'Debo darte una palabra de cautela: ¡ve con cuidado! Algo no está bien, y no sé qué planes tiene Amarthiel para quienes se oponen a ella.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Usar la Piedra Élfica te permite acceder a la bonificación de inspiración cuando juegas en solitario o en una pequeña comunidad.</rgb>","'Tienes la llave y el número de los Tarkrîp ha sido reducido... ¡estamos listos para nuestro asalto! Debemos avanzar rápido y en secreto, pues si despertamos sospechas, Laerdan sin duda sería llevado a un final cruel antes de que pudiéramos acudir en su ayuda.'","Este es un buen lugar para invocar el poder de la Piedra Élfica","'Has realizado grandes hazañas, ${PLAYER}.'","Regresa con Gwathryn con la llave de la puerta de Sammath Baul","Recupera la llave de la puerta de Sammath Baul","Gwathryn está en Tármunn Súrsa, al este de Sammath Baul.\
\
Debes regresar con Gwathryn con la llave de la puerta de Sammath Baul.","Libro 12, Capítulo 5: Guardianes extraños","Lozudurkh reside en el cuerpo de guardia de la puerta de Sammath Baul. El cuerpo de guardia está a la izquierda de la puerta de Sammath Baul y tiene dos antorchas frente a él.\
\
Aún debes derrotar a Lozudurkh y obtener la llave de Sammath Baul.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Usar la Piedra Élfica te permite acceder a la bonificación de inspiración cuando juegas en solitario o en una pequeña comunidad.</rgb>","Derrota a los envenenadores Tarkrîp (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¿No tienes la llave? Entonces parece que aún no estás ${PLAYER:listo[m]|lista[f]} para partir en tu misión, ${PLAYER}.'","Llave de la puerta de Sammath Baul recuperada","'Creo que Laerdan puede estar retenido en Sammath Baul, en Carn Dûm. Debes tener cuidado cuando viajes allí.","'¡Estamos listos para nuestro asalto!'","'Creo que Laerdan puede estar retenido en Sammath Baul, en Carn Dûm. Debes tener cuidado cuando viajes allí.'","Envenenadores Tarkrîp derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[1950]={"Has obtenido la llave de la puerta de Sammath Baul, y Gwathryn está preparado para liderar un asalto contra la terrible prisión.","'¡Debemos darnos prisa si queremos salvar a Laerdan! Lleva contigo a los compañeros en quienes más confíes y entra en Sammath Baul. No sé qué puedas encontrar en ese lugar oscuro, pero es el único camino que nos queda.\
\
'Habla conmigo de nuevo cuando estés ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para partir.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión está diseñada para una comunidad. Si decides emprenderla en solitario, recibirás una bonificación de inspiración, pero el desafío será grande.</rgb>","Elrond está en Rivendel, en el Bosque de los Trolls.\
\
Debes viajar hacia el sur y hablar con Elrond.","'¡Debes hablar con Elrond en Imladris, ${PLAYER}!'","Gwathryn está en Tármunn Súrsa, en Angmar.\
\
Debes hablar con Gwathryn cuando estés ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para entrar en Sammath Baul.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión está diseñada para una comunidad. Si decides emprenderla en solitario, recibirás una bonificación de inspiración, pero el desafío será grande.</rgb>","Libro 12, Capítulo 6: La huida de Laerdan","Habla con Gwathryn y entra en Sammath Baul","'¿Estás ${PLAYERNAME:preparado[m]|preparada[f]} para entrar a Sammath Baul? Será un viaje peligroso. ¡Prepárate!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión está diseñada para una comunidad. Si decides emprenderla en solitario, recibirás una bonificación de inspiración, pero el desafío será grande.</rgb>","'${PLAYER}; has hecho un largo viaje cargando un gran peso. Descansa aquí un momento.'","'Debes llevar a Laerdan a Rivendel, donde su cuerpo y su espíritu podrán sanar.'"},
[1951]={"Talk to Reeve Fríthild in the Mead Hall of Stoke","The town of Stoke is located north of Edoras, in the Broadacres.\
\
You have given Éowyn your word that you will travel to Stoke to find the ally of Wormtongue that fled the city. He wears a blood-red brooch, but otherwise his appearance remains unknown to you.","Someone seems to have carelessly run through this nest, ripping it in twain","Reeve Fríthild is in the Mead Hall of Stoke, in the Broadacres.\
\
You have learned that a suspicious man left the town, heading west, and may have joined with the Orcs. You should report what the child Adgyth saw to the Reeve.","You find booted footprints in the mud at the base of this fence","These leaves have been scattered, but it might only have been the wind","'You say you are looking for someone? Well, I've seen scores of people coming through the gate today. What can you tell me about his appearance?'\
\
You admit to Wigbald that you do not have a good idea of your prey's appearance.\
\
'That makes it more difficult to find someone, no doubt about it. There was one fellow I thought seemed worthy of suspicion, now that you mention it. He kept asking about the Norcrofts, so it could be he has left this village entirely and is heading east.'\
\
You tell Wigbald that you may search around Stoke for any other clues, just to be certain, and he shrugs.\
\
'You are welcome to do as you like, of course. It is your time you'd be wasting. The only suspicious fellow I've seen was asking about the Norcrofts.'","Corudan has called a halt just outside the entrance to the town of Stoke.\
\
You should speak to Corudan and ask him what he has found.","Talk to Adgyth on the northern reaches of Stoke","You have found a discarded helmet, but whose helmet is it?","Search either the Norcrofts or the town of Stoke for sign of Wormtongue's ally","Corudan calls a halt as you approach the entrance of the city","Reeve Fríthild is in the Mead Hall of Stoke.\
\
You have pursued Wormtongue's secret ally to Stoke, but he escaped into the city and discarded the brooch by which you would know him. Now you must warn the Reeve of the danger he poses.","'Are you looking for the man who dropped that helmet? I saw him come back for it, but when he saw me he ran! I followed him for awhile, but he kept running west of town, and I think he might have been looking for the Orcs!\
\
'I could tell he was trouble! Did I do the right thing? If I see him again I'll tell you or Reeve Fríthild. You had better tell her who I am so she'll let me in to the Mead Hall. My name is Adgyth, and I've lived here in Stoke my whole life! My mother says I need to stay inside the walls. That's the only reason I didn't follow that man and bring him back for the King's justice. I knew he was a villain. You tell Reeve Fríthild that I'll let her know if I see him again, all right? Promise that you will. Promise!'","Talk to Wigbald by the southern entrance to Stoke","Talk to Corudan outside the entrance of Stoke, in the Broadacres","'It seems our fortunes turn for the worse, ${PLAYER}. A glint of light caught my eye from afar, and my worries are now confirmed.'\
\
Corudan holds up the small object he has found in the grass: a blood-red ruby fitted into a silver brooch shaped in the form of an eye.\
\
'Our friend knew of our pursuit, and discarded the only thing by which we would know him. Now he vanishes into the city, free to strike at his leisure. I will give you this brooch, but I confess this is not the outcome for which I hoped. Now we must deliver a warning only to the Reeve, and not the means of ending the threat.'","'Tell the Reeve that I may have more information for her! If I see that man again I will be sure to let her know!'","A deadly ally of Gríma Wormtongue's seeks to escape capture, and his trail leads into the Broadacres.","Book 12, Chapter 6: Through the Net","'You say this child saw the man for whom you seek? I would like to meet Adgyth and speak with her myself. My hall will be open to her as well.\
\
'If this man you pursued from Edoras has joined the Orcs, the danger he poses has turned from a secret one to a threat we here in Stoke know all too well. We have been endangered by the ravages of Orcs and their half-orc brethren for many months now.'","'Wigbald is the guard at the southern gate. He would have seen your mysterious interloper if any did.'","'¿No tienes nada para mí?'","You found a discarded helmet, and nearby a small child has sought to get your attention.","'Our mysterious foe seems to have fled Edoras to the north, ${PLAYER}. There are a few settlements in that direction, but my guess is that he is making his way for Stoke, in the Broadacres. You and your companions travel with haste to Stoke, there to see if you can apprehend this ally of Gríma Wormtongue before he can wreak further mischief.\
\
'Reeve Fríthild rules from Stoke, and she has been an inspiration to me since I was very young. Her strength is second to no man, and she has earned the respect of all who dwell in her Riding. Still, this is not the sort of danger for which she is best-suited. She faces enemies that attack over the fields and engage in open battle, not snakes in the grass that strike from in hiding. Bring news of this secret foe to her, and warn her that he may lurk within Stoke. I do not know what evil webs he might yet spin.'","Wigbald thinks you should investigate the Norcrofts, in East Rohan, but your instincts tell you that Wormtongue's ally is still somewhere in Stoke.","Wigbald is at the southern entrance to Stoke.\
\
Reeve Fríthild has heard your warning about the mysterious foe that may have come to Stoke, and thinks you should speak with Wigbald at the southern entrance to the city. He may have seen something.","This banner is broken, as if it had been brought down upon something with great force","Travel to the entrance of Stoke, in the Broadacres","This mound of earth indicates a scuffle of some sort took place here","'Reeve Fríthild has always been an inspiration for me. Travel to the town of Stoke in pursuit of our mystery foe, and warn the Reeve of the danger he could pose to her city and her Riding.'","Lleva el broche Ojosangriento a Fríthild en el Salón del Hidromiel de Stoke","'We will find Reeve Fríthild in the Mead Hall. Let us bring her the brooch and warn her of the secret danger that may threaten Stoke.'","'It is always a pleasure to meet a new ${CLASS}, ${PLAYER}! If you maintain the peace and do no harm to my people or these lands, you will be welcome to my hall at any time.'\
\
Fríthild listens as you recount your pursuit of Wormtongue's mysterious ally and the mischief he wrought at Edoras. She smiles when you mention that Éowyn desired you to bring word of the danger he might pose for the Broadacres.\
\
'She has always been a strong girl, and in truth she reminds me of myself at that age. When she has grown some more, and broken a nose or two, she will be quite a woman. She must chafe at remaining behind to shepherd the people to safety while others ride to war. I would do the same, had the war not come right to my own lands. There is battle enough in the Broadacres!\
\
'Someone may have seen your secret interloper as he came to Stoke, ${PLAYER}. You should speak with Wigbald, the guard at the southern gate. If anyone saw anything, it would be Wigbald. He misses little.'"},
[1952]={"You cannot tell how long it has been since Wigbald was slain, but it seems he suffered a blow to the head from some heavy object. Dirt and mud on his clothes indicate that he was killed somewhere else and then dragged into the heavy grass.\
\
As you stare down at the body of the slain guard, something that has bothered you since you heard the news from Adgyth slowly resolves itself.\
\
This is not the same Wigbald with whom you spoke when you arrived at Stoke.","Talk to Reeve Fríthild in the Mead Hall of Stoke","Talk to Adgyth in the Mead Hall of Stoke","'We have been deceived, ${PLAYER}! The man we spoke to when we arrived was not Wigbald at all... he was our quarry instead!\
\
'I believe I can piece together the tale, but it brings me no joy to do so. Our secret foe arrived at the gates of Stoke sometime during the night, where he was challenged by Wigbald to identify himself. What name did he give? Perhaps Ednoth, or Góding, or another we do not yet know. What story did he weave for Wigbald? I cannot say, but my guess is that it played upon the guard's sympathies. From this I draw another conclusion: our cunning foe must appear, from the outside, to be a good man of Rohan. There will be little about him to mark him as an enemy, or Wigbald would never have let him into Stoke.\
\
'But let him in he did, and at some point Wigbald was overcome and slain. What does it reveal about our foe that he was so bold as to take Wigbald's place, and speak falsehoods to the very people in pursuit of him? That is what worries me the most, ${PLAYER}. Our foe is bold, and he is cunning, and he is unafraid. It is clear to me, now, why he spoke of the Norcrofts, though it was not at the time. He was trying to steer us in the wrong direction.\
\
'We must give this news to the Reeve.'","Talk to Corudan outside the south gate of Stoke","'I will grieve for Wigbald later. For now, I want justice brought to the man who slew him.\
\
'Adgyth says she found his body on the eastern side of the city. Go there and see if you can find any evidence of how his body came to be there.'","Bring the torn map of Stoke to Reeve Fríthild in the Mead Hall","'I found a dead body! I was just telling the Reeve about it!\
\
'I was running around on the eastern side of the town, looking for that sour-faced fellow we talked about, when I stumbled upon a body lying in the grass! I stayed just long enough to see if I knew who it was... and I did! It was Wigbald, one of the town guards! I remember his big red beard. He was always kind to me, and now I think that man you were looking for must have killed Wigbald before he fled the city. I can point out to you where I found his body, if you like. I was just telling the Reeve about it, and she says that I did the right thing to come to her at once!'\
\
You tell Adgyth you will investigate the place she described, but you have your doubts. You do not remember Wigbald having a red beard.","'Orcs and half-orcs from Bardh-dorám have raided Stoke before, and we have always fended off their assaults. We may not continue to be so fortunate if they are trained by the secret enemy you pursued to my city.'","If Wigbald's body lies in the tall grass on the eastern side of Stoke, who did you speak to at the south gate who claimed to be Wigbald?","'This tale is believable, but it makes my sorrow no less. Instead, it fans the flames of my anger! This man you pursue must be made to pay for his crimes. He sought to send you to the Norcrofts? His pride will be his undoing, for by revealing his charade we have discerned his next course. He wanted you to look eastward? Turn your eyes westward, and you will find where next lead his schemes.\
\
'After teaching the Orcs of Bardh-dorám how best to attack Stoke, this cunning snake of yours fled the Broadacres. I am certain of it. He has gone to the Stonedeans.'","'He is gone, as we knew he must be!'","Defeat Orc and half-orc raiders from Bardh-dorám (7/8)","Corudan is outside the south gate of Stoke.","'Bardh-dorám is still a danger to Stoke, ${PLAYER}. Return to that place, foul as it is, and strike a blow against the foes you find there.'","'You say you found this map of Stoke on the body of a villain from Bardh-dorám? I am not surprised. See these markings? Someone has made notes on this map, and though I cannot read the writing, I am familiar enough with my own walls to know what these annotations represent: vulnerabilities in our defences. Your secret foe is seeking to improve the Orcs' chances of razing Stoke.\
\
'But you return to sorrowful news. Adgyth found something, and hastened to bring the news to me at once. Wigbald has been murdered. Speak to the child and hear her account.'","Examine the body of slain Wigbald, in the eastern part of Stoke","The man you spoke to is gone, and left no sign","Defeated raiders from Bardh-dorám (${CURRENT}/8)","'What have you done? Is something amiss?'","Adgyth is in the Mead Hall of Stoke, with Reeve Fríthild.\
\
You have returned to Stoke to be greeted with troubling news: Adgyth stumbled upon a dead body.","Return to the south gate of Stoke and look for the man who claimed to be Wigbald","If this is Wigbald, who was it with whom you spoke at the south gate of town?","'I found something! A dead body! Can you believe it?'","'The Orcs have launched attacks on Stoke before, but we have always fended off their assaults. If this secret foe you chased here is as canny as he seems, he might be able to help the Orcs attack more effectively. The camp is called Bardh-dorám in their filthy tongue. Wipe the land clean of its foul inhabitants, and see if you can find any sign of their plans.'","Reeve Fríthild is in the Mead Hall of Stoke.\
\
Corudan has pieced together what must have happened to Wigbald, and you should relate this information to the Reeve.","'We must tell the Reeve of this. We have been deceived, and the entirety of her Riding is in danger.'","If this is the body of Wigbald, who was it you spoke with at the entrance to Stoke?","'Wigbald was proud and strong, a good man. Stoke is less safe now without him guarding the south entrance. Find his body and see if you can reveal what led to his death.'","'Wigbald was always kind to me! I liked his bushy red beard! I wish it wasn't his body I found. He's in the long grass on the eastern side of town. Maybe you can learn what killed him?'","You have found a torn map of Stoke, and should return it to Reeve Fríthild in the Mead Hall.","The camp called Bardh-dorám is to the west of Stoke.\
\
Reeve Fríthild has asked you to defeat Orcs and half-orcs at the camp of Bardh-dorám, and to keep alert for sign of their plans.","You pry a torn map from the clutches of your fallen foe","The village of Stoke is threatened by Orcs from Bardh-dorám and the ally of Wormtongue that fled from Edoras.","Adgyth says she found Wigbald's body on the eastern side of the town of Stoke.","Book 12, Chapter 7: Burning Secrets","Defeat Orc and half-orc raiders from Bardh-dorám (${CURRENT}/8)"},
[1953]={"'Has realizado actos valientes que pocos otros han logrado, y por ello mereces gran honor. Laerdan resultó gravemente herido y soportó largas torturas, pero ahora duerme, aunque su sueño es inquieto y a menudo sus pensamientos vuelven a lugares oscuros. Sus torturadores le infligieron males terribles; temo que, aunque su cuerpo pueda recuperarse, su espíritu quede para siempre sumido en la angustia de aquellos tormentos infernales.\
\
'A menudo ahora, Laerdan llama en sueños a Narmeleth... y a Elbereth... y siempre busca el anillo Narchuil. Pero ahora me asaltan dudas y tribulación, pues en sus sueños más perturbados grita afirmando que el anillo Narchuil está cerca, y que solo apresurándonos podrá recuperarse.\
\
'Sea esto algún secreto arrancado al Enemigo por su propia torpeza, o sea otra artimaña de Amarthiel, debes descubrir la verdad. Laerdan ha hablado de un lugar, Barad Dúrgul... busca al Dúnadan Gwathryn y recupera Narchuil.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Viajarás automáticamente a Tármunn Súrsa, en Angmar, cuando aceptes esta misión.</rgb>","Gwathryn está en Tármunn Súrsa, al este de Carn Dûm, en Angmar.\
\
Elrond te ha ordenado volver con Gwathryn y buscar la ubicación de Narchuil, el anillo de Amarthiel.","Libro 12, Capítulo 7: Nuevas de Narchuil","'Has regresado justo a tiempo, ${PLAYER}.'","'${PLAYER}, has regresado antes de lo que esperaba, aunque nunca dudé de que finalmente volverías.'","'Gwathryn conocerá Barad Dúrgul. Regresa con él a Tármunn Súrsa.'","Has descubierto que el anillo Narchuil está siendo guardado en Barad Dúrgul, en Carn Dûm; debes regresar con Gwathryn e intentar recuperarlo."},
[1954]={"'El nombre Barad Dúrgul no me es desconocido. Fue uno de los lugares que mis exploradores observaron primero. Al principio, parecía que estaba custodiado por grandes piedras vigilantes, pero no era así, pues las piedras vigilantes permanecen en silencio y no tienen poder alguno sobre la mente de amigos o enemigos.\
\
'Debes averiguar noticias sobre esas piedras, porque creo que el Enemigo puede estar intentando atraernos a una trampa, no distinta del Rammas Deluon. Sin duda, los guardianes angmarim de la puerta frente a Barad Dúrgul están esperando nuestro asalto para cerrar la puerta tras nosotros.\
\
'Aprende lo que puedas y luego regresa conmigo.'","'Esta noticia me da esperanza, pues si es cierta, entonces realmente hemos encontrado el lugar donde se halla el anillo Narchuil. Si Elrond el Medio Elfo cree que debes ser tú quien lo recupere, no lo contradeciré.'","'¿Has encontrado noticias sobre las piedras vigilantes, ${PLAYER}?'","Gwathryn está en Tármunn Súrsa, al este de Barad Dúrgul.\
\
Debes llevar las órdenes de las piedras vigilantes a Gwathryn.","'¿Estás ${PLAYER:listo[m]|lista[f]} para el asalto a Barad Dúrgul, ${PLAYER}? ¡Debemos actuar rápido!","Barad Dúrgul está al oeste de Tármunn Súrsa.\
\
Gwathryn te ha enviado a derrotar a los guardianes angmarim de la puerta y a aprender cuanto puedas sobre las piedras vigilantes en silencio.","Libro 12, Capítulo 8: Un enemigo incansable","Lleva las órdenes de las piedras vigilantes a Gwathryn","'Barad Dúrgul se encuentra al oeste de aquí, ${PLAYER}.'","Elrond te ha ordenado regresar a Tármunn Súrsa y buscar el escondite del anillo de Amarthiel, Narchuil."},
[1955]={"Book 12, Chapter 8: Hill Tribes and Horse-lords","'I have no close ties with my neighbours to the west, save the oaths we share, but I wish them no harm. If this snake has entered the Stonedeans, they must be warned of the danger he poses. A secret enemy, combined with the dangers they already face, endangers the whole of my Riding. He must be stopped, and now only a few know his face. You have seen it, as has poor, departed Wigbald. Bring this knowledge to Reeve Heremond, in the Stonedeans.\
\
'His seat is in the town of Woodhurst, located in the northern region of the Stonedeans. Heremond is very old, and there are whispers that he has been in poor health of late. If he is indisposed, you should speak to his wife Briant. She is of Dunlendish blood, but she is strong in her own right.'","'You have done well, my friend. Soon this land will be free of their clutches. My son and I will do what we can against the Draig-lûth, for they cannot defeat us.'\
\
Herubrand smiles at your puzzled expression.\
\
'I speak not in riddles, ${PLAYER}, and do not exaggerate my prowess or that of my heir. The Dunlendings cannot defeat us. We are invincible.'","'Horn tells me this town is home to many people of mixed blood-lines. Do they maintain the traditions of my people and of Horn's people? Or have they forgotten from where they came in order to survive in this land?'","'I see the Dunlending influence in this place, to be certain.'","'You are welcome in Woodhurst, but you do not see her at her best. My husband has finally succumbed to death, but I cannot properly mourn for him. I must mourn too for our city, for it is held in the grip of Dunlending invaders. The blood of the hill-tribes flows through my veins, but they are no longer my people. When I wed Heremond and came to live in his lands, and when I gave him a son, then I was no longer of my tribe. I was part of a new tribe.\
\
Briant's eyes flash, and you see a fire in them that reminds you of Nona.\
\
'Those who hold the Mead Hall and bring war to my home may share my blood, but they spill the blood of those I love. Now we are enemies. You have my thanks for this warning you bring, but Woodhurst is already imperiled. What is one more threat upon the pile of many? Speak to my son Herubrand. He rules now in place of his father. I will answer any questions of yours I am able.'","Nona and Horn are at the northern entrance to Woodhurst, in the Stonedeans.","You have arrived at Woodhurst, in the Stonedeans","'This is Woodhurst. I have desired to see it for some time.'","Talk to Herubrand in the hideout on the outskirts of Woodhurst","Herubrand is in the hideout on the outskirts of Woodhurst.\
\
You have defeated many Dunlending invaders and should report of your success to Herubrand.","'There will be no shortage of Dunlending invaders throughout the Stonedeans, friend. Fight them, and defeat them, wherever you are able to do so.'","Talk to Briant in the hideout on the outskirts of Woodhurst","Defeat Dunlending invaders throughout the Stonedeans (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Bring word of the danger that threatens the Stonedeans to the town of Woodhurst!'","Defeated Dunlending invaders throughout the Stonedeans (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Dunlending invaders can be found throughout the Stonedeans, especially in Woodhurst.","'Horn tells me this town is home to many people of Dunlending and Rohirric blood. Do they maintain the traditions both of my people and of Horn's people? Or have they forgotten from where they came in order to survive in this land? I do not see much I recognize of the Uch-lûth in this town. The buildings are wrong, the land is wrong. Will the people prove otherwise?'","Talk to Horn by the entrance to Woodhurst","Travel to the entrance of Woodhurst, in the Stonedeans","Woodhurst is located in the northern stretches of the Stonedeans, west of the Broadacres.","Heremond has died. His wife Briant or his son Herubrand must rule Woodhurst now in his stead.","'This is Woodhurst. I have desired to see it for some time. So near to Dunland, many of the folk of this town share ancestry with the Dunlending tribes. Perhaps Nona and I will be able to find a place here, when all is through?\
\
'That is still a good while hence, I do not doubt it! But my heart tells me that Woodhurst would be more welcoming to us than my own home of Eaworth. Well, we have more pressing matters than this! Let us find Reeve Heremond and report to him of the danger his town may face!'","Herubrand is in the hideout on the outskirts of Woodhurst.\
\
Briant has told you to speak with her son Herubrand about the situation in Woodhurst.","Reeve Fríthild believes that the man you pursue has gone westward, into the Stonedeans.","'This looks like any other village of the horse-lords to me.'","'You wish to help? Good. There are not enough folk willing to help with the problems of others in these trying times. My son Herefara is doing all he can, as am I, but we cannot be everywhere. There will always be somewhere we are not. You may not know much of these invaders, but I do. They are called Draig-lûth, and they worship worms and lizards of all sorts, but their loyalty has been bought by Saruman and they go where he commands.\
\
'Defeat these Dunlending invaders, wherever you find them throughout the Stonedeans. You will find Draig-lûth aplenty in Woodhurst, to my sorrow and my mother's.'","Talk to Nona by the entrance to Woodhurst","Briant is inside her son's hideout, in Woodhurst. You do not know where Reeve Heremond is. The hideout is on the outskirts of Woodhurst.\
\
You should find Reeve Heremond or his wife Briant in Woodhurst, and convey the message from Reeve Fríthild that Woodhurst may be in danger.","'Speak to my son Herubrand and help him defeat the invaders from Dunland. They are my people no longer.'"},
[1956]={"Horn is at the entrance to Woodhurst.\
\
Heruband has offered to bring you before the soothsayer Hildegard, but first you should see what Horn and Nona think of the prospect.","Herubrand believes that he is invincible and cannot be slain by the Dunlendings that invade the Stonedeans.","'Are you prepared to depart? Very good! Let us see what Hildegard has to say of your own future. May it be so rosy as my own, which frees my hand in battle against the Dunlending invaders!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>","Nona is at the entrance to Woodhurst.\
\
Heruband has offered to bring you before the soothsayer Hildegard, but first you should see what Horn and Nona think of the prospect.","'Herubrand is a wise man to listen to the words of Hildegard. She has unusual powers, and can see much that is hidden to the rest of us. Horn denies her power at his peril!'","Book 12, Chapter 9: The Soothsayer","Horn and Nona are at the entrance to Woodhurst, in the Stonedeans.\
\
You have had a curious encounter with the soothsayer, Hildegard, and should now speak of the experience with your companions.","Talk to Horn at the entrance to Woodhurst","'We have to do something! I need time to think, ${PLAYER}. Hildegard is as powerful as I had hoped, and now I wish that she was not! Her words give shape to a grim tomorrow, and I do not want to believe it will come to pass. Am I to lose Horn as I lost my brother?'","'Herubrand is a fool. His belief in Hildegard will get him killed, and perhaps not at the hands of an Orc! It will be little consolation to me, or to him, but there it is.'","Talk to Horn by the entrance to Woodhurst","'A soothsayer? Such mystics never speak plain, but deal in riddles to confuse the weak-minded. Herubrand is a fool to believe the words of this Hildegard. I will go with you to this cave if Nona desires it, but I beg of you: do not put too much stock in the words of this soothsayer. There are many mysteries in the world, but I think it likely this Hildegard is merely a woman with an addled mind.\
\
'This soothsayer will speak in riddles and lies. Mark my words well, for they tell the future. Pah!'","Talk to Herubrand and go with him to meet the soothsayer","'What is it? A soothsayer lives in this land?'","'Now do you understand, my friend? Hildegard has unusual powers, and she speaks of the future with a convincing tongue. I have no doubt that I will cast the Dunlending invaders from Woodhurst, for none of them can hope to slay me, or my son. If my death be at Orkish hand, then no Man can hope to harm me!'","'It is true. An old soothsayer lives in a remote cave among the mounds, and she speaks words of prophecy. She has foretold that I will die at Orkish hand, as will my firstborn son.'\
\
Herubrand laughs boisterously.\
\
'Never before has knowledge of coming death been so welcome, ${PLAYER}! For if it be my fate to die at Orkish hand, well, no Dunlending will be able to land a hand upon me! Thus far it has proven so! Speak to your companions, and if they agree to the journey I will bring you before the soothsayer Hildegard. Perhaps she will read your fate, as well?'","Talk to Nona at the entrance to Woodhurst","'Rubbish and lies. The words of that woman prey on the fears and hopes of all who listen to her. Herubrand is a fool if he believes himself to be invincible on account of Hildegard's witless ramblings. I cannot believe Nona sets any stock upon the words of this woman. She has my heart, always, but I am saddened by her belief in this nonsense.'","Herubrand is in the cellar of his hideout, on the outskirts of Woodhurst.\
\
Horn and Nona have agreed to meet with the soothsayer, with varying degrees of excitement, and now you should tell Herubrand you are ready to go.","Talk to Nona by the entrance to Woodhurst","Herubrand is in the cellar of his hideout, on the outskirts of Woodhurst.\
\
You have returned from meeting the soothsayer Hildegard, and should report now to Herubrand.","'This soothsayer will speak in riddles and lies. Mark my words well, for they tell the future. Pah!'","Talk to Herubrand in his hideout, in Woodhurst","'A soothsayer lives in this land? I am filled with delight, ${PLAYER}! Such folk truly possess the power of foretelling the fates. Do you remember the dream that drew us across the mountains? We could not fathom its meaning, but a soothsayer such as the one of which Herubrand speaks is more skilled at reading such visions than the like of us.\
\
'Return to Herubrand and humbly beg him to bring us before this soothsayer. She could tell us much!'"},
[1957]={"'Barad Dúrgul nos espera. Si hemos de recuperar Narchuil de las manos del Enemigo, hará falta más que tu valor. Necesitarás reunir aliados si deseas asaltar esa fortaleza.\
\
'Enviaré a Narucham por delante para explorar el camino. Debes buscarlo en cuanto entres en Barad Dúrgul.\
\
'Cuando estés {listo[m]|lista[f]} para partir, vuelve a hablar conmigo.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión está diseñada para una comunidad. Si decides emprenderla en solitario, recibirás una bonificación de inspiración, pero el desafío será grande.</rgb>","'¡Has regresado con las manos vacías! Debes volver a Barad Dúrgul y buscar el anillo Narchuil.'","Libro 12, Capítulo 9: Las armas del Enemigo","'¿Estás ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para entrar en Barad Dúrgul? Sin duda estamos caminando hacia una trampa, ¡pero debemos recuperar Narchuil si está en nuestro poder hacerlo!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión está diseñada para una comunidad. Si decides emprenderla en solitario, recibirás una bonificación de inspiración, pero el desafío será grande.</rgb>","Las órdenes que recuperaste de los Angmarim en Barad Dúrgul parecen confirmar que Narchuil se encuentra allí.","Habla con Gwathryn","Gwathryn está en Tármunn Súrsa, en Angmar.\
\
Debes presentar tu informe a Gwathryn de inmediato.","'Este es un día triste para mí, ${PLAYER}. ¿Cuántos más de mis hermanos deberán morir antes del final?\
\
'Es fácil perder el ánimo, pero alégrate, porque hoy hemos arrebatado un gran poder de las manos del Enemigo, aunque no sea exactamente lo que buscábamos.'","Gwathryn está en Tármunn Súrsa, en Angmar.\
\
Gwathryn te ha pedido entrar en Barad Dúrgul y recuperar el anillo Narchuil. Narucham te espera dentro de la fortaleza.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión está diseñada para una comunidad. Si decides emprenderla en solitario, recibirás una bonificación de inspiración, pero el desafío será grande.</rgb>","Recupera Narchuil","Mitad de Narchuil recuperada","'Tus acciones en Barad Dúrgul me han dejado preocupado, ${PLAYER}.'"},
[1958]={"Libro 13, Capítulo 10: Un Regreso Triunfal","'Ve con Aragorn y cuéntale de tu encuentro con Arvedui... a diferencia de muchos Hombres, verás que no teme a los Muertos ni a la palabra de ellos. Él está en una de las habitaciones de invitados a lo largo del camino que asciende por la ladera sur del Valle de Imladris.'","'Es bueno que hayas encontrado el fragmento final de Narchuil...'","Aragorn está en una de las habitaciones de invitados de la casa de Elrond.\
\
Elrond te ha pedido que hables con Aragorn acerca de tu encuentro con la sombra de Arvedui, su antepasado.","'¡Has regresado de Forochel y con el fragmento de Narchuil! ¿Y qué dices? ¿La sombra de Arvedui permaneció allí? ¡Un final cruel para un buen hombre! Que los Valar tengan misericordia de su espíritu.\
\
'Sus saludos son bien recibidos, aunque creo que serán aún mejor recibidos por su heredero. Ve con Aragorn y cuéntale de tu encuentro con Arvedui... a diferencia de muchos Hombres, verás que no teme a los Muertos ni a la palabra de ellos. Está en una de las habitaciones de invitados a lo largo del camino que asciende por la ladera sur del Valle de Imladris.'","En la cueva donde Aearil pereció, te enfrentaste a Mordrambor, y Saija reveló ser en realidad Amarthiel, usando una vez más sus poderes de engaño. Sin embargo, recuperaste un fragmento de anillo mientras Mordrambor y Amarthiel combatían.","'Este fragmento de anillo debe ser llevado a Elrond de Rivendel, pues es sabio en asuntos del Enemigo. Un Anillo de Poder, por menor que sea, es algo peligroso.\
\
'Dale al señor Elrond mi gratitud, pues fue bajo su cuidado que mi progenie fue criada. Si alguno de mi linaje aún permanece, habladles bien de mí y llevadles la esperanza de grandes hazañas por venir.'","Habla con Aragorn en Rivendel.","'Ay por Arvedui de Arthedain. Que pronto encuentre descanso.'","Elrond está en la biblioteca, en el piso superior de la Última Morada, en Rivendel, en el Bosque de los Trolls.\
\
Arvedui confirmó que el fragmento de anillo era la mitad perdida de Narchuil y te pidió que lo llevaras a Elrond en Rivendel.","'Dad al señor Elrond mi gratitud, pues fue bajo su cuidado que mis descendientes crecieron. Si alguno de mi linaje aún vive, habladles bien de mí y llevadles la esperanza de que grandes hazañas pueden lograrse.'","'¡Ay, qué peso debe cargar el rey Arvedui! Gracias por tus noticias, mi ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}. Cuando tengamos más tiempo, quizá podamos hablar más largamente de vuestro encuentro.'","Lleva el fragmento de anillo a Elrond en Rivendel"},
[1959]={"Day has dawned, and with it comes new hope for Rohan.\
\
Gléowine has hurried off to hear what has happened, but Thurketel is nearby and his face speaks volumes.","'Find Gléowine, and see what you can do for him. We cannot last much longer, and he is no warrior. He needs someone to protect him.'","'Our options are exhausted, as are the defenders. I do not know how much longer we can hold the fortress, ${PLAYER}. We must fall back into the Hornburg and defend it for as long as we can! We must fall back to the keep!'\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>There are two ways to participate in the defence of the Hornburg. You can speak to Cenric for the Storied Tale, a story-focused experience. Or you can use the Epic Battles Panel for a more gameplay-intensive experience.</rgb>\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>To participate in the defence of the Hornburg, open the Epic Battles Panel and select 'The Hornburg' from the menu. After you successfully complete the defence, you will be returned to the location from which you entered it.</rgb>","The long night wears on and Saruman's forces show no sign of relenting.","Gléowine is gone, but Thurketel excitedly takes the banner from you","Book 13, Chapter 10: The Hornburg","Talk to Cenric and complete 'Storied Tale: The Hornburg' <rgb=#00FF00>OR</rgb> complete 'The Hornburg' from the Epic Battles Panel","'I do not know how much longer we can hold the fortress, ${PLAYER}. We must fall back into the Hornburg and defend it for as long as we can! We must fall back to the keep!'\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>There are two ways to participate in the defence of the Hornburg. You can speak to Cenric for the Storied Tale, a story-focused experience. Or you can use the Epic Battles Panel for a more gameplay-intensive experience.</rgb>\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>To participate in the defence of the Hornburg, open the Epic Battles Panel and select 'The Hornburg' from the menu. After you successfully complete the defence, you will be returned to the location from which you entered it.</rgb>","'Théoden King makes his final stand within the Hornburg. I must go to join him. I belong at his side. Pick up the banner where it lies against the wall and come with me! If we must die, let us die with honour!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Interacting with the leaning banner near Gléowine will allow time to pass. Action will resume with the dawning of the day.</rgb>","Day has dawned, and with it comes new hope for Rohan.\
\
Thurketel is by the map table west of the Hornburg.","Talk to Gléowine by the map table near the western wall of the Hornburg","'My friend! Come quickly! Do you hear that sound? It is the sound of celebration! The battle is won!'","'It is the end, my friend. Do you hear that sound? Théoden King makes his final stand within the Hornburg. I must go to join him. I belong at his side. Pick up the banner where it lies against the wall and come with me! If we must die, let us die with honour!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Interacting with the leaning banner near Gléowine will allow time to pass. Action will resume with the dawning of the day.</rgb>","Pick up the banner leaning against the western wall, and time will pass","In the hours before dawn, the forces of Saruman press their advantage.\
\
Gléowine is on the first level, west of the Hornburg.","In the hours before dawn, the forces of Saruman press their advantage.\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>There are two ways to participate in the defence of the Hornburg. You can speak to Cenric for the Storied Tale, a story-focused experience. Or you can use the Epic Battles Panel for a more gameplay-intensive experience.</rgb>\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>To participate in the defence of the Hornburg, open the Epic Battles Panel and select 'The Hornburg' from the menu. After you successfully complete the defence, you will be returned to the location from which you entered it.</rgb>","'My friend, you still live! I have sustained a number of injuries, and my shield was cloven in two, but still I stand strong for Rohan!\
\
'What is that? You encountered my dear wife Ardith and my daughter Léofa? They are still in good health, safe within the caves? You have eased my worries, ${PLAYER}! I thank you for that, but there is no time to rest. We must defend the Hornburg!'"},
[1960]={"'We have been fighting. What has our Wizard been up to, do you think?'","Talk to Gimli on the field of victory","'I am glad to see you survived the night, my fortunate friend! Théoden, too, has had a turn of fortune, though he may not realize its true extent. Do you see the forest away yonder? That is no doing of mine. Those trees were brought here by a power much older than my own, and much greater in its own way.\
\
'Théoden calls it sorcery, but name it not that. Name it, rather, a power that bodes ill for Orcs and all others who harm the natural order of things. Saruman should fear this power; I believe he has already come to know his mistake.\
\
'But we will learn the truth of this later. For now, celebrate the ally that arrives in time, and the courage of friends. The day brings with it the dawning of hope for Rohan.'","'Where are our friends, Gimli and Legolas? Did they survive the battle?'","'Fortune was with us, ${PLAYER}. I came out upon the wall to see the dawn, and the Orcs mocked me. They did not know their doom was at hand. They jeered me, and threw stones, but I despaired not. Théoden spoke of one last ride through the gates, and I saw the glory in it, but still I dared not hope for victory. And yet: the sight of the King riding forth gave to his people the fire they needed!\
\
'Did you hear the horn-blast as the king rode forth? I do not know what man blew the horn of Helm Hammerhand, but it filled our foes with terror, especially the wild men of Dunland. They thought Helm came again among the living! Who is to say he did not?'","'¡El día es nuestro!'","'The Orcs have been defeated, if not by blade then by powers older than the kingdom of Eorl. The warriors of Dunland have fallen or fled, and those that remain have thrown down their weapons.\
\
'The battle for Helm's Deep is over, and Théoden has emerged into the sunlight and victory. We will soon need to travel to Isengard, there to see what will become of Saruman now that his army is defeated and his treacherous goals laid low.\
\
'But for now, there is the work of recovery to be done. We will nurse our wounds, tend to our fallen, and see what must be done in the Deep and in the ravaged fields of Rohan. I will call for you when the time has come to set our sights upon Isengard, and Saruman.'","'What has Gandalf been up to while the battle was underway, I wonder?'","'Most of the Dunlending warriors cast down their weapons when the horn of Helm Hammerhand rang through the Deep, ${PLAYER}. Even his memory is enough to fill them with fear.\
\
'I am having some difficulty convincing these warriors that their lives will be spared. I think Saruman painted for them a picture of my people rather different than the reality.'","Day has dawned, and with it comes new hope for Rohan.\
\
Thurketel has asked you to go out the front gate, and see what has become of the battle.","'The battle is ended, and so is my contest with Legolas! You stand before a victorious dwarf, ${PLAYER}!'\
\
Gimli laughs heartily.\
\
'You were quite a help within the caves, my friend, and I thank you for the aid. The fighting was thick, and the outcome was not certain. But we triumphed, and now the light of day banishes the fears of the night. I am glad we are here to see it!'","Day has dawned, and with it comes new hope for Rohan.\
\
Éomer is on the field of battle, trying to accept the surrender of some surviving Dunlending warriors.","'The day is won! Go out the gates and find the King on the field of victory!'","'Saruman told many lies to drive the men of Dunland against us.'","You have found Aragorn and Théoden, astride their steeds, on the field of victory","Talk to Théoden on the field of victory","Day has dawned, and with it comes new hope for Rohan.\
\
Gandalf has arrived at Helm's Deep. What part did he play in the victory?","Talk to Gandalf on the field of victory","Talk to the frightened Dunlending warrior by Éomer","The Dunlending warrior stares at you suspiciously, and says nothing.","The Dunlending warrior stares at you with fear in his eyes.\
\
'I know what the horse-men do to their captives, and I will not let that happen to my men! This strawhead says they will be spared, but how can I trust this man, who weighs the value of a horse above that of his own children? The horse-men burn their captives alive, and feed upon the dead! Saruman saw it with his sorceries!'\
\
You assure the Dunlending warrior that this is simply one more lie of Saruman's, and that Éomer is a man of honour. The warrior's fear abates slightly, but it will take some more time before he is at ease. In time the lies of Saruman will be proven to be falsehoods. You leave Éomer to his charges.","'Éomer oversees the surrender of the surviving Dunlending warriors. Help him with his task. He seems to be having some difficulty.'","Day has dawned, and with it comes new hope for Rohan.\
\
Aragorn and Théoden are outside the walls of the Deep, on the field of victory.","The coming of the dawn has brought with it the end of the battle, and renewed the hopes of Rohan.","Talk to Aragorn on the field of victory","Talk to Éomer on the field of victory","'Dawn brings with it an end to our struggle, for now! Joyful sunrise!'\
\
Legolas grins at Gimli, and nods his head respectfully.\
\
'Gimli has won our little competition, for his tally exceeds mine by one. I begrudge him not the contest, for I was very worried when the fighting drove him back to the caves and none seemed to know his fate. But he tells me you were a staunch ally, ${PLAYER}, and I thank you for it. Doubtless you softened some of his foes, as well, and helped him win our competition! I forgive you for it, my friend! It was said only in jest, for the light of this morning seems more ripe for jesting than any we have seen of late!'","'What are those trees? Some sorcery of Gandalf, I warrant. Still I am glad of them, for they bear no love for the Orcs, and neither do I!'","Day has dawned, and with it comes new hope for Rohan.\
\
Gandalf is on the field of victory before the walls of Helm's Deep.","'I cannot believe our good fortune, ${PLAYER}! Dawn has come, and with it the renewal of our hopes! Go out the front gate of the fortress and see for yourself!'","Day has dawned, and with it comes new hope for Rohan.\
\
Éomer is overseeing the surrender of many Dunlendings following the battle.","Find Aragorn and Théoden on the field outside the gates","Day has dawned, and with it comes new hope for Rohan.\
\
Legolas and Gimli are somewhere on the field of victory.","Book 13, Chapter 11: Dawn Comes","'We have seen victory this day, ${PLAYER}! The Eorlingas rode forth from the gates, driving Orcs and wild men before them! I have never been so proud of my people as when they charged beside me into the mass of our foes. Many brave warriors perished this night, but the glory that is theirs can never be taken away. Rohan lives still because of their courage.\
\
'The Orcs fled before us, but they knew not what to make of the forest that lies now at Helm's Dike. Gandalf may know, for it seems a thing of sorcery. I know only that the wood is no friend to the Orcs, for none that passed that way have emerged.'","'What would Gandalf have to say about those trees, I wonder? They were not here when the sun set, but came with the dawning of the day. They have no love for the Orcs, that much is plain.'","Talk to Legolas on the field of victory"},
[1961]={"'Laerdan ha estado esperando noticias de tus esfuerzos. Deberías ir con él y contarle tus aventuras. Está en sus aposentos, en el primer piso de la Última Morada.\
\
'Ve con la buena voluntad de todos los Pueblos Libres.'","'Narchuil pronto será destruido, mi ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}...'","Habla con Laerdan","'Te agradezco nuevamente por traer noticias de tu encuentro con la sombra de Arvedui. Espero que su espíritu encuentre descanso tras su largo exilio.\
\
'Mientras tanto, Laerdan ha estado aguardando noticias de tus esfuerzos. Deberías ir con él y contarle tus aventuras. Está en sus aposentos, en el primer piso de la Última Morada.\
\
'Ve con la buena voluntad de todos los Pueblos Libres.'","Recuperaste la mitad perdida del anillo Narchuil y la devolviste a Elrond en Rivendel. Elrond te envió luego a hablar con Aragorn acerca de tu encuentro con la sombra de Arvedui, último rey de Arthedain.","Laerdan está en sus aposentos en la Última Morada.\
\
Aragorn te pidió que lo buscaras y le hablaras de tu investigación de Narchuil.","Libro 13, Capítulo 11: Narchuil Va al Sur","'¡Por fin! ¡El fragmento final de Narchuil ha sido hallado! Debo prepararme ahora para llevar el anillo hacia el sur... los planes están casi completos.\
\
'Tal vez me equivoqué al desear que Narchuil fuera reforjado. Ahora comprendo cuán peligrosa puede ser esta cosa. Debe ser destruido, y creo que hay un solo lugar donde eso puede hacerse.\
\
'No está lejos, pero creo que será peligroso. Los enemigos nos atacarán desde todos los lados, pero debemos triunfar. Ni Amarthiel ni Mordrambor deben recuperarlo. Por ahora, adiós, ${PLAYER}.'"},
[1962]={"Follow the road that runs from Helm's Dike to the Hornburg","Find Théoden and Éomer outside the keep of the Hornburg","Háma and Déorwine have a great deal to do to reinforce the guard-house","'You should climb to the top of the wall, and see the strength of our defence. The view will be a good one, as well. You should see it before the view is marred by the sight of ugly Orcs!'","Talk to Théoden outside the keep of the Hornburg","'You ride a fast steed, my friend! Were you able to be a help to my sister Éowyn? And how did you find my own home of Aldburg? Has Arcil maintained the village as well as his father once did?'\
\
You give Éomer what tidings you can in the little time you both have to spare.\
\
'I see. My uncle believes this battle will be over quickly, but I am not so certain. I hope he is right. There will be much work to do to restore the Mark, even once the fighting is done. But first we must survive the coming battle.'","Déorwine believes the guard-house doors will not last, if tested","Find the guard-house of the Hornburg","Talk to Gimli at Helm's Dike","You have arrived at Helm's Deep as the King's men prepare to defend the Hornburg.","Háma is neither confident nor without hope, but he seeks to make his father proud","Book 13, Chapter 1: The Lay of the Land","Legolas waves a greeting as you approach","'You should climb the wall and see how fare its defenders.'","Gimli is confident","Aragorn believes the Hornburg's defences are not strong enough","Thurketel sees you and heartily calls a greeting","Talk to Sigferth atop the wall","'We meet once more, my friend! If you seek battle, you have come to the right place, but if you seek a good rest or peaceful quiet you should leave this ravine at once! If the numbers reported by Théoden's scouts can be trusted, this entire gorge will be filled with Orcs before the moon is down.\
\
'From here I will have a clear shot upon any foe that seeks to cross the flat plain before the Deeping Wall. Every arrow I loose will spell death for one of our enemies, but which will I first exhaust: my arrows or our foes?\
\
'All of us will have our part to play during the coming night.'","'This is the home of Erkenbrand, but none know what has become of him. Now the King will rely on the walls of the Hornburg, and on the strong arms of his people. Will you help us defend the Deep?'\
\
Thurketel smiles when you say that you will.\
\
'The Hornburg has never fallen, and if fortune be with us I will one day tell my children and theirs that it still has not, even many years hence. This night may be its gravest test, and ours. May we be found sufficient!'","Talk to Háma at the guard-house of the Hornburg","'I am glad to see you, my well-travelled friend! My heart tells me we are in for a long night. The Men of Rohan have sheltered in the Hornburg before, and its walls have never failed them. I have seen many points of weakness already, and we have only been here a short while. We must ensure this fortress does not fall. If Rohan falls, I fear the rest of Middle-earth will not stand long.'","Sigferth is incredibly confident","Talk to Thurketel along the road from the Dike","Legolas fears he will run out of arrows before the battle is done","'Welcome to the Hornburg, ${PLAYER}. This is where I will make my stand. Let Saruman's armies come! They will break upon our walls and we will scatter them across the fields. There is no shortage of tasks to be done. The only thing we lack is time: the scouts tell me Saruman's forces will be here before the moon is high.'","The Deeping Wall provides a sturdy defence for the Hornburg, and allows its defenders a commanding view of the gorge.","'If Aragorn says our defences are not sufficient, I believe him. He is a strong man, and wiser than you might think to look at him.'","'Travel up the road and see the fortress, my friend. It is quite well-built, by the standards of men. Dwarves could do better, but is this not always true?'","'We are trying to reinforce the doors, but there is not enough sturdy wood in the Deep! Everything is either rotted or dry and old. Brittle wood will do us no good. We must hope that Gamling and the other soldiers are able to keep the armies of Saruman from breaching the Dike, for these doors will not keep them long.\
\
'Háma says I am wrong. I hope he is right.'","Théoden is confident the Hornburg will not be breached","Talk to Legolas atop the wall","Théoden and Éomer are overseeing the preparations outside the Hornburg.","A road runs from Helm's Dike through the valley and to the Hornburg.","Aragorn is outside the keep of the Hornburg, alongside Éomer and not far from Théoden.","'The Hornburg has never fallen to any enemies of the Mark. I pray we may still say this on the morrow!'","'We are well-met, my new friend! These are the times that prove the strength of our hearts, are they not? We are lucky to live in such times, for the opportunity to prove ourselves up to the task!\
\
'Saruman's Orcs will arrive at the Dike, and if they are not defeated outright, they will push into the space before our walls. We will whittle down their numbers with arrows and with thrown spears, and they will shake their blades and gnash their teeth and will have no choice but to turn away.\
\
'The Hornburg has never been breached. It will not be breached tonight, either!'","'Your friends can be found along the road from the Dike, and near the Hornburg. Speak to them and assess their moods.'","Talk to Déorwine at the guard-house of the Hornburg","'The tides of war bring you once again to the King's shore, ${PLAYER}! No, this time I will not take your weapons, or keep you from seeing Théoden. Now I am pleased you are here, and hope that your skill in battle is as great as I am told!'\
\
'Déorwine and I seek to reinforce the doors of this guard-house, but it is to be hoped that the forces of Saruman do not get this far into the Deep. Still, it is good to be prepared.'\
\
You tell Háma of your meeting with Léoferth, in Brockbridge, and the doorward sighs heavily.\
\
'Thank you for the news of my father. He has been in poor health for many years, but I am glad to know that he thinks of his son from time to time. He is often in my thoughts. If there is some measure of glory to be had in the hours ahead, I hope it is my lot to make Léoferth proud.'","'The armies of Saruman assaulted the men at the Fords of Isen, and the survivors of the rout are scattered now across the Westfold. No one seems to know where Erkenbrand might be found. He is the lord of the Hornburg, during time of peace, and would make his way here if he could.\
\
'Théoden King turned aside from his course and made for the Deep when the size of Saruman's force became clear. His army is already on the march, and will soon be here. I welcome all able folk willing to offer assistance, but I know you by reputation and count your aid double!\
\
'Friends of yours already lend us what help they can. You will find them in the Dike, throughout the Deep, and at the Hornburg.'","'Hail, friend! I knew you would not miss this chance! This dwarf has had enough of running, and riding, and talking! Now is the time for fighting, and quite a battle it is shaping up to be, too!\
\
'The walls of the fortress seem very sturdy, and the men say that the Deep has never been taken by an enemy. Aye, and may it not be taken this time, either, but I tell you true that I will be a mite disappointed if my axe sees little use. There are Orc necks to hew, and I am just the dwarf to do it!\
\
'I expect you will find Legolas atop the fortress wall. He would prefer a nice long view of the approaching Orcs, whereas I want to see their ugly faces up close!'","Éomer is worried that the battle will be neither easy nor quick","Thurketel is confident","Find Legolas atop the Deeping Wall","'Aragorn tells me the defences of the Hornburg are not strong enough. Speak to him and learn what he means by this.'","Talk to Éomer outside the keep of the Hornburg","The guard-house provides a sturdy defence for the Hornburg.","Talk to Aragorn outside the keep of the Hornburg","There is a maelstrom of activity outside the walls of the Hornburg","'Aragorn and the King are outside the keep of the Hornburg, seeing to the preparations. You should ask them if there is aught you can do to help. There is sure to be something you can do.'"},
[1963]={"Laerdan está en sus aposentos, en el primer piso de la Última Morada.\
\
Elrond te ha pedido que hables con Laerdan y averigües qué curso de acción piensa seguir.","Libro 13, Capítulo 1: El Camino hacia el Norte","'No sé qué destino aguarda a Laerdan...'","'${PLAYER}, estos últimos días han sido inquietantes. El Consejo de Narchuil no terminó como yo habría deseado, pero no negaré a Laerdan la búsqueda que ansía. Sin embargo, temo que pueda partir de Rivendel siguiendo un camino impulsivo.\
\
'¿Hablarías con él por mí? Averigua qué planea hacer y con qué propósito. No creo que Narmeleth pueda ser recuperada jamás, pues un poder oscuro domina su mente. Siento la influencia de una Fuerza mayor que la de un simple anillo menor.\
\
'Encontrarás a Laerdan en sus aposentos, en el piso inferior de mi casa. Con tu ayuda, espero que Laerdan actúe con mayor sabiduría en sus decisiones.'","Habla con Laerdan","El Consejo de Narchuil no terminó como Elrond había previsto, y teme que Laerdan pueda actuar con precipitación en su búsqueda de Narchuil.","'Temo que el camino que Laerdan ha tomado solo nos traerá pesar... y ya hemos tenido más que suficiente.'","'¿Quieres saber qué camino he decidido tomar? Muy bien. Dije al Consejo que Narchuil nunca sería reforjado, pero creo que mis palabras pudieron haber sido apresuradas.\
\
'Ya no creo que el anillo se hundiera con Arvedui en la Bahía Helada de Forochel. Aearil, uno de los miembros de la tripulación, conocía Narchuil y su poder. No creo que hubiera permitido que una reliquia tan preciada de mi casa se hundiera en el Mar.\
\
'Por esa razón, regresaré yo mismo a Forochel para buscar el anillo. Puedes acompañarme si lo deseas... así quizá las preocupaciones de Elrond se verán aliviadas.'","'Encontrarás a Laerdan en sus aposentos, en el piso inferior de mi casa. Con tu ayuda, espero que actúe con mayor sabiduría en sus decisiones.'"},
[1964]={"Laerdan está en sus aposentos, en el primer piso de la Última Morada.\
\
Elrond te ha pedido que hables con Laerdan y averigües qué curso de acción piensa seguir.","Libro 13, Capítulo 1: El Camino hacia el Norte","'No sé qué destino aguarda a Laerdan...'","'${PLAYER}, estos últimos días han sido inquietantes. El Consejo de Narchuil no terminó como yo habría deseado, pero no negaré a Laerdan la búsqueda que ansía. Sin embargo, temo que pueda partir de Rivendel siguiendo un camino impulsivo.\
\
'¿Hablarías con él por mí? Averigua qué planea hacer y con qué propósito. No creo que Narmeleth pueda ser recuperada jamás, pues un poder oscuro domina su mente. Siento la influencia de una Fuerza mayor que la de un simple anillo menor.\
\
'Encontrarás a Laerdan en sus aposentos, en el piso inferior de mi casa. Con tu ayuda, espero que Laerdan actúe con mayor sabiduría en sus decisiones.'","'Me temo que el camino que ha tomado Laerdan solo nos traerá dolor... y de eso ya hemos tenido más que suficiente'","Habla con Laerdan","El Consejo de Narchuil no terminó como Elrond había previsto, y teme que Laerdan pueda actuar con precipitación en su búsqueda de Narchuil.","'¿Quieres saber qué camino he decidido tomar? Muy bien. Dije al Consejo que Narchuil nunca sería reforjado, pero creo que mis palabras pudieron haber sido apresuradas.\
\
'Ya no creo que el anillo se hundiera con Arvedui en la Bahía Helada de Forochel. Aearil, uno de los miembros de la tripulación, conocía Narchuil y su poder. No creo que hubiera permitido que una reliquia tan preciada de mi casa se hundiera en el Mar.\
\
'Por esa razón, regresaré yo mismo a Forochel para buscar el anillo. Puedes acompañarme si lo deseas... así quizá las preocupaciones de Elrond se verán aliviadas.'"},
[1965]={"You can use one of the mats near Aragorn to sort the iron goods contributed by the farmers of Westfold.","Book 13, Chapter 2: Final Preparations","Pick up one of the training dummies near Éomer","Legolas is atop the wall.\
\
You have carried a training dummy to the top of the wall and Legolas has caught your eye.","Éomer has asked you to carry one of the nearby training dummies up to the wall by Legolas, the better to draw fire away from the defenders.","Gamling is at Helm's Dike.\
\
There is always work to be done to get ready for battle, and Gamling will tell you what he needs.","'You should return to Aragorn outside the keep of the Hornburg and see what else needs to be done.'","'Weapons are in short supply here. Erkenbrand had a small amount for the garrison, but his men took most of the weapons and armour with them when they rode to the Fords, and most of them have not returned. Théoden has called for the people of the Westfold to send as many iron goods as they can spare to the Deep. It is not much, but we may be able to fashion weapons and crude armour from these iron goods in the hours we have before the battle is joined.\
\
'Search through one of the barrels of iron goods, and sort its contents on the nearby mat. Any strong iron could be useful, but we need to know what we have available.'","'Éomer has had a very cunning idea. I think you should speak with him and help carry it out. It is very clever and may save some lives before the Orcs realize what we have done.'","'We have been fortunate so far, ${PLAYER}. Farmers of Westfold have brought more iron goods for us to use. Carry one of these barrels of iron goods to your friend Aragorn, outside the walls of the Hornburg. He has been sorting through the barrels for anything of use in preparing the defences.'","Corudan has gone down to the Dike, beyond the walls of the Hornburg.\
\
Legolas told you that Corudan planned to scout the armies of Saruman, and you should speak to him before he leaves.","'I will see you again. I will only be gone for a short time, and will return before the battle is joined.'","Gamling has asked you to carry a barrel of iron goods from Helm's Dike to Aragorn outside the keep of the Hornburg.","'There you are, my friend! I am glad to see you before I leave. I am going to ride from the Dike and see what I can tell of Saruman's forces. There may be some weakness in their ranks we will be able to exploit, but until I see his armies on the march all we have is rumour and fear. I will return before long, and tell you what I have seen.\
\
'Do not fear! I will return before the battle is joined, and perhaps with news that can help us. Stand strong and inspire the Men of Rohan, ${PLAYER}! I know you will not let them down.'","With all of the goods set on the mat, you see one or two useable pieces","'Aragorn will be pleased to receive another barrel of iron goods. Bring it to him outside the keep of the Hornburg.'","Retrieve iron goods from a barrel near Aragorn, outside the keep of the Hornburg","'I have had an idea, friend. While watching the men training, I realized something interesting: from a great distance, I could not tell if a man was training with a straw dummy or if his opponent was merely parrying his blows without a great deal of motion. If I, with the keen eyes of my people, could not tell the difference, what would one of Saruman's ill-bred minions make of it?\
\
'I think we should carry some training dummies to the top of the wall, ${PLAYER}. It will make our numbers seem the greater, and any arrow wasted upon a dummy is one which could have struck a fighting man. That is a trade worth any amount of heavy lifting!'","Talk to Corudan by his horse at Helm's Dike","Talk to Legolas atop the wall","'I am glad more barrels of iron are coming into the Deep, but there is no certainty that we will be able to make use of their contents. It is worth the wager. Thank you for bringing this all the way here.'","With a third of the goods set out on the mat, you see little of use","'You should check on your Elf friend atop the wall, where you brought the training dummy.'","'The farmers of Westfold have contributed barrels of iron goods. Sort through the iron goods on the nearby mats, for there may be some use we can make of their contents.'","Aragorn is outside the keep of the Hornburg, and wishes to speak with you.","With most of the goods set on the mat, you still see little of use","Pick up the barrel of iron goods near Gamling, in Helm's Dike","You retrieve a pile of iron goods from the barrel","'Use the mat right over there to sort through the iron goods contributed by the farmers of Westfold. There may be something we can use in the defence, and if there is I want to be certain we find it.'","Talk to Gamling at Helm's Dike","Barrels of iron goods from the farmers of Westfold can be found outside the keep of the Hornburg, near Aragorn.\
\
Aragorn has asked you to sort through an iron goods barrel using one of the nearby sorting mats.","Use the mat near Aragorn to sort through the iron goods","Talk to Éomer outside the keep of the Hornburg","Talk to Aragorn outside the keep of the Hornburg","Aragorn is desperate to ensure that the Hornburg is well-defended before Saruman's forces arrive.","'Corudan wished to speak with you before he left to scout the forces of Saruman. He said he would wait for you at Helm's Dike.'","Éomer is outside the keep of the Hornburg.","'I think we should carry some training dummies to the top of the wall, ${PLAYER}. It will make our numbers seem the greater, and any arrow wasted upon a dummy is one which could have struck a fighting man. That is a trade worth any amount of heavy lifting! Pick up one of the dummies and carry it to the top of the wall by your friend Legolas.'","You set down the barrel of iron goods, and Aragorn nods gratefully","You set the dummy atop the wall and hope it will draw fire away from the defenders","'That is a clever idea, if it proves successful. Unless Saruman's armies turn aside for some reason I cannot tell, they will arrive at the Deep during the hours of darkness. They will not be able to tell the difference between these dummies and the defenders atop the wall until they get very near to the wall. And by then I will have claimed many lives of Orcs.\
\
'I spoke for a time with your friend Corudan. I met his sister when we stayed in Lothlórien. If Sigileth were here, with her deadly knives, the Orcs would have a great deal to fear! While I am wishing for unlikely happenstance, why not hope for the arrival of an army of my own kin? That would be a sight indeed! But they are far from here, and have their own concerns and their own lands to defend. The Rohirrim are on their own. They will have to make do with two Elves, one dwarf, and two Men.\
\
'Speaking of Corudan, he wanted me to send you to him. He rode down to the Dike, and said he wished to see the approaching armies with his own eyes.'"},
[1966]={"'Conozco a un enano que comercia en las regiones meridionales de Forochel. Quizá él pueda darte alguna idea de por dónde comenzar la búsqueda.\
\
'Puedes encontrar a Dáthi en Kauppa-kohta, en Taur Orthon. Él conoce mejor Forochel —si puede decirse tal cosa— que yo.'","'¡Eh, tú! ¿Dices venir de parte de Laerdan el Elfo? Sí, estuvo aquí hace algún tiempo, buscando un anillo perdido o algo por el estilo, pero sin éxito. ¿Puedes imaginarte buscar un anillo en las nieves de Forochel?\
\
'Aun así, quizá su búsqueda no fuese tan insensata como pensé al principio, pues Hombres de Angmar han pasado por esta región, y con ellos otros que jamás había visto. Me recordaron a los Hombres de Gondor, pero más extraños. También buscan algo aquí, y puede que vuestras búsquedas estén relacionadas.\
\
'Si deseas encontrar tu anillo perdido, debes hablar con los Hombres de las Nieves, los Lossoth, que se llaman a sí mismos los Lumi-väki. Esta es su tierra y la conocen mejor que nadie. Te recomiendo hablar con Lassi en Sûri-kylä, pues él conoce mejor que nadie el pensamiento de su caudillo.'","'Si deseas encontrar tu anillo perdido, debes hablar con los Hombres de las Nieves, los Lossoth, que se llaman a sí mismos los Lumi-väki. Esta es su tierra y la conocen mejor que nadie. Te recomiendo hablar con Lassi en Sûri-kylä, pues él conoce mejor que nadie el pensamiento de su caudillo.'","Una sombra de duda se cierne sobre Laerdan, y teme abandonar Rivendel en busca de Narchuil.","'Si deseas encontrar tu anillo, necesitarás la ayuda de los Lossoth.'","Habla con Lassi","Habla con Dáthi","'La Última Morada se está convirtiendo rápidamente en una prisión para mí. No me siento bienvenido aquí. Y, sin embargo, tampoco siento que sea correcto marcharme todavía. Temo que, si abandono estos salones, nunca regrese, y no deseo partir con tanta amargura.\
\
'¿Podrías continuar mi búsqueda hasta que llegue el momento en que pueda irme con la conciencia tranquila? Conozco a un enano que comercia en las regiones meridionales de Forochel. Quizá él tenga alguna idea de por dónde deberías comenzar la búsqueda.\
\
'Puedes encontrar a Dáthi en Kauppa-kohta, en Taur Orthon. Él sabe más sobre Forochel —si puede decirse tal cosa de alguien— que yo.'","Dáthi está en Kauppa-kohta, en la tierra de Forochel, al norte de Evendim y más allá de la Puerta del Norte.\
\
Laerdan te ha pedido que vayas a Forochel y hables con el comerciante enano Dáthi. Puede que el enano sepa por dónde comenzar la búsqueda de Narchuil.","Lassi está en Sûri-kylä, al norte y al este a lo largo de la Bahía de Hielo de Forochel.\
\
Dáthi te habló de la última visita de Laerdan y de la llegada de los Angmarim. Te dijo que hablaras con Lassi si esperas recuperar Narchuil antes que los Angmarim.","Libro 13, Capítulo 2: Los Hombres de las Nieves de Forochel","'Eres ${PLAYERNAME:un desconocido[m]|una desconocida[f]} aquí, ${PLAYERNAME:un[m]|una[f]}  del Sur. Vemos muy pocos de los tuyos, y recibimos aún menos...'"},
[1967]={"'Ahora puedes regresar con Sini. Has hecho un buen trabajo.'","Libro 13, Capítulo 3: Favor de la Resistencia","Para obtener el favor de Yrjänä, debes realizar tres tareas para el pueblo Lossoth.","'Si puedes encontrar a Urmas, uno de mis mejores rastreadores, ganarás el favor de los míos. Ve a las tierras salvajes y busca a Urmas... si lo encuentras, vuelve conmigo.\
\
'Urmas fue visto por última vez yendo hacia el sur por el camino en Itä-mâ.'","Sini está en las afueras de Sûri-kylä.\
\
Has encontrado a Urmas y ahora deberías volver con Sini para informar de tu éxito.","Urmas encontrado","'Sini puede tener una tarea para ti. La encontrarás en las afueras de Sûri-kylä.'","Sini está en las afueras de Sûri-kylä.\
\
Lassi te indicó que hablaras con Sini sobre las tareas necesarias para obtener el favor de Yrjänä.","'Se requiere gran resistencia y entereza para sobrevivir en la fría naturaleza con tan poco. Te otorgo el Favor de la Resistencia, aunque no será suficiente por sí solo para obtener todo el favor de Yrjänä. Puede que otros también necesiten tu ayuda.'","Urmas fue visto por última vez dirigiéndose hacia el sur, en dirección a Itä-mâ.\
\
Sini te ha pedido que te adentres en lo salvaje para encontrar a Urmas.","'¿Deseas el favor de Yrjänä? Entonces debes ganártelo, y en eso puedo ayudarte. Los Lumi-väki valoran muchas cualidades, pero una de las más importantes es la resistencia.\
\
'A menudo, nuestros cazadores deben sobrevivir en la fría naturaleza con nada más que un cuchillo sin filo y la ropa que llevan encima. Si puedes encontrar a Urmas, uno de mis mejores rastreadores, ganarás gran favor ante los ojos de mi pueblo. Ve a las tierras salvajes y busca a Urmas; si lo encuentras, vuelve aquí conmigo.\
\
'Urmas fue visto por última vez yendo hacia el sur por el camino en Itä-mâ.'","Encuentra a Urmas","Habla con Sini"},
[1968]={"'Busca a Emeli, frente a la cabaña de vapor. Puede tener una tarea para ti que te ayudará a obtener el favor de Yrjänä.'","'¿Buscas el favor de los Lumi-väki? No es asunto trivial, pues desconfiamos de la mayoría de los tuyos. Si deseas ganar el favor de Yrjänä, debes realizar una hazaña de fuerza que rivalice con la de los cazadores de los Lumi-väki.\
\
'Durante mucho tiempo, nuestros cazadores han buscado al sierpe de nieve Paksu-karva. Yrjänä deseaba hacer de su colmillo un gran cuerno, pero Paksu-karva ha eludido a nuestros cazadores cada vez.\
\
'Ve y encuentra a Paksu-karva y tráeme su colmillo, y obtendrás mi favor. Solo entonces podrás hablar con Yrjänä. El gusano de nieve fue visto por última vez entre otros gusanos cerca de la bahía; merodean al sureste de aquí.'","'Ve y encuentra a Paksu-karva y tráeme su colmillo, y obtendrás mi favor. Solo entonces podrás hablar con Yrjänä. El sierpe de nieve fue visto por última vez entre otros gusanos cerca de la bahía; merodean al sureste de aquí.'","Emeli está cerca de la entrada de Sûri-kylä.\
\
Debes buscar a Emeli si deseas obtener el favor de la fortaleza.","Para obtener el favor de Yrjänä, debes realizar tres tareas para el pueblo Lossoth.","Recolecta el colmillo de Paksu-karva","Libro 13, Capítulo 3: Favor de la Fortaleza","'Así que has obtenido el Favor de la Fortaleza... estoy impresionado.'","Entrega el colmillo de Paksu-karva a Emeli","Habla con Emeli","'Has logrado lo que los cazadores de los Lumi-väki no pudieron y me has traído el colmillo de Paksu-karva. Te otorgo el Favor de la Fortaleza, aunque no será suficiente por sí solo para obtener el favor completo de Yrjänä.'","Emeli está en Sûri-kylä, frente a la cabaña de vapor.\
\
Debes devolverle a Emeli el colmillo de Paksu-karva como señal de tu éxito.","Paksu-karva fue visto por última vez entre sierpes al sureste, a lo largo de la Bahía Helada.\
\
Emeli te pidió que busques a Paksu-karva y le lleves su colmillo como prueba de que has completado la hazaña de fuerza requerida.","Colmillo de Paksu-karva recogido"},
[1969]={"'Si deseas ganar el favor de Yrjänä, debes hablar con Jalmari en Sûri-kylä, cerca de la cabaña de vapor. Él te guiará en tu camino.'","Jalmari está en Sûri-kylä, cerca de la cabaña de vapor.\
\
Debes volver con Jalmari con la solución a su acertijo.","Libro 13, Capítulo 3: Favor de la Sabiduría","'Has tenido sabiduría al seguir mi guía.'","'Con sabiduría te enviaron a mí, y solo con sabiduría obtendrás el favor de los Lumi-väki. Yrjänä no hablará contigo hasta que hayas ganado el Favor de la Sabiduría, que te otorgaré cuando completes mi tarea.\
\
'Mira junto a mí. Allí encontrarás cosas importantes para los Lumi-väki, cosas que nos permiten sobrevivir en estas tierras heladas. Pon estas cosas en su orden correcto y luego regresa a mí. ¿Cómo sabrás cuál es el orden correcto? Con sabiduría, por supuesto.\
\
'El calor es de gran importancia en estas tierras congeladas, así que el fuego es un compañero valioso. Aún más importante es el agua, porque sin agua no hay vida.\
\
'Una vez que tengas fuego y agua a tu alcance, habrás hecho mucho, pero ¡no descanses todavía! Debes tener armas resistentes para protegerte, pero primero obtén alimentos suficientes que te den la fuerza para empuñarlas.\
\
'Pero antes de obtener cualquiera de estas cosas necesarias, un viajero en estas tierras debe tener ropa lo suficientemente abrigada para protegerse del frío cuando no puede encender fuego ni encontrar agua.'","Elige el primer objeto","Elige el tercer objeto","Elige el segundo objeto","Elige el quinto objeto","Elige el cuarto objeto","Para obtener el favor de Yrjänä, debes completar tres tareas para el pueblo Lossoth.","Los objetos se encuentran junto a Jalmari.\
\
Jalmari te ha pedido que uses sabiduría para ordenar ciertos objetos importantes para los Lossoth. Te dijo lo siguiente sobre ellos:\
\
'El calor es de gran importancia en estas tierras congeladas, así que el fuego es un compañero valioso. Aún más importante es el agua, porque sin agua no hay vida.\
\
'Aun con fuego y agua a tu alcance, estas tierras no son seguras. Una persona sabia llevará consigo armas resistentes para protegerse, aunque primero debe tener alimentos suficientes para darle la fuerza necesaria para manejarlas.\
\
'Sobre todo, un viajero en estas tierras debe tener ropa lo suficientemente abrigada para protegerse del frío cuando no puede encender fuego.'","'¡Has terminado! ¿Y qué has aprendido?\
\
'En efecto, ese es el orden correcto. Escuchaste con sabiduría, así que te otorgaré el Favor de la Sabiduría. Esto por sí solo no te dará el favor total de Yrjänä, pero es un comienzo firme.'","Jalmari está en Sûri-kylä, cerca de la cabaña de vapor.\
\
Lassi te indicó que hablaras con Jalmari para recibir su guía y así ganarte el favor de Yrjänä.","'Pon estas cosas en su orden correcto y luego regresa a mí. ¿Cómo sabrás cuál es el orden correcto? Con sabiduría, por supuesto.\
\
'El calor es de gran importancia en estas tierras congeladas, así que el fuego es un compañero valioso. Aún más importante es el agua, porque sin agua no hay vida.\
\
'Una vez que tengas fuego y agua a tu alcance, habrás hecho mucho, pero ¡no descanses todavía! Debes tener armas resistentes para protegerte, pero primero obtén alimentos suficientes que te den la fuerza para empuñarlas.\
\
'Pero antes de obtener cualquiera de estas cosas necesarias, un viajero en estas tierras debe tener ropa lo suficientemente abrigada para protegerse del frío cuando no puede encender fuego ni encontrar agua.'","Habla con Jalmari","'Si deseas obtener el favor de Yrjänä, debes hablar con Jalmari en Sûri-kylä, cerca de la cabaña de vapor. Él te guiará en tu camino.'"},
[1970]={"'¡Has demostrado tu valía ante los Lumi-väki!'","Los Lossoth son un pueblo desconfiado y no te ayudarán a menos que ganes el favor de su caudillo, Yrjänä.","Libro 13, Capítulo 3: El Favor del Caudillo","'${PLAYERNAME:Bienvenido, extraño del sur[m]|Bienvenida, extraña del sur[f]}. Has demostrado gran valía ante los Lumi-väki y has ganado mi favor. ¿En qué podemos ayudarte?'","Yrjänä está en la Gran Cabaña de Sûri-kylä.\
\
Ahora que has completado las tareas requeridas, deberías hablar con Yrjänä.","'¡Tienes mucha dignidad y honor!'","Obtén el Favor de la Fortaleza","Habla con Yrjänä","Obtén el Favor de la Resistencia","'Recordamos a ese Vanha-väki del que hablas, ese Laerdan. Vino ante los Lumi-väki buscando un anillo perdido. Fue una tontería, buscar una baratija en estas tierras. No deberías ser tan insensato.\
\
'El Vanha-väki no obtuvo el favor de Yrjänä y apenas escapó con vida de los peligros que enfrentamos aquí. Sin la ayuda de los Lumi-väki no tendrías esperanza alguna de encontrar tu anillo, y no tendrás la ayuda de los Lumi-väki sin el favor de Yrjänä.\
\
'Si deseas ganar el favor de nuestro caudillo, debes realizar tres tareas para los Lumi-väki. Solo entonces podrás hablar con Yrjänä. Si deseas conocer estas tareas, vuelve a hablar conmigo.'","Obtén el Favor de la Sabiduría","Jalmari está dentro de Sûri-kylä, cerca de la cabaña de vapor. Emeli está frente a la cabaña de vapor. Sini se encuentra en las afueras de Sûri-kylä.\
\
Lassi te ha dicho que debes completar tres tareas antes de poder hablar con Yrjänä. Si deseas saber más, deberías volver a hablar con él."},
[1971]={"Aragorn speaks to you in hushed tones.\
\
'The next few hours will sorely test us all, my friend, but none more than the King of Rohan. It will be Théoden's resolve, as much as the strength of his fighting men, that will govern our chances of survival. He will not speak plainly to me, or to any of us, on this matter. It is not his way, nor the way of most who rule.\
\
'Find Gléowine and ask him what he makes of the King's mood and temperament. I cannot tell if the King is putting on a brave face, but Gléowine has served him for many years and will know better than I the truth of this. I last saw the minstrel below us, by a pile of straw near the western wall.'","As the night deepens, battle approaches the defenders of the Hornburg.","'Thank you for the lesson in strategy and tactics, my friend. I cannot say the lesson will remain long in this old head of mine, but for now I feel glad having learned something of what awaits us here.\
\
'But look! It is Gamling, from the Dike. He seeks our help!'\
\
<rgb=#FFFF00><b>Interact with Gamling to experience 'Epic Battles: Basic Training,' the tutorial for the Epic Battles system, if you are interested in the Epic Battles system. The tutorial is optional, and can be skipped if you intend to play the Storied Tales in Helm's Deep.</b></rgb>","'I saw the King not long ago, and he seems to be in fine spirits, ${PLAYER}. He is not blind to the danger, but he does not ignore it, either. His is not bravery without cause, but courage based on confidence in his men and his own strength. He sheltered too long in his own hall, and now that he emerges and sees battle he is ready for it.\
\
'I do not think Aragorn should worry about my King. Théoden will surprise him, when the battle is upon us. Ah, I speak of battle, but I am a minstrel and know little of strategy or tactics. You have seen more of war than I have, and this old man counts himself fortunate! There is a map on the table over there. Will you show to me how the attack will progress, while we wait?'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Interacting with the map table near Gléowine will allow time to pass. Action will resume after midnight, when the battle is joined.</rgb>","'I think battle is almost upon us. If you are willing to stand with my men, come with me to hold Helm's Dike for as long as we are able!'","Gamling gestures at you, and seeks to catch his breath","Gléowine is on the lowest level of the fortress, by a pile of straw near the west wall.\
\
Aragorn wants to determine the mood of Théoden, but has sent you not to the King but to Gléowine to learn it.","Talk to Gléowine near the map table by the western wall","'Gamling has come from the Dike, and he seeks our aid! Speak to him and find out what we can do! There is little hope we can hold that pass for long, but standing for even a short while may save some lives.'\
\
<rgb=#FFFF00><b>Interact with Gamling to experience 'Epic Battles: Basic Training,' the tutorial for the Epic Battles system, if you are interested in the Epic Battles system. The tutorial is optional, and can be skipped if you intend to play the Storied Tales in Helm's Deep.</b></rgb>","'You have seen more of war than I have, and this old man counts himself fortunate! There is a map on the table over there. Will you show to me how the attack will progress, while we wait?'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Interacting with the map table near Gléowine will allow time to pass. Action will resume after midnight, when the battle is joined.</rgb>","Talk to Gléowine, by the map table near the western wall, after midnight","The sound of fighting reaches your ears... the battle is joined!","Book 13, Chapter 3: Night Deepens","It is after midnight at Helm's Deep.\
\
Gamling is by the map table with Gléowine, on the lowest level of the fortress, by the western wall.","It is after midnight at Helm's Deep.\
\
Gléowine is by the map table, near the pile of straw by the western wall.","Talk to Gamling by the pile of straw near the western wall","'You will find Gléowine below us, by the western wall. Ask him what he makes of Théoden's mood and temperament. We will need the King to be strong of will if we are to survive what this night promises.'","Study the map table near the western wall, by Gléowine, and time will pass","Gléowine wants you to show him on the nearby map table what the night may hold for the defenders of Helm's Deep.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Interacting with the map table near Gléowine will allow time to pass. Action will resume after midnight, when the battle is joined.</rgb>"},
[1972]={"'The time passed slowly here atop the wall when the noise from the Dike reached us. I saw the Orc torches go out when they sought to pass the breach, and then scatter when they met resistance. You fought at the Dike? That was well-done, ${PLAYER}! It was a mere taste of what is to come on this night, but you and the men did what needed to be done: you taught our foes that we will not give them one foot more without battle.\
\
'Now the battle is before the Deeping Wall, and it is a time for arrows and for stones! Gimli's axe thirsts for Orc-necks, but it will not thirst long!'","'Your friends wait for you on the Deeping Wall. Go to them while there is still time! They may have need of you!'","'You fought well, my new friend, and claimed the lives of many foes! The Dike is filled with the bodies of Orcs, but still others come, clambering onto the bank. We slowed them. That is what we sought to do. It was foolhardy to expect to do more. Take the eastern stairs and climb onto the Deeping Wall, ${PLAYER}. Your friends will be in the thick of the fighting before long, and they will want you by their side!'","Book 13, Chapter 4: Helm's Dike","Talk to Thenca and complete 'Storied Tale: Helm's Dike' <rgb=#00FF00>OR</rgb> complete 'Helm's Dike' from the Epic Battles Panel","'We cannot hold the Dike indefinitely. But we will make them fight for it, will we not? Aye, we will! Come with me and let us stand against the vanguard!'\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>There are two ways to participate in the defence of Helm's Dike. You can speak to Thenca for the Storied Tale, a story-focused experience. Or you can use the Epic Battles Panel for a more gameplay-intensive experience.</rgb>\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>To participate in the defence of Helm's Dike, open the Epic Battles Panel and select 'Helm's Dike' from the menu. After you successfully complete the defence, you will be returned to the location from which you entered it.</rgb>","It is after midnight at Helm's Deep.\
\
Gimli and Legolas are on the Deeping Wall. Gamling told you to take the eastern stairs up onto the wall in order to reach them.","Talk to Legolas on the Deeping Wall","'We may have a problem, my friend.'","Talk to Gimli on the Deeping Wall","'Look at them down there! Ha! Come up here, you cowards!'","Helm's Dike is under attack, and Gamling seeks your help in defending it from Saruman's forces.","It is after midnight at Helm's Deep.\
\
Aragorn wishes to speak with you atop the Deeping Wall.","'Our foes are numerous, and now they are here. The next few hours will be trying indeed.'","Gamling has asked for your help defending Helm's Dike.\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>There are two ways to participate in the defence of Helm's Dike. You can speak to Thenca for the Storied Tale, a story-focused experience. Or you can use the Epic Battles Panel for a more gameplay-intensive experience.</rgb>\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>To participate in the defence of Helm's Dike, open the Epic Battles Panel and select 'Helm's Dike' from the menu. After you successfully complete the defence, you will be returned to the location from which you entered it.</rgb>","'Let us hurry to Helm's Dike! If we have victory there, perhaps we can slow or stop the advance of the Orcs!'","Talk to Aragorn on the Deeping Wall","'I am no fool. Even if Saruman's forces were a quarter of the size the scouts say they are, I know we cannot hold the Dike indefinitely. But we will make them fight for it, will we not? Aye, we will! Come with me and let us stand against the vanguard!'\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>There are two ways to participate in the defence of Helm's Dike. You can speak to Thenca for the Storied Tale, a story-focused experience. Or you can use the Epic Battles Panel for a more gameplay-intensive experience.</rgb>\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>To participate in the defence of Helm's Dike, open the Epic Battles Panel and select 'Helm's Dike' from the menu. After you successfully complete the defence, you will be returned to the location from which you entered it.</rgb>","'It has begun, friend! Now is the time for battle! The Orcs fill the gorge before the wall. Just look at them down there! I have never seen so many of the foul creatures in one place. There are Dunlending wild-men down there too. Every now and then I can hear one of their war-cries over the rest of the tumult.\
\
'We must stand and fight!'","Talk to Gamling by the pile of straw near the western wall","It is after midnight at Helm's Deep.\
\
Gamling is by the pile of straw on the lower level of the fortress, by the western wall."},
[1973]={"'¿Estás ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para enfrentar a tu adversario?'","'Puede que el Rey Brujo ya no reine desde Carn Dûm, pero su voluntad aún guía el mal que habita allí. No podemos ayudarte.'","'Y así está, ${RACE}. Los siervos de la Corona de Hierro se alzan contra ti. Debe ponerse fin a las maldades de Angmar, pero mi pueblo no te ayudará mientras esta sombra se cierna sobre nosotros.\
\
'Hay, sin embargo, alguien que podría ayudarte...","'Has ganado el favor de los Lumi-väki, pero no eres ${PLAYERNAME:el único[m]|la única[f]} que ha venido buscando nuestra ayuda para encontrar este anillo. ¿Por qué es tan importante? No, no hables de ello... temo que solo traería un viento oscuro sobre nosotros.\
\
'Primero vino el Vanha-väki, Laerdan, y luego tú, pero hay otro que espera una audiencia conmigo. Hace afirmaciones poderosas... ¿vendrás conmigo a tratar con él? Debes conocer la reclamación que hace sobre el anillo.\
\
'Pero esperaremos hasta que estés ${PLAYERNAME:preparado[m]|preparada[f]}. Cuando estés ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]}, vuelve a hablar conmigo.'","Ve con Yrjänä a encontrarte con tu rival","Habla con Yrjänä","Completaste las tres tareas que te encomendaron los Lossoth, ganando su favor y el derecho de hablar con Yrjänä.","Yrjänä está en la Gran Cabaña de Sûri-kylä.\
\
Debes hablar con Yrjänä acerca de las amenazas de Mordrambor.","Libro 13, Capítulo 4: La Mano de Angmar","Yrjänä está en la Gran Cabaña de Sûri-kylä.\
\
Yrjänä te informó de que otro ha venido reclamando Narchuil y buscando la ayuda de los Lossoth para encontrarlo."},
[1975]={"Habla con Arvedui","Arvedui ronda los restos de un gran barco élfico congelado en la Bahía Helada de Forochel.\
\
Has descubierto la sombra de Arvedui, último rey de Arthedain, rondando los restos del barco élfico que había venido a rescatarlo hace tanto tiempo. Puede que la sombra conozca el paradero de Narchuil.","'¿Vienes de parte de Yrjänä? No temo a los moradores de piedra de Angmar. No pueden hacerme daño. Compartiré contigo la sabiduría que poseo.\
\
'Hace mucho, un rey del Sur vino a Forochel buscando refugio del Rey Brujo de Angmar. Arvedui era su nombre, pero lo llamamos el Rey Demacrado, pues estaba debilitado tras esconderse en antiguas minas de los enanos.\
\
'El Rey Demacrado suplicó ayuda a los Lossoth, y se le concedió, aunque con dudas, pues temíamos la ira del Rey Brujo. Permaneció con los Lossoth hasta que apareció un enorme monstruo marino en la Bahía Helada, llevando muchos Elfos sobre su lomo. Aconsejamos al Rey Demacrado no subir a la criatura y esperar al verano, cuando el poder del Rey Brujo sería menor. No escuchó, y las tormentas mataron a la bestia.\
\
'Se dice que el cuerpo de la bestia aún puede verse en la Bahía Helada, al norte y al este de aquí. Puede que halles en su cadáver el conocimiento que buscas.'","Habla con Saija","Busca el cuerpo del monstruo marino en la Bahía Helada de Forochel","'Llevo sobre mí un gran pesar.'","El Númenóreano Negro Mordrambor llegó a la aldea de los Lossoth exigiendo la lealtad de su pueblo, infundiendo temor en sus corazones.","'Encontrarás a Saija en Näky-kolo, al noroeste de Kuru-leiri; se halla en el borde occidental de la Bahía Helada. Es orgullosa y altiva, pero quizá en ella encuentres una aliada contra Mordrambor.\
\
'Ve, busca la sabiduría de los tiempos.'","Saija está en Näky-kolo, al noroeste de Kuru-leiri.\
\
Yrjänä te pidió que acudieras a la sabiduría de Saija para encontrar Narchuil.","'Existe una näkijä, una vidente, que vive fuera de la aldea. Es poderosa y no teme al Señor de las Tormentas. Puede que te ayude a encontrar tu anillo.\
\
'Encontrarás a Saija en Näky-kolo, al noroeste de Kuru-leiri; se halla en el borde occidental de la Bahía Helada. Es orgullosa y altiva, pero quizá en ella encuentres una aliada contra Mordrambor.\
\
'Ve, busca la sabiduría de los tiempos.'","'Se dice que el cuerpo de la bestia aún puede verse en la Bahía Helada, al norte y al este de aquí. Puede que halles en su cadáver el conocimiento que buscas.'","'No eres de los Lossoth, sino alguien procedente de mis tierras de antaño. ¿Qué buscas en este lugar terrible?'","El cuerpo del monstruo marino del que habló Saija yace en la Bahía Helada de Forochel, al este de Kuru-leiri.\
\
Saija te indicó que buscaras Narchuil, o noticias de él, sobre el cuerpo del monstruo marino visible en la Bahía Helada de Forochel.","Has encontrado a la sombra de Arvedui, último rey de Arthedain","Libro 13, Capítulo 5: El Mito del Monstruo"},
[1976]={"'We felt the blast from here, ${PLAYER}! I am glad you survived.\
\
'Our own sortie did not go well. The causeway is hard-pressed, and the hinges and bars of the main gates have greatly suffered. We scattered a number of Orcs who carried rams, and the archers supporting them, but our victory was short-lived. As we attempted to return, I was tripped by Orcs lying in ambush, and it nearly spelled my end.'","Aragorn has decided to lead a sortie through the postern gate in the Deeping Wall, in order to strike against the forces of Saruman.","It is after midnight at Helm's Deep.\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>There are two ways to participate in the defence of the Deeping Wall. You can speak to Thurketel for the Storied Tale, a story-focused experience. Or you can use the Epic Battles Panel for a more gameplay-intensive experience.</rgb>\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>To participate in the defence of the Deeping Wall, open the Epic Battles Panel and select 'The Deeping Wall' from the menu. After you successfully complete the defence, you will be returned to the location from which you entered it.</rgb>","Book 13, Chapter 6: Atop the Wall","It is after midnight at Helm's Deep. Rohirric Swordsmen can be found in the open space between the Hornburg and the Deeping Wall.\
\
Aragorn has asked you to gather swordsmen to accompany him on a sortie beyond the wall.","'Éomer is fortunate I was there!'","Talk to Legolas atop the Deeping Wall","'The Orcs are bringing up great ladders with which to scale the Deeping Wall! Prepare for battle!'","Find swordsmen and tell them to meet Aragorn at the postern gate (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","It is after midnight at Helm's Deep. Legolas is atop the Deeping Wall, accessible from ground-level by the eastern staircase.\
\
Aragorn has sent you to watch over the battle alongside Legolas.","'We need to set the forces of Saruman back on their heels, ${PLAYER}. Descend to the open space between the wall and the Hornburg, and speak with any swordsmen you see. Tell them to meet me by the postern gate. I wish to lead them on a sortie against the Orcs!'","'Return to Legolas and assist him with the defence of the Deeping Wall! We will strike a blow against the Orcs from the postern gate, and may it prove a worthy distraction!'","Talk to Aragorn by the postern gate below the north-west tower","'Éomer!' Aragorn cries, 'This is the hour in which we draw swords together!'","'I will go with Aragorn! This is the hour! We will teach the enemy a lesson in steel!'","Éomer is below the north-west tower, by the postern gate.\
\
You have survived an attack on the Deeping Wall, and should see how Éomer and Aragorn fared in their sortie.","It is after midnight at Helm's Deep. Aragorn and Éomer are by the postern gate, below the north-west tower.\
\
You have given word to several swordsmen that Aragorn plans a sortie through the postern gate, and should see if that be enough.","'These swordsmen will accompany me, ${PLAYER}, and Éomer has pledged his sword as well! But I wish for you to return to Legolas atop the wall and watch our sortie from above! There will be fighting enough for all of us, I do not doubt it!'","'Find swordsmen willing to accompany me on a sortie against the Orcs. Tell them to meet me at the postern gate, if they are able and ready!'","Talk to Éomer by the postern gate","'You have returned just in time, my friend! They prepare another assault!'\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>There are two ways to participate in the defence of the Deeping Wall. You can speak to Thurketel for the Storied Tale, a story-focused experience. Or you can use the Epic Battles Panel for a more gameplay-intensive experience.</rgb>\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>To participate in the defence of the Deeping Wall, open the Epic Battles Panel and select 'The Deeping Wall' from the menu. After you successfully complete the defence, you will be returned to the location from which you entered it.</rgb>","'We survived the assault, for now. Did Aragorn and Éomer fare as well as we did? Go to the postern gate in the north-west tower and see if their sortie led to victory.'","Talk to Thurketel and complete 'Storied Tale: The Deeping Wall' <rgb=#00FF00>OR</rgb> complete 'The Deeping Wall' from the Epic Battles Panel"},
[1977]={"'No perteneces a este lugar, mas no importa. ¡Ay!, tanto mal ha caído sobre este mundo. Permanezco aquí en penitencia, pues mi propia maldición recayó sobre mí.\
\
'Por orgullo ignoré las advertencias de los Lossoth, porque deseaba regresar a mi reino. Las tormentas de la Bahía de Hielo trajeron ruina al navío y a todos los que iban a bordo, y en desesperación y furia me maldije a mí mismo por mi orgullo. Pero la redención no está más allá de la esperanza, y quienes sigan mis pasos quizá puedan traerme paz.\
\
'En las minas de los enanos al sur, en Länsi-mâ, donde primero nos ocultamos de los agentes del Rey Brujo, fuimos obligados a abandonar muchas cosas. Una de ellas es un libro de heráldica que detalla la estirpe de mi pueblo. Ve y encuéntralo, luego llévalo al Dúnadan que vigila estas tierras frías en Sûri-kylä. Él lo llevará ante su señor.'","Encuentra el libro de heráldica","Habla con Arvedui","'Regresa ahora a la sombra de Arvedui, junto a los restos del barco que intentó llevarlo lejos de estas tierras.'","'Elrond y Aragorn querrán ver este libro y conocer la historia que lo acompaña...'","Al hallar los restos del barco que vino a llevar al rey Arvedui de vuelta a los Puertos Grises, hiciste un descubrimiento aún más sorprendente: la sombra del propio Arvedui.","'¿Qué es esto? ¿Un libro de heráldica que perteneció a Arvedui de Arthedain? ¡Increíble! ¿Dices que has visto al espíritu del propio Arvedui?\
\
'Llevaré esto de inmediato a Rivendel, pues esta historia debe ser contada a Elrond y a Aragorn.'","Arvedui está entre los restos del barco élfico, hacia el norte a lo largo de la Bahía de Hielo, en Talvi-mûri.\
\
Después de entregar el libro, deberías regresar con Arvedui para recibir más indicaciones.","Libro 13, Capítulo 6: Las Minas de los Enanos","'En las minas de los enanos al sur, en Länsi-mâ, donde primero nos ocultamos de los agentes del Rey Brujo, fuimos obligados a abandonar muchas cosas. Una de ellas es un libro de heráldica que detalla la estirpe de mi pueblo. Ve y encuéntralo, luego llévalo al Dúnadan que vigila estas tierras frías en Sûri-kylä. Él lo llevará ante su señor.'","El libro de heráldica yace en las minas de los enanos donde Arvedui y su gente se ocultaron en Länsi-mâ.\
\
Arvedui te pidió que encontraras el libro de heráldica, abandonado en las antiguas minas de los enanos, y que lo llevaras a un Montaraz acampado en Forochel.","El Montaraz está acampado en Sûri-kylä.\
\
Ahora que has encontrado el libro de heráldica, como indicó Arvedui, debes entregárselo al Montaraz del que habló el antiguo rey.","Entrega el libro de heráldica a un Montaraz acampado en Forochel","Has encontrado el libro de heráldica","'Gracias, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]} del Sur. Me has acercado un paso más a la redención.\
\
'El orgullo puede ser algo terrible. Por orgullo deseé regresar a Fornost y causé la muerte de muchos Elfos.\
\
'Ah, pero hablo de cosas sobre las que no debería seguir lamentándome...'"},
[1978]={"'The Orcs brought foul sorcery of Saruman with them! The wall is breached!'","Gléowine wants you to set the fallen barrel of weapons upright.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Interacting with the tipped-over barrel near Gléowine will allow time to pass. Action will resume in the hours before dawn, with the next onslaught of the enemy.</rgb>","Find the breach in the Deeping Wall","'I followed Éomer and Aragorn not for hope of glory, but only to shake the sleep from my eyes! The wild-men seemed rather too large for me, so I sat beside a stone and watched their swordplay. When Éomer ran afoul of the Orcs I could not stand idle! If he wishes to repay me the favour, I am certain he will have opportunity enough as the night progresses!\
\
'My count now is two! I must tell Legolas, and see how he fares. But he is a fighter. That minstrel of the King's, the one who travelled with you for a time... Gléowine? You should find him and tell him how the battle progresses. He will need to make a song of this, if we survive the night. Make certain he knows how I saved Éomer by the causeway! It would be a shame if he did not include a verse or three about that.'","'The blast knocked me down, ${PLAYER}, even from such a distance. Béorcla and Fisc were not so fortunate. They were much closer. Foul craft of Saruman!\
\
'We must retreat! There are too many, and they will be through the breach and upon us in no time!'","Book 13, Chapter 7: Defending the Deep","Defeat attacking uruks at the breach (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Gléowine by the map table west of the Hornburg","You set the barrel upright and replace the fallen weapons where they belong","Talk to Théoden outside the Hornburg","'Quickly, we must get to the breach! Make for the first level, and hurry east to the breach in the wall, there to do what you can!'","Defeated attacking uruks at the breach (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Saruman's attack on Helm's Deep continues, and the battle is beginning to take its toll on the fortress and on its defenders.","Sensing victory, Saruman's forces muster just beyond the breach","'You have to retreat! The Orcs have breached the wall!'","'The King is outside the Hornburg! Find him and see how the battle progresses from his vantage!'","In the hours before dawn, the forces of Saruman press their advantage.\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>There are two ways to participate in the defence of the Deeping-coomb. You can speak to Háma for the Storied Tale, a story-focused experience. Or you can use the Epic Battles Panel for a more gameplay-intensive experience.</rgb>\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>To participate in the defence of the Deep, open the Epic Battles Panel and select 'The Deeping-coomb' from the menu. After you successfully complete the defence, you will be returned to the location from which you entered it.</rgb>","'Speak to Gimli and let him know I am grateful for his assistance beyond the gate.'","'We must defend the Deep! Rally our soldiers, and fight back for as long as you are able!'\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>There are two ways to participate in the defence of the Deeping-coomb. You can speak to Háma for the Storied Tale, a story-focused experience. Or you can use the Epic Battles Panel for a more gameplay-intensive experience.</rgb>\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>To participate in the defence of the Deep, open the Epic Battles Panel and select 'The Deeping-coomb' from the menu. After you successfully complete the defence, you will be returned to the location from which you entered it.</rgb>","In the hours before dawn, the forces of Saruman press their advantage.\
\
Théoden King is outside the Hornburg.","'How goes the battle? It is said that the finest warriors can tell the number and strength of an enemy force simply by listening to the sound of their cries and their weapons, but it is not so with me. I am no warrior, and to me the sound of battle is a tumult without meaning.\
\
'The barrel of swords got knocked over in the confusion. Could you take some time to set it back upright? Then you should enter the Hornburg and speak with Théoden my master.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Interacting with the tipped-over barrel near Gléowine will allow time to pass. Action will resume in the hours before dawn, with the next onslaught of the enemy.</rgb>","Set the tipped barrel near the western wall upright, and time will pass","'I cannot leave the king's side, nor would I! But we have need of swords in the Deeping-coomb, ${PLAYER}! Go with Aragorn and keep the Orcs from passing through the hole in the wall! They may have brought more such blasting devices with them!'","Talk to Aragorn on the second level, outside the Hornburg","Talk to Gimli by the postern gate","In the hours before dawn, the forces of Saruman press their advantage.\
\
Aragorn wants you to hurry to the breach in the Deeping Wall, east of the Hornburg, and help the survivors in the aftermath of the blast.","'Set the tipped barrel upright and gather up the fallen weapons.'","'I have still not found Gimli, but I heard tell that he might have been pushed back to the Glittering Caves during the fighting. He is a staunch fellow, but the fighting is very heavy around the caves.'","'The Orcs by the gate had feigned death, and as I passed by with Aragorn they leapt onto me, dragging me to the stones. I was overcome by their grasping arms, and would have perished were it not for my heroic friend here. I speak of Gimli, the staunchest dwarf I have ever met! I did not know he was with us in the battle, but at my time of need he charged from the shadows and felled the Orcs that pinned me.\
\
'Speak to him and see if there is anything he lacks, and it will be his.'","It is after midnight at Helm's Deep.\
\
Gimli is by the postern gate, below the north-west tower.","'How does the King's minstrel fare? He is not a warrior like us, and we should keep his mood in mind.'","'The night wears on, and the enemy shows no sign of relenting. We have lost many men on the wall, but for each loss we claim a dozen enemy lives. This is not a favourable exchange for us, ${PLAYER}, though it speaks well of our fighting prowess. We will run out of defenders well before Saruman's forces tire of the fight.\
\
'We must defend the Deep! Rally our soldiers, and fight back for as long as you are able!'\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>There are two ways to participate in the defence of the Deeping-coomb. You can speak to Háma for the Storied Tale, a story-focused experience. Or you can use the Epic Battles Panel for a more gameplay-intensive experience.</rgb>\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>To participate in the defence of the Deep, open the Epic Battles Panel and select 'The Deeping-coomb' from the menu. After you successfully complete the defence, you will be returned to the location from which you entered it.</rgb>","In the hours before dawn, the forces of Saruman press their advantage.\
\
Aragorn is on the second level, outside the entrance to the Hornburg.","Talk to Sigferth by the breach","Talk to Háma and complete 'Storied Tale: The Deeping-coomb' <rgb=#00FF00>OR</rgb> complete 'The Deeping-coomb' from the Epic Battles Panel","'That explosion destroyed much of the Deeping Wall! Many of our allies may be dazed or wounded by the blast, and even if they still survive they will not last long.\
\
'We must get to the breach quickly! Make for the first level, and hurry east to the breach in the wall to do what you can!'","It is after midnight at Helm's Deep.\
\
Gimli has asked you to check on Gléowine by the map table west of the Hornburg."},
[1979]={"Libro 13, Capítulo 7: El Marinero Perdido","'Quizá algún día perdone mi orgullo, pero ese día aún no ha llegado.\
\
'Mucho después de que el Thoroval naufragara, otro barco entró en la Bahía de Hielo. También provenía de Mithlond, y solo puedo suponer que buscaba noticias del Thoroval y de su tripulación. Ese barco también naufragó, pero los Elfos intentaron escapar de su destrucción. No creo que todos murieran en las aguas heladas, al menos no todos, pero no puedo decir cuál fue su destino final.\
\
'¿Quizá la vidente de los Lossoth que te envió a encontrar el barco lo sabrá? Regresa con ella y busca su guía una vez más.'","'¿Hallaste el cuerpo del monstruo marino? ¿Y también encontraste a la sombra del Rey Demacrado? Es algo inesperado, aunque quizá no tanto como pudiera parecer.'","Habla con Saija","'Mucho después de que el Thoroval naufragara, otro barco entró en la Bahía de Hielo. También provenía de Mithlond, y solo puedo suponer que buscaba noticias del Thoroval y de su tripulación. Ese barco también naufragó, pero los Elfos intentaron escapar de su destrucción. No creo que todos murieran en las aguas heladas, al menos no todos, pero no puedo decir cuál fue su destino final.\
\
'¿Quizá la vidente de los Lossoth que te envió a encontrar el barco lo sabrá? Regresa con ella y busca su guía una vez más.'","Para ganarte la confianza del espíritu inquieto de Arvedui, realizaste un acto de bondad por él y entregaste un tomo perdido a uno de los descendientes de su linaje.","Saija está en Näky-kolo, al noroeste de Kuru-leiri.\
\
Arvedui te dijo que el capitán del barco élfico no pereció con su navío y sugirió que buscaras la sabiduría de Saija para conocer el destino de Aearil y su tripulación.","'Encontrar al espíritu del Rey Demacrado es un encuentro verdaderamente inesperado...'"},
[1980]={"Habla con Saija","'Ya que has hablado con el Rey Demacrado, te diré lo que he aprendido de su historia, pero antes hay cosas que debes hacer. Mi conocimiento no viene sin un precio.\
\
'Habla conmigo cuando estés ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para oír las tareas que tengo para ti.'","'¿Así que sabes dónde encontrar la cueva donde se ocultaron los Elfos?'","Realiza dos tareas para Saija","'Has ganado el derecho de oír este relato, guardado durante generaciones por mi familia y conocido solo por ellos y por unos pocos Sabios instruidos. \
\
'Cuando el gran monstruo marino vino a llevarse al Laiha-herra, mi pueblo le suplicó que no montara sobre él, pues el Rey Brujo podía enviar terribles tormentas para ahogarlos a todos, pero no escuchó. Y así, cuando la criatura se internó en las grandes aguas, una tormenta violentísima vino del norte y la estrelló contra el hielo, dándole muerte.\
\
'Durante muchos días la tormenta rugió, y todos los que se hallaban fuera de la aldea perecieron bajo la nieve profunda y la cegadora lluvia helada que caía del cielo. Cuando por fin terminó, buscamos supervivientes, tanto de los Lumi-väki como de quienes habían subido al monstruo marino, pero no hallamos a ninguno.\
\
'Al año siguiente apareció otro monstruo marino, semejante al primero, y también fue abatido antes de llegar a la orilla. Los Vanha-väki que lo montaban huyeron de su ruina. Aunque encontramos muchos cuerpos congelados en el hielo, la pista se perdió en la entrada de una cueva sellada por el hielo.'","Saija está en Näky-kolo, al noroeste de Kuru-leiri.\
\
Saija te dirá lo que necesitas saber, pero quiere que realices dos tareas para ella.","'Debes buscar la sabiduría de Saija.'","Libro 13, Capítulo 8: Una Tormenta Oscura","Saija está en Näky-kolo, al noroeste de Kuru-leiri.\
\
Ahora que has completado las dos tareas que te encomendó, deberías hablar con Saija nuevamente.","No solo encontraste los restos del barco élfico que había llevado al rey Arvedui desde las costas de Forochel, sino que hallaste también a la sombra del propio Arvedui."},
[1981]={"Saija te ha encomendado dos tareas que debes realizar antes de que te revele su conocimiento.","Saija está en Näky-kolo, al noroeste de Kuru-leiri.\
\
Habiendo derrotado a los gigantes de hielo, debes regresar de inmediato con Saija.","'Hacia el sur y el oeste, gigantes de hielo han descendido de las montañas y amenazan a todos los que cazan en esas tierras. Ve y enfréntalos, expúlsalos de las tierras de los Lossoth. Tal acto ayudará a demostrar tu lealtad.\
\
'Puede resultarte más fácil si los atraes hacia las aguas termales que brotan dentro de su campamento. Cuando hayas completado esta tarea, vuelve conmigo para recibir nuevas instrucciones.'","Derrota gigantes de hielo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Habla con Saija","Se pueden encontrar gigantes de hielo al sur y al oeste de Näky-kolo.\
\
Saija te ha encargado derrotar a los gigantes de hielo que descendieron de las montañas. También sugiere atraerlos a las aguas termales para debilitarlos.","Gigantes de hielo derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Solo alguien con gran valor se atrevería a enfrentar criaturas tan poderosas y terribles. Has demostrado tu destreza.'","Libro 13, Capítulo 8: Una Prueba del Frío","'Tienes la fuerza necesaria para enfrentarte a criaturas como los gigantes de hielo.'"},
[1982]={"In the hours before dawn, the forces of Saruman press their advantage.\
\
Gimli is in the Glittering Caves, and wanted to speak with you about the next phase of the battle.","In the hours before dawn, the forces of Saruman press their advantage.\
\
Aragorn has asked you to find Gimli in the Glittering Caves. The entrance to the caves is south of the Deeping Wall, where the stream runs out of the mountains.","Talk to Gimli and secure the Glittering Caves","'Find Gimli within the Glittering Caves. I hope my friend fares well in the battle. The entrance to the caves is south of the Deeping Wall, where the stream runs down from the mountains.'","'I know that Gimli can handle himself in battle, but still I worry about him. If you can make your way to the Glittering Caves, I would ask that you do. Keep an eye on our friend. I fear that at times his desire for battle and the thirst of his axe may cloud his judgement. He may get in over his head.'\
\
Aragorn laughs, an unusual sound over the din of battle.\
\
'I ask that you do not repeat my unfortunate choice of words, ${PLAYER}. But if you do bring Gimli back to safety, I would be glad to relearn my manners at his request! The entrance to the caves is south of the Deeping Wall, where the stream runs down out of the mountains.'","Book 13, Chapter 8: Secret Ways","'I do not like knowing that there are tunnels into the mountains through which our enemies may pass, but we cannot seal them. If the battle turns ill, we may need to bring as many folk as we can through those passages and out of the caverns. At least we have dealt with one threat, but on this night I will not be surprised if three more dangers leap to take the place now vacated by the one!'","Find Gimli in the Glittering Caves","'Look around you, my friend! Have you seen such a place? Éomer spoke at great length of the fields and grasslands of this kingdom, but he failed to speak of its greatest wonders. See how the cavern shines in the half-light? With a dozen of my people I could fashion such delights from the walls and ceilings that it would steal the breath of even Legolas, or any of his kin!\
\
'But there is little time to admire the sights. There is fighting to be done! Those who are not warriors shelter now in the cavern, and we must protect them or none else will. Speak to me if you are ready to join the battle once again!'","'Did you find Gimli? I heard tell that he was pushed back into the Glittering Caves during the fighting, and I worry for his safety.'","In the hours before dawn, the forces of Saruman press their advantage.\
\
Gimli is in the Glittering Caves, waiting to speak with you.","'We must make safe these caves before the next attack begins. Come with me and we will ensure that the safety of this cavern is no phantom.'","In the hours before dawn, the forces of Saruman press their advantage.\
\
Gimli has been forced into the Glittering Caves during the fighting.","Aragorn has heard that Gimli may have been pushed back into the Glittering Caves during the fighting, and wants you to find the dwarf and assist him.","You have found Gimli. He seems tired, but is otherwise healthy enough","Talk to Gimli in the Glittering Caves"},
[1983]={"'En las costas occidentales de la Bahía de Hielo, donde las tormentas arrecian con mayor violencia, moran espíritus malignos enviados desde Angmar para atormentar a los Lossoth. Estos demonios alzan terribles espectros del hielo y convierten la zona en un lugar de gran desasosiego. Ve y destierra a estas criaturas de las costas de Forochel.\
\
'Los encontrarás sobre esta cueva, al sur y oeste de su entrada y luego al norte, entre las ruinas. Cuando hayas cumplido tu tarea, regresa aquí conmigo.'","Saija te ha encomendado dos tareas que debes realizar antes de que te revele su conocimiento.","Espectros del hielo derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Habla con Saija","Saija está en Näky-kolo.\
\
Ahora que has derrotado a numerosos espectros del hielo, deberías volver con Saija tal como te indicó.","Derrota espectros del hielo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Libro 13, Capítulo 8: Espíritus de Angmar","Se pueden encontrar espectros del hielo sobre Näky-kolo, al sur y oeste del lugar.\
\
Saija te ha encomendado desterrar a los espectros del hielo de las costas de Forochel.","'Tu tarea fue en vano, pues ${PLAYERNAME:un[m]|una[f]} mortal no puede desterrar eternamente a un espíritu, pero tu valentía ante tal horror habla bien de ti.'"},
[1984]={"The battle has come to the Glittering Caves, and the people of Rohan that shelter there must be protected!","In the hours before dawn, the forces of Saruman press their advantage.\
\
Gimli is in the Glittering Caves, and wishes to speak with you after pushing back the latest assault.","'Well done, well done! We have pushed them back for now. Return to Aragorn before we get hard-pressed again, and tell him that you found me in fine spirits, flush with the thrill of battle! I trust that you will find him the same. And keep an eye on Legolas, if you see him. I have not forgotten our little contest, and with the fighting in the caves I feel certain I must pass his tally.'","'Return to Aragorn before we get hard-pressed again, and tell him that you found me in fine spirits, flush with the thrill of battle! I trust that you will find him the same!'","In the hours before dawn, the forces of Saruman press their advantage.\
\
Aragorn is on the second level, outside the Hornburg, and Gimli wants you to report to him of the dwarf's successes.","Talk to Éomer and complete 'Storied Tale: The Glittering Caves' <rgb=#00FF00>OR</rgb> complete 'The Glittering Caves' from the Epic Battles Panel","'So Gimli lives and is in high spirits? That is good, but I fear that I do not share in his confidence. The fortress cannot stand much longer. We are nearly overrun.'","In the hours before dawn, the forces of Saruman press their advantage.\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>There are two ways to participate in the defence of the Glittering Caves. You can speak to Éomer for the Storied Tale, a story-focused experience. Or you can use the Epic Battles Panel for a more gameplay-intensive experience.</rgb>\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>To participate in the defence of the Glittering Caves, open the Epic Battles Panel and select 'Glittering Caves' from the menu. After you successfully complete the defence, you will be returned to the location from which you entered it.</rgb>","Book 13, Chapter 9: Glittering Caves","'That Dunlending chief thought to sneak into these caves with murder in his heart, but he has been repaid in kind. I am glad he is dead, but I fear other dangers may seek to ensnare the folk who shelter here.'","Talk to Aragorn outside the Hornburg","'The battle will soon be upon us! We must protect the folk that shelter here, or I will bring shame upon my name, that of my father, and that of my King. The Orcs and the wild-men have no place defiling this magnificent cavern, ${PLAYER}. Let us cast them out and send them howling back to their Wizard master!'\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>There are two ways to participate in the defence of the Glittering Caves. You can speak to Éomer for the Storied Tale, a story-focused experience. Or you can use the Epic Battles Panel for a more gameplay-intensive experience.</rgb>\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>To participate in the defence of the Glittering Caves, open the Epic Battles Panel and select 'Glittering Caves' from the menu. After you successfully complete the defence, you will be returned to the location from which you entered it.</rgb>","Talk to Gimli in the Glittering Caves"},
[1985]={"'¿Entonces el capitán elfo pereció? No derramaré lágrimas, pues escapó de esta Tierra Media hacia un lugar mucho más verde, o eso dicen los Elfos.'","Habla con Arvedui","La sombra de Arvedui se encuentra en la Ruina del Thoroval, al norte y al este a lo largo de la Bahía de Hielo, en Talvi-mûri.\
\
Habiendo recuperado un fragmento del anillo entre las pertenencias de Aearil, deberías buscar a la sombra de Arvedui y comunicarle el destino de quien intentó rescatarlo, además de averiguar si el fragmento que hallaste es realmente la mitad perdida de Narchuil.","'Esta cueva se encuentra dentro de Talvi-mûri. Es un lugar peligroso, pero no creo que debas temer ir allí. Yo mismo te guiaré cuando estés ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]}.\
\
'Si el Elfo no vive, probablemente no encontrarás más que sus ropas. Si llevaba el anillo que buscas, debería hallarse entre sus pertenencias, si es que permanecen allí.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión está pensada para una comunidad. Si decides afrontarla en solitario, recibirás una bonificación de inspiración, pero el desafío será grande.</rgb>","Saija te reveló la ubicación de una cueva donde los Lossoth creen que el capitán del segundo barco élfico pudo refugiarse tras el naufragio.","El capitán elfo, o sus pertenencias, podrían aún encontrarse dentro de la cueva.\
\
Saija sugirió que volvieras a hablar con ella para buscar la cueva, y que te guiaría hasta allí.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión está pensada para una comunidad. Si decides afrontarla en solitario, recibirás una bonificación de inspiración, pero el desafío será grande.</rgb>","'¿Estás ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para partir?'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión está pensada para una comunidad. Si decides afrontarla en solitario, recibirás una bonificación de inspiración, pero el desafío será grande.</rgb>","Encuentra a Narchuil","Has encontrado un fragmento de Narchuil","Libro 13, Capítulo 9: El Sendero de Aearil","'Ahora conozco una pequeña paz... mi redención llegará con el tiempo.'"},
[1986]={"Libro 14, Capítulo 10: Tras la Pista de Angmar","'Hay poco más en lo que pueda ayudarte, ${PLAYER}. Es una pena que esa herramienta haya sido robada... me habría encantado verla.\
\
'En fin, quizá deberías regresar junto al elfo que te envió... ¿Eglamír, era su nombre? Puede que tenga otras palabras de sabiduría para ti.\
\
'Celondim queda muy lejos, según tengo entendido... a la sombra de las Montañas Azules. Harías bien en partir cuanto antes.'","Newbold Cortahoja te dirigió a la tumba de Maenadar el Artesano, pero llegaste demasiado tarde para recuperar la herramienta de forja de Celebrimbor.","Eglamír se encuentra en Celondim, en las Montañas Azules, muy al oeste de las Tierras de Bree.\
\
Newbold Cortahoja te sugirió que regresaras con Eglamír para recibir más consejos.","Habla con Eglamír en Celondim","'Creo recordar que dijiste que venías de Celondim... ¿no es así?'","'Son malas noticias, ${PLAYER}. Con esa herramienta, Angmar podría causar grandes estragos en Eriador...'"},
[1987]={"'¿Uno de los Vanha-väki te envía hasta mí? El último que recuerdo haber visto se llamaba Laerdan, y fracasó en su cometido.\
\
'¿Qué desean ahora los Vanha-väki de los Lumi-väki?'","Habla con Yrjänä en Sûri-kylä","'Son noticias trágicas las que traes desde las Tierras de Bree. Si tuviera que aventurar una suposición, diría que Angmar intenta reavivar las forjas de Mirobel, en Eregion... quizá con la intención de forjar un anillo nuevo o reparar uno antiguo.\
\
'Sea como sea, poco importa. Mucho mal podría desatarse si Angmar tuviera éxito. Sin embargo, antes de que puedan reavivar las forjas, deberán reparar los grandes fuelles. Originalmente, los fuelles se construyeron con un fino cuero élfico capaz de resistir el paso del tiempo, pero ahora están podridos.\
\
'Angmar podría, no obstante, reemplazar el cuero élfico por piel de dragón, que es fuerte y duradera. Circulan rumores de que un dragón —aunque de menor poder— habitó antaño las tierras heladas y desoladas de Forochel. Ve a Sûri-kylä y habla con su jefa, Yrjänä. Tal vez ella sepa algo más.'","Libro 14, Capítulo 11: Los Grandes Fuelles de Mirobel","'Yrjänä habita en el poblado lossoth de Sûri-kylä, en Forochel. Tal vez pueda guiarte hasta la guarida del dragón.'","Yrjänä se encuentra en Sûri-kylä, en Forochel, muy al norte y al este de Celondim.\
\
Eglamír cree que los esbirros de Amarthiel podrían estar tratando de encontrar la guarida de un dragón que quizá aún habite en Forochel, cuya piel podría usarse para reparar los fuelles de las forjas de Mirobel. Te sugiere viajar al norte helado y hablar con la jefa lossoth Yrjänä.","Newbold Cortahoja ya no pudo ayudarte y te sugirió regresar con Eglamír en Celondim."},
[1988]={"Encuentra y entra en la guarida de Bregmor","'Bregmor era una criatura malvada, pero aun así es triste que una bestia tan imponente haya perecido en una soledad semejante.\
\
'Lo que resulta aún más inquietante es que los Rauta-väki lograran profanar al lohikârme. ¿Y Mordrambor? ¿Por qué habría de ayudar de ese modo? ¿No es acaso enemigo de Amarthiel, y busca su anillo para sí? Todo esto es muy extraño y profundamente perturbador.'","Libro 14, Capítulo 12: La Piel de Bregmor","Yrjänä se encuentra en Sûri-kylä, muy al este de la guarida de Bregmor.\
\
No lograste impedir que Angmar se apoderara de la piel del dragón Bregmor y ahora deberías regresar con Yrjänä para darle la noticia.","Habla con Yrjänä en Sûri-kylä","Eglamír cree que los esbirros de Amarthiel podrían estar buscando la piel del dragón de Forochel para reparar los grandes fuelles de Mirobel, las Forjas de los Anillos de Eregion, y te envió a informarte sobre Bregmor con Yrjänä, la jefa de Sûri-kylä.","La guarida de Bregmor se encuentra muy al oeste de Sûri-kylä, al sudeste de Jotunstath.\
\
Yrjänä te contó que el dragón Bregmor aterrorizó Forochel en otro tiempo, pero ya no lo hace. También indicó que no arriesgaría a su gente para guiarte hasta la guarida de Bregmor, dejándote valerte por tu cuenta.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión está pensada para una comunidad. Si decides emprenderla en solitario, recibirás un bono de inspiración, pero el desafío será considerable.</rgb>","'¿Tu Vanha-väki te envía a buscar la guarida del gran lohikârme, la criatura llamada Bregmor? Sé algo de él, aunque nunca lo he visto.\
\
'Se cuenta entre los Lumi-väki que Bregmor fue antaño el azote de estas tierras heladas. Muchos cazadores lo persiguieron, pero ninguno regresó jamás. Llegó el día en que Bregmor dejó de cazar al Lumi-väki, y no vimos necesidad de provocarlo más.\
\
'Si deseas visitar al lohikârme, deberás hacerlo por tus propios medios. Encontrarás su guarida muy al oeste, al sudeste de Jotunstath, el hogar de los Elukka, los gigantes de hielo, como ustedes los llaman.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión está pensada para una comunidad. Si decides emprenderla en solitario, recibirás un bono de inspiración, pero el desafío será considerable.</rgb>","'No enviaré a mi gente a morir por ti. Si deseas ver al lohikârme, ve por tu cuenta.'"},
[1989]={"No lograste frustrar las maquinaciones de Angmar en Forochel, dejando a les servidores de Amarthiel libres para reavivar las forjas de Mirobel.","Libro 14, Capítulo 13: Esperanzas Frustradas","'Deberías regresar con tu Vanha-väki, este Eglamír. Estoy seguro de que querrá conocer tu fracaso de primera mano. No olvides mencionar la participación de Mordrambor. No sé qué significa exactamente, pero quizá algunes otros sepan interpretar lo que presagia.\
\
'Creo que dijiste que mora en el lugar de los Vanha-väki llamado Celondim, lejos al sur y al oeste, en las Montañas Azules. Yo iría allí sin demora para hablar con él.'","'Sería conveniente que regreses con tu Vanha-väki y confieses tu fracaso.'","'¡Ay! Ahora hay pocas esperanzas de impedir que Amarthiel reforge a Narchuil y lance a sus ejércitos contra Eriador. ¡Especialmente si ese Señor de Umbar, ese Mordrambor del que hablaste, vuelve a prestarle su ayuda!'","Habla con Eglamír en Celondim","Eglamír se encuentra en Celondim, en las Montañas Azules, lejos al sur y al oeste de Forochel.\
\
Yrjänä te dijo que regresaras con Eglamír para informarle de tu fracaso."},
[1990]={"Habla con Elrond en Rivendel","Libro 14, Capítulo 14: Una Carga Pesada","'Así que las Forjas de los Anillos volverán a arder. Amarthiel reforjará a Narchuil y lo usará para liderar a sus ejércitos contra Eriador. A su lado estará Mordrambor, que al parecer se ha aliado con ella una vez más.\
\
'Si eso sucede, el Norte será aplastado, y aunque Rivendel resista, solo será cuestión de tiempo antes de que también nosotros seamos superados.\
\
'Debemos poner fin a los planes de Amarthiel, de una vez por todas.'","Elrond se encuentra en Rivendel, en el Bosque de los Trolls, muy al este de Celondim.\
\
Eglamír sugirió que lleves noticias de tu fracaso a Elrond, en Rivendel.","'No hay más ayuda que pueda darte. Con la piel de Bregmor y la herramienta de forja de Celebrimbor, ya no queda nada que impida a Angmar reavivar las forjas de Eregion y reforjar a Narchuil. Has fracasado, pero no te juzgues con demasiada dureza... las probabilidades nunca estuvieron de tu lado.\
\
'Deberías regresar a Rivendel y llevar estas terribles noticias a Elrond Mediolfo. Tal vez él sepa qué hacer ahora.\
\
'Rivendel se encuentra en el Bosque de los Trolls, muy al este, a la sombra de las Montañas Nubladas.'","Con la piel del dragón Bregmor y la herramienta de forja de Celebrimbor, no hay nada más que Eglamír sepa que Amarthiel necesite para reavivar las forjas de Eregion y reforjar a Narchuil.","'Angmar está un paso más cerca de adueñarse de todo Eriador. ¡Debes regresar junto a Elrond de inmediato!'"},
[1991]={"Habla con Elrond en Rivendel","Con tus derrotas en las Tierras de Bree y en Forochel, ya queda poco por hacer salvo arrojarte contra las fuerzas de Amarthiel en un intento vano por poner fin a sus planes.","'Aún queda una última esperanza, ${PLAYER}, aunque bien puede ser vana. Debes viajar a Mirobel e intentar poner fin allí a los planes de Amarthiel.\
\
'Debes darte prisa... quizá ya sea demasiado tarde, pero existe una leve esperanza de que aún no haya recibido los materiales que necesita para reavivar las forjas de Eregion y reforjar a Narchuil.\
\
'Mirobel se encuentra muy al sur de Rivendel, en las tierras de Eregion. Que las estrellas iluminen tu camino.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión está pensada para una comunidad. Si decides emprenderla en solitario, recibirás un bono de inspiración, pero el desafío será considerable.</rgb>","'El maestro Elrond te espera en su biblioteca... ¡deberías ir allí sin demora!'","El capitán de la guardia Glorenthol se encuentra en Delossad, en Tâl Bruinen.\
\
No lograste detener a Amarthiel, pero finalmente fue derrotada con el regreso inesperado de Mordirith. Narchuil ha caído en manos del Rey Falso, y Amarthiel es ahora prisionera de los Pueblos Libres. Deberías hablar con el capitán de la guardia Glorenthol.","'La sombra aún no se ha disipado —no mientras Narchuil permanezca en manos de Mordirith—, pero al menos has obtenido una victoria importante para Eriador: Amarthiel ha sido capturada.\
\
'Por desgracia, Laerdan se ha perdido. Creía que podría rescatar a su hija de Amarthiel... debemos averiguar si lo logró.'","'Tu resistencia frente a Amarthiel es la última esperanza de Eriador, a menos que la Compañía cumpla su cometido...\
\
'Debes viajar a Mirobel, en Eregion, muy al sur, si deseas tener alguna oportunidad de detenerla.'","Viaja a Mirobel e intenta detener a Amarthiel","Libro 14, Capítulo 15: La Perdición del Norte","Puedes llegar a Mirobel viajando muy al sur, hasta las tierras de Eregion.\
\
Elrond te ordenó viajar a Mirobel y hacer todo lo que esté a tu alcance para detener a Amarthiel.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión está pensada para una comunidad. Si decides emprenderla en solitario, recibirás un bono de inspiración, pero el desafío será considerable.</rgb>","Elrond se encuentra en la biblioteca de la Última Morada en Rivendel.\
\
El capitán de la guardia te indicó que hables con Elrond acerca de tu misión en Mirobel.","Habla con el capitán de la guardia","'El maestro Elrond te espera en su biblioteca, ${PLAYER}. Deberías hablar con él de inmediato.'"},
[1992]={"'Sí, esto servirá perfectamente. Un dorado profundo y dulce, directo del panal.\
\
'Puedes hacerle saber a Laerdan que las lembas estarán listas antes de que comience su viaje.'","Laerdan te envió con Filegnaneth para reunir provisiones para el viaje a Eregion, pero ella no tiene la fina miel de trébol que necesita para hacer lembas, el pan de camino de los elfos.","Miel de trébol fina encontrada (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¿No tienes miel de trébol fina? Puedes comprarla al cocinero experto que vive en la Comarca. Tengo entendido que reside en el pueblo de Cavada Grande.'","El cocinero experto se encuentra en Cavada Grande, en la Comarca, muy al oeste de Rivendel. Filegnaneth está en Rivendel, en el Bosque de los Trolls, muy al este de la Comarca.\
\
Filegnaneth te ha pedido viajar a la Comarca y comprar miel de trébol fina al cocinero experto allí.","'¡Saludos, ${PLAYER}! El viaje de Laerdan no me es desconocido. He reunido muchas provisiones, pero me falta la fina miel de trébol que necesito para preparar lembas, el pan de camino de los elfos.\
\
'Entiendo, sin embargo, que hay un cocinero experto en la Comarca, la tierra de los medianos. El joven Peregrin Tuk me sugirió enviar a alguien a Cavada Grande para encontrar a este cocinero, pero el viaje es largo y estamos ocupados con muchos preparativos.\
\
'¿Quizá podrías encargarte de esta tarea? Viaja a Cavada Grande, en la Comarca, muy al oeste de Rivendel, y compra algo de fina miel de trébol, luego vuelve a verme.'","Encuentra miel de trébol fina (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Libro 14, Capítulo 1: Muchas provisiones","Lleva la miel de trébol fina a Filegnaneth"},
[1993]={"Talk to Éomer on the field of victory outside the Hornburg, after sunrise","This man insists that his injuries are not severe, and will not take a poultice","'We spoke yesterday, around sunset, do you remember? It feels a lifetime ago, ${PLAYER}!'","'This is a proud day for the Riders of the Mark, ${PLAYER}. We have wrested victory from the very claw of Saruman, even as he thought his triumph assured. The House of Eorl is stronger than he supposed, despite thrice-cursed Wyrgende and the whispers of frailty that have been uttered throughout the Mark. Théoden King has fight in him still, as does his sister-son Éomer!'\
\
Erkenbrand strikes his shield with the side of his sword, and cries 'Victory for the Eorlingas!' a cry that is answered from others of the Rohirrim throughout the field. After a moment he turns again to you with a smile.\
\
'We have put the Dunlendings to work, ${PLAYER}, hauling away the bodies of the Orcs and cleaning the field of battle. Any who take a solemn vow not to cross the Fords in war ever again will have the forgiveness of our King.'","'You will find Théoden King to the south, enjoying the victory. Tend to his hurts, if he is injured, and heed any commands he may have.'","'Éomer has indicated to me a desire to ride with the King to Isengard. He will wish for you to ride there as well.'","Book 14, Chapter 1: The Battle Is Won","'We have seen victory this day, but our work is not ended. We have earned a brief respite only, and must take steps to ensure the safety of the Mark without much pause.'\
\
The King sees the bundle of poultices in your hands and shakes his head.\
\
'I am fine, ${PLAYER}. I have suffered bruises only, and the strength of my fathers has kept me from sustaining grievous injury. Many of my men will have need of that healing; bring those packets to them and see to their hurts. Look too for men with swift horses, and command them to ride for all corners of the Mark with news of what happened at the Hornburg. I want every vale in the Riddermark to have tidings of our victory, and to send their strongest fighters to Edoras by the second day of the full moon.\
\
'After you have exhausted the poultices and the riders have set forth, find Erkenbrand and give him my thanks for his timely arrival. Without his men this sun might have risen on a different day for Rohan.'","Éomer is on the field of victory outside the Hornburg, after sunrise.","Gandalf has asked you to bring healing poultices to injured men in Helm's Deep, and the King has asked you to bring his command to any men nearby who own swift horses.","Treat injured men with healing poultices (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The battle has been won, and now the defenders of Helm's Deep recover from their hurts and look to the future.","Erkenbrand is on the field of battle outside the Hornburg, after sunrise.\
\
Théoden asked you to find Erkenbrand on the field of victory and to thank him for his timely arrival.","Talk to Théoden on the field of victory at Helm's Deep, after sunrise","'The battle is won, my friend, and now we must look to the future! The design of Saruman has been ruined, not by any spell or magic, but by the stout hearts of the Rohirrim and the swift speed of Shadowfax!'\
\
Gandalf notices your study of the curious trees beyond the Dike.\
\
'Ah, that forest is no magic of mine, ${PLAYER}. A power much older than my own drives it to be here, and I could not have hoped for a more timely arrival than this!'\
\
He hands you a number of healing poultices.\
\
'Before we can proceed, we must attend to the hurts of those injured during the battle. These poultices will bring them some measure of relief. Speak with the King and see if he has need of such treatment, and then do what you can for the wounded.'","'Find Erkenbrand on the field of victory and give him my thanks for his timely arrival. This victory would not have been possible without him.'","'Many of our injured men have need of the poultices you carry. Bring them to those who do, and ease the sting of their wounds. Look too for men who own swift horses, and send them to every corner of the Mark with tidings of our victory here!\
\
'I want every able-bodied warrior summoned to Edoras by the second day of the full moon. Our work here is only beginning, but it is far better to begin with a victory than from a defeat!'","'Gandalf has decided to ride to Isengard to confront Saruman, and my uncle has determined he should ride with him. Some others will go as well, but first we have need of rest. It will be a few hours before we ride for the Ring of Isengard and its evil master, and all of us toiled greatly during the night.\
\
'Find Déorwine inside the Hornburg. He has begun to arrange bedrolls for those seeking to rest for the journey.'","Théoden King is to the south of Gandalf, on the field before the Hornburg, after sunrise.\
\
Gandalf has given you a number of healing poultices and wants you to tend to the hurts of the King and his men.","'Find Déorwine inside the fortress of the Hornburg. He will arrange a place for you to rest before the company sets forth for Isengard.'","The poultice has eased the man's pain (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Erkenbrand on the field of victory outside the Hornburg, after sunrise","Déorwine is inside the fortress of the Hornburg, after sunrise.\
\
Éomer thinks you should rest for a few hours inside the fortress of the Hornburg, before going with the King's company to the Ring of Isengard to confront Saruman.","The man agrees to ride forth at once","Issue Théoden's command to men who own swift horses (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","This man regretfully owns no horse swift enough to carry the King's tidings","Talk to Déorwine inside the fortress of the Hornburg, after sunrise"},
[1994]={"Encuentra el peto de Laerdan","'Veo que has encontrado el peto, pero está en demasiado mal estado para dárselo a Laerdan tal como está. Permíteme pedir a uno de los enanos de aquí que lo repare. Lo consideraré un regalo para mi amigo.\
\
'Haré que uno de nuestros mensajeros lo lleve a Esteldín y luego a Rivendel.'","Libro 14, Capítulo 1: La heráldica de Lindon","Dolendath se encuentra en Imlad Balchorth, al sur y oeste de Myrkworth.\
\
Golodir sugirió que podrías encontrar el peto de Laerdan en Dolendath, el lugar donde su ejército se refugió por primera vez en Angmar.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión está pensada para una comunidad. Si decides completarla en solitario recibirás una bonificación de inspiración, pero el desafío será grande.</rgb>","Lleva el peto de Laerdan de vuelta a Golodir en Gath Forthnír","'El peto de Laerdan podría encontrarse dentro de los límites de Dolendath, en Imlad Balchorth, pero debes tener cuidado... ahora son los Muertos quienes gobiernan allí.'","Laerdan te envió a Gath Forthnír para pedirle su peto al montaraz Golodir.","Peto de Laerdan encontrado","'Por desgracia, no sé dónde puede encontrarse el peto de Laerdan. No recuerdo que lo llevara puesto cuando vinimos a Gath Forthnír.\
\
'Hay un lugar donde podrías buscar, pero es un sitio terrible y peligroso. Cuando atravesamos por primera vez los Rammas Deluon, nos refugiamos en un lugar llamado Dolendath, en Imlad Balchorth. Cuando los Muertos se alzaron, huimos y dejamos muchas cosas atrás. Quizá el peto de Laerdan estuviera entre esas pertenencias.\
\
'Si deseas buscar en Dolendath, encontrarás la entrada en Imlad Balchorth, al sur y oeste de Myrkworth. ¡Pero cuidado con los Muertos!\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión está pensada para una comunidad. Si decides completarla en solitario recibirás una bonificación de inspiración, pero el desafío será grande.</rgb>'"},
[1995]={"La puerta de la habitación de Laerdan parece estar cerrada con llave, y una nota ha sido clavada cerca","Habla con Elrond en Rivendel","Habla con Golodir en Gath Forthnír","'¿No has terminado aún? ¡Debes darte prisa!\
\
'Filegnaneth está aquí en Rivendel, en la Sala del Fuego de la casa de Elrond. Nat Tajada se encuentra en los establos de Tinnudír, en la región de Evendim, y Golodir sigue en Gath Forthnír, en Angmar.'","Libro 14, Capítulo 1: El largo camino al sur","Has leído la nota de Laerdan","'¿Laerdan ha llevado los fragmentos de Narchuil a Amarthiel? Esta es una noticia terrible, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo mío[m]|amiga mía[f]}. Este giro de los acontecimientos nos obliga a actuar...'","Habla con Laerdan en Rivendel","'¡Saludos, ${PLAYER}! Me has sido de gran ayuda en el pasado, y ahora necesito de tu ayuda una vez más. Como sabes, pronto partiremos hacia Eregion, pero hay mucho que hacer antes de que me vaya.\
\
'Primero, quisiera pedirte que visites a Filegnaneth en el Salón del Fuego aquí en Rivendel y le solicites provisiones. Luego, quiero que viajes a la isla de Tinnudír, en Evendim, y pidas a Nat Tajada que envíe de vuelta a mi fiel corcel Arel. Por último, quisiera que te aventures a Gath Forthnír y pidas a Golodir que me devuelva mi peto — ha estado perdido durante demasiado tiempo.\
\
'Cuando hayas completado estas tareas, vuelve a verme y partiremos.'","Laerdan se está preparando para viajar a Eregion, pero necesita tu ayuda para terminar sus preparativos.","'${PLAYER}, debo disculparme, pero no pensé que lo entenderías. Tus tareas no eran más que una distracción.\
\
'Ya he partido de Rivendel y me he llevado conmigo los fragmentos de Narchuil. Debo llevarlos a Narmeleth, o su mente nunca volverá a ser completa.\
\
'El amor por mi hija, por desgracia, debe ponerse por encima de todo. Que la luz de las estrellas ilumine tu camino.'","Laerdan está en la Última Morada de Rivendel.\
\
Debes volver cuanto antes junto a Laerdan con noticias de tus éxitos, pero también de los retrasos resultantes.","Filegnaneth se encuentra en el Salón del Fuego en Rivendel. Nat Tajada está en Tinnudír, en Evendim, muy al oeste y al norte del Bosque de los Trolls. Golodir está en Gath Forthnír, en Angmar, muy al norte del Bosque de los Trolls.\
\
Laerdan te ha pedido realizar varias tareas en su nombre.","Elrond está en su biblioteca en la Última Morada de Rivendel.\
\
Debes contarle de inmediato a Elrond acerca de la nota de Laerdan.","Habla con Nat Tajada en Tinnudír","Habla con Filegnaneth en Rivendel"},
[1996]={"La Mansión de Thorin está en Ered Luin, muy al oeste y al sur de Evendim.\
\
Nat Tajada te ha pedido que hables con el maestro herrero de la Mansión de Thorin y obtengas algunos moldes de acero enano para cubiertos.","Encuentra moldes de acero enano para cubiertos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¿Así que Laerdan te envía para traer de vuelta a su caballo? Eso será un poco complicado. Verás, necesita urgentemente herraduras nuevas y no tengo los materiales para terminarlas.\
\
'Sin moldes de acero enano para cubiertos, no puedo hacer mucho más. He oído que hay un maestro herrero en la Mansión de Thorin, en las Montañas Azules, muy al oeste, que podría tener algunos, pero no puedo marcharme.\
\
'¿Quizá podrías viajar a la Mansión de Thorin y comprar algunos moldes? Estoy seguro de que sabré recompensarte por tus esfuerzos...'","Lleva los moldes de acero enano para cubiertos a Nat Tajada en Tinnudír","Moldes de acero enano para cubiertos encontrados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Laerdan te ha pedido que hables con Nat Tajada, un hombre de Ost Forod que supervisa el establo de Tinnudír, sobre enviar su caballo Arel a Rivendel.","'No puedo terminar estas herraduras sin moldes de acero enano para cubiertos. Creo que puedes comprarlos a un maestro herrero en la Mansión de Thorin.'","Libro 14, Capítulo 1: El corcel Arel","'¡Bueno, estos servirán de maravilla, ${PLAYER}! ¿Dónde mejor conseguir moldes de acero enano que de los propios enanos?\
\
'Dile al maestro Laerdan que enviaré un jinete con Arel en cuanto estén terminados los nuevos herraduras.'"},
[1997]={"'I believed we would see each other again, my friend, but I did not know it would be so soon! Sending you from us was not an easy decision, but I knew Théodred had need of your aid. What sadness that he could not be saved from that fate, but perhaps that too contributed to the resolve of the Eorlingas.\
\
'The Grey Company has done what it set out to do; we have ridden to our chieftain in Rohan, and it seems we have come in time, after all. Some of our number were lost on the way, but those of us that remain will do everything in our power to ensure that Aragorn can fulfill his destiny.\
\
'I am glad to see you again, ${PLAYER}.'","'This is an unexpected joy, my friend! Had I known they were journeying to find me...'\
\
Aragorn looks at you wryly.\
\
'When you spoke to me of the Dúnedain, I did not suspect you had travelled with them in recent days, ${PLAYER}. I do not think I would have changed my course had I known, but perhaps that is the power of hindsight. Perhaps it is the wisdom of Elrond behind your silence, my friend. He is never quick to volunteer information, which makes the word of his sons even more curious.\
\
'I have much to think about, and little time in which to do so!'","Book 14, Chapter 2: Allies Unexpected","'I will show you to a quiet corner of the keep where you can rest, my friend. And then it is my understanding that you will set forth with the King for Isengard?'","'Hold on a moment, friend. Did you sleep too long? The company has already departed for the Fords of Isen!'","Talk to Déorwine and rest before setting out with the company","'The King and some others of his guard plan to ride for Isengard, but first they will take some hours rest. You should do so as well, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Speak to me if you are ready and I will prepare a place for you.'","Déorwine is inside the keep of the Hornburg, after sunrise, at Helm's Deep.\
\
Déorwine is waiting for your word, and then he will prepare a place for you to rest before setting out for Isengard with the King.","'I am delighted to see you again, my friend! The Grey Company has accomplished this first leg of its journey, and now we turn to our new purpose!'","Halbarad is on the road beyond the Fords of Isen.\
\
You have both been through much, and Halbarad greatly wishes to hear what has transpired since last you spoke.","Sometimes the best allies are those that arrive when they are not expected.","''This is an unexpected joy, my friend!'","Aragorn is beyond the Fords of Isen, and wishes to speak with you."},
[1998]={"Habla con Elrond en Rivendel","Las noticias se vuelven más nefastas a cada momento. Ay de Laerdan.\
\
'No queda tiempo que perder... ¡debemos actuar de inmediato!'","Libro 14, Capítulo 2: El rastro de Laerdan","Has encontrado una nota dejada por Laerdan en la que indica que ha salido de Rivendel con la intención de llevar los fragmentos de Narchuil a Amarthiel.","Elrond está en su biblioteca en la Última Morada de Rivendel, al este del establo.\
\
Ladrochan te dijo que Laerdan había dejado Rivendel hace dos días. Debes volver a ver a Elrond con esta información de inmediato.","Ladrochan, el maestro de establos, se encuentra en las caballerizas de Rivendel, al oeste de la Última Morada.\
\
Elrond te ha dicho que hables con Ladrochan para saber cuánto tiempo hace que Laerdan dejó Rivendel.","Habla con Ladrochan en el establo de Rivendel","'${PLAYER}, parece que los torturadores de Amarthiel lograron quebrar la mente de Laerdan. Ha abandonado Rivendel y busca llevar los fragmentos de Narchuil a Amarthiel con la vana esperanza de devolver la cordura de Narmeleth.\
\
'¡El tiempo apremia! Debemos averiguar rápidamente cuánto se ha adelantado Laerdan. Tenemos que intentar alcanzarlo antes de que logre su propósito.\
\
'Habla con Ladrochan, el maestro de establos, al oeste de aquí. Sin duda habrá visto a Laerdan.'","'¿Buscas noticias de Laerdan? Vino a verme hace dos días pidiéndome un caballo... me dijo que el señor Elrond le había dado permiso para ir en busca de la traidora Amarthiel...\
\
'¿No era así? ¡Por favor, informa al señor Elrond de inmediato!'","'Parece que me equivoqué al darle una montura a Laerdan... ¡deberías hablar con Elrond sin demora!'","'Apresúrate a ver a Ladrochan y averigua todo lo que puedas sobre la partida de Laerdan.'"},
[1999]={"Paquete examinado","Este paquete fue evidentemente dejado atrás a propósito, pues está terriblemente gastado y probablemente no habría sobrevivido a un largo viaje.","'Registra la habitación de Laerdan y vuelve cuando hayas descubierto su propósito completo.'","Mapa de Eregion examinado","Examina el diario de Laerdan","'¿Has encontrado ya algo que revele el propósito de Laerdan?'","Bobina de cuerda examinada","Elrond quedó consternado por la partida secreta de Laerdan. Ahora recaen dudas sobre el honor del señor elfo, y Elrond desea conocer la verdad tras su desaparición.","Libro 14, Capítulo 3: Arrojando luz","La habitación de Laerdan está en la Última Morada de Rivendel.\
\
Elrond te ha pedido que registres los aposentos de Laerdan en busca de cualquier cosa que revele su propósito completo.","Elrond está en la biblioteca de la Última Morada en Rivendel.\
\
Has encontrado un diario en la habitación de Laerdan. Podría revelar los planes de Laerdan.","Este diario contiene muchas entradas, pero estaba abierto en un pasaje en particular...","Registra la habitación de Laerdan","Encuentras una bobina de cuerda que Laerdan claramente había planeado llevar consigo, pero que aparentemente olvidó en su apuro por marcharse.","'Tus noticias son muy inquietantes, ${PLAYER}. Temo que la voluntad de Laerdan haya sido quebrada por los tormentos de Amarthiel.\
\
'Tienes mi aprobación para registrar la habitación de Laerdan en busca de algo que revele el propósito completo de su partida. Temo que queda poco tiempo, porque si lleva los fragmentos de Narchuil a Mirobel, Amarthiel seguramente lo estará esperando allí.\
\
'La habitación de Laerdan está en esta misma casa. Ve ahora y vuelve cuando hayas descubierto más.'","Este mapa muestra una ruta dibujada desde Rivendel hacia el sur, hasta Eregion, pero no contiene ninguna otra pista."},
}
